window.MARKET_QUESTIONS=[{"id":"indicator-beginner-01","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[1],"stem":"某资产连续五根已收盘K线的收盘价为10、11、12、13、14。下一根收盘15，仍使用5根收盘价的SMA。新SMA是多少？","options":["12","12.5","13","14"],"answer":2,"explanation":"新窗口是11、12、13、14、15，总和65除以5等于13。","optionExplanations":["12是上一根的五期均值，尚未移除10。","12.5是六个价格一起平均，窗口已经不是五期。","新窗口是11、12、13、14、15，总和65除以5等于13。","14接近近期价格，但不是这五个收盘价的均值。"],"skills":["滚动窗口","单位"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Simple Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000696841-simple-moving-average/"}],"stemEn":"An asset’s last five completed bars closed at 10, 11, 12, 13 and 14. The next bar closes at 15, and you still use a 5-bar SMA of closes. What is the new SMA?","optionsEn":["12","12.5","13","14"],"explanationEn":"The new window is 11, 12, 13, 14 and 15; the sum of 65 divided by 5 is 13.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 12 is the previous five-bar average; 10 has not been dropped yet.","Wrong: 12.5 averages six prices, so the window is no longer five bars.","Correct: The new window is 11, 12, 13, 14 and 15; 65 ÷ 5 = 13.","Wrong: 14 is close to recent prices but is not the average of these five closes."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-02","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[11],"stem":"日线RSI从65升到76，价格连续三天创收盘新高。只根据这些信息，哪种解读最贴近指标本身？","options":["上涨相对力量增强，暂未给出价格与RSI的顶背离","RSI超过70，价格创新高应解释为反弹末端信号","价格与RSI一起创新高，属于价格强而动量弱的顶背离","RSI由65到76，说明价格上涨速度提高约17%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"RSI升高且价格走高，表近期上涨相对力量增强；没有价格新高而RSI弱化的顶背离证据。","optionExplanations":["RSI升高且价格走高，表近期上涨相对力量增强；没有价格新高而RSI弱化的顶背离证据。","70是常见观察线，强趋势可持续高读数，不能单凭越线认定反弹末端。","两者同步增强不符合此处所说的顶背离特征。","RSI读数相对增加不能直接换算价格上涨速度的增加幅度。"],"skills":["动量解释","信号边界"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Relative Strength Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502338-relative-strength-index-rsi/"}],"stemEn":"Daily RSI rises from 65 to 76 while price makes new closing highs three days in a row. From this information alone, which reading stays closest to what the indicator says?","optionsEn":["Relative upside strength is increasing; there is no price–RSI bearish divergence yet","RSI above 70 with a new price high should be read as the end of the rally","Price and RSI making new highs together is a bearish divergence of strong price and weak momentum","RSI going from 65 to 76 means price is rising about 17% faster"],"explanationEn":"Rising RSI with rising price shows stronger recent upside; there is no evidence of a bearish divergence, which needs a new price high with a weaker RSI.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Rising RSI with higher prices shows stronger recent upside, with no evidence of bearish divergence.","Wrong: 70 is a common reference line; strong trends can hold high readings, so crossing it does not mark the end of a rally.","Wrong: Both strengthening together does not match the bearish divergence pattern.","Wrong: A relative rise in the RSI reading cannot be converted into a rise in the speed of price gains."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-03","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[12],"stem":"某MACD实现的柱值定义为“MACD线减信号线”。MACD线为-1.2，信号线为-1.5。应如何读？","options":["柱值-0.3，MACD在信号线下方、零轴下方","柱值0.3，MACD在信号线上方、零轴上方","柱值-2.7，MACD线与信号线都在零轴下方","柱值0.3，MACD在信号线上方、零轴下方"],"answer":3,"explanation":"两条线都负，MACD线较高，因此柱值正0.3；相对改善与绝对位置是两回事。","optionExplanations":["把相减方向弄反了，-1.2-(-1.5)应为正0.3。","柱值符号对，但MACD线是-1.2，仍在零轴下方。","把两线相加当成了柱值，柱值应是两线之差。","正确：-1.2减-1.5得0.3，MACD线高于信号线，但两线都为负，仍在零轴下方。"],"skills":["坐标阅读","差值"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — MACD","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502344-macd-moving-average-convergence-divergence/"}],"stemEn":"In one MACD implementation the histogram is defined as “MACD line minus signal line”. The MACD line is −1.2 and the signal line −1.5. How should this be read?","optionsEn":["Histogram −0.3; MACD is below the signal line and below zero","Histogram 0.3; MACD is above the signal line and above zero","Histogram −2.7; both MACD and signal lines are below zero","Histogram 0.3; MACD is above the signal line but below zero"],"explanationEn":"Both lines are negative and the MACD line is higher, so the histogram is +0.3; relative improvement and absolute position are separate things.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The subtraction is reversed; −1.2 − (−1.5) is +0.3.","Wrong: The sign of the histogram is right, but the MACD line at −1.2 is still below zero.","Wrong: This adds the two lines; the histogram is their difference.","Correct: −1.2 minus −1.5 is 0.3, so MACD is above the signal line, but both are negative and still below zero."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-04","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[21,22],"stem":"价格仍在布林带内部，带宽连续下降。已知中轨近乎水平，仅凭带宽最适合得出什么？","options":["近期价格分散度下降，已经暗示随后向下突破","近期价格分散度下降，但突破方向尚未给出","近期价格分散度下降，下一根K线振幅也按比例缩小","近期价格分散度下降，价格处于超卖并将回升"],"answer":1,"explanation":"带宽变窄说明近期波动收缩；收缩可为后续扩张提供观察背景，方向要另找证据。","optionExplanations":["带宽只衡量波动大小，不提供突破方向。","正确：带宽收窄表示近期波动收缩，方向需另找证据。","带宽收窄是对近期的描述，不能推出下一根K线的具体振幅。","带宽不衡量超买超卖，也不预告回升。"],"skills":["波动与方向","证据范围"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bollinger Bands","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501840-bollinger-bands-bb/"},{"title":"TradingView — Bollinger BandWidth","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501972-bollinger-bandwidth-bbw/"}],"stemEn":"Price is still inside the Bollinger Bands and the bandwidth keeps falling. The middle band is nearly flat. What is the best conclusion from bandwidth alone?","optionsEn":["Recent dispersion is falling, which already hints at a downside breakout","Recent dispersion is falling, but the breakout direction is not given","Recent dispersion is falling, so the next bar’s range will shrink proportionally","Recent dispersion is falling, price is oversold and will rebound"],"explanationEn":"A narrowing bandwidth shows recent volatility contracting; contraction can be the backdrop for later expansion, but direction needs other evidence.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Bandwidth measures only the size of volatility, not breakout direction.","Correct: Narrowing bands show contracting volatility; direction needs other evidence.","Wrong: Narrowing describes the recent past and cannot give the next bar’s exact range.","Wrong: Bandwidth does not measure overbought or oversold and does not forecast a rebound."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-05","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[27,28],"stem":"A价格100，ATR为2；B价格20，ATR为1。同周期同算法，若只比较“相对价格的波动大小”，应怎样排？","options":["B较大，ATR占价格5%，高于A的2%","A较大，ATR数值2大于1，数值越大波动越大","A较大，价格100高于20，价格越高百分比越大","两者相当，同周期同算法的ATR可直接等同"],"answer":0,"explanation":"换算成百分比后B为5%，A为2%，B的相对波动较高。","optionExplanations":["正确：1/20=5%，2/100=2%，换算成百分比后B的相对波动更大。","ATR是价格单位的绝对值，不同价位不能直接比数值。","价格高低本身不决定波动百分比，要看ATR与价格之比。","同算法只保证口径一致，价位不同时仍需换算成百分比。"],"skills":["波动标准化","百分比"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Average True Range","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501823-average-true-range-atr/"},{"title":"TradingView — ATR and ATR% screening","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501823-average-true-range-atr/"}],"stemEn":"Asset A is priced at 100 with an ATR of 2; asset B is priced at 20 with an ATR of 1. Same timeframe and method. Comparing only volatility relative to price, how do they rank?","optionsEn":["B is higher: ATR is 5% of price, above A’s 2%","A is higher: an ATR of 2 is bigger than 1, and bigger means more volatile","A is higher: a price of 100 is above 20, and higher prices mean bigger percentages","They are equal: ATRs on the same timeframe and method are directly equivalent"],"explanationEn":"In percentage terms B is 5% and A is 2%, so B is relatively more volatile.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 1/20 = 5% and 2/100 = 2%, so B is relatively more volatile.","Wrong: ATR is in price units; values at different price levels cannot be compared directly.","Wrong: Price level alone does not set the percentage; look at ATR divided by price.","Wrong: The same method only keeps the definition consistent; different price levels still need converting to percentages."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-06","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[34],"stem":"上一根OBV为1000，本根收盘低于前收盘，成交量为200；按常见OBV规则，新值是多少？","options":["1200","1000","800","200"],"answer":2,"explanation":"收盘较前收盘低，把本根成交量从累计值扣除，1000-200=800。","optionExplanations":["把下跌日的成交量加了上去，方向弄反。","误以为下跌日OBV保持不变，实际要扣减成交量。","正确：收盘低于前收盘，从累计值扣除本根成交量，1000-200=800。","把本根成交量当成了新的OBV，忽略了累计性质。"],"skills":["累计与单期","量价"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — On Balance Volume","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502593-on-balance-volume-obv/"}],"stemEn":"The previous OBV was 1,000. This bar closes below the prior close on volume of 200. Under the common OBV rule, what is the new value?","optionsEn":["1,200","1,000","800","200"],"explanationEn":"The close is below the prior close, so this bar’s volume is subtracted: 1,000 − 200 = 800.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This adds a down day’s volume, which is the wrong direction.","Wrong: This assumes OBV is unchanged on a down day; the volume must be subtracted.","Correct: The close is lower, so subtract this bar’s volume: 1,000 − 200 = 800.","Wrong: This uses the bar’s volume as the new OBV, ignoring that OBV is cumulative."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-07","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[37],"stem":"同一交易时段已成交两笔：100元成交1单位，110元成交3单位。忽略其他成交，该时段VWAP为多少？","options":["105元","103.33元","110元","107.5元"],"answer":3,"explanation":"总成交金额100×1+110×3=430，总量4，VWAP=107.5。","optionExplanations":["105是两种价格的简单平均，忽略了成交单位差异。","这个数没有使用题设的正确权重；总金额应为430。","110只是较大一笔的成交价，不是全部成交均价。","总成交金额100×1+110×3=430，总量4，VWAP=107.5。"],"skills":["成交量权重","均价"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Volume Weighted Average Price","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502018-volume-weighted-average-price-vwap/"}],"stemEn":"Two trades have printed in the same session: 1 unit at 100 and 3 units at 110. Ignoring other trades, what is the session VWAP?","optionsEn":["105","103.33","110","107.5"],"explanationEn":"Total value is 100×1 + 110×3 = 430 on 4 units, so VWAP = 107.5.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 105 is the simple average of the two prices and ignores the different sizes.","Wrong: This does not use the correct weights; the total value should be 430.","Wrong: 110 is only the price of the larger trade, not the average of all trades.","Correct: Total value 100×1 + 110×3 = 430 on 4 units gives a VWAP of 107.5."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-08","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[41,42],"stem":"ADX从18升到30，同期-DI高于+DI，价格高点和低点都在降低。哪种解释最合理？","options":["趋势强度上升，ADX升高本身就指向价格上行","趋势强度上升，-DI与价格高低点都指向下行","趋势强度上升，ADX到30说明下跌接近耗尽","趋势强度上升，+DI与-DI此时相互抵消方向"],"answer":1,"explanation":"强度看ADX，方向结合DI与高低点；这里三者支持下行趋势增强。","optionExplanations":["ADX只衡量强度，不给方向，方向要看DI和价格结构。","正确：ADX表示强度，-DI高于+DI且高低点下移，共同指向下行趋势增强。","ADX升高说明趋势在增强，并不等于过度或将要反弹。","ADX与DI分工不同，不会互相抵消，这里三者同指下行。"],"skills":["强度与方向","组合阅读"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Average Directional Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589099-average-directional-index-adx/"},{"title":"TradingView: Directional Movement Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502250-directional-movement-dmi/"}],"stemEn":"ADX rises from 18 to 30 while −DI is above +DI and price highs and lows keep falling. Which interpretation is most reasonable?","optionsEn":["Trend strength is rising, and a rising ADX itself points to higher prices","Trend strength is rising, and −DI and the price swings both point down","Trend strength is rising, and ADX at 30 means the decline is nearly exhausted","Trend strength is rising, and +DI and −DI cancel each other’s direction"],"explanationEn":"ADX shows strength; direction comes from the DIs and the swings. Here all three support a strengthening downtrend.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: ADX measures strength only, not direction; direction comes from the DIs and price structure.","Correct: ADX shows strength, −DI above +DI and falling swings point to a strengthening downtrend.","Wrong: A rising ADX means the trend is strengthening, not that it is overdone or about to bounce.","Wrong: ADX and the DIs have different roles and do not cancel; here all three point down."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-09","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[40],"stem":"本月A下跌2%，基准B下跌8%。以A/B价格比值观察相对表现，下列哪种判断正确？","options":["A本身下跌，所以A/B比值同步下降，相对较弱","A跌幅较小，所以本月持有A仍能取得小幅收益","A绝对下跌，但A/B比值上升，相对更强","两者都在下跌，A/B比值保持不变，相对无差异"],"answer":2,"explanation":"比值变化为0.98/0.92，大于1；A可在亏损的同时相对抗跌。","optionExplanations":["绝对涨跌与相对强弱是两件事，比值要看两者的相对变化。","A本月下跌2%，持有仍是亏损，相对强不等于绝对盈利。","正确：比值变化为0.98/0.92大于1，A亏损的同时相对抗跌。","跌幅不同，比值就会变化，不会保持不变。"],"skills":["相对与绝对","基准"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Spread charts explained","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502298-spread-charts-explained/"}],"stemEn":"This month A falls 2% while benchmark B falls 8%. Looking at relative performance through the A/B price ratio, which statement is correct?","optionsEn":["A fell, so the A/B ratio fell with it and A is relatively weaker","A fell less, so holding A this month still earned a small gain","A fell in absolute terms, but the A/B ratio rose, so A is relatively stronger","Both fell, so the A/B ratio is unchanged and there is no relative difference"],"explanationEn":"The ratio changes by 0.98/0.92, which is above 1; A can lose money while holding up better.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Absolute and relative performance are different; the ratio depends on the relative change of both.","Wrong: A fell 2% this month, so holding it was still a loss; relative strength is not absolute profit.","Correct: The ratio changes by 0.98/0.92 > 1, so A lost money while holding up better.","Wrong: Different declines change the ratio; it does not stay the same."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-10","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[101],"stem":"某数据源按成交主动方分类：一根K线主动买成交700单位，主动卖成交500单位。Delta=买减卖。可以直接读出什么？","options":["总成交量为200，同时买方更占优","买卖差为200，同时净新增多头持仓200","买卖差为200，分类成交合计700","买卖差为200，分类成交合计1200"],"answer":3,"explanation":"700-500=200，700+500=1200；差值和总量需分别看。","optionExplanations":["200只是差值，不是总成交量。","Delta是主动成交的差，不等于持仓的净增加。","把主动买成交量当成了合计，漏掉了主动卖的500。","正确：700-500=200是差值，700+500=1200是分类成交合计。"],"skills":["成交分类","差值与总量"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume Delta official tutorial","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XL5KiP2mBUQ"}],"stemEn":"A data source classifies trades by aggressor: in one bar, 700 units were aggressive buys and 500 aggressive sells. Delta = buys minus sells. What can be read directly?","optionsEn":["Total volume is 200, and buyers are dominant","The buy–sell difference is 200, and net new long positions rose by 200","The buy–sell difference is 200, and classified volume totals 700","The buy–sell difference is 200, and classified volume totals 1,200"],"explanationEn":"700 − 500 = 200 and 700 + 500 = 1,200; the difference and the total must be read separately.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 200 is only the difference, not total volume.","Wrong: Delta is the difference in aggressive trades, not a net change in positions.","Wrong: This counts aggressive buys as the total and leaves out the 500 aggressive sells.","Correct: 700 − 500 = 200 is the difference and 700 + 500 = 1,200 is the classified total."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-11","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[106],"stem":"固定100只股票的样本中，65只位于各自200日均线上方，昨天60只。该读数最直接说明什么？","options":["长期均线上方占比升到65%，不是当日收涨家数","当日收涨家数从60家增加到65家，短线参与面扩大","突破昨日最高价的股票增加了5只，短线动能明显转强","少数权重股推动指数的程度下降，上涨的广度变得更好"],"answer":0,"explanation":"从60%到65%说明更多样本位于长期均线上方；当日涨跌家数是另一种统计。","optionExplanations":["正确：占比从60%升到65%反映长期均线上方参与面扩大，当日涨跌家数是另一种统计。","该读数统计的是位于200日均线上方的数量，不是当日收涨家数。","读数与昨日最高价无关，只比较股价与各自200日均线。","样本等权计数，无法直接判断权重股对指数的贡献。"],"skills":["广度","百分点"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Market breadth — Above moving averages","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000794827-market-breadth-above-moving-averages/"}],"stemEn":"In a fixed sample of 100 stocks, 65 are above their own 200-day moving average, versus 60 yesterday. What does this reading most directly show?","optionsEn":["The share above the long-term average rose to 65%, which is not today’s count of advancers","Today’s advancers rose from 60 to 65, so short-term participation widened","Five more stocks broke yesterday’s high, so short-term momentum clearly improved","Fewer heavyweight stocks are driving the index, so breadth is improving"],"explanationEn":"Going from 60% to 65% means more of the sample is above its long-term average; today’s advancers and decliners are a different statistic.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The share rising from 60% to 65% shows wider participation above the long-term average; daily advancers are a different statistic.","Wrong: The reading counts stocks above their 200-day average, not today’s advancers.","Wrong: The reading has nothing to do with yesterday’s high; it compares each stock with its own 200-day average.","Wrong: The sample is an equal-weighted count and cannot show heavyweight stocks’ contribution to the index."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-12","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[95],"stem":"一个高点枢轴要求右边两根K线都收盘后才能确认。候选高点出现在周一日线，周二、周三也都符合条件。最早何时可据此作“已确认”判断？","options":["周一收盘，因为高点最终画在周一","周二开盘，因为已经出现了右侧K线","周二收盘，因为只需看到一次回落","周三收盘，因为右侧两根此时才完成"],"answer":3,"explanation":"周三收盘才拥有完整右侧两根信息；回测信号时间也必须相应推后。","optionExplanations":["图上标记可以回画到周一，但周一还不知道右侧两根结果。","开盘只产生了一根未完成K线，没有满足两根确认。","题目明确要求右侧两根，不是一根回落。","周三收盘才拥有完整右侧两根信息；回测信号时间也必须相应推后。"],"skills":["确认时间","避免前视"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Pivot Points High/Low example","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/v4/essential/drawings/"}],"stemEn":"A pivot high is confirmed only after two bars to its right have closed. The candidate high is on Monday’s daily bar, and Tuesday and Wednesday both meet the condition. When is the earliest you can call it “confirmed”?","optionsEn":["Monday’s close, because the high is ultimately drawn on Monday","Tuesday’s open, because a bar to the right has appeared","Tuesday’s close, because only one pullback is needed","Wednesday’s close, because the two right-hand bars are complete only then"],"explanationEn":"Only at Wednesday’s close are both right-hand bars complete; backtest signal times must be delayed accordingly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The marker can be drawn back on Monday, but on Monday the two right-hand bars were unknown.","Wrong: At the open only one unfinished bar exists, so two-bar confirmation is not met.","Wrong: The rule clearly requires two bars to the right, not one pullback.","Correct: Only Wednesday’s close completes the two right-hand bars; backtest signals must be delayed accordingly."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-01","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[9,11,12],"stem":"同一资产同一日线的均线交叉、MACD和RSI同时转强。研究员将三者当作三份彼此独立的证据。最应先修正什么？","options":["它们公式各不相同，给相同权重后就能视为独立证据","它们同源于价格序列，应检验组合的增量与样本外表现","它们周期不同，统一改成更长周期即可消除重复信息","它们都支持上涨，应再添加几个同类指标来提高证据强度"],"answer":1,"explanation":"这些指标虽公式不同，却多从同一价格序列派生；需要验证组合是否增加有效信息。","optionExplanations":["公式不同不等于信息独立，等权不会消除相关性。","正确：三者都由同一价格序列派生，需验证组合是否增加有效信息。","换周期仍来自同一价格，重复信息不会消失。","再加同类指标只会增加重复，不增加独立证据。"],"skills":["证据相关","样本外"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — MA Cross","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000599879-ma-cross/"},{"title":"TradingView — Relative Strength Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502338-relative-strength-index-rsi/"},{"title":"TradingView — MACD","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502344-macd-moving-average-convergence-divergence/"}],"stemEn":"On one asset’s daily chart, a moving-average crossover, MACD and RSI all turn bullish at once. A researcher treats them as three independent pieces of evidence. What should be corrected first?","optionsEn":["Their formulas differ, so equal weights make them independent evidence","They all derive from price, so test the combination’s added value and out-of-sample results","Their periods differ, so switching all to a longer period removes the overlap","They all point up, so add a few similar indicators to strengthen the case"],"explanationEn":"Although their formulas differ, these indicators mostly derive from the same price series; check whether the combination adds real information.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Different formulas do not make information independent, and equal weights do not remove correlation.","Correct: All three derive from the same price series, so test whether the combination adds information.","Wrong: Changing the period still uses the same prices, so the overlap remains.","Wrong: Adding similar indicators only adds overlap, not independent evidence."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-02","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[56],"stem":"过去60天日收益相关系数ρ=0.90，A波动率2%，B波动率3%。以“每1美元A多头，对冲h美元B空头”的最小方差公式h=ρ×σA/σB，且暂不考虑基差和费用。应选多少？","options":["0.90美元","1.35美元","0.67美元","0.60美元"],"answer":3,"explanation":"0.90×2/3=0.60。公式输出为给定样本估计，并不保证未来最优。","optionExplanations":["0.90仅采用相关，忽略两个资产波动差异。","1.35把波动比倒置为3%/2%。","0.67采用波动比但漏乘相关0.90。","0.90×2/3=0.60。公式输出为给定样本估计，并不保证未来最优。"],"skills":["对冲比例","相关与波动"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Correlation Coefficient","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502022-correlation-coefficient-cc/"}],"stemEn":"Over the past 60 days the correlation of daily returns is ρ = 0.90; A’s volatility is 2% and B’s is 3%. Using the minimum-variance hedge ratio h = ρ × σA/σB for “$1 long A, $h short B”, and ignoring basis and fees, what h should be used?","optionsEn":["$0.90","$1.35","$0.67","$0.60"],"explanationEn":"0.90 × 2/3 = 0.60. The formula is an estimate from the sample and does not guarantee the best hedge in future.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 0.90 uses only the correlation and ignores the different volatilities.","Wrong: 1.35 inverts the volatility ratio to 3%/2%.","Wrong: 0.67 uses the volatility ratio but leaves out the 0.90 correlation.","Correct: 0.90 × 2/3 = 0.60; it is a sample estimate, not a guaranteed future optimum."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-03","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[98],"stem":"ZigZag在第10根画出低点90；到第13根收盘上涨达到算法的5%确认门槛，随后才确认第10根为低点。第13根收盘94.5，第14根开盘95。策略规定确认后下一根开盘成交。回测应记录哪组信号/成交？","options":["第13根确认，第14根95成交","第10根确认，第11根按开盘成交","第13根确认，回填第10根90成交","第14根确认，第15根按开盘成交"],"answer":0,"explanation":"低点归属第10根，但最早第13根确认；按题设下一根开盘在第14根95执行。","optionExplanations":["低点归属第10根，但最早第13根确认；按题设下一根开盘在第14根95执行。","第10根尚不知道确认条件之后会满足，提前发出信号。","信号时点写对，但用已过去的低点价格成交仍是前视执行。","题设第13根已满足确认，不需额外延迟到第14根。"],"skills":["重绘","确认与执行"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Zig Zag","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591664-zig-zag/"}],"stemEn":"ZigZag draws a low of 90 on bar 10; only when bar 13 closes up enough to hit the algorithm’s 5% threshold is bar 10 confirmed as the low. Bar 13 closes at 94.5 and bar 14 opens at 95. The strategy fills at the next bar’s open after confirmation. What signal and fill should the backtest record?","optionsEn":["Confirmed on bar 13, filled at 95 on bar 14","Confirmed on bar 10, filled at bar 11’s open","Confirmed on bar 13, back-filled at 90 on bar 10","Confirmed on bar 14, filled at bar 15’s open"],"explanationEn":"The low belongs to bar 10, but the earliest confirmation is bar 13; by the rules the fill is at bar 14’s open of 95.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The low belongs to bar 10, but it is confirmed on bar 13 and filled at bar 14’s open of 95.","Wrong: On bar 10 it was not yet known that the confirmation condition would be met, so this signal is early.","Wrong: The signal time is right, but filling at a price already in the past is still look-ahead execution.","Wrong: Bar 13 already meets the confirmation rule, so there is no need to wait until bar 14."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-04","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[21,23],"stem":"定义%B=(价格-下轨)/(上轨-下轨)。A时点下轨90、上轨110、价格112；B时点下轨98、上轨102、价格103。按这个定义哪个相对越轨更大？","options":["A，价格高于上轨2，而B只高1","两者相同，因为都高于各自上轨","B，%B为1.25，而A为1.10","A，%B为1.20，而B为1.10"],"answer":2,"explanation":"A=(112-90)/20=1.10，B=(103-98)/4=1.25，B相对轨道越得更多。","optionExplanations":["按绝对越轨距离比较，忽略了轨道宽度。","都越轨不等于标准化距离相同。","A=(112-90)/20=1.10，B=(103-98)/4=1.25，B相对轨道越得更多。","所列数值不符合公式，需分别按各自上下轨计算。"],"skills":["标准化","布林位置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bollinger Bands","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501840-bollinger-bands-bb/"},{"title":"John Bollinger — %b companion indicator","url":"https://www.bollingerbands.com/bollinger-bands"}],"stemEn":"Define %B = (price − lower band) ÷ (upper band − lower band). At time A the lower band is 90, upper 110, price 112; at time B the lower band is 98, upper 102, price 103. By this definition, which is further outside the band relative to its width?","optionsEn":["A, because it is 2 above the upper band while B is only 1 above","They are the same, because both are above their upper band","B, with %B of 1.25 versus A’s 1.10","A, with %B of 1.20 versus B’s 1.10"],"explanationEn":"A = (112 − 90)/20 = 1.10 and B = (103 − 98)/4 = 1.25, so B is further outside relative to its band.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This compares absolute distances and ignores band width.","Wrong: Both being outside does not make their normalised distances equal.","Correct: A = (112 − 90)/20 = 1.10 and B = (103 − 98)/4 = 1.25.","Wrong: These values do not follow the formula; compute each with its own bands."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-05","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[24],"stem":"用过去20根最高价作为突破线，规则要求本根收盘高于该线。程序误把本根最高价也放进20根窗口。为恢复原来的突破定义，应怎样修正？","options":["比较本根收盘与此前20根上轨，窗口不含本根","比较本根最高价与含本根的20根上轨，替代收盘判断","保持含本根窗口，把窗口增加到21根后再比较收盘","保持含本根窗口，改为要求收盘等于上轨才算突破"],"answer":0,"explanation":"普通OHLC中收盘不可能高于自身最高价，因此也不可能严格高于包含自身最高价的上轨；应比较此前20根上轨。","optionExplanations":["正确：窗口应排除本根，收盘才可能严格高于此前20根的最高价。","含本根的上轨至少等于本根最高价，永远无法被它严格超过，且改变了原定义。","窗口仍含本根，收盘依旧不可能高于含自身最高价的上轨。","这改变了突破定义，并非原来的“高于”。"],"skills":["窗口排除","规则实现"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Donchian Channels","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502253-donchian-channels-dc/"}],"stemEn":"A breakout line uses the highest high of the past 20 bars, and the rule requires this bar to close above it. The program mistakenly includes the current bar’s high in the 20-bar window. How should it be fixed to restore the original definition?","optionsEn":["Compare the current close with the prior 20 bars’ high, excluding the current bar","Compare the current high with a 20-bar high that includes it, instead of the close","Keep the current bar in the window, widen it to 21 bars and then compare the close","Keep the current bar in the window and require the close to equal the line"],"explanationEn":"On ordinary OHLC bars the close can never exceed its own high, so it can never be strictly above a line that includes that high; compare with the prior 20 bars.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Excluding the current bar lets the close be strictly above the prior 20-bar high.","Wrong: A line that includes the current bar is at least its high, so it can never be strictly exceeded, and this changes the definition.","Wrong: The window still includes the current bar, so the close still cannot exceed a line containing its own high.","Wrong: This changes the breakout definition; it is no longer “above”."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-06","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[27,89],"stem":"策略用“已观察到的最高价减3×ATR”作多头跟踪止损。本次最高价从100升到101，ATR从2升到4。若系统要求止损只收紧不放宽，旧止损94，新候选89，应怎样处理？","options":["保留94，因为候选89会把止损放宽","改成89，因为公式已反映最新波动","改成101，因为最高价上升需要同步保护","改成97，因为最高价上升1，ATR也应只加1"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只收紧的约束要求新止损=max(旧止损,候选)，即max(94,89)=94。","optionExplanations":["只收紧的约束要求新止损=max(旧止损,候选)，即max(94,89)=94。","89是候选公式值，但违反题设明确规定的只收紧约束。","最高价不是止损价，题目没有零距离保护规则。","ATR从2到4不是加1；也没有如此混合修改的规则。"],"skills":["风险规则","波动变化"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Average True Range","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501823-average-true-range-atr/"},{"title":"TradingView: Chandelier Exit","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773013-chandelier-exit/"}],"stemEn":"A long trailing stop is “highest high seen minus 3 × ATR”. The high rises from 100 to 101 and ATR rises from 2 to 4. If the stop may only tighten, never loosen, and the old stop is 94 while the new candidate is 89, what should be done?","optionsEn":["Keep 94, because 89 would loosen the stop","Switch to 89, because the formula reflects the latest volatility","Switch to 101, because the higher high needs matching protection","Switch to 97, because the high rose by 1, so ATR should only add 1"],"explanationEn":"A tighten-only rule means new stop = max(old stop, candidate) = max(94, 89) = 94.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Tighten-only means max(old stop, candidate) = max(94, 89) = 94.","Wrong: 89 is the formula’s candidate, but it breaks the stated tighten-only rule.","Wrong: The high is not the stop price, and there is no zero-distance rule here.","Wrong: ATR went from 2 to 4, not up by 1, and there is no such mixed rule."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-07","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[86],"stem":"美股5分钟图上午10:00，同日累计成交量是过去20个完整交易日10:00累计均量的1.8倍。另一脚本用最近20根5分钟柱均量作分母，得到3.0倍。先怎样判断差异？","options":["以反应更快的脚本数值为准，把另一个视为数据滞后","取1.8与3.0的平均值，当作同一时点的相对活跃度","判定1.8倍更保守、3.0倍更激进，两者只是灵敏度不同","先统一累计或单柱、同刻或近期的口径，再比较倍数"],"answer":3,"explanation":"两个分母比较对象不同，应先校准时点与累计/单柱口径，再解释数值。","optionExplanations":["差异来自口径不同，不是速度或滞后问题。","平均两个口径不同的数没有意义。","两者是不同分母的比较，不是灵敏度差别。","正确：两个分母比较对象不同，应先校准口径再解释数值。"],"skills":["时段季节性","统计口径"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Relative Volume at Time","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000705489-relative-volume-at-time/"}],"stemEn":"On a US stock’s 5-minute chart at 10:00, today’s cumulative volume is 1.8× the average cumulative volume at 10:00 over the past 20 full sessions. Another script divides by the average of the last 20 five-minute bars and gets 3.0×. What should you check first about the difference?","optionsEn":["Trust the faster script and treat the other as lagging data","Average 1.8 and 3.0 as the relative activity at that moment","Call 1.8× conservative and 3.0× aggressive; they only differ in sensitivity","First align cumulative versus single-bar and same-time versus recent bases, then compare"],"explanationEn":"The two denominators compare different things; align the time basis and cumulative/single-bar definition before interpreting the numbers.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The difference comes from different definitions, not speed or lag.","Wrong: Averaging two numbers built on different definitions is meaningless.","Wrong: They use different denominators; it is not a difference in sensitivity.","Correct: The two denominators compare different things, so align the definitions first."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-08","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[55,54],"stem":"给定同一回归窗口：总离差平方和SST=100，残差平方和SSE=4，回归斜率=-0.8。使用R²=1-SSE/SST。下列哪个同时把数值和含义解释正确？","options":["R²=0.96，未来继续下跌的概率约为96%","R²=0.04，样本内价格围绕下降直线很分散","R²=0.96，样本内价格较贴近这条下降直线","R²=-0.96，负号由斜率决定，表示下降拟合"],"answer":2,"explanation":"1-4/100=0.96，结合负斜率说明样本内贴近下降直线，不提供未来胜率。","optionExplanations":["R²衡量样本内拟合，不是预测命中率。","算错了，0.04是SSE/SST，R²应为1减去它。","正确：1-4/100=0.96，结合负斜率说明样本内贴近下降直线，不给未来胜率。","R²由1-SSE/SST计算，不随斜率正负改变。"],"skills":["回归运算","拟合与预测"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Linear Regression R-Squared","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644936-linear-regression/"},{"title":"TradingView: Linear Regression Slope","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644936-linear-regression/"}],"stemEn":"For the same regression window: total sum of squares SST = 100, residual sum of squares SSE = 4, slope = −0.8. Using R² = 1 − SSE/SST, which option gets both the number and its meaning right?","optionsEn":["R² = 0.96, so there is about a 96% chance the decline continues","R² = 0.04, so in-sample prices are widely scattered around the falling line","R² = 0.96, so in-sample prices sit fairly close to this falling line","R² = −0.96; the sign comes from the slope and shows a downward fit"],"explanationEn":"1 − 4/100 = 0.96; with the negative slope it means in-sample prices hug a falling line. It gives no future win rate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: R² measures in-sample fit, not prediction accuracy.","Wrong: This is miscalculated: 0.04 is SSE/SST, and R² is 1 minus that.","Correct: 1 − 4/100 = 0.96; with the negative slope, in-sample prices hug a falling line, with no future win rate implied.","Wrong: R² is 1 − SSE/SST and does not change sign with the slope."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-09","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[95],"stem":"高点枢轴要求右边3根K线完成才确认。候选高点在第20根，之后第21至23根均满足条件。规则只在收盘更新信号，下根开盘执行。最早哪根执行且无未来信息？","options":["第24根开盘","第21根开盘","第23根开盘","第20根收盘"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第23根收盘才完成右侧三根，因此最早第24根开盘执行。","optionExplanations":["第23根收盘才完成右侧三根，因此最早第24根开盘执行。","第21根刚在候选后出现，缺少三根确认。","第23根开盘时该根尚未完成，第三根确认仍未知。","图可回画在第20根，但当时没有右侧三根信息。"],"skills":["右侧确认","执行时点"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Pivot Points High/Low example","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/v4/essential/drawings/"}],"stemEn":"A pivot high needs three completed bars to its right. The candidate high is bar 20, and bars 21 to 23 all meet the condition. Signals update only on closes and execute at the next bar’s open. What is the earliest execution with no future information?","optionsEn":["Bar 24’s open","Bar 21’s open","Bar 23’s open","Bar 20’s close"],"explanationEn":"Bar 23’s close completes the three right-hand bars, so the earliest execution is bar 24’s open.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Bar 23’s close completes the three bars, so the earliest execution is bar 24’s open.","Wrong: Bar 21 has only just appeared after the candidate; three-bar confirmation is missing.","Wrong: At bar 23’s open that bar is unfinished, so the third confirmation is still unknown.","Wrong: The marker can be drawn back on bar 20, but at the time there were no right-hand bars."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-10","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[102],"stem":"同币种同时间段，交易所A现货CVD上升，交易所B永续CVD下降。最合适的下一步是什么？","options":["把永续CVD反号，与现货方向对齐后再判断","把两条CVD求平均，抵消不同市场的各自噪声","只采用成交量较小的市场，认为其杠杆影响较少","先核对分类方法、单位和覆盖市场，再比较"],"answer":3,"explanation":"不同场所和产品可以真实出现分歧，也可能有口径差异；需要先校准再解释。","optionExplanations":["随意反号会扭曲数据，掩盖真实分歧。","口径不同的数据平均后失去解释意义。","成交量小不代表更可靠，也不能解决口径问题。","正确：不同场所和产品可能真实分歧，也可能口径不同，需先校准。"],"skills":["数据覆盖","跨市场"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Cumulative Volume Delta","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000725058-cumulative-volume-delta/"}],"stemEn":"For the same coin over the same period, spot CVD on exchange A rises while perpetual CVD on exchange B falls. What is the most appropriate next step?","optionsEn":["Flip the sign of the perpetual CVD to match spot, then judge","Average the two CVDs to cancel each market’s noise","Use only the lower-volume market, assuming it has less leverage influence","First check classification method, units and market coverage, then compare"],"explanationEn":"Different venues and products can genuinely diverge, or differ in definition; calibrate first, then interpret.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Flipping signs at will distorts the data and hides real divergence.","Wrong: Averaging data built on different definitions loses its meaning.","Wrong: Lower volume does not mean more reliable, and it does not fix definitions.","Correct: Venues and products may genuinely diverge or define CVD differently, so calibrate first."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-11","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[104,105,106],"stem":"指数创新高，但固定股票样本的均线上方占比下降、创新高家数也减少。下列哪项最符合现有证据？","options":["上涨参与面收窄，已确认顶部形成，指数将在数日内回落","指数新高更具说服力，广度下降只是滞后信号可以忽略","参与面收窄，提示集中度风险，但无法确定反转时点","两个广度指标同向走弱，相当于两次独立的反转确认"],"answer":2,"explanation":"这属于内部参与减弱的警示，能提示脆弱性，但不给出确定反转日期。","optionExplanations":["广度背离不能确定反转时点，也不保证短期回落。","广度下降恰是对指数新高的质疑，不应忽略。","正确：内部参与减弱是警示，能提示脆弱性，但不给确定日期。","两个指标来自同一批样本，并非独立证据。"],"skills":["市场广度","证据相关"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Advance/Decline Line","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589092-advance-decline-line/"},{"title":"TradingView: Market breadth — New highs and lows","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000794826-market-breadth-new-highs-and-lows/"},{"title":"TradingView: Market breadth — Above moving averages","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000794827-market-breadth-above-moving-averages/"}],"stemEn":"An index makes a new high, but in a fixed stock sample the share above its moving average falls and the number of new highs shrinks. Which statement best fits the evidence?","optionsEn":["Participation is narrowing, a top is confirmed and the index will fall within days","The index high is more convincing; falling breadth is just a lagging signal to ignore","Participation is narrowing, a warning of concentration risk, but the timing of any reversal is unknown","Two breadth measures weakening together equal two independent reversal confirmations"],"explanationEn":"This is a warning that internal participation is weakening; it points to fragility but gives no reversal date.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A breadth divergence cannot fix the timing of a reversal or guarantee a near-term drop.","Wrong: Falling breadth is exactly what questions the index high; it should not be ignored.","Correct: Weaker internal participation is a warning of fragility, with no reversal date.","Wrong: Both measures come from the same sample and are not independent evidence."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-12","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[49,6,7,8],"stem":"你在同一段历史上比较40组HMA、DEMA、TEMA和KAMA参数，选出收益最高组合。要判断是否值得继续研究，最有帮助的验证是哪一项？","options":["冻结流程，用新数据计成本，并检查邻近参数是否稳定","把候选参数扩充到数百组，看最优组合在历史中是否依然领先","先去掉手续费重算毛收益，再确认指标本身是否有优势","报告最优组的样本内收益，并附上误差区间作为稳健性证据"],"answer":0,"explanation":"保留未参与选参的数据，冻结后计成本验证，并考察参数附近稳定性，更有助判断泛化。","optionExplanations":["正确：用未参与选参的新数据验证，并计成本、看参数邻域稳定性，更能判断泛化。","继续在同一历史上扩大搜索，只会增加过拟合。","忽略成本会高估表现，也没有解决样本内选参问题。","样本内误差区间不能代替样本外检验。"],"skills":["多重试验","稳健性"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Kaufman's Adaptive Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773012-kaufman-s-adaptive-moving-average-kama/"},{"title":"TradingView — Hull Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589149-hull-moving-average/"},{"title":"TradingView — Double Exponential Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589132-double-exponential-moving-average-ema/"},{"title":"TradingView — Triple EMA","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591346-triple-ema/"}],"stemEn":"On one stretch of history you compare 40 parameter sets for HMA, DEMA, TEMA and KAMA and pick the most profitable. Which check helps most in deciding whether it deserves further research?","optionsEn":["Freeze the process, test on new data with costs, and check that nearby parameters are stable","Expand to hundreds of parameter sets and see whether the best still leads historically","Remove fees, recompute gross returns, and then confirm whether the indicator has an edge","Report the best set’s in-sample return with an error band as evidence of robustness"],"explanationEn":"Keeping data that played no part in selection, freezing the process, testing with costs and checking stability near the chosen parameters says more about generalisation.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Validating on unseen data with costs and checking neighbouring parameters says more about generalisation.","Wrong: Searching more on the same history only increases overfitting.","Wrong: Ignoring costs overstates results and does not solve in-sample selection.","Wrong: An in-sample error band cannot replace an out-of-sample test."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-01","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[96],"stem":"把上涨段100→140作为斐波那契回撤范围，“从高点回撤50%”对应哪个价格？","options":["130","120","110","70"],"answer":1,"explanation":"涨幅40，回吐一半20，从140减20得到120；这是观察位置，不是反弹承诺。","optionExplanations":["这相当于只回撤25%。","正确：涨幅40，回吐一半20，140-20=120。","这相当于回撤75%。","把100到140的一半误当成价格140的一半。"],"skills":["绘图锚点","回撤"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"Using a rally from 100 to 140 as the Fibonacci retracement range, what price corresponds to a 50% retracement from the high?","optionsEn":["130","120","110","70"],"explanationEn":"The rally is 40; giving back half is 20, and 140 − 20 = 120. It is a level to watch, not a promise of a bounce.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is only a 25% retracement.","Correct: The rally is 40, half is 20, and 140 − 20 = 120.","Wrong: That is a 75% retracement.","Wrong: This takes half of the price 140 instead of half of the 100–140 move."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-02","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[99],"stem":"固定区间成交量分布中，100元价位成交500单位，101元成交900单位，102元成交600单位；其他价位更少。POC在哪，代表什么？","options":["100元，区间内最早成交、容易形成支撑的价格档","102元，区间内价位最高、容易形成压力的价格档","101元，该固定区间内成交量最大的价格档","101元，该价格档上未成交挂单最多的位置"],"answer":2,"explanation":"POC按指定区间与分档统计最大成交量，这里900最大。","optionExplanations":["POC看成交量大小，与最早成交无关。","POC不是最高价，也不自动是压力位。","正确：POC是指定区间内成交量最大的价格档，这里900最大。","成交量分布统计已成交的量，不是挂单。"],"skills":["成交量分布","成交与挂单"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040-volume-profile-indicators-basic-concepts/"}],"stemEn":"In a fixed-range volume profile, 500 units traded at 100, 900 at 101 and 600 at 102, with less at every other price. Where is the POC and what does it represent?","optionsEn":["100: the earliest-traded price in the range, likely to become support","102: the highest price in the range, likely to become resistance","101: the price level with the most volume in this fixed range","101: the level with the most unfilled resting orders"],"explanationEn":"The POC is the price level with the most volume for the chosen range and bins; here that is 900.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The POC is about volume, not which price traded first.","Wrong: The POC is not the highest price and is not automatically resistance.","Correct: The POC is the level with the most volume in the chosen range; here 900.","Wrong: A volume profile counts executed volume, not resting orders."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-03","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[100],"stem":"一个TPO图每半小时给一个字母，同一价格档出现6个不同时段字母，另一档出现2个。仅由此能判断什么？","options":["前者被交易触及的半小时时段更多","前者的成交量大约是后者的三倍","前者聚集的不同参与者更多，后者较少","前者未来被回访时的停留时间也会更长"],"answer":0,"explanation":"6比2说明该价格档被更多时段覆盖，描述时间分布。","optionExplanations":["正确：TPO统计的是被触及的时段数，描述时间分布。","TPO字母数不代表成交量。","TPO不区分参与者身份。","TPO描述已发生的时间分布，不预告未来停留。"],"skills":["时间分布","统计对象"],"references":[{"title":"Wiley: Steidlmayer on Markets","url":"https://www.wiley.com/en-us/-p-9780471215561"}],"stemEn":"A TPO chart assigns one letter per half hour. One price level has letters from 6 different periods, another has 2. What can be concluded from this alone?","optionsEn":["The first level was traded in more half-hour periods","The first level had about three times the volume of the second","The first level drew more distinct participants than the second","The first level will hold price longer when revisited"],"explanationEn":"6 versus 2 means the first level was visited in more periods; it describes how time was distributed.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: TPO counts the periods in which a level traded, describing the distribution of time.","Wrong: The number of TPO letters does not measure volume.","Wrong: TPO does not distinguish who the participants were.","Wrong: TPO describes time already spent and does not forecast future behaviour."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-04","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[103],"stem":"某足迹图明确约定每档左列=主动卖成交，右列=主动买成交。一档显示“120×300”。最准确的初步解读是什么？","options":["该档净持仓增加180，说明偏向多头","该档主动买较多，买减卖差值为+180","该档仍有120卖单和300买单等待成交","该档买方新开仓300，卖方平仓120"],"answer":1,"explanation":"按题设300-120=180，反映该档主动买成交较多，不单独证明价格将上涨。","optionExplanations":["足迹图的差值是主动成交之差，不是持仓变化。","正确：按题设右列300减左列120为+180，反映主动买较多，不单独证明会上涨。","这是已成交的主动买卖量，不是挂单。","成交数据不区分开仓与平仓。"],"skills":["成交足迹","列定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume footprint complete guide","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000726164-volume-footprint-charts-a-complete-guide/"}],"stemEn":"A footprint chart states that each cell’s left column is aggressive sells and the right column aggressive buys. One cell shows “120 × 300”. What is the most accurate first reading?","optionsEn":["Net positions at this level rose by 180, so it leans bullish","Aggressive buying dominated at this level, with a buy-minus-sell difference of +180","There are still 120 sell orders and 300 buy orders waiting at this level","Buyers opened 300 new positions and sellers closed 120"],"explanationEn":"By the stated convention 300 − 120 = 180, so aggressive buying dominated at this level; it does not by itself prove price will rise.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The footprint difference is between aggressive trades, not a change in positions.","Correct: Right minus left is 300 − 120 = +180, showing more aggressive buying, which alone does not prove a rise.","Wrong: These are executed aggressive volumes, not resting orders.","Wrong: Trade data does not distinguish opening from closing."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-05","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[107],"stem":"某期货合约原未平仓量100张。一名新多头与一名新空头成交10张，双方均为开仓；按一张合约只计一次的OI口径，交易后OI是多少？","options":["110张","120张","100张","90张"],"answer":0,"explanation":"10对新多空形成10张新未平仓合约，OI从100增到110。","optionExplanations":["10对新多空形成10张新未平仓合约，OI从100增到110。","一张合约同时有多空双方，但OI按合约计一次，不把两边相加。","双方均开仓会增加OI，不是仅转移旧仓位。","减少OI需要双方关闭既有对应仓位，题设不是平仓。"],"skills":["未平仓量","双边记账"],"references":[{"title":"CME Group: Open Interest","url":"https://www.cmegroup.com/education/lessons/open-interest"}],"stemEn":"A futures contract has open interest of 100. A new long and a new short trade 10 contracts, both opening positions. Counting each contract once, what is the open interest afterwards?","optionsEn":["110","120","100","90"],"explanationEn":"Ten new long–short pairs create ten new open contracts, so OI rises from 100 to 110.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Ten new long–short pairs create ten new contracts, taking OI from 100 to 110.","Wrong: Each contract has a long and a short, but OI counts the contract once, not both sides.","Wrong: Both sides opening increases OI; it is not just a transfer of old positions.","Wrong: OI falls only when both sides close existing positions, which is not the case here."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-06","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[108],"stem":"某永续合约规定本次正资金费率由多头向空头支付。结算时多头名义仓位10000美元，费率0.01%，忽略其他费用。本次资金费是多少？","options":["多头付10美元","多头付100美元","多头收1美元","多头付1美元"],"answer":3,"explanation":"10000×0.0001=1美元，由题设中的多头支付。","optionExplanations":["把0.01%当成了0.1%。","把0.01%当成了1%。","方向弄反，题设正费率由多头支付。","正确：10000×0.0001=1美元，由多头支付。"],"skills":["费率单位","支付方向"],"references":[{"title":"BitMEX: 2016 perpetual launch","url":"https://www.bitmex.com/blog/site-announcement/2432"}],"stemEn":"A perpetual contract says a positive funding rate is paid by longs to shorts. At settlement a long holds a notional position of $10,000 and the rate is 0.01%, ignoring other fees. What is the funding payment?","optionsEn":["The long pays $10","The long pays $100","The long receives $1","The long pays $1"],"explanationEn":"10,000 × 0.0001 = $1, paid by the long as stated.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This treats 0.01% as 0.1%.","Wrong: This treats 0.01% as 1%.","Wrong: The direction is reversed; a positive rate is paid by longs here.","Correct: 10,000 × 0.0001 = $1, paid by the long."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-07","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[109],"stem":"某交易所报告净多账户600、净空账户400，多空账户比为1.5。仅根据这个统计，哪项成立？","options":["统计范围内多头合约总张数是空头合约的1.5倍","统计范围内多头持仓资金量是空头资金量的1.5倍","统计范围内净多账户数量是净空账户的1.5倍","多头占优，所以下一期资金费率约为正0.5%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"600/400=1.5，描述该交易所和规则下账户数量的比例。","optionExplanations":["比值统计账户数，不是合约张数。","账户数量比不代表资金规模比。","正确：600/400=1.5，描述的是账户数量比例。","账户比与资金费率没有这样的换算关系。"],"skills":["账户与仓位","覆盖范围"],"references":[{"title":"Binance derivatives API: Global long/short account ratio","url":"https://developers.binance.com/docs/derivatives/usds-margined-futures/market-data/rest-api/Long-Short-Ratio"}],"stemEn":"An exchange reports 600 net-long accounts and 400 net-short accounts, a long/short account ratio of 1.5. Based only on this statistic, which is true?","optionsEn":["Within the sample, the number of long contracts is 1.5 times the short contracts","Within the sample, long capital is 1.5 times short capital","Within the sample, net-long accounts number 1.5 times net-short accounts","Longs dominate, so the next funding rate will be about +0.5%"],"explanationEn":"600/400 = 1.5 describes the ratio of account counts on that exchange under its rules.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The ratio counts accounts, not contracts.","Wrong: An account-count ratio is not a capital ratio.","Correct: 600/400 = 1.5 describes the ratio of account counts.","Wrong: The account ratio has no such conversion to a funding rate."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-08","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[110],"stem":"一个页面显示过去1小时“多头强平800万美元，空头强平200万美元”。你正在找“未来可能触发强平的价位”。这组数据能直接给你什么？","options":["多头在未来被强平的概率大约是空头的4倍","当前全市场未平仓的多头规模约是空头的4倍","多头强平会集中发生在现价下方约800美元处","这是已发生的强平金额，不能定位未来价位"],"answer":3,"explanation":"这些是事后流量数据；定位未来潜在强平还需模型和仓位假设。","optionExplanations":["历史金额比不是未来概率。","强平流量不是未平仓存量。","800万是金额，不是价格距离。","正确：这是事后流量，定位未来强平还需模型和仓位假设。"],"skills":["已发生与预测","金额单位"],"references":[{"title":"Binance: Liquidation order streams","url":"https://developers.binance.com/docs/derivatives/usds-margined-futures/websocket-market-streams/Liquidation-Order-Streams"}],"stemEn":"A page shows “long liquidations $8 million, short liquidations $2 million” over the past hour. You are looking for price levels where liquidations may be triggered in future. What does this data give you directly?","optionsEn":["Longs are about four times as likely as shorts to be liquidated in future","Open long positions across the market are about four times open shorts","Long liquidations will cluster about $800 below the current price","These are liquidation amounts that already happened; they cannot locate future levels"],"explanationEn":"These are after-the-fact flows; locating potential future liquidations needs a model and position assumptions.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A historical amount ratio is not a future probability.","Wrong: Liquidation flows are not the stock of open positions.","Wrong: $8 million is an amount, not a price distance.","Correct: This is after-the-fact flow; future liquidation levels need a model and assumptions."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-09","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[99,100],"stem":"同一天同一价格分档，100元档被很多半小时TPO字母覆盖，101元档却有最大的成交量。两个图是否矛盾？","options":["不矛盾，时间停留多与成交量最大是两种统计","矛盾，停留时段最多的价位成交量也应最大","不矛盾，TPO用分钟数据，成交量分布用日线数据","矛盾，同一天同一分档的两图应得到相同POC"],"answer":0,"explanation":"少数时段也可能集中大量成交，因此时间集中档与量集中档可以不同。","optionExplanations":["正确：少数时段也可能集中大量成交，两者本来统计不同。","时间和成交量是不同维度，不必一致。","两者并不是按数据周期这样区分的。","两种图的统计维度不同，POC可以不同。"],"skills":["时间与成交量","口径"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040-volume-profile-indicators-basic-concepts/"},{"title":"Wiley: Steidlmayer on Markets","url":"https://www.wiley.com/en-us/-p-9780471215561"}],"stemEn":"On the same day with the same price bins, the 100 level is covered by many half-hour TPO letters, yet the 101 level has the most volume. Do the two charts contradict each other?","optionsEn":["No: time spent and volume traded are two different statistics","Yes: the level with the most time should also have the most volume","No: TPO uses minute data while volume profile uses daily data","Yes: two charts on the same day and bins should give the same POC"],"explanationEn":"A lot of volume can trade in a few periods, so the busiest level by time and by volume can differ.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Much volume can trade in a few periods; the two measure different things.","Wrong: Time and volume are different dimensions and need not agree.","Wrong: The two are not distinguished by data frequency like this.","Wrong: The charts measure different dimensions, so their POCs can differ."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-10","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[107],"stem":"在同一合约同一窗口，成交量为1000张，OI只增加20张。哪项最合理？","options":["成交里只有20张找到了交易对手，其余尚未撮合","成交可反复换手或开平相抵，OI只记录净存量","窗口内大量成交记录丢失，才会令OI增量偏小","20张就是主动买成交减去主动卖成交的差额"],"answer":1,"explanation":"成交量累加窗口内交易，OI反映未结束合约存量；多次换手可使两者差很大。","optionExplanations":["每笔成交都有对手方，不存在未撮合的成交。","正确：成交累加窗口内交易，OI是存量，多次换手可使两者差很大。","无需假设数据丢失，流量与存量本就不同。","OI变化不是主动买卖差。"],"skills":["存量与流量","成交与持仓"],"references":[{"title":"CME Group: Open Interest","url":"https://www.cmegroup.com/education/lessons/open-interest"}],"stemEn":"For the same contract and window, volume is 1,000 contracts but open interest rises by only 20. Which explanation is most reasonable?","optionsEn":["Only 20 of the contracts found a counterparty; the rest have not matched","Contracts can change hands repeatedly or open and close against each other; OI records only the net stock","A lot of trade records in the window were lost, making the OI rise look small","The 20 is aggressive buy volume minus aggressive sell volume"],"explanationEn":"Volume adds up trades in the window, while OI reflects the stock of open contracts; heavy turnover can make the two very different.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Every trade has a counterparty; there are no unmatched trades.","Correct: Volume accumulates trades while OI is a stock, so heavy turnover can separate them.","Wrong: There is no need to assume lost data; flow and stock are simply different.","Wrong: A change in OI is not the aggressive buy–sell difference."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-11","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[96],"stem":"同一上涨段，两个人分别把起点放在盘中最低价95和收盘最低价100，终点都用140。两人的61.8%回撤线不同。最先该做什么？","options":["先统计哪条线过去引发的反弹更多，再决定锚点","先统一用极值还是收盘、范围和方向，再比较","把两线之间的区域当作标准区，不再争论锚点","只统一日线周期，各自保留原来选的起点终点"],"answer":1,"explanation":"回撤值由锚点决定；统一锚点定义和范围才能比较计算结果。","optionExplanations":["先看结果再选锚点是事后挑选。","正确：回撤线由锚点决定，应先统一锚点定义。","锚点分歧未解决，区域仍不确定。","周期一致不能消除锚点差异。"],"skills":["锚点一致性","复现"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"For the same rally, one person anchors at the intraday low of 95 and another at the lowest close of 100, both ending at 140. Their 61.8% retracement lines differ. What should be done first?","optionsEn":["Count which line produced more bounces in the past, then choose the anchor","First agree on extremes or closes, the range and the direction, then compare","Treat the zone between the two lines as standard and stop debating anchors","Just agree on the daily timeframe and keep each person’s own anchors"],"explanationEn":"Retracement levels depend on the anchors; only with the same anchor definition and range can results be compared.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Choosing the anchor after seeing results is hindsight selection.","Correct: Retracement levels depend on the anchors, so agree on the anchor definition first.","Wrong: The anchor disagreement is unresolved, so the zone is still uncertain.","Wrong: A shared timeframe does not remove the anchor difference."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-12","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[103],"stem":"足迹图某档主动买成交明显多于主动卖成交，但该根K线收盘低于开盘。最合理的认识是什么？","options":["多半是左右列放反了，应先交换再解释这根K线","整根收跌说明未显示的其余档位以主动卖出为主","该档主动买差值可当作整根K线收盘强弱的替代","局部档位成交不代表整根结果，需结合其他档"],"answer":3,"explanation":"主动买可遇到被动卖承接；局部成交与整根价格结果应放在各自范围理解。","optionExplanations":["主动买多而价格跌是可能出现的，不必归咎于列放反。","没有其他档位数据，不能这样推断。","单档差值不能代表整根K线的结果。","正确：局部成交与整根价格结果范围不同，主动买可被被动卖承接。"],"skills":["局部与整体","成交与价格"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume footprint complete guide","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000726164-volume-footprint-charts-a-complete-guide/"}],"stemEn":"In a footprint chart, one level shows clearly more aggressive buying than selling, yet the bar closes below its open. What is the most reasonable understanding?","optionsEn":["The columns are probably swapped; swap them before interpreting the bar","The bar closing lower means the other, unseen levels were dominated by aggressive selling","This level’s buy-minus-sell difference can stand in for the bar’s closing strength","Trading at one level does not represent the whole bar; look at the other levels too"],"explanationEn":"Aggressive buying can be absorbed by passive sellers; local trading and the bar’s overall result should be understood at their own scales.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Aggressive buying with a lower close can happen; there is no need to blame swapped columns.","Wrong: Without the other levels’ data, this cannot be inferred.","Wrong: One level’s difference cannot represent the whole bar’s result.","Correct: Local trading and the whole bar differ in scope; aggressive buying can be absorbed by passive sellers."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-01","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[99],"stem":"用“可见范围成交量分布”比较两张截图，POC从100变成106；期间行情数据未更新，只缩放了图表。如何验证这是范围变化而非新增成交造成？","options":["把分档数量调到最大，不再理会横轴范围变化","用最新成交价代替POC，以排除历史范围影响","固定起止时间和分档，重算同一区间的POC","比较两张截图中成交量柱的整体形状是否相似"],"answer":2,"explanation":"可见范围改变了输入样本；固定时间与分档后才可判断同一批数据的结果。","optionExplanations":["范围变化的影响仍然存在。","最新价不是POC，无法回答POC变化原因。","正确：可见范围改变了输入样本，固定时间与分档后才能判断。","形状相似不能判断样本范围是否一致。"],"skills":["样本范围","复现"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040-volume-profile-indicators-basic-concepts/"}],"stemEn":"Comparing two screenshots of a “visible range” volume profile, the POC moved from 100 to 106; no new data arrived and only the zoom changed. How can you verify the change came from the range rather than new trading?","optionsEn":["Raise the number of bins to the maximum and ignore the change in horizontal range","Replace the POC with the last price to remove the effect of the historical range","Fix the start and end times and the bins, then recompute the POC for that same range","Compare whether the overall shape of the volume bars looks similar in both screenshots"],"explanationEn":"Changing the visible range changes the input sample; only with fixed times and bins can you judge results on the same data.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The effect of the range change remains.","Wrong: The last price is not the POC and cannot explain why the POC changed.","Correct: The visible range changes the sample, so fix the times and bins before judging.","Wrong: A similar shape does not show whether the sample range was the same."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-02","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[107],"stem":"某平台将OI显示为币数量，并按“美元OI=币数量×币价”折算。题设如下：OI币数量=10000币，美元名义OI=币数量×币价。期初币价100美元，期末币价110美元且币数量仍10000。随后币价维持110，OI币数量再升到10500。总美元OI增加多少，其中第二步数量变化贡献多少？","options":["总增15.5万美元，第二步贡献5.5万美元","总增15万美元，其中第二步贡献5万美元","总增10万美元，其中第二步没有贡献","总增5.5万美元，其中第二步贡献5.5万美元"],"answer":0,"explanation":"10000×100=100万；10000×110=110万；10500×110=115.5万。总增15.5万，第二步增5.5万。","optionExplanations":["正确：100万→110万→115.5万，总增15.5万，第二步5.5万。","第二步用了旧价100，应按110计算。","漏算了第二步数量变化的贡献。","漏算了第一步价格变化的10万。"],"skills":["价格折算","数量变化"],"references":[{"title":"CME Group: Open Interest","url":"https://www.cmegroup.com/education/lessons/open-interest"}],"stemEn":"A platform shows open interest in coins and converts it as “USD OI = coins × price”. OI is 10,000 coins and the price starts at $100, ending at $110 with OI still 10,000 coins. The price then stays at $110 while OI rises to 10,500 coins. How much did USD OI rise in total, and how much came from the second step’s change in quantity?","optionsEn":["Up $155,000 in total; the second step contributes $55,000","Up $150,000 in total; the second step contributes $50,000","Up $100,000 in total; the second step contributes nothing","Up $55,000 in total; the second step contributes $55,000"],"explanationEn":"10,000 × 100 = $1.0m; 10,000 × 110 = $1.1m; 10,500 × 110 = $1.155m. The total rise is $155,000, of which $55,000 is the second step.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: $1.0m → $1.1m → $1.155m, a total rise of $155,000 with $55,000 in the second step.","Wrong: The second step uses the old price of 100; it should use 110.","Wrong: This leaves out the second step’s change in quantity.","Wrong: This leaves out the first step’s $100,000 price effect."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-03","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[108],"stem":"A所报价资金费率0.01%/8小时，B所0.004%/小时。你想比较当前报价对应的日费用负担，假设这些报价保持不变、简单相加且不复利。哪项正确？","options":["A为0.24%/日，B为0.012%/日","A为0.03%/日，B为0.096%/日","两者均为0.014%/日，因为应先相加","A较高，因为0.01大于0.004"],"answer":1,"explanation":"A=0.01%×3，B=0.004%×24；题设为静态简单比较，非预测实际全天费率。","optionExplanations":["结算频次用反了，A每天3次，B每天24次。","A=0.01%×3，B=0.004%×24；题设为静态简单比较，非预测实际全天费率。","不同场所的费率不应该相加来表示各自成本。","单次报价没统一时间，不能直接比较数字大小。"],"skills":["时间标准化","费率"],"references":[{"title":"BitMEX: 2016 perpetual launch","url":"https://www.bitmex.com/blog/site-announcement/2432"}],"stemEn":"Exchange A quotes funding of 0.01% per 8 hours and exchange B 0.004% per hour. To compare the daily cost of the current quotes, assuming they stay unchanged and add up simply without compounding, which is correct?","optionsEn":["A is 0.24% per day, B is 0.012% per day","A is 0.03% per day, B is 0.096% per day","Both are 0.014% per day, because they should be added first","A is higher, because 0.01 is greater than 0.004"],"explanationEn":"A = 0.01% × 3 and B = 0.004% × 24; this is a static simple comparison, not a forecast of the actual daily rate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The settlement frequencies are reversed: A settles 3 times a day and B 24 times.","Correct: A = 0.01% × 3 and B = 0.004% × 24; a static comparison, not a forecast.","Wrong: Rates from different venues should not be added to represent each one’s cost.","Wrong: The quotes use different intervals, so the raw numbers cannot be compared directly."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-04","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[109],"stem":"本题三类账户互斥，净多账户600个、净空300个、无方向100个。发布规则的多空账户比=净多数/净空数；“有方向账户中净多占比”排除无方向者。哪组数正确？","options":["比值2.0；有方向账户中净多占比为60%","比值1.5；有方向账户中净多占比为60%","比值0.5；有方向账户中净多占比约33.3%","比值2.0；有方向账户净多占比约66.7%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"比值600/300=2；有方向账户900个，600/900≈66.7%。两者依旧只描述账户数。","optionExplanations":["分母误用了全部账户1000，没排除无方向者。","比值1.5没有依据，60%也把无方向账户算进了分母。","把净空当成了分子，方向弄反。","正确：600/300=2，600/900≈66.7%。"],"skills":["样本分母","账户比"],"references":[{"title":"Binance derivatives API: Global long/short account ratio","url":"https://developers.binance.com/docs/derivatives/usds-margined-futures/market-data/rest-api/Long-Short-Ratio"}],"stemEn":"Three account types are mutually exclusive: 600 net-long, 300 net-short and 100 with no direction. The published long/short ratio = net longs ÷ net shorts; “the net-long share of directional accounts” excludes accounts with no direction. Which pair of numbers is correct?","optionsEn":["Ratio 2.0; net longs are 60% of directional accounts","Ratio 1.5; net longs are 60% of directional accounts","Ratio 0.5; net longs are about 33.3% of directional accounts","Ratio 2.0; net longs are about 66.7% of directional accounts"],"explanationEn":"The ratio is 600/300 = 2; there are 900 directional accounts, so 600/900 ≈ 66.7%. Both still describe account counts only.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The denominator wrongly uses all 1,000 accounts instead of excluding those with no direction.","Wrong: A ratio of 1.5 has no basis, and 60% also counts accounts with no direction.","Wrong: This puts net shorts in the numerator, reversing the direction.","Correct: 600/300 = 2 and 600/900 ≈ 66.7%."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-05","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[110],"stem":"公开强平流每个1秒窗口最多给出该窗口最新一笔。观察到两个非空窗口分别报告10万和5万美元；不知道窗口内其他事件。仅根据这条流，“两个窗口实际总强平金额”能得到什么界限？","options":["至少15万美元，现有数据无法给出有限上界","约等于15万美元，因为两个窗口都已有记录","介于10万到15万美元，因为每秒取最新一笔","至多15万美元，因为推送已过滤掉重复事件"],"answer":0,"explanation":"已看到的15万必须包含在实际总额中；其余事件量未知，所以只有下界，没有可由本数据确定的有限上界。","optionExplanations":["正确：已看到的15万必须包含在内，其余未知，只有下界。","每窗口只给最新一笔，其余事件可能没有显示。","这里不存在这样的上下界。","过滤并不意味着总额不超过已见数。"],"skills":["抽样下界","数据覆盖"],"references":[{"title":"Binance: Liquidation order streams","url":"https://developers.binance.com/docs/derivatives/usds-margined-futures/websocket-market-streams/Liquidation-Order-Streams"}],"stemEn":"A public liquidation feed reports at most the latest event in each one-second window. Two non-empty windows report $100,000 and $50,000; other events in those windows are unknown. From this feed alone, what bounds can be put on the true total liquidated in the two windows?","optionsEn":["At least $150,000; the data gives no finite upper bound","About $150,000, because both windows have records","Between $100,000 and $150,000, because each second shows the latest event","At most $150,000, because the feed filters out duplicates"],"explanationEn":"The $150,000 seen must be part of the true total; the rest is unknown, so there is a lower bound but no finite upper bound from this data.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The $150,000 seen must be included and the rest is unknown, so there is only a lower bound.","Wrong: Each window shows only the latest event; others may not appear.","Wrong: No such bounds exist here.","Wrong: Filtering does not mean the total cannot exceed what was seen."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-06","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[103],"stem":"某“足迹”脚本按低周期涨跌估算：一个低周期柱若收盘高于开盘，则全部量计主动买；若低于则计主动卖。本分钟只有两个子柱：上涨柱量800、下跌柱量200。真实逐笔主动买450、主动卖550。估算与真实Delta各是多少？","options":["估算+600；真实-100","估算+100；真实-600","估算+600；真实+100","估算-100；真实+600"],"answer":0,"explanation":"估算800-200=+600，真实450-550=-100；同一分钟可出现相反符号，估算不可当逐笔分类。","optionExplanations":["估算800-200=+600，真实450-550=-100；同一分钟可出现相反符号，估算不可当逐笔分类。","估算与真实数值混淆且符号不合定义。","真实450-550为-100，不是+100。","把真实与估算互换，同时没有使用题设买减卖符号。"],"skills":["估算误差","Delta计算"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume footprint complete guide","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000726164-volume-footprint-charts-a-complete-guide/"}],"stemEn":"A “footprint” script estimates aggression from lower-timeframe bars: if a sub-bar closes above its open, all its volume counts as aggressive buying; below, as aggressive selling. This minute has two sub-bars: an up bar with 800 volume and a down bar with 200. True tick data shows 450 aggressive buys and 550 aggressive sells. What are the estimated and true deltas?","optionsEn":["Estimated +600; true −100","Estimated +100; true −600","Estimated +600; true +100","Estimated −100; true +600"],"explanationEn":"Estimated 800 − 200 = +600, true 450 − 550 = −100; the same minute can show opposite signs, so the estimate cannot stand in for tick classification.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Estimated 800 − 200 = +600 and true 450 − 550 = −100; the signs can differ, so the estimate is not tick classification.","Wrong: This mixes up the estimated and true values and the signs do not fit the definition.","Wrong: True delta is 450 − 550 = −100, not +100.","Wrong: This swaps true and estimated and does not use buys minus sells."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-07","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[100,99],"stem":"以下仅做简化权重练习，不是通用平台价值区算法。本题把价值区定义为“按各档权重由大到小累计，至少覆盖总权重70%的最少档集合”，不要求相邻。三个价格档100/101/102的TPO次数为6/3/1，成交量为100/200/700。两种价值区各包含哪些档？","options":["TPO仅100；成交量100与101","TPO100与101；成交量100与102","TPO100与101；成交量仅102","TPO仅100；成交量仅102"],"answer":2,"explanation":"TPO先取100占60%，再取101累计90%；成交量102占70%，单档已足。题设是简化算法，不代表所有平台实现。","optionExplanations":["TPO的100档只占60%，不足70%；成交量100与101只占30%。","TPO组合对，但成交量102单档已恰好70%，无须额外加入100。","TPO先取100占60%，再取101累计90%；成交量102占70%，单档已足。题设是简化算法，不代表所有平台实现。","成交量单档对，但TPO的60%未达70%条件。"],"skills":["加权集合","时间与成交量"],"references":[{"title":"Wiley: Steidlmayer on Markets","url":"https://www.wiley.com/en-us/-p-9780471215561"},{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040-volume-profile-indicators-basic-concepts/"}],"stemEn":"This is a simplified weighting exercise, not any platform’s value-area algorithm. Define the value area as the smallest set of price levels, taken from largest weight down, that covers at least 70% of the total weight; levels need not be adjacent. Levels 100/101/102 have TPO counts of 6/3/1 and volumes of 100/200/700. Which levels are in each value area?","optionsEn":["TPO: 100 only; volume: 100 and 101","TPO: 100 and 101; volume: 100 and 102","TPO: 100 and 101; volume: 102 only","TPO: 100 only; volume: 102 only"],"explanationEn":"For TPO, 100 gives 60%, then 101 brings it to 90%; for volume, 102 alone is 70%. This is a simplified method, not every platform’s implementation.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The 100 level is only 60% of TPOs, short of 70%; volume at 100 and 101 is only 30%.","Wrong: The TPO set is right, but 102 alone already reaches exactly 70% of volume, so 100 is not needed.","Correct: TPO takes 100 (60%) then 101 (90%); volume at 102 alone is 70%. This is a simplified method.","Wrong: The volume level is right, but 60% of TPOs does not reach 70%."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-08","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[96],"stem":"你回看历史，试了十多组不同高低点，最终选出三次准确触及61.8%反弹的案例。若要检验这个方法，哪项设计最有说服力？","options":["把61.8%放宽成价格区域，使三个案例都能被覆盖","改用更小周期，把三次精确触及的截图并排展示","事先定好锚点、触发和失效规则，再用新样本检验","只保留离回撤线最近的成交价，以便减少滑点影响"],"answer":2,"explanation":"预先规定并保留失败样本，才可以估计真实表现，容差也须事先确定。","optionExplanations":["事后放宽容差是为了迎合结果。","展示精度并不检验方法，还是挑选了成功案例。","正确：预先规定并保留失败样本才能估计真实表现。","这是事后过滤，会美化结果。"],"skills":["选择偏差","预注册规则"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"Looking back at history, you tried more than ten different high/low anchors and picked three cases where price bounced exactly at 61.8%. Which test design would be most convincing?","optionsEn":["Widen 61.8% into a price zone so all three cases are covered","Switch to a smaller timeframe and show the three exact touches side by side","Fix the anchor, trigger and invalidation rules in advance, then test on new samples","Keep only the fill price closest to the retracement line to reduce slippage effects"],"explanationEn":"Only rules fixed in advance, keeping failed cases, can estimate real performance; any tolerance must also be set beforehand.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Widening the tolerance afterwards just fits the result.","Wrong: Showing precision does not test the method and still cherry-picks successes.","Correct: Rules fixed in advance and keeping failures are needed to estimate real performance.","Wrong: This is after-the-fact filtering that flatters the results."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-09","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[108,107],"stem":"你做“现货多头+等名义永续空头”收正资金费。哪一项最能解释为什么对冲价格方向后仍需风险控制？","options":["两腿名义金额一致，剩下的风险只有资金费波动","仍有基差、保证金强平、执行成本与场所风险","收到资金费后，现货价格的波动就不再重要了","按当前费率年化，就能确定这笔交易的保本收益"],"answer":1,"explanation":"对冲可减少部分价格方向敞口，但两腿的产品、保证金和可成交条件并不相同。","optionExplanations":["基差、强平等风险依然存在。","正确：对冲减少方向敞口，但两腿的产品、保证金和成交条件不同。","价格波动仍影响保证金与基差。","资金费率会变，不能由当前值直接推算。"],"skills":["对冲残余风险","路径"],"references":[{"title":"BitMEX: 2016 perpetual launch","url":"https://www.bitmex.com/blog/site-announcement/2432"},{"title":"CME Group: Open Interest","url":"https://www.cmegroup.com/education/lessons/open-interest"}],"stemEn":"You hold “spot long plus an equal-notional perpetual short” to collect positive funding. Which best explains why risk control is still needed after hedging price direction?","optionsEn":["The two legs have equal notional, so the only remaining risk is funding volatility","Basis, margin liquidation, execution costs and venue risk remain","Once funding is received, spot price moves no longer matter","Annualising the current rate fixes the trade’s break-even return"],"explanationEn":"Hedging reduces some directional exposure, but the two legs differ in product, margin and fill conditions.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Basis, liquidation and other risks still exist.","Correct: The hedge cuts directional exposure, but the legs differ in product, margin and execution.","Wrong: Price moves still affect margin and basis.","Wrong: Funding rates change, so the current rate cannot be extrapolated."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-10","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[99],"stem":"同一交易区间，价格分档从0.1元改为1元，最高成交档的位置发生小幅变化。你要比较两个时期的POC迁移，应先怎样处理？","options":["只采用分档更细的一期，因为它的POC更真实","两期采用一致的分档规则，并记录范围与粒度","每一期都选取最贴近收盘价的分档，来对齐位置","把两期POC的差值除以10，抵消分档宽度变化"],"answer":1,"explanation":"POC是分箱统计结果；保持分档、区间与数据口径一致才能更公平比较。","optionExplanations":["细分档不一定更真实，且无法比较两期。","正确：POC是分箱结果，保持分档、区间一致才可比。","按收盘价选档会改变POC的定义。","简单除以常数不能消除分档影响。"],"skills":["分箱敏感","可比性"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040-volume-profile-indicators-basic-concepts/"}],"stemEn":"For the same trading range, the price bin size changes from 0.1 to 1, and the highest-volume bin shifts slightly. To compare POC migration between two periods, what should be done first?","optionsEn":["Use only the period with finer bins, since its POC is more accurate","Use the same binning rules for both periods and record range and granularity","In each period choose the bin closest to the close to line up the positions","Divide the difference between the two POCs by 10 to offset the bin-size change"],"explanationEn":"The POC is a binned statistic; keeping bins, range and data definitions consistent makes the comparison fairer.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Finer bins are not necessarily more accurate, and the periods still cannot be compared.","Correct: The POC is a binned result, so consistent bins and ranges are needed.","Wrong: Choosing bins by the close changes the POC’s definition.","Wrong: Dividing by a constant does not remove the binning effect."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-11","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[110,107],"stem":"假设同一合约、固定计价，OI按一张只计一次。起始1000张；事件甲：双方新开100张；乙：双方平仓150张；丙：旧多头平仓50张由新多头接手，空方持仓不变。三事件全为窗口成交。期末OI与窗口成交量是什么？","options":["OI900张；成交量300张","OI1050张；成交量300张","OI950张；成交量300张","OI950张；成交量250张"],"answer":2,"explanation":"新开加100，双平减150，转手不变；成交100+150+50=300。","optionExplanations":["把转手当成了减仓50张。","漏算了双方平仓150张。","正确：OI=1000+100-150=950；成交100+150+50=300。","漏算了转手的50张成交。"],"skills":["开平与转手","存量流量"],"references":[{"title":"Binance: Liquidation order streams","url":"https://developers.binance.com/docs/derivatives/usds-margined-futures/websocket-market-streams/Liquidation-Order-Streams"},{"title":"CME Group: Open Interest","url":"https://www.cmegroup.com/education/lessons/open-interest"}],"stemEn":"Same contract, fixed pricing, open interest counted once per contract. Start: 1,000 contracts. Event A: both sides open 100 new. Event B: both sides close 150. Event C: an old long closes 50 and a new long takes them over, with shorts unchanged. All three trade in the window. What are the ending OI and the window’s volume?","optionsEn":["OI 900; volume 300","OI 1,050; volume 300","OI 950; volume 300","OI 950; volume 250"],"explanationEn":"New opens add 100, mutual closes remove 150, a hand-over leaves OI unchanged; volume is 100 + 150 + 50 = 300.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This treats the hand-over as reducing OI by 50.","Wrong: This leaves out the 150 contracts closed by both sides.","Correct: OI = 1,000 + 100 − 150 = 950; volume = 100 + 150 + 50 = 300.","Wrong: This leaves out the 50 contracts traded in the hand-over."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-12","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[103,99],"stem":"现货订单簿在100元有很厚的卖单，足迹图显示100元已经成交很多主动买单，但价格暂未站上100。若想研究“承接/吸收”，哪项做法更有依据？","options":["同时跟踪成交、挂单补撤与价格，检验假说","以订单簿卖单厚度为主要依据，预测后续成交量","以主动买差值为主要信号，把价格停滞视为噪声","用卖单厚度与成交量之比，识别卖方机构身份"],"answer":0,"explanation":"连续跟踪三类信息比单点判断更有依据；仍需保留不同参与者和流动性变化等解释。","optionExplanations":["正确：连续跟踪三类信息比单点判断更有依据。","单一的挂单厚度不足以预测成交。","价格停滞正是需要解释的现象。","这类比值无法识别机构身份。"],"skills":["挂单与成交","行为推断"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume footprint complete guide","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000726164-volume-footprint-charts-a-complete-guide/"},{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040-volume-profile-indicators-basic-concepts/"}],"stemEn":"The spot order book shows heavy sell orders at 100, and the footprint shows a lot of aggressive buying already executed at 100, yet price has not held above 100. If you want to study “absorption”, which approach is best grounded?","optionsEn":["Track trades, order additions and cancellations, and price together to test the hypothesis","Rely mainly on the size of resting sell orders to forecast later volume","Rely mainly on the aggressive buy difference and treat the price stall as noise","Use the ratio of resting sell size to volume to identify the seller as an institution"],"explanationEn":"Tracking all three continuously is better grounded than a single snapshot; other explanations, such as different participants or shifting liquidity, must stay open.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Tracking all three continuously is better grounded than a single snapshot.","Wrong: Resting size alone is not enough to forecast trades.","Wrong: The price stall is exactly what needs explaining.","Wrong: No such ratio can identify an institution."]},{"id":"method-beginner-01","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[111],"stem":"某资产多次在99至101间止跌。你把它记为支撑区，下一次价格到100。最合理的学习性判断是什么？","options":["以往止跌次数越多，这次的反弹幅度也应越大","价格一触及100就算止跌确认，不必再看收盘","99至101之间每个价位上的买单数量大致一样","100是以往买卖反应区，这次需观察能否守住"],"answer":3,"explanation":"历史反应使这一区域值得观察，但本次仍须看承接与失守，支撑是可失效的假设。","optionExplanations":["次数多不能推出幅度更大。","触及不等于确认。","没有依据假设买单均匀分布。","正确：历史反应使该区域值得观察，但支撑是可失效的假设。"],"skills":["区域与点","确认"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"An asset has repeatedly stopped falling between 99 and 101. You mark it as a support zone, and price comes back to 100. What is the most reasonable learning judgement?","optionsEn":["The more times it held before, the bigger this bounce should be","Touching 100 confirms support; there is no need to watch the close","Buy orders are spread roughly evenly at every price from 99 to 101","100 is an area where buyers and sellers reacted before; watch whether it holds this time"],"explanationEn":"Past reactions make the area worth watching, but this time you still need to see whether it holds or breaks; support is a hypothesis that can fail.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: More past holds does not imply a bigger bounce.","Wrong: Touching is not confirmation.","Wrong: There is no basis for assuming evenly spread buy orders.","Correct: Past reactions make the area worth watching, but support is a hypothesis that can fail."]},{"id":"method-beginner-02","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[112],"stem":"你用两个已确认的更高低点画出上升趋势线，之后一根K线收在其下方。仅凭这一点，最贴切的描述是什么？","options":["已形成更低高点和更低低点，下降结构成立","原上升节奏受挑战，结构反转仍要看高低点","把趋势线平移到最新低点即可维持原来的判断","跌破趋势线与跌破最近确认低点含义相同"],"answer":1,"explanation":"趋势线破坏先表原节奏受挑战，不等于结构转向已完整确认。","optionExplanations":["一根收盘不足以形成高低点结构。","正确：趋势线被破先表示节奏受挑战，不等于结构转向。","随意平移线是迎合价格。","两者含义不同，后者才是结构破坏。"],"skills":["节奏与结构","失效"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"You draw a rising trend line through two confirmed higher lows; then a bar closes below it. From this alone, what is the most accurate description?","optionsEn":["Lower highs and lower lows have formed, so a down structure is in place","The upward rhythm is being challenged; a structural reversal still depends on highs and lows","Shifting the trend line to the latest low keeps the original view intact","Breaking the trend line means the same as breaking the latest confirmed low"],"explanationEn":"A broken trend line first shows the rhythm is being challenged; it is not a complete confirmation that the structure has turned.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: One close is not enough to form a high–low structure.","Correct: A broken trend line shows the rhythm is challenged, not that the structure has turned.","Wrong: Shifting the line at will just fits it to price.","Wrong: They mean different things; only the latter breaks the structure."]},{"id":"method-beginner-03","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[113],"stem":"两根K线实体大小相同、下影线都很长；一根出现在连续下跌后的支撑区，另一根出现在无明显边界的区间中部。分析时最应比较什么？","options":["两根实体和影线形态一致，因此信号强度可视为等同","应以成交价更低的一根为准，因为它的反转更可靠","位置只用来确定止损，信号含义由K线外形决定","位置与前期走势不同，不能只凭外形给同一信号"],"answer":3,"explanation":"同样形状在不同背景下意义可能不同，应把形态放回价格环境。","optionExplanations":["忽略了位置与背景。","价格高低与可靠性无关。","位置同样影响信号含义。","正确：同样形状在不同背景下意义可能不同。"],"skills":["形态背景","位置"],"references":[{"title":"Steve Nison — CandleCharts","url":"https://candlecharts.com/"}],"stemEn":"Two bars have the same body size and long lower shadows. One appears at support after a run of declines; the other in the middle of a range with no clear boundary. What should the analysis compare most?","optionsEn":["Their bodies and shadows match, so their signal strength can be treated as equal","Use the bar with the lower price, because its reversal is more reliable","Location only sets the stop; the signal’s meaning comes from the bar’s shape","Their location and prior moves differ, so the same shape does not give the same signal"],"explanationEn":"The same shape can mean different things in different contexts; put the pattern back into its price setting.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This ignores location and context.","Wrong: Price level has nothing to do with reliability.","Wrong: Location also affects what the signal means.","Correct: The same shape can mean different things in different contexts."]},{"id":"method-beginner-04","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[114],"stem":"某双顶候选在110附近两次遇阻，颈线100。规则事先规定“日收盘跌破100才确认”。今天盘中最低99，收盘101。按该规则应记作什么？","options":["已经确认，因为盘中价格曾低于颈线100","已经失效，因为收盘价重新回到颈线之上","仍是候选，尚未满足事先规定的收盘确认","算作半个信号，等次日涨跌再决定如何补记"],"answer":2,"explanation":"收盘101仍高于100，不能把盘中穿越代替收盘确认。","optionExplanations":["规则要求收盘跌破，不是盘中。","未确认不等于失效，仍是候选。","正确：收盘101仍高于100，盘中穿越不能代替收盘确认。","规则里没有半个信号。"],"skills":["形态确认","规则执行"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"A double-top candidate has met resistance twice near 110 with a neckline at 100. The rule set in advance says it confirms only on a daily close below 100. Today the intraday low is 99 and the close 101. How should it be recorded under this rule?","optionsEn":["Confirmed, because price traded below the 100 neckline intraday","Invalidated, because the close returned above the neckline","Still a candidate; the pre-set closing confirmation has not been met","Half a signal; decide how to record it after tomorrow’s move"],"explanationEn":"The 101 close is still above 100; an intraday cross cannot replace the closing confirmation.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The rule requires a close below, not an intraday move.","Wrong: Not confirmed is not the same as invalidated; it is still a candidate.","Correct: The 101 close is above 100, and an intraday cross cannot replace closing confirmation.","Wrong: The rules have no such thing as half a signal."]},{"id":"method-beginner-05","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[115,120],"stem":"价格依次形成高点105、110，低点100、104；随后回落到106，尚未出现低于104的确认低点。按高低点结构，应怎样描述？","options":["高低点仍在逐步抬高，结构暂未被这次回落破坏","106低于110，已形成更低高点，结构转为下降","回落4元已等同趋势反转，无需再检查前低","回落已接近前低104，因此上升结构视为结束"],"answer":0,"explanation":"106仍高于最近确认低点104，仅凭回落不能认定结构已反转。","optionExplanations":["正确：106仍高于最近确认低点104，不能认定结构反转。","更低高点还需随后跌破前低才能成立。","结构判断必须看低点。","尚未跌破104，结构仍未破坏。"],"skills":["价格结构","确认点"],"references":[{"title":"Brooks Trading Course","url":"https://www.brookstradingcourse.com/"},{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"Price forms highs of 105 and 110 and lows of 100 and 104, then pulls back to 106 without a confirmed low below 104. In terms of swing structure, how should it be described?","optionsEn":["Highs and lows are still rising; this pullback has not broken the structure","106 is below 110, so a lower high has formed and the structure has turned down","A 4-point pullback equals a trend reversal, so the prior low need not be checked","The pullback is near the prior low of 104, so the up structure is over"],"explanationEn":"106 is still above the latest confirmed low of 104; a pullback alone cannot establish a structural reversal.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 106 is still above the confirmed low of 104, so the structure has not reversed.","Wrong: A lower high needs a subsequent break of the prior low to stand.","Wrong: Structure must be judged with the lows.","Wrong: 104 has not been broken, so the structure is intact."]},{"id":"method-beginner-06","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[116],"stem":"在以两种相关市场平均指数相互确认为观察原则的道氏分析中，工业指数创新高，运输指数尚未创新高。最严谨的说法是什么？","options":["运输未创新高，说明工业指数新高是假突破","两指数出现背离，所以应暂时忽略二者走势","工业指数一个创新高，就已满足共同确认条件","尚未获得共同确认，但也不等于已确认反转"],"answer":3,"explanation":"共同确认条件尚未满足，仍需区分未确认与已反转。","optionExplanations":["未确认不等于假突破。","背离是需要关注的信息。","共同确认需要两个指数同步。","正确：共同确认条件尚未满足，需区分未确认与已反转。"],"skills":["共同确认","逻辑状态"],"references":[{"title":"CMT Association: Dow Theory history","url":"https://cmtassociation.org/technically_speaking/technically-speaking-october-2011/"}],"stemEn":"In Dow analysis, where two related market averages are meant to confirm each other, the Industrials make a new high but the Transports have not. What is the most rigorous statement?","optionsEn":["The Transports not making a new high shows the Industrials’ high is a false breakout","The two averages diverge, so both should be ignored for now","One new high in the Industrials already meets the joint-confirmation condition","Joint confirmation is still missing, but that is not the same as a confirmed reversal"],"explanationEn":"The joint-confirmation condition is not yet met; unconfirmed must still be kept separate from reversed.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Unconfirmed is not the same as a false breakout.","Wrong: Divergence is information worth watching.","Wrong: Joint confirmation needs both averages to agree.","Correct: Joint confirmation is missing, and unconfirmed must be kept separate from reversed."]},{"id":"method-beginner-07","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[117],"stem":"学习波浪时，你画出一个上涨五浪候选；随后价格跌破你事先标明的失效价。最合理的研究记录是什么？","options":["记录计数失效，按事先规则重新评估其他结构","保留原计数不变，等待反弹后再看是否重新成立","把失效价上移一些，让原计数继续贯穿整段行情","删去这一段，让历史案例只留下清晰的五浪"],"answer":0,"explanation":"计数是有条件假设，应承认失效并保留记录，避免事后解释一切。","optionExplanations":["正确：计数是有条件假设，失效后应承认并保留记录。","失效价已被跌破，不应继续保留原判断。","事后移动失效价是自我保护。","删除失败案例会产生幸存者偏差。"],"skills":["假设失效","计数"],"references":[{"title":"Elliott Wave International: Introduction to the Wave Principle","url":"https://www.elliottwave.com/free/introduction-to-the-wave-principle/"}],"stemEn":"While studying waves, you mark a candidate five-wave rally; price then falls through the invalidation level you set in advance. What is the most reasonable research record?","optionsEn":["Record that the count failed and reassess other structures by the pre-set rules","Keep the original count and wait for a bounce to see whether it holds again","Move the invalidation level a little higher so the original count still covers the move","Delete this stretch so the history only shows clean five-wave examples"],"explanationEn":"A count is a conditional hypothesis; admit the failure and keep the record, rather than explaining everything afterwards.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A count is a conditional hypothesis, so admit the failure and keep the record.","Wrong: The invalidation level has been broken, so the original view should not be kept.","Wrong: Moving the invalidation level afterwards is self-protection.","Wrong: Deleting failures creates survivorship bias."]},{"id":"method-beginner-08","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[118],"stem":"价格短暂跌破区间下沿后收回。用威科夫语言可以先把它视为“spring候选”。要让判断更有依据，接下来最值得观察什么？","options":["只看跌破的最低价，越低就越像吸筹完成","回测时供给是否减弱，能否守住并转强","把下影线长度当作机构买入金额的粗略估计","价格一收回区间就算确认，不必再观察回测"],"answer":1,"explanation":"回测与供需、后续上行表现共同支持或推翻spring假设。","optionExplanations":["最低价深度不是确认条件。","正确：回测、供需与后续上行表现共同支持或推翻spring。","下影线不能换算买入金额。","收回只是候选，仍需观察回测。"],"skills":["威科夫背景","后续验证"],"references":[{"title":"Wyckoff Analytics: Method and history","url":"https://www.wyckoffanalytics.com/wyckoff-method/"}],"stemEn":"Price briefly breaks below the bottom of a range and then closes back inside. In Wyckoff terms you can first call it a “spring candidate”. What is most worth watching next to firm up the judgement?","optionsEn":["Only the low of the break: the lower it went, the more it looks like completed accumulation","Whether supply weakens on the retest, and whether price holds and strengthens","Use the length of the lower shadow as a rough estimate of institutional buying","Count it as confirmed once price closes back inside; no need to watch the retest"],"explanationEn":"The retest, supply and demand, and the subsequent rise together support or refute the spring hypothesis.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The depth of the low is not a confirmation condition.","Correct: The retest, supply and demand, and what follows together support or refute the spring.","Wrong: A lower shadow cannot be converted into a buying amount.","Wrong: Closing back inside only makes it a candidate; the retest still matters."]},{"id":"method-beginner-09","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[119],"stem":"在谐波形态练习中，规定某候选B点须回撤XA的61.8%，容差±2个百分点。你测得回撤50%。哪项处理符合规则？","options":["50%接近黄金分割的一半，可按61.8%处理","后面出现了反弹，就可以把B点回填为合格","50%落在容差区间外，不能因图形相似而接受","把容差事后放宽到12个百分点，再判为合格"],"answer":2,"explanation":"50%不在59.8%至63.8%区间，形似不能代替事先比例条件。","optionExplanations":["规则的容差只有±2个百分点。","不能用事后走势回填条件。","正确：50%不在59.8%至63.8%内，不符合事先条件。","事后改容差违背事先规定。"],"skills":["比例条件","容差"],"references":[{"title":"Harmonic Trader: Gartley history and ratios","url":"https://harmonictrader.com/harmonic-patterns/gartley-pattern/"}],"stemEn":"In a harmonic-pattern exercise, a candidate point B must retrace 61.8% of XA, with a tolerance of ±2 percentage points. You measure a 50% retracement. Which handling follows the rules?","optionsEn":["50% is close to half the golden ratio, so treat it as 61.8%","A later bounce allows B to be back-filled as valid","50% falls outside the tolerance, so it cannot be accepted just because the shape looks similar","Widen the tolerance afterwards to 12 points and then accept it"],"explanationEn":"50% is outside 59.8%–63.8%; looking similar cannot replace a ratio condition set in advance.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The rule’s tolerance is only ±2 points.","Wrong: Conditions cannot be back-filled from later price moves.","Correct: 50% is outside 59.8%–63.8%, so it fails the pre-set condition.","Wrong: Changing the tolerance afterwards breaks the pre-set rule."]},{"id":"method-beginner-10","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[123,124],"stem":"某SMC/ICT课程把一段三K线结构中“第一根最高价低于第三根最低价”的区域称为看涨FVG。价格首次回到该区域。仅据这个定义应怎么理解？","options":["首次回访即为已确认的反转，可直接作为触发","该区域代表三根K线间真实存在的成交空白","该区域可直接用来估算尚未成交的买单量","按图形定义划出的观察区，需检验反应"],"answer":3,"explanation":"结构标签提供观察位置，是否有效仍需用本次反应检验。","optionExplanations":["回访只是观察点，不是确认。","它是按K线高低点定义的区域，不是实际成交空白。","价格区域无法给出挂单数量。","正确：FVG是结构标签，有效性要用本次反应检验。"],"skills":["概念与证据","区域"],"references":[{"title":"Michael J. Huddleston: ICT official teaching source","url":"https://www.theinnercircletrader.com/"},{"title":"ICT official home: Michael J. Huddleston","url":"https://www.theinnercircletrader.com/"}],"stemEn":"An SMC/ICT course calls the zone in a three-bar structure where “bar 1’s high is below bar 3’s low” a bullish FVG. Price returns to that zone for the first time. Under this definition alone, how should it be understood?","optionsEn":["The first revisit is a confirmed reversal and can be used as a trigger","The zone represents a genuine gap in trading between the three bars","The zone can be used to estimate the size of unfilled buy orders","It is an observation zone drawn by a chart definition, and the reaction needs testing"],"explanationEn":"A structural label gives a place to watch; whether it works still has to be tested by this reaction.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A revisit is a point to watch, not confirmation.","Wrong: It is a zone defined by bar highs and lows, not an actual gap in trading.","Wrong: A price zone cannot reveal order sizes.","Correct: An FVG is a structural label, and its validity must be tested by the reaction."]},{"id":"method-beginner-11","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[125],"stem":"在同一交易所，同一分钟主动买成交持续增加，但价格在阻力附近推进很小。订单流分析里，最合适的初步假设是哪项？","options":["主动买增多说明卖方已离场，价格将很快突破","被动卖出承接可能较强，需看后续成交","价格没动是因为图表延迟，阻力其实已经突破","主动买多于主动卖，因此这根K线应记作上涨"],"answer":1,"explanation":"主动买却难推进与被动卖出承接相容，但还需后续数据，不能直接确认身份。","optionExplanations":["无法由此断定卖方离场。","正确：主动买难推进与被动卖出承接相容，但还需后续数据。","没有依据假设图表延迟。","K线涨跌由价格决定，不能改记。"],"skills":["主动与被动","价格反应"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume footprint guide and calculation","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000726164-volume-footprint-charts-a-complete-guide/"}],"stemEn":"On one exchange, aggressive buying keeps rising within the same minute, but price barely moves near resistance. In order-flow analysis, what is the most suitable initial hypothesis?","optionsEn":["More aggressive buying means sellers have left, so price will break out soon","Passive selling may be absorbing strongly; watch what trades next","Price has not moved because the chart is delayed; resistance has really broken","Aggressive buys exceed aggressive sells, so the bar should be recorded as up"],"explanationEn":"Aggressive buying that struggles to move price is consistent with passive sellers absorbing it, but more data is needed; it cannot confirm who is behind it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This cannot show that sellers have left.","Correct: Buying that struggles to move price fits passive absorption, but more data is needed.","Wrong: There is no basis for assuming a chart delay.","Wrong: A bar’s direction is set by price and cannot be relabelled."]},{"id":"method-beginner-12","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[126,127],"stem":"价格从一处此前横盘的区域快速上涨。你将原区域标为潜在需求区。下次回到这里时，哪项最符合供需区与拍卖观察的用途？","options":["过去的上涨说明这里仍留有同等规模买单","区域画得越早，下次触及时的反弹概率越高","看是否再现承接或跌穿，按预设条件验证","区域中心价可以视作该资产的基本面公允价"],"answer":2,"explanation":"区域是观察假设，可被本次成交和价格行为支持或推翻。","optionExplanations":["买单可能早已成交或撤销。","画的早晚与概率无关。","正确：区域是观察假设，可被本次价格行为支持或推翻。","供需区不等于基本面价值。"],"skills":["供需假设","接受与拒绝"],"references":[{"title":"Wiley: Steidlmayer on Markets","url":"https://www.wiley.com/en-us/-p-9780471215561"},{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"Price rallied quickly out of an area where it had moved sideways. You mark that area as a potential demand zone. When price returns, which use best fits supply-and-demand and auction analysis?","optionsEn":["The earlier rally shows the same size of buy orders still sits there","The earlier the zone was drawn, the higher the chance of a bounce on the next touch","See whether buyers step in again or price breaks through, testing it against pre-set conditions","The middle of the zone can be treated as the asset’s fundamental fair value"],"explanationEn":"The zone is a working hypothesis that this round of trading and price behaviour can support or refute.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The buy orders may have been filled or cancelled long ago.","Wrong: When the zone was drawn has nothing to do with the probability.","Correct: The zone is a hypothesis that this round of price behaviour can support or refute.","Wrong: A supply-demand zone is not fundamental value."]},{"id":"method-advanced-01","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[111,114],"stem":"你在回测支撑反弹：进入价100，失效价98，目标104，胜率45%；假设每笔都恰好在目标或失效价退出，交易成本折合每笔0.2价格单位。每单位仓位的期望收益是多少？","options":["0.9，因45%×2减55%×0","0.5，因0.45×4-0.55×2-0.2","0.7，因0.45×4-0.55×2，不必计入成本","1.8，因只统计盈利交易的平均贡献"],"answer":1,"explanation":"盈利贡献1.8，亏损贡献1.1，再扣每笔0.2，期望0.5。该结果依赖题设执行假定。","optionExplanations":["把盈利幅度误写为2并忽略了亏损贡献和成本。","盈利贡献1.8，亏损贡献1.1，再扣每笔0.2，期望0.5。该结果依赖题设执行假定。","0.7是成本前期望，题目明确给了每笔成本0.2。","1.8只算赢单贡献，没有减去输单损失和成本。"],"skills":["期望值","风险收益"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"You are backtesting support bounces: entry 100, invalidation 98, target 104, win rate 45%. Assume every trade exits exactly at the target or the invalidation level, with costs of 0.2 price units per trade. What is the expected return per unit?","optionsEn":["0.9, because 45% × 2 − 55% × 0","0.5, because 0.45 × 4 − 0.55 × 2 − 0.2","0.7, because 0.45 × 4 − 0.55 × 2, with no need to include costs","1.8, counting only the average contribution of winning trades"],"explanationEn":"Wins contribute 1.8, losses 1.1, and 0.2 per trade comes off, giving 0.5. The result depends on the stated execution assumptions.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This writes the gain as 2 and ignores the losses and costs.","Correct: Wins contribute 1.8, losses 1.1, minus 0.2 per trade gives 0.5, under the stated assumptions.","Wrong: 0.7 is the expectation before costs, but the question gives 0.2 per trade.","Wrong: 1.8 counts only the winners without subtracting losses and costs."]},{"id":"method-advanced-02","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[112,121],"stem":"江恩练习明确固定线性轴，以每天上升2美元定义本图的1×1线；第0天起点100美元。到第10天，该线价格是多少？若切换对数轴仍想保留同一“每天2美元”路径，应怎样做？","options":["120；按原价格与日期路径重画，不沿用视觉角度","120；直接保持屏幕上的45度角，不再核对价格","110；改按每天的百分比增长，重新计算该路径","130；把斜率调陡到每天3美元，以便维持45度角"],"answer":0,"explanation":"100+10×2=120；坐标变换会改变视觉形状，应保留定义的价格时间坐标。","optionExplanations":["正确：100+10×2=120；坐标变换会改变视觉形状，应保留价格时间路径。","视觉角度会随坐标变化，不等于定义的路径。","改成百分比会改变题设的每天2美元定义。","为保视觉角度而改斜率，偏离了定义。"],"skills":["价格时间单位","坐标尺度"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"},{"title":"TradingView: Gann fan drawing tool","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000518151-gann-fan-drawing-tool/"}],"stemEn":"A Gann exercise fixes a linear axis and defines this chart’s 1×1 line as rising $2 per day, starting at $100 on day 0. What is the line’s price on day 10? If you switch to a log axis but want to keep the same “$2 per day” path, what should you do?","optionsEn":["120; redraw by the original price–date path rather than keeping the visual angle","120; just keep the 45-degree angle on screen and stop checking prices","110; recompute the path as a daily percentage growth","130; steepen the slope to $3 per day to keep the 45-degree angle"],"explanationEn":"100 + 10 × 2 = 120; changing the axis changes the visual shape, so keep the defined price–time coordinates.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 100 + 10 × 2 = 120; a new axis changes the visual shape, so keep the price–time path.","Wrong: The visual angle changes with the axis and is not the defined path.","Wrong: Switching to percentages changes the stated $2-per-day definition.","Wrong: Changing the slope to keep the angle departs from the definition."]},{"id":"method-advanced-03","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[113,115],"stem":"你筛选500个长下影样本，发现支撑区内胜率58%，区间中部45%。但支撑区样本都来自牛市，中部样本多来自熊市。要检验位置是否有独立作用，先怎么做？","options":["把500个样本混合算总胜率，样本越多越公平","只保留支撑区样本，因为58%已经高于50%","把58%减45%的差值，直接当作位置的因果贡献","在相近市场状态和成本口径内分层比较，再验证"],"answer":3,"explanation":"市场状态是潜在混杂因素；分层或匹配后再验证，才更能分辨位置贡献。","optionExplanations":["混合会掩盖牛熊差异。","忽略了对照组，也忽略了牛市背景。","差值混合了市场状态的影响。","正确：市场状态是混杂因素，分层或匹配后才能分辨位置贡献。"],"skills":["混杂因素","样本分层"],"references":[{"title":"Steve Nison — CandleCharts","url":"https://candlecharts.com/"},{"title":"Brooks Trading Course","url":"https://www.brookstradingcourse.com/"}],"stemEn":"You screen 500 long-lower-shadow samples and find a 58% win rate at support versus 45% mid-range. But the support samples all come from bull markets and the mid-range ones mostly from bear markets. To test whether location has an independent effect, what should you do first?","optionsEn":["Pool all 500 samples into one win rate; more samples are fairer","Keep only the support samples, since 58% is already above 50%","Treat the 58% − 45% gap directly as location’s causal contribution","Compare within similar market regimes and cost assumptions, then validate"],"explanationEn":"Market regime is a likely confounder; only after stratifying or matching can location’s contribution be separated.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Pooling hides the bull–bear difference.","Wrong: This ignores the comparison group and the bull-market backdrop.","Wrong: The gap mixes in the effect of market regime.","Correct: Regime is a confounder, so stratify or match before judging location’s contribution."]},{"id":"method-advanced-04","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[116,120],"stem":"按结构规则：只有跌破“最近已确认周线低点”才判周线上升结构失效。该低点90，最近周线高点110。15分钟前低103被跌破，最新价101，尚未跌破90。哪组记录符合这套规则？","options":["周线已失效；15分钟前低先破，等于提前确认","周线未失效；小周期破位不属于需要记录的信息","周线未失效；15分钟局部破位可单独记录","周线待定；需等价格回到103上方才能判断"],"answer":2,"explanation":"101仍高于给定周线失效点90，周线条件未触发；小周期破位却已发生，应分层记录。","optionExplanations":["小周期破位不能代替周线条件。","小周期破位仍应分层记录。","正确：101高于周线失效点90，小周期破位应分层记录。","规则只看是否跌破90，与103无关。"],"skills":["多周期层级","条件判断"],"references":[{"title":"CMT Association: Dow Theory history","url":"https://cmtassociation.org/technically_speaking/technically-speaking-october-2011/"},{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"By the structure rule, the weekly uptrend fails only if price breaks the latest confirmed weekly low. That low is 90 and the latest weekly high 110. On 15 minutes, the prior low of 103 has broken and price is now 101, still above 90. Which record fits these rules?","optionsEn":["Weekly failed; the 15-minute break came first and counts as early confirmation","Weekly intact; lower-timeframe breaks are not worth recording","Weekly intact; record the local 15-minute break separately","Weekly undecided; wait for price to get back above 103"],"explanationEn":"101 is still above the weekly failure level of 90, so the weekly condition is not triggered; the lower-timeframe break has happened and should be recorded on its own layer.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A lower-timeframe break cannot replace the weekly condition.","Wrong: The lower-timeframe break should still be recorded on its own layer.","Correct: 101 is above the weekly failure level of 90, and the 15-minute break is recorded separately.","Wrong: The rule only asks whether 90 breaks; 103 is irrelevant."]},{"id":"method-advanced-05","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[117],"stem":"本题只讨论标准推动浪，不含对角线，采用“2浪不越1浪起点、3浪不是1/3/5中最短、4浪不进入1浪价格区间”三条规则。某计数1浪长10、3浪长8、5浪长12，其他两条均满足。应如何判定？","options":["不合格，3浪比1、5浪都短，违反规则","合格，3浪长度为正数就算符合给定规则","合格，5浪最长，可补偿3浪偏短这一违规","暂时无法判定，还需知道2浪耗费的时间"],"answer":0,"explanation":"8小于10和12，直接违反给定规则；其他条件满足不能补偿该违规。","optionExplanations":["正确：8小于10和12，违反给定规则，其他条件不能补偿。","规则要求3浪不是最短，而非大于零。","规则不允许用其他浪补偿。","规则只涉及价格长度，与时间无关。"],"skills":["波浪约束","反证"],"references":[{"title":"Elliott Wave International: Introduction to the Wave Principle","url":"https://www.elliottwave.com/free/introduction-to-the-wave-principle/"}],"stemEn":"Considering only standard impulse waves (not diagonals) and three rules — wave 2 does not go beyond the start of wave 1, wave 3 is not the shortest of 1, 3 and 5, and wave 4 does not enter wave 1’s price range — a count has wave 1 = 10, wave 3 = 8 and wave 5 = 12, with the other two rules met. How should it be judged?","optionsEn":["Invalid: wave 3 is shorter than both 1 and 5, breaking the rule","Valid: wave 3 having a positive length meets the given rule","Valid: wave 5 is longest and makes up for wave 3 being short","Undecided: you also need to know how long wave 2 took"],"explanationEn":"8 is less than 10 and 12, a direct breach of the given rule; meeting the other conditions cannot compensate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 8 is less than 10 and 12, breaching the rule, and other conditions cannot compensate.","Wrong: The rule requires wave 3 not to be the shortest, not merely positive.","Wrong: The rules do not allow other waves to compensate.","Wrong: The rule concerns price length only, not time."]},{"id":"method-advanced-06","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[118,127],"stem":"区间下沿100。一次跌到98后收回102，提出spring候选。规则预先规定：“再次测试不破98、下跌量小于首次破位量一半，随后收盘突破104”才确认。首次量1000，随后三步为：回测最低99且下跌量400；收盘103；再收盘105。最早哪步确认？","options":["第一步：回测99且量400，低量已是核心条件","第三步：收盘105，三项条件至此才全部满足","第二步：收盘103，重回原区间已经足够确认","更早：首次收回102时，回测只是附加展示"],"answer":1,"explanation":"回测99高于98、400小于500，之后105高于104，第三步才完成全部条件。","optionExplanations":["突破104的条件还未满足。","正确：回测99高于98且量400小于500，之后收盘105才突破104，第三步才齐备。","103未超过104，不满足突破条件。","回测是规则规定的必要条件。"],"skills":["威科夫测试","联合条件"],"references":[{"title":"Wyckoff Analytics: Method and history","url":"https://www.wyckoffanalytics.com/wyckoff-method/"},{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"stemEn":"A range’s floor is 100. A drop to 98 and close back at 102 makes a spring candidate. The pre-set rule confirms it only if “a retest holds above 98, the retest’s down volume is under half the first break’s volume, and a later close is above 104”. The first break’s volume was 1,000. Then: a retest low of 99 on down volume of 400; a close at 103; a close at 105. At which step is it first confirmed?","optionsEn":["Step one: the retest at 99 on 400 volume, since low volume is the core condition","Step three: the 105 close, when all three conditions are finally met","Step two: the 103 close, since returning to the range is enough","Earlier: at the first close back at 102; the retest is just extra"],"explanationEn":"The retest at 99 holds above 98 and 400 is less than 500; only the later 105 close clears 104, so all conditions are met at step three.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The close above 104 has not happened yet.","Correct: The retest holds at 99 on 400 (< 500) volume, and only the 105 close clears 104, completing step three.","Wrong: 103 is not above 104, so the breakout condition fails.","Wrong: The retest is a required condition in the rule."]},{"id":"method-advanced-07","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[119],"stem":"谐波测试规定D点目标为XA自A回撤78.6%，允许±1个百分点。X=100，A=150，D=110.8，暂不考虑其他比例。D点这一项是否合格？","options":["合格，39.2/50=78.4%，在容差内","不合格，D应精确等于110.7才算","不合格，110.8/150≈73.9%，低于下限","合格，因为D高于X，无需计算比例"],"answer":0,"explanation":"XA长50，A到D回撤39.2，比例78.4%；符合题设容差，但不代表整套形态其他项也合格。","optionExplanations":["XA长50，A到D回撤39.2，比例78.4%；符合题设容差，但不代表整套形态其他项也合格。","题目明确允许±1个百分点，不能擅自改为零容差。","回撤比例分母是XA幅度50，分子是A-D，不是D/A。","D在X上方只是位置信息，不能替代给定比例检查。"],"skills":["比例运算","局部合格"],"references":[{"title":"Harmonic Trader: Gartley history and ratios","url":"https://harmonictrader.com/harmonic-patterns/gartley-pattern/"}],"stemEn":"A harmonic test sets point D at a 78.6% retracement of XA from A, allowing ±1 percentage point. X = 100, A = 150, D = 110.8; ignore other ratios. Does D pass this check?","optionsEn":["Yes: 39.2/50 = 78.4%, within tolerance","No: D must equal exactly 110.7","No: 110.8/150 ≈ 73.9%, below the lower limit","Yes: D is above X, so no ratio is needed"],"explanationEn":"XA is 50 long and the retracement from A to D is 39.2, a ratio of 78.4%; it fits the tolerance, but that says nothing about the pattern’s other checks.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: XA is 50 and A to D is 39.2, so 78.4% is within tolerance, though other checks still apply.","Wrong: The question allows ±1 point; you cannot switch to zero tolerance.","Wrong: The ratio’s denominator is the XA move of 50 and the numerator A − D, not D/A.","Wrong: D being above X is only location information and cannot replace the ratio check."]},{"id":"method-advanced-08","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[122],"stem":"两份缠论标注对同一行情得到不同“笔”。甲先合并包含K线，乙直接用原始K线，且两人对笔的最小间隔采用不同版本。怎样才能公平比较？","options":["直接比较谁标出的买点更接近后来的最低价","先固定包含、分型、成笔规则再复核","以标出笔数更多的一方为准，因为更精细","取两份标注重叠的笔，把其余部分视为错误"],"answer":1,"explanation":"缠论实现可存在版本差异，比较前须固定定义与可知时点，避免把规则差异当错误。","optionExplanations":["用后见之明比较，且未统一规则。","正确：缠论实现存在版本差异，先统一定义才能公平比较。","数量多不等于规则正确。","差异可能来自规则版本，不一定是错误。"],"skills":["规则版本","确认时点"],"references":[{"title":"缠中说禅原文博客（历史原站）","url":"https://blog.sina.com.cn/u/1215172700"}],"stemEn":"Two Chan Theory annotations of the same move produce different “strokes”. One merges inclusive bars first; the other uses raw bars, and they use different versions of the minimum stroke gap. How can they be compared fairly?","optionsEn":["See whose buy point is closer to the later low","First fix the inclusion, fractal and stroke rules, then re-check","Use the one with more strokes, since it is more detailed","Keep the strokes they share and treat the rest as errors"],"explanationEn":"Chan Theory implementations vary by version; fix the definitions and what was knowable when before comparing, so rule differences are not mistaken for errors.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This compares with hindsight and without shared rules.","Correct: Chan Theory implementations vary, so agree the definitions first.","Wrong: More strokes does not mean the rules are right.","Wrong: Differences may come from rule versions, not errors."]},{"id":"method-advanced-09","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[123,124],"stem":"某策略把三个K线的看涨FVG定义为第一根高点低于第三根低点，并在第三根形成后确认。回测却在第二根收盘进场。这个回测最主要的问题是什么？","options":["第三根完成后FVG已过旧，不再适合用来研究","第二根实体足够大时，可视为第三根条件已成立","改用限价单进场，就能保留第二根的信号时间","第二根收盘时未知第三根低点，用了未来信息"],"answer":3,"explanation":"三根结构到第三根完成才可按题设确认，第二根收盘不可能已知第三根低点。","optionExplanations":["形成后的FVG仍可研究。","实体大小不能代替第三根低点条件。","进场方式不能解决信息提前的问题。","正确：三根结构需到第三根完成后才能确认。"],"skills":["结构确认","前视偏差"],"references":[{"title":"Michael J. Huddleston: ICT official teaching source","url":"https://www.theinnercircletrader.com/"},{"title":"ICT official home: Michael J. Huddleston","url":"https://www.theinnercircletrader.com/"}],"stemEn":"A strategy defines a three-bar bullish FVG as bar 1’s high below bar 3’s low, confirmed once bar 3 forms. The backtest, however, enters at bar 2’s close. What is the main problem with this backtest?","optionsEn":["Once bar 3 completes, the FVG is too old to study","When bar 2’s body is large enough, bar 3’s condition can be treated as met","Entering with a limit order keeps bar 2’s signal time valid","At bar 2’s close, bar 3’s low is unknown, so it uses future information"],"explanationEn":"By the stated rule a three-bar structure can be confirmed only when bar 3 completes; bar 3’s low cannot be known at bar 2’s close.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: An FVG can still be studied after it forms.","Wrong: Body size cannot replace bar 3’s low condition.","Wrong: The order type does not fix the use of early information.","Correct: The three-bar structure can only be confirmed once bar 3 completes."]},{"id":"method-advanced-10","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[125],"stem":"两家交易所在同一币种出现相反主动成交Delta。A按逐笔成交主动方分类，B按低周期价格变化估算，且一所现货、一所永续。哪种处理更适合得出可靠结论？","options":["先分产品和分类方法，再用同口径数据交叉核验","先把两个Delta除以现价，统一单位后合并","先按两所成交规模加权，再用合成Delta判方向","以与同期价格方向一致的来源作为主要证据"],"answer":0,"explanation":"现货/永续和估算/逐笔是实质区别，先核查来源再解释相反结果。","optionExplanations":["正确：现货/永续和估算/逐笔是实质区别，应先核查来源。","除以现价不能消除分类方法与产品的差异。","加权合并混合了不同口径。","按结果选来源是事后挑选。"],"skills":["跨市场","数据来源"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume footprint guide and calculation","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000726164-volume-footprint-charts-a-complete-guide/"}],"stemEn":"Two exchanges show opposite aggressive-volume deltas for the same coin. A classifies tick trades by aggressor; B estimates from lower-timeframe price changes; one is spot and the other perpetual. Which approach best leads to a reliable conclusion?","optionsEn":["Separate by product and classification method first, then cross-check with like-for-like data","Divide both deltas by the current price to unify units, then combine them","Weight by each exchange’s volume and judge direction from the combined delta","Treat the source that agrees with price direction as the main evidence"],"explanationEn":"Spot versus perpetual and estimated versus tick are real differences; check the sources before interpreting the opposite results.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Spot/perpetual and estimated/tick are real differences, so check the sources first.","Wrong: Dividing by price does not remove differences in method and product.","Wrong: A weighted combination mixes different definitions.","Wrong: Picking the source by its result is hindsight selection."]},{"id":"method-advanced-11","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[126,99],"stem":"昨日价值区100至104。今天A段：价格105至106停留90分钟，成交900；B段：短暂上探108停留2分钟，成交20；C段：回到103至104停留30分钟，成交300。仅比较今天在105以上的A/B两段，哪项最有依据？","options":["108离旧价值区更远，比A更能证明高位接受","A与B都在旧价值区上方，接受证据可视为同等","A停留久成交多，更支持105—106被接受","C又回到旧价值区，A和B的成交都不能当作证据"],"answer":2,"explanation":"A的时间与成交均明显较多，比单次快速探索更支持该价带接受；结论不能外推到108，C也提示后续仍需跟踪。","optionExplanations":["短暂探索不等于接受。","时间与成交差别很大，证据强度不同。","正确：A的时间与成交明显更多，比快速探索更支持该价带的接受。","C是后续需要跟踪的信息，不会让A的证据作废。"],"skills":["拍卖接受","价带范围"],"references":[{"title":"Wiley: Steidlmayer on Markets","url":"https://www.wiley.com/en-us/-p-9780471215561"},{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040-volume-profile-indicators-basic-concepts/"}],"stemEn":"Yesterday’s value area was 100–104. Today, segment A: price stays at 105–106 for 90 minutes on volume of 900; segment B: a brief probe to 108 for 2 minutes on volume of 20; segment C: back at 103–104 for 30 minutes on volume of 300. Comparing only A and B above 105, which statement is best supported?","optionsEn":["108 is further from the old value area, so it shows acceptance higher up better than A","A and B are both above the old value area, so their evidence of acceptance is equal","A spent longer with more volume, which better supports acceptance at 105–106","C returned to the old value area, so neither A’s nor B’s trading counts as evidence"],"explanationEn":"A has clearly more time and volume, which supports acceptance of that band better than a quick probe; this cannot be extended to 108, and C shows it still needs following.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A brief probe is not acceptance.","Wrong: The time and volume differences are large, so the evidence differs in strength.","Correct: A has far more time and volume, supporting acceptance of that band better than a quick probe.","Wrong: C is information to follow, but it does not cancel A’s evidence."]},{"id":"method-advanced-12","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[121,122,117],"stem":"比较两种结构策略的一笔多头交易，各1单位。甲的转折点画在100，但第3根收盘才确认；按确认后开盘实际成交103，最终退出108。乙当时即可确认，成交104，退出108。两者每笔总费用均1。若统一按当时可知信息计收益，结果如何？","options":["甲净赚5，乙净赚4，甲多1","甲净赚7，乙净赚3，甲多4","甲净赚3，乙净赚2，甲多1","甲净赚4，乙净赚3，甲多1"],"answer":3,"explanation":"甲108-103-1=4，乙108-104-1=3。确认延迟已计入真实入场价，甲仅多1。","optionExplanations":["错误：漏扣了每笔1的总费用。","错误：按画出的转折点100计入场价，忽略了确认后才能成交的事实。","错误：把每笔费用重复扣了两次。","正确：确认延迟已计入真实成交价，扣费后甲4、乙3。"],"skills":["确认延迟","执行与成本"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Gann fan drawing tool","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000518151-gann-fan-drawing-tool/"},{"title":"缠中说禅原文博客（历史原站）","url":"https://blog.sina.com.cn/u/1215172700"},{"title":"Elliott Wave International: Introduction to the Wave Principle","url":"https://www.elliottwave.com/free/introduction-to-the-wave-principle/"}],"stemEn":"Compare one long trade under two structure strategies, 1 unit each. Strategy A draws its turning point at 100 but confirms only at bar 3’s close; filled at the next open, it enters at 103 and exits at 108. Strategy B confirms immediately, enters at 104 and exits at 108. Each trade costs 1 in total. Using only information available at the time, what are the results?","optionsEn":["A nets 5, B nets 4; A makes 1 more","A nets 7, B nets 3; A makes 4 more","A nets 3, B nets 2; A makes 1 more","A nets 4, B nets 3; A makes 1 more"],"explanationEn":"A: 108 − 103 − 1 = 4; B: 108 − 104 − 1 = 3. The confirmation delay is already in the real entry price, so A makes only 1 more.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This leaves out the cost of 1 per trade.","Wrong: This enters at the drawn turning point of 100, ignoring that the fill comes only after confirmation.","Wrong: This deducts the cost twice.","Correct: The delay is already in the real fill price; after costs A makes 4 and B 3."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-13","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[2],"stem":"某3期EMA的平滑系数为α=2÷(3+1)=0.5。上一根EMA为100，新一根收盘104。新EMA是多少？","options":["102","101","103","104"],"answer":0,"explanation":"100+0.5×(104−100)=102。EMA把新收盘与旧EMA按α加权，所以只向新价格移动一半。","optionExplanations":["100+0.5×(104−100)=102。EMA把新收盘与旧EMA按α加权，所以只向新价格移动一半。","这相当于α=0.25，只适用于7期EMA，不是本题的3期。","103不是本题公式能得到的结果；EMA不会把新收盘权重放到0.75。","只有α=1时EMA才等于最新收盘；3期EMA仍保留旧EMA的一半权重。"],"skills":["递推公式","权重"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Moving Averages","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502589-moving-averages/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A 3-period EMA has a smoothing factor α = 2 ÷ (3 + 1) = 0.5. The previous EMA is 100 and the new close is 104. What is the new EMA?","optionsEn":["102","101","103","104"],"explanationEn":"100 + 0.5 × (104 − 100) = 102. The EMA weights the new close and the old EMA by α, so it moves only halfway toward the new price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 100 + 0.5 × (104 − 100) = 102; the EMA moves halfway toward the new close.","Wrong: This is α = 0.25, which fits a 7-period EMA, not this 3-period one.","Wrong: 103 cannot come from this formula; the EMA does not give the new close a 0.75 weight.","Wrong: Only with α = 1 would the EMA equal the latest close; a 3-period EMA keeps half the old value."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-14","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[3],"stem":"3根收盘价依次为10、11、15（15最新）。3期WMA的权重依次为1、2、3。WMA与3期SMA分别约为多少？","options":["WMA约12.00，SMA为12.00","WMA约12.83，SMA为12.00","WMA约11.17，SMA为12.00","WMA约12.83，SMA约12.83"],"answer":1,"explanation":"WMA=(10×1+11×2+15×3)÷6=77÷6≈12.83；SMA=(10+11+15)÷3=12。最新价格权重最大，所以WMA更靠近15。","optionExplanations":["错误：加权没有起作用，等于把WMA当成SMA。","正确：(10×1+11×2+15×3)÷6≈12.83，SMA=36÷3=12。","错误：把权重顺序弄反，让最旧价格权重最大。","错误：SMA对三根价格等权，不会受权重影响。"],"skills":["加权平均","滞后"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Weighted Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594680-weighted-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Three closes are 10, 11 and 15 (15 is the latest). A 3-period WMA uses weights 1, 2 and 3. What are the WMA and the 3-period SMA, approximately?","optionsEn":["WMA about 12.00, SMA 12.00","WMA about 12.83, SMA 12.00","WMA about 11.17, SMA 12.00","WMA about 12.83, SMA about 12.83"],"explanationEn":"WMA = (10×1 + 11×2 + 15×3) ÷ 6 = 77 ÷ 6 ≈ 12.83; SMA = (10 + 11 + 15) ÷ 3 = 12. The latest price has the largest weight, so the WMA sits closer to 15.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The weights had no effect, treating the WMA as an SMA.","Correct: (10×1 + 11×2 + 15×3) ÷ 6 ≈ 12.83 and the SMA is 36 ÷ 3 = 12.","Wrong: The weights are reversed, giving the oldest price the largest weight.","Wrong: The SMA weights the three prices equally and is unaffected by the weights."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-13","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[4],"stem":"某14期RMA（SMMA）上一值为2.0，新输入值为3.4。按RMA递推：新值=(旧值×13+新输入)÷14。新RMA约为多少？若误用同长度EMA（α=2÷15）会得到多少？","options":["RMA 2.19；EMA约2.10","RMA 2.70；EMA约2.70","RMA 2.10；EMA约2.19","RMA 3.40；EMA约3.40"],"answer":2,"explanation":"RMA=(2.0×13+3.4)÷14=29.4÷14=2.10；EMA=2.0+(2÷15)×1.4≈2.19。RMA的α=1/14，比同长度EMA更平滑。","optionExplanations":["把两种平滑的α对调了；RMA的α=1/14小于EMA的2/15。","2.70是旧值与新值的简单平均，两种递推都不会这样算。","RMA=(2.0×13+3.4)÷14=29.4÷14=2.10；EMA=2.0+(2÷15)×1.4≈2.19。RMA的α=1/14，比同长度EMA更平滑。","平滑线不会直接跳到最新输入值。"],"skills":["平滑系数","参数换算"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Smoothed Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591343-smoothed-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A 14-period RMA (SMMA) was 2.0 and the new input is 3.4. Using the RMA recursion new = (old × 13 + input) ÷ 14, what is the new RMA? What would a same-length EMA (α = 2 ÷ 15) give by mistake?","optionsEn":["RMA 2.19; EMA about 2.10","RMA 2.70; EMA about 2.70","RMA 2.10; EMA about 2.19","RMA 3.40; EMA about 3.40"],"explanationEn":"RMA = (2.0 × 13 + 3.4) ÷ 14 = 29.4 ÷ 14 = 2.10; EMA = 2.0 + (2 ÷ 15) × 1.4 ≈ 2.19. The RMA’s α = 1/14 is smoother than a same-length EMA.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The two smoothing factors are swapped; the RMA’s α of 1/14 is smaller than the EMA’s 2/15.","Wrong: 2.70 is the simple average of old and new values; neither recursion works that way.","Correct: RMA = 29.4 ÷ 14 = 2.10 and EMA = 2.0 + (2 ÷ 15) × 1.4 ≈ 2.19; the RMA is smoother.","Wrong: A smoothed line does not jump straight to the latest input."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-15","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[5],"stem":"3根K线收盘为10、10、13，对应成交量为100、100、800。3期VWMA与3期SMA的关系是？","options":["VWMA约12.4，高于SMA的11","VWMA约11.0，与SMA的11相同","VWMA约13.0，只反映放量那根","VWMA约10.3，低于SMA的11"],"answer":0,"explanation":"VWMA=(10×100+10×100+13×800)÷1000=12.4；SMA=(10+10+13)÷3=11。成交量大的那根把平均拉向13。","optionExplanations":["正确：(10×100+10×100+13×800)÷1000=12.4，放量那根把平均拉高。","错误：VWMA按成交量加权，大量那根会改变结果。","错误：VWMA仍是加权平均，其余K线也有权重。","错误：把成交量权重分配给了错误的K线。"],"skills":["成交量加权","单位"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Volume-Weighted Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592293-volume-weighted-moving-average-vwma/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Three bars close at 10, 10 and 13 on volumes of 100, 100 and 800. How does the 3-period VWMA compare with the 3-period SMA?","optionsEn":["VWMA about 12.4, above the SMA of 11","VWMA about 11.0, the same as the SMA of 11","VWMA about 13.0, reflecting only the high-volume bar","VWMA about 10.3, below the SMA of 11"],"explanationEn":"VWMA = (10×100 + 10×100 + 13×800) ÷ 1,000 = 12.4; SMA = (10 + 10 + 13) ÷ 3 = 11. The high-volume bar pulls the average toward 13.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: (10×100 + 10×100 + 13×800) ÷ 1,000 = 12.4; the high-volume bar pulls it up.","Wrong: The VWMA weights by volume, so the heavy bar changes the result.","Wrong: The VWMA is still a weighted average; the other bars also carry weight.","Wrong: This gives the volume weights to the wrong bars."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-14","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[10],"stem":"均线带统一用SMA 10、20、40、80。经过一段下跌后，SMA10已上穿SMA20，但两者仍低于SMA40和SMA80，四线间距开始收窄。较稳妥的描述是？","options":["均线带已形成多头排列，趋势转为向上","SMA80位于最上方，说明长期均价仍在上升","短期有转强迹象，中长期仍未形成多头排列","四线间距收窄，表明这轮下跌趋势已经结束"],"answer":2,"explanation":"均线带读的是各周期平均价的相对位置。只有短周期转强，中长期仍压在上方，属于过渡状态。","optionExplanations":["错误：多头排列要求四线由短到长依次自上而下，这里并不满足。","错误：SMA80在上方只表示长期平均价较高，并不表示上升。","正确：SMA10上穿SMA20只说明短期转强，SMA40、SMA80仍压在上方。","错误：间距收窄只是过渡状态，不能确认趋势结束。"],"skills":["多周期比较","排列顺序"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Moving Average Ribbon","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644913-moving-average-ribbon/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A moving-average ribbon uses SMAs of 10, 20, 40 and 80. After a decline, SMA10 has crossed above SMA20, but both are still below SMA40 and SMA80, and the gaps between the four lines are narrowing. What is the more prudent description?","optionsEn":["The ribbon has formed a bullish alignment and the trend has turned up","SMA80 is on top, so the long-term average price is still rising","Short-term strength is appearing, but the medium and long term are not yet aligned bullishly","The narrowing gaps show this decline is over"],"explanationEn":"A ribbon shows the relative positions of the averages. Only the short term has strengthened while the medium and long averages still sit above: a transition.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Bullish alignment needs all four lines stacked from short on top to long at the bottom, which is not the case.","Wrong: SMA80 on top only means the long-term average price is higher, not that it is rising.","Correct: SMA10 crossing SMA20 shows short-term strength, while SMA40 and SMA80 still sit above.","Wrong: Narrowing gaps only show a transition and cannot confirm the decline is over."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-16","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[13],"stem":"最近14根K线最高120、最低100，当前已收盘价115。Stochastic未平滑的原始%K是多少？","options":["25","75","15","95.8"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原始%K=100×(115−100)÷(120−100)=75，表示收盘位于14根区间从下往上75%的位置。","optionExplanations":["25是收盘距离区间顶部的比例，对应Williams %R的−25，不是%K。","原始%K=100×(115−100)÷(120−100)=75，表示收盘位于14根区间从下往上75%的位置。","15只是收盘减最低价的价格差，没有除以区间宽度。","95.8是115÷120，与区间最低价无关，不是随机指标的算法。"],"skills":["区间位置","公式"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Stochastic","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502332-stochastic-stoch/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Over the last 14 bars the high is 120 and the low 100; the current close is 115. What is the unsmoothed raw Stochastic %K?","optionsEn":["25","75","15","95.8"],"explanationEn":"Raw %K = 100 × (115 − 100) ÷ (120 − 100) = 75, meaning the close sits 75% of the way up the 14-bar range.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 25 is the distance from the top of the range, matching a Williams %R of −25, not %K.","Correct: Raw %K = 100 × (115 − 100) ÷ (120 − 100) = 75, 75% of the way up the range.","Wrong: 15 is only close minus low, without dividing by the range width.","Wrong: 95.8 is 115 ÷ 120, which ignores the range low and is not the stochastic formula."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-15","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[14],"stem":"同一组最近14根K线：最高120、最低100、收盘115。TradingView的Williams %R(14)读数是多少？它与同窗口原始Stochastic %K是什么关系？","options":["−75；%R等于原始%K取负","25；%R是正数刻度","−25；等于原始%K减100","75；两者完全相同"],"answer":2,"explanation":"%R=−100×(120−115)÷(120−100)=−25；原始%K=75，75−100=−25。两者是同一位置的不同刻度。","optionExplanations":["取负会让接近顶部的收盘显示为−75，与标准刻度相反。","标准%R刻度在0到−100之间；有些变体会镜像成正数，要先看说明。","%R=−100×(120−115)÷(120−100)=−25；原始%K=75，75−100=−25。两者是同一位置的不同刻度。","两者描述同一位置，但%R把0放在顶部、−100放在底部。"],"skills":["刻度换算","区间位置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Williams %R","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501985-williams-r-r/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"With the same 14 bars — high 120, low 100, close 115 — what does TradingView’s Williams %R(14) read, and how does it relate to the raw Stochastic %K for the same window?","optionsEn":["−75; %R is the raw %K made negative","25; %R uses a positive scale","−25; it equals raw %K minus 100","75; the two are identical"],"explanationEn":"%R = −100 × (120 − 115) ÷ (120 − 100) = −25; raw %K = 75 and 75 − 100 = −25. They are different scales for the same position.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Making it negative would show a close near the top as −75, the reverse of the standard scale.","Wrong: The standard %R scale runs from 0 to −100; some variants mirror it to positive values, so check the documentation.","Correct: %R = −25 and raw %K = 75, with 75 − 100 = −25; two scales for one position.","Wrong: They describe the same position, but %R puts 0 at the top and −100 at the bottom."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-17","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[15],"stem":"CCI=(典型价−均值)÷(0.015×平均偏差)。某资产CCI(20)读数为150。下面哪项解读正确？","options":["价格比20期均价高出约150%","典型价高出均值约2.25倍平均偏差","读数超过100，价格接近回落到均值","典型价高出均值约1.5倍平均偏差"],"answer":1,"explanation":"CCI=(典型价−均值)÷(0.015×平均偏差)，150×0.015=2.25。它衡量相对偏离，不是涨幅。","optionExplanations":["错误：CCI不是涨幅百分比。","正确：150×0.015=2.25，CCI按平均偏差为单位衡量偏离。","错误：读数超过100只表示偏离较大，并不保证回落。","错误：忽略了0.015的常数，把150直接除以100。"],"skills":["标准化","阈值边界"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Commodity Channel Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502001-commodity-channel-index-cci/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"CCI = (typical price − mean) ÷ (0.015 × mean deviation). An asset’s CCI(20) reads 150. Which interpretation is correct?","optionsEn":["Price is about 150% above its 20-period average","The typical price is about 2.25 mean deviations above the mean","The reading is above 100, so price is about to fall back to the mean","The typical price is about 1.5 mean deviations above the mean"],"explanationEn":"150 × 0.015 = 2.25. CCI measures relative deviation, not a percentage gain.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: CCI is not a percentage gain.","Correct: 150 × 0.015 = 2.25; CCI measures deviation in units of mean deviation.","Wrong: A reading above 100 only shows a large deviation, not a guaranteed pullback.","Wrong: This ignores the 0.015 constant and simply divides 150 by 100."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-18","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[16],"stem":"某小时图ROC(10)：当前收盘99，10根以前收盘90。ROC读数是多少？","options":["+10%","+9%","+9.09%","−10%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ROC=100×(99−90)÷90=+10%，比较的是当前收盘与10根以前那根收盘。","optionExplanations":["ROC=100×(99−90)÷90=+10%，比较的是当前收盘与10根以前那根收盘。","+9是价格差，单位是价格，不是百分比；那是Momentum的读法。","9.09%是除以当前价99，ROC的分母是N根以前的收盘90。","当前收盘高于10根以前，读数为正。"],"skills":["百分比变化","基准"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Rate of Change","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502343-rate-of-change-roc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"On an hourly chart, ROC(10): the current close is 99 and the close 10 bars ago was 90. What does ROC read?","optionsEn":["+10%","+9%","+9.09%","−10%"],"explanationEn":"ROC = 100 × (99 − 90) ÷ 90 = +10%; it compares the current close with the close 10 bars ago.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: ROC = 100 × (99 − 90) ÷ 90 = +10%, comparing the current close with the close 10 bars ago.","Wrong: +9 is the price difference in price units, not a percentage; that is how Momentum reads.","Wrong: 9.09% divides by the current price of 99; ROC divides by the close N bars ago, 90.","Wrong: The current close is above the close 10 bars ago, so the reading is positive."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-16","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[17],"stem":"资产A的10根以前收盘为10，现在12；资产B的10根以前收盘为1000，现在1010。用差值版Momentum(10)比较两者的推进速度，哪种说法正确？","options":["B的Momentum为10，大于A的2，B更快","B的Momentum是1010，大于12，B更快","按百分比A涨得更快，应看ROC才能比较","两者Momentum相同，因为都比10根前高"],"answer":2,"explanation":"差值版Momentum的单位是价格，高价资产天然读数大。比较不同价位的资产要换成百分比。","optionExplanations":["错误：差值版读数受价格水平影响，不能直接比较大小。","错误：把价格水平当成Momentum，而它是现价减10根前价。","正确：A涨20%，B只涨1%，应换成百分比的ROC比较。","错误：差值版读数取决于涨了多少，两者并不相同。"],"skills":["单位","跨资产比较"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Momentum","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589187-momentum/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Asset A closed at 10 ten bars ago and is now 12; asset B closed at 1,000 ten bars ago and is now 1,010. Using difference-based Momentum(10) to compare how fast they are rising, which statement is correct?","optionsEn":["B’s Momentum of 10 is above A’s 2, so B is faster","B’s Momentum is 1,010, above 12, so B is faster","In percentage terms A rose faster; compare with ROC instead","Their Momentum is the same, since both are above 10 bars ago"],"explanationEn":"Difference Momentum is in price units, so higher-priced assets naturally read larger. Compare assets at different price levels in percentages.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The difference reading depends on price level and cannot be compared directly.","Wrong: This uses the price level as Momentum, which is the current price minus the price 10 bars ago.","Correct: A rose 20% and B only 1%, so compare with percentage-based ROC.","Wrong: The difference reading depends on how much each rose, and they differ."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-19","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[18],"stem":"某时刻EMA12为103，EMA26为100。PPO(12,26)读数是多少？","options":["3美元","2.91%","3%","0.03%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"PPO=100×(103−100)÷100=3%，即快线高出慢线的百分比；同一时刻MACD为3（价格单位）。","optionExplanations":["3美元是MACD的价格差，PPO再除以慢线变成百分比。","2.91%是除以EMA12；标准PPO以慢线EMA26为分母。","PPO=100×(103−100)÷100=3%，即快线高出慢线的百分比；同一时刻MACD为3（价格单位）。","0.03是比例小数，换成百分比是3%。"],"skills":["百分比","与MACD比较"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Percentage Price Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502346-percentage-price-oscillator-ppo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"At one moment EMA12 is 103 and EMA26 is 100. What is PPO(12,26)?","optionsEn":["$3","2.91%","3%","0.03%"],"explanationEn":"PPO = 100 × (103 − 100) ÷ 100 = 3%, the percentage by which the fast line exceeds the slow line; MACD at the same moment is 3 in price units.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: $3 is MACD’s price difference; PPO divides it by the slow line to get a percentage.","Wrong: 2.91% divides by EMA12; standard PPO divides by the slow EMA26.","Correct: PPO = 100 × (103 − 100) ÷ 100 = 3%; MACD is 3 in price units.","Wrong: 0.03 is a decimal ratio; as a percentage it is 3%."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-17","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[19],"stem":"某14期窗口内，典型价上升那些K线的“典型价×成交量”合计300万，下降那些合计100万。MFI(14)是多少？","options":["66.7","25","3","75"],"answer":3,"explanation":"资金比率=300÷100=3，MFI=100−100÷(1+3)=75。","optionExplanations":["66.7来自把300除以(300+150)之类的错误分母，不是MFI公式。","25是负向部分占总资金流的比例，方向读反了。","3只是资金比率，还需代入100−100÷(1+比率)。","资金比率=300÷100=3，MFI=100−100÷(1+3)=75。"],"skills":["比率转换","成交量"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Money Flow Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502348-money-flow-mfi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"In a 14-period window, the bars with a rising typical price sum to 3 million in “typical price × volume”, and those with a falling typical price sum to 1 million. What is MFI(14)?","optionsEn":["66.7","25","3","75"],"explanationEn":"Money ratio = 300 ÷ 100 = 3, so MFI = 100 − 100 ÷ (1 + 3) = 75.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 66.7 comes from a wrong denominator, not the MFI formula.","Wrong: 25 is the share of negative flow in total flow; the direction is reversed.","Wrong: 3 is only the money ratio; it still goes into 100 − 100 ÷ (1 + ratio).","Correct: Money ratio = 300 ÷ 100 = 3, so MFI = 100 − 100 ÷ (1 + 3) = 75."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-20","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[20],"stem":"按Elder原始定义，Bull Power=最高价−EMA13，Bear Power=最低价−EMA13。某根K线最高104、最低98，EMA13为100。两者分别是多少？","options":["Bull Power −4，Bear Power +2","Bull Power +4，Bear Power +2","Bull Power +6，Bear Power 0","Bull Power +4，Bear Power −2"],"answer":3,"explanation":"104−100=+4，98−100=−2。部分平台会把两者合成一条线，读之前先看说明。","optionExplanations":["错误：把减法方向弄反了。","错误：Bear Power取了绝对值，漏掉了最低价低于EMA的负号。","错误：用高低价差或收盘价代入，没有按定义减EMA13。","正确：104−100=+4，98−100=−2。"],"skills":["相对距离","符号"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bull Bear Power","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000717955-bull-bear-power/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"By Elder’s original definitions, Bull Power = high − EMA13 and Bear Power = low − EMA13. A bar has a high of 104, a low of 98 and EMA13 of 100. What are the two values?","optionsEn":["Bull Power −4, Bear Power +2","Bull Power +4, Bear Power +2","Bull Power +6, Bear Power 0","Bull Power +4, Bear Power −2"],"explanationEn":"104 − 100 = +4 and 98 − 100 = −2. Some platforms combine both into one line, so read the documentation first.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The subtraction is reversed.","Wrong: Bear Power was taken as an absolute value, losing the minus sign when the low is below the EMA.","Wrong: This uses the high–low range or the close instead of subtracting EMA13.","Correct: 104 − 100 = +4 and 98 − 100 = −2."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-18","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[25],"stem":"Keltner通道设为EMA20、ATR10、倍数2。某根EMA20为100、ATR为1.5；之后EMA仍为100，ATR升到2.5。上下轨如何变化，说明什么？","options":["上轨103→105，说明上涨趋势加强","两侧各外移2，反映波动扩大","ATR增加1，所以上下轨各外移1","上轨105、下轨仍为97"],"answer":1,"explanation":"轨道=EMA±2×ATR。ATR增加1，两侧各外移2。宽度变化说的是波动大小。","optionExplanations":["下轨同时下移，两侧对称扩张，与方向无关。","轨道=EMA±2×ATR。ATR增加1，两侧各外移2。宽度变化说的是波动大小。","倍数为2，ATR增加1时每侧外移2。","ATR同时影响上下两侧。"],"skills":["ATR倍数","波动与方向"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Keltner Channels","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502266-keltner-channels-kc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Keltner Channels use EMA20, ATR10 and a multiplier of 2. At one bar EMA20 is 100 and ATR 1.5; later EMA is still 100 and ATR rises to 2.5. How do the bands change, and what does it show?","optionsEn":["The upper band goes from 103 to 105, showing a stronger uptrend","Both bands move out by 2, reflecting higher volatility","ATR rose by 1, so each band moves out by 1","The upper band is 105 and the lower band stays at 97"],"explanationEn":"Bands = EMA ± 2 × ATR. ATR rising by 1 moves each band out by 2. A change in width is about volatility.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The lower band also moves down; the bands widen symmetrically, regardless of direction.","Correct: Bands = EMA ± 2 × ATR, so a 1-point rise in ATR moves each band out by 2; width reflects volatility.","Wrong: With a multiplier of 2, each band moves out by 2 when ATR rises by 1.","Wrong: ATR affects both bands."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-21","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[26],"stem":"均线包络线设为SMA20、偏移3%。某时刻SMA20为100，上下轨分别是多少？","options":["100.03和99.97","106和94","103和97","随标准差变化，无法计算"],"answer":2,"explanation":"上轨=100×1.03=103，下轨=100×0.97=97。宽度只随中线成比例变化。","optionExplanations":["3%是0.03的比例，不是0.03个价格单位。","这相当于偏移6%。","上轨=100×1.03=103，下轨=100×0.97=97。宽度只随中线成比例变化。","随标准差变化的是布林带；包络线是固定百分比。"],"skills":["百分比偏移","与布林带区别"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Envelope","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502260-envelope-env/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A moving-average envelope uses SMA20 with a 3% offset. With SMA20 at 100, where are the upper and lower bands?","optionsEn":["100.03 and 99.97","106 and 94","103 and 97","They depend on the standard deviation and cannot be computed"],"explanationEn":"Upper = 100 × 1.03 = 103 and lower = 100 × 0.97 = 97. The width changes only in proportion to the middle line.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 3% is a ratio of 0.03, not 0.03 price units.","Wrong: This is an offset of 6%.","Correct: Upper = 100 × 1.03 = 103 and lower = 100 × 0.97 = 97.","Wrong: Bands that depend on standard deviation are Bollinger Bands; an envelope uses a fixed percentage."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-22","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[29],"stem":"切到日线，最近3天的最高−最低分别为4、6、5美元。3日ADR是多少？它说明什么？","options":["5美元，最近3天的平均每日振幅","5美元，预计明天还会波动5美元","15美元，最近3天的累计波动","5美元，最近3天的平均涨幅"],"answer":0,"explanation":"(4+6+5)÷3=5。ADR描述日内波动范围，不说明涨跌。","optionExplanations":["正确：(4+6+5)÷3=5，ADR描述波动范围。","错误：ADR只是历史平均，不是对明天的预测。","错误：15是总和，ADR还要除以天数。","错误：ADR用最高减最低，不区分涨跌方向。"],"skills":["振幅","历史描述"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Average Daily Range","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000695003-average-daily-range-adr-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"On the daily chart, the last three days’ high minus low were $4, $6 and $5. What is the 3-day ADR, and what does it show?","optionsEn":["$5, the average daily range of the last 3 days","$5, meaning tomorrow is expected to move $5","$15, the total range over the last 3 days","$5, the average gain of the last 3 days"],"explanationEn":"(4 + 6 + 5) ÷ 3 = 5. ADR describes the daily range, not direction.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: (4 + 6 + 5) ÷ 3 = 5; ADR describes the range.","Wrong: ADR is a historical average, not a forecast for tomorrow.","Wrong: 15 is the sum; ADR divides by the number of days.","Wrong: ADR uses high minus low and ignores direction."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-19","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[30],"stem":"对收盘98、100、102计算标准差，脚本甲显示1.63，脚本乙显示2.00。最可能的原因是？","options":["甲只取最近2根价格，乙取全部3根价格","甲除以3（总体），乙除以2（样本）","甲用的是算术均值，乙用的是加权均值","乙输入的是收益率，甲输入的是价格数据"],"answer":1,"explanation":"均值100，偏差平方和8。8÷3开方≈1.63，8÷2开方=2.00。读数前先确认公式。","optionExplanations":["错误：两个读数都用了三根价格，差别在分母。","正确：偏差平方和8，÷3开方≈1.63，÷2开方=2.00。","错误：两者均值都是100，差异不在均值。","错误：题中两者对同一组收盘价计算，输入并不同。"],"skills":["总体与样本","公式核对"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bollinger Bands and price standard deviation","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501840-bollinger-bands-bb/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"For closes of 98, 100 and 102, script A shows a standard deviation of 1.63 and script B shows 2.00. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["A uses only the last 2 prices while B uses all 3","A divides by 3 (population) and B by 2 (sample)","A uses an arithmetic mean and B a weighted mean","B uses returns as input while A uses prices"],"explanationEn":"The mean is 100 and the sum of squared deviations 8; √(8 ÷ 3) ≈ 1.63 and √(8 ÷ 2) = 2.00. Check the formula before reading the value.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Both readings use all three prices; the difference is the denominator.","Correct: The squared deviations sum to 8; √(8 ÷ 3) ≈ 1.63 and √(8 ÷ 2) = 2.00.","Wrong: Both have a mean of 100, so the mean is not the difference.","Wrong: Both are computed on the same closes, so the input is not different."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-20","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[31],"stem":"同一资产的日对数收益率标准差约2%。平台甲显示历史波动率约31.7%，平台乙显示约38.2%。最可能的原因是？","options":["年化天数不同（252对365）","乙用样本标准差，甲用总体标准差","乙用普通收益率，甲用对数收益率","乙用了更短的窗口，所以数值更大"],"answer":0,"explanation":"股票常按交易日252年化，24小时交易的加密资产常按365。读数前先看年化设置。","optionExplanations":["正确：31.7%≈2%×√252，38.2%≈2%×√365。","错误：在较长窗口内这点差别很小，解释不了20%的差距。","错误：2%的日收益两种算法差别很小。","错误：题中日波动已同为2%，差距来自年化天数。"],"skills":["年化","参数设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Historical Volatility","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589145-historical-volatility/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"An asset’s daily log-return standard deviation is about 2%. Platform A shows historical volatility of about 31.7% and platform B about 38.2%. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["Different annualisation days (252 versus 365)","B uses the sample standard deviation and A the population","B uses simple returns and A log returns","B uses a shorter window, so its value is larger"],"explanationEn":"Stocks are usually annualised with 252 trading days; crypto, which trades around the clock, often uses 365. Check the annualisation setting first.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 31.7% ≈ 2% × √252 and 38.2% ≈ 2% × √365.","Wrong: Over a long window this difference is tiny and cannot explain a 20% gap.","Wrong: At 2% daily returns the two methods differ very little.","Wrong: Daily volatility is already 2% in both; the gap comes from annualisation."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-23","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[32],"stem":"某1小时K线收盘高于开盘，下方量柱为绿色且是近20根最高。以下哪项描述最准确？","options":["买方资金净流入达到近20根最高","放量收涨，说明下一根大概率继续上涨","这根K线的成交几乎全部是买单","成交较多，但不能据此判断买方净流入"],"answer":3,"explanation":"量柱颜色沿用K线开收关系，高度只表示成交数量。","optionExplanations":["错误：每笔成交都有买卖双方，量柱高度不是净流入。","错误：单根量价不足以预测下一根走势。","错误：绿色只说明收盘高于开盘，不说明成交方向。","正确：量柱颜色沿用开收关系，高度只表示成交数量。"],"skills":["单位","颜色含义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Volume","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591617-volume/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"An hourly bar closes above its open, and its volume bar below is green and the highest of the last 20. Which description is most accurate?","optionsEn":["Net buying inflow reached its highest in 20 bars","Rising on high volume means the next bar will probably rise too","Almost all of this bar’s trades were buy orders","Volume was heavy, but it does not show net buying"],"explanationEn":"The volume bar’s colour follows the candle’s open–close relation; its height only shows how much traded.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Every trade has a buyer and a seller; volume height is not net inflow.","Wrong: One bar of volume and price is not enough to predict the next.","Wrong: Green only means the close was above the open, not who traded.","Correct: The colour follows open versus close, and height only shows quantity."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-21","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[33],"stem":"某股票开盘第一小时的成交量通常是午间的3倍。用普通RVOL（除以过去20根小时平均）读到2.0，用同时段RVOL（与以往同一开盘时段比）读到0.9。较合理的解释是？","options":["0.9说明开盘成交只有往常的9%","两种读数矛盾，说明至少有一个算错","比全天平均放量，但同时段不突出","开盘资金流入翻倍，0.9只是噪声"],"answer":2,"explanation":"普通RVOL受日内量能季节性影响；同时段RVOL把比较基准换成同一时段，0.9说明略低于往常。","optionExplanations":["错误：0.9是比值，表示约为往常的90%。","错误：两者基准不同，结果不同很正常。","正确：开盘本就放量，同时段RVOL才是公平比较。","错误：2.0受开盘季节性影响，不代表资金流入翻倍。"],"skills":["比较基准","日内季节性"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Relative Volume calculation","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000635874-how-do-we-calculate-relative-volume-and-relative-volume-at-time/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A stock’s first trading hour usually has three times the midday volume. Ordinary RVOL (divided by the last 20 hourly bars) reads 2.0, while time-of-day RVOL (compared with past opening hours) reads 0.9. What is the more reasonable explanation?","optionsEn":["0.9 means opening volume is only 9% of normal","The readings contradict, so at least one is wrong","Heavy against the whole day, but not unusual for this time of day","Opening inflows doubled; 0.9 is just noise"],"explanationEn":"Ordinary RVOL is distorted by intraday volume patterns; time-of-day RVOL compares with the same period, and 0.9 means slightly below normal.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 0.9 is a ratio, about 90% of normal.","Wrong: The baselines differ, so different results are normal.","Correct: The open is always busy, so time-of-day RVOL is the fair comparison.","Wrong: 2.0 reflects the opening pattern, not a doubling of inflows."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-24","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[35],"stem":"PVT每根增量=成交量×(收盘−前收)÷前收。前收100，本根收盘102，成交量5000。PVT增加多少？同一根OBV增加多少？","options":["PVT +100；OBV +100","PVT +10000；OBV +5000","PVT +5000；OBV +100","PVT +100；OBV +5000"],"answer":3,"explanation":"PVT=5000×2÷100=100，只计入与涨幅成比例的量；OBV只看涨跌方向，整根5000都加上。","optionExplanations":["错误：OBV只看涨跌方向，不按涨幅比例缩放。","错误：把涨幅2当成2倍，漏除以前收100。","错误：把两个指标的算法对调了。","正确：PVT=5000×2÷100=100，OBV整根成交量都加上。"],"skills":["比例加权","与OBV比较"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Price Volume Trend","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502345-price-volume-trend-pvt/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"PVT adds volume × (close − prior close) ÷ prior close each bar. The prior close is 100, this bar closes at 102 on volume of 5,000. How much does PVT rise? How much does OBV rise on the same bar?","optionsEn":["PVT +100; OBV +100","PVT +10,000; OBV +5,000","PVT +5,000; OBV +100","PVT +100; OBV +5,000"],"explanationEn":"PVT = 5,000 × 2 ÷ 100 = 100, adding only volume in proportion to the gain; OBV looks only at direction and adds the full 5,000.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: OBV only looks at direction and does not scale by the gain.","Wrong: This treats a 2-point gain as 2× and forgets to divide by the prior close of 100.","Wrong: The two indicators’ formulas are swapped.","Correct: PVT = 5,000 × 2 ÷ 100 = 100, while OBV adds the full volume."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-25","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[36],"stem":"成交量的EMA12为12,000，EMA26为10,000。PVO(12,26)读数是多少？","options":["+2000","+20%","−16.7%","+0.2%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"PVO=100×(12000−10000)÷10000=+20%，表示短期平均成交量比长期高20%。","optionExplanations":["2000是成交量差，PVO再除以慢线变成百分比。","PVO=100×(12000−10000)÷10000=+20%，表示短期平均成交量比长期高20%。","这是以12000为分母且方向相反。","0.2是比例小数，换成百分比是20%。"],"skills":["百分比","成交量平滑"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Percentage Volume Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591350-percentage-volume-oscillator-pvo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The 12-period EMA of volume is 12,000 and the 26-period EMA is 10,000. What is PVO(12,26)?","optionsEn":["+2,000","+20%","−16.7%","+0.2%"],"explanationEn":"PVO = 100 × (12,000 − 10,000) ÷ 10,000 = +20%: short-term average volume is 20% above long-term.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 2,000 is the volume difference; PVO divides by the slow line to get a percentage.","Correct: PVO = 100 × (12,000 − 10,000) ÷ 10,000 = +20%.","Wrong: This divides by 12,000 and reverses the direction.","Wrong: 0.2 is a decimal ratio; as a percentage it is 20%."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-22","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[38],"stem":"上升阶段的Parabolic SAR：当前SAR 95.0，极值点EP 105，加速因子AF 0.04；最近两根K线最低价分别为95.2和96.0。按Wilder规则（上升阶段SAR不得高于前两根K线的最低价），下一根SAR是多少？","options":["95.4","95.8","95.2","105"],"answer":2,"explanation":"95.0+0.04×(105−95.0)=95.4，但上升阶段SAR不得高于前两根最低价，因此限制为95.2。","optionExplanations":["95.4是未做前两根最低价限制的值。","95.8相当于AF用了0.08。","95.0+0.04×(105−95.0)=95.4，但上升阶段SAR不得高于前两根最低价，因此限制为95.2。","只有反转时SAR才跳到原EP。"],"skills":["递推规则","限制条件"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Parabolic SAR","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502597-parabolic-sar-sar/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Parabolic SAR in an uptrend: current SAR 95.0, extreme point EP 105, acceleration factor AF 0.04; the last two bars’ lows are 95.2 and 96.0. Under Wilder’s rule that an uptrend SAR may not exceed the lows of the prior two bars, what is the next SAR?","optionsEn":["95.4","95.8","95.2","105"],"explanationEn":"95.0 + 0.04 × (105 − 95.0) = 95.4, but in an uptrend SAR may not exceed the prior two lows, so it is capped at 95.2.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 95.4 is the value before applying the two-bar low cap.","Wrong: 95.8 corresponds to an AF of 0.08.","Correct: The formula gives 95.4, but the prior two lows cap it at 95.2.","Wrong: SAR jumps to the old EP only on a reversal."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-26","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[39],"stem":"标准Supertrend线位于K线下方并连续上移。某根K线盘中最低价跌破该线，但收盘仍在线上方。按标准版本应如何理解？","options":["线会下移到最低价下方，保持向上","线会在下一根直接跳到K线上方","未翻转，标准版以收盘价判断","盘中最低价跌破就已翻转向下"],"answer":2,"explanation":"盘中刺破只是过程，收盘仍在线上方，跟踪方向保持向上。","optionExplanations":["错误：向上的跟踪线只上移，不会因盘中刺破而下移。","错误：只有收盘穿线才会翻转。","正确：盘中刺破不算，收盘仍在线上方就不翻转。","错误：标准版看收盘价，不看盘中最低价。"],"skills":["收盘确认","规则边界"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Supertrend","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000634738-supertrend/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A standard Supertrend line sits below price and keeps moving up. One bar’s intraday low breaks below the line, but it closes above. How should this be read in the standard version?","optionsEn":["The line moves down below the low and stays bullish","The line jumps above price on the next bar","No flip: the standard version uses the close","The intraday break already flipped it bearish"],"explanationEn":"An intraday poke is part of the bar’s path; with the close still above the line, the trailing direction stays up.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A rising trailing line only moves up and does not drop because of an intraday poke.","Wrong: Only a close through the line flips it.","Correct: An intraday poke does not count; a close above the line means no flip.","Wrong: The standard version uses the close, not the intraday low."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-27","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[43],"stem":"Aroon长度设为25，Aroon Up=100×(25−距窗口最高点的根数)÷25。若窗口内最高点出现在5根以前，Aroon Up是多少？","options":["80","20","5","100"],"answer":0,"explanation":"100×(25−5)÷25=80。数值越接近100，说明窗口内最高点出现得越近。","optionExplanations":["100×(25−5)÷25=80。数值越接近100，说明窗口内最高点出现得越近。","20是距离占比（5÷25），方向读反了。","5只是根数，还要换算成0—100的分数。","只有最高点就是当前这根时才是100。"],"skills":["时间距离","刻度"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Aroon","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501801-aroon-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Aroon length 25; Aroon Up = 100 × (25 − bars since the window high) ÷ 25. If the window high was 5 bars ago, what is Aroon Up?","optionsEn":["80","20","5","100"],"explanationEn":"100 × (25 − 5) ÷ 25 = 80. The closer to 100, the more recent the window high.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 100 × (25 − 5) ÷ 25 = 80; values near 100 mean a recent high.","Wrong: 20 is the share of the distance (5 ÷ 25), read the wrong way.","Wrong: 5 is only the number of bars; it still needs converting to a 0–100 score.","Wrong: It is 100 only when the high is the current bar."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-23","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[44],"stem":"同一窗口内Aroon Up为80，Aroon Down为40。Aroon Oscillator是多少？如何理解？","options":["+40，高点比低点更近","120，表示两条线合计的强度","+40，表示价格上涨了40%","−40，表示下跌力量更强"],"answer":0,"explanation":"振荡器=Up−Down=80−40=+40。它比较高低点的新鲜程度，单位不是百分比收益。","optionExplanations":["正确：80−40=+40，比较高低点的新鲜程度。","错误：振荡器是两线之差，不是之和。","错误：Aroon读数不是收益率。","错误：减反了，应为Up减Down。"],"skills":["差值","含义边界"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Aroon Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773004-aroon-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"In the same window Aroon Up is 80 and Aroon Down 40. What is the Aroon Oscillator, and how should it be read?","optionsEn":["+40: the high is more recent than the low","120: the combined strength of the two lines","+40: price rose 40%","−40: downside force is stronger"],"explanationEn":"Oscillator = Up − Down = 80 − 40 = +40. It compares how recent the high and low are; it is not a percentage return.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 80 − 40 = +40, comparing how recent the high and low are.","Wrong: The oscillator is the difference of the two lines, not their sum.","Wrong: Aroon readings are not returns.","Wrong: This subtracts the wrong way; it is Up minus Down."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-28","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[45],"stem":"Vortex指标中VI+升到1.10，VI−降到0.92，VI+刚上穿VI−。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["1.10表示波动率为10%","向上运动相对较大，读数为比值","VI+为1.10，价格涨了10%","VI+上穿VI−是买入信号"],"answer":1,"explanation":"VI+与VI−都用真实波幅标准化，交叉说明两种方向运动的相对大小变化。","optionExplanations":["错误：VI+不是波动率百分比。","正确：VI用真实波幅标准化，交叉反映方向运动的相对大小。","错误：VI+是比值，不是涨幅。","错误：交叉只是线索，不能机械入场。"],"skills":["比值","交叉含义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Vortex Indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591352-vortex-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"In the Vortex indicator VI+ rises to 1.10 and VI− falls to 0.92; VI+ has just crossed above VI−. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["1.10 means volatility is 10%","Upward movement is relatively larger; the readings are ratios","VI+ at 1.10 means price rose 10%","VI+ crossing above VI− is a buy signal"],"explanationEn":"VI+ and VI− are both normalised by true range; the cross shows a change in the relative size of the two directions of movement.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: VI+ is not a volatility percentage.","Correct: VI is normalised by true range, and the cross reflects relative directional movement.","Wrong: VI+ is a ratio, not a gain.","Wrong: A cross is only a clue, not a mechanical entry."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-24","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[46],"stem":"Choppiness Index(14)=100×log10(14根真实波幅之和÷14根最高最低差)÷log10(14)。若14根真实波幅之和为28，区间最高减最低为7，读数约为多少？","options":["约25","4.0","约60.2","约52.5"],"answer":3,"explanation":"28÷7=4，log10(4)≈0.602，log10(14)≈1.146，100×0.602÷1.146≈52.5，介于常用38.2与61.8参考之间。读数衡量走势是否曲折，不指示方向。","optionExplanations":["25不是本题公式的结果，可能把比值倒过来理解了。","4只是比值，还需取对数并除以log10(14)。","60.2只做了log10(4)×100，漏掉除以log10(14)。","28÷7=4，log10(4)≈0.602，log10(14)≈1.146，100×0.602÷1.146≈52.5，介于常用38.2与61.8参考之间。读数衡量走势是否曲折，不指示方向。"],"skills":["对数公式","方向无关"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Choppiness Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501980-choppiness-index-chop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Choppiness Index(14) = 100 × log10(sum of 14 true ranges ÷ 14-bar high-to-low range) ÷ log10(14). If the true ranges sum to 28 and the range is 7, about what is the reading?","optionsEn":["About 25","4.0","About 60.2","About 52.5"],"explanationEn":"28 ÷ 7 = 4; log10(4) ≈ 0.602 and log10(14) ≈ 1.146, so 100 × 0.602 ÷ 1.146 ≈ 52.5, between the common 38.2 and 61.8 references. It measures how choppy the move is, not direction.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 25 is not what this formula gives; the ratio may have been inverted.","Wrong: 4 is only the ratio; it still needs the log and dividing by log10(14).","Wrong: 60.2 is only log10(4) × 100 and leaves out dividing by log10(14).","Correct: 100 × log10(4) ÷ log10(14) ≈ 52.5, between 38.2 and 61.8; it measures choppiness, not direction."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-29","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[47],"stem":"一目均衡表转换线（Tenkan-sen）=最近9根最高与最低的中点。若最近9根最高110、最低100，转换线是多少？","options":["105","9根收盘价的简单平均","110","10"],"answer":0,"explanation":"(110+100)÷2=105。转换线是区间中点，不是收盘价平均。","optionExplanations":["(110+100)÷2=105。转换线是区间中点，不是收盘价平均。","转换线使用最高和最低的中点，不使用收盘均值。","110是区间最高，不是中点。","10是区间宽度。"],"skills":["区间中点","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ichimoku Cloud","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589152-ichimoku-cloud/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Ichimoku conversion line (Tenkan-sen) is the midpoint of the highest high and lowest low of the last 9 bars. If the high is 110 and the low 100, what is it?","optionsEn":["105","The simple average of the 9 closes","110","10"],"explanationEn":"(110 + 100) ÷ 2 = 105. The conversion line is the range midpoint, not an average of closes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: (110 + 100) ÷ 2 = 105; it is the range midpoint.","Wrong: The conversion line uses the midpoint of high and low, not the average close.","Wrong: 110 is the range high, not the midpoint.","Wrong: 10 is the width of the range."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-25","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[48],"stem":"鳄鱼指标的Lips、Teeth、Jaw三条线互相缠绕并走平。下面哪项描述最合适？","options":["Jaw在最下方说明已出现买入信号","缠绕说明多头力量在积累，通常先涨","缠绕说明趋势不明，且线条带滞后","位移让线条提前反映未来价格"],"answer":2,"explanation":"三条平滑均线缠绕说明不同周期的平均价接近；位移设计让线条看起来更靠后。","optionExplanations":["错误：线的排列只是参考，不是自动买入信号。","错误：缠绕只表示没有明确趋势，方向未定。","正确：三条平滑均线缠绕，说明各周期平均价接近。","错误：位移使线条更靠后，并不能预测未来。"],"skills":["无趋势状态","位移"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Williams Alligator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592305-williams-alligator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Alligator’s Lips, Teeth and Jaw lines are intertwined and flat. Which description fits best?","optionsEn":["The Jaw at the bottom means a buy signal has appeared","Intertwining means bullish strength is building, so price usually rises first","Intertwining means no clear trend, and the lines lag","The offset lets the lines reflect future prices in advance"],"explanationEn":"Three smoothed averages intertwining means the average prices over different periods are close; the offset shifts the lines further back.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The order of the lines is only a reference, not an automatic buy signal.","Wrong: Intertwining only shows no clear trend; direction is undecided.","Correct: Three smoothed averages intertwining means the averages over different periods are close.","Wrong: The offset shifts the lines back and cannot predict the future."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-30","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[50],"stem":"ALMA常见设置为Length 9、Offset 0.85、Sigma 6。把Offset改为0.5，线条通常会怎样变化？","options":["权重中心移向中间，线更平滑更滞后","权重中心移向最新，线更贴近价格","窗口长度缩短一半，线反应更灵敏","只改变线向右位移的根数，数值不变"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Offset决定高斯权重的中心；0.85偏向近期，0.5居中，更少依赖最新价格。","optionExplanations":["正确：Offset决定高斯权重中心，0.5居中，较少依赖最新价格。","错误：Offset越接近1越贴近最新价格，0.5是居中。","错误：Offset不改变Length，窗口仍为9根。","错误：Offset是权重中心参数，不是图形位移。"],"skills":["权重分布","滞后"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Arnaud Legoux Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594683-arnaud-legoux-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A common ALMA setting is Length 9, Offset 0.85, Sigma 6. If Offset is changed to 0.5, how does the line usually change?","optionsEn":["The weighting centre moves to the middle, so the line is smoother and lags more","The weighting centre moves to the latest bar, so the line hugs price","The window is halved, so the line reacts faster","Only the number of bars the line is shifted right changes; the values stay the same"],"explanationEn":"Offset sets the centre of the Gaussian weights; 0.85 leans toward recent bars and 0.5 is centred, relying less on the latest price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Offset sets the Gaussian centre; 0.5 is centred and relies less on the latest price.","Wrong: The closer Offset is to 1, the closer the line hugs the latest price; 0.5 is centred.","Wrong: Offset does not change Length; the window is still 9 bars.","Wrong: Offset is the weighting centre, not a visual shift."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-26","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[51],"stem":"价格急速下跌后，McGinley Dynamic线仍明显落后于价格。最合理的解释是？","options":["计算出错，线本应紧贴价格","它仍是平滑线，急转时会滞后","落后说明价格多数会反弹回到线上","它只在价格上涨时才调整速度"],"answer":1,"explanation":"McGinley Dynamic减少了均线的固定滞后，但不能消除滞后。","optionExplanations":["错误：指标本身是平滑线，急转时落后是正常的。","正确：McGinley减少了固定滞后，但不能消除。","错误：落后是计算特性，不是反弹预告。","错误：它在两个方向都会自动调整。"],"skills":["自适应平滑","局限"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: McGinley Dynamic","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589175-mcginley-dynamic/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"After a sharp drop in price, the McGinley Dynamic line is still well behind price. What is the most reasonable explanation?","optionsEn":["It is miscalculated; the line should hug price","It is still a smoothed line, so it lags on sharp turns","Lagging behind means price will usually bounce back to the line","It adjusts its speed only when price is rising"],"explanationEn":"McGinley Dynamic reduces a moving average’s fixed lag but cannot remove lag.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It is a smoothed line, so lagging on sharp turns is normal.","Correct: McGinley reduces fixed lag but cannot remove it.","Wrong: Lag is a property of the calculation, not a forecast of a bounce.","Wrong: It adjusts automatically in both directions."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-31","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[52],"stem":"最近3根收盘依次为100、102、104，恰好在一条直线上。3期LSMA（最小二乘回归线在最新一根的值）是多少？同期SMA是多少？","options":["LSMA 104，SMA 102","LSMA 102，SMA 102","LSMA 106，SMA 102","LSMA 103，SMA 102"],"answer":0,"explanation":"回归线完全贴合这三点，在最新一根的值就是104；SMA是三者平均102。LSMA更贴近趋势末端。","optionExplanations":["回归线完全贴合这三点，在最新一根的值就是104；SMA是三者平均102。LSMA更贴近趋势末端。","LSMA取回归线末端值，不是均值。","106是把直线再外推一根，标准LSMA（Offset 0）不外推。","103不是这三点回归线在最新一根的值。"],"skills":["回归末端","与SMA区别"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Least Squares Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000599877-least-squares-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The last three closes are 100, 102 and 104, lying exactly on a straight line. What is the 3-period LSMA (the least-squares regression line’s value at the latest bar), and what is the SMA?","optionsEn":["LSMA 104, SMA 102","LSMA 102, SMA 102","LSMA 106, SMA 102","LSMA 103, SMA 102"],"explanationEn":"The regression line fits the three points exactly, so its value at the latest bar is 104; the SMA is their average, 102. LSMA sits closer to the end of the trend.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The line fits all three points, so LSMA is 104 and the SMA is 102.","Wrong: LSMA takes the line’s end value, not the mean.","Wrong: 106 extrapolates one more bar; standard LSMA with Offset 0 does not.","Wrong: 103 is not the regression line’s value at the latest bar."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-27","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[53],"stem":"在日线上画Linear Regression通道（上下线按标准差倍数放在回归线两侧）。新增几根K线后，整条通道的斜率和位置都改变了。原因是？","options":["只有上下轨会变，回归中线固定","通道变化说明趋势已经反转","标准差倍数自动调大，斜线因此改变","新数据进入窗口，整条通道会重算"],"answer":3,"explanation":"回归通道是对窗口数据的统计拟合，不是一次画定的固定线。","optionExplanations":["错误：中线是回归线，数据变了也会变。","错误：重新拟合引起的变化不等于趋势反转。","错误：倍数是固定设置，斜率变化来自回归重算。","正确：回归通道是对窗口数据的统计拟合，不是画定后固定的线。"],"skills":["滚动窗口","统计拟合"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Linear Regression","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644936-linear-regression/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"You draw a Linear Regression channel on the daily chart (bands at a multiple of standard deviation either side of the regression line). After a few new bars, the whole channel’s slope and position change. Why?","optionsEn":["Only the bands change; the middle regression line is fixed","The change shows the trend has reversed","The standard deviation multiple grows automatically, changing the slope","New data enters the window, so the whole channel is recalculated"],"explanationEn":"A regression channel is a statistical fit to the window’s data, not a line drawn once and fixed.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The middle line is a regression line and changes when the data changes.","Wrong: Changes from refitting are not a trend reversal.","Wrong: The multiple is a fixed setting; the slope change comes from refitting.","Correct: The channel is a statistical fit to the window, not a fixed drawing."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-32","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[57],"stem":"StochRSI(14)：最近14个RSI读数中最高70、最低40，当前RSI为55。按0—100刻度显示的原始StochRSI是多少？","options":["55","15","50","78.6"],"answer":2,"explanation":"100×(55−40)÷(70−40)=50。它描述RSI在自身近期范围中的位置，不是价格位置。","optionExplanations":["55是RSI本身，不是RSI在区间中的位置。","15只是55−40，没有除以RSI近期区间宽度30。","100×(55−40)÷(70−40)=50。它描述RSI在自身近期范围中的位置，不是价格位置。","78.6是55÷70，忽略了最低值40。"],"skills":["二次指标","刻度"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Stochastic RSI","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502333-stochastic-rsi-stoch-rsi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"StochRSI(14): over the last 14 RSI readings the high is 70 and the low 40, and current RSI is 55. On a 0–100 scale, what is the raw StochRSI?","optionsEn":["55","15","50","78.6"],"explanationEn":"100 × (55 − 40) ÷ (70 − 40) = 50. It shows where RSI sits within its own recent range, not where price sits.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 55 is RSI itself, not its position within the range.","Wrong: 15 is just 55 − 40, not divided by the range width of 30.","Correct: 100 × (55 − 40) ÷ (70 − 40) = 50, RSI’s position within its own range.","Wrong: 78.6 is 55 ÷ 70, which ignores the low of 40."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-28","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[58],"stem":"ConnorsRSI为三项的平均：价格RSI(3)、连涨连跌天数的RSI(2)、单日涨跌幅百分位(100)。若三项分别为80、60、40，ConnorsRSI是多少？","options":["180","80","40","60"],"answer":3,"explanation":"(80+60+40)÷3=60。三个组成部分衡量不同东西，先看分项再看合成值。","optionExplanations":["180是三项之和，还需取平均。","只取了价格RSI一项。","只取了百分位一项。","(80+60+40)÷3=60。三个组成部分衡量不同东西，先看分项再看合成值。"],"skills":["合成指标","分项"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Connors RSI","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502017-connors-rsi-crsi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"ConnorsRSI averages three parts: price RSI(3), RSI(2) of the up/down streak, and the 100-day percentile rank of the daily change. If the parts are 80, 60 and 40, what is ConnorsRSI?","optionsEn":["180","80","40","60"],"explanationEn":"(80 + 60 + 40) ÷ 3 = 60. The three parts measure different things, so read them before the composite.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 180 is the sum; it still needs averaging.","Wrong: This uses only the price RSI.","Wrong: This uses only the percentile.","Correct: (80 + 60 + 40) ÷ 3 = 60; read the parts before the composite."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-33","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[59],"stem":"某窗口内上涨幅度合计30，下跌幅度合计10。CMO是多少？同样数据的RSI式比值又是多少？","options":["CMO 75；RSI式读数50","CMO 20；RSI式读数75","CMO 50；RSI式读数75","CMO 50；RSI式读数50"],"answer":2,"explanation":"CMO=100×(30−10)÷(30+10)=50，范围−100到+100；RSI式=100−100÷(1+3)=75，范围0到100。","optionExplanations":["错误：把两个指标的结果对调了。","错误：只用了上涨减下跌，没有除以总和。","正确：CMO=100×20÷40=50，RSI式=100−100÷4=75。","错误：RSI式读数是上涨占比，应为75。"],"skills":["刻度","与RSI比较"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chande Momentum Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589109-chande-momentum-oscillator-cmo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"In a window, gains total 30 and losses total 10. What is CMO? What is the RSI-style ratio on the same data?","optionsEn":["CMO 75; RSI-style 50","CMO 20; RSI-style 75","CMO 50; RSI-style 75","CMO 50; RSI-style 50"],"explanationEn":"CMO = 100 × (30 − 10) ÷ (30 + 10) = 50, ranging from −100 to +100; RSI-style = 100 − 100 ÷ (1 + 3) = 75, ranging from 0 to 100.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The two results are swapped.","Wrong: This only subtracts losses from gains without dividing by the total.","Correct: CMO = 100 × 20 ÷ 40 = 50 and the RSI-style value = 100 − 100 ÷ 4 = 75.","Wrong: The RSI-style reading is the gains’ share, so it is 75."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-29","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[60],"stem":"True Strength Index=100×双重平滑的价格变化÷双重平滑的价格变化绝对值。若前者为0.6、后者为1.2，TSI是多少？","options":["TSI = 200","TSI = −50","TSI = 0.5","TSI = 50"],"answer":3,"explanation":"100×0.6÷1.2=50，表示平滑后的净变化约占总变化幅度的一半，方向偏上。","optionExplanations":["错误：把分子分母颠倒了。","错误：分子为正，结果不应为负。","错误：漏乘了100。","正确：100×0.6÷1.2=50。"],"skills":["双重平滑","比值"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: True Strength Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592290-true-strength-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"True Strength Index = 100 × double-smoothed price change ÷ double-smoothed absolute price change. If the first is 0.6 and the second 1.2, what is TSI?","optionsEn":["TSI = 200","TSI = −50","TSI = 0.5","TSI = 50"],"explanationEn":"100 × 0.6 ÷ 1.2 = 50: the smoothed net change is about half the total movement, leaning upward.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The numerator and denominator are swapped.","Wrong: The numerator is positive, so the result cannot be negative.","Wrong: This forgets to multiply by 100.","Correct: 100 × 0.6 ÷ 1.2 = 50."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-34","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[61],"stem":"TRIX从负值上穿零线。下面哪项描述最准确？","options":["三重平滑线由降转升，信号滞后","当天收盘价已高于前一天收盘价","三重平滑让它比原始价格更早转向","TRIX读数可当作下期收益率预测"],"answer":0,"explanation":"TRIX是三重EMA的变化率，零线代表平滑线由降转升，不等于当天价格上涨。","optionExplanations":["正确：TRIX是三重EMA的变化率，上穿零线代表平滑线转升。","错误：TRIX转正不等于当天价格上涨。","错误：平滑只会让信号更滞后。","错误：TRIX是历史变化率，不是预测值。"],"skills":["平滑与滞后","零线"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: TRIX","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502331-trix/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"TRIX crosses above zero from negative. Which description is most accurate?","optionsEn":["The triple-smoothed line has turned from falling to rising, with lag","Today’s close is above yesterday’s close","Triple smoothing makes it turn earlier than raw price","The TRIX reading can be used as a forecast of next period’s return"],"explanationEn":"TRIX is the rate of change of a triple EMA; crossing zero means the smoothed line turned up, not that price rose today.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: TRIX is the rate of change of a triple EMA, so crossing zero means the smoothed line turned up.","Wrong: TRIX turning positive does not mean price rose today.","Wrong: Smoothing only makes the signal lag more.","Wrong: TRIX is a historical rate of change, not a forecast."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-30","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[62],"stem":"终极振荡器用7、14、28三个窗口的买压比率A7、A14、A28，按4:2:1加权：UO=100×(4×A7+2×A14+A28)÷7。若A7=0.7、A14=0.6、A28=0.5，UO约为多少？","options":["UO约为4.50","UO约为64.3","UO约为60.0","UO约为70.0"],"answer":1,"explanation":"100×(2.8+1.2+0.5)÷7≈64.3。短窗口权重最大，所以结果偏向A7。","optionExplanations":["错误：漏掉了除以7和乘100。","正确：100×(2.8+1.2+0.5)÷7≈64.3。","错误：把三个比率做了简单平均，没按4:2:1加权。","错误：只取了最短窗口A7。"],"skills":["加权平均","多窗口"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ultimate Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502328-ultimate-oscillator-uo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Ultimate Oscillator weights buying-pressure ratios A7, A14 and A28 from three windows 4:2:1: UO = 100 × (4×A7 + 2×A14 + A28) ÷ 7. If A7 = 0.7, A14 = 0.6 and A28 = 0.5, about what is UO?","optionsEn":["About 4.50","About 64.3","About 60.0","About 70.0"],"explanationEn":"100 × (2.8 + 1.2 + 0.5) ÷ 7 ≈ 64.3. The short window has the most weight, so the result leans toward A7.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This leaves out dividing by 7 and multiplying by 100.","Correct: 100 × (2.8 + 1.2 + 0.5) ÷ 7 ≈ 64.3.","Wrong: This takes a simple average instead of weighting 4:2:1.","Wrong: This uses only the shortest window, A7."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-35","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[63],"stem":"Awesome Oscillator=中点价(最高+最低)÷2的5期SMA−34期SMA。若两者分别为105.0和103.5，AO是多少？","options":["104.25美元，两线的平均值","+1.5美元，单位同价格","−1.5美元，用34期减5期","+1.5%，以百分比表示"],"answer":1,"explanation":"105.0−103.5=+1.5美元。AO是两条平均线的价格差，单位跟随价格。","optionExplanations":["错误：AO是两线之差，不是平均值。","正确：105.0−103.5=+1.5美元。","错误：减数顺序反了。","错误：AO是价格差，不是百分比。"],"skills":["价格单位","快慢线差"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Awesome Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501826-awesome-oscillator-ao/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Awesome Oscillator = 5-period SMA minus 34-period SMA of the midpoint (high + low) ÷ 2. If they are 105.0 and 103.5, what is AO?","optionsEn":["$104.25, the average of the two lines","+$1.5, in price units","−$1.5, subtracting 5-period from 34-period","+1.5%, as a percentage"],"explanationEn":"105.0 − 103.5 = +$1.5. AO is the price difference between two averages, so its unit follows price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: AO is the difference, not the average.","Correct: 105.0 − 103.5 = +$1.5.","Wrong: The subtraction order is reversed.","Wrong: AO is a price difference, not a percentage."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-31","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[64],"stem":"某窗口最高120、最低100、收盘115。Stochastic原始%K为75。SMI（随机动量指数）在平滑前，按“(收盘−区间中点)÷区间一半×100”计算，原始值是多少？","options":["原始SMI为75","原始SMI为25","原始SMI为5","原始SMI为50"],"answer":3,"explanation":"中点110，收盘高出5，区间一半为10，100×5÷10=50。SMI以中点为0，范围约−100到+100。","optionExplanations":["错误：把SMI当成了随机%K。","错误：用整个区间20而不是一半10作分母。","错误：只算了距离5，漏除以区间一半并乘100。","正确：中点110，(115−110)÷10×100=50。"],"skills":["中点基准","与Stochastic区别"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Stochastic Momentum Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000707882-stochastic-momentum-index-smi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A window has a high of 120, a low of 100 and a close of 115; raw Stochastic %K is 75. Before smoothing, the SMI (Stochastic Momentum Index) is (close − range midpoint) ÷ half the range × 100. What is the raw value?","optionsEn":["Raw SMI 75","Raw SMI 25","Raw SMI 5","Raw SMI 50"],"explanationEn":"The midpoint is 110, the close is 5 above it, and half the range is 10, so 100 × 5 ÷ 10 = 50. SMI centres on the midpoint at 0 and runs about −100 to +100.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This treats SMI as Stochastic %K.","Wrong: This divides by the whole range of 20 instead of half, 10.","Wrong: This computes only the distance of 5, without dividing by half the range and multiplying by 100.","Correct: Midpoint 110, so (115 − 110) ÷ 10 × 100 = 50."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-36","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[65],"stem":"SMI Ergodic的主线与信号线都在零线上方，主线刚下穿信号线。较合理的解读是？","options":["价格已转为下跌趋势","主线低于信号线，净动量已为负","动量仍为正，但增速在放缓","主线下穿信号线是明确卖出信号"],"answer":2,"explanation":"零线上方说明净动量仍为正；下穿信号线说明增速放缓。","optionExplanations":["错误：主线仍在零线上方，动量仍为正。","错误：负值要看零线，不是看信号线。","正确：零线上方表示净动量为正，下穿信号线表示放缓。","错误：交叉只表示放缓，不是明确卖点。"],"skills":["零线","交叉含义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: SMI Ergodic Indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594669-smi-ergodic-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The SMI Ergodic main line and signal line are both above zero, and the main line has just crossed below the signal line. What is the more reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["Price has turned into a downtrend","The main line is below the signal line, so net momentum is negative","Momentum is still positive, but its growth is slowing","The main line crossing below the signal line is a clear sell signal"],"explanationEn":"Being above zero means net momentum is still positive; crossing below the signal line means it is slowing.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The main line is still above zero, so momentum is still positive.","Wrong: Negative values are judged against zero, not the signal line.","Correct: Above zero is positive net momentum, and crossing below the signal line shows slowing.","Wrong: The cross only shows slowing, not a clear sell point."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-32","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[66],"stem":"Relative Vigor Index的核心比值是(收盘−开盘)÷(最高−最低)。某根K线开盘100、收盘104、最高105、最低99。这一根的原始比值是多少？（正式指标还会做4根加权平滑）","options":["0.8","4","1.04","0.67"],"answer":3,"explanation":"(104−100)÷(105−99)=4÷6≈0.67，说明收盘相对开盘的推进占全天范围的三分之二。","optionExplanations":["0.8是4÷5，分母用错了。","4是实体长度，没有除以全天范围。","1.04是收盘÷开盘。","(104−100)÷(105−99)=4÷6≈0.67，说明收盘相对开盘的推进占全天范围的三分之二。"],"skills":["实体与范围","原始比值"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Relative Vigor Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591593-relative-vigor-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The core ratio of the Relative Vigor Index is (close − open) ÷ (high − low). A bar opens at 100, closes at 104, with a high of 105 and a low of 99. What is this bar’s raw ratio? (The full indicator also applies 4-bar weighted smoothing.)","optionsEn":["0.8","4","1.04","0.67"],"explanationEn":"(104 − 100) ÷ (105 − 99) = 4 ÷ 6 ≈ 0.67: the close’s advance from the open covers two thirds of the range.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 0.8 is 4 ÷ 5, using the wrong denominator.","Wrong: 4 is the body length, not divided by the range.","Wrong: 1.04 is close ÷ open.","Correct: (104 − 100) ÷ (105 − 99) ≈ 0.67, two thirds of the range."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-37","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[67],"stem":"Relative Volatility Index读数为70。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["上涨日的波动占比较大","价格位于近期区间的70%位置","近期价格的涨跌幅为70%","读数到70代表超买，价格将回落"],"answer":0,"explanation":"RVI的结构类似RSI，但把涨跌幅换成了标准差。","optionExplanations":["RVI的结构类似RSI，但把涨跌幅换成了标准差。","那是随机指标的含义。","RVI不输出涨跌幅。","70只是常用参考，不是反转开关。"],"skills":["波动方向","与RSI区别"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Relative Volatility Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594684-relative-volatility-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Relative Volatility Index reads 70. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["Volatility on up days makes up the larger share","Price sits at 70% of its recent range","Recent price changes were 70%","Reaching 70 means overbought, so price will fall"],"explanationEn":"RVI is built like RSI but uses standard deviation instead of price changes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: RVI is built like RSI but uses standard deviation instead of price changes.","Wrong: That is what a stochastic means.","Wrong: RVI does not output price changes.","Wrong: 70 is only a common reference, not a reversal switch."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-33","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[68],"stem":"最近9根收盘每一根都只比前一根高0.01。RCI(9)读数最可能是多少？","options":["接近+100，因为只比较排名","接近0，因为每根涨幅小到可以忽略","约+0.01，读数等于每根涨幅","约+50，因为只有一半名次与时间一致"],"answer":0,"explanation":"价格名次与时间先后完全一致，秩相关系数为+1，即+100。","optionExplanations":["正确：名次与时间完全一致，秩相关为+1。","错误：RCI只比较排名，不看涨幅大小。","错误：RCI不是涨幅，范围是−100到+100。","错误：每根都在上涨，名次完全一致。"],"skills":["排名","幅度无关"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Rank Correlation Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000765570-rank-correlation-index-rci/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Each of the last 9 closes is just 0.01 above the one before. What is RCI(9) most likely to read?","optionsEn":["Close to +100, because it compares only ranks","Close to 0, because each rise is negligibly small","About +0.01, equal to each bar’s gain","About +50, because only half the ranks match the time order"],"explanationEn":"The price ranks match the time order exactly, so the rank correlation is +1, or +100.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The ranks match the time order exactly, so the rank correlation is +1.","Wrong: RCI compares only ranks, not the size of gains.","Wrong: RCI is not a gain; it ranges from −100 to +100.","Wrong: Every bar rises, so the ranks match completely."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-38","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[69],"stem":"Fisher Transform从2.8回落并下穿触发线。下面哪项描述最恰当？","options":["下穿触发线说明价格已确认见顶","读数超过2通常就是行情最终顶部","价格已经下跌了约2.8%","极端读数后转向，动量转弱"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Fisher把价格位置做了非线性放大，常在极端处转折。","optionExplanations":["错误：下穿只是动量转弱的线索，不是确认见顶。","错误：极端读数可以持续，不一定是最终顶部。","错误：Fisher读数不是涨跌幅。","正确：Fisher放大价格位置，常在极端处转折。"],"skills":["非线性变换","阈值边界"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Fisher Transform","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589141-fisher-transform/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Fisher Transform falls back from 2.8 and crosses below its trigger line. Which description fits best?","optionsEn":["Crossing below the trigger confirms that price has topped","A reading above 2 usually marks the final top","Price has already fallen about 2.8%","It turned from an extreme reading, so momentum is weakening"],"explanationEn":"Fisher amplifies price position non-linearly and often turns at extremes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The cross is only a sign of weakening momentum, not a confirmed top.","Wrong: Extreme readings can persist and need not mark the final top.","Wrong: The Fisher reading is not a price change.","Correct: Fisher amplifies price position and often turns at extremes."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-34","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[70],"stem":"DPO(21)把价格与错位的21期SMA对齐，以去掉长期趋势。为什么它通常不适合当实时买卖信号？","options":["主要用来测周期；居中版最新几根没有读数","DPO去掉趋势后只剩噪声，读数通常接近零","DPO只适合月线，日线读数没有参考意义","DPO把价格前移后会提前出现信号，容易有假信号"],"answer":0,"explanation":"DPO的错位是为了看清循环长度：居中版本最新约11根没有读数，非居中版本虽有读数但仍滞后，所以它主要用来测周期，而不是在最新K线上发信号。","optionExplanations":["正确：DPO的错位为了看清循环长度，不适合最新K线信号。","错误：DPO保留循环成分，用来测周期。","错误：DPO可用于日线，问题不在周期。","错误：DPO是为了对齐历史，不是预测未来。"],"skills":["去趋势","位移"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Detrended Price Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502246-detrended-price-oscillator-dpo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","reviewed":"2026-10-30: wording fixed after blind re-solve","stemEn":"DPO(21) aligns price with a displaced 21-period SMA to remove the long-term trend. Why is it usually unsuitable as a real-time trade signal?","optionsEn":["It is mainly for measuring cycles; the centred version has no values for the latest bars","Once the trend is removed only noise remains, so readings are usually near zero","DPO only suits monthly charts; daily readings are meaningless","DPO shifts price forward, so signals appear early and are often false"],"explanationEn":"DPO’s displacement is meant to reveal cycle length: the centred version has no values for the latest 11 or so bars, and the non-centred version still lags, so it is mainly for measuring cycles rather than signalling on the latest bar.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: DPO’s displacement reveals cycle length, which makes it unsuitable for signals on the latest bar.","Wrong: DPO keeps the cyclical component and is used to measure cycles.","Wrong: DPO works on daily charts; the timeframe is not the problem.","Wrong: DPO aligns history; it does not predict the future."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-39","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[71],"stem":"KST把四个平滑后的ROC按1、2、3、4加权相加（周期越长权重越大）。若四项依次为2、1、1、0.5，KST是多少？","options":["KST = 13.5","KST = 4.5","KST = 9","KST = 1.125"],"answer":2,"explanation":"2×1+1×2+1×3+0.5×4=9。长周期ROC权重较大，所以KST更偏重中长期动量。","optionExplanations":["错误：把权重顺序反过来用了。","错误：只把四项相加，没乘权重。","正确：2×1+1×2+1×3+0.5×4=9。","错误：把加权和又除以了4。"],"skills":["加权求和","多周期"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Know Sure Thing","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502329-know-sure-thing-kst/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"KST adds four smoothed ROCs weighted 1, 2, 3 and 4 (longer periods get more weight). If the four values are 2, 1, 1 and 0.5, what is KST?","optionsEn":["KST = 13.5","KST = 4.5","KST = 9","KST = 1.125"],"explanationEn":"2×1 + 1×2 + 1×3 + 0.5×4 = 9. Longer ROCs carry more weight, so KST leans toward medium- and long-term momentum.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The weights are applied in reverse order.","Wrong: This just adds the four values without weights.","Correct: 2×1 + 1×2 + 1×3 + 0.5×4 = 9.","Wrong: This divides the weighted sum by 4."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-35","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[72],"stem":"一枚上市约3个月的币，在日线加载Pring Special K后出现空白或报错。最可能的原因是？","options":["Special K只适用于股票","需要很长历史，这枚币数据不足","日线太长，需改用小时线显示","币类资产没有成交量，无法计算"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Special K包含长周期成分，日线只有约90根时无法完成计算。","optionExplanations":["错误：指标适用性不取决于资产类别，问题在数据长度。","正确：Special K含长周期成分，约90根日线无法算完。","错误：周期不是问题，是历史数据长度不足。","错误：指标与是否有成交量无关。"],"skills":["历史长度","数据要求"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Pring's Special K","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773011-pring-s-special-k/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A coin listed about three months ago shows a blank chart or an error after adding Pring Special K on the daily chart. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["Special K works only on stocks","It needs a long history, and this coin does not have enough data","The daily timeframe is too long; switch to hourly","Coins have no volume, so it cannot be computed"],"explanationEn":"Special K includes long-period components that cannot be computed with only about 90 daily bars.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Suitability does not depend on asset class; the issue is data length.","Correct: Special K has long components that about 90 daily bars cannot fill.","Wrong: The timeframe is not the problem; the history is too short.","Wrong: The indicator does not use volume."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-40","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[73],"stem":"用社区版PMO（DecisionPoint公式，常见参数35/20/10）观察：PMO与信号线都在零上，PMO刚上穿信号线。较合理的解读是？","options":["各平台PMO公式相同，读数可直接互相比较","动量为正且在加强，但需核对脚本公式","PMO是成交量指标，上穿说明量能放大","上穿信号线说明价格接下来会继续上涨"],"answer":1,"explanation":"PMO是双重平滑的ROC。社区脚本参数和公式可能不同，结论要以核对后的实现为准。","optionExplanations":["错误：社区脚本参数和公式可能不同。","正确：PMO是双重平滑ROC，社区脚本可能不同。","错误：PMO由ROC平滑得到，与成交量无关。","错误：交叉只是动量线索，不是预测。"],"skills":["平滑ROC","实现核对"],"references":[{"title":"DecisionPoint: Using DecisionPoint Timing Signals to Improve your Portfolio","url":"https://articles.stockcharts.com/article/articles-decisionpoint-2016-09-using-decisionpoint-timing-signals-to-improve-your-portfolio/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Using a community PMO (DecisionPoint formula, common settings 35/20/10): PMO and its signal line are both above zero, and PMO has just crossed above the signal line. What is the more reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["All platforms use the same PMO formula, so readings are directly comparable","Momentum is positive and strengthening, but check the script’s formula","PMO is a volume indicator, so the cross means volume is expanding","Crossing above the signal line means price will keep rising"],"explanationEn":"PMO is a double-smoothed ROC. Community scripts may differ in settings and formula, so conclusions rest on the implementation you have checked.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Community scripts may use different settings and formulas.","Correct: PMO is a double-smoothed ROC, and community scripts may differ.","Wrong: PMO is smoothed ROC and has nothing to do with volume.","Wrong: The cross is a momentum clue, not a forecast."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-36","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[74],"stem":"科波克曲线原设计用于月线：WMA10(ROC14+ROC11)。曲线在零线下方开始回升。下面哪种说法最恰当？","options":["该信号在日线、周线、分钟线上同样可靠","零线下回升说明长期成交量正在放大","可作长期底部线索，不宜直接用于1分钟图","零线下回升表示价格已从低点上涨约14%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"科波克曲线是为月度长周期设计的，参数和周期一起改变才有意义。","optionExplanations":["错误：它为月线设计，不能照搬到短周期。","错误：科波克曲线由价格变化率构成，不含成交量。","正确：它为月线设计，参数和周期需一起改变。","错误：14是ROC周期，不是涨幅。"],"skills":["原始周期","滞后"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Coppock Curve","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589114-coppock-curve/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Coppock Curve was designed for monthly charts: WMA10(ROC14 + ROC11). The curve starts rising while below zero. Which statement is most appropriate?","optionsEn":["The signal is equally reliable on daily, weekly and minute charts","Rising below zero means long-term volume is expanding","It can be a clue to a long-term bottom, but should not be applied directly to a 1-minute chart","Rising below zero means price is about 14% off its low"],"explanationEn":"The Coppock Curve was built for monthly, long-horizon use; changing the timeframe makes sense only if the parameters change with it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It was designed for monthly charts and cannot be copied to short timeframes.","Wrong: The curve is built from price rates of change and has no volume.","Correct: It was built for monthly charts, and parameters must change with the timeframe.","Wrong: 14 is the ROC period, not a gain."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-41","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[75],"stem":"MACD-V=(EMA12−EMA26)÷ATR26×100（社区实现，需核对公式）。若EMA12−EMA26=3，ATR26=2，MACD-V是多少？","options":["150","1.5","6","300"],"answer":0,"explanation":"3÷2×100=150。它用波动率标准化MACD，便于不同价位和波动的资产比较。","optionExplanations":["3÷2×100=150。它用波动率标准化MACD，便于不同价位和波动的资产比较。","1.5是还没乘以100的比值。","6是3乘以2，方向用反了。","300是3×100，没有除以ATR。"],"skills":["波动率标准化","单位"],"references":[{"title":"Alex Spiroglou: MACD-V original paper","url":"https://www.naaim.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/MACD-V-Alex-Spiroglou-WEB.pdf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"MACD-V = (EMA12 − EMA26) ÷ ATR26 × 100 (a community implementation; check the formula). If EMA12 − EMA26 = 3 and ATR26 = 2, what is MACD-V?","optionsEn":["150","1.5","6","300"],"explanationEn":"3 ÷ 2 × 100 = 150. It normalises MACD by volatility, so assets at different prices and volatilities can be compared.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 3 ÷ 2 × 100 = 150; MACD normalised by volatility.","Wrong: 1.5 is the ratio before multiplying by 100.","Wrong: 6 multiplies 3 by 2, which is the wrong operation.","Wrong: 300 is 3 × 100 without dividing by ATR."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-37","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[76],"stem":"Mass Index(9,25)从低位升到27.3，随后回落到26.4。按经典“反转隆起”定义，这说明什么？","options":["出现反转隆起，但不提示方向","出现反转隆起，提示价格向上反转","读数超过27就是反向交易确认信号","27.3表示波动区间扩大27%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"经典定义是升破27再跌回26.5以下。方向需要结合价格判断。","optionExplanations":["正确：升破27后回落到26.5以下，方向需另看价格。","错误：指标只提示反转可能，不给方向。","错误：超过27只是隆起的一部分，还需回落确认。","错误：Mass Index不是百分比。"],"skills":["形态定义","方向无关"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Mass Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589169-mass-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Mass Index(9,25) rises from a low level to 27.3 and then falls back to 26.4. Under the classic “reversal bulge” definition, what does this show?","optionsEn":["A reversal bulge has formed, but it gives no direction","A reversal bulge has formed, pointing to an upward reversal","A reading above 27 is confirmation to trade the reverse","27.3 means the range has widened by 27%"],"explanationEn":"The classic definition is a rise above 27 followed by a drop below 26.5. Direction must come from price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Rising above 27 then falling below 26.5; direction must come from price.","Wrong: The indicator only flags a possible reversal, not its direction.","Wrong: Rising above 27 is only part of the bulge; the drop back confirms it.","Wrong: The Mass Index is not a percentage."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-42","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[77],"stem":"累积派发线（ADL）每根增量=成交量×[(收盘−最低)−(最高−收盘)]÷(最高−最低)。某根K线最高110、最低100、收盘108，成交量10,000。ADL增加多少？","options":["ADL增加+2,000","ADL增加+10,000","ADL增加+8,000","ADL增加+6,000"],"answer":3,"explanation":"位置系数=(8−2)÷10=0.6，增量=10,000×0.6=6,000。收盘越靠近最高价，计入的比例越大。","optionExplanations":["错误：只用了最高价与收盘价之差的比例。","错误：把整根成交量全部计入。","错误：只用了收盘距最低价的比例0.8。","正确：位置系数(8−2)÷10=0.6，10,000×0.6=6,000。"],"skills":["位置系数","成交量"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Accumulation/Distribution","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501979-chaikin-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Accumulation/Distribution Line adds volume × [(close − low) − (high − close)] ÷ (high − low) each bar. A bar has a high of 110, a low of 100 and a close of 108, on volume of 10,000. How much does the ADL rise?","optionsEn":["+2,000","+10,000","+8,000","+6,000"],"explanationEn":"The location factor = (8 − 2) ÷ 10 = 0.6, so the increment = 10,000 × 0.6 = 6,000. The closer the close is to the high, the larger the share counted.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This uses only the high-to-close proportion.","Wrong: This counts the whole bar’s volume.","Wrong: This uses only the close-to-low proportion of 0.8.","Correct: Location factor (8 − 2) ÷ 10 = 0.6, so 10,000 × 0.6 = 6,000."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-38","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[78],"stem":"CMF(20)=20根“资金流量”之和÷20根成交量之和。若资金流量合计30,000，成交量合计200,000，CMF是多少？","options":["CMF = 6.67","CMF = 0.15","CMF = −0.15","CMF = 15"],"answer":1,"explanation":"30,000÷200,000=0.15，表示收盘整体偏向各根区间的上半部；范围在−1到+1之间。","optionExplanations":["错误：把分子分母颠倒了。","正确：30,000÷200,000=0.15。","错误：资金流量合计为正，结果不应为负。","错误：CMF范围在−1到+1，不是百分数。"],"skills":["比值","范围"],"references":[{"title":"Chaikin Analytics: Chaikin Money Flow","url":"https://help.chaikinanalytics.com/knowledge-center/chaikin-money-flow"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"CMF(20) = sum of 20 bars’ money flow volume ÷ sum of 20 bars’ volume. If money flow volume totals 30,000 and volume 200,000, what is CMF?","optionsEn":["CMF = 6.67","CMF = 0.15","CMF = −0.15","CMF = 15"],"explanationEn":"30,000 ÷ 200,000 = 0.15: closes have leaned toward the upper half of their ranges overall; CMF runs from −1 to +1.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The numerator and denominator are swapped.","Correct: 30,000 ÷ 200,000 = 0.15.","Wrong: The money flow total is positive, so the result cannot be negative.","Wrong: CMF ranges from −1 to +1; it is not a percentage."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-43","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[79],"stem":"蔡金振荡器=ADL的3期EMA−ADL的10期EMA。若前者为5,000、后者为4,200，读数是多少？","options":["读数为−800","读数为1.19","读数为9,200","读数为+800"],"answer":3,"explanation":"5,000−4,200=+800，说明ADL短期平均高于长期平均。","optionExplanations":["错误：减数顺序反了。","错误：是两者相除，不是相减。","错误：是两者相加，不是相减。","正确：5,000−4,200=+800。"],"skills":["快慢差","ADL"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chaikin Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501979-chaikin-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Chaikin Oscillator = 3-period EMA of the ADL − 10-period EMA of the ADL. If they are 5,000 and 4,200, what is the reading?","optionsEn":["−800","1.19","9,200","+800"],"explanationEn":"5,000 − 4,200 = +800: the ADL’s short-term average is above its long-term average.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The subtraction order is reversed.","Wrong: This divides instead of subtracting.","Wrong: This adds instead of subtracting.","Correct: 5,000 − 4,200 = +800."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-39","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[80],"stem":"克林格振荡器上穿其信号线，但价格仍在下跌。较稳妥的解读是？","options":["KO上穿说明买方资金净流入","KO与价格背离，说明计算有误","量能趋势改善，但仍需价格确认","通常预示价格很快反转向上"],"answer":2,"explanation":"KO把成交量与价格方向结合，背离只是提醒，需要价格确认。","optionExplanations":["错误：KO是成交量趋势指标，不测净买入。","错误：背离是正常现象。","正确：KO背离只是提醒，需要价格确认。","错误：背离不等于立即反转。"],"skills":["背离","数据依赖"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Klinger Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589157-klinger-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Klinger Oscillator crosses above its signal line while price is still falling. What is the more prudent reading?","optionsEn":["KO crossing up means net buying inflows","KO diverging from price means it is miscalculated","The volume trend is improving, but price still needs to confirm","It usually means price will soon reverse up"],"explanationEn":"KO combines volume with price direction; a divergence is only a warning and needs price confirmation.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: KO is a volume-trend indicator and does not measure net buying.","Wrong: Divergence is normal.","Correct: A KO divergence is only a warning that needs price confirmation.","Wrong: Divergence does not mean an immediate reversal."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-44","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[81],"stem":"原始Elder力度指数=(本根收盘−前收)×本根成交量。前收50，本根收盘51，成交量20,000。原始读数是多少？","options":["原始读数为+20,000","原始读数为1,020,000","原始读数为−20,000","原始读数为+1"],"answer":0,"explanation":"(51−50)×20,000=20,000。同样涨1美元，成交量越大读数越大。","optionExplanations":["正确：(51−50)×20,000=20,000。","错误：用了收盘价而不是涨跌差。","错误：价格上涨，读数应为正。","错误：只算了价格变化，漏乘成交量。"],"skills":["价量乘积","符号"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Elder Force Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502259-elder-s-force-index-efi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Elder’s raw Force Index = (close − prior close) × volume. The prior close is 50, this bar closes at 51 on volume of 20,000. What is the raw reading?","optionsEn":["+20,000","1,020,000","−20,000","+1"],"explanationEn":"(51 − 50) × 20,000 = 20,000. For the same $1 rise, the bigger the volume, the bigger the reading.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: (51 − 50) × 20,000 = 20,000.","Wrong: This uses the close instead of the change.","Wrong: Price rose, so the reading is positive.","Wrong: This computes only the price change and forgets the volume."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-40","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[82],"stem":"两根K线中点价都上移2美元，但第二根的成交量是第一根的5倍，高低范围相同。简易波动指标（EMV）的读数谁更高？","options":["第二根更高，放量说明移动更有力","两者相同，因为中点上移相同","第一根更高，因为它出现得更早","第一根更高，同样上移用量更少"],"answer":3,"explanation":"EMV的分母包含成交量，量越大，同样价格移动对应的读数越小。","optionExplanations":["错误：EMV中量大反而使读数变小。","错误：EMV还除以成交量，量不同读数不同。","错误：读数取决于量与价格移动，与先后无关。","正确：EMV分母含成交量，量越大读数越小。"],"skills":["单位量移动","成交量方向"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ease of Movement","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502256-ease-of-movement-eom/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Two bars both move their midpoint up by $2 over the same high–low range, but the second has five times the first’s volume. Which has the higher Ease of Movement (EMV) reading?","optionsEn":["The second, because heavy volume means a stronger move","They are the same, because the midpoint moved the same","The first, because it came earlier","The first, because it made the same move on less volume"],"explanationEn":"EMV’s denominator includes volume, so more volume makes the same price move read lower.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: In EMV, more volume makes the reading smaller.","Wrong: EMV also divides by volume, so different volume gives different readings.","Wrong: The reading depends on volume and the price move, not order.","Correct: EMV’s denominator includes volume, so more volume lowers the reading."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-45","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[83],"stem":"今天成交量比昨天少，收盘上涨2%。正量指标（PVI）会怎样变化？","options":["保持不变，缩量日沿用前值","上升2%，因为收盘上涨了","按量比缩小后上升，升幅不足2%","下降2%，缩量上涨被视为乏力"],"answer":0,"explanation":"PVI的规则只处理放量日，缩量日直接沿用前值。","optionExplanations":["正确：PVI只在放量日更新，缩量日沿用前值。","错误：PVI缩量日不更新。","错误：PVI在缩量日完全沿用前值。","错误：PVI不会因缩量上涨而下降。"],"skills":["更新条件","规则"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Positive Volume Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773006-positive-volume-index-pvi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Today’s volume is lower than yesterday’s and the close is up 2%. How does the Positive Volume Index (PVI) change?","optionsEn":["It stays the same; on lower-volume days it carries the prior value","It rises 2%, because the close rose","It rises by less than 2%, scaled by the volume ratio","It falls 2%, because a rise on lower volume counts as weak"],"explanationEn":"PVI updates only on higher-volume days; on lower-volume days it carries the prior value.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: PVI updates only on higher-volume days and carries the prior value otherwise.","Wrong: PVI does not update on lower-volume days.","Wrong: PVI carries the prior value unchanged on lower-volume days.","Wrong: PVI does not fall because of a rise on lower volume."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-41","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[84],"stem":"负量指标（NVI）当前为1000。今天成交量比昨天少，收盘上涨2%。NVI变为多少？","options":["NVI变为1002","NVI变为1020","NVI变为980","NVI变为1000"],"answer":1,"explanation":"NVI只在缩量日更新：1000×(1+2%)=1020。放量日则保持不变。","optionExplanations":["错误：把2%当成了0.2%。","正确：1000×(1+2%)=1020。","错误：涨2%不应下降。","错误：1000是放量日（不更新）的规则，缩量日要更新。"],"skills":["更新条件","百分比"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Negative Volume Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773005-negative-volume-index-nvi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Negative Volume Index (NVI) is 1,000. Today’s volume is lower than yesterday’s and the close is up 2%. What does NVI become?","optionsEn":["1,002","1,020","980","1,000"],"explanationEn":"NVI updates only on lower-volume days: 1,000 × (1 + 2%) = 1,020. On higher-volume days it stays unchanged.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This treats 2% as 0.2%.","Correct: 1,000 × (1 + 2%) = 1,020.","Wrong: A 2% rise should not lower it.","Wrong: Staying at 1,000 is the rule for higher-volume days; on lower-volume days it updates."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-46","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[85],"stem":"均势指标原始值BOP=(收盘−开盘)÷(最高−最低)。某根K线开盘100、收盘103、最高105、最低99。BOP是多少？","options":["BOP为3","BOP为−0.5","BOP为0.5","BOP为0.6"],"answer":2,"explanation":"(103−100)÷(105−99)=3÷6=0.5，范围在−1到+1之间。","optionExplanations":["错误：只算收盘减开盘，没除以区间。","错误：收盘高于开盘，结果应为正。","正确：(103−100)÷(105−99)=3÷6=0.5。","错误：把分母用了最高价减开盘价。"],"skills":["实体比例","范围"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Balance of Power","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589100-balance-of-power-bop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The raw Balance of Power (BOP) = (close − open) ÷ (high − low). A bar opens at 100, closes at 103, with a high of 105 and a low of 99. What is BOP?","optionsEn":["3","−0.5","0.5","0.6"],"explanationEn":"(103 − 100) ÷ (105 − 99) = 3 ÷ 6 = 0.5; BOP ranges from −1 to +1.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This computes close minus open without dividing by the range.","Wrong: The close is above the open, so the result is positive.","Correct: (103 − 100) ÷ (105 − 99) = 3 ÷ 6 = 0.5.","Wrong: This uses high minus open as the denominator."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-42","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[87],"stem":"某TTM Squeeze脚本显示“挤压”状态：布林带上下轨都在肯特纳通道之内。这说明什么？","options":["成交量正在快速萎缩","不同脚本的挤压判定条件基本相同","价格大概率将向上突破","波动收缩，方向需另看"],"answer":3,"explanation":"挤压比较两种波动度量；结束挤压后的方向不由挤压本身决定。","optionExplanations":["错误：挤压比较的是布林带与肯特纳通道，与成交量无关。","错误：脚本参数和判定条件可能不同。","错误：挤压不提供突破方向。","正确：挤压只说明两种波动度量收缩，方向不由挤压决定。"],"skills":["波动收缩","实现差异"],"references":[{"title":"John Carter — Simpler Trading","url":"https://www.simplertrading.com/traders/john-carter/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A TTM Squeeze script shows a “squeeze”: both Bollinger Bands are inside the Keltner Channels. What does this show?","optionsEn":["Volume is shrinking fast","Different scripts use essentially the same squeeze condition","Price will probably break out upward","Volatility is contracting; direction must be judged separately"],"explanationEn":"The squeeze compares two volatility measures; the direction after it ends is not determined by the squeeze itself.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The squeeze compares Bollinger Bands with Keltner Channels and has nothing to do with volume.","Wrong: Scripts may use different settings and conditions.","Wrong: The squeeze does not give a breakout direction.","Correct: The squeeze only shows contraction in two volatility measures; it sets no direction."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-47","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[88],"stem":"溃疡指数=√(窗口内各根回撤百分比平方的平均)。若三根的回撤依次为0%、−3%、−4%，读数约为多少？","options":["约2.89","约2.33","4","约8.33"],"answer":0,"explanation":"(0+9+16)÷3≈8.33，开方≈2.89。平方让较深回撤占更大权重。","optionExplanations":["(0+9+16)÷3≈8.33，开方≈2.89。平方让较深回撤占更大权重。","2.33是回撤绝对值的简单平均，没有平方再开方。","4是最大回撤，不是溃疡指数。","8.33还没有开方。"],"skills":["回撤","平方平均"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ulcer Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773115-ulcer-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Ulcer Index = √(mean of the squared percentage drawdowns in the window). If three bars’ drawdowns are 0%, −3% and −4%, about what is the reading?","optionsEn":["About 2.89","About 2.33","4","About 8.33"],"explanationEn":"(0 + 9 + 16) ÷ 3 ≈ 8.33, and its square root ≈ 2.89. Squaring gives deeper drawdowns more weight.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: (0 + 9 + 16) ÷ 3 ≈ 8.33 and √8.33 ≈ 2.89; squaring weights deeper drawdowns.","Wrong: 2.33 is the simple average of the absolute drawdowns, without squaring and rooting.","Wrong: 4 is the maximum drawdown, not the Ulcer Index.","Wrong: 8.33 has not been square-rooted yet."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-43","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[90],"stem":"钱德克罗止损先计算“p根最高价−x倍ATR”的初始止损，再取最近q根初始止损中的最高值。为什么它通常比只用“最高价−ATR”更平稳？","options":["q越大，止损越贴近当前价","再取q根最高值，过滤单根波动","它不再用ATR，只看最高价","它按收盘价而非最高价算，更平稳"],"answer":1,"explanation":"两步结构让止损线只在新的较高初始止损出现时上移。","optionExplanations":["错误：取更长的最高值会使止损更滞后，不是更贴近。","正确：初始止损只在更高的值出现时上移。","错误：它仍使用x倍ATR。","错误：钱德止损基于最高价。"],"skills":["两步结构","平滑"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chande Kroll Stop","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589105-chande-kroll-stop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Chande Kroll Stop first computes an initial stop of “p-bar highest high − x × ATR”, then takes the highest initial stop of the last q bars. Why is it usually steadier than just “high − ATR”?","optionsEn":["A larger q keeps the stop closer to the current price","Taking the highest of q bars filters out single-bar swings","It no longer uses ATR, only the high","It uses the close instead of the high, so it is steadier"],"explanationEn":"The two-step structure moves the stop up only when a higher initial stop appears.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Taking the highest over a longer span makes the stop lag more, not hug price.","Correct: The stop moves up only when a higher initial value appears.","Wrong: It still uses x × ATR.","Wrong: The Chande Kroll Stop is based on the high."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-48","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[91],"stem":"多头ATR跟踪止损：止损=收盘−3×ATR，且只上移不下移。上一根收盘100、ATR 2，止损为94。本根收盘98、ATR仍为2。新的止损是多少？","options":["止损上移到98，贴着收盘","止损上移到96","止损仍为94","止损下移到92"],"answer":2,"explanation":"新候选值98−6=92低于94；跟踪止损只上移不下移，所以保持94。","optionExplanations":["错误：止损应为收盘减3×ATR，而不是收盘本身。","错误：没有依据，应在候选值高于94时才上移。","正确：候选值92低于94，跟踪止损只上移不下移。","错误：跟踪止损不会下移。"],"skills":["只升不降","倍数"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volatility Stop methods","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594676-volatility-stop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A long ATR trailing stop: stop = close − 3 × ATR, moving only up, never down. Last bar closed at 100 with ATR 2, so the stop is 94. This bar closes at 98 with ATR still 2. What is the new stop?","optionsEn":["It moves up to 98, right at the close","It moves up to 96","It stays at 94","It moves down to 92"],"explanationEn":"The new candidate 98 − 6 = 92 is below 94; a trailing stop moves only up, so it stays at 94.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The stop is the close minus 3 × ATR, not the close itself.","Wrong: There is no basis for this; it moves up only when the candidate exceeds 94.","Correct: The candidate of 92 is below 94, and a trailing stop moves only up.","Wrong: A trailing stop does not move down."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-44","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[92],"stem":"某平台的Volatility Stop在收盘跌破多头止损线后，把线翻到价格上方。较稳妥的理解是？","options":["规则方向已翻转，需核对触发价","翻转说明平台调高了ATR倍数","翻到上方说明价格接下来多数会继续下跌","各平台都用盘中最低价触发，无需核对"],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同实现的触发条件可能不同，读信号前要看说明。","optionExplanations":["正确：不同实现的触发条件可能不同。","错误：倍数是设置，不会因翻转自动调整。","错误：翻转是规则状态，不是预测。","错误：不同实现的触发价可能是收盘价或盘中价。"],"skills":["规则翻转","实现差异"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volatility Stop","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594676-volatility-stop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"On one platform, Volatility Stop flips the line above price after a close below the long stop line. What is the more prudent understanding?","optionsEn":["The rule’s direction has flipped; check what price triggered it","The flip means the platform raised the ATR multiple","Flipping above means price will usually keep falling","Every platform triggers on the intraday low, so there is nothing to check"],"explanationEn":"Different implementations may use different triggers, so read the documentation before reading the signal.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Different implementations may trigger differently.","Wrong: The multiple is a setting and does not change because of a flip.","Wrong: A flip is a rule state, not a forecast.","Wrong: Implementations may trigger on the close or on intraday prices."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-49","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[93],"stem":"从财报日锚定VWAP。锚点后第一段典型价100、成交量1000；第二段典型价104、成交量3000。锚定VWAP是多少？","options":["103","102","104","101"],"answer":0,"explanation":"(100×1000+104×3000)÷4000=412,000÷4000=103。量大的104权重更大。","optionExplanations":["(100×1000+104×3000)÷4000=412,000÷4000=103。量大的104权重更大。","102是两个价格的简单平均。","只取了量大的那段价格。","101不是本题的加权结果。"],"skills":["锚点","成交量加权"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Anchored VWAP drawing tool","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000669764-anchored-vwap-drawing-tool/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"An anchored VWAP starts at an earnings date. After the anchor, the first segment has a typical price of 100 on volume of 1,000; the second, 104 on volume of 3,000. What is the anchored VWAP?","optionsEn":["103","102","104","101"],"explanationEn":"(100 × 1,000 + 104 × 3,000) ÷ 4,000 = 412,000 ÷ 4,000 = 103. The heavier 104 segment carries more weight.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: (100 × 1,000 + 104 × 3,000) ÷ 4,000 = 103; the heavier segment carries more weight.","Wrong: 102 is the simple average of the two prices.","Wrong: This takes only the heavier segment’s price.","Wrong: 101 is not the weighted result here."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-45","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[94],"stem":"前一交易日最高110、最低100、收盘105。标准枢轴点P=(最高+最低+收盘)÷3，R1=2P−最低，S1=2P−最高。三者分别是多少？","options":["P 105，R1 115，S1 95","P 105，R1 100，S1 110","P 107.5，R1 115，S1 100","P 105，R1 110，S1 100"],"answer":3,"explanation":"P=315÷3=105，R1=210−100=110，S1=210−110=100。枢轴点是根据前一周期计算的参考价位。","optionExplanations":["错误：把R1、S1当成P±10。","错误：把R1和S1对调了。","错误：P用了高低价平均，R1用错了。","正确：P=315÷3=105，R1=210−100=110，S1=210−110=100。"],"skills":["公式","前一周期"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Pivot formulas and examples","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/v4/essential/drawings/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Yesterday’s high was 110, low 100 and close 105. Standard pivots: P = (high + low + close) ÷ 3, R1 = 2P − low, S1 = 2P − high. What are the three?","optionsEn":["P 105, R1 115, S1 95","P 105, R1 100, S1 110","P 107.5, R1 115, S1 100","P 105, R1 110, S1 100"],"explanationEn":"P = 315 ÷ 3 = 105, R1 = 210 − 100 = 110, S1 = 210 − 110 = 100. Pivots are reference levels computed from the prior period.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This treats R1 and S1 as P ± 10.","Wrong: R1 and S1 are swapped.","Wrong: P uses the high–low average and R1 is wrong.","Correct: P = 105, R1 = 210 − 100 = 110, S1 = 210 − 110 = 100."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-50","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[97],"stem":"最新一根K线的最高价是近期最高，却还没有出现威廉分形标记。原因最可能是？","options":["平台漏画了标记，需要刷新才会显示","近期高点要先回调到20期均线才算分形","分形需右侧两根确认，标记会延迟","分形只在下跌后的低点出现，不标记高点"],"answer":2,"explanation":"分形需要中间那根两侧各有两根作比较，最新一根右侧还没有数据。","optionExplanations":["错误：这是分形的正常延迟。","错误：分形只比较相邻K线，与均线无关。","正确：最新一根右侧还没有数据，无法确认。","错误：分形有向上和向下两种。"],"skills":["确认延迟","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Williams fractal indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591663-williams-fractal-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The latest bar’s high is the highest recently, but no Williams fractal marker has appeared. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["The platform missed the marker; refresh to show it","A recent high must first pull back to the 20-period average to count as a fractal","A fractal needs two bars on the right to confirm, so the marker is delayed","Fractals mark only lows after declines, not highs"],"explanationEn":"A fractal compares the middle bar with two bars on each side; the latest bar has no data to its right yet.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This is the fractal’s normal delay.","Wrong: Fractals compare neighbouring bars and have nothing to do with moving averages.","Correct: The latest bar has nothing to its right yet, so it cannot be confirmed.","Wrong: There are both up and down fractals."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-51","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[1],"stem":"同一只股票，在日线和1小时图上各加一条SMA(20)。下面哪项正确？","options":["日线取20根日K，小时图取20根小时K","两条线都取最近20个交易日的收盘价","小时图只取每个交易日最后一小时的收盘价","小时图自动按20天换算，两线数值相近"],"answer":0,"explanation":"SMA的Length是根数：日线上是20个交易日，小时图上是20个小时。","optionExplanations":["正确：SMA的Length按根数，不按天数。","错误：小时图的20是20根小时K。","错误：SMA取连续最近20根，不筛选。","错误：平台不会自动换算周期。"],"skills":["周期","参数含义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Simple Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000696841-simple-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"For the same stock, you add an SMA(20) on the daily chart and on the 1-hour chart. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["The daily uses 20 daily bars; the hourly uses 20 hourly bars","Both lines use the last 20 trading days’ closes","The hourly uses only the last hour’s close of each trading day","The hourly converts automatically to 20 days, so the two lines are close"],"explanationEn":"SMA length counts bars: 20 trading days on the daily chart, 20 hours on the hourly chart.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: SMA length is in bars, not days.","Wrong: On the hourly chart 20 means 20 hourly bars.","Wrong: SMA takes the latest 20 consecutive bars without filtering.","Wrong: Platforms do not convert periods automatically."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-52","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[2],"stem":"价格横盘许久后突然连续上涨。同为20期的EMA和SMA，通常哪条先拐头向上？为什么？","options":["SMA，因为它等权对待每根K线","EMA，因为近期价格权重更大","两者同时拐头，因为周期都是20","EMA，因为它的窗口实际只有几根"],"answer":1,"explanation":"EMA给近期价格更大权重，旧价格影响逐渐衰减，所以通常先转弯。","optionExplanations":["错误：等权重使SMA对新价格反应更慢。","正确：EMA对近期价格更敏感，通常先转弯。","错误：权重不同，转弯时点不同。","错误：EMA用全部历史但权重递减，窗口并非很短。"],"skills":["权重","滞后"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Moving Averages","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502589-moving-averages/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"After a long sideways stretch, price suddenly rises several bars in a row. Of a 20-period EMA and a 20-period SMA, which usually turns up first, and why?","optionsEn":["The SMA, because it weights every bar equally","The EMA, because recent prices carry more weight","Both turn at the same time, since both are 20-period","The EMA, because its window is really only a few bars"],"explanationEn":"The EMA gives recent prices more weight while older prices fade, so it usually turns first.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Equal weights make the SMA slower to react to new prices.","Correct: The EMA is more sensitive to recent prices and usually turns first.","Wrong: Their weights differ, so they turn at different times.","Wrong: The EMA uses all history with decaying weights; its window is not short."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-53","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[3],"stem":"20期线性WMA的权重是1、2、…、20（最新一根为20）。最新一根收盘在WMA里的权重占比约是多少？同期SMA里又是多少？","options":["约5%；约5%","约9.52%；约5%","约9.52%；约10%","约20%；约5%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"权重总和1+2+…+20=210，最新一根占20÷210≈9.52%；SMA每根都是1÷20=5%。","optionExplanations":["错误：WMA最新一根权重大于平均权重。","正确：20÷210≈9.52%，SMA每根1÷20=5%。","错误：SMA每根占比是1/20，即5%。","错误：误把20当成权重占比。"],"skills":["权重计算","WMA与SMA"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Weighted Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594680-weighted-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"A 20-period linear WMA uses weights 1, 2, …, 20 (the latest bar gets 20). About what share of the WMA does the latest close carry? What share does it carry in the SMA?","optionsEn":["About 5%; about 5%","About 9.52%; about 5%","About 9.52%; about 10%","About 20%; about 5%"],"explanationEn":"The weights sum to 1 + 2 + … + 20 = 210, so the latest bar carries 20 ÷ 210 ≈ 9.52%; in the SMA each bar is 1 ÷ 20 = 5%.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The WMA’s latest bar carries more than the average weight.","Correct: 20 ÷ 210 ≈ 9.52%, and each SMA bar is 1 ÷ 20 = 5%.","Wrong: Each SMA bar carries 1/20, i.e. 5%.","Wrong: This treats the weight of 20 as a percentage."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-46","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[4],"stem":"某指标（例如RSI）的设置里有“Smoothing: SMMA (RMA)”选项。它最可能表示什么？","options":["在主图上叠加一条按收盘价算的均线","说明二者算法相同，只是名字不同","把这个指标的周期改为14根","对指标数值再平滑，未必是价格均线"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：其他指标设置里的SMMA(RMA)通常是对该指标数值再平滑，不一定是价格均线。","optionExplanations":["错误：它作用于指标输出，不是价格。","错误：RMA与SMA算法并不相同。","错误：它是平滑方法选项，不是周期。","正确：其他指标设置里的SMMA(RMA)通常是平滑该指标数值。"],"skills":["设置辨认","RMA"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Smoothed Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591343-smoothed-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"An indicator’s settings (RSI, for example) include an option “Smoothing: SMMA (RMA)”. What does it most likely mean?","optionsEn":["Overlay a moving average of closes on the main chart","The two are the same algorithm under different names","Change the indicator’s period to 14 bars","Smooth the indicator’s values further; it is not necessarily a price average"],"explanationEn":"In other indicators’ settings, SMMA (RMA) usually smooths that indicator’s values, not price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It acts on the indicator’s output, not on price.","Wrong: RMA and SMA are different algorithms.","Wrong: It is a smoothing-method option, not a period.","Correct: In other indicators’ settings, SMMA (RMA) usually smooths that indicator’s values."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-54","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[5],"stem":"VWMA(20)和日内会话VWAP都用成交量加权。两者最主要的区别是什么？","options":["VWMA滚动取20根；VWAP从起点累计","二者算法相同，只是不同平台的叫法不同","VWMA用典型价加权，VWAP只用收盘价","VWMA从起点累计，VWAP滚动20根"],"answer":0,"explanation":"VWMA滚动取最近N根；会话VWAP从选定起点一路累计，到新会话重新开始。","optionExplanations":["正确：VWMA是滚动窗口，会话VWAP累计到新会话重置。","错误：二者窗口方式不同。","错误：差别在窗口方式，不在价格类型。","错误：说反了。"],"skills":["窗口","VWAP与VWMA"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Volume-Weighted Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592293-volume-weighted-moving-average-vwma/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"VWMA(20) and a session VWAP both weight by volume. What is the main difference between them?","optionsEn":["VWMA rolls over 20 bars; VWAP accumulates from a starting point","They use the same algorithm under different platform names","VWMA weights typical price, while VWAP uses only closes","VWMA accumulates from a starting point; VWAP rolls over 20 bars"],"explanationEn":"VWMA rolls over the latest N bars; a session VWAP accumulates from a chosen start and resets at a new session.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: VWMA is a rolling window, while session VWAP accumulates and resets each session.","Wrong: Their windows work differently.","Wrong: The difference is the window, not the price type.","Wrong: This is the reverse."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-47","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[6],"stem":"HMA(n)的常见算法是：先算WMA(n/2)×2−WMA(n)，再对这串结果做一次WMA。HMA(16)最后这一步WMA用多少根？","options":["最后一步WMA取2根（最短的WMA）","最后一步WMA取8根（16÷2）","最后一步WMA取4根（√16）","最后一步WMA取16根（n本身）"],"answer":2,"explanation":"最后一步的长度是√n，16的平方根为4。","optionExplanations":["错误：最后一步取√n，而不是最短的。","错误：8是中间WMA的长度，不是最后一步。","正确：最后一步长度是√n，√16=4。","错误：16是原始WMA的长度。"],"skills":["公式结构","HMA"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Hull Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589149-hull-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"A common HMA(n) algorithm computes 2 × WMA(n/2) − WMA(n), then takes a WMA of that series. For HMA(16), how many bars does that final WMA use?","optionsEn":["2 bars (the shortest WMA)","8 bars (16 ÷ 2)","4 bars (√16)","16 bars (n itself)"],"explanationEn":"The final step uses √n bars; the square root of 16 is 4.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The final step uses √n, not the shortest length.","Wrong: 8 is the intermediate WMA’s length, not the final step.","Correct: The final step uses √n, and √16 = 4.","Wrong: 16 is the original WMA’s length."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-55","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[7],"stem":"DEMA=2×EMA−EMA(EMA)。某时刻EMA(20)=105，它的再平滑EMA=102。DEMA是多少？","options":["103.5","105","108","207"],"answer":2,"explanation":"2×105−102=108。DEMA可以超出第一层EMA，这来自公式而不是平台画错。","optionExplanations":["103.5是两者平均，不是DEMA公式。","105只是第一层EMA。","2×105−102=108。DEMA可以超出第一层EMA，这来自公式而不是平台画错。","207漏减了第二层EMA。"],"skills":["计算","DEMA"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Double Exponential Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589132-double-exponential-moving-average-ema/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"DEMA = 2 × EMA − EMA(EMA). At one moment EMA(20) = 105 and its re-smoothed EMA = 102. What is DEMA?","optionsEn":["103.5","105","108","207"],"explanationEn":"2 × 105 − 102 = 108. DEMA can go beyond the first EMA; that comes from the formula, not a platform drawing error.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 103.5 is the average of the two, not the DEMA formula.","Wrong: 105 is only the first EMA.","Correct: 2 × 105 − 102 = 108; going beyond the first EMA comes from the formula.","Wrong: 207 forgets to subtract the second EMA."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-56","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[8],"stem":"TEMA=3×E1−3×E2+E3（E1为EMA，E2为E1的EMA，E3为E2的EMA）。若E1=105、E2=103、E3=102，TEMA是多少？","options":["103.33","105","110","108"],"answer":3,"explanation":"3×105−3×103+102=108。","optionExplanations":["103.33是三者的简单平均。","105只是第一层EMA。","110来自把E3也减掉的错误组合。","3×105−3×103+102=108。"],"skills":["计算","TEMA"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Triple EMA","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591346-triple-ema/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"TEMA = 3 × E1 − 3 × E2 + E3 (E1 is the EMA, E2 the EMA of E1, E3 the EMA of E2). If E1 = 105, E2 = 103 and E3 = 102, what is TEMA?","optionsEn":["103.33","105","110","108"],"explanationEn":"3 × 105 − 3 × 103 + 102 = 108.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 103.33 is the simple average of the three.","Wrong: 105 is only the first EMA.","Wrong: 110 comes from wrongly subtracting E3 as well.","Correct: 3 × 105 − 3 × 103 + 102 = 108."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-57","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[9],"stem":"MA9在第30根K线收盘时上穿MA21（金叉）。下面哪项描述最准确？","options":["近21根均价高于近9根均价，信号通常领先于价格","收盘价高于近9根与近21根均价，信号通常滞后","近9根成交量高于近21根成交量，信号通常领先","近9根均价高于近21根均价，信号通常滞后于价格"],"answer":3,"explanation":"交叉只比较两段平均价，平均价要等价格先动才会改变，所以有滞后。","optionExplanations":["错误：金叉是短均线(9)上穿长均线(21)，方向弄反了，且均线信号是滞后的。","错误：金叉比较的是两条均线之间的位置，而不是收盘价与均线。","错误：均线交叉比较的是价格均值，不是成交量。","正确：交叉只比较两段平均价，均价要等价格先动才变，所以有滞后。"],"skills":["交叉含义","滞后"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — MA Cross","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000599879-ma-cross/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"MA9 crosses above MA21 (a golden cross) at the close of bar 30. Which description is most accurate?","optionsEn":["The 21-bar average is above the 9-bar average, and the signal usually leads price","The close is above both the 9-bar and 21-bar averages, and the signal usually lags","The 9-bar volume is above the 21-bar volume, and the signal usually leads","The 9-bar average is above the 21-bar average, and the signal usually lags price"],"explanationEn":"A cross only compares two average prices, and averages change only after price moves first, so it lags.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A golden cross is the short (9) average crossing above the long (21); the direction is reversed, and MA signals lag.","Wrong: A golden cross compares the two averages, not the close with the averages.","Wrong: A moving-average cross compares average prices, not volume.","Correct: A cross compares two average prices, which change only after price moves, so it lags."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-58","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[10],"stem":"均线带用SMA 10、20、40、80。四条线从上到下依次是SMA10、20、40、80，并一起向上。较准确的描述是？","options":["短期均价都高于长期均价，各周期方向一致","四条均线相互独立验证，上涨概率约为单线四倍","均线排列整齐，说明价格未来会继续上涨","成交量同步放大，说明买方资金持续流入"],"answer":0,"explanation":"短线在上、长线在下且同向，说明近期和较长期价格方向一致。","optionExplanations":["正确：短线在上、长线在下且同向，说明各周期近期价格方向一致。","错误：四条线都由同一组价格算出，不是独立证据，概率不会成倍增加。","错误：排列只描述已发生的价格关系，不能保证未来走势。","错误：均线只用价格计算，排列不反映成交量。"],"skills":["排列","非独立证据"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Moving Average Ribbon","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644913-moving-average-ribbon/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"A ribbon uses SMAs of 10, 20, 40 and 80. From top to bottom the lines are SMA10, 20, 40, 80, and they all rise together. What is the more accurate description?","optionsEn":["Short-term averages are above long-term ones, and all periods point the same way","Four averages confirm each other independently, so a rise is about four times as likely as with one","The orderly stack shows price will keep rising","Volume is expanding too, showing steady buying inflows"],"explanationEn":"Short averages above long ones, all moving the same way, means recent and longer-term prices agree in direction.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Short above long, all moving together, means the periods agree in direction.","Wrong: All four come from the same prices, so they are not independent and the odds do not multiply.","Wrong: The stack only describes past price relationships and guarantees nothing.","Wrong: Moving averages use only price, so the stack says nothing about volume."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-59","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[13],"stem":"TradingView内置Stochastic(14,3,3)显示两条线。其中%D是什么？","options":["RSI在最近14个读数高低范围中的位置","最近3根K线的收盘位置，是较快的那条线","KDJ指标里比K、D更敏感的那条J线","%K再取3期平均，是较慢的那条线"],"answer":3,"explanation":"%K经过平滑后再取3期平均就是%D，比%K更慢。","optionExplanations":["错误：这是StochRSI的思路，不是Stochastic的%D。","错误：%D是较慢的信号线，不是更快的线。","错误：J线属于KDJ指标，TradingView内置Stochastic没有J线。","正确：%D是%K的3期平均，比%K更慢更平滑。"],"skills":["设置辨认","K与D"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Stochastic","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502332-stochastic-stoch/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"TradingView’s built-in Stochastic(14,3,3) shows two lines. What is %D?","optionsEn":["Where RSI sits within its last 14 readings’ range","The close’s position over the last 3 bars, the faster line","The J line in KDJ, more sensitive than K and D","A 3-period average of %K, the slower line"],"explanationEn":"%D is a 3-period average of the smoothed %K, so it is slower than %K.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is the idea behind StochRSI, not Stochastic %D.","Wrong: %D is the slower signal line, not the faster one.","Wrong: The J line belongs to KDJ; TradingView’s built-in Stochastic has none.","Correct: %D is a 3-period average of %K, slower and smoother."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-60","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[14],"stem":"Williams %R(14)读数为−5。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["收盘靠近最近14根高低区间的底部","读数接近0，表示价格处于超卖区域","收盘靠近最近14根高低区间的顶部","价格在最近14根里下跌了5%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"%R刻度为0到−100，越接近0越靠近区间顶部。","optionExplanations":["错误：−100附近才是区间底部，−5接近顶部。","错误：接近0是靠近顶部（常被视为超买区），超卖在接近−100一侧。","正确：%R刻度0到−100，越接近0越靠近区间顶部。","错误：%R不是涨跌幅，而是收盘在区间中的位置。"],"skills":["刻度","位置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Williams %R","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501985-williams-r-r/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Williams %R(14) reads −5. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["The close is near the bottom of the last 14 bars’ range","A reading near 0 means price is oversold","The close is near the top of the last 14 bars’ range","Price fell 5% over the last 14 bars"],"explanationEn":"%R runs from 0 to −100; the closer to 0, the closer to the top of the range.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The bottom of the range is near −100; −5 is near the top.","Wrong: Near 0 is near the top (often seen as overbought); oversold is near −100.","Correct: %R runs from 0 to −100, and near 0 is near the top of the range.","Wrong: %R is not a price change but the close’s position in the range."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-48","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[15],"stem":"CCI=(典型价−典型价均值)÷(0.015×平均偏差)。某时刻典型价106，20期典型价均值100，平均偏差4。CCI是多少？","options":["150","6","100","1.5"],"answer":2,"explanation":"(106−100)÷(0.015×4)=6÷0.06=100。","optionExplanations":["150把平均偏差误当成了2.67。","6只是典型价与均值之差，还没标准化。","(106−100)÷(0.015×4)=6÷0.06=100。","1.5漏乘了常数的倒数。"],"skills":["计算","标准化"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Commodity Channel Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502001-commodity-channel-index-cci/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"CCI = (typical price − its mean) ÷ (0.015 × mean deviation). At one moment the typical price is 106, the 20-period mean of typical price is 100 and the mean deviation is 4. What is CCI?","optionsEn":["150","6","100","1.5"],"explanationEn":"(106 − 100) ÷ (0.015 × 4) = 6 ÷ 0.06 = 100.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 150 treats the mean deviation as 2.67.","Wrong: 6 is only the typical price minus the mean, not yet normalised.","Correct: (106 − 100) ÷ (0.015 × 4) = 6 ÷ 0.06 = 100.","Wrong: 1.5 leaves out the reciprocal of the constant."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-61","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[16],"stem":"ROC(10)从+8%降到+3%，同期价格仍在创新高。较准确的描述是？","options":["价格仍比10根前高，只是涨幅在缩小","价格比10根前下跌了3%，趋势已经反转","价格仍高于10根前，且涨幅正在扩大","价格已低于10根前，开始转为下跌"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ROC下降但为正，表示比10根前高但涨得没那么多；旧的大波动离开窗口也会让读数下降。","optionExplanations":["正确：ROC为正表示高于10根前，数值下降表示涨得没那么多。","错误：+3%表示上涨3%，不是下跌。","错误：ROC从8%降到3%，涨幅是在缩小而不是扩大。","错误：ROC仍为+3%，说明仍高于10根前。"],"skills":["正负含义","基数效应"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Rate of Change","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502343-rate-of-change-roc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"ROC(10) falls from +8% to +3% while price is still making new highs. What is the more accurate description?","optionsEn":["Price is still above where it was 10 bars ago; the gain is just shrinking","Price is 3% below 10 bars ago, and the trend has reversed","Price is still above 10 bars ago, and the gain is widening","Price is now below 10 bars ago and is turning down"],"explanationEn":"A falling but positive ROC means price is above 10 bars ago but rising less; a big old move leaving the window can also lower the reading.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A positive ROC means above 10 bars ago, and a falling value means the gain is smaller.","Wrong: +3% is a 3% gain, not a fall.","Wrong: ROC fell from 8% to 3%, so the gain is shrinking, not widening.","Wrong: ROC is still +3%, so price is still above 10 bars ago."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-62","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[17],"stem":"差值版Momentum(10)=现价−10根前收盘。现价48，10根前收盘50。读数是多少？","options":["−4%（百分比写法）","−2（价格单位）","+2（价格单位）","0.96（比值写法）"],"answer":1,"explanation":"48−50=−2，单位与价格相同。","optionExplanations":["−4%是ROC的写法，差值版用价格单位。","48−50=−2，单位与价格相同。","方向反了。","0.96是比值写法，不是差值版。"],"skills":["公式版本","单位"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Momentum","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589187-momentum/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Difference-based Momentum(10) = current price − close 10 bars ago. The current price is 48 and the close 10 bars ago was 50. What is the reading?","optionsEn":["−4% (percentage form)","−2 (price units)","+2 (price units)","0.96 (ratio form)"],"explanationEn":"48 − 50 = −2, in the same units as price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: −4% is how ROC is written; the difference version uses price units.","Correct: 48 − 50 = −2, in price units.","Wrong: The direction is reversed.","Wrong: 0.96 is the ratio form, not the difference version."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-49","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[18],"stem":"资产A价格约10元，资产B约1000元，两者MACD(12,26)都为0.5。改用PPO比较，结论是？","options":["B的价格更高，PPO中B的动能更大","A的MACD占价格比例大，PPO中A高于B","两者PPO相同，因为MACD数值都是0.5","两者PPO都约为0.5%，与价格高低无关"],"answer":1,"explanation":"PPO=差值÷慢线×100：A约5%，B约0.05%，相对动能A大得多。","optionExplanations":["错误：价格越高，同样差值占的比例越小，B的PPO更小。","正确：PPO把差值除以慢线，A约5%，B约0.05%。","错误：PPO会按价格归一化，价格不同结果就不同。","错误：PPO需要除以慢线价格，数值不会直接等于0.5%。"],"skills":["跨资产比较","百分比"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Percentage Price Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502346-percentage-price-oscillator-ppo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Asset A trades around 10 and asset B around 1,000, and both have a MACD(12,26) of 0.5. Comparing with PPO instead, what is the conclusion?","optionsEn":["B’s price is higher, so its PPO momentum is larger","A’s MACD is a bigger share of its price, so A’s PPO is above B’s","Their PPOs are equal, because both MACD values are 0.5","Both PPOs are about 0.5%, regardless of price"],"explanationEn":"PPO = difference ÷ slow line × 100: about 5% for A and 0.05% for B, so A’s relative momentum is far larger.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The higher the price, the smaller the same difference is in percentage terms, so B’s PPO is smaller.","Correct: PPO divides by the slow line, about 5% for A and 0.05% for B.","Wrong: PPO normalises by price, so different prices give different results.","Wrong: PPO divides by the slow line’s price, so it is not simply 0.5%."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-63","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[19],"stem":"MFI与RSI都在0—100之间。MFI多用了什么信息？","options":["典型价和成交量","高低价差和涨跌幅","收盘价和成交笔数","典型价和持仓量"],"answer":0,"explanation":"MFI用典型价×成交量，按典型价升降分组，所以把量也算进来。","optionExplanations":["正确：MFI用典型价×成交量，所以比RSI多用了量。","错误：MFI按典型价升降分组，并乘上成交量。","错误：MFI用典型价和成交量，不用成交笔数。","错误：MFI用的是成交量，不是期货持仓量。"],"skills":["输入","量价"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Money Flow Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502348-money-flow-mfi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"MFI and RSI both run from 0 to 100. What extra information does MFI use?","optionsEn":["Typical price and volume","High–low range and percentage change","Close and number of trades","Typical price and open interest"],"explanationEn":"MFI uses typical price × volume, grouped by whether the typical price rose or fell, so it brings volume in.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: MFI uses typical price × volume, so it uses volume where RSI does not.","Wrong: MFI groups by rising or falling typical price and multiplies by volume.","Wrong: MFI uses typical price and volume, not the number of trades.","Wrong: MFI uses volume, not futures open interest."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-64","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[20],"stem":"TradingView内置Bull Bear Power只显示一条线（Bull Power与Bear Power之和）。某根最高104、最低98、EMA13为100，读数是多少？","options":["+2","+4","−2","+6"],"answer":0,"explanation":"(104−100)+(98−100)=+2。","optionExplanations":["正确：(104−100)+(98−100)=+2。","错误：+4只是Bull Power，漏加了Bear Power。","错误：−2只是Bear Power，漏加了Bull Power。","错误：把两项取了绝对值相加，Bear Power应为负。"],"skills":["内置版本","计算"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bull Bear Power","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000717955-bull-bear-power/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"TradingView’s built-in Bull Bear Power shows a single line (Bull Power plus Bear Power). A bar has a high of 104, a low of 98 and EMA13 of 100. What is the reading?","optionsEn":["+2","+4","−2","+6"],"explanationEn":"(104 − 100) + (98 − 100) = +2.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: (104 − 100) + (98 − 100) = +2.","Wrong: +4 is only Bull Power, leaving out Bear Power.","Wrong: −2 is only Bear Power, leaving out Bull Power.","Wrong: This adds absolute values; Bear Power should be negative."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-65","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[22],"stem":"布林带上轨104、下轨96、中轨100。BandWidth=(上轨−下轨)÷中轨。读数是多少？","options":["8，即上下轨相差8美元","1.04，即上轨相对中轨的倍数","0.08，即上下轨差占中轨8%","0.04，即只算上轨到中轨"],"answer":2,"explanation":"(104−96)÷100=0.08；平台常按百分比显示为8。","optionExplanations":["错误：BandWidth要再除以中轨，不是价格差本身。","错误：BandWidth是宽度占中轨的比例，不是上轨÷中轨。","正确：(104−96)÷100=0.08。","错误：BandWidth用上轨减下轨，不是只算一侧。"],"skills":["计算","单位"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bollinger BandWidth","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501972-bollinger-bandwidth-bbw/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Bollinger Bands: upper 104, lower 96, middle 100. BandWidth = (upper − lower) ÷ middle. What is the reading?","optionsEn":["8, the bands are $8 apart","1.04, the upper band as a multiple of the middle","0.08, the gap between the bands is 8% of the middle","0.04, counting only the upper band to the middle"],"explanationEn":"(104 − 96) ÷ 100 = 0.08; platforms often show it as 8 in percentage terms.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: BandWidth divides by the middle band; it is not the price gap itself.","Wrong: BandWidth is the width relative to the middle, not upper ÷ middle.","Correct: (104 − 96) ÷ 100 = 0.08.","Wrong: BandWidth uses upper minus lower, not one side."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-66","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[23],"stem":"布林带%B读数为−0.2。下面哪项正确？","options":["收盘在下轨之下约0.2个带宽","价格在这段时间下跌了20%","未来价格下跌的概率是20%","收盘位于中轨与下轨之间的位置"],"answer":0,"explanation":"%B小于0表示收在下轨之外；−0.2即低于下轨约0.2个带宽。","optionExplanations":["%B小于0表示收在下轨之外；−0.2即低于下轨约0.2个带宽。","%B是位置，不是涨跌幅。","%B不是概率。","中轨与下轨之间对应0到0.5。"],"skills":["位置","越轨"],"references":[{"title":"John Bollinger — %b companion indicator","url":"https://www.bollingerbands.com/bollinger-bands"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Bollinger %B reads −0.2. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["The close is about 0.2 band-widths below the lower band","Price fell 20% over this period","There is a 20% probability that price will fall","The close lies between the middle and lower bands"],"explanationEn":"%B below 0 means the close is outside the lower band; −0.2 is about 0.2 band-widths below it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: %B below 0 is outside the lower band; −0.2 is about 0.2 band-widths below it.","Wrong: %B is a position, not a price change.","Wrong: %B is not a probability.","Wrong: Between the middle and lower bands corresponds to 0 to 0.5."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-67","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[24],"stem":"Donchian通道(20)上轨112、下轨100。中线是多少？","options":["最近20根收盘的平均值，无法由上下轨得出","106","112","100"],"answer":1,"explanation":"(112+100)÷2=106。","optionExplanations":["唐奇安中线是上下轨的中点，不是收盘均值。","(112+100)÷2=106。","112是上轨。","100是下轨。"],"skills":["定义","中点"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Donchian Channels","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502253-donchian-channels-dc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"A Donchian Channel(20) has an upper band of 112 and a lower band of 100. What is the middle line?","optionsEn":["The average of the last 20 closes, which cannot be derived from the bands","106","112","100"],"explanationEn":"(112 + 100) ÷ 2 = 106.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The Donchian middle line is the midpoint of the bands, not an average of closes.","Correct: (112 + 100) ÷ 2 = 106.","Wrong: 112 is the upper band.","Wrong: 100 is the lower band."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-50","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[25],"stem":"肯特纳通道与布林带都在均线两侧画线。两者宽度的来源有什么不同？","options":["两者都按ATR定宽，只是中线均线类型不同","肯特纳按ATR定宽，布林带按收盘价标准差定宽","肯特纳按收盘价标准差定宽，布林带按ATR定宽","肯特纳按固定百分比定宽，布林带按ATR定宽"],"answer":1,"explanation":"肯特纳通道宽度=倍数×ATR；布林带宽度=倍数×收盘标准差。","optionExplanations":["错误：布林带用标准差，不用ATR。","正确：肯特纳宽度=倍数×ATR，布林带宽度=倍数×收盘价标准差。","错误：两者说反了。","错误：固定百分比是包络线的做法，布林带用标准差。"],"skills":["宽度算法","比较"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Keltner Channels","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502266-keltner-channels-kc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Keltner Channels and Bollinger Bands both draw lines on either side of a moving average. Where does each one’s width come from?","optionsEn":["Both set width with ATR; only the middle average differs","Keltner uses ATR; Bollinger uses the standard deviation of closes","Keltner uses the standard deviation of closes; Bollinger uses ATR","Keltner uses a fixed percentage; Bollinger uses ATR"],"explanationEn":"Keltner width = multiplier × ATR; Bollinger width = multiplier × standard deviation of closes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Bollinger Bands use standard deviation, not ATR.","Correct: Keltner width = multiple × ATR and Bollinger width = multiple × standard deviation of closes.","Wrong: The two are reversed.","Wrong: A fixed percentage is how envelopes work; Bollinger uses standard deviation."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-68","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[26],"stem":"市场波动突然扩大一倍，但SMA20水平不变。包络线(SMA20，±3%)的宽度会怎样？","options":["变宽一些，因为均线会先平滑部分波动","变窄，因为价格偏离均线时通道会向中线收缩","不变，因为宽度固定为中线价格的±3%","变宽到两倍，因为通道会跟随波动自动放大"],"answer":2,"explanation":"包络线宽度固定为中线的±3%，不随波动自动调整。","optionExplanations":["错误：宽度只取决于中线水平和固定百分比。","错误：包络线没有这种收缩机制。","正确：包络线宽度固定为中线的±3%，不随波动调整。","错误：包络线不跟随波动，宽度只由固定百分比决定。"],"skills":["固定宽度","与布林带区别"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Envelope","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502260-envelope-env/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Market volatility suddenly doubles, but SMA20 stays level. What happens to the width of an envelope (SMA20, ±3%)?","optionsEn":["A little wider, because the average first smooths part of the volatility","Narrower, because the channel shrinks toward the middle when price strays","Unchanged, because the width is fixed at ±3% of the middle price","Twice as wide, because the channel scales with volatility automatically"],"explanationEn":"An envelope’s width is fixed at ±3% of the middle line and does not adjust to volatility.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Width depends only on the middle level and the fixed percentage.","Wrong: Envelopes have no such shrinking mechanism.","Correct: The width is fixed at ±3% of the middle line and does not adjust to volatility.","Wrong: Envelopes do not follow volatility; width comes only from the fixed percentage."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-69","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[28],"stem":"某资产ATR(14)=1.5，最新收盘60。ATR%是多少？","options":["0.025%","40%","2.5%","1.5%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"1.5÷60=0.025，即2.5%。","optionExplanations":["错误：忘记把0.025乘以100换算成百分比。","错误：把除法颠倒成60÷1.5。","正确：1.5÷60=0.025，即2.5%。","错误：把ATR数值直接当成百分比。"],"skills":["计算","单位换算"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — ATR and ATR% screening","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501823-average-true-range-atr/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"An asset’s ATR(14) is 1.5 and its latest close is 60. What is ATR%?","optionsEn":["0.025%","40%","2.5%","1.5%"],"explanationEn":"1.5 ÷ 60 = 0.025, i.e. 2.5%.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This forgets to multiply 0.025 by 100 to get a percentage.","Wrong: The division is reversed to 60 ÷ 1.5.","Correct: 1.5 ÷ 60 = 0.025, i.e. 2.5%.","Wrong: This uses the ATR value directly as a percentage."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-70","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[29],"stem":"日线上14日ADR为5美元，今天已经走出6美元的高低差。下面哪项正确？","options":["ADR是均值而非上限，今天范围仍可能继续扩大","今天范围超过ADR，说明明天的范围通常小于5美元","ADR随当天数据即时更新，读数随即变成6美元","今天范围超过ADR，说明价格大概率很快反向回落"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：已走出一倍ADR不代表一定停止。","optionExplanations":["正确：已走出一倍ADR不代表一定停止。","错误：今天的范围不能直接预测明天的范围。","错误：ADR是14日平均，单日数据只会小幅改变它。","错误：ADR不是反转信号，范围超过后仍可能扩大。"],"skills":["平均不是上限","解读"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Average Daily Range","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000695003-average-daily-range-adr-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"On the daily chart the 14-day ADR is $5, and today has already moved $6 from high to low. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["ADR is an average, not a ceiling; today’s range can keep expanding","Today exceeded ADR, so tomorrow’s range is usually under $5","ADR updates instantly with today’s data and now reads $6","Today exceeded ADR, so price will probably reverse soon"],"explanationEn":"Covering one full ADR does not mean the move has to stop.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Covering one full ADR does not mean the move has to stop.","Wrong: Today’s range cannot directly forecast tomorrow’s.","Wrong: ADR is a 14-day average; one day changes it only a little.","Wrong: ADR is not a reversal signal; the range can still expand."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-71","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[30],"stem":"某资产20期标准差从1.2升到2.4。下面哪项正确？","options":["近20期收盘更分散，读数本身不指示方向","近20期波动加大，读数升高通常预示价格下跌","近20期涨幅扩大到原来两倍，说明趋势向上","价格之后大概率留在均值±2.4的范围之内"],"answer":0,"explanation":"标准差变大表示近期收盘更分散，涨跌都可能造成。","optionExplanations":["正确：标准差只衡量分散程度，涨跌都可能使其升高。","错误：标准差升高与方向无关，上涨加速也会升高。","错误：标准差翻倍只表示分散度翻倍，不是涨幅翻倍。","错误：标准差描述已发生的分散，不是未来的保证区间。"],"skills":["离散程度","无方向"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bollinger Bands and price standard deviation","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501840-bollinger-bands-bb/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"An asset’s 20-period standard deviation rises from 1.2 to 2.4. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["The last 20 closes are more spread out; the reading itself gives no direction","Volatility has increased, and a higher reading usually precedes a fall","The 20-period gain has doubled, showing an uptrend","Price will probably stay within ±2.4 of the mean from now on"],"explanationEn":"A larger standard deviation means recent closes are more dispersed, which rises or falls can cause.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Standard deviation measures only dispersion, which rises or falls can increase.","Wrong: Standard deviation has no direction; an accelerating rally raises it too.","Wrong: Doubling means dispersion doubled, not the gain.","Wrong: Standard deviation describes past dispersion, not a guaranteed future range."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-51","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[31],"stem":"某资产日对数收益率标准差为1%，按252个交易日年化，历史波动率约为多少？","options":["19.10%","15.87%","252%","0.06%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"年化通常乘√252≈15.87，所以1%×15.87≈15.87%。","optionExplanations":["错误：这是按365天√365计算，题目指定252个交易日。","正确：1%×√252≈15.87%。","错误：直接乘252是线性相加，波动按平方根时间缩放。","错误：把乘法误作除以√252。"],"skills":["年化","平方根"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Historical Volatility","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589145-historical-volatility/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"An asset’s daily log-return standard deviation is 1%. Annualised over 252 trading days, about what is historical volatility?","optionsEn":["19.10%","15.87%","252%","0.06%"],"explanationEn":"Annualising usually multiplies by √252 ≈ 15.87, so 1% × 15.87 ≈ 15.87%.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This uses √365; the question specifies 252 trading days.","Correct: 1% × √252 ≈ 15.87%.","Wrong: Multiplying by 252 adds linearly; volatility scales with the square root of time.","Wrong: This divides by √252 instead of multiplying."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-72","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[32],"stem":"同一个币在两家交易所的成交量柱高度相差很大。最可能的原因是？","options":["成交量本应相同，差异多来自数据延迟","每张图只统计所选交易所或市场的成交量","纵轴自动缩放不同，实际成交量多半相同","其中一家交易所的成交数据有误，应以高者为准"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：成交量来自所选市场，不同交易所的量不等于全市场总量。","optionExplanations":["错误：各交易所成交本就不同，不是延迟造成。","正确：不同交易所的量不等于全市场总量。","错误：差异来自统计范围，不是纵轴缩放。","错误：两家数据可以都是准确的，只是统计范围不同。"],"skills":["数据来源","单位"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Volume","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591617-volume/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The same coin’s volume bars differ greatly in height on two exchanges. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["Volume should be the same; the difference mostly comes from data delays","Each chart counts only the selected exchange’s or market’s volume","The vertical axes scale differently; actual volume is probably the same","One exchange’s data is wrong; trust the higher one"],"explanationEn":"Volume comes from the selected market; one exchange’s volume is not the whole market’s.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Exchanges genuinely trade different amounts; it is not a delay.","Correct: One exchange’s volume is not the whole market’s.","Wrong: The difference comes from scope, not axis scaling.","Wrong: Both can be accurate; they just cover different scopes."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-73","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[33],"stem":"过去20根的平均成交量为5万，本根已收盘成交量为12万。普通RVOL是多少？","options":["0.42倍","2.4倍","7万","1.2倍"],"answer":1,"explanation":"12÷5=2.4倍。","optionExplanations":["那是5÷12，方向反了。","12÷5=2.4倍。","7万是两者之差，不是相对倍数。","1.2倍漏了一位。"],"skills":["计算","基准"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Relative Volume calculation","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000635874-how-do-we-calculate-relative-volume-and-relative-volume-at-time/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Average volume over the last 20 bars is 50,000, and the bar that just closed traded 120,000. What is ordinary RVOL?","optionsEn":["0.42×","2.4×","70,000","1.2×"],"explanationEn":"120,000 ÷ 50,000 = 2.4×.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is 50 ÷ 120, the wrong way round.","Correct: 120,000 ÷ 50,000 = 2.4×.","Wrong: 70,000 is the difference, not a ratio.","Wrong: 1.2× is off by a factor of two."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-74","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[34],"stem":"两天的数据：第1天收盘上涨0.1%、成交100万；第2天收盘下跌5%、成交80万。OBV两天合计变化多少？","options":["−80万，以跌幅大的一天为准","+100万，只计上涨日的量","−4.9万，按涨跌幅给量加权","+20万，只看涨跌方向"],"answer":3,"explanation":"+100万−80万=+20万；即便第2天跌幅大得多，OBV仍上升，这正是它忽略幅度的特点。","optionExplanations":["错误：OBV是逐日累加，不会只取跌幅大的一天。","错误：下跌日的量也要减去。","错误：按涨跌幅加权的是PVT，不是OBV。","正确：+100万−80万=+20万，OBV不看涨跌幅大小。"],"skills":["计算","OBV局限"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — On Balance Volume","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502593-on-balance-volume-obv/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Two days of data: day 1 closes up 0.1% on volume of 1 million; day 2 closes down 5% on volume of 800,000. What is OBV’s total change over the two days?","optionsEn":["−800,000, following the day with the bigger move","+1 million, counting only the up day","−49,000, weighting volume by the size of the move","+200,000, looking only at direction"],"explanationEn":"+1,000,000 − 800,000 = +200,000; even though day 2 fell much more, OBV still rises, because it ignores the size of moves.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: OBV accumulates every day; it does not just take the bigger day.","Wrong: Down-day volume is also subtracted.","Wrong: Weighting by the size of the move is PVT, not OBV.","Correct: +1,000,000 − 800,000 = +200,000; OBV ignores the size of moves."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-52","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[35],"stem":"某根K线收盘只比前收高0.1%，但成交量是平时的10倍。OBV和PVT的反应有何不同？","options":["PVT加全部成交量，OBV只加其中0.1%","两者都加全部成交量，因为这根K线收涨","两者都只加其中0.1%，因为涨幅很小","OBV加全部成交量，PVT只加其中0.1%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"OBV上涨日加全量；PVT按涨跌百分比乘成交量，所以微涨只贡献很小一部分。","optionExplanations":["错误：两者说反了。","错误：只有OBV加全量，PVT按涨跌百分比加权。","错误：OBV不看涨幅大小，涨日加全量。","正确：OBV涨日加全量；PVT按涨幅比例乘量。"],"skills":["OBV与PVT","比较"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Price Volume Trend","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502345-price-volume-trend-pvt/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"A bar closes only 0.1% above the prior close, but on ten times normal volume. How do OBV and PVT respond differently?","optionsEn":["PVT adds all the volume, OBV only 0.1% of it","Both add all the volume, because the bar closed up","Both add only 0.1% of it, because the gain is small","OBV adds all the volume, PVT only 0.1% of it"],"explanationEn":"OBV adds the full volume on up days; PVT multiplies volume by the percentage change, so a tiny gain contributes very little.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The two are reversed.","Wrong: Only OBV adds the full volume; PVT weights by the percentage change.","Wrong: OBV ignores the size of the gain and adds the full volume on up days.","Correct: OBV adds the full volume on up days; PVT scales volume by the gain."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-75","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[36],"stem":"价格大跌的同时，PVO急升到+60%。正确的理解是？","options":["短期成交量低于长期均量，说明抛压正在衰竭","短期成交量高于长期均量，说明买方明显占优","短期成交量高于长期均量，读数不指示方向","价格变化高于长期均值，说明下跌将继续"],"answer":2,"explanation":"PVO比较短期与长期成交量均值；恐慌卖出同样会放量。","optionExplanations":["错误：PVO大幅为正说明近期量更高，而不是更低。","错误：放量不分买卖方向，价格大跌时放量多是卖出。","正确：PVO比较短期与长期成交量均值，恐慌卖出同样会放量。","错误：PVO衡量的是成交量，不是价格变化。"],"skills":["无方向","成交量"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Percentage Volume Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591350-percentage-volume-oscillator-pvo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"As price drops sharply, PVO jumps to +60%. What is the correct understanding?","optionsEn":["Short-term volume is below the long-term average, showing selling pressure is fading","Short-term volume is above the long-term average, showing buyers clearly dominate","Short-term volume is above the long-term average; the reading gives no direction","Price change is above its long-term average, showing the decline will continue"],"explanationEn":"PVO compares short- and long-term average volume; panic selling also lifts volume.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A large positive PVO means recent volume is higher, not lower.","Wrong: Volume has no buy or sell direction; heavy volume in a sharp drop is mostly selling.","Correct: PVO compares short- and long-term average volume, and panic selling also lifts it.","Wrong: PVO measures volume, not price change."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-76","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[37],"stem":"加密货币24小时交易，但图上的VWAP在UTC 0点突然从头起算。最可能的原因是？","options":["VWAP每满24根K线就自动重新起算","UTC 0点该市场暂停撮合，成交量清零","会话VWAP按平台设定的日界线重新累计","平台数据缺失，VWAP需要重新加载才恢复"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：加密市场虽连续交易，会话VWAP仍按平台日界线重置。","optionExplanations":["错误：重置按会话日界线，不按K线根数。","错误：加密市场24小时交易，不会暂停。","正确：加密市场虽连续交易，会话VWAP仍按日界线重置。","错误：这是会话VWAP的正常重置，不是数据缺失。"],"skills":["重置","会话"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Volume Weighted Average Price","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502018-volume-weighted-average-price-vwap/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Crypto trades 24 hours a day, yet the VWAP on the chart restarts at 00:00 UTC. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["VWAP restarts automatically after every 24 bars","The market stops matching at 00:00 UTC and volume resets","Session VWAP restarts at the platform’s day boundary","Platform data is missing, and VWAP needs reloading to recover"],"explanationEn":"Although crypto trades continuously, session VWAP still resets at the platform’s day boundary.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It resets at the session boundary, not after a number of bars.","Wrong: Crypto trades around the clock and does not stop.","Correct: Crypto trades continuously, but session VWAP resets at the day boundary.","Wrong: This is the normal session reset, not missing data."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-77","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[38],"stem":"横盘震荡中，Parabolic SAR的点频繁在K线上下翻转。最合理的解释是？","options":["SAR提前识别出横盘，翻转是发出的预警信号","SAR随趋势跟踪，价格碰点就翻边，横盘易反复","横盘时波动变小，SAR点翻转是成交量不足造成","翻转越频繁，说明当前趋势越强、越可靠"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：横盘时SAR容易频繁来回。","optionExplanations":["错误：SAR并不预测横盘，只是被来回触发。","正确：横盘时价格容易触及点位，SAR来回翻转。","错误：SAR只用价格，与成交量无关。","错误：频繁翻转恰恰说明没有清晰趋势。"],"skills":["趋势跟随","横盘"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Parabolic SAR","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502597-parabolic-sar-sar/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"In a sideways chop, Parabolic SAR dots keep flipping above and below the bars. What is the most reasonable explanation?","optionsEn":["SAR spotted the range early, and the flips are warnings","SAR follows trends and flips when price touches the dots, so ranges cause repeated flips","Volatility is lower in ranges, and the flips come from thin volume","The more often it flips, the stronger and more reliable the trend"],"explanationEn":"In sideways markets SAR tends to flip back and forth.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: SAR does not forecast ranges; it is just triggered back and forth.","Correct: In a range price touches the dots easily, so SAR keeps flipping.","Wrong: SAR uses only price and has nothing to do with volume.","Wrong: Frequent flips show there is no clear trend."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-53","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[39],"stem":"Supertrend(10,3)：某根中价(最高+最低)÷2=100，ATR(10)=2。基础下轨（尚未套用沿用前值的规则）是多少？","options":["98","106","97","94"],"answer":3,"explanation":"100−3×2=94；最终显示值还要看是否沿用前一根。","optionExplanations":["98只减了1倍ATR。","106是基础上轨。","97用错了倍数。","100−3×2=94；最终显示值还要看是否沿用前一根。"],"skills":["计算","ATR倍数"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Supertrend","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000634738-supertrend/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Supertrend(10,3): one bar’s median price (high + low) ÷ 2 is 100 and ATR(10) is 2. What is the basic lower band, before the carry-forward rule is applied?","optionsEn":["98","106","97","94"],"explanationEn":"100 − 3 × 2 = 94; the displayed value also depends on whether the prior bar’s value is carried forward.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 98 subtracts only one ATR.","Wrong: 106 is the basic upper band.","Wrong: 97 uses the wrong multiple.","Correct: 100 − 3 × 2 = 94; the displayed value depends on the carry-forward rule."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-78","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[40],"stem":"A从50涨到55，B从200涨到210。用A/B比值观察，比值怎样变化，说明什么？","options":["A/B约0.25→0.238，说明A相对更强","A/B约0.25→0.262，说明B相对更强","A/B约0.25→0.25，说明两者表现相同","A/B约0.25→0.262，说明A相对更强"],"answer":3,"explanation":"A涨10%、B涨5%，比值从0.25升到约0.262，说明A相对更强。","optionExplanations":["错误：55÷210约0.262，不是0.238。","错误：比值上升表示分子A相对更强。","错误：只看涨的点数会误判，应看百分比，A涨幅更大。","正确：A涨10%、B涨5%，A/B上升，A相对更强。"],"skills":["计算","相对强弱"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Spread charts explained","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502298-spread-charts-explained/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"A rises from 50 to 55 and B from 200 to 210. Watching the A/B ratio, how does it change and what does it show?","optionsEn":["A/B about 0.25 → 0.238, so A is relatively stronger","A/B about 0.25 → 0.262, so B is relatively stronger","A/B about 0.25 → 0.25, so they performed the same","A/B about 0.25 → 0.262, so A is relatively stronger"],"explanationEn":"A rose 10% and B 5%, so the ratio rises from 0.25 to about 0.262: A is relatively stronger.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 55 ÷ 210 is about 0.262, not 0.238.","Wrong: A rising ratio means the numerator, A, is relatively stronger.","Wrong: Comparing point gains misleads; in percentage terms A rose more.","Correct: A rose 10% and B 5%, so A/B rises and A is relatively stronger."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-79","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[41],"stem":"价格持续大跌，同期ADX从20升到45。下面哪项正确？","options":["ADX只量趋势强弱、不分方向，大跌也会升高","ADX只在上涨时升高，大跌时通常会回落","ADX升到45说明超跌严重，价格即将反弹","ADX升到45说明一轮新的上涨趋势已经形成"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程强调ADX很高不等于适合买入，下跌很猛时它也能很高。","optionExplanations":["正确：ADX很高不等于适合买入，下跌猛时它也能很高。","错误：ADX在强下跌趋势中同样升高。","错误：ADX衡量趋势强度，不是超跌指标。","错误：ADX不表示方向，大跌时同样会升高。"],"skills":["强度与方向","解读"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Average Directional Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589099-average-directional-index-adx/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Price keeps falling sharply while ADX rises from 20 to 45. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["ADX measures trend strength without direction, so it rises in sharp declines too","ADX rises only in rallies and usually falls during sharp declines","ADX at 45 shows price is deeply oversold and about to bounce","ADX at 45 shows a new uptrend has formed"],"explanationEn":"A high ADX does not mean it is time to buy; it can be high during a steep decline.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A high ADX does not mean buy; it can be high in a steep decline.","Wrong: ADX rises in strong downtrends as well.","Wrong: ADX measures trend strength; it is not an oversold gauge.","Wrong: ADX has no direction and rises in sharp declines too."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-54","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[42],"stem":"DMI中+DI为28、−DI为14。DX=|+DI−(−DI)|÷(+DI+(−DI))×100。DX约为多少？","options":["约14.0","约33.3","约50.0","约66.7"],"answer":1,"explanation":"|28−14|÷(28+14)×100=14÷42×100≈33.3；ADX是DX的平滑。","optionExplanations":["14只是两线之差，还没有除以两线之和再乘100。","正确：|28−14|÷(28+14)×100=14÷42×100≈33.3。","50是14÷28，分母应是两线之和42。","66.7是28÷42，分子误用了+DI而不是两者之差。"],"skills":["计算","DX与ADX"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Directional Movement Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502250-directional-movement-dmi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"In DMI, +DI is 28 and −DI is 14. DX = |+DI − (−DI)| ÷ (+DI + (−DI)) × 100. About what is DX?","optionsEn":["About 14.0","About 33.3","About 50.0","About 66.7"],"explanationEn":"|28 − 14| ÷ (28 + 14) × 100 = 14 ÷ 42 × 100 ≈ 33.3; ADX is the smoothed DX.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 14 is only the difference, not yet divided by the sum and multiplied by 100.","Correct: |28 − 14| ÷ (28 + 14) × 100 ≈ 33.3.","Wrong: 50 is 14 ÷ 28; the denominator should be the sum, 42.","Wrong: 66.7 is 28 ÷ 42, using +DI instead of the difference."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-80","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[43],"stem":"Aroon Up为100、Aroon Down为0。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["刚创窗口新高，窗口最低点在最早一根","刚创窗口新低，窗口最高点在最早一根","窗口新高出现在最早一根，目前正在下跌","窗口内价格已经上涨了100%，涨幅达到上限"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Up=100表示刚创窗口新高；Down=0表示窗口最低点出现在最早一根。","optionExplanations":["正确：Up=100为刚创新高；Down=0为最低点在窗口最早处。","错误：Up与Down说反了。","错误：Up=100表示新高刚刚出现，不是最早。","错误：Aroon读数衡量新高新低的远近，不是涨幅。"],"skills":["时间","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Aroon","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501801-aroon-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Aroon Up is 100 and Aroon Down is 0. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["A new window high has just been made, and the window low is at the earliest bar","A new window low has just been made, and the window high is at the earliest bar","The window high is at the earliest bar, and price is now falling","Price has risen 100% in the window, the maximum possible"],"explanationEn":"Up = 100 means a new window high just formed; Down = 0 means the window low is at the earliest bar.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Up = 100 is a fresh high and Down = 0 puts the low at the start of the window.","Wrong: Up and Down are reversed.","Wrong: Up = 100 means the high has just formed, not that it is the earliest.","Wrong: Aroon measures how recent the high and low are, not a gain."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-81","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[44],"stem":"Aroon Up为20，Aroon Down为92。Aroon Oscillator是多少？如何理解？","options":["+72，最近一次新高比新低更近","+112，即Up与Down两线之和","−72%，价格在窗口内下跌了72%","−72，最近一次新低比新高更近"],"answer":3,"explanation":"20−92=−72，负值表示新低相对更新。","optionExplanations":["错误：符号弄反了，Up减Down为负。","错误：振荡器是Up减Down，不是相加。","错误：读数不是价格涨跌幅。","正确：20−92=−72，负值表示新低相对更新。"],"skills":["计算","时间"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Aroon Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773004-aroon-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Aroon Up is 20 and Aroon Down 92. What is the Aroon Oscillator, and how should it be read?","optionsEn":["+72: the latest high is more recent than the latest low","+112: the sum of the Up and Down lines","−72%: price fell 72% in the window","−72: the latest low is more recent than the latest high"],"explanationEn":"20 − 92 = −72; a negative value means the low is more recent.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The sign is reversed; Up minus Down is negative.","Wrong: The oscillator is Up minus Down, not the sum.","Wrong: The reading is not a price change.","Correct: 20 − 92 = −72; a negative value means the low is more recent."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-55","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[45],"stem":"14根内VM+之和为21，VM−之和为14，真实波幅之和为20。VI+和VI−分别是多少？","options":["VI+=1.05，VI−=0.70","VI+=1.50，VI−=0.67","VI+=0.60，VI−=0.40","VI+=21，VI−=14"],"answer":0,"explanation":"VI+=21÷20=1.05，VI−=14÷20=0.70。","optionExplanations":["正确：VI+=21÷20=1.05，VI−=14÷20=0.70。","错误：用VM+与VM−互相相除，而不是除以真实波幅之和。","错误：误用VM+与VM−之和35作分母。","错误：这是VM之和，还没除以真实波幅之和。"],"skills":["计算","比值"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Vortex Indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591352-vortex-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Over 14 bars VM+ sums to 21, VM− to 14 and true range to 20. What are VI+ and VI−?","optionsEn":["VI+ = 1.05, VI− = 0.70","VI+ = 1.50, VI− = 0.67","VI+ = 0.60, VI− = 0.40","VI+ = 21, VI− = 14"],"explanationEn":"VI+ = 21 ÷ 20 = 1.05 and VI− = 14 ÷ 20 = 0.70.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: VI+ = 21 ÷ 20 = 1.05 and VI− = 14 ÷ 20 = 0.70.","Wrong: This divides VM+ and VM− by each other instead of by the true range sum.","Wrong: This divides by VM+ plus VM−, 35.","Wrong: These are the VM sums, not yet divided by the true range sum."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-82","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[46],"stem":"Choppiness Index从65降到30。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["价格转为下跌，指数下降代表空头占优","走势更像单边推进，但不指示涨跌方向","走势转为横盘整理，震荡幅度正在收窄","价格转为上涨，指数下降代表多头占优"],"answer":1,"explanation":"值低更像有趋势，值高更像横盘；课程提醒低值可能伴随上涨，也可能伴随下跌。","optionExplanations":["错误：指数不带方向，不能据此判断空头占优。","正确：低值更像有趋势，但上涨下跌都可能出现。","错误：Choppiness降低代表更像趋势，不是横盘。","错误：指数不带方向，下降也可能伴随下跌。"],"skills":["无方向","趋势与横盘"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Choppiness Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501980-choppiness-index-chop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The Choppiness Index drops from 65 to 30. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["Price has turned down, and a falling index means bears dominate","The move looks more one-directional, but the index gives no direction","The move has turned into a sideways range with narrowing swings","Price has turned up, and a falling index means bulls dominate"],"explanationEn":"Low values look more like a trend and high values more like a range; a low reading can come with either a rise or a fall.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The index has no direction, so it cannot show bears dominating.","Correct: A low value looks more like a trend, rising or falling.","Wrong: A falling Choppiness Index looks more like a trend, not a range.","Wrong: The index has no direction; a drop can come with a decline."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-83","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[47],"stem":"一目均衡表在最新K线右侧还画出了未来26根位置的云。这片云代表什么？","options":["未来26根K线里大概率生效的支撑与阻力区","平台根据模型对未来26根价格作出的预测","用当前和过去数据算出，再右移26根显示","把过去26根的K线原样复制到未来位置显示"],"answer":2,"explanation":"先行带A、B用当前数据计算后向右平移26根显示，课程强调这不是未来价格预告。","optionExplanations":["错误：云只是已有数据的平移，不保证未来有效。","错误：云不是预测，只是平移显示。","正确：先行带由当前数据算出后向前平移，不是未来价格预告。","错误：云由公式计算而来，不是复制K线。"],"skills":["平移","非预测"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ichimoku Cloud","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589152-ichimoku-cloud/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Ichimoku also draws a cloud 26 bars to the right of the latest bar. What does that cloud represent?","optionsEn":["Support and resistance likely to work over the next 26 bars","The platform’s model forecast of price over the next 26 bars","Values computed from current and past data, shifted 26 bars right","The last 26 bars copied as-is into the future positions"],"explanationEn":"Leading spans A and B are computed from current data and shifted 26 bars to the right; this is not a forecast of future price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The cloud is only shifted existing data and guarantees nothing.","Wrong: The cloud is not a forecast, just shifted display.","Correct: The leading spans come from current data shifted forward, not a forecast.","Wrong: The cloud is computed by formula, not copied bars."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-56","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[48],"stem":"鳄鱼指标的颚（Jaw）常见设置为中价的13期SMMA、向右平移8根。图上第100根位置的颚线数值，来自截至哪一根K线的数据？","options":["第87根","第108根","第92根","第100根"],"answer":2,"explanation":"向右平移8根，所以第100根位置显示的是截至第92根算出的值。","optionExplanations":["错误：误用13期而非8根的平移。","错误：平移方向弄反，向右平移是用更早的数据。","正确：向右平移8根，第100根位置显示的是第92根算出的值。","错误：忽略了平移，平移后位置与数据不再对应。"],"skills":["平移","滞后"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Williams Alligator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592305-williams-alligator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The Alligator’s Jaw is commonly a 13-period SMMA of the median price shifted 8 bars right. The Jaw value shown at bar 100 comes from data up to which bar?","optionsEn":["Bar 87","Bar 108","Bar 92","Bar 100"],"explanationEn":"It is shifted 8 bars right, so the value shown at bar 100 was computed through bar 92.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This uses the 13-period length instead of the 8-bar shift.","Wrong: The shift is reversed; shifting right uses earlier data.","Correct: Shifted 8 bars right, the value at bar 100 was computed at bar 92.","Wrong: This ignores the shift; after shifting, position and data no longer line up."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-57","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[49],"stem":"KAMA的效率比ER=|10根净变化|÷10根逐根变化绝对值之和。净变化+4，逐根路程合计20。ER是多少？KAMA会跟得快还是慢？","options":["5；跟得较快","0.2；跟得较慢","0.8；跟得较快","0.2；跟得较快"],"answer":1,"explanation":"4÷20=0.2，说明来回折腾多、净推进少，KAMA会接近慢速平滑。","optionExplanations":["把分子分母倒过来了。","4÷20=0.2，说明来回折腾多、净推进少，KAMA会接近慢速平滑。","0.8不是这组数据的结果。","ER低时KAMA放慢，不是加快。"],"skills":["效率比","自适应"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Kaufman's Adaptive Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773012-kaufman-s-adaptive-moving-average-kama/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"KAMA’s efficiency ratio ER = |net change over 10 bars| ÷ sum of the absolute bar-to-bar changes. The net change is +4 and the total path 20. What is ER, and will KAMA follow price quickly or slowly?","optionsEn":["5; quickly","0.2; slowly","0.8; quickly","0.2; quickly"],"explanationEn":"4 ÷ 20 = 0.2: lots of back-and-forth with little net progress, so KAMA moves close to its slow smoothing.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The numerator and denominator are swapped.","Correct: 4 ÷ 20 = 0.2, much back-and-forth and little net progress, so KAMA slows.","Wrong: 0.8 is not what this data gives.","Wrong: When ER is low KAMA slows down, it does not speed up."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-58","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[50],"stem":"ALMA按高斯权重平均，s=窗口长度÷Sigma。把Sigma从6改为2（Length与Offset不变），权重会怎样变化？","options":["钟形形状不变，只是窗口长度缩短，线更灵敏","钟形中心后移，权重偏向较早数据，线更滞后","钟形变窄，权重更集中，线更贴近价格","钟形变宽，权重更接近平均，线更平滑"],"answer":3,"explanation":"s=9÷2=4.5比9÷6=1.5大，钟形更宽，权重更接近平均，线更平滑但更滞后。","optionExplanations":["错误：Sigma改变钟形宽度，窗口长度由Length决定。","错误：改变中心位置的是Offset，不是Sigma。","错误：Sigma变小使s变大，钟形变宽而非变窄。","正确：s=9÷2=4.5大于9÷6=1.5，钟形更宽，权重更接近平均。"],"skills":["参数含义","高斯权重"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Arnaud Legoux Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594683-arnaud-legoux-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"ALMA averages with Gaussian weights, with s = window length ÷ Sigma. If Sigma changes from 6 to 2 (Length and Offset unchanged), how do the weights change?","optionsEn":["The bell shape is the same, only the window shortens, so the line is more responsive","The bell’s centre moves back, favouring older data, so the line lags more","The bell narrows and weights concentrate, so the line hugs price","The bell widens and weights become more even, so the line is smoother"],"explanationEn":"s = 9 ÷ 2 = 4.5 is larger than 9 ÷ 6 = 1.5, so the bell is wider, weights are more even, and the line is smoother but lags more.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Sigma changes the bell’s width; Length sets the window.","Wrong: Offset moves the centre, not Sigma.","Wrong: A smaller Sigma makes s larger, so the bell widens, not narrows.","Correct: S = 9 ÷ 2 = 4.5 exceeds 9 ÷ 6 = 1.5, so the bell is wider and weights more even."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-59","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[51],"stem":"McGinley：MD=MD前+(价格−MD前)÷(N×(价格÷MD前)^4)，N=14，MD前=100。价格为110和90两种情况下，新MD分别约为多少？","options":["100.71；99.29（上下对称）","101.00；99.00（上下对称）","101.05；99.53（上涨时追得快）","100.49；98.91（下跌时追得快）"],"answer":3,"explanation":"110：10÷(14×1.1^4)≈0.49；90：−10÷(14×0.9^4)≈−1.09，下跌时调整更快。","optionExplanations":["这是忽略价格比值修正的结果，McGinley上下并不对称。","这是除以N×1的粗略算法，没有按公式修正。","指数符号用反了，实际是下跌时追得更快。","正确，下跌时调整幅度更大。"],"skills":["计算","调速"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: McGinley Dynamic","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589175-mcginley-dynamic/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"McGinley: MD = MD_prev + (price − MD_prev) ÷ (N × (price ÷ MD_prev)^4), with N = 14 and MD_prev = 100. For prices of 110 and 90, about what are the new MD values?","optionsEn":["100.71; 99.29 (symmetric)","101.00; 99.00 (symmetric)","101.05; 99.53 (catches up faster when rising)","100.49; 98.91 (catches up faster when falling)"],"explanationEn":"At 110: 10 ÷ (14 × 1.1^4) ≈ 0.49; at 90: −10 ÷ (14 × 0.9^4) ≈ −1.09, so it adjusts faster on declines.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This ignores the price-ratio correction; McGinley is not symmetric.","Wrong: This divides by N × 1, a rough version without the formula’s correction.","Wrong: The exponent effect is reversed; it actually catches up faster on declines.","Correct: It adjusts more on declines."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-60","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[52],"stem":"价格从一段直线上涨突然转为横盘。LSMA(25)与SMA(25)相比，通常会怎样？","options":["LSMA比SMA更滞后，通常落后价格更多根","LSMA与SMA走势几乎重合，通常不会冲过价格","LSMA按回归线外推，通常会短暂冲过价格","LSMA与价格同时转平，通常没有滞后"],"answer":2,"explanation":"LSMA取回归直线在最新一根的值，转折时会“冲过头”。","optionExplanations":["错误：LSMA通常比SMA滞后更小，转折时甚至冲过头。","错误：两者算法不同，LSMA会冲过价格。","回归直线取最新一根的拟合值，趋势突然转平时会先“冲过头”。","LSMA仍按25根回归，会先冲过价格再回落，不会和价格同时转平。"],"skills":["回归端点","滞后与超调"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Least Squares Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000599877-least-squares-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Price switches abruptly from a straight-line rally to sideways. Compared with SMA(25), what does LSMA(25) usually do?","optionsEn":["LSMA lags more than the SMA, usually by more bars","LSMA and SMA nearly coincide and usually do not overshoot price","LSMA extrapolates the regression line and usually overshoots price briefly","LSMA flattens at the same time as price, with no lag"],"explanationEn":"LSMA takes the regression line’s value at the latest bar, so it overshoots at turns.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: LSMA usually lags less than the SMA and even overshoots at turns.","Wrong: Their algorithms differ, and LSMA overshoots price.","Correct: The regression line’s latest fitted value overshoots when the trend suddenly flattens.","Wrong: LSMA still regresses over 25 bars, so it overshoots and then falls back; it does not flatten with price."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-84","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[53],"stem":"回归通道上下线设为±2倍标准差。某根收盘落在上线之外。下面哪项正确？","options":["上线是硬阻力，价格下一根通常会回到通道内","超出上线说明通道计算有误，应重新设定","通道上线固定不动，之后会一直作为阻力","偏离回归线超过两倍标准差，未必会反转"],"answer":3,"explanation":"边线描述偏离程度；课程提醒通道会随新价格重算。","optionExplanations":["错误：边线不是硬阻力，价格可以继续走出通道。","错误：收盘落在上线之外是正常情形。","错误：通道会随新价格重新计算。","正确：边线只描述偏离程度，通道也会随新价格重算。"],"skills":["偏离","重算"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Linear Regression","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644936-linear-regression/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"A regression channel’s bands are set at ±2 standard deviations. One bar closes outside the upper band. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["The upper band is hard resistance, so the next bar usually returns inside","Closing outside the band means the channel is miscalculated and should be reset","The upper band stays fixed and will act as resistance from now on","Price is more than two standard deviations from the regression line, which need not mean a reversal"],"explanationEn":"The bands describe how far price has strayed, and the channel is recalculated as new prices arrive.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The band is not hard resistance; price can keep going outside it.","Wrong: Closing outside the upper band is normal.","Wrong: The channel is recalculated with new prices.","Correct: The bands only describe deviation, and the channel is recalculated with new prices."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-61","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[54],"stem":"最近5根收盘依次为100、101、103、104、107（等间隔）。用最小二乘回归，斜率约为每根多少？","options":["约7","约1.7","约1.75","约1.4"],"answer":1,"explanation":"按最小二乘，Σ(x−x̄)(y−ȳ)=17，Σ(x−x̄)²=10，斜率=1.7。","optionExplanations":["错误：这是5根内的总涨幅，不是每根斜率。","正确：Σ(x−x̄)(y−ȳ)=17，Σ(x−x̄)²=10，斜率=1.7。","错误：这是首尾差除以4，不是最小二乘斜率。","错误：把总涨幅7除以5，而不是做回归。"],"skills":["回归计算","斜率"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Linear Regression Slope","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644936-linear-regression/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The last five closes are 100, 101, 103, 104 and 107 (evenly spaced). Using least-squares regression, about what is the slope per bar?","optionsEn":["About 7","About 1.7","About 1.75","About 1.4"],"explanationEn":"By least squares, Σ(x − x̄)(y − ȳ) = 17 and Σ(x − x̄)² = 10, so the slope is 1.7.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This is the total gain over five bars, not the slope per bar.","Correct: Σ(x − x̄)(y − ȳ) = 17 and Σ(x − x̄)² = 10, giving 1.7.","Wrong: This is first-to-last change divided by 4, not the least-squares slope.","Wrong: This divides the total gain of 7 by 5 instead of regressing."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-62","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[55],"stem":"两个窗口：A的R²=0.95、斜率+0.1；B的R²=0.40、斜率+1.2。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["A更像直线但上升较缓，B更陡但更不规则","两者趋势强度相同，因为斜率都是正数","B的趋势更可靠，因为斜率更大意味着拟合更好","A的上涨概率约95%，B的上涨概率约40%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"R²看像不像直线，斜率看陡不陡；两者回答不同问题。","optionExplanations":["正确：R²看像不像直线，斜率看陡不陡。","错误：正数只说明方向，斜率与R²仍不同。","错误：斜率大不代表拟合好，B的R²较低。","错误：R²是拟合程度，不是上涨概率。"],"skills":["R²与斜率","解读"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Linear Regression R-Squared","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644936-linear-regression/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Two windows: A has R² = 0.95 and slope +0.1; B has R² = 0.40 and slope +1.2. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["A is closer to a straight line but rises gently; B is steeper but more irregular","Their trend strength is equal, since both slopes are positive","B’s trend is more reliable, since a bigger slope means a better fit","A has about a 95% chance of rising, B about 40%"],"explanationEn":"R² shows how straight-line-like it is, and the slope how steep; they answer different questions.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: R² shows how straight the move is, and the slope how steep.","Wrong: Being positive only gives the direction; slope and R² still differ.","Wrong: A bigger slope does not mean a better fit; B’s R² is lower.","Wrong: R² is goodness of fit, not a probability of rising."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-63","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[56],"stem":"A与B价格的20日相关系数为0.9，但两者日收益率的相关系数只有0.1。最可能的原因是？","options":["价格相关0.9说明A的涨跌推动了B的涨跌","两种相关用同一批数据，数值本应基本一致","收益率相关本应高于价格相关，说明计算有误","两者各自走趋势，价格相关被趋势拉高"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：价格水平的相关不等于收益率相关。趋势会让价格相关虚高。","optionExplanations":["错误：相关不等于因果。","错误：价格和收益率是不同序列，相关可以差很多。","错误：趋势常使价格相关虚高，两者差很多并不奇怪。","正确：价格水平的相关不等于收益率相关，趋势会使价格相关虚高。"],"skills":["价格与收益率","虚假相关"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Correlation Coefficient","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502022-correlation-coefficient-cc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The 20-day correlation of A’s and B’s prices is 0.9, but the correlation of their daily returns is only 0.1. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["A price correlation of 0.9 shows A’s moves drive B’s moves","Both correlations use the same data, so they should be about equal","Return correlation should exceed price correlation, so there is an error","Both are trending on their own, which inflates the price correlation"],"explanationEn":"Correlation of price levels is not correlation of returns; trends make price correlation look artificially high.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Correlation is not causation.","Wrong: Prices and returns are different series, and their correlations can differ a lot.","Wrong: Trends often inflate price correlation, so a large gap is not surprising.","Correct: Price-level correlation is not return correlation, and trends inflate the former."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-85","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[57],"stem":"TradingView的StochRSI纵轴为0—100，参考线20/80；某教程写的是0.2/0.8。两者是什么关系？","options":["只是刻度不同，0.8相当于80，信号含义一样","0.2/0.8适用于短周期，20/80适用于长周期","两者是不同指标，0.2/0.8来自另一套公式","0.8比80更严格，同样的行情提示信号更少"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：读坐标先确认20/80与0.2/0.8的换算。","optionExplanations":["正确：读坐标先确认20/80与0.2/0.8的换算。","错误：两种写法与周期长短无关。","错误：StochRSI只是刻度写法不同。","错误：只是换算，阈值含义相同。"],"skills":["刻度","换算"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Stochastic RSI","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502333-stochastic-rsi-stoch-rsi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"TradingView’s StochRSI uses a 0–100 axis with 20/80 reference lines; a tutorial uses 0.2/0.8. How are they related?","optionsEn":["Only the scale differs; 0.8 equals 80, and the signals mean the same","0.2/0.8 is for short timeframes, 20/80 for long ones","They are different indicators; 0.2/0.8 comes from another formula","0.8 is stricter than 80, so the same market gives fewer signals"],"explanationEn":"When reading the axis, first check the conversion between 20/80 and 0.2/0.8.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Check the conversion between 20/80 and 0.2/0.8 when reading the axis.","Wrong: The two notations have nothing to do with timeframe.","Wrong: StochRSI is the same; only the scale is written differently.","Wrong: It is only a conversion, and the thresholds mean the same."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-64","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[58],"stem":"某资产已连续上涨4天。ConnorsRSI中“连涨连跌”这一项，喂进RSI(2)的数值是什么？","options":["+4%（4天累计涨幅），再算RSI(2)","+1（只记今天上涨），再算RSI(2)","+4，直接当作该项得分，不再算RSI","+4（连涨天数），再算RSI(2)"],"answer":3,"explanation":"连涨记为正天数、连跌为负天数，再对这串数计算2期RSI。","optionExplanations":["错误：连涨连跌项记的是天数，不是涨幅。","错误：连涨项记的是连续天数，不是只看当天。","错误：还要把这串数代入RSI(2)。","正确：连涨记正天数、连跌记负天数，再对这串数算RSI(2)。"],"skills":["组成部分","连涨天数"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Connors RSI","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502017-connors-rsi-crsi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"An asset has risen four days in a row. In ConnorsRSI’s streak component, what value is fed into RSI(2)?","optionsEn":["+4% (the four-day gain), then RSI(2) is computed","+1 (only today’s rise), then RSI(2) is computed","+4, used directly as the component’s score without RSI","+4 (the streak length in days), then RSI(2) is computed"],"explanationEn":"Up streaks count as positive days and down streaks as negative days, and RSI(2) is computed on that series.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The streak component counts days, not gains.","Wrong: The streak counts consecutive days, not just today.","Wrong: The series still goes into RSI(2).","Correct: Up streaks count positive days and down streaks negative days, then RSI(2) is applied."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-86","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[59],"stem":"在不做平滑、使用相同涨跌输入时，CMO=+60相当于RSI式读数多少？","options":["60","30","80","160"],"answer":2,"explanation":"RSI式读数=(CMO+100)÷2=80。","optionExplanations":["错误：直接把CMO当成RSI。","错误：只把CMO除以2。","正确：RSI式读数=(CMO+100)÷2=80。","错误：把CMO加100后没有除以2。"],"skills":["换算","刻度"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chande Momentum Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589109-chande-momentum-oscillator-cmo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Without smoothing and with the same up/down inputs, what RSI-style reading corresponds to CMO = +60?","optionsEn":["60","30","80","160"],"explanationEn":"RSI-style reading = (CMO + 100) ÷ 2 = 80.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This treats CMO as RSI directly.","Wrong: This only halves CMO.","Correct: RSI-style reading = (CMO + 100) ÷ 2 = 80.","Wrong: This adds 100 to CMO without dividing by 2."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-87","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[60],"stem":"在TradingView搜索TSI时，列表里同时出现“True Strength Index”和“Trend Strength Index”。本课应选哪个？","options":["选Trend Strength Index，它才是常说的TSI","都不选，TradingView没有内置TSI，要自己写","选True Strength Index，另一个是别的指标","任选其一，两者只是名称写法不同，公式相同"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：选True Strength Index/Indicator，别选Trend Strength Index。","optionExplanations":["错误：本课的TSI是True Strength Index。","错误：True Strength Index在平台上可直接使用。","正确：别选Trend Strength Index。","错误：两者是不同的指标。"],"skills":["设置辨认","同名缩写"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: True Strength Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592290-true-strength-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Searching TradingView for TSI shows both “True Strength Index” and “Trend Strength Index”. Which should this lesson’s TSI be?","optionsEn":["Trend Strength Index, which is the usual TSI","Neither; TradingView has no built-in TSI, so write your own","True Strength Index; the other is a different indicator","Either; only the names differ, and the formula is the same"],"explanationEn":"Choose True Strength Index (or Indicator), not Trend Strength Index.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This lesson’s TSI is the True Strength Index.","Wrong: True Strength Index is available directly on the platform.","Correct: Do not choose Trend Strength Index.","Wrong: They are different indicators."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-88","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[61],"stem":"TRIX与TEMA都用了三层EMA。两者最主要的区别是？","options":["两者都是价格均线，TRIX只是平滑次数更多","两者都是振荡器，TEMA只是平滑次数更少","TRIX是叠加价格的均线，TEMA是变化率振荡器","TEMA是叠加价格的均线，TRIX是变化率振荡器"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程强调TEMA是价格线，TRIX看三重平滑后价格的变化率。","optionExplanations":["错误：TRIX是振荡器，不叠加在价格上。","错误：TEMA是叠加在价格上的均线。","错误：两者说反了。","正确：TEMA是价格线，TRIX看三重平滑后价格的变化率。"],"skills":["易混指标","输出类型"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: TRIX","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502331-trix/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"TRIX and TEMA both use three layers of EMA. What is the main difference between them?","optionsEn":["Both are price averages; TRIX just smooths more times","Both are oscillators; TEMA just smooths fewer times","TRIX is an average plotted on price; TEMA is a rate-of-change oscillator","TEMA is an average plotted on price; TRIX is a rate-of-change oscillator"],"explanationEn":"TEMA is a price line; TRIX looks at the rate of change of the triple-smoothed price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: TRIX is an oscillator and is not plotted on price.","Wrong: TEMA is an average plotted on price.","Wrong: The two are reversed.","Correct: TEMA is a price line, and TRIX is the rate of change of triple-smoothed price."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-65","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[62],"stem":"终极振荡器中，买压BP=收盘−min(最低,前收)，真实范围TR=max(最高,前收)−min(最低,前收)。前收100，本根最高104、最低101、收盘103。BP和TR分别是多少？","options":["BP 3，TR 3","BP 3，TR 4","BP 4，TR 4","BP 2，TR 3"],"answer":1,"explanation":"min(101,100)=100，BP=103−100=3；TR=104−100=4。","optionExplanations":["错误：TR用了最高减最低，没有考虑前收。","正确：BP=103−100=3，TR=104−100=4。","错误：BP应以收盘减去最低与前收的较小者。","错误：忽略了前收，用本根最低101计算。"],"skills":["计算","前收的作用"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ultimate Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502328-ultimate-oscillator-uo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"In the Ultimate Oscillator, buying pressure BP = close − min(low, prior close) and true range TR = max(high, prior close) − min(low, prior close). The prior close is 100; this bar has a high of 104, a low of 101 and a close of 103. What are BP and TR?","optionsEn":["BP 3, TR 3","BP 3, TR 4","BP 4, TR 4","BP 2, TR 3"],"explanationEn":"min(101, 100) = 100, so BP = 103 − 100 = 3; TR = 104 − 100 = 4.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: TR used high minus low and ignored the prior close.","Correct: BP = 103 − 100 = 3, TR = 104 − 100 = 4.","Wrong: BP is the close minus the smaller of the low and the prior close.","Wrong: This ignores the prior close and uses this bar's low of 101."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-89","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[63],"stem":"Awesome Oscillator的柱子是绿色，但位于零线下方。这表示什么？","options":["绿色只表示AO为正值，红色表示负值","这一根价格上涨，所以柱子标成绿色","AO仍在零线下方，但比上一根高","AO已经升过零线，转为正值区域"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：柱色反映比上一根增减，绿柱可以在零线下。","optionExplanations":["错误：柱色由与上一根的比较决定，不由正负决定。","错误：柱色看的是AO自身增减，不是单根价格涨跌。","正确：柱色反映比上一根增减，绿柱可以在零线下。","错误：柱子位于零线下，仍为负。"],"skills":["柱色含义","正负"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Awesome Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501826-awesome-oscillator-ao/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"An Awesome Oscillator bar is green but sits below the zero line. What does that mean?","optionsEn":["Green only means AO is positive; red means negative","Price rose on this bar, so the bar is green","AO is still below zero but higher than the previous bar","AO has crossed above zero into positive territory"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, bar colour shows a rise or fall versus the previous bar, so a green bar can sit below zero.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Colour comes from comparison with the previous bar, not from the sign.","Wrong: Colour reflects AO's own change, not one bar's price move.","Correct: Colour shows the change versus the previous bar, so a green bar can be below zero.","Wrong: The bar is below zero, so AO is still negative."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-90","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[64],"stem":"同一窗口里随机指标原始%K=50。SMI（随机动量指数）在平滑前的原始值是多少？","options":["0","50","25","−50"],"answer":0,"explanation":"%K=50表示收盘正好在区间中点，SMI以中点为0，原始值为0。","optionExplanations":["%K=50表示收盘正好在区间中点，SMI以中点为0，原始值为0。","SMI不是%K。","25是混淆刻度。","负值表示在下半区，这里正好在中点。"],"skills":["换算","中点"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Stochastic Momentum Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000707882-stochastic-momentum-index-smi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"In the same window, the stochastic raw %K = 50. What is the raw SMI (Stochastic Momentum Index) before smoothing?","optionsEn":["0","50","25","−50"],"explanationEn":"%K = 50 means the close is exactly at the middle of the range; SMI treats the midpoint as 0, so the raw value is 0.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: %K = 50 means the close is exactly at the middle of the range; SMI treats the midpoint as 0, so the raw value is 0.","Wrong: SMI is not %K.","Wrong: 25 mixes up the scales.","Wrong: A negative value means the lower half; here the close is exactly at the midpoint."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-66","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[65],"stem":"SMI Ergodic指标与SMI（随机动量指数）都叫SMI。下面哪项区别正确？","options":["两者是同一个指标，只是不同平台命名不同","Ergodic用平滑后的价格变化计算，不能套用±40","Ergodic只改用收盘价与区间中点，阈值仍用±40","Ergodic只是SMI的平滑版本，仍可套用±40"],"answer":1,"explanation":"SMI Ergodic把涨跌变化平滑后与总变化比较，与用区间中点的SMI不同。","optionExplanations":["错误：两者计算和刻度都不同。","正确：它与用区间中点的SMI计算不同，阈值不能照搬。","错误：Ergodic用的是平滑价格变化，阈值不同。","错误：Ergodic刻度不同，不能照搬±40。"],"skills":["易混指标","阈值"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: SMI Ergodic Indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594669-smi-ergodic-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The SMI Ergodic indicator and the SMI (Stochastic Momentum Index) are both called SMI. Which difference is correct?","optionsEn":["They are the same indicator under different platform names","Ergodic uses smoothed price changes, so ±40 does not carry over","Ergodic only switches to close versus range midpoint and still uses ±40","Ergodic is just a smoothed SMI and ±40 still applies"],"explanationEn":"SMI Ergodic smooths up and down changes and compares them with total change, unlike the SMI, which uses the range midpoint.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Their calculations and scales both differ.","Correct: Its calculation differs from the midpoint-based SMI, so thresholds cannot be copied over.","Wrong: Ergodic uses smoothed price changes, and its thresholds differ.","Wrong: Ergodic has a different scale, so ±40 cannot be copied over."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-91","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[66],"stem":"Relative Vigor Index与Relative Volatility Index缩写都是RVI。Vigor版的核心比较是什么？","options":["上涨日与下跌日的标准差","成交量与价格","收盘−开盘与最高−最低","收盘在区间中的位置"],"answer":2,"explanation":"活力指数比较收盘相对开盘推进了多少，占当根范围的几成。","optionExplanations":["那是Relative Volatility Index。","两者都不用成交量。","活力指数比较收盘相对开盘推进了多少，占当根范围的几成。","那是随机指标类。"],"skills":["易混指标","输入"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Relative Vigor Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591593-relative-vigor-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The Relative Vigor Index and the Relative Volatility Index are both abbreviated RVI. What does the Vigor version compare at its core?","optionsEn":["The standard deviation on up days versus down days","Volume versus price","Close − open versus high − low","Where the close sits within the range"],"explanationEn":"The Vigor Index compares how far the close moved from the open as a share of the bar's range.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is the Relative Volatility Index.","Wrong: Neither one uses volume.","Correct: The Vigor Index compares how far the close moved from the open as a share of the bar's range.","Wrong: That is the stochastic family."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-92","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[67],"stem":"Relative Volatility Index长得像RSI。两者的主要区别是？","options":["它只用成交量，不用价格计算","它没有0—100的范围，可以无限大","它直接给出未来风险的百分比","它累计的是标准差，不是涨跌幅"],"answer":3,"explanation":"相对波动指数用的是波动大小（标准差），不是普通涨跌幅。","optionExplanations":["它用价格的标准差，不用成交量。","它同样是0—100，50为中点。","课程提醒它不是直接测未来风险的百分比。","相对波动指数用的是波动大小（标准差），不是普通涨跌幅。"],"skills":["与RSI区别","输入"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Relative Volatility Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594684-relative-volatility-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The Relative Volatility Index looks like RSI. What is the main difference?","optionsEn":["It uses only volume, not price","It has no 0–100 range and can grow without limit","It gives a direct percentage of future risk","It accumulates standard deviation instead of price changes"],"explanationEn":"The Relative Volatility Index uses the size of volatility (standard deviation), not ordinary price changes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It uses the standard deviation of price, not volume.","Wrong: It also runs 0–100 with 50 as the midpoint.","Wrong: The lesson notes that it does not measure a percentage of future risk.","Correct: The Relative Volatility Index uses the size of volatility (standard deviation), not ordinary price changes."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-67","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[68],"stem":"最近5根收盘依次为101、103、102、104、105（最右为最新）。RCI(5)=(1−6Σd²÷(n(n²−1)))×100，d为时间排名与价格排名之差。RCI是多少？","options":["100","90","80","4"],"answer":1,"explanation":"价格排名1、3、2、4、5对时间排名1—5，Σd²=2，(1−12÷120)×100=90。","optionExplanations":["只有一路递增才是100，这里第2、3根顺序颠倒。","价格排名1、3、2、4、5对时间排名1—5，Σd²=2，(1−12÷120)×100=90。","80把Σd²算成了4。","4是涨幅，不是排名相关。"],"skills":["计算","排名"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Rank Correlation Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000765570-rank-correlation-index-rci/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The last 5 closes are 101, 103, 102, 104, 105 (rightmost is newest). RCI(5) = (1 − 6Σd² ÷ (n(n² − 1))) × 100, where d is the difference between time rank and price rank. What is the RCI?","optionsEn":["100","90","80","4"],"explanationEn":"Price ranks 1, 3, 2, 4, 5 against time ranks 1–5 give Σd² = 2, so (1 − 12 ÷ 120) × 100 = 90.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Only a steady rise gives 100; here bars 2 and 3 are out of order.","Correct: Price ranks 1, 3, 2, 4, 5 against time ranks 1–5 give Σd² = 2, so (1 − 12 ÷ 120) × 100 = 90.","Wrong: 80 counts Σd² as 4.","Wrong: 4 is the price gain, not a rank correlation."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-68","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[69],"stem":"Fisher Transform在甲资产上常见±3的读数，在乙资产上很少超过±1.5。下面哪项正确？","options":["没有统一界限，极端值因资产而异","各资产都应统一用±2作为超买超卖界线","甲资产读数达到±3，通常说明计算出了错","乙资产读数偏小，说明它的走势缺乏趋势"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：数值没有统一的超买上限。","optionExplanations":["正确：Fisher数值没有统一上限。","错误：不存在适用于各资产的统一界线。","错误：不同资产极端值本就不同。","错误：读数大小与资产特征有关，不能据此判断趋势有无。"],"skills":["无固定界限","跨资产"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Fisher Transform","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589141-fisher-transform/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The Fisher Transform often reads ±3 on asset A but rarely goes beyond ±1.5 on asset B. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["There is no universal limit; extremes vary by asset","Every asset should use ±2 as the overbought/oversold line","A reading of ±3 on asset A usually means a calculation error","Asset B's smaller readings show its moves lack trend"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, the values have no universal overbought ceiling.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Fisher values have no universal ceiling.","Wrong: No single threshold fits every asset.","Wrong: Different assets naturally have different extremes.","Wrong: Reading size depends on the asset's character and does not show whether a trend exists."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-93","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[70],"stem":"把DPO的Centered（居中）开关打开后，图上的线会怎样变化？","options":["线位置不变，只是改为用收盘价计算","线向右平移约半周期，提前显示未来走势","线改为显示价格与均线的比值，不再是差值","线向左平移约半周期，最新约11根没有值"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：开启居中会向左显示，不可当成实时提前信号。","optionExplanations":["错误：该开关改变线的位置，不改变价格输入。","错误：居中是向左平移，不是向右。","错误：该开关只改变线的位置。","正确：开启居中会向左显示，不可当成实时信号。"],"skills":["居中开关","回看偏差"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Detrended Price Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502246-detrended-price-oscillator-dpo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"What happens to the line when you turn on DPO's Centered setting?","optionsEn":["The line stays put and only switches to close prices","The line shifts right about half a period and shows the future early","The line becomes a price-to-average ratio instead of a difference","The line shifts left about half a period, leaving the latest ~11 bars blank"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, centering shifts the plot to the left, so it cannot be treated as an early real-time signal.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The setting moves the line; it does not change the price input.","Wrong: Centering shifts it left, not right.","Wrong: The setting only moves where the line is drawn.","Correct: Centering shifts the plot left, so it cannot be used as a real-time signal."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-94","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[71],"stem":"KST上穿它的9期信号线，但价格仍在下跌。较稳妥的理解是？","options":["价格已转为上涨，交叉可视为反转确认","动量有所改善，但KST滞后需确认","交叉说明短期动量弱于长期动量，仍偏空","KST已升到零线上方，动量转为正值"],"answer":1,"explanation":"KST是多层平滑的综合动量，课程提醒会延迟反应。","optionExplanations":["错误：价格仍在下跌，交叉不是反转确认。","正确：KST是多层平滑的综合动量，反应有延迟。","错误：上穿信号线表示动量改善。","错误：上穿信号线不等于升过零线。"],"skills":["交叉含义","滞后"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Know Sure Thing","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502329-know-sure-thing-kst/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"KST crosses above its 9-period signal line, but price is still falling. What is the more careful reading?","optionsEn":["Price has turned up, so the cross confirms a reversal","Momentum has improved, but KST lags and needs confirmation","The cross shows short-term momentum weaker than long-term, still bearish","KST has risen above zero, so momentum is now positive"],"explanationEn":"KST is a multi-layer smoothed composite momentum measure, and the lesson notes that it reacts late.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Price is still falling, so the cross does not confirm a reversal.","Correct: KST is a heavily smoothed composite momentum, so it reacts with a delay.","Wrong: A cross above the signal line means momentum is improving.","Wrong: Crossing the signal line is not the same as crossing zero."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-95","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[72],"stem":"Pring Special K的设计特点是什么？","options":["按成交量变化计算，属于量能指标","合成多个周期的平滑ROC，只需约50根历史","只比较最近10根涨跌，是一个快速指标","合成多个周期平滑ROC，需要很长历史"],"answer":3,"explanation":"它综合多个周期的涨跌速度，最长一项需约725根历史。","optionExplanations":["错误：它由价格的ROC合成。","错误：最长一项需要约725根历史。","错误：Special K包含很长周期的ROC。","正确：它综合12个ROC，最长一项需约725根历史。"],"skills":["组成","历史长度"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Pring's Special K","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773011-pring-s-special-k/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"What is the defining design feature of Pring's Special K?","optionsEn":["It is built from volume changes, so it is a volume indicator","It combines smoothed ROC over several periods and needs only ~50 bars","It compares only the last 10 bars, making it a fast indicator","It combines smoothed ROC over several periods and needs long history"],"explanationEn":"It combines the rate of change over many periods; the longest component needs about 725 bars of history.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It is built from price ROC.","Wrong: The longest component needs about 725 bars.","Wrong: Special K includes very long-period ROC.","Correct: It combines 12 ROC terms, the longest needing about 725 bars."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-96","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[73],"stem":"PMO从−1.5升到−0.5。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["价格已经从低位反弹，动量由弱转强","PMO升过零线，动量已由负转为正","下跌速度放缓，但动量仍在零线下方","下跌速度加快，因为读数仍低于零线"],"answer":2,"explanation":"PMO是平滑后的涨跌速度，读数仍为负，只是下降速度放缓。","optionExplanations":["错误：PMO上升不等于价格已经上涨。","错误：−0.5仍为负。","正确：PMO仍为负，只是下降速度放缓。","错误：读数上升表示速度放缓。"],"skills":["正负与方向","解读"],"references":[{"title":"DecisionPoint: Using DecisionPoint Timing Signals to Improve your Portfolio","url":"https://articles.stockcharts.com/article/articles-decisionpoint-2016-09-using-decisionpoint-timing-signals-to-improve-your-portfolio/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"PMO rises from −1.5 to −0.5. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["Price has bounced from its low and momentum has turned strong","PMO has crossed zero and momentum is now positive","The decline is slowing, but momentum is still below zero","The decline is speeding up because the reading is still below zero"],"explanationEn":"PMO is a smoothed rate of change; the reading is still negative, and the decline is merely slowing.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A rising PMO does not mean price has risen.","Wrong: −0.5 is still negative.","Correct: PMO is still negative; the decline is only slowing.","Wrong: A rising reading means the pace is slowing."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-97","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[74],"stem":"科波克曲线的输入是ROC14+ROC11，再做WMA10。某月ROC14=−6%，ROC11=−4%。这个月的“ROC14+ROC11”是多少？","options":["−5%","+10%","−10%","−24%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"−6%+(−4%)=−10%，之后再参与10期加权平均。","optionExplanations":["错误：取了平均，而不是相加。","错误：忽略了负号。","正确：−6%+(−4%)=−10%。","错误：把两者相乘而不是相加。"],"skills":["计算","组成"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Coppock Curve","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589114-coppock-curve/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The Coppock Curve input is ROC14 + ROC11, then a WMA10. One month ROC14 = −6% and ROC11 = −4%. What is that month's ROC14 + ROC11?","optionsEn":["−5%","+10%","−10%","−24%"],"explanationEn":"−6% + (−4%) = −10%, which then goes into the 10-period weighted average.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This averages them instead of adding.","Wrong: This ignores the minus signs.","Correct: −6% + (−4%) = −10%.","Wrong: This multiplies them instead of adding."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-69","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[75],"stem":"资产A与B的MACD都为2；A的ATR26为1，B的ATR26为8。MACD-V分别是多少？说明什么？","options":["两者都是2，动能完全相同","A 2、B 16，B的动能更强","A 50、B 400，B的动能更强","A 200、B 25，A的动能更强"],"answer":3,"explanation":"A：2÷1×100=200；B：2÷8×100=25，相当于平常几份波动。","optionExplanations":["MACD-V要除以ATR。","乘错了方向。","把除法写反了。","A：2÷1×100=200；B：2÷8×100=25，相当于平常几份波动。"],"skills":["计算","波动标准化"],"references":[{"title":"Alex Spiroglou: MACD-V original paper","url":"https://www.naaim.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/MACD-V-Alex-Spiroglou-WEB.pdf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Assets A and B both have MACD = 2; A's ATR26 is 1 and B's is 8. What are their MACD-V values, and what does that show?","optionsEn":["Both are 2, so momentum is identical","A 2, B 16; B has stronger momentum","A 50, B 400; B has stronger momentum","A 200, B 25; A has stronger momentum"],"explanationEn":"A: 2 ÷ 1 × 100 = 200; B: 2 ÷ 8 × 100 = 25, i.e. how many units of normal volatility the move represents.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: MACD-V divides by ATR.","Wrong: This multiplies in the wrong direction.","Wrong: This inverts the division.","Correct: A: 2 ÷ 1 × 100 = 200; B: 2 ÷ 8 × 100 = 25, i.e. how many units of normal volatility the move represents."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-98","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[76],"stem":"Mass Index每根的比值=EMA9(高−低)÷EMA9(EMA9(高−低))，再把25根比值相加。若25根比值都恰好为1，Mass Index是多少？","options":["25","225","0.04","1"],"answer":0,"explanation":"25根比值都是1，相加得25；读数常在25附近就是这个原因。","optionExplanations":["正确：25根比值都是1，相加得25。","错误：误把9期与25期相乘。","错误：取了25根比值的倒数，而不是求和。","错误：只算了一根的比值，还没有求25根之和。"],"skills":["计算","基准"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Mass Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589169-mass-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Each Mass Index ratio = EMA9(high − low) ÷ EMA9(EMA9(high − low)), and 25 ratios are summed. If all 25 ratios equal exactly 1, what is the Mass Index?","optionsEn":["25","225","0.04","1"],"explanationEn":"25 ratios of 1 sum to 25, which is why readings tend to hover near 25.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 25 ratios of 1 sum to 25.","Wrong: This multiplies the 9 and 25 periods.","Wrong: This takes the reciprocal instead of summing the 25 ratios.","Wrong: This is only one bar's ratio, not the 25-bar sum."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-99","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[77],"stem":"某天跳空大跌5%，但收盘在当天最高价附近。累积派发线（ADL）会怎样？","options":["下降，ADL按收盘相对昨收的涨跌来累计","下降，ADL按涨跌幅乘以成交量来累计","不变，ADL会把跳空缺口那段排除在外","上升，ADL看收盘在当天区间中的位置"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：跳空下跌却收在当天高位，ADL也可能上升。","optionExplanations":["错误：ADL看收盘在当天高低区间中的位置。","错误：按涨跌幅乘量是PVT的做法。","错误：ADL照常按当天区间位置计算。","正确：跳空下跌却收在高位，ADL也可能上升。"],"skills":["定义","跳空"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Accumulation/Distribution","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501979-chaikin-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"A stock gaps down 5% but closes near the day's high. What happens to the Accumulation/Distribution Line (ADL)?","optionsEn":["Falls; ADL accumulates the close's change versus the prior close","Falls; ADL accumulates percentage change times volume","Unchanged; ADL excludes the gap","Rises; ADL looks at where the close sits in the day's range"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, a gap down that closes near the day's high can still lift the ADL.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: ADL uses where the close sits within the day's high–low range.","Wrong: Percentage change times volume is how PVT works.","Wrong: ADL is calculated from the day's range position as usual.","Correct: A gap down that closes near the high can still lift the ADL."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-100","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[78],"stem":"CMF(20)=+0.25。下面哪项正确？","options":["20根内机构净买入占成交额的25%","20根内成交多伴随收盘落在区间上半部","读数高于0.2，说明价格接下来会上涨","20根内价格累计上涨了约25%，量能配合"],"answer":1,"explanation":"CMF=Σ(位置系数×量)÷Σ量，正值说明成交多伴随偏高的收盘位置。","optionExplanations":["错误：CMF不是实际资金流入占比。","正确：CMF正值说明成交多伴随偏高的收盘位置。","错误：CMF描述过去，不预测未来价格。","错误：CMF不是价格涨幅。"],"skills":["解读","非资金流"],"references":[{"title":"Chaikin Analytics: Chaikin Money Flow","url":"https://help.chaikinanalytics.com/knowledge-center/chaikin-money-flow"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"CMF(20) = +0.25. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["Institutions net-bought 25% of turnover over 20 bars","Over 20 bars, volume mostly came with closes in the upper half of the range","A reading above 0.2 means price will rise next","Price rose about 25% over 20 bars with supportive volume"],"explanationEn":"CMF = Σ(location factor × volume) ÷ Σvolume; a positive value means volume mostly came with higher closing positions.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: CMF is not an actual share of money flowing in.","Correct: A positive CMF means volume mostly came with higher closing positions.","Wrong: CMF describes the past and does not predict future price.","Wrong: CMF is not a price gain."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-70","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[79],"stem":"蔡金振荡器与CMF同时转正。能把它们当成两份独立证据吗？","options":["能，一个是振荡器，一个是资金流","能，因为两者的计算周期不同","不能，因为CMF不使用成交量","不能，两者都源自收盘位置×量"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：和CMF使用近似输入，二者同意不等于两份完全独立的证据。","optionExplanations":["形式不同不代表输入独立。","周期不同仍是同一份原料。","CMF使用成交量。","课程提醒：和CMF使用近似输入，二者同意不等于两份完全独立的证据。"],"skills":["共线性","证据"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chaikin Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501979-chaikin-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The Chaikin Oscillator and CMF both turn positive. Can you treat them as two independent pieces of evidence?","optionsEn":["Yes; one is an oscillator and the other is money flow","Yes, because their calculation periods differ","No, because CMF does not use volume","No; both come from close location × volume"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, it uses inputs close to CMF's, so their agreement is not two fully independent pieces of evidence.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A different form does not mean independent inputs.","Wrong: Different periods still use the same raw material.","Wrong: CMF does use volume.","Correct: As the lesson notes, it uses inputs close to CMF's, so their agreement is not two fully independent pieces of evidence."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-101","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[80],"stem":"克林格振荡器常见参数34/55/13分别指什么？","options":["价格的34期RSI、55期RSI及13期信号线","量能力度的34期、55期EMA及13期信号线","收盘价的34期、55期EMA及13期信号线","成交量的34期、55期SMA及13期信号线"],"answer":1,"explanation":"KVO=量能力度的EMA34−EMA55，再用EMA13做信号线。","optionExplanations":["错误：KVO不使用RSI。","正确：KVO=量能力度EMA34−EMA55，再用EMA13做信号线。","错误：KVO的输入是量能力度，不是收盘价。","错误：用的是量能力度的EMA，不是成交量的SMA。"],"skills":["参数","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Klinger Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589157-klinger-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"What do the common Klinger Oscillator settings 34/55/13 refer to?","optionsEn":["A 34-period RSI, a 55-period RSI and a 13-period signal line","34- and 55-period EMAs of volume force, plus a 13-period signal line","34- and 55-period EMAs of the close, plus a 13-period signal line","34- and 55-period SMAs of volume, plus a 13-period signal line"],"explanationEn":"KVO = EMA34 − EMA55 of volume force, with an EMA13 as the signal line.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: KVO does not use RSI.","Correct: KVO = EMA34 − EMA55 of volume force, with an EMA13 signal line.","Wrong: KVO's input is volume force, not the close.","Wrong: It uses EMAs of volume force, not SMAs of volume."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-71","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[81],"stem":"股票甲价格5元、每天成交1亿股；股票乙价格500元、每天成交10万股。两者的力度指数数值能直接比较强弱吗？","options":["能，数值越大就说明背后的力度越强","不能，数值受价格和成交量量级影响","不能，因为力度指数不适用于低价股","能，两者使用相同的EMA周期设置即可"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：数值受价格和量单位影响，不宜直接跨标的比较。","optionExplanations":["错误：数值大小受价格和量的单位影响。","正确：力度指数不宜直接跨标的比较。","错误：不能比较的原因是量级差异，不是低价股。","错误：周期相同不能消除量级差异。"],"skills":["单位","跨资产比较"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Elder Force Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502259-elder-s-force-index-efi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Stock A trades at 5 with 100 million shares a day; stock B trades at 500 with 100,000 shares a day. Can their Force Index values be compared directly for strength?","optionsEn":["Yes; a bigger number means stronger force behind it","No; the value depends on the scale of price and volume","No, because the Force Index does not work on low-priced stocks","Yes, as long as both use the same EMA period"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, the value depends on price and volume units, so it should not be compared directly across instruments.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The size of the number depends on the units of price and volume.","Correct: The Force Index should not be compared directly across instruments.","Wrong: The reason is the difference in scale, not low prices.","Wrong: The same period does not remove the difference in scale."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-72","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[82],"stem":"EMV原始值=中点变化÷((成交量÷10000)÷(最高−最低))。某根中点上移1，成交量20万，最高−最低为2。EMV原始值是多少？","options":["10","0.4","0.1","2"],"answer":2,"explanation":"(200000÷10000)÷2=10，1÷10=0.1。","optionExplanations":["10是分母（Box Ratio）。","0.4用错了范围。","(200000÷10000)÷2=10，1÷10=0.1。","2是高低差。"],"skills":["计算","比例"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ease of Movement","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502256-ease-of-movement-eom/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Raw EMV = midpoint move ÷ ((volume ÷ 10,000) ÷ (high − low)). On one bar the midpoint rises 1, volume is 200,000 and high − low is 2. What is the raw EMV?","optionsEn":["10","0.4","0.1","2"],"explanationEn":"(200,000 ÷ 10,000) ÷ 2 = 10, and 1 ÷ 10 = 0.1.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 10 is the denominator (the box ratio).","Wrong: 0.4 uses the wrong range.","Correct: (200,000 ÷ 10,000) ÷ 2 = 10, and 1 ÷ 10 = 0.1.","Wrong: 2 is the high–low range."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-102","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[83],"stem":"PVI当前为1000。今天成交量比昨天多，收盘下跌3%。PVI变为多少？","options":["1000","1030","997","970"],"answer":3,"explanation":"放量日按涨跌幅更新：1000×(1−3%)=970。","optionExplanations":["放量日PVI会更新。","方向反了。","把3%当成3点。","放量日按涨跌幅更新：1000×(1−3%)=970。"],"skills":["计算","更新条件"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Positive Volume Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773006-positive-volume-index-pvi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"PVI is currently 1000. Today volume is higher than yesterday and the close falls 3%. What does PVI become?","optionsEn":["1000","1030","997","970"],"explanationEn":"On a higher-volume day it updates by the percentage change: 1000 × (1 − 3%) = 970.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: PVI does update on higher-volume days.","Wrong: The direction is reversed.","Wrong: This treats 3% as 3 points.","Correct: On a higher-volume day it updates by the percentage change: 1000 × (1 − 3%) = 970."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-103","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[84],"stem":"今天成交量比昨天多，收盘上涨5%。NVI会怎样？","options":["不变，NVI只在成交量减少日更新","上升约5%，因为NVI只看收盘涨跌","下降，因为放量日NVI会反向扣减","上升约5%，因为NVI在放量日更新"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：只在量减少时更新，放量时线不动正常。","optionExplanations":["正确：放量日NVI不更新。","错误：NVI还要求成交量减少才更新。","错误：NVI放量日保持不变，不会扣减。","错误：放量日更新的是PVI。"],"skills":["更新条件","NVI"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Negative Volume Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773005-negative-volume-index-nvi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Today volume is higher than yesterday and the close rises 5%. What does NVI do?","optionsEn":["Stays the same; NVI updates only on lower-volume days","Rises about 5%, because NVI looks only at the close","Falls, because NVI subtracts on higher-volume days","Rises about 5%, because NVI updates on higher-volume days"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, it updates only when volume falls, so a flat line on a higher-volume day is normal.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: NVI does not update on a higher-volume day.","Wrong: NVI also needs volume to fall before it updates.","Wrong: NVI stays unchanged on higher-volume days; it does not subtract.","Wrong: PVI is the one that updates on higher-volume days."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-104","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[85],"stem":"一根K线开在最低、收在最高，BOP=1。这能说明什么？","options":["本根成交量放大，买盘力量明显偏强","下一根K线通常会延续这根的上涨走势","本根推进到全幅，但无法反映成交量大小","本根涨幅达到100%，属于极端上涨行情"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：它不含成交量，一根强阳线不证明大量买盘或下一根必涨。","optionExplanations":["BOP不含成交量，无法判断买盘大小。","BOP只描述当前这一根，不预测下一根。","课程提醒：它不含成交量，一根强阳线不证明大量买盘或下一根必涨。","BOP是净推进占高低范围的比例，不是价格涨幅。"],"skills":["局限","无成交量"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Balance of Power","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589100-balance-of-power-bop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"A candle opens at its low and closes at its high, so BOP = 1. What does this tell you?","optionsEn":["Volume expanded on this bar and buying was clearly strong","The next candle will usually extend this bar's rise","This bar moved across its full range, but it says nothing about volume","This bar gained 100%, an extreme rally"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, it contains no volume, so one strong white candle does not prove heavy buying or a rise on the next bar.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: BOP contains no volume, so it cannot gauge the size of buying.","Wrong: BOP describes only the current bar and does not predict the next one.","Correct: As the lesson notes, it contains no volume, so one strong white candle does not prove heavy buying or a rise on the next bar.","Wrong: BOP is the net move as a share of the high–low range, not a price gain."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-105","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[86],"stem":"今天10:00前的累计成交量为36万；过去5个交易日10:00前的累计量分别为30、40、20、30、30万。同时段相对成交量是多少？","options":["1.0","0.83","1.2","12"],"answer":2,"explanation":"过去均值30万，36÷30=1.2。","optionExplanations":["1.0忽略了今天比平均多。","0.83是平均÷今天。","过去均值30万，36÷30=1.2。","12没有除以平均。"],"skills":["计算","同时段比较"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Relative Volume at Time","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000705489-relative-volume-at-time/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Today's cumulative volume before 10:00 is 360,000; over the past 5 sessions it was 300,000, 400,000, 200,000, 300,000 and 300,000 by 10:00. What is the time-of-day relative volume?","optionsEn":["1.0","0.83","1.2","12"],"explanationEn":"The past average is 300,000, and 360,000 ÷ 300,000 = 1.2.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 1.0 ignores that today is above average.","Wrong: 0.83 is average ÷ today.","Correct: The past average is 300,000, and 360,000 ÷ 300,000 = 1.2.","Wrong: 12 skips dividing by the average."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-73","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[87],"stem":"TTM Squeeze的“挤压中”通常用什么条件判断？","options":["布林带整体收进肯特纳通道之内","布林带带宽降到近一年的最低值","肯特纳通道整体收进布林带之内","价格连续数根收在中轨附近窄幅内"],"answer":0,"explanation":"布林带比肯特纳通道更窄，表示波动收缩；具体倍数要核对脚本。","optionExplanations":["布林带比肯特纳通道更窄，表示波动收缩；具体倍数要核对脚本。","带宽低只是相对自己的历史，不是挤压的判断条件。","方向说反了：是布林带比肯特纳通道更窄。","价格贴近中轨不是挤压条件，关键是两种通道的宽窄比较。"],"skills":["定义","脚本差异"],"references":[{"title":"John Carter — Simpler Trading","url":"https://www.simplertrading.com/traders/john-carter/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"What condition is usually used to mark a TTM Squeeze as \"on\"?","optionsEn":["The Bollinger Bands sit entirely inside the Keltner Channel","Bollinger BandWidth hits its lowest level in about a year","The Keltner Channel sits entirely inside the Bollinger Bands","Price closes in a narrow range near the middle band for several bars"],"explanationEn":"Bollinger Bands narrower than the Keltner Channel mean volatility is contracting; check the script for the exact multipliers.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Bollinger Bands narrower than the Keltner Channel mean volatility is contracting; check the script for the exact multipliers.","Wrong: A low BandWidth is relative only to its own history and is not the squeeze condition.","Wrong: This is reversed: the Bollinger Bands are the narrower ones.","Wrong: Price near the middle band is not the condition; the key is comparing the widths of the two channels."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-106","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[88],"stem":"资产A暴涨暴跌但每次都很快收复，资产B缓慢阴跌了两个月。溃疡指数更可能哪个更高？","options":["A；它看价格上下波动幅度有多大","A；它看单日涨跌幅出现得有多频繁","两者接近；它只看区间起点与终点","B；它看回撤有多深、持续多久"],"answer":3,"explanation":"它专门看从近期高位跌下来有多深、低迷了多久。","optionExplanations":["溃疡指数不是波动幅度，快速收复的暴涨暴跌回撤时间短。","它不统计单日涨跌的频繁程度。","它看的是区间内的回撤过程，而不只是起终点。","它专门看从近期高位跌下来有多深、低迷了多久，B更符合。"],"skills":["回撤","与波动率区别"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ulcer Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773115-ulcer-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Asset A has sharp spikes and drops but always recovers quickly; asset B has drifted lower slowly for two months. Which is likely to have the higher Ulcer Index?","optionsEn":["A; it measures how large the swings are","A; it measures how often daily moves occur","About the same; it looks only at the start and end of the period","B; it measures how deep drawdowns are and how long they last"],"explanationEn":"It specifically measures how far price falls from a recent high and how long it stays down.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The Ulcer Index is not swing size; quickly recovered spikes and drops have short drawdowns.","Wrong: It does not count how often daily moves occur.","Wrong: It looks at the drawdown path within the period, not just the start and end.","Correct: It measures how far price falls from a recent high and how long it stays down, which fits B better."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-107","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[89],"stem":"吊灯止损（多头）=最近22根最高价−3×ATR(22)。最高价120，ATR(22)=2.5。止损参考线是多少？","options":["117.5","112.5","117","127.5"],"answer":1,"explanation":"120−3×2.5=112.5。","optionExplanations":["只减了1倍ATR，漏乘了倍数。","120−3×2.5=112.5。","只减了倍数3，忘了乘ATR。","把减号当成加号，方向错了。"],"skills":["计算","ATR倍数"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chandelier Exit","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773013-chandelier-exit/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Chandelier Exit (long) = highest high of the last 22 bars − 3 × ATR(22). The high is 120 and ATR(22) = 2.5. What is the stop line?","optionsEn":["117.5","112.5","117","127.5"],"explanationEn":"120 − 3 × 2.5 = 112.5.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This subtracts only 1 ATR and leaves out the multiplier.","Correct: 120 − 3 × 2.5 = 112.5.","Wrong: This subtracts only the multiplier 3 and forgets the ATR.","Wrong: This adds instead of subtracting, so the direction is wrong."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-74","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[90],"stem":"钱德克罗止损第一步：初始高位止损=p根最高价−x×ATR(p)。p=10根最高价110，ATR(10)=2，x=1。初始值是多少？","options":["112","110","108","106"],"answer":2,"explanation":"110−1×2=108；之后再取最近q根中的极值。","optionExplanations":["加错了方向。","漏减ATR。","110−1×2=108；之后再取最近q根中的极值。","用了2倍ATR。"],"skills":["计算","两步构造"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chande Kroll Stop","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589105-chande-kroll-stop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Chande Kroll Stop step one: initial high stop = highest high of p bars − x × ATR(p). With p = 10, the 10-bar high is 110, ATR(10) = 2 and x = 1. What is the initial value?","optionsEn":["112","110","108","106"],"explanationEn":"110 − 1 × 2 = 108; the extreme over the last q bars is then taken.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This adds in the wrong direction.","Wrong: This leaves out the ATR.","Correct: 110 − 1 × 2 = 108; the extreme over the last q bars is then taken.","Wrong: This uses 2 ATRs."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-108","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[91],"stem":"ATR跟踪止损的倍数从3改为1.5，其余不变。止损线会怎样？","options":["离价格更远，给价格更多回撤空间","离价格更近，但触发机会反而变少","距离不变，只是止损线的更新频率放慢一半","离价格更近，更容易被正常波动触发"],"answer":3,"explanation":"距离=倍数×ATR，倍数减半，线更贴近价格。","optionExplanations":["倍数变小，距离是缩短而不是拉远。","更近的止损线更容易被触发。","倍数改变的是距离，不是更新频率。","正确，距离=倍数×ATR，倍数减半线更贴近价格。"],"skills":["参数影响","止损距离"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volatility Stop methods","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594676-volatility-stop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"An ATR trailing stop's multiplier changes from 3 to 1.5, with everything else unchanged. What happens to the stop line?","optionsEn":["It moves farther from price, giving more room to pull back","It moves closer to price but triggers less often","Same distance; it just updates half as often","It moves closer to price and is more easily hit by normal swings"],"explanationEn":"Distance = multiplier × ATR; halving the multiplier puts the line closer to price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A smaller multiplier shortens the distance rather than widening it.","Wrong: A closer stop is easier to hit.","Wrong: The multiplier changes the distance, not the update frequency.","Correct: Distance = multiplier × ATR, so halving the multiplier puts the line closer to price."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-75","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[92],"stem":"Volatility Stop(20,2)正在向上跟踪：翻转以来最高收盘110，ATR(20)=3，上一根止损103。新止损是多少？","options":["104","103","107","98"],"answer":0,"explanation":"候选=110−2×3=104，比103高，按只上移规则取104。","optionExplanations":["候选=110−2×3=104，比103高，按只上移规则取104。","候选更高，应上移。","只减了1倍ATR。","98用了4倍ATR。"],"skills":["计算","只上移"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volatility Stop","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594676-volatility-stop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Volatility Stop(20, 2) is trailing upward: the highest close since the flip is 110, ATR(20) = 3 and the previous stop is 103. What is the new stop?","optionsEn":["104","103","107","98"],"explanationEn":"The candidate is 110 − 2 × 3 = 104, which is above 103, so under the only-move-up rule it becomes 104.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The candidate is 110 − 2 × 3 = 104, which is above 103, so under the only-move-up rule it becomes 104.","Wrong: The candidate is higher, so the stop should move up.","Wrong: This subtracts only 1 ATR.","Wrong: 98 uses 4 ATRs."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-109","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[93],"stem":"两位分析师在同一张图上从不同锚点画Anchored VWAP，得到两条不同的线。哪个对？","options":["只有锚在最近明显低点的那条才算正确","两条都成立，只是各自对应不同起点","锚点更晚的那条更新，应以它为准","应取两条线的中间值作为真正的VWAP"],"answer":1,"explanation":"锚定VWAP=从你选的起点按量加权的平均价；锚点换了，线就不同。","optionExplanations":["锚点选在哪里是分析选择；换个锚点算出的线同样是正确的锚定VWAP。","锚定VWAP=从你选的起点按量加权的平均价；锚点换了，线就不同，问题也不同。","锚点早晚不决定对错，只决定回答的问题。","VWAP不能把两条线取平均，那样失去了起点含义。"],"skills":["锚点","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Anchored VWAP drawing tool","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000669764-anchored-vwap-drawing-tool/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Two analysts draw Anchored VWAP on the same chart from different anchors and get two different lines. Which is right?","optionsEn":["Only the one anchored at the latest clear low counts","Both are valid; each reflects a different starting point","The later anchor is more recent, so it should be used","The midpoint of the two lines is the true VWAP"],"explanationEn":"Anchored VWAP is the volume-weighted average price from the starting point you choose; change the anchor and the line changes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Where to anchor is an analytical choice; a line from a different anchor is just as valid an anchored VWAP.","Correct: Anchored VWAP is the volume-weighted average price from the starting point you choose; change the anchor and the line changes, and so does the question it answers.","Wrong: An earlier or later anchor does not decide which is right, only which question it answers.","Wrong: Averaging two VWAP lines loses the meaning of their starting points."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-76","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[94],"stem":"前一交易日最高110、最低100、收盘105，P=105。R2=P+(最高−最低)，S2=P−(最高−最低)。R2与S2是多少？","options":["110与100","120与90","112.5与97.5","115与95"],"answer":3,"explanation":"105+10=115，105−10=95。","optionExplanations":["那是R1与S1的数值，不是R2与S2。","把范围加了两次。","只加了半个范围。","105+10=115，105−10=95。"],"skills":["计算","枢轴点"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Pivot formulas and examples","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/v4/essential/drawings/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"The prior session's high is 110, low 100 and close 105, so P = 105. R2 = P + (high − low) and S2 = P − (high − low). What are R2 and S2?","optionsEn":["110 and 100","120 and 90","112.5 and 97.5","115 and 95"],"explanationEn":"105 + 10 = 115 and 105 − 10 = 95.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Those are the R1 and S1 values, not R2 and S2.","Wrong: This adds the range twice.","Wrong: This adds only half the range.","Correct: 105 + 10 = 115 and 105 − 10 = 95."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-110","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[97],"stem":"连续5根K线的最高价依次为10、12、15、13、11（第3根居中）。是否形成向上分形？","options":["是，标在第3根，第5根收完才确认","是，标在第5根，即最新确认的一根","否，常见分形至少要7根K线才成立","否，第3根的收盘价也须是最高才算"],"answer":0,"explanation":"中间一根最高价15高于左右各2根，就是向上分形；要等第5根收完才能确认。","optionExplanations":["中间一根最高价15高于左右各2根，就是向上分形；要等第5根收完才能确认。","分形标在中间那根，而不是最新一根。","常见默认是5根K线。","分形按最高价比较，不看收盘价。"],"skills":["定义","确认"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Williams fractal indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591663-williams-fractal-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Five consecutive highs are 10, 12, 15, 13, 11 (bar 3 is in the middle). Does this form an up fractal?","optionsEn":["Yes, marked on bar 3 and confirmed once bar 5 closes","Yes, marked on bar 5, the newest confirmed bar","No; a fractal usually needs at least 7 bars","No; bar 3's close must also be the highest"],"explanationEn":"The middle bar's high of 15 is above the two bars on each side, so it is an up fractal; it is confirmed only when bar 5 closes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The middle bar's high of 15 is above the two bars on each side, so it is an up fractal; it is confirmed only when bar 5 closes.","Wrong: The fractal is marked on the middle bar, not the newest one.","Wrong: The common default is 5 bars.","Wrong: Fractals compare highs, not closes."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-111","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[98],"stem":"ZigZag门槛设为5%。价格从低点100涨到104，再回落到101。104这个高点会被确认为转折点吗？","options":["会，104是这段上涨的最高点，直接画出","会，价格已从104回落，说明转折成立","不会，回落约2.9%，尚未达到5%门槛","不会，要等价格跌回起点100以下才确认"],"answer":2,"explanation":"确认转折要等从极值反向运动达到门槛；104到101约2.9%，尚未确认。","optionExplanations":["最高点不等于已确认的转折。","只回落一点不足以成立，要达到门槛。","确认转折要等从极值反向运动达到门槛；104到101约2.9%，尚未确认。","确认看反向幅度是否达到门槛，不要求跌回起点。"],"skills":["确认规则","门槛"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Zig Zag","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591664-zig-zag/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"ZigZag's threshold is 5%. Price rises from a low of 100 to 104, then pulls back to 101. Is 104 confirmed as a turning point?","optionsEn":["Yes; 104 is the top of the rise and is drawn right away","Yes; price has pulled back from 104, so the turn holds","No; the pullback is about 2.9%, short of the 5% threshold","No; it is confirmed only after price falls back below 100"],"explanationEn":"A turn is confirmed only when price reverses from the extreme by the threshold; 104 to 101 is about 2.9%, so it is not yet confirmed.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The highest point is not the same as a confirmed turn.","Wrong: A small pullback is not enough; it must reach the threshold.","Correct: A turn is confirmed only when price reverses from the extreme by the threshold; 104 to 101 is about 2.9%, so it is not yet confirmed.","Wrong: Confirmation depends on whether the reversal reaches the threshold, not on falling back to the start."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-112","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[101],"stem":"TradingView内置Volume Delta如何判断每笔量偏买还是偏卖？","options":["读取交易所里真实的买卖账户","用更小周期K线的涨跌来估算","只看本根K线是红色还是绿色","按收盘在高低区间的位置估算"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：内置版本主要用更小周期价格变化估算方向，需看下级周期设置。","optionExplanations":["它不读取账户身份。","课程提醒：内置版本主要用更小周期价格变化估算方向，需看下级周期设置。","单根颜色太粗糙，不是它的方法。","那是ADL一类的方法。"],"skills":["估算方法","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume Delta official tutorial","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XL5KiP2mBUQ"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"How does TradingView's built-in Volume Delta decide whether volume leans to buying or selling?","optionsEn":["It reads real buyer and seller accounts from the exchange","It estimates from the up and down moves of lower-timeframe bars","It looks only at whether this bar is red or green","It estimates from where the close sits in the high–low range"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, the built-in version mainly estimates direction from lower-timeframe price changes, so check the lower-timeframe setting.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It does not read account identities.","Correct: As the lesson notes, the built-in version mainly estimates direction from lower-timeframe price changes, so check the lower-timeframe setting.","Wrong: A single bar's colour is too coarse and is not its method.","Wrong: That is the ADL-style method."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-113","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[102],"stem":"同一个Anchor期间内，三根K线的Delta依次为+300、−100、+50。CVD是多少？","options":["+450","−50","+250","+150"],"answer":2,"explanation":"300−100+50=250。","optionExplanations":["−100应减去。","符号算错。","300−100+50=250。","漏加了+50或多减了。"],"skills":["累计","计算"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Cumulative Volume Delta","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000725058-cumulative-volume-delta/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"Within the same anchor period, three bars have deltas of +300, −100 and +50. What is the CVD?","optionsEn":["+450","−50","+250","+150"],"explanationEn":"300 − 100 + 50 = 250.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The −100 should be subtracted.","Wrong: The signs are wrong.","Correct: 300 − 100 + 50 = 250.","Wrong: This leaves out the +50 or subtracts too much."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-114","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[104],"stem":"某日上涨1800家、下跌1200家、平盘100家。昨日腾落线为5000。今日腾落线是多少？","options":["5700","6800","5600","4400"],"answer":2,"explanation":"5000+(1800−1200)=5600，平盘不计。","optionExplanations":["把平盘也加了。","只加了上涨家数。","5000+(1800−1200)=5600，平盘不计。","把差额符号弄反，减成了下跌多于上涨。"],"skills":["计算","累计"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Advance/Decline Line","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589092-advance-decline-line/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"On one day 1,800 stocks advance, 1,200 decline and 100 are unchanged. Yesterday's advance-decline line was 5,000. What is today's value?","optionsEn":["5,700","6,800","5,600","4,400"],"explanationEn":"5,000 + (1,800 − 1,200) = 5,600; unchanged stocks are not counted.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This also adds the unchanged stocks.","Wrong: This adds only the advancers.","Correct: 5,000 + (1,800 − 1,200) = 5,600; unchanged stocks are not counted.","Wrong: This flips the sign of the difference, as if decliners outnumbered advancers."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-115","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[105],"stem":"某日52周新高150家、新低30家。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["新高远多于新低，说明上涨的参与面偏广","新高减新低的120，就是指数的涨幅点数","新低只有30家，所以明天通常继续走高","新高家数这么多，说明指数已在历史高位"],"answer":0,"explanation":"新高新低数描述广度，不描述涨幅。","optionExplanations":["新高新低数描述广度，不描述涨幅，也不预测明天。","家数之差不是指数涨幅。","广度不预测明天走势。","新高家数只说明参与面，不能确定指数位置。"],"skills":["广度","解读"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Market breadth — New highs and lows","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000794826-market-breadth-new-highs-and-lows/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"second-question-per-topic","stemEn":"On one day there are 150 new 52-week highs and 30 new lows. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["New highs far outnumber new lows, so participation in the rise is broad","The 120 of highs minus lows is the index's gain in points","Only 30 new lows means the market usually keeps rising tomorrow","So many new highs means the index is at an all-time high"],"explanationEn":"New-high and new-low counts describe breadth, not the size of the gain.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: New-high and new-low counts describe breadth, not the size of the gain, and they do not predict tomorrow.","Wrong: The difference in counts is not the index's gain.","Wrong: Breadth does not predict tomorrow's move.","Wrong: The number of new highs shows participation only; it cannot pin down where the index stands."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-116","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[1],"stem":"SMA设置里把Offset从0改成5，线会怎样？","options":["整条线向左平移5根，提前显示未来均值","只用最近5根K线重新计算，线更灵敏","跳过最近5根，改用更早的20根来计算","整条线向右平移5根显示，计算不变"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Offset只移动显示位置，不改变用哪些K线计算。","optionExplanations":["正的Offset向右平移，且不会得到未来数据。","用几根K线是Length决定的。","Offset不改变计算所用的数据。","Offset只移动显示位置，不改变用哪些K线计算。"],"skills":["设置","Offset"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Simple Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000696841-simple-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In an SMA's settings, Offset changes from 0 to 5. What happens to the line?","optionsEn":["The whole line shifts 5 bars left and shows the future average early","It recalculates using only the last 5 bars, so it is more sensitive","It skips the latest 5 bars and uses 20 earlier bars instead","The whole line is drawn 5 bars to the right; the calculation is unchanged"],"explanationEn":"Offset only moves where the line is drawn; it does not change which bars are used.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A positive Offset shifts right, and it never produces future data.","Wrong: The number of bars used is set by Length.","Wrong: Offset does not change the data used in the calculation.","Correct: Offset only moves where the line is drawn; it does not change which bars are used."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-117","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[2],"stem":"EMA设置中把Source从Close改成HL2，这条线计算的是什么？","options":["每根K线最高价与收盘价中点的指数平均","每根K线最高价与最低价中点的指数平均","每根K线开盘价与收盘价中点的指数平均","每根K线最高、最低、收盘三者均值的指数平均"],"answer":1,"explanation":"HL2是每根K线最高与最低的中点，EMA对这串中点做指数平均。","optionExplanations":["HL2不含收盘价。","HL2是每根K线最高与最低的中点，EMA对这串中点做指数平均。","那是开收均价，不是HL2。","那是HLC3，含收盘价。"],"skills":["设置","Source"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Moving Averages","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502589-moving-averages/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In an EMA's settings, Source changes from Close to HL2. What does the line now calculate?","optionsEn":["An exponential average of each bar's high–close midpoint","An exponential average of each bar's high–low midpoint","An exponential average of each bar's open–close midpoint","An exponential average of each bar's high, low and close mean"],"explanationEn":"HL2 is the midpoint of each bar's high and low, and the EMA averages that series of midpoints exponentially.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: HL2 does not include the close.","Correct: HL2 is the midpoint of each bar's high and low, and the EMA averages that series of midpoints exponentially.","Wrong: That is the open–close average, not HL2.","Wrong: That is HLC3, which includes the close."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-118","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[3],"stem":"WMA(20)和EMA(20)在“用到哪些K线”上有什么区别？","options":["WMA还含更早价格；EMA仅用最近20根","WMA仅用最近20根；EMA还含更早价格","两者都只用最近20根，仅权重分配不同","两者都含全部历史，仅衰减快慢不同"],"answer":1,"explanation":"WMA窗口外的价格完全不计；EMA的旧价格影响逐渐变小但不会被删除。","optionExplanations":["刚好说反了。","WMA窗口外的价格不计；EMA的旧价格影响逐渐变小但不会被删除。","EMA并不局限于20根。","WMA窗口外的价格不再计入。"],"skills":["窗口","权重"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Weighted Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594680-weighted-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How do WMA(20) and EMA(20) differ in which bars they use?","optionsEn":["WMA also includes older prices; EMA uses only the last 20 bars","WMA uses only the last 20 bars; EMA also includes older prices","Both use only the last 20 bars and differ only in weighting","Both include all history and differ only in decay speed"],"explanationEn":"Prices outside the WMA window are not counted at all; in an EMA, older prices fade but are never dropped.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This is exactly reversed.","Correct: Prices outside the WMA window are not counted; in an EMA, older prices fade but are never dropped.","Wrong: An EMA is not limited to 20 bars.","Wrong: Prices outside the WMA window are no longer counted."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-119","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[4],"stem":"RSI和ATR的经典算法内部，用的是哪一种平滑？","options":["EMA，按2/(N+1)比例吸收新值","SMA，丢掉最旧值后对N根等权平均","Wilder RMA，按1/N吸收新值","WMA，对最近N根做线性加权平均"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Wilder在RSI与ATR中用的就是每次吸收1/N新值的平滑，即RMA。","optionExplanations":["EMA的系数不同，经典RSI与ATR用的不是它。","SMA没有递推平滑，不是经典算法。","正确，RSI与ATR经典算法用RMA。","WMA不是Wilder所用的平滑。"],"skills":["RMA","来源"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Smoothed Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591343-smoothed-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which smoothing do the classic RSI and ATR formulas use internally?","optionsEn":["EMA, taking in new values at 2/(N + 1)","SMA, equal-weighting N bars after dropping the oldest","Wilder's RMA, taking in new values at 1/N","WMA, a linearly weighted average of the last N bars"],"explanationEn":"In RSI and ATR, Wilder used smoothing that takes in 1/N of each new value, i.e. RMA.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: An EMA uses a different factor; it is not what classic RSI and ATR use.","Wrong: An SMA has no recursive smoothing and is not the classic method.","Correct: Classic RSI and ATR use RMA.","Wrong: WMA is not the smoothing Wilder used."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-77","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[5],"stem":"在一个成交量只代表报价笔数（tick volume）的品种上加VWMA，第一步应做什么？","options":["先把Source从Close改成HLC3","先把周期加长以减少噪声","先换成EMA再观察结果","先确认成交量来源是否真实"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：先确认品种有真实可用的成交量，再加VWMA。","optionExplanations":["价格源与成交量来源无关。","周期长短不改变量的含义。","平台不会自动换算。","课程提醒：先确认品种有真实可用的成交量，再加VWMA。"],"skills":["数据来源","前置检查"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Volume-Weighted Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592293-volume-weighted-moving-average-vwma/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"You add a VWMA to an instrument whose volume only counts quote updates (tick volume). What should you do first?","optionsEn":["Change Source from Close to HLC3","Lengthen the period to cut noise","Switch to an EMA and see what happens","Check whether the volume source is real"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, first confirm the instrument has real, usable volume before adding a VWMA.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The price source has nothing to do with the volume source.","Wrong: The period length does not change what the volume means.","Wrong: The platform does not convert it for you.","Correct: As the lesson notes, first confirm the instrument has real, usable volume before adding a VWMA."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-120","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[6],"stem":"同一张图上HMA(20)比SMA(20)先拐头。第一次使用HMA时，较合适的理解是？","options":["拐头较早，可视为趋势已经成立","拐头较晚，因为经过了多次平滑","拐头较早，可据此预判下一根方向","滞后较少，但横盘时也会反复拐头"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：减少滞后不等于没有滞后，更不等于没有假信号。","optionExplanations":["拐头只是平均线变化，不是趋势确认。","HMA设计目的是减少滞后，通常拐得更早。","它仍用已收盘价格计算，不能预判下一根。","课程提醒：减少滞后不等于没有滞后，更不等于没有假信号。"],"skills":["滞后","假信号"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Hull Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589149-hull-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"On the same chart, HMA(20) turns before SMA(20). Using HMA for the first time, what is the sensible reading?","optionsEn":["It turns earlier, so the trend can be treated as established","It turns later, because it is smoothed several times","It turns earlier, so you can call the next bar's direction","It lags less, but it also turns back and forth in ranges"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, less lag is not zero lag, still less zero false signals.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A turn is only a change in the average, not trend confirmation.","Wrong: HMA is designed to reduce lag, so it usually turns earlier.","Wrong: It is still calculated from closed prices and cannot predict the next bar.","Correct: As the lesson notes, less lag is not zero lag, still less zero false signals."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-121","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[7],"stem":"关于DEMA，下面哪项描述正确？","options":["对价格连续做两次EMA得到的线","把两条不同周期的EMA取平均得到的线","用2×EMA减EMA的EMA合成的线","把EMA周期缩短一半后得到的线"],"answer":2,"explanation":"DEMA=2×EMA−EMA(EMA)，课程强调不是简单画两条EMA。","optionExplanations":["这只是双重平滑，没有2×EMA−EMA(EMA)的合成。","DEMA不是两条EMA的平均。","正确，DEMA由两者合成。","DEMA不是改周期，而是合成公式。"],"skills":["定义","易混"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Double Exponential Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589132-double-exponential-moving-average-ema/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which description of DEMA is correct?","optionsEn":["A line made by applying an EMA to price twice","A line averaging two EMAs of different periods","A line combining 2 × EMA minus the EMA of the EMA","A line made by halving the EMA period"],"explanationEn":"DEMA = 2 × EMA − EMA(EMA); the lesson stresses that it is not simply two EMAs drawn on the chart.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is just double smoothing, without the 2 × EMA − EMA(EMA) combination.","Wrong: DEMA is not the average of two EMAs.","Correct: DEMA combines the two.","Wrong: DEMA does not change the period; it is a combination formula."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-78","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[8],"stem":"TEMA(20)比EMA(20)更贴近价格。这样做的代价通常是什么？","options":["对小波动更敏感，容易被来回扫动误导","线更平滑，代价是转弯时间更晚","对成交量依赖更高，缺量时会失真","线贴价更紧，穿越价格的次数反而更少"],"answer":0,"explanation":"三层EMA让滞后更小，代价是对小波动更敏感；课程提醒“三重”不代表三倍可靠。","optionExplanations":["三层EMA让滞后更小，代价是对小波动更敏感；课程提醒“三重”不代表三倍可靠。","更平滑更晚是加长周期的效果，与TEMA相反。","TEMA只用价格，不用成交量。","贴价更紧通常穿越更频繁，而不是更少。"],"skills":["取舍","敏感度"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Triple EMA","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591346-triple-ema/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"TEMA(20) hugs price more closely than EMA(20). What is the usual cost?","optionsEn":["More sensitivity to small moves, so whipsaws can mislead","A smoother line at the cost of turning later","More dependence on volume, so it distorts without it","It hugs price tighter yet crosses price less often"],"explanationEn":"Three layers of EMA reduce lag at the cost of more sensitivity to small moves; the lesson notes that \"triple\" does not mean three times as reliable.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Three layers of EMA reduce lag at the cost of more sensitivity to small moves; the lesson notes that \"triple\" does not mean three times as reliable.","Wrong: Smoother and later is the effect of a longer period, the opposite of TEMA.","Wrong: TEMA uses only price, not volume.","Wrong: Hugging price tighter usually means crossing it more often, not less."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-122","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[9],"stem":"在TradingView添加内置MA Cross后，图上两条线的默认周期是多少？","options":["20和50","12和26","50和200","9和21"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程注明：官方默认MA9与MA21，可再调整。","optionExplanations":["20/50不是本指标默认。","12/26是MACD的参数。","50/200是常见“黄金交叉”讨论用的长周期，不是本指标默认。","课程注明：官方默认MA9与MA21，可再调整。"],"skills":["默认参数","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — MA Cross","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000599879-ma-cross/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"After adding TradingView's built-in MA Cross, what are the default periods of its two lines?","optionsEn":["20 and 50","12 and 26","50 and 200","9 and 21"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes the official defaults are MA9 and MA21, which you can change.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 20/50 is not this indicator's default.","Wrong: 12/26 are MACD settings.","Wrong: 50/200 is the long-period pair often discussed for a \"golden cross\", not this indicator's default.","Correct: The lesson notes the official defaults are MA9 and MA21, which you can change."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-123","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[10],"stem":"TradingView内置Moving Average Ribbon最多显示几条均线？每条能单独设置什么？","options":["6条，类型和周期可分别设置","4条，类型须统一，仅周期可调","4条，类型和周期可分别设置","3条，周期固定，仅类型可调"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程注明：最多四条，可分别选类型、周期和是否显示。","optionExplanations":["条数不对，课程是四条。","类型也可以分别选择。","课程注明：最多四条，可分别选类型、周期和是否显示。","条数不对，周期也可调。"],"skills":["设置","条数"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Moving Average Ribbon","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644913-moving-average-ribbon/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How many averages can TradingView's built-in Moving Average Ribbon show, and what can be set for each one?","optionsEn":["6, each with its own type and period","4, with one shared type; only periods change","4, each with its own type and period","3, with fixed periods; only the type changes"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes up to four, each with its own type, period and visibility.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Wrong count; the lesson says four.","Wrong: The type can also be chosen separately.","Correct: The lesson notes up to four, each with its own type, period and visibility.","Wrong: Wrong count, and the periods can also be changed."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-124","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[11],"stem":"RSI(14)读数在50附近，最基础的含义是？","options":["收盘处在近14根高低区间的中间位置","近14根里上涨的K线根数约占一半","近14根平均涨幅与平均跌幅大致相当","近14根平均成交量处在中间水平"],"answer":2,"explanation":"RSI比较平滑后的平均涨幅与平均跌幅，50表示两者接近。","optionExplanations":["那是随机指标%K=50的含义。","RSI比较的是幅度，不是K线根数。","RSI比较平滑后的平均涨幅与平均跌幅，50表示两者接近。","RSI不使用成交量。"],"skills":["读数含义","基础"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Relative Strength Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502338-relative-strength-index-rsi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the most basic meaning of an RSI(14) reading near 50?","optionsEn":["The close is mid-way in the 14-bar high–low range","About half of the last 14 bars closed up","Average gains and average losses over 14 bars are about equal","Average volume over 14 bars is at a middling level"],"explanationEn":"RSI compares smoothed average gains with smoothed average losses; 50 means the two are close.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is what stochastic %K = 50 means.","Wrong: RSI compares the size of moves, not the number of bars.","Correct: RSI compares smoothed average gains with smoothed average losses; 50 means the two are close.","Wrong: RSI does not use volume."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-125","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[12],"stem":"MACD的默认参数12、26、9分别指什么？","options":["快线EMA12、慢线EMA26、信号线EMA9","快线EMA9、慢线EMA12、信号线EMA26","快线EMA26、慢线EMA12、信号线EMA9","快线SMA12、慢线SMA26、信号线SMA9"],"answer":0,"explanation":"MACD线=EMA12−EMA26，信号线是MACD线的9期EMA。","optionExplanations":["MACD线=EMA12−EMA26，信号线是MACD线的9期EMA。","参数顺序与含义对不上。","快慢线颠倒了，12期才是快线。","默认用EMA，不是SMA。"],"skills":["参数","结构"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — MACD","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502344-macd-moving-average-convergence-divergence/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do MACD's default settings 12, 26, 9 mean?","optionsEn":["Fast EMA12, slow EMA26, signal EMA9","Fast EMA9, slow EMA12, signal EMA26","Fast EMA26, slow EMA12, signal EMA9","Fast SMA12, slow SMA26, signal SMA9"],"explanationEn":"MACD line = EMA12 − EMA26, and the signal line is a 9-period EMA of the MACD line.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: MACD line = EMA12 − EMA26, and the signal line is a 9-period EMA of the MACD line.","Wrong: The order does not match the meanings.","Wrong: Fast and slow are swapped; 12 is the fast line.","Wrong: The default uses EMAs, not SMAs."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-126","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[13],"stem":"Stochastic设置为14、3、3。第一个“14”控制什么？","options":["%K线要再平滑多少根","%D线要再平滑多少根","收盘价与几根前的价格比较","回看几根取最高最低价"],"answer":3,"explanation":"14是计算原始%K时取最高最低的窗口。","optionExplanations":["%K平滑是第二个参数。","%D平滑是第三个参数。","随机指标比较的是区间位置，不是与几根前价格比较。","14是计算原始%K时取最高最低的窗口。"],"skills":["参数","窗口"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Stochastic","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502332-stochastic-stoch/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"A Stochastic is set to 14, 3, 3. What does the first 14 control?","optionsEn":["How many bars smooth the %K line","How many bars smooth the %D line","How many bars back the close is compared with","How many bars to look back for the high and low"],"explanationEn":"14 is the window for the high and low used in the raw %K.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: %K smoothing is the second setting.","Wrong: %D smoothing is the third setting.","Wrong: The stochastic compares position in a range, not price a number of bars ago.","Correct: 14 is the window for the high and low used in the raw %K."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-127","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[14],"stem":"Williams %R(14)在5根K线内从−90升到−15。最直接的描述是？","options":["收盘从区间顶部附近移到底部附近","收盘从区间底部附近移到顶部附近","多空力量对比从偏空转为接近平衡","近14根的高低区间宽度明显收窄了"],"answer":1,"explanation":"%R从接近−100移到接近0，就是收盘位置由底到顶。","optionExplanations":["方向说反了：越接近0越靠近顶部。","%R从接近−100移到接近0，就是收盘位置由底到顶。","−15已很靠近顶部，不是平衡点。","读数变化描述位置，不是区间宽度。"],"skills":["位置","读数变化"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Williams %R","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501985-williams-r-r/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Williams %R(14) rises from −90 to −15 within 5 bars. What is the most direct description?","optionsEn":["The close moved from near the top of the range to near the bottom","The close moved from near the bottom of the range to near the top","The balance of buyers and sellers moved from bearish to roughly even","The 14-bar high–low range narrowed sharply"],"explanationEn":"%R moving from near −100 to near 0 means the close moved from the bottom of the range to the top.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This is reversed: the closer to 0, the closer to the top.","Correct: %R moving from near −100 to near 0 means the close moved from the bottom of the range to the top.","Wrong: −15 is already near the top, not a balance point.","Wrong: The reading describes position, not range width."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-128","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[15],"stem":"TradingView内置CCI默认使用哪种价格源？","options":["OC2，即(开盘价+收盘价)÷2","HLC3，即(最高+最低+收)÷3","HL2，即(最高价+最低价)÷2","OHLC4，即(开高低收四价)÷4"],"answer":1,"explanation":"CCI经典定义与内置默认都用典型价HLC3。","optionExplanations":["OC2不是CCI默认。","CCI经典定义与内置默认都用典型价HLC3。","HL2不含收盘价。","OHLC4含开盘价，不是CCI默认。"],"skills":["价格源","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Commodity Channel Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502001-commodity-channel-index-cci/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which price source does TradingView's built-in CCI use by default?","optionsEn":["OC2, i.e. (open + close) ÷ 2","HLC3, i.e. (high + low + close) ÷ 3","HL2, i.e. (high + low) ÷ 2","OHLC4, i.e. (open + high + low + close) ÷ 4"],"explanationEn":"Both the classic definition of CCI and the built-in default use the typical price, HLC3.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: OC2 is not CCI's default.","Correct: Both the classic definition of CCI and the built-in default use the typical price, HLC3.","Wrong: HL2 does not include the close.","Wrong: OHLC4 includes the open and is not CCI's default."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-129","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[16],"stem":"ROC(10)的零线代表什么？","options":["当前收盘与近10根平均收盘相同","近10根里涨跌的K线根数各一半","当前收盘与10根前的开盘相同","当前收盘与10根前的收盘相同"],"answer":3,"explanation":"ROC=(现价÷10根前−1)×100%，等于零即两者相同。","optionExplanations":["ROC不与平均价比较。","ROC比较的是价格，不是涨跌根数。","ROC比较的是收盘与收盘。","ROC=(现价÷10根前−1)×100%，等于零即两者相同。"],"skills":["零线","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Rate of Change","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502343-rate-of-change-roc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the zero line of ROC(10) represent?","optionsEn":["The current close equals the 10-bar average close","Half of the last 10 bars rose and half fell","The current close equals the open 10 bars ago","The current close equals the close 10 bars ago"],"explanationEn":"ROC = (current price ÷ price 10 bars ago − 1) × 100%, so zero means the two are equal.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: ROC does not compare with an average price.","Wrong: ROC compares prices, not counts of up and down bars.","Wrong: ROC compares close with close.","Correct: ROC = (current price ÷ price 10 bars ago − 1) × 100%, so zero means the two are equal."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-130","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[17],"stem":"指标列表里同时有“Momentum”和“Momentum Strategy”。想学习读动量读数，应选哪个？为什么？","options":["Momentum；另一个是回测策略版","Strategy版；买卖标记更直观","Momentum；另一个需要付费订阅","任选其一；两者读数相同，仅画法不同"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：不要误选Momentum Strategy，后者是策略回测。","optionExplanations":["课程提醒：不要误选Momentum Strategy，后者是策略回测。","策略版是回测工具，不是读数指标。","两者区别不在付费，而在用途。","两者用途不同，不能随便互换。"],"skills":["设置辨认","策略与指标"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Momentum","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589187-momentum/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The indicator list has both \"Momentum\" and \"Momentum Strategy\". To learn to read momentum values, which should you choose, and why?","optionsEn":["Momentum; the other is a backtesting strategy version","The Strategy version; its buy/sell marks are clearer","Momentum; the other needs a paid subscription","Either; both give the same reading and only draw differently"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, don't pick Momentum Strategy by mistake; it is for strategy backtesting.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: As the lesson notes, don't pick Momentum Strategy by mistake; it is for strategy backtesting.","Wrong: The strategy version is a backtesting tool, not a reading indicator.","Wrong: The difference is purpose, not payment.","Wrong: They serve different purposes and cannot be swapped freely."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-131","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[18],"stem":"PPO面板里的柱状图表示什么？","options":["PPO线与零线之间的距离","价格与快均线之间的百分比距离","PPO线减去它的信号线","快均线与慢均线之间的价差"],"answer":2,"explanation":"与MACD一样，柱=主线−信号线，只是单位为%。","optionExplanations":["柱是主线与信号线之差，不是与零线的距离。","那更接近包络或%距离。","与MACD一样，柱=主线−信号线，只是单位为%。","那是MACD线的价差，不是PPO柱。"],"skills":["柱状图","结构"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Percentage Price Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502346-percentage-price-oscillator-ppo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the histogram in the PPO panel show?","optionsEn":["The distance between the PPO line and zero","The percentage distance between price and the fast average","The PPO line minus its signal line","The price gap between the fast and slow averages"],"explanationEn":"As with MACD, histogram = main line − signal line; the unit is just %.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The histogram is the main line minus the signal line, not the distance to zero.","Wrong: That is closer to an envelope or percentage distance.","Correct: As with MACD, histogram = main line − signal line; the unit is just %.","Wrong: That is the MACD line's price gap, not the PPO histogram."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-132","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[19],"stem":"MFI在什么情况下读数不可靠，应先检查？","options":["图表使用了日线而不是分钟线","品种的价格波动幅度偏大","品种没有可用的成交量数据","品种上市时间还不到一年"],"answer":2,"explanation":"MFI依赖成交量；课程提醒先确认有成交量再添加。","optionExplanations":["日线可以正常使用。","波动大小不影响MFI可用性。","MFI依赖成交量；课程提醒先确认有成交量再添加。","MFI只需要14根左右的数据。"],"skills":["前置检查","成交量"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Money Flow Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502348-money-flow-mfi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"When is an MFI reading unreliable, so that you should check first?","optionsEn":["When the chart uses daily bars instead of minute bars","When the instrument's price swings are large","When the instrument has no usable volume data","When the instrument has been listed for less than a year"],"explanationEn":"MFI depends on volume; the lesson reminds you to confirm there is volume before adding it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Daily bars work fine.","Wrong: Swing size does not affect whether MFI is usable.","Correct: MFI depends on volume; the lesson reminds you to confirm there is volume before adding it.","Wrong: MFI needs only about 14 bars of data."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-79","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[20],"stem":"某根K线的Bull Power为+3，Bear Power为+1（Elder原版两条线）。这说明什么？","options":["最高价与最低价都在EMA13上方","买方成交人数约是卖方的3倍","最低价低于EMA13，最高价高于它","读数有误，Bear不应出现正数"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Bear Power=最低价−EMA13为正，表示连最低价都高于EMA13。","optionExplanations":["Bear Power=最低价−EMA13为正，表示连最低价都高于EMA13。","指标只由价格推算，不知道人数。","最低价低于EMA时Bear Power才是负数。","最低价高于EMA时Bear Power就是正数。"],"skills":["读数","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bull Bear Power","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000717955-bull-bear-power/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"On one bar, Bull Power is +3 and Bear Power is +1 (Elder's original two lines). What does this mean?","optionsEn":["Both the high and the low are above EMA13","There were about 3 times as many buyers as sellers","The low is below EMA13 and the high is above it","The reading is wrong; Bear Power cannot be positive"],"explanationEn":"Bear Power = low − EMA13; a positive value means even the low is above EMA13.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Bear Power = low − EMA13; a positive value means even the low is above EMA13.","Wrong: The indicator is derived from price alone and knows nothing about head counts.","Wrong: Bear Power is negative only when the low is below the EMA.","Wrong: When the low is above the EMA, Bear Power is positive."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-133","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[21],"stem":"布林带默认参数20、2是什么意思？","options":["中轨20期EMA，上下轨为±2倍标准差","中轨20期SMA，上下轨为±2倍ATR","中轨20期EMA，上下轨为±2倍ATR","中轨20期SMA，上下轨为±2倍标准差"],"answer":3,"explanation":"这是布林带的标准定义。","optionExplanations":["布林带默认中轨是SMA。","±2倍ATR是肯特纳通道的思路。","中轨和宽度来源都不是布林带默认。","这是布林带的标准定义。"],"skills":["参数","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bollinger Bands","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501840-bollinger-bands-bb/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do the Bollinger Bands defaults 20, 2 mean?","optionsEn":["A 20-period EMA middle band with bands at ±2 standard deviations","A 20-period SMA middle band with bands at ±2 ATR","A 20-period EMA middle band with bands at ±2 ATR","A 20-period SMA middle band with bands at ±2 standard deviations"],"explanationEn":"That is the standard definition of Bollinger Bands.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The default Bollinger middle band is an SMA.","Wrong: ±2 ATR is the Keltner Channel approach.","Wrong: Neither the middle band nor the width source is the Bollinger default.","Correct: That is the standard definition of Bollinger Bands."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-134","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[22],"stem":"想知道“布林带此刻有多宽”，应该看哪个指标？","options":["%B，把上下轨距离换成0到1的数","BandWidth，量上下轨的距离","Keltner，是布林带上下轨的间距","Donchian，是最近高低价的差距"],"answer":1,"explanation":"BandWidth把上下轨距离变成一个数字。","optionExplanations":["%B看收盘在带中的位置，不是宽度。","BandWidth把上下轨距离变成一个数字。","肯特纳是另一种通道，不是布林带宽度。","唐奇安是最高最低价通道，不是布林带宽度。"],"skills":["选择指标","用途"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bollinger BandWidth","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501972-bollinger-bandwidth-bbw/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"To find out how wide the Bollinger Bands are right now, which indicator should you check?","optionsEn":["%B, which turns the band gap into a number from 0 to 1","BandWidth, which measures the distance between the bands","Keltner, which is the gap between the Bollinger Bands","Donchian, which is the gap between recent highs and lows"],"explanationEn":"BandWidth turns the distance between the bands into a single number.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: %B shows where the close sits within the bands, not their width.","Correct: BandWidth turns the distance between the bands into a single number.","Wrong: Keltner is a different channel, not Bollinger width.","Wrong: Donchian is a high–low channel, not Bollinger width."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-135","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[23],"stem":"%B读数为0.5时，收盘在布林带的哪里？","options":["下轨上","上轨上","轨道之外","中轨附近"],"answer":3,"explanation":"0是下轨、0.5是中间、1是上轨。","optionExplanations":["下轨对应0。","上轨对应1。","轨道外对应小于0或大于1。","0是下轨、0.5是中间、1是上轨。"],"skills":["位置","刻度"],"references":[{"title":"John Bollinger — %b companion indicator","url":"https://www.bollingerbands.com/bollinger-bands"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"When %B reads 0.5, where is the close relative to the Bollinger Bands?","optionsEn":["On the lower band","On the upper band","Outside the bands","Near the middle band"],"explanationEn":"0 is the lower band, 0.5 the middle and 1 the upper band.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The lower band corresponds to 0.","Wrong: The upper band corresponds to 1.","Wrong: Outside the bands means below 0 or above 1.","Correct: 0 is the lower band, 0.5 the middle and 1 the upper band."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-136","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[24],"stem":"唐奇安通道(20)的上轨取的是什么价格？","options":["最近20根K线的最高收盘价","最近20根的最高价（含影线）","最近20根K线最高价的平均值","最近20根最高价与最低价的中点"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程定义：上轨记录最近N根的最高价，下轨记录最低价。","optionExplanations":["上轨按最高价，不是收盘价。","课程定义：上轨记录最近N根的最高价，下轨记录最低价。","上轨取最高价本身，不取平均。","那是中线的算法，不是上轨。"],"skills":["定义","价格源"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Donchian Channels","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502253-donchian-channels-dc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What price does the upper line of a Donchian Channel(20) use?","optionsEn":["The highest close of the last 20 bars","The highest high of the last 20 bars, wicks included","The average of the last 20 bars' highs","The midpoint of the last 20 bars' high and low"],"explanationEn":"By the lesson's definition, the upper line tracks the highest high of the last N bars and the lower line the lowest low.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The upper line uses highs, not closes.","Correct: By the lesson's definition, the upper line tracks the highest high of the last N bars and the lower line the lowest low.","Wrong: The upper line takes the highest high itself, not an average.","Wrong: That is how the middle line is calculated, not the upper line."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-137","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[25],"stem":"本课练习Keltner Channels时，要求把“Bands Style”设为哪一项（也是平台默认）？","options":["True Range（单根波幅）","Range（当根最高价减最低价）","Standard Deviation","Average True Range"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程要求确认Bands Style选ATR，即平均真实波幅。","optionExplanations":["True Range是单根真实波幅，没有平均。","Range只用当根高低差，不含跳空。","标准差是布林带的宽度来源。","课程要求确认Bands Style选ATR，即平均真实波幅。"],"skills":["设置","宽度算法"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Keltner Channels","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502266-keltner-channels-kc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"When practising Keltner Channels in this lesson, which Bands Style must you select (also the platform default)?","optionsEn":["True Range (a single bar's range)","Range (the bar's high minus low)","Standard Deviation","Average True Range"],"explanationEn":"The lesson asks you to confirm that Bands Style is set to ATR, the average true range.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: True Range is a single bar's true range, with no averaging.","Wrong: Range uses only the bar's high–low and ignores gaps.","Wrong: Standard deviation is where Bollinger width comes from.","Correct: The lesson asks you to confirm that Bands Style is set to ATR, the average true range."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-138","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[26],"stem":"Envelope设置里勾选“Exponential”后，会改变什么？","options":["上下轨偏移由百分比改为按ATR计算","上下轨宽度由固定百分比改为按标准差计算","中间线的均线类型由SMA改为EMA","价格源由收盘价改为最高价与最低价平均"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：确认用SMA还是EMA，这个选项就决定中线类型。","optionExplanations":["该选项不改变轨道偏移的算法。","那是布林带的做法，不是此选项。","正确，该选项决定中线类型。","该选项与价格源无关。"],"skills":["设置","中线类型"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Envelope","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502260-envelope-env/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What changes when you tick \"Exponential\" in the Envelope settings?","optionsEn":["The band offset is calculated from ATR instead of a percentage","The band width uses standard deviation instead of a fixed percentage","The middle line's average changes from SMA to EMA","The price source changes from the close to the high–low average"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, confirm whether it uses SMA or EMA; this option sets the middle line's type.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The option does not change how the band offset is calculated.","Wrong: That is the Bollinger approach, not this option.","Correct: This option sets the middle line's type.","Wrong: The option has nothing to do with the price source."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-139","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[27],"stem":"ATR(14)读数为2.5。它的单位是什么？","options":["与价格相同的单位，如美元","百分比，即价格的2.5%","0到100之间的强度分数","与成交量相同的单位，如股数"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ATR是价格距离，单位与报价相同。","optionExplanations":["ATR是价格距离，单位与报价相同。","百分比是ATR%（NATR）的单位。","ATR没有固定上下限。","ATR不用成交量。"],"skills":["单位","读数"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Average True Range","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501823-average-true-range-atr/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"ATR(14) reads 2.5. What is its unit?","optionsEn":["The same unit as price, such as dollars","A percentage, i.e. 2.5% of price","A strength score from 0 to 100","The same unit as volume, such as shares"],"explanationEn":"ATR is a price distance, in the same unit as the quote.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: ATR is a price distance, in the same unit as the quote.","Wrong: A percentage is the unit of ATR% (NATR).","Wrong: ATR has no fixed upper or lower bound.","Wrong: ATR does not use volume."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-80","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[28],"stem":"某资产价格不变，ATR%从2%升到3%。ATR本身变化了多少？","options":["增加1个百分点，也就是ATR增加1%","增加50%","不变，因为价格没变","增加1美元"],"answer":1,"explanation":"价格不变时ATR与ATR%同比例变化：3÷2−1=50%。","optionExplanations":["ATR%增加1个百分点，但ATR本身增加的是50%。","价格不变时ATR与ATR%同比例变化：3÷2−1=50%。","价格不变，ATR%上升就意味着ATR上升。","不知道价格，无法给出美元值。"],"skills":["计算","百分点与百分比"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — ATR and ATR% screening","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501823-average-true-range-atr/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"An asset's price is unchanged and ATR% rises from 2% to 3%. How much did ATR itself change?","optionsEn":["Up 1 percentage point, i.e. ATR rose 1%","Up 50%","Unchanged, because price did not change","Up $1"],"explanationEn":"With price unchanged, ATR and ATR% move in the same proportion: 3 ÷ 2 − 1 = 50%.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: ATR% rose 1 percentage point, but ATR itself rose 50%.","Correct: With price unchanged, ATR and ATR% move in the same proportion: 3 ÷ 2 − 1 = 50%.","Wrong: With price unchanged, a higher ATR% means a higher ATR.","Wrong: Without knowing the price, a dollar figure cannot be given."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-81","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[29],"stem":"在1小时图上添加ADR，读数前应先核对什么，才能确保读到的是“每天”的振幅？","options":["计算所用的时间周期是否设为日线","Length是否设为24以覆盖全天","价格源是否设为收盘价而非最高最低","是否勾选包含盘前盘后的延长时段"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：小周期使用时务必核对计算Timeframe，确保读的是每天。","optionExplanations":["正确，要确保读的是每天的振幅。","1小时图上取24根不是日线振幅，且Length不是关键。","ADR需要的是最高最低，且与是否日线无关。","这影响数据范围，却不决定读到的是每天。"],"skills":["设置","周期"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Average Daily Range","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000695003-average-daily-range-adr-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"You add ADR to a 1-hour chart. Before reading it, what should you check to make sure it shows the daily range?","optionsEn":["Whether the calculation timeframe is set to daily","Whether Length is 24 to cover a full day","Whether the price source is the close rather than high/low","Whether extended pre- and post-market hours are included"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, on lower timeframes always check the calculation timeframe so you are reading the daily range.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: This makes sure you are reading the daily range.","Wrong: 24 one-hour bars are not the daily range, and Length is not the key.","Wrong: ADR needs highs and lows, and this has nothing to do with being daily.","Wrong: This affects the data window but does not decide whether you read a daily figure."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-82","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[30],"stem":"同一个标准差脚本，输入改成“收益率”后，读数的单位会怎样变化？","options":["价格的离散程度，仍以美元计","自动年化后的波动率百分比","收益率的离散程度，以%计","价格相对均价的偏离百分比"],"answer":2,"explanation":"对收益率算标准差，结果是收益率的离散程度。","optionExplanations":["输入为价格时才是价格单位。","是否年化取决于是否乘周期换算，标准差本身不年化。","对收益率算标准差，结果是收益率的离散程度。","那是均价偏离，不是标准差。"],"skills":["输入","单位"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Bollinger Bands and price standard deviation","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501840-bollinger-bands-bb/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The same standard-deviation script is switched to use returns as input. How does the unit of the reading change?","optionsEn":["Dispersion of price, still in dollars","Volatility as an automatically annualised percentage","Dispersion of returns, in %","Percentage deviation of price from its average"],"explanationEn":"Standard deviation of returns gives the dispersion of returns.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Price units apply only when the input is price.","Wrong: Annualisation depends on scaling by the period; standard deviation itself is not annualised.","Correct: Standard deviation of returns gives the dispersion of returns.","Wrong: That is deviation from the average, not standard deviation."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-140","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[31],"stem":"某资产历史波动率显示30%。最恰当的理解是？","options":["对未来一年涨跌区间的估计值","过去一年内价格从高点下跌的幅度","对过去收益率起伏程度的年化度量","未来一年下跌超过30%的概率"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程说明：年化只是统一计量尺度，不是涨跌预测。","optionExplanations":["HV描述过去，不是预测区间。","那是回撤指标的概念。","课程说明：年化只是统一计量尺度，不是涨跌预测。","HV不是概率。"],"skills":["年化","解读"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Historical Volatility","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589145-historical-volatility/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"An asset's historical volatility shows 30%. What is the most appropriate reading?","optionsEn":["An estimate of next year's price range","How far price fell from its high over the past year","An annualised measure of how much past returns fluctuated","The probability of a fall of more than 30% next year"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson explains, annualising only puts it on a common scale; it is not a forecast.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: HV describes the past; it is not a forecast range.","Wrong: That is the idea of a drawdown measure.","Correct: As the lesson explains, annualising only puts it on a common scale; it is not a forecast.","Wrong: HV is not a probability."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-141","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[32],"stem":"成交量面板上的Volume MA线是什么？用来做什么？","options":["最近N根的平均成交量","最近N根成交量的累计总和","最近N根中最大的成交量","最近N根成交价格的移动平均"],"answer":0,"explanation":"均量线是成交量的平均，用来判断当前量是否高于平常。","optionExplanations":["均量线是成交量的平均，用来判断当前量是否高于平常。","累计是OBV一类的概念。","那是最大值，不是均值。","它画在成交量面板，算的是量，不是价格。"],"skills":["均量线","用途"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Volume","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591617-volume/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the Volume MA line in the volume panel, and what is it for?","optionsEn":["The average volume of the last N bars","The cumulative total volume of the last N bars","The largest volume of the last N bars","A moving average of traded prices over N bars"],"explanationEn":"The volume average shows typical volume, so you can judge whether current volume is above normal.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The volume average shows typical volume, so you can judge whether current volume is above normal.","Wrong: A running total is an OBV-type idea.","Wrong: That is the maximum, not the average.","Wrong: It sits in the volume panel and averages volume, not price."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-142","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[33],"stem":"盘中一根尚未收完的K线，RVOL读数通常会怎样？","options":["已经是最终值，K线收完后也不再变化","会按整根时长自动折算成预估的全根量","会随成交累积而下降，因为基准量也在增加","会随成交累积而变化，收完才是最终值"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：当前未收完的量不能当成最终量。","optionExplanations":["K线还在累积成交，读数会继续变。","普通RVOL不自动折算。","基准是过去均量，当根量累积使读数上升而非下降。","课程提醒：当前未收完的量不能当成最终量。"],"skills":["未收盘","读数"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Relative Volume calculation","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000635874-how-do-we-calculate-relative-volume-and-relative-volume-at-time/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What usually happens to the RVOL reading on an intraday bar that has not yet closed?","optionsEn":["It is already final and will not change after the bar closes","It automatically projects the full-bar volume from elapsed time","It falls as trading accumulates, because the baseline also grows","It changes as trading accumulates; it is final only at the close"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, an unfinished bar's volume cannot be treated as its final volume.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The bar is still accumulating volume, so the reading keeps changing.","Wrong: Standard RVOL does not project automatically.","Wrong: The baseline is past average volume; accumulating volume pushes the reading up, not down.","Correct: As the lesson notes, an unfinished bar's volume cannot be treated as its final volume."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-143","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[34],"stem":"两个平台的OBV数值差几百万，但走势形状相同。较合理的解释是？","options":["其中一个平台的成交量数据有误","起点不同，绝对数不同方向可比","两个平台对涨跌判断用了不同的价格","两个平台选用的K线周期不同"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：起始数字换了不改变基本方向，先看方向。","optionExplanations":["不一定有错，只是起点不同。","课程提醒：起始数字换了不改变基本方向，先看方向。","OBV都按收盘涨跌判断。","形状相同说明周期一致。"],"skills":["起算点","读法"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — On Balance Volume","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502593-on-balance-volume-obv/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Two platforms show OBV values millions apart, but the curves have the same shape. What is the more reasonable explanation?","optionsEn":["One platform's volume data is wrong","Different starting points; absolute values differ but direction compares","The two platforms judge up and down with different prices","The two platforms use different bar timeframes"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, changing the starting number does not change the basic direction, so look at direction first.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Not necessarily an error; the starting points simply differ.","Correct: As the lesson notes, changing the starting number does not change the basic direction, so look at direction first.","Wrong: OBV always judges by up or down closes.","Wrong: The same shape suggests the same timeframe."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-144","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[35],"stem":"某根K线收盘正好等于前一根收盘。PVT和OBV这一根分别加多少？","options":["PVT加0，OBV加全部成交量","PVT加全部成交量，OBV加0","都加全部成交量","都加0"],"answer":3,"explanation":"价格变化为0：PVT增量=量×0=0；OBV平收也不加不减。","optionExplanations":["OBV平收时不变。","PVT按涨跌百分比，平收为0。","平收两者都不变。","价格变化为0：PVT增量=量×0=0；OBV平收也不加不减。"],"skills":["平收","规则"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Price Volume Trend","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502345-price-volume-trend-pvt/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"A bar closes exactly at the previous close. How much do PVT and OBV add on this bar?","optionsEn":["PVT adds 0; OBV adds the full volume","PVT adds the full volume; OBV adds 0","Both add the full volume","Both add 0"],"explanationEn":"The price change is 0, so PVT's increment = volume × 0 = 0, and OBV neither adds nor subtracts on an unchanged close.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: OBV is unchanged on an unchanged close.","Wrong: PVT uses the percentage change, which is 0 on an unchanged close.","Wrong: Neither changes on an unchanged close.","Correct: The price change is 0, so PVT's increment = volume × 0 = 0, and OBV neither adds nor subtracts on an unchanged close."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-145","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[36],"stem":"PVO的参数12、26、9作用在什么数据上？","options":["收盘价","成交量","ATR","RSI"],"answer":1,"explanation":"PVO=成交量EMA12与EMA26的百分比差，再取9期信号线。","optionExplanations":["那是PPO。","PVO=成交量EMA12与EMA26的百分比差，再取9期信号线。","与ATR无关。","与RSI无关。"],"skills":["输入","易混"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Percentage Volume Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591350-percentage-volume-oscillator-pvo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What data do PVO's settings 12, 26, 9 apply to?","optionsEn":["The close","Volume","ATR","RSI"],"explanationEn":"PVO = the percentage difference between EMA12 and EMA26 of volume, with a 9-period signal line.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is PPO.","Correct: PVO = the percentage difference between EMA12 and EMA26 of volume, with a 9-period signal line.","Wrong: It has nothing to do with ATR.","Wrong: It has nothing to do with RSI."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-146","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[37],"stem":"为什么本课建议在日线以下周期（如15分钟）看会话VWAP？","options":["日线没有成交量数据，所以算不出VWAP","会话VWAP每天重置，日内图才看得出变化","日线级别的成交量统计口径与日内不同","分钟图的成交量更精确，所以VWAP也更准"],"answer":1,"explanation":"每个会话重新累计，日内图上才能看到它怎样随成交变化。","optionExplanations":["日线有成交量；问题在于会话VWAP每天重置，日线上看不到它在一天内的变化。","每个会话重新累计，日内图上才能看到它怎样随成交变化。","日线有完整成交量，问题不在口径。","精度与周期无关。"],"skills":["周期","重置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Volume Weighted Average Price","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502018-volume-weighted-average-price-vwap/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Why does this lesson suggest viewing session VWAP below the daily timeframe (for example 15 minutes)?","optionsEn":["Daily bars have no volume data, so VWAP cannot be calculated","Session VWAP resets each day, so only intraday charts show its changes","Daily volume is counted differently from intraday volume","Minute bars have more accurate volume, so VWAP is more precise"],"explanationEn":"It restarts accumulating each session, so only an intraday chart shows how it moves with trading.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Daily bars do have volume; the issue is that session VWAP resets each day, so a daily chart cannot show how it moves within the day.","Correct: It restarts accumulating each session, so only an intraday chart shows how it moves with trading.","Wrong: Daily bars have complete volume; counting is not the issue.","Wrong: Precision has nothing to do with the timeframe."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-147","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[38],"stem":"Parabolic SAR默认参数0.02、0.02、0.20分别指？","options":["快线EMA周期、慢线EMA周期、信号线周期","起始止损距离、每次移动步长、最大止损距离","起始回看根数、每次增加根数、最大回看根数","起始加速因子、每次增量、最高加速因子"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程注明：设置中有起始、增量、最大加速因子。","optionExplanations":["那是MACD的参数结构。","参数是加速因子，不是止损距离。","参数不是回看根数。","课程注明：设置中有起始、增量、最大加速因子。"],"skills":["参数","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Parabolic SAR","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502597-parabolic-sar-sar/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do Parabolic SAR's defaults 0.02, 0.02, 0.20 refer to?","optionsEn":["Fast EMA period, slow EMA period, signal period","Starting stop distance, step per move, maximum stop distance","Starting lookback bars, bars added each time, maximum lookback","Starting acceleration factor, increment, maximum acceleration factor"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that the settings are the starting, increment and maximum acceleration factors.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is MACD's parameter structure.","Wrong: The settings are acceleration factors, not stop distances.","Wrong: The settings are not lookback bar counts.","Correct: The lesson notes that the settings are the starting, increment and maximum acceleration factors."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-148","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[39],"stem":"Supertrend默认参数10和3分别控制什么？","options":["ATR计算周期10，距离倍数3","均线周期10，信号线周期3","高低价回看10根，缓冲3%","ATR倍数10，ATR计算周期3"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程演示：ATR10期、倍数3，线的距离由ATR×倍数决定。","optionExplanations":["课程演示：ATR10期、倍数3，线的距离由ATR×倍数决定。","它不使用均线和信号线。","它不取高低价窗口，也不设百分比缓冲。","把周期和倍数颠倒了。"],"skills":["参数","ATR"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Supertrend","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000634738-supertrend/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do Supertrend's defaults 10 and 3 control?","optionsEn":["ATR period 10, distance multiplier 3","Average period 10, signal period 3","High–low lookback of 10 bars, buffer 3%","ATR multiplier 10, ATR period 3"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson shows, ATR period 10 and multiplier 3; the line's distance is ATR × multiplier.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: As the lesson shows, ATR period 10 and multiplier 3; the line's distance is ATR × multiplier.","Wrong: It does not use moving averages or a signal line.","Wrong: It does not use a high–low window or a percentage buffer.","Wrong: This swaps the period and the multiplier."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-149","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[40],"stem":"在TradingView上怎样得到“A相对B”的比值图？","options":["在指标里添加Price Relative","把B叠加到A的图上，再选比值显示方式","在左上角品种搜索框输入A/B写法","用趋势线工具在两张图之间量出比值"],"answer":2,"explanation":"品种搜索支持“/”运算，直接得到比值走势。","optionExplanations":["课程提醒：这不是Indicators里的同名按钮。","叠加只能比形状，得不到比值数值。","品种搜索支持“/”运算，直接得到比值走势。","画线工具量不出连续的比值走势。"],"skills":["操作入口","比值"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView — Spread charts explained","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502298-spread-charts-explained/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How do you get an \"A relative to B\" ratio chart on TradingView?","optionsEn":["Add Price Relative from the indicators","Overlay B on A's chart and pick a ratio display","Type A/B into the symbol search box at the top left","Measure the ratio between two charts with the trend line tool"],"explanationEn":"Symbol search supports the \"/\" operator, which gives the ratio chart directly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: As the lesson notes, this is not the similarly named button under Indicators.","Wrong: An overlay only compares shapes; it gives no ratio values.","Correct: Symbol search supports the \"/\" operator, which gives the ratio chart directly.","Wrong: Drawing tools cannot measure a continuous ratio series."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-150","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[41],"stem":"只添加ADX指标，能否看到+DI和−DI？想看应选什么？","options":["不能，应改选Aroon才有方向线","能，ADX默认同时画出+DI与−DI","不能，ADX只显示强度，应另选DMI","能，把平滑长度调小后会显示方向线"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程注明：ADX独立指标只显示强度，想看+DI/−DI应另选DMI。","optionExplanations":["Aroon是另一类指标。","独立ADX只显示强度一条线。","课程注明：ADX独立指标只显示强度，想看+DI/−DI应另选DMI。","参数不改变显示的线。"],"skills":["设置辨认","DMI"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Average Directional Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589099-average-directional-index-adx/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"If you add only the ADX indicator, can you see +DI and −DI? If not, what should you choose?","optionsEn":["No; switch to Aroon to get direction lines","Yes; ADX draws +DI and −DI by default","No; ADX shows only strength, so add DMI instead","Yes; a shorter smoothing length shows the direction lines"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that the standalone ADX shows only strength; to see +DI/−DI, choose DMI.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Aroon is a different kind of indicator.","Wrong: Standalone ADX shows only a single strength line.","Correct: The lesson notes that the standalone ADX shows only strength; to see +DI/−DI, choose DMI.","Wrong: Settings do not change which lines are shown."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-151","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[42],"stem":"DMI中+DI持续高于−DI，最基础的含义是？","options":["窗口内向上的方向运动强于向下","窗口内上涨的K线根数多于下跌的","趋势强度已经很高，可视为强趋势","收盘价高于窗口内的平均收盘价"],"answer":0,"explanation":"+DI与−DI比较向上和向下的推动。","optionExplanations":["+DI与−DI比较向上和向下的推动。","DI比较的是运动幅度，不是根数。","强度要看ADX，不是DI谁高。","DI不与平均价比较。"],"skills":["读数","方向"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Directional Movement Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502250-directional-movement-dmi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In DMI, +DI stays above −DI. What is the most basic meaning?","optionsEn":["Upward directional movement in the window is stronger than downward","More bars in the window closed up than down","Trend strength is already high, so this is a strong trend","The close is above the window's average close"],"explanationEn":"+DI and −DI compare upward and downward thrust.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: +DI and −DI compare upward and downward thrust.","Wrong: DI compares the size of movement, not the number of bars.","Wrong: Strength comes from ADX, not from which DI is higher.","Wrong: DI does not compare with an average price."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-83","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[43],"stem":"Aroon长度为14，Aroon Up=100×(14−距最高点根数)÷14。读数为50，最高点出现在几根以前？","options":["3.5根以前","14根以前","7根以前","50根以前"],"answer":2,"explanation":"50=100×(14−n)÷14，得n=7。","optionExplanations":["代入错误。","14根以前对应0。","50=100×(14−n)÷14，得n=7。","超出窗口。"],"skills":["计算","时间"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Aroon","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501801-aroon-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"With an Aroon length of 14, Aroon Up = 100 × (14 − bars since the high) ÷ 14. If it reads 50, how many bars ago was the high?","optionsEn":["3.5 bars ago","14 bars ago","7 bars ago","50 bars ago"],"explanationEn":"50 = 100 × (14 − n) ÷ 14, so n = 7.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Substituted incorrectly.","Wrong: 14 bars ago corresponds to 0.","Correct: 50 = 100 × (14 − n) ÷ 14, so n = 7.","Wrong: That is outside the window."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-152","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[44],"stem":"Aroon Up与Aroon Down相等时，Aroon Oscillator是多少？","options":["−100","0","50","100"],"answer":1,"explanation":"振荡器=Up−Down，相等即为0。","optionExplanations":["−100表示相反。","振荡器=Up−Down，相等即为0。","50不是差值结果。","100表示Up=100且Down=0。"],"skills":["计算","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Aroon Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773004-aroon-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"When Aroon Up equals Aroon Down, what is the Aroon Oscillator?","optionsEn":["−100","0","50","100"],"explanationEn":"The oscillator = Up − Down, so equal values give 0.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: −100 means the opposite extreme.","Correct: The oscillator = Up − Down, so equal values give 0.","Wrong: 50 is not the result of the difference.","Wrong: 100 means Up = 100 and Down = 0."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-153","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[45],"stem":"VI+和VI−都接近1，并且反复交叉。较合适的描述是？","options":["趋势正在加速，频繁交叉说明动能增强","多空正在蓄势，交叉多预示将有大行情","价格波动极小，交叉没有参考价值","推动接近，方向不明，交叉多为噪声"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：窄幅来回走时会产生很多假转向提示。","optionExplanations":["两线接近说明谁都不占优，不是加速。","反复交叉说明没有持续方向，不是蓄势。","比值接近1不等于价格不动。","课程提醒：窄幅来回走时会产生很多假转向提示。"],"skills":["横盘","假交叉"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Vortex Indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591352-vortex-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"VI+ and VI− are both near 1 and keep crossing. What is the more fitting description?","optionsEn":["The trend is accelerating; frequent crosses show rising momentum","Both sides are building up; many crosses foretell a big move","Price barely moves, so the crosses mean nothing","Thrust is balanced, direction is unclear, and crosses are mostly noise"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, choppy back-and-forth trading produces many false turn signals.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Two lines close together mean neither side dominates, not acceleration.","Wrong: Repeated crosses show no sustained direction, not a build-up.","Wrong: Ratios near 1 do not mean price is not moving.","Correct: As the lesson notes, choppy back-and-forth trading produces many false turn signals."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-154","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[46],"stem":"Choppiness Index图上常见的61.8和38.2两条参考线，用来做什么？","options":["环境参考：高于61.8偏趋势，低于38.2偏横盘","环境参考：高于61.8偏横盘，低于38.2偏趋势","买卖界线：高于61.8应卖出，低于38.2应买入","方向参考：高于61.8看涨，低于38.2看跌"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程注明：只作环境观察，不说明方向。","optionExplanations":["说反了：值高更像横盘。","课程注明：只作环境观察，不说明方向。","CHOP不是超买超卖指标。","CHOP不说明方向。"],"skills":["参考线","用途"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Choppiness Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501980-choppiness-index-chop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What are the 61.8 and 38.2 reference lines often seen on a Choppiness Index chart for?","optionsEn":["Context: above 61.8 leans trending, below 38.2 leans ranging","Context: above 61.8 leans ranging, below 38.2 leans trending","Trade lines: sell above 61.8, buy below 38.2","Direction: bullish above 61.8, bearish below 38.2"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes these are for reading the market environment only and say nothing about direction.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This is reversed: high values look more like a range.","Correct: The lesson notes these are for reading the market environment only and say nothing about direction.","Wrong: CHOP is not an overbought/oversold indicator.","Wrong: CHOP does not indicate direction."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-155","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[47],"stem":"价格位于一目均衡表的云下方，常见的描述是？","options":["即将反转向上","偏强","方向模糊","偏弱"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：云上偏强、云内模糊、云下偏弱。","optionExplanations":["位置描述不预测反转。","云上才偏强。","云内才模糊。","课程：云上偏强、云内模糊、云下偏弱。"],"skills":["位置","读法"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ichimoku Cloud","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589152-ichimoku-cloud/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Price is below the Ichimoku cloud. What is the usual description?","optionsEn":["About to reverse upward","Leaning strong","Direction unclear","Leaning weak"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: above the cloud leans strong, inside is unclear, below leans weak.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Describing position does not predict a reversal.","Wrong: Only above the cloud leans strong.","Wrong: Only inside the cloud is unclear.","Correct: The lesson: above the cloud leans strong, inside is unclear, below leans weak."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-156","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[48],"stem":"鳄鱼指标的三条线里，反应最快的是哪条？","options":["Teeth（齿），周期居中（8期）","Lips（唇），周期最短（5期）","Jaw（颚），周期最长（13期）","三条同速，只是向右平移的根数不同"],"answer":1,"explanation":"5期最短，反应最快。","optionExplanations":["8期居中，不是最快。","5期最短，反应最快。","13期最慢。","三条线周期不同，速度也不同。"],"skills":["参数","快慢"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Williams Alligator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592305-williams-alligator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which of the Alligator's three lines reacts fastest?","optionsEn":["Teeth, the middle period (8)","Lips, the shortest period (5)","Jaw, the longest period (13)","All three move at the same speed and differ only in forward shift"],"explanationEn":"The 5-period line is the shortest and reacts fastest.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The 8-period line is in the middle, not the fastest.","Correct: The 5-period line is the shortest and reacts fastest.","Wrong: The 13-period line is the slowest.","Wrong: The three lines have different periods, so different speeds."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-84","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[49],"stem":"KAMA设置中的ER length、Fast length、Slow length分别是什么？","options":["三条均线各自的周期，分别代表短、中、长期","效率比窗口，以及两条信号线的周期","趋势、波动、成交量三项各自的回看根数","效率比的回看窗口，以及速度的快慢上下限"],"answer":3,"explanation":"ER length决定算效率比的根数；Fast/Slow限定跟随速度的上下限。","optionExplanations":["课程提醒：别把三项都当普通周期。","KAMA没有信号线。","KAMA不使用成交量或独立的波动窗口。","ER length决定算效率比的根数；Fast/Slow限定跟随速度的上下限。"],"skills":["参数","自适应"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Kaufman's Adaptive Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773012-kaufman-s-adaptive-moving-average-kama/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What are ER length, Fast length and Slow length in KAMA's settings?","optionsEn":["The periods of three averages: short, medium and long term","The efficiency-ratio window and two signal-line periods","Lookbacks for trend, volatility and volume respectively","The efficiency-ratio lookback, plus the fast and slow speed limits"],"explanationEn":"ER length sets how many bars the efficiency ratio uses; Fast/Slow set the upper and lower limits of how fast it follows.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: As the lesson notes, don't treat all three as ordinary periods.","Wrong: KAMA has no signal line.","Wrong: KAMA does not use volume or a separate volatility window.","Correct: ER length sets how many bars the efficiency ratio uses; Fast/Slow set the upper and lower limits of how fast it follows."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-157","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[50],"stem":"ALMA相对普通SMA，设计目标是什么？","options":["既让线更平滑，又尽量减少滞后","提前给出下一根K线的价格预测","给成交量大的K线更高的计算权重","把价格换成相对百分比后再平均"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：想让线既平滑，又不要跟价格差太远。","optionExplanations":["课程：想让线既平滑，又不要跟价格差太远。","它不是预测。","ALMA不用成交量。","它仍是价格单位。"],"skills":["用途","设计"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Arnaud Legoux Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594683-arnaud-legoux-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Compared with an ordinary SMA, what is ALMA designed to do?","optionsEn":["Make the line smoother while keeping lag low","Forecast the next bar's price in advance","Give more weight to high-volume bars","Average price after converting it to relative percentages"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: it aims to be smooth without straying too far from price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The lesson: it aims to be smooth without straying too far from price.","Wrong: It is not a forecast.","Wrong: ALMA does not use volume.","Wrong: It stays in price units."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-158","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[51],"stem":"McGinley Dynamic在横盘时会怎样？","options":["会自动放慢，价格很少再穿越这条线","会紧贴价格同步移动，两者几乎重叠","仍会被价格反复穿越，自适应不能避开","会停在横盘区中间，直到出现突破才动"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：横盘仍会多次穿线。","optionExplanations":["它不会因自适应而避开横盘穿越。","它是平滑线，不会与价格重叠。","课程提醒：横盘仍会多次穿线。","它仍随价格调整，不会停住。"],"skills":["横盘","局限"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: McGinley Dynamic","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589175-mcginley-dynamic/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does McGinley Dynamic do in a sideways market?","optionsEn":["It slows down automatically, so price rarely crosses it","It hugs price and moves in step, nearly overlapping","Price still crosses it repeatedly; adaptiveness does not prevent it","It parks in the middle of the range until a breakout"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, price still crosses the line many times in a range.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Adaptiveness does not prevent crosses in a range.","Wrong: It is a smoothed line and does not overlap price.","Correct: As the lesson notes, price still crosses the line many times in a range.","Wrong: It still adjusts with price and does not stop."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-85","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[52],"stem":"LSMA(25)在最新一根的值，与同一窗口（25根）回归通道的中线有什么关系？","options":["等于同窗口25根收盘价的简单平均","等于回归通道上轨在最新一根的取值","等于回归通道中线在最新一根的取值","与中线走势相似，数值通常略低于中线"],"answer":2,"explanation":"LSMA就是最近25根回归直线末端的值，与同窗口回归中线右端一致。","optionExplanations":["平均值是SMA，回归线在末端通常不同。","上轨还加了标准差倍数。","LSMA就是最近25根回归直线末端的值，与同窗口回归中线右端一致。","两者同源，数值一致而不是略低。"],"skills":["关系","回归"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Least Squares Moving Average","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000599877-least-squares-moving-average/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does LSMA(25) on the latest bar relate to the midline of a regression channel over the same 25-bar window?","optionsEn":["It equals the simple average of the same 25 closes","It equals the channel's upper line on the latest bar","It equals the channel's midline on the latest bar","It moves like the midline but usually sits slightly below it"],"explanationEn":"LSMA is the endpoint of the regression line over the last 25 bars, matching the right end of the same-window regression midline.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The average is an SMA; the regression line usually differs at its end.","Wrong: The upper line adds a standard-deviation multiple.","Correct: LSMA is the endpoint of the regression line over the last 25 bars, matching the right end of the same-window regression midline.","Wrong: They come from the same calculation, so the values match rather than sit slightly lower."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-159","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[53],"stem":"TradingView的Linear Regression通道里，Count与Deviation分别控制什么？","options":["回看的K线数量，以及边线的标准差倍数","回看的K线数量，以及边线的百分比偏移","回看的K线数量，以及向右延伸的根数","回归线的平滑周期，以及边线的ATR倍数"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程注明：Count控制回看数量，Deviation控制通道宽度。","optionExplanations":["课程注明：Count控制回看数量，Deviation控制通道宽度。","宽度按标准差倍数，不是百分比。","它不向右预测延伸。","回归线没有平滑周期，宽度也不是ATR倍数。"],"skills":["参数","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Linear Regression","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644936-linear-regression/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In TradingView's Linear Regression channel, what do Count and Deviation control?","optionsEn":["The number of bars looked back, and the standard-deviation multiple of the outer lines","The number of bars looked back, and the percentage offset of the outer lines","The number of bars looked back, and how many bars it extends right","The regression's smoothing period, and the ATR multiple of the outer lines"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that Count sets the lookback and Deviation sets the channel width.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The lesson notes that Count sets the lookback and Deviation sets the channel width.","Wrong: Width is a standard-deviation multiple, not a percentage.","Wrong: It does not project forward to the right.","Wrong: The regression has no smoothing period, and the width is not an ATR multiple."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-86","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[54],"stem":"两个资产的回归斜率都是每根+0.5。一个价格约10元，另一个约1000元。下面哪项正确？","options":["1000元的资产涨得更快，因为价位更高","两者按金额和按比例的涨速都相同，因为斜率相同","斜率受周期影响，价位不同时无法比较","10元资产相对自身价格涨得明显更快"],"answer":3,"explanation":"0.5相当于10元的5%，却只是1000元的0.05%。","optionExplanations":["绝对价位高不等于相对涨得快。","绝对涨速相同，但相对各自价格差别很大，不能说相对涨速也相同。","可以折算成相对自身价格的比例后比较。","正确，0.5是10元的5%，只是1000元的0.05%。"],"skills":["单位","跨资产"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Linear Regression Slope","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644936-linear-regression/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Two assets both have a regression slope of +0.5 per bar. One trades around 10 and the other around 1000. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["The 1000 asset is rising faster because its price is higher","Both rise at the same rate in money and in percent, since slopes match","Slope depends on the period, so different price levels cannot be compared","The 10 asset is rising much faster relative to its own price"],"explanationEn":"0.5 is 5% of 10 but only 0.05% of 1000.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A higher price level does not mean a faster relative rise.","Wrong: The absolute pace is the same, but relative to each price it differs greatly, so the relative pace is not the same.","Wrong: They can be compared after converting to a share of each price.","Correct: 0.5 is 5% of 10 but only 0.05% of 1000."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-160","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[55],"stem":"一个R²脚本显示0.82，另一个显示82。两者是什么关系？","options":["前者按样本公式，后者按总体公式","前者是拟合程度，后者是趋势斜率","后者拟合更好，因为读数大了100倍","同一拟合程度，仅显示刻度不同"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：核对显示0—1还是0—100。","optionExplanations":["刻度不同，不是样本与总体之分。","两者都是R²，不是斜率。","只是刻度不同，拟合程度相同。","课程提醒：核对显示0—1还是0—100。"],"skills":["刻度","换算"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Linear Regression R-Squared","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000644936-linear-regression/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"One R² script shows 0.82 and another shows 82. How are they related?","optionsEn":["The first uses the sample formula, the second the population formula","The first is goodness of fit, the second is trend slope","The second fits better, because the reading is 100 times larger","Same goodness of fit, only displayed on a different scale"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, check whether it is shown as 0–1 or 0–100.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The scales differ; it is not sample versus population.","Wrong: Both are R², not slope.","Wrong: Only the scale differs; the fit is the same.","Correct: As the lesson notes, check whether it is shown as 0–1 or 0–100."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-161","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[56],"stem":"内置Correlation Coefficient指标的Inputs里，Symbol一栏应填什么？","options":["用来对照的大盘指数，仅限指数代码","要与当前图表比较的第二个标的","相关系数使用的回看窗口根数","计算相关系数所用的价格来源"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程注明：在Inputs的Symbol填第二个标的；Length是比较窗口。","optionExplanations":["可以填任何有数据的标的，不限指数。","课程注明：在Inputs的Symbol填第二个标的；Length是比较窗口。","回看长度是Length。","价格源是Source。"],"skills":["设置","输入"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Correlation Coefficient","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502022-correlation-coefficient-cc/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In the built-in Correlation Coefficient indicator's Inputs, what goes in the Symbol field?","optionsEn":["A benchmark index for comparison, index codes only","The second instrument to compare with the current chart","The number of bars in the correlation lookback","The price source used to calculate correlation"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that Symbol in Inputs takes the second instrument; Length is the comparison window.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Any instrument with data works, not just indices.","Correct: The lesson notes that Symbol in Inputs takes the second instrument; Length is the comparison window.","Wrong: The lookback is Length.","Wrong: The price source is Source."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-162","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[57],"stem":"与普通RSI相比，StochRSI的走势通常怎样？","options":["更平缓，较少到达0或100的边缘","更敏感，经常贴近0或100的边缘","走势大致相同，仅刻度压缩到0—1","更滞后，因为多叠加了一层平滑"],"answer":1,"explanation":"它看RSI在自身近期范围中的位置，反应特别快。","optionExplanations":["恰好相反，它更敏感。","它看RSI在自身近期范围中的位置，反应特别快。","两者走势不同，不只是刻度差别。","它不是更慢，而是更快。"],"skills":["敏感度","读法"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Stochastic RSI","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502333-stochastic-rsi-stoch-rsi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Compared with an ordinary RSI, how does StochRSI usually move?","optionsEn":["More gently, rarely reaching 0 or 100","More sensitively, often pinned near 0 or 100","About the same, only compressed to 0–1","With more lag, because it adds a layer of smoothing"],"explanationEn":"It shows where RSI sits within its own recent range, so it reacts very quickly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The opposite: it is more sensitive.","Correct: It shows where RSI sits within its own recent range, so it reacts very quickly.","Wrong: The two move differently; it is not just a scale difference.","Wrong: It is faster, not slower."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-87","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[58],"stem":"ConnorsRSI常见参数3、2、100分别对应什么？","options":["价格RSI周期、涨幅百分位回看、连涨连跌RSI周期","价格RSI周期、成交量RSI周期、涨幅百分位回看","短期RSI周期、长期RSI周期、均线回看周期","价格RSI周期、连涨连跌RSI周期、涨幅百分位回看"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程注明：RSI length 3、UpDown length 2、ROC length 100。","optionExplanations":["顺序错了，100是百分位回看。","第二项是连涨连跌，不是成交量。","ConnorsRSI不是由三条均线周期构成。","正确，对应3、2、100。"],"skills":["参数","组成"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Connors RSI","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502017-connors-rsi-crsi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do ConnorsRSI's common settings 3, 2, 100 correspond to?","optionsEn":["Price RSI period, percentile lookback of gains, streak RSI period","Price RSI period, volume RSI period, percentile lookback of gains","Short RSI period, long RSI period, moving-average lookback","Price RSI period, streak RSI period, percentile lookback of gains"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes RSI length 3, UpDown length 2 and ROC length 100.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The order is wrong; 100 is the percentile lookback.","Wrong: The second is the up/down streak, not volume.","Wrong: ConnorsRSI is not built from three moving-average periods.","Correct: These match 3, 2 and 100."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-163","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[59],"stem":"CMO读数在零线以上，最基础的含义是？","options":["窗口内上涨K线的根数多于下跌的","收盘价高于窗口内的平均收盘价","上涨总幅度至少是下跌总幅度的2倍","窗口内上涨总幅度大于下跌总幅度"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：零线区分上涨总幅与下跌总幅谁占优。","optionExplanations":["CMO比较幅度，不是根数。","CMO不与均价比较。","零线以上只表示占优，不要求达到2倍。","课程：零线区分上涨总幅与下跌总幅谁占优。"],"skills":["零线","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chande Momentum Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589109-chande-momentum-oscillator-cmo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the most basic meaning of a CMO reading above zero?","optionsEn":["More bars in the window closed up than down","The close is above the window's average close","Total gains are at least twice total losses","Total gains in the window exceed total losses"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the zero line separates whether total gains or total losses dominate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: CMO compares magnitudes, not bar counts.","Wrong: CMO does not compare with the average price.","Wrong: Above zero only means gains dominate; it does not require twice as much.","Correct: The lesson: the zero line separates whether total gains or total losses dominate."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-164","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[60],"stem":"TSI常见参数25与13指什么？","options":["对价格变化先后两次平滑的长度","回看25根与13根的价格区间","主线周期25，信号线周期13","分别平滑价格和成交量的长度"],"answer":0,"explanation":"TSI把逐根价格变化先平滑25、再平滑13（常见长、短）。","optionExplanations":["TSI把逐根价格变化先平滑25、再平滑13（常见长、短）。","都是平滑长度，不是价格区间的回看。","信号线需按版本另核对，不是这两个参数。","TSI不使用成交量。"],"skills":["参数","双重平滑"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: True Strength Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592290-true-strength-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do TSI's common settings 25 and 13 refer to?","optionsEn":["The lengths of two successive smoothings of price change","Price ranges looked back over 25 and 13 bars","Main line period 25, signal line period 13","Lengths for smoothing price and volume respectively"],"explanationEn":"TSI smooths bar-to-bar price change over 25 and then 13 (the usual long and short).","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: TSI smooths bar-to-bar price change over 25 and then 13 (the usual long and short).","Wrong: Both are smoothing lengths, not price-range lookbacks.","Wrong: The signal line depends on the version; it is not one of these two settings.","Wrong: TSI does not use volume."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-165","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[61],"stem":"TRIX读数正好等于0（落在零线上），含义是什么？","options":["价格正好等于三重平滑线","三重平滑线本根没有变化","三重平滑线与信号线相交","价格正好等于TEMA的读数"],"answer":1,"explanation":"TRIX是三重平滑结果的变化率，零表示这一根没变。","optionExplanations":["TRIX不比较价格与平滑线的距离。","TRIX是三重平滑结果的变化率，零表示这一根没变。","那是信号线交叉，不是零线。","与TEMA无关。"],"skills":["零线","变化率"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: TRIX","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502331-trix/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"TRIX reads exactly 0 (on the zero line). What does that mean?","optionsEn":["Price exactly equals the triple-smoothed line","The triple-smoothed line did not change on this bar","The triple-smoothed line crosses its signal line","Price exactly equals the TEMA reading"],"explanationEn":"TRIX is the rate of change of the triple-smoothed result, so zero means it did not change on this bar.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: TRIX does not compare price with the smoothed line.","Correct: TRIX is the rate of change of the triple-smoothed result, so zero means it did not change on this bar.","Wrong: That is a signal-line cross, not the zero line.","Wrong: It has nothing to do with TEMA."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-166","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[62],"stem":"终极振荡器为什么同时用7、14、28三个窗口？","options":["加入成交量信息，让读数更可靠","把三个独立指标合成一个读数","合并三窗口，减少单窗口偏差","压缩读数范围，避免出现极端值"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：合并短、中、长三个窗口，减少只看一个窗口的偏差。","optionExplanations":["它不用成交量。","它是一个指标的三个窗口，不是三个指标。","课程：合并短、中、长三个窗口，减少只看一个窗口的偏差。","仍可能出现极端读数。"],"skills":["设计","多窗口"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ultimate Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502328-ultimate-oscillator-uo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Why does the Ultimate Oscillator use three windows of 7, 14 and 28 at once?","optionsEn":["To add volume information and make readings more reliable","To combine three separate indicators into one reading","To blend three windows and reduce single-window bias","To compress the range and avoid extreme readings"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: blending short, medium and long windows reduces the bias of looking at just one.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It does not use volume.","Wrong: It is one indicator with three windows, not three indicators.","Correct: The lesson: blending short, medium and long windows reduces the bias of looking at just one.","Wrong: Extreme readings can still occur."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-167","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[63],"stem":"Awesome Oscillator计算时用的是什么价格？","options":["典型价，即（最高+最低+收盘）÷3","中点价，即（最高+最低）÷2","加权价，即（最高+最低+收盘×2）÷4","开收平均价，即（开盘+收盘）÷2"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程注明：比较中点价的5与34根SMA。","optionExplanations":["那是典型价，不是AO所用。","正确，AO用中点价。","那是加权收盘价，不是AO所用。","AO不使用开收平均。"],"skills":["价格源","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Awesome Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501826-awesome-oscillator-ao/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What price does the Awesome Oscillator use in its calculation?","optionsEn":["Typical price, i.e. (high + low + close) ÷ 3","Median price, i.e. (high + low) ÷ 2","Weighted price, i.e. (high + low + close × 2) ÷ 4","Open–close average, i.e. (open + close) ÷ 2"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that it compares 5- and 34-bar SMAs of the median price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is the typical price, which AO does not use.","Correct: AO uses the median price.","Wrong: That is the weighted close, which AO does not use.","Wrong: AO does not use the open–close average."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-168","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[64],"stem":"SMI（随机动量指数）在零线以上，最基础的含义是？","options":["平滑后收盘位于近期区间中点之上","平滑后收盘接近近期区间最高点","平滑后收盘高于一段时间前的收盘","平滑后的%K线位于%D线的上方"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：正数偏上半区，负数偏下半区。","optionExplanations":["正确：SMI为正表示平滑后的收盘偏在近期高低区间的上半区。","错误：零线以上只表示偏上半区，不要求贴近区间最高点。","错误：SMI比较的是收盘在高低区间中的位置，不是与旧收盘的涨跌。","错误：主线与平均线的上下关系看交叉，零线看的是区间中点。"],"skills":["零线","位置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Stochastic Momentum Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000707882-stochastic-momentum-index-smi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the most basic meaning of the SMI (Stochastic Momentum Index) being above zero?","optionsEn":["The smoothed close is above the midpoint of the recent range","The smoothed close is near the top of the recent range","The smoothed close is above the close some time ago","The smoothed %K line is above the %D line"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: positive leans to the upper half of the range, negative to the lower half.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A positive SMI means the smoothed close sits in the upper half of the recent high–low range.","Wrong: Above zero only means the upper half; it does not require being near the top of the range.","Wrong: SMI compares the close's position in the high–low range, not its change from an old close.","Wrong: The main line versus its average is about crossovers; the zero line is the range midpoint."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-169","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[65],"stem":"SMI Ergodic Indicator设置中需要核对哪三项？","options":["回看长度、%K平滑与%D平滑三项","快速长度、慢速长度与信号线长度","RSI长度、随机长度与信号线长度","超买水平、超卖水平与零线水平"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：核对Fast/Slow/Signal三项。","optionExplanations":["错误：这是Stochastic Momentum Index的参数，不是SMI Ergodic的。","正确：SMI Ergodic核对Fast/Slow/Signal三项长度。","错误：该指标不使用RSI长度，把它与StochRSI混淆了。","错误：这些是参考水平，不是需要核对的计算长度。"],"skills":["设置","参数"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: SMI Ergodic Indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594669-smi-ergodic-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"Which three settings should you check in the SMI Ergodic Indicator?","optionsEn":["Lookback length, %K smoothing and %D smoothing","Fast length, slow length and signal length","RSI length, stochastic length and signal length","Overbought, oversold and zero-line levels"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: check the Fast, Slow and Signal settings.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: These are Stochastic Momentum Index settings, not SMI Ergodic ones.","Correct: For SMI Ergodic, check the Fast, Slow and Signal lengths.","Wrong: This indicator has no RSI length; that confuses it with StochRSI.","Wrong: These are reference levels, not the calculation lengths to check."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-170","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[66],"stem":"Relative Vigor Index主线持续为正，最基础的含义是？","options":["近期K线多收在当日区间的上半部","近期K线多收在开盘价之上（平滑后）","近期收盘价多高于前一根收盘价","近期上涨K线的波动幅度大于下跌K线"],"answer":1,"explanation":"它比较收盘−开盘与最高−最低，正值说明收盘多高于开盘。","optionExplanations":["那更接近随机指标的含义。","正确，RVI比较收盘−开盘与区间。","RVI比较的是同一根K线的收盘与开盘。","那是相对波动率指数的含义。"],"skills":["读数","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Relative Vigor Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591593-relative-vigor-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The Relative Vigor Index main line stays positive. What is the most basic meaning?","optionsEn":["Recent bars mostly closed in the upper half of their range","Recent bars mostly closed above their open (after smoothing)","Recent closes were mostly above the previous close","Recent up bars had larger ranges than down bars"],"explanationEn":"It compares close − open with high − low; a positive value means closes were mostly above opens.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is closer to what a stochastic means.","Correct: RVI compares close − open with the range.","Wrong: RVI compares each bar's close with its own open.","Wrong: That is what the Relative Volatility Index means."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-171","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[67],"stem":"Relative Volatility Index读数在50附近，表示什么？","options":["收盘大致位于近期价格区间的中点","上涨与下跌时的波动幅度大致相当","近期涨跌幅合计接近零，价格走平","近期波动大小处于历史中位数水平"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：范围0—100，50为中点。","optionExplanations":["那是区间位置，不是波动对比。","正确，50是中点。","它比较的是波动幅度，不是涨跌幅之和。","它不是与历史比较。"],"skills":["中点","读数"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Relative Volatility Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594684-relative-volatility-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does a Relative Volatility Index reading near 50 mean?","optionsEn":["The close is around the midpoint of the recent price range","Volatility on up moves and down moves is about equal","Recent gains and losses net to about zero, so price is flat","Recent volatility is at its historical median"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the range is 0–100 and 50 is the midpoint.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is range position, not a volatility comparison.","Correct: 50 is the midpoint.","Wrong: It compares volatility size, not the sum of price changes.","Wrong: It does not compare with history."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-172","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[68],"stem":"RCI常见的±80参考线表示什么？","options":["价格在窗口内的累计涨跌幅约80%","价格已进入超买超卖，通常要反转","价格涨跌顺序与时间先后高度一致","价格排名与时间先后几乎没有联系"],"answer":2,"explanation":"RCI看先后顺序与价格排名的一致程度，±80表示接近单调排列；只是常见参考。","optionExplanations":["错误：RCI比较的是排名顺序，不反映涨跌幅大小。","错误：±80只是一致性较强的参考，不是反转的信号线。","正确：±80表示价格排名与时间顺序接近单调排列，只是常见参考。","错误：这恰好相反，±80表示排名与时间高度一致。"],"skills":["参考线","排名"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Rank Correlation Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000765570-rank-correlation-index-rci/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do RCI's common ±80 reference lines indicate?","optionsEn":["Price has moved about 80% cumulatively in the window","Price is overbought or oversold and usually reverses","The order of price moves closely matches the time order","Price ranks have almost no link to time order"],"explanationEn":"RCI measures how closely time order matches price ranking; ±80 means a near-monotonic sequence and is only a common reference.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: RCI compares rank order and does not reflect the size of moves.","Wrong: ±80 is only a reference for strong agreement, not a reversal signal line.","Correct: ±80 means price ranks follow time order almost monotonically; it is only a common reference.","Wrong: This is the opposite; ±80 means ranks closely match time order."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-173","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[69],"stem":"Fisher Transform面板上的触发线（Trigger）通常是什么？","options":["Fisher主线的9期简单均线","价格自身的9期指数移动均线","上一轮极端值所画出的水平线","Fisher主线后移一根的值"],"answer":3,"explanation":"触发线就是Fisher向后错一根，用来看转向。","optionExplanations":["错误：触发线不是均线，而是主线向后错开一根。","错误：触发线来自Fisher本身，不是价格均线。","错误：触发线随每根K线移动，不是固定水平线。","正确：触发线就是Fisher向后错一根，用来看转向。"],"skills":["结构","触发线"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Fisher Transform","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589141-fisher-transform/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the Trigger line on a Fisher Transform panel usually?","optionsEn":["A 9-period simple average of the Fisher line","A 9-period EMA of price itself","A horizontal line drawn at the last extreme","The Fisher line shifted back by one bar"],"explanationEn":"The trigger is simply the Fisher line lagged one bar, used to spot turns.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The trigger is not an average but the main line lagged one bar.","Wrong: The trigger comes from Fisher itself, not a price average.","Wrong: The trigger moves with each bar and is not a fixed horizontal line.","Correct: The trigger is the Fisher line lagged one bar, used to spot turns."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-174","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[70],"stem":"DPO常见Period 21，用来做什么？","options":["去掉较长趋势，看短周期起伏","平滑价格后确认长期趋势方向","用居中后的峰谷预测未来21根走势","计算价格偏离均线的百分比幅度"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：减掉大方向影响，方便回看短期高低循环。","optionExplanations":["正确：DPO减掉大方向的影响，方便回看短期高低循环。","错误：DPO的目的恰好是去掉长趋势，不是确认它。","错误：居中只是回移显示，过去循环不会准时重演。","错误：DPO通常以价格差表示，且重点在去趋势看循环。"],"skills":["用途","去趋势"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Detrended Price Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502246-detrended-price-oscillator-dpo/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is DPO's common Period of 21 used for?","optionsEn":["Removing the longer trend to see short-cycle swings","Smoothing price to confirm the long-term trend direction","Using centered peaks and troughs to forecast the next 21 bars","Measuring the percentage deviation of price from its average"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: it strips out the broad direction so you can review short-term high–low cycles.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: DPO strips out the broad direction so you can review short-term high–low cycles.","Wrong: DPO's purpose is to remove the long trend, not confirm it.","Wrong: Centering only shifts the display back; past cycles will not repeat on schedule.","Wrong: DPO is usually a price difference, and its focus is detrending to see cycles."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-175","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[71],"stem":"KST内置默认的四个ROC周期是？","options":["10、15、20、30","9、12、26、50","14、28、56、112","5、34、50、200"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程注明：默认ROC 10/15/20/30，平滑10/10/10/15，信号9。","optionExplanations":["课程注明：默认ROC 10/15/20/30，平滑10/10/10/15，信号9。","不是这些组合。","不是这些组合。","不是这些组合。"],"skills":["默认参数","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Know Sure Thing","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502329-know-sure-thing-kst/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What are KST's four default ROC periods in the built-in version?","optionsEn":["10, 15, 20, 30","9, 12, 26, 50","14, 28, 56, 112","5, 34, 50, 200"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes defaults of ROC 10/15/20/30, smoothing 10/10/10/15 and signal 9.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The lesson notes defaults of ROC 10/15/20/30, smoothing 10/10/10/15 and signal 9.","Wrong: Not this combination.","Wrong: Not this combination.","Wrong: Not this combination."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-176","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[72],"stem":"Pring Special K主要适合观察哪种尺度的走势？","options":["分钟图上的即时短线进出点","日线及以上的中长期大方向","单日内买卖盘的逐笔变化","周内一两根K线的突发波动"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：合成短中长期涨跌速度看大方向，不适合即时追价。","optionExplanations":["错误：它需要大量历史，不适合即时追价。","正确：Special K合成短中长期涨跌速度，适合日线以上看大方向。","错误：它不读取逐笔数据，只合成多尺度涨跌速度。","错误：它刻意综合长期动力，不盯单个突发波动。"],"skills":["用途","周期"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Pring's Special K","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773011-pring-s-special-k/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What scale of move is Pring's Special K mainly suited to watching?","optionsEn":["Instant short-term entries and exits on minute charts","The broad medium- to long-term direction on daily charts and above","Tick-by-tick changes in intraday order flow","Sudden swings over one or two bars within a week"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: it combines short-, medium- and long-term rates of change to show the broad direction and is not for chasing price in real time.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It needs a lot of history and is not for chasing price in real time.","Correct: Special K combines short-, medium- and long-term rates of change and suits daily-and-above views of the broad direction.","Wrong: It reads no tick data; it only combines multi-scale rates of change.","Wrong: It deliberately blends long-term momentum rather than focusing on a single sudden swing."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-88","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[73],"stem":"想在TradingView使用PMO，本课给出的做法是？","options":["在内置指标库里直接搜索并加载PMO","把MACD周期改成35/20/10后用","找DecisionPoint公式脚本","把ROC周期改成35/20/10后用"],"answer":2,"explanation":"需要核对社区脚本的公式和参数（常见35/20/10）。","optionExplanations":["错误：本课做法是找并核对社区脚本，而非直接用内置版本。","错误：改参数不会让MACD变成PMO，两者公式不同。","正确：需要核对社区脚本的公式和参数（常见35/20/10）。","错误：PMO是对涨跌百分比做两次平滑，单改ROC周期不等价。"],"skills":["获取方式","脚本核对"],"references":[{"title":"DecisionPoint: Using DecisionPoint Timing Signals to Improve your Portfolio","url":"https://articles.stockcharts.com/article/articles-decisionpoint-2016-09-using-decisionpoint-timing-signals-to-improve-your-portfolio/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What approach does this lesson give for using PMO on TradingView?","optionsEn":["Search for and load PMO directly from the built-in library","Use MACD with its periods changed to 35/20/10","Find a script with the DecisionPoint formula","Use ROC with its periods changed to 35/20/10"],"explanationEn":"Check the community script's formula and settings (commonly 35/20/10).","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The lesson's approach is to find and check a community script, not use a built-in version.","Wrong: Changing settings does not turn MACD into PMO; the formulas differ.","Correct: Check the community script's formula and settings (commonly 35/20/10).","Wrong: PMO double-smooths percentage change; changing ROC periods alone is not equivalent."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-177","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[74],"stem":"科波克曲线的原始设计用在哪个周期？","options":["成交量图","1分钟图","小时图","月线"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：先在月线观察，原本用于看股市长期低迷后是否回暖。","optionExplanations":["它用价格计算。","一分钟图不是原始用途。","不是小时图。","课程：先在月线观察，原本用于看股市长期低迷后是否回暖。"],"skills":["周期","原始用途"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Coppock Curve","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589114-coppock-curve/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What timeframe was the Coppock Curve originally designed for?","optionsEn":["A volume chart","A 1-minute chart","An hourly chart","Monthly"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: watch it on the monthly chart first; it was originally meant to see whether the stock market was recovering after a long slump.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It is calculated from price.","Wrong: A 1-minute chart is not its original use.","Wrong: Not an hourly chart.","Correct: The lesson: watch it on the monthly chart first; it was originally meant to see whether the stock market was recovering after a long slump."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-178","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[75],"stem":"MACD-V里的“V”指什么？","options":["速度：用价格变化速率来加权","成交量：用成交量对MACD加权","价值：用估值水平对MACD调整","波动：用ATR衡量日常波动幅度"],"answer":3,"explanation":"MACD-V把MACD除以ATR，ATR代表日常波动尺度。","optionExplanations":["错误：V不是速度，而是用ATR衡量的波动。","错误：MACD-V不使用成交量，而是除以ATR。","错误：V与估值无关，指的是波动。","正确：MACD-V把MACD除以ATR，V代表波动尺度。"],"skills":["定义","易混"],"references":[{"title":"Alex Spiroglou: MACD-V original paper","url":"https://www.naaim.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/MACD-V-Alex-Spiroglou-WEB.pdf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the \"V\" in MACD-V stand for?","optionsEn":["Velocity: weighting by the rate of price change","Volume: weighting MACD by volume","Value: adjusting MACD by valuation","Volatility: measuring normal range with ATR"],"explanationEn":"MACD-V divides MACD by ATR, which represents the scale of normal volatility.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: V is not velocity but volatility measured by ATR.","Wrong: MACD-V does not use volume; it divides by ATR.","Wrong: V has nothing to do with valuation; it refers to volatility.","Correct: MACD-V divides MACD by ATR, and V stands for the volatility scale."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-179","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[76],"stem":"Mass Index用的是每根K线的什么信息？","options":["每根K线最高价与最低价的范围","每根K线收盘价相对前收的涨跌","每根K线开盘价与收盘价的差距","每根K线成交量相对均量的倍数"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：看K线高低范围怎样先扩大再收缩。","optionExplanations":["正确：Mass Index看K线高低范围怎样先扩大再收缩。","错误：它看的是高低范围，不是收盘涨跌。","错误：那是实体大小，Mass Index用的是最高减最低。","错误：Mass Index不使用成交量。"],"skills":["输入","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Mass Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589169-mass-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What information from each bar does the Mass Index use?","optionsEn":["The range between each bar's high and low","Each bar's close versus the prior close","The gap between each bar's open and close","Each bar's volume as a multiple of average volume"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: it watches how bar ranges first widen and then narrow.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The Mass Index watches how high–low ranges first widen and then narrow.","Wrong: It looks at the high–low range, not the close-to-close change.","Wrong: That is body size; the Mass Index uses high minus low.","Wrong: The Mass Index does not use volume."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-180","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[77],"stem":"添加累积派发线（ADL）前，应先确认什么？","options":["图表周期是否已设为日线以上","品种是否有可用的成交量数据","价格源是否已设为收盘价","是否已设好累计重置的时点"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：先确认成交量可用；ADL为累计线，关注升降。","optionExplanations":["错误：ADL在各周期都能计算，关键是有无成交量。","正确：ADL依赖成交量，要先确认成交量可用。","错误：ADL使用每根K线的高低收和成交量，不靠改价格源。","错误：ADL是持续累计线，先要确认的是成交量数据。"],"skills":["前置检查","成交量"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Accumulation/Distribution","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501979-chaikin-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Before adding the Accumulation/Distribution Line (ADL), what should you confirm first?","optionsEn":["Whether the chart timeframe is daily or above","Whether the instrument has usable volume data","Whether the price source is set to the close","Whether the cumulative reset time has been set"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: first confirm volume is available; ADL is cumulative, so focus on whether it rises or falls.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: ADL works on any timeframe; the key is whether volume exists.","Correct: ADL depends on volume, so confirm volume is available first.","Wrong: ADL uses each bar's high, low, close and volume, not a changed price source.","Wrong: ADL is a continuous cumulative line; what you need to confirm first is volume data."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-181","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[78],"stem":"CMF在一个平台显示0.15，在另一个平台显示15。最可能的原因是？","options":["一个用了收盘价，一个用了开盘价","其中一个是错误数据","两个平台的成交量完全不同","纵轴是否乘100不同"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：核对纵轴是否乘100。","optionExplanations":["CMF不按开盘价计算。","先核对刻度。","刻度差正好100倍，更像显示设置。","课程提醒：核对纵轴是否乘100。"],"skills":["刻度","设置"],"references":[{"title":"Chaikin Analytics: Chaikin Money Flow","url":"https://help.chaikinanalytics.com/knowledge-center/chaikin-money-flow"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"CMF shows 0.15 on one platform and 15 on another. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["One uses the close and the other the open","One of them has bad data","The two platforms have completely different volume","They differ in whether the axis is multiplied by 100"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, check whether the axis is multiplied by 100.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: CMF is not calculated from the open.","Wrong: Check the scale first.","Wrong: An exact 100-fold difference looks like a display setting.","Correct: As the lesson notes, check whether the axis is multiplied by 100."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-182","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[79],"stem":"蔡金振荡器的默认快、慢参数是？","options":["3和10","12和26","20和21","9和14"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程注明：常见Fast3/Slow10。","optionExplanations":["课程注明：常见Fast3/Slow10。","12/26是MACD。","20/21是CMF的常见周期。","不是本指标默认。"],"skills":["默认参数","易混"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chaikin Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000501979-chaikin-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What are the Chaikin Oscillator's default fast and slow settings?","optionsEn":["3 and 10","12 and 26","20 and 21","9 and 14"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes the common Fast 3 / Slow 10.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The lesson notes the common Fast 3 / Slow 10.","Wrong: 12/26 is MACD.","Wrong: 20/21 are common CMF periods.","Wrong: This is not the indicator's default."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-183","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[80],"stem":"克林格振荡器在零线上方，最基础的含义是？","options":["当根成交量高于近期平均成交量","力度线高于它自己的信号线","力度的快速均线高于慢速均线","收盘价高于最近的指数均线"],"answer":2,"explanation":"KVO=力度EMA34−EMA55，为正表示快平均高于慢平均。","optionExplanations":["错误：零线讲的是力度两条均线之差，不是单根量能。","错误：那是与信号线的关系，不是零线上方的含义。","正确：KVO=力度EMA34−EMA55，为正即快平均高于慢平均。","错误：KVO由力度计算，不直接比较价格与均线。"],"skills":["零线","结构"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Klinger Oscillator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589157-klinger-oscillator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the most basic meaning of the Klinger Oscillator being above zero?","optionsEn":["This bar's volume is above recent average volume","The force line is above its own signal line","The fast average of volume force is above the slow average","The close is above its recent exponential average"],"explanationEn":"KVO = EMA34 − EMA55 of volume force; positive means the fast average is above the slow one.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The zero line concerns the gap between two averages of volume force, not one bar's volume.","Wrong: That is the relation to the signal line, not the meaning of being above zero.","Correct: KVO = EMA34 − EMA55 of volume force, so positive means the fast average is above the slow.","Wrong: KVO is calculated from volume force and does not compare price with an average directly."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-184","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[81],"stem":"Elder力度指数内置常见的平滑长度是？","options":["200","9","26","13"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程注明：常见平滑长度13。","optionExplanations":["不是200。","不是9。","不是26。","课程注明：常见平滑长度13。"],"skills":["默认参数","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Elder Force Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502259-elder-s-force-index-efi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the common built-in smoothing length for Elder's Force Index?","optionsEn":["200","9","26","13"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes a common smoothing length of 13.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Not 200.","Wrong: Not 9.","Wrong: Not 26.","Correct: The lesson notes a common smoothing length of 13."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-89","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[82],"stem":"EOM设置里的Divisor参数改大10倍，线会怎样？","options":["对成交量变化更敏感，波动更大","线条更平滑，但数值尺度不变","零线位置上移，读数多数为正","数值尺度改变，正负与形状不变"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程注明：Divisor调数值尺度。","optionExplanations":["错误：Divisor只缩放数值，不改变灵敏度。","错误：平滑度由Length控制，Divisor改变的正是尺度。","错误：零线是固定的，缩放不会让读数偏正。","正确：课程注明Divisor调数值尺度，不改变方向与形状。"],"skills":["参数","尺度"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ease of Movement","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502256-ease-of-movement-eom/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In EOM's settings, the Divisor is increased tenfold. What happens to the line?","optionsEn":["It becomes more sensitive to volume changes and swings more","It becomes smoother, but the scale stays the same","The zero line moves up and most readings turn positive","The scale changes; the sign and shape do not"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that Divisor sets the numeric scale.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Divisor only rescales values; it does not change sensitivity.","Wrong: Smoothness is set by Length; Divisor changes the scale itself.","Wrong: The zero line is fixed, and rescaling does not push readings positive.","Correct: The lesson notes Divisor sets the numeric scale without changing direction or shape."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-185","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[83],"stem":"PVI常搭配的信号线是什么？","options":["EMA200","EMA255","SMA255","SMA200"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程注明：内置初值1000，常见EMA255。","optionExplanations":["EMA200是常见长期均线，但不是PVI的常见信号线。","正确，常见信号线是EMA255。","类型不同，常见的是EMA而非SMA。","SMA200是通用长期均线，不是PVI的搭配。"],"skills":["默认参数","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Positive Volume Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773006-positive-volume-index-pvi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What signal line is commonly paired with PVI?","optionsEn":["EMA200","EMA255","SMA255","SMA200"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes a built-in starting value of 1000 and a common EMA255.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: EMA200 is a common long-term average, but not PVI's usual signal line.","Correct: The common signal line is EMA255.","Wrong: Wrong type; the usual one is an EMA, not an SMA.","Wrong: SMA200 is a generic long-term average, not PVI's usual pairing."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-90","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[84],"stem":"NVI位于自身EMA255之上。传统解读常怎样描述？其性质是什么？","options":["缩量日偏强，属传统读法","大资金正在缩量日持续吸筹","放量日的价格表现整体更强","接下来成交量大概率将放大"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：上升不能证明机构买入，它不读取账户身份。","optionExplanations":["正确：这是传统观点，不能证明机构买入。","错误：指标不读取账户身份，不能证明机构买入。","错误：NVI只看成交量下降日的价格变化。","错误：NVI位置不预测后续成交量。"],"skills":["解读","局限"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Negative Volume Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773005-negative-volume-index-nvi/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"NVI is above its own EMA255. How is this traditionally described, and what is the nature of that reading?","optionsEn":["Strength on lower-volume days, a traditional reading","Big money is steadily accumulating on quiet days","Price performs better overall on higher-volume days","Volume is likely to expand next"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, a rise does not prove institutional buying; the indicator does not read account identities.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: This is a traditional view and does not prove institutional buying.","Wrong: The indicator does not read account identities, so it cannot prove institutional buying.","Wrong: NVI looks only at price changes on lower-volume days.","Wrong: NVI's position does not predict future volume."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-186","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[85],"stem":"BOP读数为0，表示这根K线怎样？","options":["收盘等于最低价","收盘等于开盘","成交量为零","最高等于最低"],"answer":1,"explanation":"BOP=(收盘−开盘)÷(最高−最低)，分子为0。","optionExplanations":["那会使BOP为负。","BOP=(收盘−开盘)÷(最高−最低)，分子为0。","BOP不用成交量。","最高等于最低时分母为零，需特殊处理。"],"skills":["读数","定义"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Balance of Power","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589100-balance-of-power-bop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"A BOP reading of 0 means what about the bar?","optionsEn":["The close equals the low","The close equals the open","Volume is zero","The high equals the low"],"explanationEn":"BOP = (close − open) ÷ (high − low), so the numerator is 0.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That would make BOP negative.","Correct: BOP = (close − open) ÷ (high − low), so the numerator is 0.","Wrong: BOP does not use volume.","Wrong: When the high equals the low the denominator is zero and needs special handling."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-91","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[86],"stem":"Relative Volume at Time的Calculation Mode选“Cumulative”时，比较的是什么？","options":["当天累计量对昨天全天总成交量","当天累计量对过去同刻累计均值","本根成交量对最近20根均量","本根成交量对过去同刻单根均量"],"answer":1,"explanation":"累计模式比较“到这个时刻为止”的累计量。","optionExplanations":["错误：比较的是过去同一时刻，而不是全天总量。","正确：累计模式比较到这个时刻为止的累计量。","错误：这不分时刻，也不是累计模式。","错误：这是非累计的单根比较。"],"skills":["设置","比较基准"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Relative Volume at Time","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000705489-relative-volume-at-time/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In Relative Volume at Time, what is compared when Calculation Mode is set to \"Cumulative\"?","optionsEn":["Today's cumulative volume versus yesterday's full-day total","Today's cumulative volume versus the past average cumulative volume at the same time","This bar's volume versus the last 20 bars' average","This bar's volume versus the past average for the same time slot"],"explanationEn":"Cumulative mode compares the volume accumulated up to this point in the day.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It compares with the same time in the past, not the full-day total.","Correct: Cumulative mode compares the volume accumulated up to this point in the day.","Wrong: This ignores time of day and is not cumulative mode.","Wrong: This is the non-cumulative single-bar comparison."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-187","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[87],"stem":"TTM Squeeze从“挤压中”变为“未挤压”，最基础的含义是？","options":["价格已确认向上突破","波动开始收缩，方向另看","波动开始扩张，方向另看","趋势结束，进入横盘"],"answer":2,"explanation":"挤压结束说明布林带走出肯特纳通道，即波动放大；课程提醒挤压不是向上信号。","optionExplanations":["方向并未由挤压本身给出。","那是进入挤压。","挤压结束说明布林带走出肯特纳通道，即波动放大；课程提醒挤压不是向上信号。","不说明趋势结束。"],"skills":["状态变化","解读"],"references":[{"title":"John Carter — Simpler Trading","url":"https://www.simplertrading.com/traders/john-carter/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"TTM Squeeze changes from \"on\" to \"off\". What is the most basic meaning?","optionsEn":["Price has confirmed an upside breakout","Volatility is starting to contract; direction is a separate question","Volatility is starting to expand; direction is a separate question","The trend has ended and a range has begun"],"explanationEn":"A squeeze ending means the Bollinger Bands moved outside the Keltner Channel, i.e. volatility is expanding; the lesson notes that a squeeze is not a bullish signal.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The squeeze itself gives no direction.","Wrong: That is entering a squeeze.","Correct: A squeeze ending means the Bollinger Bands moved outside the Keltner Channel, i.e. volatility is expanding; the lesson notes that a squeeze is not a bullish signal.","Wrong: It does not indicate that a trend has ended."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-188","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[88],"stem":"溃疡指数的Length参数控制什么？","options":["平滑回撤读数的均线周期","回撤从最低点起算的根数","计算回撤时观察多少根K线","回撤超过多少百分比才计入"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程注明：Length是观察多少根K线。","optionExplanations":["它不是额外的平滑。","回撤从近期高点起算。","课程注明：Length是观察多少根K线。","没有这种门槛。"],"skills":["参数","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Ulcer Index","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773115-ulcer-index/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the Ulcer Index's Length setting control?","optionsEn":["The period of an average that smooths the drawdown reading","The number of bars counted from the low of the drawdown","How many bars to look at when calculating drawdown","What percentage a drawdown must exceed to count"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that Length is how many bars are examined.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It is not extra smoothing.","Wrong: Drawdowns are measured from the recent high.","Correct: The lesson notes that Length is how many bars are examined.","Wrong: There is no such threshold."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-92","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[89],"stem":"吊灯止损设置里勾选“用收盘价求极值”后，多头止损线会怎样？","options":["用最高收盘价减ATR倍数，通常略高","用最高价减ATR倍数，但周期缩短一半","用最高收盘价减ATR倍数，通常略低","用收盘价均线减ATR倍数，通常更平滑"],"answer":2,"explanation":"收盘最高通常不高于最高价，所以止损线通常略低。","optionExplanations":["错误：最高收盘不会高于最高价，所以不会更高。","错误：勾选只改变极值取法，不改变ATR周期。","正确：最高收盘通常不高于最高价，因此止损线通常略低。","错误：勾选后取的是最高收盘，不是均线。"],"skills":["设置","变体"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chandelier Exit","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000773013-chandelier-exit/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In the Chandelier Exit settings you tick \"use close for extremes\". What happens to the long stop line?","optionsEn":["Highest close minus the ATR multiple, usually a little higher","Highest high minus the ATR multiple, with the period halved","Highest close minus the ATR multiple, usually a little lower","A moving average of closes minus the ATR multiple, usually smoother"],"explanationEn":"The highest close is usually no higher than the highest high, so the stop is usually a little lower.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The highest close cannot exceed the highest high, so it will not be higher.","Wrong: The option changes only how the extreme is taken, not the ATR period.","Correct: The highest close is usually no higher than the highest high, so the stop is usually a little lower.","Wrong: With the option ticked it uses the highest close, not an average."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-189","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[90],"stem":"钱德克罗止损的p、x、q三个参数分别控制什么？","options":["ATR倍数、ATR周期、止损回看根数","ATR周期、止损回看根数、ATR倍数","止损回看根数、ATR周期、ATR倍数","ATR周期、ATR倍数、止损回看根数"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程注明：p、x、q各自控制波动周期、倍数和止损回看。","optionExplanations":["错误：p与x的含义被调换了。","错误：x与q的含义被调换了。","错误：三项的顺序全部错位。","正确：p是波动周期，x是倍数，q是止损回看。"],"skills":["参数","设置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Chande Kroll Stop","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589105-chande-kroll-stop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do the Chande Kroll Stop's three settings p, x and q control?","optionsEn":["ATR multiple, ATR period, stop lookback","ATR period, stop lookback, ATR multiple","Stop lookback, ATR period, ATR multiple","ATR period, ATR multiple, stop lookback"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that p, x and q set the volatility period, the multiple and the stop lookback.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The meanings of p and x are swapped.","Wrong: The meanings of x and q are swapped.","Wrong: All three are out of order.","Correct: P is the volatility period, x the multiple and q the stop lookback."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-190","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[91],"stem":"图上画出的ATR跟踪止损线，与账户里的止损单是什么关系？","options":["只是图上的参考线，不会自动下单","触线时平台会自动按市价平仓","画出后相当于已挂出一张止损单","连接券商账户后会自动转为止损单"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：图上的线不是自动成交的止损单。","optionExplanations":["正确：图上的线不是自动成交的止损单。","错误：画线不等于下单，触线不会自动成交。","错误：指标线与券商挂单是两回事。","错误：连接账户也不会让指标线变成委托。"],"skills":["用途","局限"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volatility Stop methods","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594676-volatility-stop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does an ATR trailing stop line drawn on the chart relate to a stop order in your account?","optionsEn":["It is only a reference line on the chart and places no orders","When price touches it, the platform closes the position at market","Once drawn, it is equivalent to a resting stop order","Linking a broker account turns it into a stop order automatically"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, a line on the chart is not a stop order that executes automatically.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A line on the chart is not a stop order that executes automatically.","Wrong: Drawing a line is not placing an order; touching it fills nothing.","Wrong: An indicator line and a broker order are two different things.","Wrong: Linking an account does not turn an indicator line into an order."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-191","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[92],"stem":"某资产平时波动很大。Volatility Stop的止损距离通常会怎样？","options":["止损距离通常更窄","止损距离通常更宽","止损距离通常不受影响","止损距离先变窄再变宽"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：平时晃得大就留宽一点，平时安静就留窄一点。","optionExplanations":["错误：方向反了，波动大需要更宽的缓冲。","正确：平时波动大就留宽一点，安静就留窄一点。","错误：止损距离正是随波动调整的。","错误：没有这种固定先后规律，距离随波动大小而定。"],"skills":["原理","ATR"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volatility Stop","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000594676-volatility-stop/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"An asset is normally very volatile. What usually happens to the Volatility Stop's distance?","optionsEn":["The stop distance is usually narrower","The stop distance is usually wider","The stop distance is usually unaffected","The stop distance first narrows and then widens"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: give more room when it normally swings a lot, less when it is normally quiet.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This is reversed; high volatility needs a wider buffer.","Correct: Give more room when it normally swings a lot and less when it is quiet.","Wrong: The stop distance is exactly what adjusts with volatility.","Wrong: There is no fixed sequence; the distance depends on volatility."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-192","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[93],"stem":"TradingView里，可以自己点选起点的锚定VWAP（Anchored VWAP）工具在哪里？","options":["指标列表里的VWMA，设置选起点","图表设置的会话选项里选择锚点","左侧绘图工具里选中后点锚点","顶部周期栏右键选择起始K线"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：这是左侧绘图工具，选中后点锚点。","optionExplanations":["错误：VWMA是成交量加权均线，不是锚定VWAP。","错误：会话选项不能自由点选起点。","正确：Anchored VWAP是左侧绘图工具，选中后点锚点。","错误：周期栏用于切换周期，不能设置锚点。"],"skills":["操作入口","易混"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Anchored VWAP drawing tool","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000669764-anchored-vwap-drawing-tool/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"Where in TradingView is the Anchored VWAP tool that lets you click your own starting point?","optionsEn":["VWMA in the indicator list, picking a start in settings","Choosing an anchor in the chart settings' session options","Selecting it from the left drawing tools and clicking an anchor","Right-clicking the top timeframe bar to pick a starting bar"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: it is a left-side drawing tool; select it and click the anchor.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: VWMA is a volume-weighted moving average, not anchored VWAP.","Wrong: Session options do not let you click any starting point.","Correct: Anchored VWAP is a left-side drawing tool; select it and click the anchor.","Wrong: The timeframe bar switches timeframes and cannot set an anchor."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-193","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[94],"stem":"在15分钟图上加枢轴点，Pivots Timeframe设为Daily。线会怎样画？","options":["每周一组水平线，按前一周高低收计算","每天一组水平线，按当天开盘价计算","每15分钟更新，按上根K线高低收计算","每天一组水平线，按前一天高低收计算"],"answer":3,"explanation":"日枢轴每天一组，由前一日数据算出。","optionExplanations":["错误：Daily对应日数据，不是周数据。","错误：枢轴用前一日高低收，不是当天开盘价。","错误：设为Daily后不按图表周期逐根重算。","正确：日枢轴每天一组，由前一日数据算出。"],"skills":["设置","周期"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Pivot formulas and examples","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/v4/essential/drawings/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"You add pivot points to a 15-minute chart with Pivots Timeframe set to Daily. How are the lines drawn?","optionsEn":["One set of horizontal lines a week, from the prior week's high, low and close","One set a day, calculated from that day's open","Updated every 15 minutes from the previous bar's high, low and close","One set of horizontal lines a day, from the prior day's high, low and close"],"explanationEn":"Daily pivots form one set each day, calculated from the prior day's data.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Daily means daily data, not weekly.","Wrong: Pivots use the prior day's high, low and close, not today's open.","Wrong: Set to Daily, they are not recalculated bar by bar on the chart timeframe.","Correct: Daily pivots form one set each day, calculated from the prior day's data."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-194","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[95],"stem":"高低点枢轴设为左右各10根。最新的一个高点标记为什么总是晚出现？","options":["右侧10根走完后才确认并回标","左侧需积累10根数据才开始标记","价格需离开高点10%才触发标记","平台每10根K线才刷新一次"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：留意左右确认长度与标记回画。","optionExplanations":["正确：需右侧10根走完才确认，再回标到高点。","错误：左侧确认并不造成最新高点晚出现。","错误：参数是K线根数，不是百分比。","错误：平台逐根更新，延迟来自右侧确认。"],"skills":["确认延迟","回画"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Pivot Points High/Low example","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/v4/essential/drawings/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"High/low pivots are set to 10 bars on each side. Why does the latest high marker always appear late?","optionsEn":["It is confirmed and back-plotted only after the 10 bars to the right finish","10 bars must build up on the left before marking starts","Price must move 10% away from the high to trigger a mark","The platform refreshes only once every 10 bars"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, watch the left/right confirmation lengths and the back-plotting of marks.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: It is confirmed only after the 10 bars to the right finish, then plotted back at the high.","Wrong: Left-side confirmation does not make the latest high appear late.","Wrong: The setting is a number of bars, not a percentage.","Wrong: The platform updates every bar; the delay comes from right-side confirmation."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-195","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[97],"stem":"为什么分形标记出现在两根K线以前，而不是最新一根？","options":["等成交量放大确认，再回标高点","等右侧两根确认，再回标中间那根","因收盘价计算而固定延迟两根显示","先标在最新一根，两根后自动平移"],"answer":1,"explanation":"分形由5根组成，中间那根才是峰谷。","optionExplanations":["错误：分形只看价格高低排列，不看成交量。","正确：分形由5根组成，需右侧两根确认后回标中间那根。","错误：延迟来自右侧确认，不是价格源。","错误：标记是回画到中间那根，而不是平移。"],"skills":["确认","回标"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Williams fractal indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591663-williams-fractal-indicator/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Why does a fractal mark appear two bars back instead of on the latest bar?","optionsEn":["It waits for volume to expand, then marks the high","It waits for two bars on the right to confirm, then marks the middle bar","Using closes fixes a two-bar display delay","It marks the latest bar first and shifts it two bars later"],"explanationEn":"A fractal is made of 5 bars, and the middle one is the peak or trough.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Fractals look only at the arrangement of highs and lows, not volume.","Correct: A fractal is made of 5 bars and is plotted on the middle bar once the two bars to its right confirm it.","Wrong: The delay comes from right-side confirmation, not the price source.","Wrong: The mark is drawn back on the middle bar, not shifted."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-196","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[98],"stem":"ZigZag设置里的Deviation（偏离门槛）控制什么？","options":["相邻两个转折点之间至少间隔多少根K线","反向运动达到多大幅度才确认一个转折","向左回看多少根K线来寻找高低点","折线相对K线价格整体上移或下移的幅度"],"answer":1,"explanation":"门槛越大，忽略的小波动越多。","optionExplanations":["那是最小间隔，不是偏离门槛。","正确，门槛越大忽略的小波动越多。","那是回看长度，不是偏离门槛。","偏离门槛不是整体位置偏移。"],"skills":["参数","门槛"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Zig Zag","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000591664-zig-zag/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does Deviation (the reversal threshold) control in ZigZag's settings?","optionsEn":["The minimum number of bars between two turning points","How large a reverse move must be to confirm a turn","How many bars back to search for highs and lows","How far the whole zigzag line is shifted up or down relative to price"],"explanationEn":"The larger the threshold, the more small swings are ignored.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is the minimum spacing, not the deviation threshold.","Correct: The larger the threshold, the more small swings are ignored.","Wrong: That is the lookback, not the deviation threshold.","Wrong: The deviation threshold is not an overall position offset."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-93","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[101],"stem":"把内置Volume Delta的下级周期从1分钟改为5分钟，读数可能怎样？","options":["会变，因为成交总量统计发生变化","不变，因为总成交量保持相同","会变，因方向由下级周期价格估算","不变，因为读取的是逐笔成交记录"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：内置版本按下级周期价格变化估算方向。","optionExplanations":["错误：总成交量不变，变的是方向估算。","错误：方向的估算依赖下级周期，所以读数会变。","正确：课程提醒：内置版本按下级周期价格变化估算方向。","错误：内置版本是估算，并非读取逐笔成交。"],"skills":["设置","估算"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume Delta official tutorial","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XL5KiP2mBUQ"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"You change the built-in Volume Delta's lower timeframe from 1 minute to 5 minutes. What may happen to the readings?","optionsEn":["They change, because the total volume count changes","They stay the same, because total volume is unchanged","They change, because direction is estimated from lower-timeframe price","They stay the same, because it reads tick-by-tick trades"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, the built-in version estimates direction from lower-timeframe price changes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Total volume is unchanged; what changes is the direction estimate.","Wrong: The direction estimate depends on the lower timeframe, so readings change.","Correct: As the lesson notes, the built-in version estimates direction from lower-timeframe price changes.","Wrong: The built-in version estimates; it does not read tick-by-tick trades."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-197","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[102],"stem":"CVD设置里的Anchor period决定什么？","options":["成交量数据取自哪家交易所","Delta按哪个周期估算方向","累计线显示所用的时区基准","累计值何时归零后重新开始"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程注明：Anchor period决定累计何时归零。","optionExplanations":["错误：锚点周期不选择数据来源。","错误：估算周期是另一项设置。","错误：时区在图表设置里，与锚点无关。","正确：Anchor period决定累计何时归零。"],"skills":["设置","重置"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Cumulative Volume Delta","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000725058-cumulative-volume-delta/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the Anchor period setting in CVD decide?","optionsEn":["Which exchange the volume data comes from","Which timeframe Delta uses to estimate direction","The time-zone basis of the cumulative line","When the cumulative value resets to zero and starts again"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that Anchor period decides when the running total resets to zero.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The anchor period does not choose the data source.","Wrong: The estimation timeframe is a separate setting.","Wrong: Time zone is in the chart settings and unrelated to the anchor.","Correct: Anchor period decides when the running total resets to zero."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-94","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[104],"stem":"在指标列表里看到“Advance/Decline Ratio (Bars)”。它和本课的腾落线有什么不同？","options":["它统计单个品种上涨与下跌K线的根数","它是腾落线的累计版本，使用成分股家数","它统计整个市场上涨与下跌的家数，但不累计","它统计指数成分股的涨跌家数，并加以累计"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：别误选Advance/Decline Ratio (Bars)；腾落线需要市场广度数据。","optionExplanations":["正确，不需要市场广度数据。","它不使用家数，也不是累计版。","它统计的是K线根数而不是家数。","那才接近腾落线，它并非如此。"],"skills":["易混","数据来源"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Advance/Decline Line","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589092-advance-decline-line/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"You see \"Advance/Decline Ratio (Bars)\" in the indicator list. How does it differ from this lesson's advance-decline line?","optionsEn":["It counts up and down bars on a single instrument","It is a cumulative version of the A/D line using constituent counts","It counts advancing and declining stocks market-wide but does not accumulate","It counts index constituents that rise and fall and accumulates them"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, don't pick Advance/Decline Ratio (Bars) by mistake; the A/D line needs market breadth data.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: It needs no market breadth data.","Wrong: It does not use stock counts and is not cumulative.","Wrong: It counts bars, not stocks.","Wrong: That would be closer to the A/D line, which it is not."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-198","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[105],"stem":"同一天，用20日新高新低和用52周新高新低得到的读数不同。原因是？","options":["回看周期不同，所以新高定义不同","20日版本把平盘日也算成新高","两个版本取自不同交易所的数据","52周版本按周线收盘而非日线计算"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：高低周期不同，结论也不同。","optionExplanations":["正确：高低周期不同，结论也不同。","错误：两者的区别在回看窗口，而非平盘规则。","错误：原因是回看周期，而不是数据来源。","错误：周期长短决定定义，两者都用同样的日线数据。"],"skills":["定义","周期"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Market breadth — New highs and lows","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000794826-market-breadth-new-highs-and-lows/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"On the same day, 20-day new highs/lows and 52-week new highs/lows give different readings. Why?","optionsEn":["The lookback periods differ, so a \"new high\" is defined differently","The 20-day version also counts unchanged days as new highs","The two versions use data from different exchanges","The 52-week version uses weekly closes instead of daily data"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, a different high/low period gives a different conclusion.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A different high/low period gives a different conclusion.","Wrong: The difference is the lookback window, not a rule for unchanged days.","Wrong: The cause is the lookback period, not the data source.","Wrong: The period length sets the definition; both use the same daily data."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-199","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[106],"stem":"均线上方占比使用200日均线，比使用20日均线时变化得怎样？","options":["更快，因为长均线更易被穿越","更慢，反映更长期的参与面","更快，因为长均线更贴近价格","速度相同，只是数值整体偏低"],"answer":1,"explanation":"均线越长，个股越不容易穿越，占比变化越慢。","optionExplanations":["错误：长均线更不易被穿越，所以变化更慢。","正确：均线越长，个股越不易穿越，占比变化越慢。","错误：长均线离价格更远、更平稳。","错误：均线长度改变了占比变化的速度。"],"skills":["周期","敏感度"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Market breadth — Above moving averages","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000794827-market-breadth-above-moving-averages/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does the percentage of stocks above their moving average change when using a 200-day average instead of a 20-day one?","optionsEn":["Faster, because a long average is crossed more easily","More slowly, reflecting longer-term participation","Faster, because a long average sits closer to price","At the same speed, just at a generally lower level"],"explanationEn":"The longer the average, the less often stocks cross it, so the percentage changes more slowly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A long average is crossed less easily, so it changes more slowly.","Correct: The longer the average, the less often stocks cross it, so the percentage changes more slowly.","Wrong: A long average sits farther from price and is steadier.","Wrong: The average's length changes how fast the percentage moves."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-95","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[109],"stem":"两家交易所的多空账户比分别为1.8和0.9。能不能平均成1.35当作全市场读数？","options":["能，按两家交易所账户数加权后可代表全市场","能，简单平均能给出全市场的大致读数","不能，多空账户比只在同一时间点才有意义","不能，各家交易所的账户范围与定义不同"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程提醒：数据依赖来源；不同交易所账户数与定义不同。","optionExplanations":["定义与范围不同，加权也不能得到全市场读数。","口径不同的比值不能简单平均。","理由不对，问题出在各家的口径不同。","正确，数据依赖来源，不能直接平均。"],"skills":["数据来源","可比性"],"references":[{"title":"Binance derivatives API: Global long/short account ratio","url":"https://developers.binance.com/docs/derivatives/usds-margined-futures/market-data/rest-api/Long-Short-Ratio"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Two exchanges report long/short account ratios of 1.8 and 0.9. Can you average them to 1.35 as a market-wide reading?","optionsEn":["Yes; weighted by each exchange's account count it represents the market","Yes; a simple average gives a rough market-wide reading","No; long/short ratios only mean something at a single point in time","No; each exchange's account coverage and definitions differ"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, the data depends on its source; exchanges differ in account numbers and definitions.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The definitions and coverage differ, so even weighting cannot give a market-wide reading.","Wrong: Ratios built on different bases cannot simply be averaged.","Wrong: Wrong reason; the problem is that each exchange counts differently.","Correct: The data depends on its source and cannot be averaged directly."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-200","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[111],"stem":"画支撑时，为什么建议画成一个“区”而不是单一价格？","options":["区间可以让止跌更可靠","几次低点不会完全相同","单一价格会被平台修正","价格多在整数位附近止跌"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程示例：三次跌到99到101附近反弹，可画成区。","optionExplanations":["课程提醒：支撑阻力是观察位置，不是墙。","课程示例：三次跌到99到101附近反弹，可画成区。","平台不会修正画线。","没有这种规律。"],"skills":["画法","容差"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"When drawing support, why is it suggested to draw a zone rather than a single price?","optionsEn":["A zone makes the bounce more reliable","Several lows will not be exactly the same","A single price would be corrected by the platform","Price usually stops falling near round numbers"],"explanationEn":"The lesson's example: price bounced three times near 99 to 101, which can be drawn as a zone.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: As the lesson notes, support and resistance are places to watch, not walls.","Correct: The lesson's example: price bounced three times near 99 to 101, which can be drawn as a zone.","Wrong: The platform does not correct drawings.","Wrong: There is no such rule."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-201","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[112],"stem":"画一条趋势线最少需要几个点？第三个点通常用来做什么？","options":["两个点；第三点用来决定斜率","三个点；缺第三点就无法成线","两个点；第三点通常用来检验","三个点；第三点用来修正前两点"],"answer":2,"explanation":"两点成线，之后的接触可作检验。","optionExplanations":["错误：斜率由前两点已确定，第三点用来检验。","错误：两点即可画出趋势线。","正确：两点成线，之后的接触可作检验。","错误：第三点用来验证，不是修正前两点。"],"skills":["画法","验证"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the minimum number of points to draw a trend line, and what is a third point usually for?","optionsEn":["Two; the third point sets the slope","Three; without a third point there is no line","Two; the third point is usually a test","Three; the third point corrects the first two"],"explanationEn":"Two points make a line, and later touches can serve as tests.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The first two points already set the slope; the third is a test.","Wrong: Two points are enough to draw a trend line.","Correct: Two points make a line, and later touches can serve as tests.","Wrong: The third point validates; it does not correct the first two."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-202","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[113],"stem":"图表类型选Candles、周期为1小时，一根K线代表什么？","options":["这一小时的平均成交价与总成交量","这一小时内每分钟收盘价的集合","这一天截至当前的开高低收价格","这一小时的开高低收四个价格"],"answer":3,"explanation":"每根K线对应所选周期内的开高低收。","optionExplanations":["错误：K线展示开高低收，不是平均价。","错误：K线只汇总四个价格，不列出每分钟数据。","错误：周期选1小时，一根K线只覆盖这一小时。","正确：每根K线对应所选周期内的开高低收。"],"skills":["基础","周期"],"references":[{"title":"Steve Nison — CandleCharts","url":"https://candlecharts.com/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"With the chart type set to Candles and the timeframe at 1 hour, what does one candle represent?","optionsEn":["The hour's average traded price and total volume","Every minute's close within the hour","The day's open, high, low and close so far","The hour's open, high, low and close"],"explanationEn":"Each candle shows the open, high, low and close for the chosen timeframe.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Candles show open, high, low and close, not an average price.","Wrong: A candle summarises four prices; it does not list each minute.","Wrong: At 1 hour, each candle covers only that hour.","Correct: Each candle shows the open, high, low and close for the chosen timeframe."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-203","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[114],"stem":"价格第二次到达前高后回落，但还没跌破颈线。此时应怎样称呼它？","options":["双顶候选，仍待跌破颈线确认","已确认的双顶，回落已完成验证","头肩顶的右肩，正在逐步形成","上升三角形突破失败后的回落"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程示例：跌破颈线后才满足某些双顶确认规则。","optionExplanations":["正确：跌破颈线后才满足某些双顶确认规则。","错误：没跌破颈线，形态尚未确认。","错误：第二次到达前高、与前高相近，更像双顶候选。","错误：没有突破，也不是三角形失败。"],"skills":["候选与确认","术语"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Price reaches the prior high a second time and pulls back, but has not broken the neckline. What should you call it now?","optionsEn":["A double-top candidate, still awaiting a neckline break","A confirmed double top, the pullback has validated it","The right shoulder of a head and shoulders, still forming","A pullback after a failed ascending-triangle breakout"],"explanationEn":"The lesson's example: some double-top confirmation rules are met only after the neckline breaks.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Some double-top confirmation rules are met only after the neckline breaks.","Wrong: The neckline has not broken, so the pattern is not confirmed.","Wrong: A second test near the prior high looks more like a double-top candidate.","Wrong: There was no breakout, and this is not a failed triangle."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-204","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[115],"stem":"练习“裸K”需要在TradingView添加什么？","options":["先添加Price Action指标","无需专门指标，用K线与画线即可练习","先把K线类型更换成平均K线图","先保留成交量柱和一条长期均线"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：不存在必须添加的“裸K”指标。","optionExplanations":["错误：裸K的含义就是不依赖专门指标。","正确：不存在必须添加的裸K指标。","错误：平均K线是加工后的图，不是裸K。","错误：裸K强调只看K线和画线本身。"],"skills":["操作","准备"],"references":[{"title":"Brooks Trading Course","url":"https://www.brookstradingcourse.com/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do you need to add on TradingView to practise \"naked\" price action?","optionsEn":["A Price Action indicator first","No special indicator; candles and drawings are enough","Switch the candle type to Heikin Ashi first","Keep volume bars and one long-term average first"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: there is no \"naked chart\" indicator you must add.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Naked price action means not relying on special indicators.","Correct: There is no naked-chart indicator you must add.","Wrong: Heikin Ashi is a processed chart, not naked price.","Wrong: Naked price action means looking only at candles and drawings."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-205","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[116],"stem":"道氏理论把走势分成主要趋势、次级回调和短期波动。三者的主要区别是？","options":["所适用的市场品种不同","所依赖的技术指标不同","时间跨度与波动规模不同","价格与成交量的单位不同"],"answer":2,"explanation":"它们是同一价格在不同时间尺度上的运动。","optionExplanations":["错误：三者出现在同一市场。","错误：区分靠时间跨度，不靠指标。","正确：它们是同一价格在不同时间尺度上的运动。","错误：三者用同样的价格与成交量单位。"],"skills":["层级","时间尺度"],"references":[{"title":"CMT Association: Dow Theory history","url":"https://cmtassociation.org/technically_speaking/technically-speaking-october-2011/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Dow Theory divides moves into primary trends, secondary reactions and minor moves. What mainly separates them?","optionsEn":["The markets they apply to","The indicators they rely on","Their time span and size of swing","The units of price and volume"],"explanationEn":"They are movements of the same price on different time scales.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: All three occur in the same market.","Wrong: They are told apart by time span, not indicators.","Correct: They are movements of the same price on different time scales.","Wrong: All three use the same price and volume units."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-206","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[118],"stem":"威科夫方法常用哪四个词描述市场阶段？","options":["突破、回踩、确认、加仓","超买、超卖、背离、交叉","开盘、盘中、收盘、盘后","吸筹、上涨、派发、下跌"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：常用吸筹、上涨、派发、下跌描述阶段。","optionExplanations":["错误：这是操作步骤，不是市场阶段。","错误：这是指标信号用语，不是威科夫阶段。","错误：这是交易时段，不是市场阶段。","正确：威科夫常用吸筹、上涨、派发、下跌描述阶段。"],"skills":["术语","阶段"],"references":[{"title":"Wyckoff Analytics: Method and history","url":"https://www.wyckoffanalytics.com/wyckoff-method/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which four words does the Wyckoff method commonly use to describe market phases?","optionsEn":["Breakout, retest, confirmation, adding","Overbought, oversold, divergence, crossover","Open, intraday, close, after-hours","Accumulation, markup, distribution, markdown"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: accumulation, markup, distribution and markdown are the usual phase names.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: These are trading steps, not market phases.","Wrong: These are indicator-signal terms, not Wyckoff phases.","Wrong: These are trading sessions, not market phases.","Correct: Wyckoff commonly uses accumulation, markup, distribution and markdown."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-207","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[119],"stem":"检查一个XABCD谐波形态，第一步应做什么？","options":["标出X到D五点并量取各段比例","先判断整体更像蝴蝶还是螃蟹","先确认D点成交量是否明显放大","先在D点附近寻找均线的支撑"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：重点是量比例，不是看形状就命名。","optionExplanations":["正确：重点是量比例，不是看形状就命名。","错误：只看形状容易误判，应先量比例。","错误：谐波形态先看比例，不是成交量。","错误：均线不是检查谐波形态的第一步。"],"skills":["步骤","比例"],"references":[{"title":"Harmonic Trader: Gartley history and ratios","url":"https://harmonictrader.com/harmonic-patterns/gartley-pattern/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"When checking an XABCD harmonic pattern, what should you do first?","optionsEn":["Mark the five points X to D and measure each leg's ratio","Decide whether it looks more like a Butterfly or a Crab","Check whether volume expanded sharply at point D","Look for moving-average support near point D"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the key is measuring ratios, not naming it by its shape.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The key is measuring ratios, not naming it by its shape.","Wrong: Judging by shape alone misleads; measure the ratios first.","Wrong: Harmonic patterns start with ratios, not volume.","Wrong: Moving averages are not the first step in checking a harmonic pattern."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-208","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[120],"stem":"市场结构里“上行排列”的定义是？","options":["收盘价持续站在长期均线之上","每个高点和低点都比前一个高","连续出现多根收阳的K线","高点依次降低，低点依次抬高"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：高点、低点都抬高通常叫上行。","optionExplanations":["错误：那是均线判断法，不是市场结构定义。","正确：高点、低点都抬高通常叫上行。","错误：阳线数量不等于高低点排列。","错误：这是收敛形态，不是上行排列。"],"skills":["定义","结构"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In market structure, what is the definition of an \"upward sequence\"?","optionsEn":["The close stays above a long-term average","Each high and each low is higher than the one before","Several up candles appear in a row","Highs get lower while lows get higher"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: rising highs and rising lows are usually called an uptrend.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is a moving-average test, not a market-structure definition.","Correct: Rising highs and rising lows are usually called an uptrend.","Wrong: The number of up candles is not the arrangement of highs and lows.","Wrong: That is a converging pattern, not an upward sequence."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-209","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[121],"stem":"画江恩角度线之前，必须先确定什么？","options":["起点是否选在历史最高价","起点至今经过了多少天","一单位时间对应多少价格","起点是否要落在整数价位"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：先确定一单位时间对应多少价格；比例不同，1×1线完全不同。","optionExplanations":["错误：起点可自由选择，关键是比例。","错误：天数不决定角度线斜率。","正确：先定一单位时间对应多少价格，比例不同1×1线完全不同。","起点不需要是整数价位；关键是先定好一单位时间对应多少价格。"],"skills":["前置设置","比例"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Gann fan drawing tool","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000518151-gann-fan-drawing-tool/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What must you decide before drawing Gann angles?","optionsEn":["Whether the starting point is the all-time high","How many days have passed since the starting point","How much price one unit of time represents","Whether the starting point must be a round number"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: first decide how much price one unit of time equals; with a different scale, the 1×1 line is completely different.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The starting point can be chosen freely; the key is the scale.","Wrong: The number of days does not set the slope of the angles.","Correct: First decide how much price one unit of time equals; with a different scale the 1×1 line is completely different.","Wrong: The start need not be a round number; the key is fixing how much price one unit of time equals."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-96","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[122],"stem":"按常见缠论流程，从原始K线开始，第一步通常做什么？","options":["先画出中枢，再回头确定笔","先找MACD背离，再标记分型","先连最高最低点，再拆分笔","先处理包含关系，再识别分型"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：用固定规则把K线整理成分型、笔、线段和中枢；包含处理在最前。","optionExplanations":["错误：中枢由笔和线段构成，不能先画。","错误：背离是后面的判断，不是整理K线的第一步。","错误：缠论按固定规则逐层整理，不是随意连线。","正确：包含处理在最前，然后才是分型、笔、线段和中枢。"],"skills":["流程","步骤"],"references":[{"title":"缠中说禅原文博客（历史原站）","url":"https://blog.sina.com.cn/u/1215172700"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In the usual Chan theory workflow, starting from raw candles, what is usually done first?","optionsEn":["Draw the pivot zone first, then work back to the strokes","Find MACD divergence first, then mark fractals","Connect the highest and lowest points first, then split into strokes","Handle containment first, then identify fractals"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: fixed rules organise candles into fractals, strokes, segments and pivot zones; containment handling comes first.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Pivot zones are built from strokes and segments and cannot be drawn first.","Wrong: Divergence is a later judgment, not the first step in organising candles.","Wrong: Chan theory organises layer by layer with fixed rules, not by freely connecting points.","Correct: Containment handling comes first, then fractals, strokes, segments and pivot zones."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-210","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[123],"stem":"SMC里常说的“流动性”，通常指什么？","options":["前高前低附近聚集的止损挂单","价格快速穿过、很少来回的区域","成交量明显放大的那几根K线","买卖价差最窄的那段交易时间"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：常把前高前低串成观察流程，但这只是假设。","optionExplanations":["正确：流动性常指前高前低附近的止损和挂单，但只是假设。","错误：那更接近失衡区，不是流动性。","错误：流动性指可能聚集的订单，不是放量K线。","错误：价差是市场深度概念，不是SMC所说的流动性。"],"skills":["术语","假设"],"references":[{"title":"Michael J. Huddleston: ICT official teaching source","url":"https://www.theinnercircletrader.com/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does \"liquidity\" usually mean in SMC?","optionsEn":["Stop and resting orders clustered near prior highs and lows","Areas price moved through quickly and rarely revisited","The candles where volume expanded sharply","The trading period with the narrowest bid–ask spread"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: prior highs and lows are often strung into a watching routine, but this is only a hypothesis.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Liquidity usually means stops and resting orders near prior highs and lows, but it is only a hypothesis.","Wrong: That is closer to an imbalance zone, not liquidity.","Wrong: Liquidity means orders that may cluster, not high-volume candles.","Wrong: Spread is a market-depth concept, not what SMC calls liquidity."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-211","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[124],"stem":"使用ICT方法前，图表上应先设置什么？","options":["先把成交量单位改为美元","先把图表时区设置正确","先把图表周期固定为日线","先把价格轴改成对数坐标"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程注明：先把图表时区设置正确。","optionExplanations":["错误：成交量单位与时间窗口无关。","正确：ICT的时间窗口依赖正确时区。","错误：ICT常用多周期，且时区对日内尤其重要。","错误：坐标类型不是ICT的前置设置。"],"skills":["前置设置","时区"],"references":[{"title":"ICT official home: Michael J. Huddleston","url":"https://www.theinnercircletrader.com/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Before using ICT methods, what should you set on the chart first?","optionsEn":["Change the volume unit to dollars","Set the chart time zone correctly","Fix the chart timeframe to daily","Switch the price axis to log scale"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that you should first set the chart time zone correctly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The volume unit has nothing to do with time windows.","Correct: ICT time windows depend on the correct time zone.","Wrong: ICT often uses several timeframes, and the time zone matters especially intraday.","Wrong: Axis type is not an ICT prerequisite."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-212","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[125],"stem":"DOM（市场深度）面板显示的是什么？","options":["每根K线内主动买入减主动卖出","各价位当天已经累计的成交量","各价位上等待成交的买卖挂单","已经成交的逐笔交易明细记录"],"answer":2,"explanation":"订单簿是还在等待的单。","optionExplanations":["错误：那是Delta，不是DOM。","错误：那是成交量分布，不是挂单。","正确：订单簿显示还在等待的单。","错误：那是成交明细（Time & Sales），不是DOM。"],"skills":["定义","订单簿"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume footprint guide and calculation","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000726164-volume-footprint-charts-a-complete-guide/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the DOM (Depth of Market) panel show?","optionsEn":["Aggressive buying minus aggressive selling within each bar","Volume already traded at each price today","Resting buy and sell orders waiting at each price","A record of each completed trade"],"explanationEn":"The order book shows orders that are still waiting.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is Delta, not DOM.","Wrong: That is a volume profile, not resting orders.","Correct: The order book shows orders that are still waiting.","Wrong: That is Time & Sales, not DOM."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-213","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[126],"stem":"拍卖市场理论里的“价值区”通常指什么？","options":["当天最高价到最低价的全范围","开盘后第一小时形成的价格带","成交量最大的那一个单独价位","约70%成交量集中的价格带"],"answer":3,"explanation":"价值区是成交集中的范围，常取约70%。","optionExplanations":["错误：那是全天区间，不是价值区。","错误：那是开盘区间，不是价值区。","错误：那是控制点（POC），价值区是一段范围。","正确：价值区是成交集中的范围，常取约70%。"],"skills":["术语","接受"],"references":[{"title":"Wiley: Steidlmayer on Markets","url":"https://www.wiley.com/en-us/-p-9780471215561"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In auction market theory, what does the \"value area\" usually mean?","optionsEn":["The full range from the day's high to its low","The price band formed in the first hour after the open","The single price with the most volume","The price band where about 70% of volume concentrated"],"explanationEn":"The value area is the range where trading concentrated, commonly about 70%.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is the full-day range, not the value area.","Wrong: That is the opening range, not the value area.","Wrong: That is the point of control (POC); the value area is a range.","Correct: The value area is the range where trading concentrated, commonly about 70%."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-214","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[127],"stem":"按本课的常见画法，需求区候选的上下沿通常怎样定？","options":["以整理K线最低到最高为界","以第一次回调的最低点为界","以整理区内收盘价均值为界","以整理之后第一次回踩的高点为界"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：把价格曾迅速离开的一小片整理区画出来。","optionExplanations":["正确：把价格曾迅速离开的一小片整理区画出来。","错误：区域来自整理区，不是后来的回调。","错误：均值不能框出整个整理区。","回踩是后来的价格行为；本课的需求区画的是价格迅速离开前那一小片整理区。"],"skills":["画法","区间"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Drawing tools available","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000703396-drawing-tools-available-on-tradingview/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"Under this lesson's common method, how are the upper and lower edges of a demand-zone candidate usually set?","optionsEn":["From the lowest to the highest of the consolidation candles","At the low of the first pullback","At the average close inside the consolidation","At the high of the first retest after the consolidation"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: mark the small consolidation that price left quickly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Mark the small consolidation that price left quickly.","Wrong: The zone comes from the consolidation, not a later pullback.","Wrong: An average cannot frame the whole consolidation.","Wrong: A retest is later price action; the lesson's demand zone frames the small consolidation price left quickly."]},{"id":"method-beginner-128-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[128],"stem":"一根K线开100、收104、高105、低99。按本课口径，它更像哪一种？","options":["趋势K：实体4占波幅6的大部分，收盘靠近高点","十字星：实体很小，开盘与收盘几乎相同","趋势K：只要收盘高于开盘就是趋势K","十字星：只要有上下影线就是十字星"],"answer":0,"explanation":"实体为 104-100=4，波幅为 105-99=6，实体占波幅约三分之二且收盘靠近高点，符合趋势K的口径。","optionExplanations":["正确：实体占波幅大部分且收盘靠近高点。","错误：十字星要求实体很小，这里实体为 4，并不小。","错误：收阳本身不够，趋势K还要看实体占波幅的比例和收盘位置。","错误：有影线不等于十字星，关键是实体是否很小。"],"skills":["K线定义","实体比例"],"references":[{"title":"StockCharts ChartSchool: TA 101 – Part 16","url":"http://chartschool.stockcharts.com/table-of-contents/overview/technical-analysis-101/ta-101-part-16"},{"title":"TradingView Support: 十字星 - 看跌","url":"https://cn.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592727/"}],"stemEn":"A candle opens at 100, closes at 104, with a high of 105 and a low of 99. Under this lesson's definitions, which is it closer to?","optionsEn":["A trend bar: a body of 4 is most of the 6 range, with the close near the high","A doji: the body is tiny and open and close are almost equal","A trend bar: any close above the open makes a trend bar","A doji: any candle with upper and lower wicks is a doji"],"explanationEn":"The body is 104 − 100 = 4 and the range is 105 − 99 = 6; the body is about two-thirds of the range and the close is near the high, which fits the trend-bar definition.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The body is most of the range and the close is near the high.","Wrong: A doji needs a tiny body; here the body is 4, which is not small.","Wrong: Closing up is not enough; a trend bar also depends on body-to-range and close position.","Wrong: Having wicks does not make a doji; the key is whether the body is tiny."]},{"id":"method-beginner-128-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[128],"stem":"一根K线开102、收102.1、高103、低101。按本课口径，它更像哪一种？","options":["趋势K：波幅2说明力量很强","十字星：收盘高于开盘就不是十字星","趋势K：实体小说明趋势很强","十字星：实体0.1远小于波幅2"],"answer":3,"explanation":"实体为 0.1，波幅为 2，实体小于波幅的十分之一，符合本课十字星的参考口径。","optionExplanations":["错误：波幅大不等于趋势K，趋势K看的是实体占比。","错误：十字星允许开盘与收盘非常接近但不完全相等。","错误：实体小与趋势强没有这种对应关系。","正确：实体远小于波幅，符合十字星口径。"],"skills":["K线定义","实体比例"],"references":[{"title":"StockCharts ChartSchool: TA 101 – Part 16","url":"http://chartschool.stockcharts.com/table-of-contents/overview/technical-analysis-101/ta-101-part-16"},{"title":"TradingView Support: 十字星 - 看跌","url":"https://cn.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592727/"}],"stemEn":"A candle opens at 102, closes at 102.1, with a high of 103 and a low of 101. Under this lesson's definitions, which is it closer to?","optionsEn":["A trend bar: a range of 2 shows strong force","Not a doji, because it closed above the open","A trend bar: a small body means a strong trend","A doji: a body of 0.1 is far smaller than the range of 2"],"explanationEn":"The body is 0.1 and the range is 2, so the body is less than a tenth of the range, which fits this lesson's doji reference.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A large range does not make a trend bar; trend bars depend on the body's share.","Wrong: A doji allows the open and close to be very close without being identical.","Wrong: A small body does not correspond to a strong trend.","Correct: The body is far smaller than the range, which fits the doji definition."]},{"id":"method-advanced-128-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[128],"stem":"一段上涨后出现十字星，下一根收盘仍在十字星高低点之间。最稳妥的读法是什么？","options":["说明十字星是反转信号，方向已经确定","说明下一根没有确认，所以十字星不成立","只说明这一段出现犹豫，后续没有方向确认","说明上涨已经结束，方向转为下跌"],"answer":2,"explanation":"十字星只说明当根多空暂时均衡，后续收盘没有走出高低点，就没有方向确认。","optionExplanations":["错误：十字星不等于反转信号，仍需位置和后续确认。","错误：十字星是否成立看当根形状，后续没有确认不改变当根的形状判断。","正确：没有后续确认时，只能读作犹豫。","错误：十字星本身不说明方向已经改变。"],"skills":["读图步骤","失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"StockCharts ChartSchool: TA 101 – Part 16","url":"http://chartschool.stockcharts.com/table-of-contents/overview/technical-analysis-101/ta-101-part-16"},{"title":"TradingView Support: 十字星 - 看跌","url":"https://cn.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592727/"}],"stemEn":"After a rally a doji appears, and the next bar closes still inside the doji's high–low range. What is the most careful reading?","optionsEn":["The doji is a reversal signal and the direction is settled","The next bar did not confirm, so the doji does not count","It only shows hesitation here, with no follow-through on direction","The rally is over and the direction has turned down"],"explanationEn":"A doji only shows a temporary balance on that bar; if later closes do not leave its range, there is no directional confirmation.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A doji is not a reversal signal by itself; it still needs location and follow-through.","Wrong: Whether it is a doji depends on that bar's shape; lack of follow-through does not change the shape.","Correct: Without follow-through, it can only be read as hesitation.","Wrong: A doji by itself does not show that direction has changed."]},{"id":"method-advanced-128-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[128],"stem":"同样一根十字星，出现在强趋势中间和出现在一段上涨末端，读法有何不同？","options":["末端的十字星可以直接当作方向信号，中间的不可以","趋势中间更像暂停，末端更值得观察后续确认","形状相同，所以读法完全相同","趋势中间的十字星更说明反转，末端的更说明延续"],"answer":1,"explanation":"同一形状放在不同位置，参考意义不同；两种情形都仍需后续收盘确认，不能只凭形状下结论。","optionExplanations":["错误：末端十字星也不能只凭形状当作方向信号。","正确：位置改变参考意义，但两种情形都需后续确认。","错误：形状相同不等于读法相同，位置是读图的一部分。","错误：位置与方向的对应关系被说反了，且仍需确认。"],"skills":["读图步骤","位置与确认"],"references":[{"title":"StockCharts ChartSchool: TA 101 – Part 16","url":"http://chartschool.stockcharts.com/table-of-contents/overview/technical-analysis-101/ta-101-part-16"},{"title":"TradingView Support: 十字星 - 看跌","url":"https://cn.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000592727/"}],"stemEn":"How does reading the same doji differ when it appears in the middle of a strong trend versus at the end of a rally?","optionsEn":["At the end it can be used directly as a direction signal; in the middle it cannot","In mid-trend it looks more like a pause; at the end it deserves watching for confirmation","The shape is the same, so the reading is identical","In mid-trend it signals reversal more; at the end it signals continuation more"],"explanationEn":"The same shape in different places carries different weight; both cases still need later closes to confirm, so the shape alone settles nothing.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A doji at the end of a rally also cannot be a direction signal on shape alone.","Correct: Location changes the weight, but both cases need follow-through.","Wrong: The same shape does not mean the same reading; location is part of reading the chart.","Wrong: This reverses how location relates to direction, and confirmation is still needed."]},{"id":"method-beginner-129-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[129],"stem":"前一根K线最高105、最低100。下一根最高104、最低101、收盘103。按本课定义，下一根属于什么？","options":["内包线：最高低于前高、最低高于前低","外包线：它的实体比前一根更长","内包线：只要收盘价在前一根范围内即可","不是内包线：它收阳而前一根收阴"],"answer":0,"explanation":"104 < 105 且 101 > 100，整根高低都在前一根之内，符合内包线定义。","optionExplanations":["正确：高低点都在前一根范围内。","错误：外包线比的是高低点是否同时超出，不是实体长短。","错误：只看收盘价不够，定义要求整根高低都在内侧。","错误：阴阳不影响是否为内包线。"],"skills":["K线定义","高低点比较"],"references":[{"title":"内包线、外包线与 ioi 怎么读","url":"https://www.xtradingtime.com/articles/inside-outside-bar-ioi/"},{"title":"EC Markets: 内包线详解：如何识别这一K线形态","url":"https://www.ecmarkets.com/zh/insights/inside-bar-explained/"}],"stemEn":"The previous bar has a high of 105 and a low of 100. The next bar has a high of 104, a low of 101 and a close of 103. Under this lesson's definition, what is the next bar?","optionsEn":["An inside bar: lower high and higher low than the prior bar","An outside bar: its body is longer than the prior bar's","An inside bar: it only needs to close within the prior bar's range","Not an inside bar: it closed up while the prior bar closed down"],"explanationEn":"104 < 105 and 101 > 100, so the whole bar sits within the prior bar, which fits the inside-bar definition.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Both the high and the low are within the prior bar's range.","Wrong: An outside bar is about exceeding both the high and the low, not body length.","Wrong: The close alone is not enough; the definition needs the whole high–low inside.","Wrong: Candle colour does not affect whether it is an inside bar."]},{"id":"method-beginner-129-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[129],"stem":"前一根K线最高105、最低100。下一根最高106、最低99。按本课定义，下一根属于什么？","options":["内包线：它的实体更小","外包线：只要收盘价超出前一根范围即可","内包线：最高与最低各破一头也算内包","外包线：最高高于前高、最低低于前低"],"answer":3,"explanation":"106 > 105 且 99 < 100，两头都超出前一根，符合外包线定义。","optionExplanations":["错误：实体大小不是外包线的判断标准。","错误：只看收盘价不够，定义要求高低点两头都超出。","错误：各破一头的是方向K线，不是内包线。","正确：两头都超出前一根。"],"skills":["K线定义","高低点比较"],"references":[{"title":"内包线、外包线与 ioi 怎么读","url":"https://www.xtradingtime.com/articles/inside-outside-bar-ioi/"},{"title":"EC Markets: 内包线详解：如何识别这一K线形态","url":"https://www.ecmarkets.com/zh/insights/inside-bar-explained/"}],"stemEn":"The previous bar has a high of 105 and a low of 100. The next bar has a high of 106 and a low of 99. Under this lesson's definition, what is the next bar?","optionsEn":["An inside bar: its body is smaller","An outside bar: it only needs to close outside the prior range","An inside bar: breaking one end each still counts","An outside bar: higher high and lower low than the prior bar"],"explanationEn":"106 > 105 and 99 < 100, so both ends exceed the prior bar, which fits the outside-bar definition.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Body size is not the test for an outside bar.","Wrong: The close alone is not enough; the definition needs both ends exceeded.","Wrong: Breaking one end is a directional bar, not an inside bar.","Correct: Both ends exceed the prior bar."]},{"id":"method-advanced-129-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[129],"stem":"母线高105、低100，内包线高103、低101。后续收盘先升破105又回到103。按本课读法，最稳妥的判断是什么？","options":["内包线本身已经给出方向，升破只是确认","回到区间内说明内包线变成外包线","走出母线高点后又回到区间内，方向确认不再成立，需重新观察","先升破105就说明方向已经确定，回到区间内不影响"],"answer":2,"explanation":"方向确认要求后续收盘走出并守住观察的一端，回到区间内就按失效处理。","optionExplanations":["错误：内包线本身不带方向，方向要等后续走出。","错误：回到区间内不改变前面两根的高低点关系，内包线不会因此变成外包线。","正确：回到区间内，确认不再成立。","错误：一次升破后又回落，不能只取第一次升破作结论。"],"skills":["读图步骤","失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"内包线、外包线与 ioi 怎么读","url":"https://www.xtradingtime.com/articles/inside-outside-bar-ioi/"},{"title":"EC Markets: 内包线详解：如何识别这一K线形态","url":"https://www.ecmarkets.com/zh/insights/inside-bar-explained/"}],"stemEn":"The mother bar has a high of 105 and a low of 100; the inside bar has a high of 103 and a low of 101. A later close first breaks above 105, then falls back to 103. Under this lesson's reading, what is the most careful judgment?","optionsEn":["The inside bar already gave the direction; the break was just confirmation","Falling back into the range turns the inside bar into an outside bar","It left the mother bar's high and returned, so confirmation no longer holds; watch again","Breaking 105 first settled the direction; returning to the range doesn't matter"],"explanationEn":"Directional confirmation needs later closes to leave and hold one end; returning into the range counts as a failure.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: An inside bar carries no direction by itself; direction waits for a later break.","Wrong: Returning into the range does not change the first two bars' high–low relation, so it does not become an outside bar.","Correct: Back inside the range, the confirmation no longer holds.","Wrong: After breaking out and falling back, you cannot rely only on the first break."]},{"id":"method-advanced-129-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[129],"stem":"后一根K线的实体被前一根的实体包住，但它的上影线超出了前一根的最高价。它是内包线还是孕线？","options":["是内包线，因为实体被包住就够了","按实体看是孕线，按整根高低点看不是内包线","既是孕线也是内包线，两者没有区别","不是孕线，因为影线超出了前一根"],"answer":1,"explanation":"孕线比实体，内包线比整根高低点；影线超出前高，就不符合本课内包线的严格口径。","optionExplanations":["错误：内包线要求整根高低点都在内侧，实体被包住不够。","正确：两套标准不同，要分开判断。","错误：孕线与内包线的判断标准不同，不能混用。","错误：孕线只看实体，影线超出不改变孕线的实体关系。"],"skills":["相近概念区别","高低点比较"],"references":[{"title":"内包线、外包线与 ioi 怎么读","url":"https://www.xtradingtime.com/articles/inside-outside-bar-ioi/"},{"title":"EC Markets: 内包线详解：如何识别这一K线形态","url":"https://www.ecmarkets.com/zh/insights/inside-bar-explained/"}],"stemEn":"A bar's body is engulfed by the previous bar's body, but its upper wick goes above the previous high. Is it an inside bar or a harami?","optionsEn":["An inside bar, because an engulfed body is enough","By body it is a harami; by the whole high–low it is not an inside bar","Both a harami and an inside bar; there is no difference","Not a harami, because the wick exceeds the previous bar"],"explanationEn":"A harami compares bodies; an inside bar compares the whole high–low. A wick above the prior high fails this lesson's strict inside-bar definition.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: An inside bar needs the whole high–low inside; an engulfed body is not enough.","Correct: The two definitions differ and must be judged separately.","Wrong: Harami and inside bar use different tests and cannot be mixed up.","Wrong: A harami looks only at bodies; a wick outside does not change the body relation."]},{"id":"method-beginner-130-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[130],"stem":"一根K线开100、收100.4、高100.6、低97.0。按本课口径，它更像哪一种？","options":["看涨 Pin Bar：下影线远长于实体，上影线很短","看跌 Pin Bar：上影线很长，实体靠近下端","普通K线：影线长短不影响这根K线的分类","锤子线：只要下影线够长就算锤子线"],"answer":0,"explanation":"实体为 0.4，下影线为 100-97=3.0，大于实体两倍，上影线为 0.2，很短，实体靠近上端，符合看涨 Pin Bar 形状。","optionExplanations":["正确：主影线、实体与反向影线同时满足形状口径。","错误：长影线在下方，不是上方。","错误：Pin Bar 的判断正是量影线、实体与反向影线。","错误：锤子线还要看位置在下跌之后，本题只给了形状，未给位置。"],"skills":["K线定义","影线比例"],"references":[{"title":"TMGM: Pin Bar K线形态：它是什么以及如何使用？","url":"https://www.tmgm.com/zh-hans/academy/trading-academy/pin-bar-candlestick-pattern"},{"title":"Capital.com: 什么是价格行为交易？","url":"https://capital.com/zh-hans/learn/trading-strategies/price-action-trading"}],"stemEn":"A candle opens at 100, closes at 100.4, with a high of 100.6 and a low of 97.0. Under this lesson's definitions, which is it closer to?","optionsEn":["A bullish pin bar: lower wick far longer than the body, short upper wick","A bearish pin bar: a long upper wick with the body near the bottom","An ordinary candle: wick length does not affect its classification","A hammer: any long enough lower wick is a hammer"],"explanationEn":"The body is 0.4, the lower wick is 100 − 97 = 3.0, more than twice the body, the upper wick is a short 0.2, and the body sits near the top, which fits a bullish pin-bar shape.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The main wick, body and opposite wick all meet the shape definition.","Wrong: The long wick is below, not above.","Wrong: Classifying a pin bar is exactly about measuring the wicks and body.","Wrong: A hammer also depends on appearing after a decline; this question gives only the shape, not the location."]},{"id":"method-beginner-130-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[130],"stem":"一根K线开100、收99.5、高103.0、低99.0。按本课口径，它更像哪一种？","options":["看涨 Pin Bar：下影线很长，实体靠近上端","普通K线：实体小就不能算 Pin Bar","看跌 Pin Bar：收阴就是看跌 Pin Bar","看跌 Pin Bar：上影线远长于实体，下影线较短"],"answer":3,"explanation":"实体为 0.5，上影线为 103-100=3.0，大于实体两倍，下影线为 0.5，实体靠近下端，符合看跌 Pin Bar 形状。","optionExplanations":["错误：长影线在上方，不是下方。","错误：实体小正是 Pin Bar 形状的一部分，不是排除条件。","错误：收阴本身不够，还要量影线与实体比例。","正确：主影线、实体与反向影线同时满足形状口径。"],"skills":["K线定义","影线比例"],"references":[{"title":"TMGM: Pin Bar K线形态：它是什么以及如何使用？","url":"https://www.tmgm.com/zh-hans/academy/trading-academy/pin-bar-candlestick-pattern"},{"title":"Capital.com: 什么是价格行为交易？","url":"https://capital.com/zh-hans/learn/trading-strategies/price-action-trading"}],"stemEn":"A candle opens at 100, closes at 99.5, with a high of 103.0 and a low of 99.0. Under this lesson's definitions, which is it closer to?","optionsEn":["A bullish pin bar: a long lower wick with the body near the top","An ordinary candle: a small body cannot be a pin bar","A bearish pin bar: any down close is a bearish pin bar","A bearish pin bar: upper wick far longer than the body, short lower wick"],"explanationEn":"The body is 0.5, the upper wick is 103 − 100 = 3.0, more than twice the body, the lower wick is 0.5, and the body sits near the bottom, which fits a bearish pin-bar shape.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The long wick is above, not below.","Wrong: A small body is part of the pin-bar shape, not a reason to rule it out.","Wrong: A down close is not enough; you still need to measure wick and body proportions.","Correct: The main wick, body and opposite wick all meet the shape definition."]},{"id":"method-advanced-130-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[130],"stem":"一段下跌后出现看涨 Pin Bar，下一根收盘跌破 Pin Bar 低点。最稳妥的读法是什么？","options":["下一根跌破只是回踩，形状仍然有效","Pin Bar 本身已经给出方向，跌破不影响","形状逻辑不再成立，拒绝没有得到后续确认","跌破低点说明 Pin Bar 变成看跌 Pin Bar"],"answer":2,"explanation":"看涨 Pin Bar 的失效点在影线低点，收盘跌破低点就按失效处理。","optionExplanations":["错误：回踩与跌破失效点是两回事，跌破低点就是失效。","错误：形状需要后续确认，跌破失效点就是确认失败。","正确：失效点被跌破，形状逻辑不再成立。","错误：跌破低点不改变前面那根的形状分类。"],"skills":["读图步骤","失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"TMGM: Pin Bar K线形态：它是什么以及如何使用？","url":"https://www.tmgm.com/zh-hans/academy/trading-academy/pin-bar-candlestick-pattern"},{"title":"Capital.com: 什么是价格行为交易？","url":"https://capital.com/zh-hans/learn/trading-strategies/price-action-trading"}],"stemEn":"After a decline a bullish pin bar appears, and the next bar closes below the pin bar's low. What is the most careful reading?","optionsEn":["The break is just a retest; the shape is still valid","The pin bar already gave the direction, so the break doesn't matter","The shape's logic no longer holds; the rejection was not confirmed","Breaking the low turns it into a bearish pin bar"],"explanationEn":"A bullish pin bar's invalidation point is the wick low; a close below it counts as a failure.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A retest and breaking the invalidation point are different; closing below the low is a failure.","Wrong: The shape needs follow-through, and breaking the invalidation point is a failed confirmation.","Correct: The invalidation point was broken, so the shape's logic no longer holds.","Wrong: Breaking the low does not change how the earlier bar's shape is classified."]},{"id":"method-advanced-130-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[130],"stem":"同样一根长下影线，出现在区间中间和出现在一段下跌后的关键价位附近，参考价值有何不同？","options":["关键价位附近的长影线可以直接当作方向信号","位置不同，参考价值不同；区间中间的长影线参考价值较低","形状相同，所以参考价值完全相同","区间中间的长影线更说明反转，关键价位附近的更说明延续"],"answer":1,"explanation":"Pin Bar 的参考价值来自形状加位置，区间中间的长影线缺乏位置背景，参考价值较低，两种情形都仍需后续确认。","optionExplanations":["错误：关键价位附近的形状也不能只凭形状当作方向信号。","正确：位置是判断的一部分，两种情形都需后续确认。","错误：形状相同不等于参考价值相同。","错误：位置与参考价值的关系被说反了。"],"skills":["读图步骤","位置与确认"],"references":[{"title":"TMGM: Pin Bar K线形态：它是什么以及如何使用？","url":"https://www.tmgm.com/zh-hans/academy/trading-academy/pin-bar-candlestick-pattern"},{"title":"Capital.com: 什么是价格行为交易？","url":"https://capital.com/zh-hans/learn/trading-strategies/price-action-trading"}],"stemEn":"How does the value of the same long lower wick differ when it appears mid-range versus near a key level after a decline?","optionsEn":["Near a key level, the long wick can be used directly as a direction signal","Location changes its value; a long wick mid-range is worth less","The shape is the same, so its value is identical","Mid-range it signals reversal more; near a key level it signals continuation more"],"explanationEn":"A pin bar's value comes from shape plus location; a long wick mid-range lacks that context and is worth less, and both cases still need follow-through.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Near a key level the shape alone still cannot be a direction signal.","Correct: Location is part of the judgment, and both cases need follow-through.","Wrong: The same shape does not mean the same value.","Wrong: This reverses how location relates to value."]},{"id":"method-beginner-131-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[131],"stem":"区间最高价是 50.0。一根K线最高到 50.8，收盘 49.7。按本课定义，它算不算向上突破？","options":["算：最高价已经越过 50.0","不算：只有影线越过，收盘仍在区间内","算：只要盘中碰过就成立","不算：因为它是一根阴线"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本课以收盘价越过边界作为突破，49.7 仍低于 50.0。","optionExplanations":["最高价越过只是影线刺破，不是收盘越过。","正确：收盘 49.7 没有越过 50.0。","盘中碰到不等于收盘站上。","阴阳不是判断依据，关键是收盘位置。"],"skills":["突破定义","收盘确认"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Breakout","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/breakout.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Breakout (technical analysis)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breakout_(technical_analysis)"}],"stemEn":"The range high is 50.0. A bar trades up to 50.8 but closes at 49.7. Under this lesson’s definition, is it an upside breakout?","optionsEn":["Yes: the high exceeded 50.0","No: only the wick went beyond; the close is inside the range","Yes: touching the level intrabar is enough","No: because it is a bearish candle"],"explanationEn":"This lesson requires a close beyond the boundary; 49.7 is still below 50.0.","optionExplanationsEn":["A high beyond the level is only a wick poke, not a close.","Correct: the 49.7 close did not clear 50.0.","An intrabar touch is not a close beyond the level.","Candle colour is not the test; the closing price is."]},{"id":"method-beginner-131-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[131],"stem":"区间最高价 20.0。突破K收在 20.5，下一根收在 19.6。按本课定义应怎样描述？","options":["突破仍然有效，回到区间只是正常回踩","还不能下结论，要等第 10 根","这是一次假突破：1 根后收盘回到区间内","这是向下突破，因为跌破了 20.0"],"answer":2,"explanation":"突破后 1–3 根内收盘回到区间内，就是本课定义的假突破。","optionExplanations":["收盘回到区间内已经满足假突破的定义。","定义只看突破后 1–3 根。","正确：19.6 已收回 20.0 以下。","向下突破要收在区间最低价之下，不是上沿之下。"],"skills":["假突破","失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Breakout","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/breakout.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Breakout (technical analysis)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breakout_(technical_analysis)"}],"stemEn":"The range high is 20.0. The breakout bar closes at 20.5 and the next bar closes at 19.6. How should this be described?","optionsEn":["The breakout still holds; returning inside is a normal retest","No conclusion until bar 10","A failed breakout: price closed back inside after one bar","A downside breakout, because it fell below 20.0"],"explanationEn":"A close back inside within 1–3 bars of the breakout is this lesson’s definition of a failed breakout.","optionExplanationsEn":["A close back inside already meets the failed-breakout definition.","The definition only looks at the next 1–3 bars.","Correct: 19.6 is back below 20.0.","A downside breakout needs a close below the range low, not the high."]},{"id":"method-advanced-131-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[131],"stem":"突破K收在区间上沿外，下一根是小十字星，再下一根收在突破K的高点之上。最稳妥的读法是？","options":["十字星说明突破已失败","三根都在区间外，所以价格之后不会再回区间","出现十字星，应该转为看空","突破得到跟随，仍需留意收盘是否回到区间"],"answer":3,"explanation":"收盘持续在区间外并创出新高，是跟随；但后续收盘回到区间内时仍要按失效处理。","optionExplanations":["十字星没有收回区间，不满足失败的定义。","任何形态都可能在之后失效。","没有证据支持转向看空。","正确：有跟随，但确认不是永久的。"],"skills":["跟随K","确认与失效"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Breakout","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/breakout.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Breakout (technical analysis)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breakout_(technical_analysis)"}],"stemEn":"The breakout bar closes above the range; the next bar is a small doji; the bar after closes above the breakout bar’s high. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["The doji shows the breakout has failed","All three bars are outside, so price will not return to the range","Switch to a bearish view because of the doji","The breakout got follow-through; still watch for a close back inside"],"explanationEn":"Closes staying outside and making a new high are follow-through, but a later close back inside would still invalidate it.","optionExplanationsEn":["The doji did not close back inside, so the failure test is not met.","Any pattern can still fail later.","Nothing here supports a bearish switch.","Correct: there is follow-through, but confirmation is never permanent."]},{"id":"method-advanced-131-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[131],"stem":"向上假突破后，价格收回区间并跌到区间中部。下列哪种描述最符合本课？","options":["价格常会转向区间另一端，但只是可能","假突破说明之后会出现大跌趋势","回到区间中部就证明区间已经结束","假突破之后应该等待同方向再突破一次"],"answer":0,"explanation":"假突破常让价格转向区间另一端，但它说明的是可能性，不是结论。","optionExplanations":["正确：描述的是常见倾向，不是保证。","假突破不能推出大趋势。","回到区间中部说明仍在区间里。","本课没有这种等待规则。"],"skills":["假突破后续","概率表述"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Breakout","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/breakout.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Breakout (technical analysis)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breakout_(technical_analysis)"}],"stemEn":"After a failed upside breakout, price closes back inside and drops to the middle of the range. Which description best fits this lesson?","optionsEn":["After a failed breakout price often tests the other side of the range, but that is only a possibility","A failed breakout means a big downtrend is coming","Reaching the middle of the range proves the range is over","After a failed breakout, wait for another breakout in the same direction"],"explanationEn":"A failed breakout often sends price toward the other side of the range, but that is a possibility, not a conclusion.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: it describes a tendency, not a guarantee.","A failed breakout does not imply a large trend.","Being in the middle means price is still in the range.","This lesson has no such rule."]},{"id":"method-beginner-132-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[132],"stem":"上涨中的回调，最高价依次为 52.0、51.6、51.2、51.5。哪一根是 H1？","options":["最高价 51.5 的那根","最高价 51.6 的那根","最高价 51.2 的那根","最高价 52.0 的那根"],"answer":0,"explanation":"51.5 高于前一根的 51.2，是回调中第一次越过前一根最高价。","optionExplanations":["正确：51.5 > 51.2。","51.6 低于前一根 52.0，没有越过。","51.2 仍低于前一根。","52.0 是回调开始前的高点。"],"skills":["H1 计数","最高价比较"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Pullback","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pullback.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Al Brooks","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Brooks"}],"stemEn":"In a pullback within an uptrend, bar highs are 52.0, 51.6, 51.2, 51.5. Which bar is H1?","optionsEn":["The bar with high 51.5","The bar with high 51.6","The bar with high 51.2","The bar with high 52.0"],"explanationEn":"51.5 exceeds the prior bar’s 51.2, the first time a high exceeds the prior high in the pullback.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 51.5 > 51.2.","51.6 is below the prior 52.0.","51.2 is still below the prior bar.","52.0 is the high before the pullback."]},{"id":"method-beginner-132-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[132],"stem":"回调中有一根大阳线，但它的最高价低于前一根最高价。按本课数法，它算 H1 吗？","options":["算，阳线说明买方已经回到市场","不算，只看最高价是否越过前一根","算，实体越大的K线越应该计入","不算，H1 要求是一根阴线"],"answer":1,"explanation":"H1/H2 只比较最高价，与K线颜色和实体大小无关。","optionExplanations":["颜色不是计数依据。","正确：没有越过前高就不计。","实体大小不是计数依据。","H1 没有颜色要求。"],"skills":["H1 计数","常见数错"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Pullback","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pullback.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Al Brooks","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Brooks"}],"stemEn":"A large bullish bar appears in the pullback, but its high is below the prior bar’s high. Under this lesson’s count, is it H1?","optionsEn":["Yes, a bullish bar means buyers are back","No, H1 only checks whether the high exceeds the prior bar’s high","Yes, larger bodies always count","No, H1 has to be a bearish bar"],"explanationEn":"H1/H2 only compare highs, regardless of colour or body size.","optionExplanationsEn":["Colour is not part of the count.","Correct: no higher high, no count.","Body size is not part of the count.","H1 has no colour requirement."]},{"id":"method-advanced-132-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[132],"stem":"H2 出现后，价格跌破了这段回调的最低点。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["H2 依然有效，只是需要更多时间","改记为 H3，继续沿用原来的判断","这次计数失效，重新观察是否已不是单纯回调","说明下跌趋势已经确立"],"answer":2,"explanation":"跌破回调低点意味着原先“回调即将结束”的读法失效，需要重新判断结构。","optionExplanations":["失效条件已经出现。","直接改名并沿用原判断，忽视了失效。","正确：计数失效，重新观察。","跌破一次低点不足以确立下跌趋势。"],"skills":["失效条件","计数重置"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Pullback","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pullback.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Al Brooks","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Brooks"}],"stemEn":"After H2, price breaks below the low of the pullback. How should this be handled?","optionsEn":["H2 is still valid and just needs time","Relabel it H3 and keep the original view","The count has failed; reassess whether this is still a simple pullback","It proves a downtrend has begun"],"explanationEn":"A break of the pullback low invalidates the “pullback is ending” reading, so the structure must be reassessed.","optionExplanationsEn":["The invalidation condition has occurred.","Relabelling while keeping the view ignores the invalidation.","Correct: the count has failed; reassess.","One broken low is not enough to establish a downtrend."]},{"id":"method-advanced-132-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[132],"stem":"为什么不少价格行为教材更重视 H2 而不是 H1？","options":["H2 的成交量总是比 H1 大","H1 在任何趋势里都会失败","H2 是交易所认可的信号","回调常分两段，第二次更可能在末端"],"answer":3,"explanation":"两段式回调很常见，H1 经常只是第一段的反弹，H2 更可能出现在回调结束处，但仍可能失败。","optionExplanations":["成交量没有这种固定关系。","H1 也可能有效，只是较常被卖回。","这是教学计数法，不是官方信号。","正确：基于回调的两段结构。"],"skills":["两段式回调","H1 与 H2"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Pullback","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pullback.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Al Brooks","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Brooks"}],"stemEn":"Why do many price-action texts emphasise H2 more than H1?","optionsEn":["H2 always has more volume than H1","H1 fails in every trend","H2 is an exchange-recognised signal","Pullbacks often finish in two legs, so the second break is more likely near the end"],"explanationEn":"Two-legged pullbacks are common; H1 is often just a bounce within the first leg, while H2 is more likely near the end, though it can still fail.","optionExplanationsEn":["Volume has no such fixed relation.","H1 can work too; it is just sold more often.","It is a teaching count, not an official signal.","Correct: it follows from the two-legged structure."]},{"id":"method-beginner-133-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[133],"stem":"三个高点依次是 60、62、63。每一推比前一推多出多少？推进是在加强还是减弱？","options":["多出 2 和 1，推进在加强","多出 2 和 3，推进在加强","无法判断，还需要先看成交量","多出 2 和 1，推进在减弱"],"answer":3,"explanation":"62−60=2，63−62=1，增幅缩小，符合三推的减弱特征。","optionExplanations":["增幅缩小是减弱，不是加强。","第二次只多出 1，不是 3。","高点差就能看推进力度，成交量只是补充。","正确：增幅从 2 缩到 1。"],"skills":["三推识别","推进幅度"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Wedge","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/wedge.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Wedge pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedge_pattern"}],"stemEn":"Three highs are 60, 62 and 63. How much does each push add, and is momentum strengthening or weakening?","optionsEn":["They add 2 then 1; momentum is strengthening","They add 2 then 3; momentum is strengthening","Cannot tell without volume","They add 2 then 1; momentum is weakening"],"explanationEn":"62−60=2 and 63−62=1: the gains shrink, matching the fading pattern of three pushes.","optionExplanationsEn":["A shrinking gain is weakening, not strengthening.","The second push adds only 1, not 3.","The high-to-high distance shows momentum; volume is only a supplement.","Correct: the gain shrinks from 2 to 1."]},{"id":"method-beginner-133-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[133],"stem":"看到第三个更高的高点、但价格还没有跌破第三推前的低点。按本课应怎样描述？","options":["三推形状出现，但还没有确认","反转已经得到了确认","三推已经宣告失败了","应该改画成头肩顶形态"],"answer":0,"explanation":"确认条件是收盘跌破第三推前的摆动低点，目前尚未发生。","optionExplanations":["正确：只有形状，还没确认。","确认条件还没满足。","也没有出现失效条件。","没有理由改画成别的形态。"],"skills":["确认条件","三推"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Wedge","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/wedge.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Wedge pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedge_pattern"}],"stemEn":"A third, higher high appears, but price has not broken the low before the third push. How should it be described?","optionsEn":["The three-push shape is there but not confirmed","The reversal is confirmed","The three pushes have failed","It should be redrawn as a head and shoulders"],"explanationEn":"Confirmation needs a close below the swing low before the third push, which has not happened.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: shape only, no confirmation.","The confirmation condition is not met yet.","No invalidation has occurred either.","There is no reason to relabel it."]},{"id":"method-advanced-133-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[133],"stem":"第三推之后价格回落，但没跌破确认线，随后又以大阳线创出更高的高点并收在其上。最合理的读法是？","options":["这是第四推，楔形更强了","三推形态失效，上涨趋势仍在延续","说明之后的反转会更猛烈","要等第五推才能判断"],"answer":1,"explanation":"没有跌破确认线、又创新高站稳，正是本课写的失效情形。","optionExplanations":["推进再次加强，不能说楔形更强。","正确：失效，趋势延续。","没有依据推出更猛的反转。","本课没有等第五推的规则。"],"skills":["失效条件","趋势延续"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Wedge","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/wedge.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Wedge pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedge_pattern"}],"stemEn":"After the third push price dips but holds the confirmation line, then a large bullish bar makes and closes above a higher high. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["A fourth push makes the wedge stronger","The three-push pattern has failed; the uptrend is continuing","The eventual reversal will be sharper","Wait for a fifth push to decide"],"explanationEn":"Holding the confirmation line and then making a higher high that holds is exactly this lesson’s invalidation case.","optionExplanationsEn":["Momentum re-accelerated, so the wedge is not stronger.","Correct: invalidated; the trend continues.","Nothing supports a sharper reversal.","This lesson has no fifth-push rule."]},{"id":"method-advanced-133-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[133],"stem":"下跌中出现三个逐次降低的低点，每次只多跌一点。它与上涨中的三推相比，读法有何不同？","options":["下跌三推不需要任何价格确认","下跌三推只要成交量放大就确认","镜像读法：收盘越过第三推前的高点才确认","三推只出现在上涨中，下跌里没有"],"answer":2,"explanation":"下跌三推是镜像：推进减弱后，收盘越过第三推前的摆动高点才确认。","optionExplanations":["两个方向都需要确认。","成交量不能代替价格确认。","正确：镜像关系。","三推在两个方向都存在。"],"skills":["镜像读法","确认"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Wedge","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/wedge.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Wedge pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedge_pattern"}],"stemEn":"In a decline, three successively lower lows each extend only slightly further. How does reading this differ from three pushes up?","optionsEn":["Downside three pushes need no confirmation","Downside three pushes confirm whenever volume rises","Opposite direction, same logic: confirmation needs a close above the swing high before the third push","Three pushes do not exist in declines"],"explanationEn":"Downside three pushes are the mirror image: after momentum fades, a close above the swing high before the third push confirms.","optionExplanationsEn":["Both directions need confirmation.","Volume cannot replace price confirmation.","Correct: a mirror image.","Three pushes occur in both directions."]},{"id":"method-beginner-134-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[134],"stem":"价格三次在 45 附近回落、两次在 41 附近反弹，收盘都在 41–45 之间。最合适的描述是？","options":["上涨趋势","下跌趋势","交易区间","已经突破"],"answer":2,"explanation":"上下沿都多次触及，收盘没有越过边界，符合交易区间的口径。","optionExplanations":["高点没有持续抬高。","低点没有持续降低。","正确：多次触及两端且收盘在内。","收盘没有越过边界。"],"skills":["区间识别","边界"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Trading Range","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tradingrange.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Range-Bound Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rangeboundtrading.asp"}],"stemEn":"Price falls back from about 45 three times and bounces from about 41 twice, with every close between 41 and 45. What is the best description?","optionsEn":["An uptrend","A downtrend","A trading range","Already broken out"],"explanationEn":"Both edges are touched repeatedly and no close goes beyond them, matching the range definition.","optionExplanationsEn":["Highs are not rising persistently.","Lows are not falling persistently.","Correct: repeated touches at both ends, closes inside.","No close beyond a boundary."]},{"id":"method-beginner-134-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[134],"stem":"在区间里，价格位于上下沿正中间。为什么本课说这里最难判断？","options":["中间位置成交量最小","中间位置最容易发生突破","中间位置适合做空","离两端都远，方向最不明确"],"answer":3,"explanation":"区间中部离两条边界都远，没有可参考的掉头位置。","optionExplanations":["成交量与位置没有这种固定关系。","中部突破的说法没有根据。","中部没有方向偏好。","正确：缺少参考位置。"],"skills":["区间中部","位置"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Trading Range","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tradingrange.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Range-Bound Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rangeboundtrading.asp"}],"stemEn":"Inside a range, price is right in the middle. Why does this lesson call it the hardest place to judge?","optionsEn":["Volume is always lowest in the middle","A breakout is certain in the middle","Only short trades work in the middle","It is far from both edges, so direction is least clear"],"explanationEn":"The middle is far from both boundaries, so there is no turning point to refer to.","optionExplanationsEn":["Volume has no such fixed relation to location.","There is no basis for a breakout there.","The middle has no directional bias.","Correct: there is no reference level."]},{"id":"method-advanced-134-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[134],"stem":"区间上沿被一根K线收盘越过，但下一根就收回区间内。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["视为一次失败的突破，仍按区间看待","区间已经结束，进入上涨趋势","区间上沿要上移到新高","改为下跌趋势"],"answer":0,"explanation":"区间结束需要收盘越过并有跟随；收回区间说明跟随不存在。","optionExplanations":["正确：失败突破，仍是区间。","缺少跟随，不能判定结束。","一次刺破不一定改变边界。","没有证据显示转为下跌。"],"skills":["区间结束","跟随"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Trading Range","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tradingrange.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Range-Bound Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rangeboundtrading.asp"}],"stemEn":"A bar closes above the range top, but the next bar closes back inside. How should it be handled?","optionsEn":["Treat it as a failed breakout and keep treating it as a range","The range is over and an uptrend has begun","Move the range top up to the new high","Switch to a downtrend view"],"explanationEn":"A range ends with a close beyond plus follow-through; closing back inside shows there was none.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: a failed breakout; still a range.","Without follow-through it has not ended.","One poke need not move the boundary.","Nothing shows a downtrend."]},{"id":"method-advanced-134-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[134],"stem":"区间持续了很久，下沿被收盘跌破，之后连续三根都收在更低处。按本课最合理的判断是？","options":["持续时间长，所以区间还会延续","已满足结束条件，但仍可能回到区间","跌破下沿后价格不会再回来","要等价格回到上沿才能判断"],"answer":1,"explanation":"收盘越过边界并有跟随，满足区间结束的口径；但任何判断都可能被后续推翻。","optionExplanations":["持续时间不能保证延续。","正确：满足条件，但保留不确定性。","任何突破都可能被收回。","本课没有这种等待规则。"],"skills":["区间结束","不确定性"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Trading Range","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tradingrange.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Range-Bound Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rangeboundtrading.asp"}],"stemEn":"After a long range, a bar closes below the bottom and the next three bars close lower still. What is the most reasonable judgement under this lesson?","optionsEn":["The range must continue because it lasted long","The end-of-range condition is met, though price could still return","Price will never return after breaking the bottom","Wait for price to reach the top before deciding"],"explanationEn":"A close beyond the boundary with follow-through meets the end-of-range test, though any judgement can be overturned later.","optionExplanationsEn":["Duration does not guarantee continuation.","Correct: condition met, uncertainty remains.","Any breakout can be reclaimed.","This lesson has no such rule."]},{"id":"method-beginner-135-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[135],"stem":"A=50，B=56，回调低点 C=53。按本课公式，上涨的等距参考 D 是多少？","options":["56","59","62","65"],"answer":1,"explanation":"D = C + (B − A) = 53 + 6 = 59。","optionExplanations":["56 是 B，不是 D。","正确：53 + 6 = 59。","62 是 B 加 6，起点用错了。","65 把幅度算成了 12。"],"skills":["等距计算"],"references":[{"title":"TrendSpider: What are measured moves","url":"https://trendspider.com/learning-center/what-are-measured-moves-in-technical-analysis/"},{"title":"Brooks Trading Course forum: Measured moves","url":"https://brookstradingcourse.com/support-forum/20-measured-moves"}],"stemEn":"A=50, B=56, pullback low C=53. Using this lesson’s formula, what is the upside measured-move reference D?","optionsEn":["56","59","62","65"],"explanationEn":"D = C + (B − A) = 53 + 6 = 59.","optionExplanationsEn":["56 is B, not D.","Correct: 53 + 6 = 59.","62 adds 6 to B; wrong starting point.","65 doubles the distance to 12."]},{"id":"method-beginner-135-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[135],"stem":"价格走到等距参考位 D 附近。按本课应怎样理解 D？","options":["价格到这里会反转","D 是价格的上限","D 是值得观察的参考位，不是承诺","价格到 D 之前不会回调"],"answer":2,"explanation":"等距位只是参考，价格可能提前掉头，也可能越过。","optionExplanations":["到达 D 不代表会反转。","D 不是上限。","正确：参考而非承诺。","D 不能约束到达前的走势。"],"skills":["参考位","概率表述"],"references":[{"title":"TrendSpider: What are measured moves","url":"https://trendspider.com/learning-center/what-are-measured-moves-in-technical-analysis/"},{"title":"Brooks Trading Course forum: Measured moves","url":"https://brookstradingcourse.com/support-forum/20-measured-moves"}],"stemEn":"Price reaches the measured-move reference D. How should D be understood?","optionsEn":["Price will reverse here","D is a ceiling for price","D is a reference worth watching, not a promise","Price will not pull back before D"],"explanationEn":"The level is only a reference; price can turn early or go beyond it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Reaching D does not imply a reversal.","D is not a ceiling.","Correct: a reference, not a promise.","D says nothing about the path before it."]},{"id":"method-advanced-135-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[135],"stem":"测量完 D 之后，价格跌破了回调低点 C。这次等距测量应怎样处理？","options":["继续有效，只是需要更多时间","把 C 下移到新低重新加幅度，原判断不变","说明价格会更快到达 D","作废：C 被跌破，第二段的起点已不成立"],"answer":3,"explanation":"等距的第二段以 C 为起点，C 被跌破，测量依据就不存在了。","optionExplanations":["起点被破坏，不能继续沿用。","随意挪动起点是在迁就价格。","跌破 C 与更快到达 D 相矛盾。","正确：测量作废。"],"skills":["失效条件","测量起点"],"references":[{"title":"TrendSpider: What are measured moves","url":"https://trendspider.com/learning-center/what-are-measured-moves-in-technical-analysis/"},{"title":"Brooks Trading Course forum: Measured moves","url":"https://brookstradingcourse.com/support-forum/20-measured-moves"}],"stemEn":"After measuring D, price falls below the pullback low C. What happens to the measurement?","optionsEn":["Still valid, just slower","Move C to the new low, add the distance again and keep the view","It means price will reach D faster","Void: with C broken, the second leg’s start no longer holds"],"explanationEn":"The second leg starts at C; once C breaks, the basis for the measurement is gone.","optionExplanationsEn":["The starting point is broken; the measurement cannot stand.","Moving the anchor just bends the rule to fit price.","Breaking C contradicts reaching D faster.","Correct: the measurement is void."]},{"id":"method-advanced-135-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[135],"stem":"两个人量同一段等距：一人用收盘价，一人用最高最低价，得到的 D 差了 0.8。最合理的看法是？","options":["口径不同，应固定一种并把 D 看成区域","两人中有一人算错了","用收盘价测量得到的才是标准答案","差 0.8 说明等距运动无效"],"answer":0,"explanation":"等距的起止取法有多种，结果不同是正常的；固定口径、把参考位看成区域更稳妥。","optionExplanations":["正确：固定口径，看区域。","两种取法都可以自洽。","没有唯一标准取法。","差异来自口径，不能据此否定方法。"],"skills":["测量口径","参考区域"],"references":[{"title":"TrendSpider: What are measured moves","url":"https://trendspider.com/learning-center/what-are-measured-moves-in-technical-analysis/"},{"title":"Brooks Trading Course forum: Measured moves","url":"https://brookstradingcourse.com/support-forum/20-measured-moves"}],"stemEn":"Two people measure the same move, one with closes and one with highs and lows, and their D differs by 0.8. What is the most reasonable view?","optionsEn":["Different anchors give different levels; fix one convention and treat D as a zone","One of them must be wrong","The close-based version is the only standard","A 0.8 gap proves measured moves do not work"],"explanationEn":"There are several anchor conventions, so different results are normal; fixing one and treating the level as a zone is sounder.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: fix a convention and think in zones.","Both conventions can be consistent.","There is no single standard anchor.","The gap comes from conventions, not proof of failure."]},{"id":"method-beginner-136-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[136],"stem":"某根K线处通道线约为 80.0。这根最高 80.6、收盘 79.5。按本课应怎样描述？","options":["超越后回落：最高越过、收盘回到线内","加速：价格冲出了通道","没有超越：收盘在线内就不算","跌破了趋势线"],"answer":0,"explanation":"最高 80.6 越过通道线是超越，收盘 79.5 回到线内是超越后回落。","optionExplanations":["正确：超越后回落。","加速要求收盘持续在线外。","超越看最高价，收盘决定是否回落。","趋势线在低点一侧，这里没有涉及。"],"skills":["超越定义","收盘位置"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Channel","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/channel.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Trend line (technical analysis)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trend_line_(technical_analysis)"}],"stemEn":"The channel line is about 80.0 at a bar. The bar’s high is 80.6 and it closes at 79.5. How should it be described?","optionsEn":["A failed overshoot: the high went beyond but the close returned inside","Acceleration: price broke out of the channel","No overshoot, since it closed inside","A break of the trend line"],"explanationEn":"The 80.6 high beyond the line is an overshoot; the 79.5 close back inside makes it a failed overshoot.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: a failed overshoot.","Acceleration needs closes holding outside.","The overshoot is judged by the high; the close decides whether it failed.","The trend line is on the lows side and is not involved."]},{"id":"method-beginner-136-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[136],"stem":"上升通道的通道线画在哪一侧？","options":["低点一侧，与趋势线重合","高点一侧，与趋势线平行","任意一侧都可以","成交量最大的位置"],"answer":1,"explanation":"上升通道中，趋势线连低点，通道线是它在高点一侧的平行线。","optionExplanations":["低点一侧是趋势线。","正确：高点一侧的平行线。","两侧作用不同，不能互换。","通道线与成交量无关。"],"skills":["通道画法"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Channel","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/channel.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Trend line (technical analysis)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trend_line_(technical_analysis)"}],"stemEn":"On which side is the channel line of a rising channel drawn?","optionsEn":["On the lows side, overlapping the trend line","On the highs side, parallel to the trend line","Either side","At the highest-volume level"],"explanationEn":"In a rising channel the trend line joins the lows, and the channel line is its parallel on the highs side.","optionExplanationsEn":["The lows side holds the trend line.","Correct: the parallel on the highs side.","The two sides play different roles.","The channel line has nothing to do with volume."]},{"id":"method-advanced-136-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[136],"stem":"连续三根K线收盘都在通道线上方，且离线越来越远。最合理的读法是？","options":["超越后回落，推进即将结束","通道没有任何变化","加速：收盘持续在线外并扩大","趋势线已经失效"],"answer":2,"explanation":"持续收在线外并扩大，符合本课对加速的描述。","optionExplanations":["收盘没有回到线内，不是回落。","原通道的斜率已被打破。","正确：加速。","趋势线在下方，并未被跌破。"],"skills":["加速","收盘持续性"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Channel","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/channel.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Trend line (technical analysis)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trend_line_(technical_analysis)"}],"stemEn":"Three bars in a row close above the channel line and move further away from it. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["A failed overshoot; the push is about to end","Nothing about the channel has changed","Acceleration: closes hold outside and widen","The trend line has failed"],"explanationEn":"Closes holding outside and widening match this lesson’s description of acceleration.","optionExplanationsEn":["The closes did not return inside, so it did not fail.","The original channel slope has been exceeded.","Correct: acceleration.","The trend line is below and unbroken."]},{"id":"method-advanced-136-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[136],"stem":"超越后回落出现了，但价格之后一直没有收盘跌破趋势线。按本课应怎样理解？","options":["通道已经随超越结束了","应把趋势线改画到更低的位置","说明之后价格会加速上涨","通道仍在，超越回落只是放慢的线索"],"answer":3,"explanation":"通道结束要看收盘跌破趋势线，仅超越后回落不足以说明通道结束。","optionExplanations":["结束条件还没满足。","随意改画会让判断失去标准。","没有依据推出加速。","正确：线索而非结论。"],"skills":["通道结束条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Channel","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/channel.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Trend line (technical analysis)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trend_line_(technical_analysis)"}],"stemEn":"A failed overshoot occurs, but price never closes below the trend line afterwards. How should this be understood?","optionsEn":["The channel has ended","Redraw the trend line lower","It means acceleration is coming","The channel is still intact; the failed overshoot is only a sign of slowing"],"explanationEn":"A channel ends with a close below the trend line; a failed overshoot alone is not enough.","optionExplanationsEn":["The ending condition is not met.","Redrawing at will removes the standard.","Nothing points to acceleration.","Correct: a clue, not a conclusion."]},{"id":"method-beginner-137-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[137],"stem":"前 20 根平均波幅 0.5。下列哪根上涨K线符合本课“高潮K”的波幅口径？","options":["波幅 0.8","波幅 0.9","波幅 1.0","波幅 1.3"],"answer":3,"explanation":"口径是大于平均波幅的 2 倍，即大于 1.0；只有 1.3 满足。","optionExplanations":["0.8 小于 1.0。","0.9 小于 1.0。","1.0 等于 2 倍，没有超过。","正确：1.3 > 1.0。"],"skills":["波幅比较"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Climax","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/climax.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Exhaustion","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/exhaustion.asp"}],"stemEn":"The average range of the prior 20 bars is 0.5. Which bullish bar meets this lesson’s climax range threshold?","optionsEn":["Range 0.8","Range 0.9","Range 1.0","Range 1.3"],"explanationEn":"The threshold is more than twice the average, i.e. above 1.0; only 1.3 qualifies.","optionExplanationsEn":["0.8 is below 1.0.","0.9 is below 1.0.","1.0 equals twice the average; it does not exceed it.","Correct: 1.3 > 1.0."]},{"id":"method-beginner-137-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[137],"stem":"出现一根放量大阳线后，价格又连续三根收盘创新高。按本课这属于？","options":["加速：趋势还在延续","衰竭：力量用尽了","反转已得到确认","交易区间开始了"],"answer":0,"explanation":"衰竭要看之后不再创新高；继续创新高说明是加速。","optionExplanations":["正确：加速。","继续创新高与衰竭相反。","没有任何反转迹象。","持续创新高不是区间。"],"skills":["衰竭判断"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Climax","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/climax.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Exhaustion","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/exhaustion.asp"}],"stemEn":"After a large high-volume bullish bar, price closes at new highs for three more bars. Under this lesson, this is?","optionsEn":["Acceleration: the trend is continuing","Exhaustion","A confirmed reversal","The start of a range"],"explanationEn":"Exhaustion requires no new highs afterwards; continued new highs mean acceleration.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: acceleration.","New highs are the opposite of exhaustion.","There is no sign of reversal.","Persistent new highs are not a range."]},{"id":"method-advanced-137-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[137],"stem":"高潮K之后价格横盘了 8 根，既没有创新高，也没有跌破高潮K的低点。最稳妥的描述是？","options":["趋势已经确认反转向下","出现衰竭迹象，但未见反转证据","高潮无效，因为没有下跌","横盘说明之后会继续大涨"],"answer":1,"explanation":"没有延续符合衰竭，但反转需要更多证据，例如跌破关键低点。","optionExplanations":["缺少跌破关键低点的证据。","正确：衰竭不等于反转。","衰竭本来就可以表现为横盘。","横盘不能推出大涨。"],"skills":["衰竭与反转","证据层级"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Climax","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/climax.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Exhaustion","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/exhaustion.asp"}],"stemEn":"After the climax bars, price moves sideways for 8 bars, with no new high and no break of the climax bars’ low. What is the most reasonable description?","optionsEn":["The trend has reversed down","Signs of exhaustion, but no evidence yet of a trend reversal","The climax is invalid because there was no drop","The sideways move means a big rally will follow"],"explanationEn":"The lack of continuation fits exhaustion, but a reversal needs more evidence, such as breaking a key low.","optionExplanationsEn":["There is no break of a key low.","Correct: exhaustion is not reversal.","Exhaustion can show up as sideways movement.","Sideways action does not imply a rally."]},{"id":"method-advanced-137-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[137],"stem":"为什么判断高潮时要同时看波幅和成交量，而不是只看K线颜色？","options":["颜色才是唯一可靠的依据","成交量与高潮没有关系","颜色反映不出力度是否异常","K线波幅越小越像高潮"],"answer":2,"explanation":"高潮的特征是异常大的波幅和成交，颜色无法反映“异常”。","optionExplanations":["只看颜色会把普通K线当成高潮。","放量是高潮的常见特征。","正确：颜色不反映异常程度。","高潮的特征是波幅大。"],"skills":["高潮特征","量价"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Climax","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/climax.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Exhaustion","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/exhaustion.asp"}],"stemEn":"Why does identifying a climax use both range and volume rather than candle colour alone?","optionsEn":["Colour is the only reliable evidence","Volume has nothing to do with climaxes","Colour only shows whether the close was above or below the open, not whether the effort was unusual","Smaller ranges look more like climaxes"],"explanationEn":"A climax is defined by unusually large ranges and volume; colour cannot show what is unusual.","optionExplanationsEn":["Colour alone would label ordinary bars as climaxes.","Rising volume is a common climax feature.","Correct: colour does not show how unusual a bar is.","Climaxes have large ranges."]},{"id":"method-beginner-138-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[138],"stem":"前一根最高 30.5，当根最低 31.2、最高 32.0。两根之间是什么？","options":["向下缺口：价格向下跳空","没有缺口：两根是连续的","向上缺口：中间没有成交","孕线：后一根被前一根包住"],"answer":2,"explanation":"当根最低 31.2 高于前一根最高 30.5，中间留下空白，是向上缺口。","optionExplanations":["价格是向上跳的。","两者没有重叠，存在缺口。","正确：向上缺口。","孕线比较的是实体，与缺口无关。"],"skills":["缺口定义"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Gap","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gap.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Breakaway Gap","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/breakawaygap.asp"}],"stemEn":"The prior bar’s high is 30.5; the current bar’s low is 31.2 and high is 32.0. What lies between them?","optionsEn":["A down gap: price jumped lower","No gap: the bars are continuous","An up gap: nothing traded in between","A harami: the second bar sits inside the first"],"explanationEn":"The current low of 31.2 is above the prior high of 30.5, leaving a blank zone: an up gap.","optionExplanationsEn":["Price jumped up, not down.","They do not overlap, so there is a gap.","Correct: an up gap.","A harami compares bodies and is unrelated."]},{"id":"method-beginner-138-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[138],"stem":"为什么在 BTC 的 1 小时K线上很少看到缺口？","options":["加密市场的规则禁止出现缺口","BTC 的价格波动太小，跳不出缺口","交易所会把缺口数据自动删除","连续交易，下一根从上根收盘附近开始"],"answer":3,"explanation":"缺口多来自休市；连续交易时，下一根通常从上一根收盘价开始。","optionExplanations":["没有这样的规定。","波动大小与是否有缺口无关。","交易所不会删除数据。","正确：连续交易。"],"skills":["市场差异"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Gap","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gap.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Breakaway Gap","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/breakawaygap.asp"}],"stemEn":"Why are gaps rare on BTC’s 1-hour chart?","optionsEn":["Crypto markets ban gaps","BTC is not volatile enough","Exchanges delete gaps automatically","Crypto trades continuously, so each bar starts near the prior close"],"explanationEn":"Gaps mostly come from market closures; with continuous trading, each bar usually opens at the prior close.","optionExplanationsEn":["There is no such rule.","Volatility is not the reason.","Exchanges do not delete data.","Correct: continuous trading."]},{"id":"method-advanced-138-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[138],"stem":"上涨末端出现向上缺口，两天后价格就回到缺口区间内并继续下跌。事后看，它更像哪种缺口？","options":["衰竭缺口","突破缺口","持续缺口","普通缺口与位置无关"],"answer":0,"explanation":"出现在趋势末端、很快被回补并反向，符合衰竭缺口的描述。","optionExplanations":["正确：末端且很快回补。","突破缺口出现在区间突破处，通常不很快回补。","持续缺口出现在趋势中途。","本课按位置和后续区分缺口。"],"skills":["缺口分类","事后确认"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Gap","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gap.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Breakaway Gap","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/breakawaygap.asp"}],"stemEn":"Near the end of a rally an up gap appears; two days later price trades back into it and keeps falling. In hindsight, which type is it most like?","optionsEn":["Exhaustion gap","Breakaway gap","Runaway gap","A common gap, regardless of location"],"explanationEn":"Appearing at the end of a trend and being filled quickly before a reversal fits the exhaustion gap.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: at the end and quickly filled.","Breakaway gaps come at range breakouts and usually do not fill quickly.","Runaway gaps come mid-trend.","This lesson classifies gaps by location and what follows."]},{"id":"method-advanced-138-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[138],"stem":"“缺口必补”这句话，按本课应怎样看？","options":["成立，所有缺口最终都会回补","不成立：回补只是一种可能","只在加密市场里成立","只要等得够久就会成立"],"answer":1,"explanation":"回补是常见现象但不是规律，突破缺口可能长期不回补。","optionExplanations":["不是所有缺口都会回补。","正确：回补只是可能。","加密K线几乎没有缺口。","等待时间不能保证回补。"],"skills":["常见误解"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Gap","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gap.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Breakaway Gap","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/breakawaygap.asp"}],"stemEn":"How does this lesson view the saying “gaps always get filled”?","optionsEn":["True: every gap is filled eventually","Not true: many breakaway gaps stay open; filling is only a possibility","True only in crypto","True as long as you wait long enough"],"explanationEn":"Filling is common but not a law; breakaway gaps may stay open for a long time.","optionExplanationsEn":["Not every gap fills.","Correct: filling is only a possibility.","Crypto bars rarely gap at all.","Waiting longer guarantees nothing."]},{"id":"method-beginner-139-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[139],"stem":"按本课常用的 4–6 倍比例，下列哪组周期最合适？","options":["1 分钟配日线","1 小时配 4 小时","4 小时配 4 小时","5 分钟配月线"],"answer":1,"explanation":"4 小时是 1 小时的 4 倍，落在常用比例内。","optionExplanations":["相差 1440 倍，跨度太大。","正确：4 倍。","同一周期不能互相提供背景。","跨度过大，失去衔接。"],"skills":["周期比例"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Multiple Time Frames","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/07/timeframes.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Dow theory","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dow_theory"}],"stemEn":"Using this lesson’s common 4–6× ratio, which pair of timeframes fits best?","optionsEn":["1-minute with daily","1-hour with 4-hour","4-hour with 4-hour","5-minute with monthly"],"explanationEn":"4 hours is 4× 1 hour, within the common ratio.","optionExplanationsEn":["1,440× apart: far too wide.","Correct: 4×.","The same timeframe cannot give context to itself.","Far too wide to connect."]},{"id":"method-beginner-139-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[139],"stem":"多周期分析中，大周期主要负责什么？","options":["给出精确的入场价格","代替小周期的全部判断","判断背景：趋势方向和关键价位","只用来看成交量"],"answer":2,"explanation":"大周期定背景，小周期看具体位置的表现。","optionExplanations":["精确位置的观察交给小周期。","两个周期分工不同。","正确：背景。","成交量不是大周期的唯一用途。"],"skills":["周期分工"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Multiple Time Frames","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/07/timeframes.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Dow theory","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dow_theory"}],"stemEn":"In multi-timeframe analysis, what is the higher timeframe mainly for?","optionsEn":["Giving exact entry prices","Replacing all lower-timeframe judgement","Setting context: trend direction and key levels","Only reading volume"],"explanationEn":"The higher timeframe sets context; the lower one shows behaviour at specific levels.","optionExplanationsEn":["Precise observation belongs to the lower timeframe.","The two timeframes have different jobs.","Correct: context.","Volume is not its only use."]},{"id":"method-advanced-139-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[139],"stem":"4 小时图上升趋势仍在，1 小时图却连续创出更低的低点。按本课应怎样处理这个冲突？","options":["以 1 小时为准，判定趋势转跌","两个周期都不可信，放弃分析","换成 15 分钟图找支持上涨的信号","以大周期为前提，把它看作回调"],"answer":3,"explanation":"冲突时以大周期背景为前提，小周期的下跌在大周期上往往就是回调。","optionExplanations":["小周期不能单独推翻大周期背景。","冲突是常态，不是放弃的理由。","临时换周期找支持是本课说的错误。","正确：大周期为前提。"],"skills":["周期冲突"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Multiple Time Frames","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/07/timeframes.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Dow theory","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dow_theory"}],"stemEn":"The 4-hour uptrend is intact, but the 1-hour chart keeps making lower lows. How should this conflict be handled?","optionsEn":["Follow the 1-hour chart and call a downtrend","Distrust both and stop","Switch to the 15-minute chart to find bullish signals","Take the higher timeframe as the premise, treat the 1-hour decline as a pullback and watch key levels"],"explanationEn":"In a conflict the higher timeframe is the premise; a lower-timeframe decline is often just a pullback on the higher one.","optionExplanationsEn":["The lower timeframe alone cannot overturn the context.","Conflicts are normal, not a reason to quit.","Switching to find support is the error this lesson warns about.","Correct: the higher timeframe is the premise."]},{"id":"method-advanced-139-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[139],"stem":"大周期的关键支撑被一根大周期K线收盘跌破了。小周期上刚出现的看涨信号应怎样看？","options":["失去背景，需要重新分析","依然有效，小周期信号更及时","信号更强了，因为价格更便宜","改用更小的周期确认"],"answer":0,"explanation":"小周期信号依赖大周期关键价位，价位被收盘跌破，背景就不存在了。","optionExplanations":["正确：重新分析。","背景已被破坏。","便宜不是依据。","更小周期无法恢复大周期背景。"],"skills":["背景失效"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Multiple Time Frames","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/07/timeframes.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Dow theory","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dow_theory"}],"stemEn":"A higher-timeframe bar closes below the key higher-timeframe support. How should a fresh bullish lower-timeframe signal be viewed?","optionsEn":["It has lost its context; reassess","Still valid; lower-timeframe signals are timelier","It is stronger because price is cheaper","Confirm it on an even lower timeframe"],"explanationEn":"The lower-timeframe signal depends on the higher-timeframe level; once that level breaks on a close, the context is gone.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: reassess.","The context has been broken.","Being cheaper is not a reason.","An even lower timeframe cannot restore the context."]},{"id":"method-beginner-140-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[140],"stem":"前一根开 20.0、收 19.4（阴线），当根开 19.4、收 20.3（阳线）。按本课是否构成看涨吞没？","options":["是：阳线实体覆盖了前一根阴线实体","不是：当根开盘等于前收就不算","不是：吞没要求当根是阴线","不是：还要比较两根的成交量"],"answer":0,"explanation":"阳线收盘 20.3 高于阴线开盘 20.0，开盘 19.4 不高于前收，满足定义。","optionExplanations":["正确：20.3 高于 20.0，实体完全覆盖。","本课允许开盘等于前收。","看涨吞没的当根是阳线。","本课定义只比较实体。"],"skills":["吞没定义","实体比较"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Bullish Engulfing Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bullishengulfingpattern.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Bearish Engulfing Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bearishengulfingp.asp"}],"stemEn":"The prior bar opens at 20.0 and closes at 19.4 (bearish); the current bar opens at 19.4 and closes at 20.3 (bullish). Is this a bullish engulfing under this lesson?","optionsEn":["Yes: the bullish body covers the bearish body","No: an open equal to the prior close disqualifies it","No: engulfing requires a bearish current bar","No: volume must be compared first"],"explanationEn":"The 20.3 close is above the 20.0 prior open and the 19.4 open is not above the prior close, so the definition is met.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 20.3 is above 20.0, so the body is fully covered.","This lesson allows an open equal to the prior close.","In a bullish engulfing the current bar is bullish.","This lesson’s definition compares bodies only."]},{"id":"method-beginner-140-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[140],"stem":"同样一根看涨吞没，出现在哪种位置时才谈得上“反转”？","options":["横盘区间的中间","一段下跌之后","一段上涨的中途","任何位置意义都一样"],"answer":1,"explanation":"反转需要先有一段可以被扭转的走势，看涨吞没要在下跌之后才有参考意义。","optionExplanations":["没有趋势可以反转。","正确：有可以被扭转的下跌。","上涨中出现看涨形态谈不上反转。","本课强调位置决定意义。"],"skills":["位置"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Bullish Engulfing Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bullishengulfingpattern.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Bearish Engulfing Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bearishengulfingp.asp"}],"stemEn":"Where must a bullish engulfing appear for it to count as a possible reversal?","optionsEn":["In the middle of a sideways range","After a decline","Midway through a rally","Anywhere; location does not matter"],"explanationEn":"A reversal needs a prior move to reverse; a bullish engulfing matters only after a decline.","optionExplanationsEn":["There is no trend to reverse.","Correct: There is a decline to reverse.","A bullish pattern in a rally reverses nothing.","This lesson stresses that location sets the meaning."]},{"id":"method-advanced-140-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[140],"stem":"看涨吞没出现后，下一根收盘跌破了吞没K的最低价。最合理的读法是？","options":["只是回踩，形态仍然有效","形态变成了看跌吞没","形态失效，看涨的理由不再成立","说明之后会更快上涨"],"answer":2,"explanation":"吞没K的最低价是失效参考，收盘跌破即按失效处理。","optionExplanations":["收盘跌破低点不是回踩。","跌破低点不改变前两根的分类。","正确：失效参考已被收盘跌破。","没有依据支持这个推论。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Bullish Engulfing Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bullishengulfingpattern.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Bearish Engulfing Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bearishengulfingp.asp"}],"stemEn":"After a bullish engulfing, the next bar closes below the engulfing bar’s low. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["Just a retest; the pattern still holds","It has turned into a bearish engulfing","The pattern has failed; the bullish case no longer holds","It means a faster rally is coming"],"explanationEn":"The engulfing bar’s low is the invalidation reference; a close below it invalidates the pattern.","optionExplanationsEn":["A close below the low is not a retest.","Breaking the low does not reclassify the earlier bars.","Correct: The invalidation level has been broken on a close.","Nothing supports that inference."]},{"id":"method-advanced-140-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[140],"stem":"两本教材对同一组K线给出不同结论：一本说是吞没，另一本说不是。最可能的原因是？","options":["其中一本把阴阳弄反了","吞没形态只在日线上成立","成交量没有达到标准","对是否把影线算进去有分歧"],"answer":3,"explanation":"有的口径只比实体，有的要求连影线一起包住，结论会不同。","optionExplanations":["这不是常见的分歧来源。","形态不限周期。","定义里没有成交量门槛。","正确：本课提到影线口径存在分歧。"],"skills":["口径分歧"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Bullish Engulfing Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bullishengulfingpattern.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Bearish Engulfing Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bearishengulfingp.asp"}],"stemEn":"Two textbooks disagree on whether the same two bars form an engulfing pattern. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["One of them mixed up bullish and bearish","Engulfing patterns exist only on daily charts","Volume did not reach a standard","They disagree on whether shadows count"],"explanationEn":"Some conventions compare bodies only while others require shadows to be engulfed too, so conclusions differ.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is not the usual source of disagreement.","The pattern is not limited to one timeframe.","The definition has no volume threshold.","Correct: This lesson notes that the shadow convention differs."]},{"id":"method-beginner-141-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[141],"stem":"开 30.0、收 30.1、高 30.15、低 29.6。下影线是实体的几倍？是否满足本课的形状口径？","options":["2 倍，刚好满足","5 倍，满足","1 倍，不满足","4 倍，满足"],"answer":3,"explanation":"下影线 = 30.0 − 29.6 = 0.4，实体 = 0.1，0.4 是实体的 4 倍；上影线 0.05 也不超过实体。","optionExplanations":["下影线是 30.0−29.6=0.4，不是 0.2。","把高低差 0.55 当成了下影线。","下影线明显长于实体。","正确：下影线 0.4，实体 0.1。"],"skills":["影线比例"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Hammer Candlestick","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/hammer.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Hanging Man","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/hangingman.asp"}],"stemEn":"Open 30.0, close 30.1, high 30.15, low 29.6. How many times the body is the lower shadow, and does it meet this lesson’s shape test?","optionsEn":["2 times; it just qualifies","5 times; it qualifies","1 time; it fails","4 times; it qualifies"],"explanationEn":"Lower shadow = 30.0 − 29.6 = 0.4, body = 0.1, so 4×; the 0.05 upper shadow is no longer than the body.","optionExplanationsEn":["The lower shadow is 30.0−29.6=0.4, not 0.2.","That treats part of the full range as the shadow.","The lower shadow is clearly longer than the body.","Correct: Lower shadow 0.4, body 0.1."]},{"id":"method-beginner-141-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[141],"stem":"同一个“小实体、长下影线”的形状，出现在一段上涨之后，叫什么？","options":["上吊线","锤子线","射击之星","十字星"],"answer":0,"explanation":"名称由位置决定：上涨之后叫上吊线。","optionExplanations":["正确：上涨之后的同形K线叫上吊线。","锤子线出现在下跌之后。","射击之星是长上影线。","十字星要求实体极小，与影线位置无关。"],"skills":["同形异名"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Hammer Candlestick","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/hammer.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Hanging Man","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/hangingman.asp"}],"stemEn":"A bar with a small body and long lower shadow appears after a rise. What is it called?","optionsEn":["Hanging man","Hammer","Shooting star","Doji"],"explanationEn":"The name depends on location: after a rise it is a hanging man.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The same shape after a rise is a hanging man.","A hammer appears after a decline.","A shooting star has a long upper shadow.","A doji needs a tiny body regardless of shadows."]},{"id":"method-advanced-141-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[141],"stem":"锤子线出现后，下一根收盘跌破了锤子线的最低价。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["改称上吊线，因为价格下跌了","锤子线失效，下跌可能继续","锤子线更可靠了","与锤子线无关，不必理会"],"answer":1,"explanation":"锤子线以最低价为失效参考，收盘跌破即失效。","optionExplanations":["名称由出现前的走势决定。","正确：失效参考被收盘跌破。","跌破低点与可靠性提高相矛盾。","这正是锤子线的失效条件。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Hammer Candlestick","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/hammer.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Hanging Man","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/hangingman.asp"}],"stemEn":"After a hammer, the next bar closes below the hammer’s low. How should this be handled?","optionsEn":["Rename it a hanging man because price fell","The hammer has failed; the decline may continue","The hammer is now more reliable","Unrelated to the hammer; ignore it"],"explanationEn":"A hammer’s low is its invalidation reference; a close below it invalidates it.","optionExplanationsEn":["The name depends on the move before it.","Correct: The reference level broke on a close.","Breaking the low contradicts higher reliability.","This is exactly the hammer’s invalidation."]},{"id":"method-advanced-141-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[141],"stem":"为什么本课说锤子线和上吊线“需要下一根确认”？","options":["交易所规定要等两根K线","下一根的颜色决定它叫什么","单根只是拉锯，方向看后续收盘","确认后形态的成功率是百分之百"],"answer":2,"explanation":"单根K线只是一段时间里的拉锯，需要后续收盘说明方向。","optionExplanations":["没有这种规定。","名称由之前的走势决定。","正确：形状本身不说明方向已改变。","确认不代表一定成功。"],"skills":["确认"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Hammer Candlestick","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/hammer.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Hanging Man","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/hangingman.asp"}],"stemEn":"Why does this lesson say hammers and hanging men need the next bar to confirm?","optionsEn":["Exchanges require two bars","The next bar’s colour decides its name","One bar only shows that period’s tug-of-war; direction depends on later closes","Once confirmed it always works"],"explanationEn":"A single bar is one period’s tug-of-war; later closes show direction.","optionExplanationsEn":["There is no such rule.","The name depends on the prior move.","Correct: The shape alone does not show a change of direction.","Confirmation does not guarantee success."]},{"id":"method-beginner-142-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[142],"stem":"开 40.0、收 39.9、高 40.6、低 39.85。上影线是实体的几倍？","options":["7 倍","1.5 倍","6 倍","3 倍"],"answer":2,"explanation":"上影线 = 40.6 − max(40.0, 39.9) = 0.6，实体 0.1，是 6 倍。","optionExplanations":["把 40.6−39.9 当成了上影线。","下影线 0.05 不是这里要量的。","正确：上影线 0.6，实体 0.1。","计算有误，上影线是 0.6。"],"skills":["影线比例"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Shooting Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/shootingstar.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Candlestick pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick_pattern"}],"stemEn":"Open 40.0, close 39.9, high 40.6, low 39.85. How many times the body is the upper shadow?","optionsEn":["7 times","1.5 times","6 times","3 times"],"explanationEn":"Upper shadow = 40.6 − max(40.0, 39.9) = 0.6 and the body is 0.1, so 6×.","optionExplanationsEn":["That uses 40.6−39.9 as the shadow.","The 0.05 lower shadow is not what is measured.","Correct: Upper shadow 0.6, body 0.1.","Miscalculated; the upper shadow is 0.6."]},{"id":"method-beginner-142-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[142],"stem":"长上影小实体的K线出现在一段下跌之后，按本课叫什么？","options":["射击之星","锤子线","上吊线","倒锤子"],"answer":3,"explanation":"名称由位置决定：下跌之后叫倒锤子。","optionExplanations":["射击之星出现在上涨之后。","锤子线是长下影线。","上吊线是长下影线、出现在上涨后。","正确：下跌之后的同形K线叫倒锤子。"],"skills":["同形异名"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Shooting Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/shootingstar.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Candlestick pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick_pattern"}],"stemEn":"A small-bodied bar with a long upper shadow appears after a decline. What is it called here?","optionsEn":["Shooting star","Hammer","Hanging man","Inverted hammer"],"explanationEn":"Location decides the name: after a decline it is an inverted hammer.","optionExplanationsEn":["A shooting star appears after a rise.","A hammer has a long lower shadow.","A hanging man has a long lower shadow and follows a rise.","Correct: The same shape after a decline is an inverted hammer."]},{"id":"method-advanced-142-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[142],"stem":"射击之星出现后，第三根K线收盘越过了射击之星的最高价。最合理的读法是？","options":["看跌读法失效，上涨仍在延续","射击之星变成了倒锤子","说明之后会大跌","射击之星仍然有效，只是来得晚"],"answer":0,"explanation":"射击之星以最高价为失效参考，收盘越过即失效。","optionExplanations":["正确：收盘越过最高价是失效条件。","名称由之前的走势决定，不会改变。","没有依据支持。","失效条件已经出现。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Shooting Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/shootingstar.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Candlestick pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick_pattern"}],"stemEn":"After a shooting star, the third bar closes above the shooting star’s high. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["The bearish reading has failed; the rally continues","The shooting star has become an inverted hammer","It means a big drop is coming","The shooting star still works, just late"],"explanationEn":"The shooting star’s high is its invalidation reference; a close above it invalidates it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A close above the high is the invalidation.","The name comes from the prior move and does not change.","Nothing supports that.","The invalidation has already occurred."]},{"id":"method-advanced-142-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[142],"stem":"为什么倒锤子通常被认为比锤子线需要更强的确认？","options":["它的成交量总是比锤子线小","收在波幅下部，冲高没守住","它只会出现在周线图上","它的颜色总是一根阴线"],"answer":1,"explanation":"倒锤子的收盘在下部，买方的试探没有守住，所以更依赖后续收高确认。","optionExplanations":["成交量没有这种固定关系。","正确：收盘位置偏弱。","形态不限周期。","颜色可阴可阳。"],"skills":["收盘位置"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Shooting Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/shootingstar.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Candlestick pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick_pattern"}],"stemEn":"Why is an inverted hammer usually thought to need stronger confirmation than a hammer?","optionsEn":["Its volume is always lower","It closes in the lower part of its range, so the push higher did not hold","It appears only on weekly charts","It is always bearish"],"explanationEn":"The inverted hammer closes low in its range, so the buyers’ probe did not hold and it relies more on a higher close afterwards.","optionExplanationsEn":["Volume has no such fixed relation.","Correct: Its close is in a weak position.","The pattern is not limited to one timeframe.","It can be either colour."]},{"id":"method-beginner-143-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[143],"stem":"开 25.00、收 25.01、高 25.80、低 24.98。按本课它属于哪种十字星？","options":["蜻蜓十字","墓碑十字","长腿十字","不是十字星"],"answer":1,"explanation":"波幅 0.82，开收距最低价不超过 0.03，在最低 10% 以内，是墓碑十字。","optionExplanations":["蜻蜓十字的开收在波幅顶部。","正确：开收都在波幅最低 10% 以内，上影线长。","这里下影线很短，不是两头都长。","实体 0.01 远小于波幅的 10%。"],"skills":["十字星分类"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Doji","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doji.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Gravestone Doji","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gravestone-doji.asp"}],"stemEn":"Open 25.00, close 25.01, high 25.80, low 24.98. Which doji is it under this lesson?","optionsEn":["Dragonfly doji","Gravestone doji","Long-legged doji","Not a doji"],"explanationEn":"The range is 0.82 and open and close are within 0.03 of the low, inside the bottom 10%: a gravestone.","optionExplanationsEn":["A dragonfly has open and close at the top.","Correct: Open and close sit in the lowest 10% with a long upper shadow.","The lower shadow is short, not long on both sides.","The 0.01 body is far below 10% of the range."]},{"id":"method-beginner-143-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[143],"stem":"实体 0.3、波幅 2.0 的K线，按本课算不算十字星？","options":["算：实体只有 0.3，很小","算：只要有上下影线就是","不算：实体占 15%，超过 10%","无法判断，要看颜色"],"answer":2,"explanation":"0.3 ÷ 2.0 = 15%，大于 10%，不满足定义。","optionExplanations":["要看实体占波幅的比例。","有影线不等于十字星。","正确：0.3 ÷ 2.0 = 15%。","颜色与是否为十字星无关。"],"skills":["实体比例"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Doji","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doji.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Gravestone Doji","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gravestone-doji.asp"}],"stemEn":"A bar has a 0.3 body and a 2.0 range. Is it a doji under this lesson?","optionsEn":["Yes: a 0.3 body is small","Yes: any bar with two shadows is one","No: the body is 15% of the range, above 10%","Cannot tell without the colour"],"explanationEn":"0.3 ÷ 2.0 = 15%, above 10%, so it does not qualify.","optionExplanationsEn":["What matters is the body’s share of the range.","Having shadows does not make a doji.","Correct: 0.3 ÷ 2.0 = 15%.","Colour is irrelevant here."]},{"id":"method-advanced-143-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[143],"stem":"下跌末端出现蜻蜓十字，之后 10 根都在它的高低点之间横盘。最合理的读法是？","options":["蜻蜓十字已确认反转向上","蜻蜓十字说明下跌会加速","应改称墓碑十字","犹豫持续，没有出现方向确认"],"answer":3,"explanation":"十字星只说明犹豫，后续横盘意味着犹豫在延续。","optionExplanations":["没有收盘突破高点。","也没有跌破低点。","分类看开收位置，不看后续。","正确：横盘说明没有确认。"],"skills":["犹豫与确认"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Doji","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doji.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Gravestone Doji","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gravestone-doji.asp"}],"stemEn":"A dragonfly doji appears at the end of a decline, and the next 10 bars move sideways within its high and low. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["The dragonfly has confirmed an upward reversal","The dragonfly means the decline will accelerate","It should be renamed a gravestone","Indecision continues; there is no directional confirmation"],"explanationEn":"A doji only shows indecision; the sideways move means it continues.","optionExplanationsEn":["There is no close above its high.","Its low was not broken either.","Classification depends on open/close location, not what follows.","Correct: The sideways move shows no confirmation."]},{"id":"method-advanced-143-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[143],"stem":"为什么本课不把墓碑十字直接当成卖出信号？","options":["只说明多空打平，方向看后续","墓碑十字只出现在下跌中","墓碑十字的成交量太小","墓碑十字其实是看涨信号"],"answer":0,"explanation":"十字星只说明多空暂时均衡，需要位置和后续收盘配合。","optionExplanations":["正确：十字星本质是犹豫。","可以出现在任何位置。","成交量不是这里的理由。","它也不是看涨信号。"],"skills":["常见误用"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Doji","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doji.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Gravestone Doji","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gravestone-doji.asp"}],"stemEn":"Why does this lesson not treat a gravestone doji as a sell signal?","optionsEn":["It only shows a stand-off; direction depends on location and what follows","Gravestones appear only in declines","Gravestone volume is too small","A gravestone is actually bullish"],"explanationEn":"A doji only shows a temporary balance; location and later closes must support any reading.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A doji is fundamentally indecision.","They can appear anywhere.","Volume is not the reason here.","It is not bullish either."]},{"id":"method-beginner-144-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[144],"stem":"第一根开 50、收 46；第三根阳线收在 47.5。它有没有越过第一根实体的中点？","options":["没有：中点是 48，47.5 低于 48","有：47.5 高于第一根收盘 46","有：中点是 47","无法判断，要看第二根"],"answer":0,"explanation":"第一根实体中点 = (50 + 46) ÷ 2 = 48，47.5 没有越过。","optionExplanations":["正确：(50+46)÷2=48。","要比的是实体中点，不是收盘。","中点算错了。","中点只由第一根决定。"],"skills":["中点计算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Morning Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/morningstar.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Evening Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/eveningstar.asp"}],"stemEn":"Bar 1 opens at 50 and closes at 46; bar 3 is bullish and closes at 47.5. Did it close beyond the midpoint of bar 1’s body?","optionsEn":["No: the midpoint is 48 and 47.5 is below it","Yes: 47.5 is above the 46 close","Yes: the midpoint is 47","Cannot tell without bar 2"],"explanationEn":"Bar 1’s body midpoint = (50 + 46) ÷ 2 = 48; 47.5 does not clear it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: (50+46)÷2=48.","Compare with the midpoint, not the close.","The midpoint is miscalculated.","The midpoint depends only on bar 1."]},{"id":"method-beginner-144-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[144],"stem":"第一根实体 3.0。第二根要成为本课的“星线”，实体最大不能超过多少？","options":["小于 1.5","小于 1.0","小于 3.0","没有限制"],"answer":1,"explanation":"星线实体要小于第一根实体的三分之一：3.0 ÷ 3 = 1.0。","optionExplanations":["那是一半，不是三分之一。","正确：三分之一是 1.0。","这只要求比第一根小。","星线必须是小实体。"],"skills":["星线定义"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Morning Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/morningstar.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Evening Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/eveningstar.asp"}],"stemEn":"Bar 1’s body is 3.0. What is the largest body bar 2 can have to count as a “star” here?","optionsEn":["Less than 1.5","Less than 1.0","Less than 3.0","No limit"],"explanationEn":"The star’s body must be under a third of the first: 3.0 ÷ 3 = 1.0.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is half, not a third.","Correct: A third of 3.0 is 1.0.","That only requires being smaller.","A star must have a small body."]},{"id":"method-advanced-144-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[144],"stem":"早晨之星形成后，价格收盘跌破了三根K线中的最低点。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["形态依然有效，只是回踩","改称黄昏之星","形态失效，下跌可能继续","说明反弹会更强"],"answer":2,"explanation":"三根K线的最低点是早晨之星的失效参考。","optionExplanations":["收盘跌破不是回踩。","黄昏之星出现在上涨之后。","正确：失效参考被收盘跌破。","没有依据。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Morning Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/morningstar.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Evening Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/eveningstar.asp"}],"stemEn":"After a morning star, price closes below the lowest point of the three bars. How should this be handled?","optionsEn":["Still valid; just a retest","Rename it an evening star","The pattern has failed; the decline may continue","The rebound will be stronger"],"explanationEn":"The lowest point of the three bars is the morning star’s invalidation level.","optionExplanationsEn":["A close below it is not a retest.","An evening star follows a rise.","Correct: The invalidation level broke on a close.","There is no basis for that."]},{"id":"method-advanced-144-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[144],"stem":"为什么本课在 24 小时市场里放宽了“星线要有缺口”这一条？","options":["缺口会让形态失败","经典定义本来就不要求缺口","有缺口的K线无法画出来","连续交易几乎没有缺口"],"answer":3,"explanation":"加密市场连续交易，K线之间几乎没有缺口；保留这条会让定义失去实用性。","optionExplanations":["缺口与成败没有这种关系。","经典定义是要求缺口的。","缺口可以正常显示。","正确：缺口来自休市。"],"skills":["市场差异"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Morning Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/morningstar.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Evening Star","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/eveningstar.asp"}],"stemEn":"Why does this lesson drop the gap requirement for the star in 24-hour markets?","optionsEn":["Gaps make the pattern fail","The classical definition never required gaps","Gapped bars cannot be drawn","Continuous markets rarely gap, so the rule would almost never be met"],"explanationEn":"Crypto trades continuously, so bars rarely gap; keeping the rule would make the definition impractical.","optionExplanationsEn":["Gaps have no such effect.","The classical definition does require gaps.","Gaps display normally.","Correct: Gaps come from market closures."]},{"id":"method-beginner-145-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[145],"stem":"三根阳线收盘依次为 10.2、10.6、10.5。是否满足三白兵的收盘条件？","options":["满足：三根都是阳线","满足：总体收盘抬高了","无法判断，要看成交量","不满足：第三根收盘低于第二根"],"answer":3,"explanation":"10.5 低于 10.6，第三根没有收得更高。","optionExplanations":["还要求收盘逐根抬高。","定义要求每一根都高于前一根。","收盘条件只看价格。","正确：10.5 < 10.6。"],"skills":["收盘条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Three White Soldiers","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/three_white_soldiers.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Three Black Crows","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/three_black_crows.asp"}],"stemEn":"Three bullish bars close at 10.2, 10.6 and 10.5. Do they meet the soldiers’ closing condition?","optionsEn":["Yes: all three are bullish","Yes: closes rose overall","Cannot tell without volume","No: the third close is below the second"],"explanationEn":"10.5 is below 10.6, so the third bar did not close higher.","optionExplanationsEn":["Closes must also rise each time.","Each close must exceed the prior one.","The closing condition is price only.","Correct: 10.5 < 10.6."]},{"id":"method-beginner-145-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[145],"stem":"一根阳线高 31.0、低 30.0、收 30.6。它的上影线占波幅多少？是否满足 30% 的口径？","options":["40%，不满足","60%，不满足","30%，刚好满足","10%，满足"],"answer":0,"explanation":"上影线 = 31.0 − 30.6 = 0.4，占波幅 1.0 的 40%，超过 30%。","optionExplanations":["正确：上影线 0.4，波幅 1.0。","把收盘到低点的距离当成了上影线。","上影线是 31.0−30.6=0.4。","计算有误。"],"skills":["影线比例"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Three White Soldiers","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/three_white_soldiers.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Three Black Crows","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/three_black_crows.asp"}],"stemEn":"A bullish bar has high 31.0, low 30.0 and close 30.6. What share of the range is its upper shadow, and does it meet the 30% test?","optionsEn":["40%; it fails","60%; it fails","30%; it just passes","10%; it passes"],"explanationEn":"Upper shadow = 31.0 − 30.6 = 0.4, which is 40% of the 1.0 range, above 30%.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Upper shadow 0.4, range 1.0.","That uses close-to-low as the shadow.","The upper shadow is 31.0−30.6=0.4.","Miscalculated."]},{"id":"method-advanced-145-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[145],"stem":"三白兵出现后价格回撤，但始终没有跌破第一根的开盘价。最合理的读法是？","options":["回撤说明三白兵已经失败","回撤属于正常消化，形态没有失效","之后价格会直线上涨","应该改称三乌鸦"],"answer":1,"explanation":"跌破第一根开盘价才是本课的失效条件，回撤本身是常见现象。","optionExplanations":["回撤不等于失效。","正确：失效参考没有被跌破。","没有依据。","三乌鸦是三根阴线。"],"skills":["过度延伸","失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Three White Soldiers","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/three_white_soldiers.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Three Black Crows","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/three_black_crows.asp"}],"stemEn":"After three white soldiers, price pulls back but never breaks the first bar’s open. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["The pullback means the pattern failed","A normal digestion; the pattern has not failed","Price will then rise in a straight line","It should be renamed three black crows"],"explanationEn":"Breaking the first bar’s open is the invalidation here; a pullback itself is common.","optionExplanationsEn":["A pullback is not invalidation.","Correct: The invalidation level held.","There is no basis for that.","Three crows are bearish bars."]},{"id":"method-advanced-145-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[145],"stem":"在已经连涨很久的位置出现三白兵，为什么本课提醒“过度延伸”？","options":["三白兵只在下跌中有效","连涨之后成交量会不足","离均值已远，常先回撤","三白兵的定义要求先跌"],"answer":2,"explanation":"连续上涨后价格偏离较大，追进去容易碰上回撤。","optionExplanations":["不是只在下跌中出现。","成交量没有固定结论。","正确：这是位置带来的风险。","定义里没有这条。"],"skills":["位置与风险"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Three White Soldiers","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/three_white_soldiers.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Three Black Crows","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/three_black_crows.asp"}],"stemEn":"Why does this lesson warn of overextension when three white soldiers appear after a long rally?","optionsEn":["The pattern works only in declines","Volume is always weak after a run","Price is far from its mean and often pulls back after consecutive big bars","The definition requires a prior drop"],"explanationEn":"After a long run price is stretched, so chasing it often runs into a pullback.","optionExplanationsEn":["It is not limited to declines.","Volume has no fixed conclusion.","Correct: The risk comes from location.","The definition has no such condition."]},{"id":"method-beginner-146-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[146],"stem":"前一根实体 50.0–52.0，后一根开 52.0、收 51.4。后一根实体是否在前一根实体之内？","options":["不在：开盘等于前一根收盘就不算","不在：要看影线是否超出","在：落在前一根实体之内","无法判断，缺少成交量"],"answer":2,"explanation":"后一根实体 51.4–52.0 在 50.0–52.0 之内，且 0.6 小于 2.0 的一半。","optionExplanations":["本课允许与边界相等。","孕线只比较实体。","正确：与边界相等也算。","定义与成交量无关。"],"skills":["实体比较"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Bullish Harami","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bullishharami.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Harami Cross","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/haramicross.asp"}],"stemEn":"The first body spans 50.0–52.0; the second bar opens at 52.0 and closes at 51.4. Is the second body inside the first?","optionsEn":["No: an open equal to the prior close disqualifies it","No: the shadows must be checked","Yes: 51.4–52.0 lies within 50.0–52.0","Cannot tell without volume"],"explanationEn":"The second body 51.4–52.0 lies within 50.0–52.0, and 0.6 is less than half of 2.0.","optionExplanationsEn":["This lesson allows touching the edge.","A harami compares bodies only.","Correct: Touching the edge counts.","The definition does not use volume."]},{"id":"method-beginner-146-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[146],"stem":"孕线和内包线最主要的区别是什么？","options":["孕线只会出现在日线图上","内包线要求两根颜色相反","两者其实完全是一回事","孕线比实体，内包线比整根高低点"],"answer":3,"explanation":"孕线只看实体，内包线连影线一起比较高低点。","optionExplanations":["两者都不限周期。","内包线不看颜色。","比较对象不同。","正确：两者用的价格不同。"],"skills":["相近概念"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Bullish Harami","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bullishharami.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Harami Cross","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/haramicross.asp"}],"stemEn":"What is the main difference between a harami and an inside bar?","optionsEn":["A harami appears only on daily charts","An inside bar requires opposite colours","They are identical","A harami compares bodies; an inside bar compares the full high and low"],"explanationEn":"A harami looks only at bodies; an inside bar compares highs and lows including shadows.","optionExplanationsEn":["Neither is limited to one timeframe.","An inside bar ignores colour.","They compare different things.","Correct: They use different prices."]},{"id":"method-advanced-146-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[146],"stem":"后一根实体在前一根实体内，但上影线越过了前一根最高价。它是孕线、内包线，还是都是？","options":["是孕线，但不是内包线","是内包线，但不是孕线","两者都是","两者都不是"],"answer":0,"explanation":"孕线只比实体，内包线比整根高低点，最高价超出就不是内包线。","optionExplanations":["正确：实体在内满足孕线；最高价超出，不满足内包线。","内包线要求最高价不超出。","内包线条件不满足。","孕线条件是满足的。"],"skills":["相近概念","口径"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Bullish Harami","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bullishharami.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Harami Cross","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/haramicross.asp"}],"stemEn":"The second body sits inside the first body, but its upper shadow exceeds the first bar’s high. Is it a harami, an inside bar, or both?","optionsEn":["A harami but not an inside bar","An inside bar but not a harami","Both","Neither"],"explanationEn":"A harami compares bodies; an inside bar compares the full range, so a higher high rules out the inside bar.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The body test passes; the high test fails.","An inside bar needs the high to stay inside.","The inside-bar condition is not met.","The harami condition is met."]},{"id":"method-advanced-146-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[146],"stem":"看跌孕线出现后，价格收盘越过了前一根实体的上沿。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["孕线变成了看涨孕线","孕线失效，上涨仍在延续","孕线仍然有效，只是需要时间","说明之后会大跌"],"answer":1,"explanation":"收盘越过前一根实体外沿即按失效处理。","optionExplanations":["分类由两根K线本身决定。","正确：这是本课的失效条件。","失效条件已经出现。","没有依据。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Bullish Harami","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bullishharami.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Harami Cross","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/haramicross.asp"}],"stemEn":"After a bearish harami, price closes above the top of the first body. How should this be handled?","optionsEn":["It becomes a bullish harami","The harami has failed; the rally continues","Still valid; it needs time","A big drop is coming"],"explanationEn":"A close beyond the first body’s outer edge invalidates it.","optionExplanationsEn":["The classification depends on the two bars.","Correct: That is this lesson’s invalidation.","The invalidation has occurred.","There is no basis for that."]},{"id":"method-beginner-147-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[147],"stem":"前一根阳线开 40、收 44。后一根阴线收在 42.5。它有没有插入实体中点以下？","options":["有：42.5 低于 44","没有：42.5 高于中点 42","有：中点是 43","无法判断，要看最高价"],"answer":1,"explanation":"中点 = (40 + 44) ÷ 2 = 42，42.5 没有插到中点以下。","optionExplanations":["要比的是中点。","正确：(40+44)÷2=42。","中点算错了。","中点只由实体决定。"],"skills":["中点计算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Dark Cloud Cover","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/darkcloud.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Candlestick pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick_pattern"}],"stemEn":"The prior bullish bar opens at 40 and closes at 44. The next bearish bar closes at 42.5. Did it close below the body midpoint?","optionsEn":["Yes: 42.5 is below 44","No: the midpoint is 42 and 42.5 is above it","Yes: the midpoint is 43","Cannot tell without the high"],"explanationEn":"Midpoint = (40 + 44) ÷ 2 = 42; 42.5 did not cut below it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Compare with the midpoint.","Correct: (40+44)÷2=42.","The midpoint is miscalculated.","The midpoint depends only on the body."]},{"id":"method-beginner-147-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[147],"stem":"乌云盖顶的后一根如果收盘跌破了前一根阳线的开盘价，它更接近哪种形态？","options":["刺透形态","早晨之星","看跌吞没","十字星"],"answer":2,"explanation":"收盘跌破前一根开盘价，阴线实体就完全覆盖了阳线实体，更接近看跌吞没。","optionExplanations":["刺透是看涨的镜像形态。","早晨之星由三根K线组成。","正确：实体已完全覆盖前一根实体。","这根实体很大。"],"skills":["相近概念"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Dark Cloud Cover","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/darkcloud.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Candlestick pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick_pattern"}],"stemEn":"If the second bar of a dark cloud cover closes below the first bar’s open, which pattern is it closer to?","optionsEn":["Piercing pattern","Morning star","Bearish engulfing","Doji"],"explanationEn":"Closing below the prior open means the bearish body covers the bullish body, closer to a bearish engulfing.","optionExplanationsEn":["Piercing is the bullish mirror.","A morning star has three bars.","Correct: The body fully covers the prior body.","This bar has a large body."]},{"id":"method-advanced-147-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[147],"stem":"本课为什么把“后一根高开”改成“后一根最高价越过前一根最高价”？","options":["高开会让形态失败","经典定义从来不要求高开","最高价比开盘价更容易计算","开盘等于前收，几乎不能高开"],"answer":3,"explanation":"加密市场连续交易，开盘就是前收；用“冲过前高”保留了“先强后弱”的含义。","optionExplanations":["两者没有这种关系。","经典定义是要求的。","这不是原因。","正确：原条件在加密市场几乎无法满足。"],"skills":["市场差异"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Dark Cloud Cover","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/darkcloud.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Candlestick pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick_pattern"}],"stemEn":"Why does this lesson replace “the second bar opens higher” with “the second bar’s high exceeds the prior high”?","optionsEn":["Opening higher makes the pattern fail","The classical definition never required a higher open","The high is easier to compute than the open","In 24-hour markets each open equals the prior close, so gap-ups barely happen"],"explanationEn":"Crypto trades continuously, so each open is the prior close; “trading above the prior high” keeps the idea of strength turning to weakness.","optionExplanationsEn":["There is no such link.","The classical definition does.","That is not the reason.","Correct: The original condition is almost never met in crypto."]},{"id":"method-advanced-147-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[147],"stem":"乌云盖顶形成后，第三根收盘越过了第二根的最高价。最合理的读法是？","options":["形态失效，上涨可能继续","形态更可靠了","变成了刺透形态","需要再等三根才能判断"],"answer":0,"explanation":"乌云盖顶以第二根的最高价为失效参考。","optionExplanations":["正确：收盘越过高点是失效条件。","与失效相矛盾。","刺透出现在下跌之后。","失效条件已经出现。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Dark Cloud Cover","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/darkcloud.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Candlestick pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candlestick_pattern"}],"stemEn":"After a dark cloud cover, the third bar closes above the second bar’s high. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["The pattern has failed; the rally may continue","The pattern is now more reliable","It has turned into a piercing pattern","Wait three more bars"],"explanationEn":"The second bar’s high is the dark cloud cover’s invalidation level.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A close above the high is the invalidation.","That contradicts the invalidation.","A piercing pattern follows a decline.","The invalidation has already occurred."]},{"id":"method-beginner-148-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[148],"stem":"左肩 60、头 63、右肩 60.5，颈线 58。参考幅度是多少？跌破后向下量出的参考位在哪？","options":["5，参考位约 53","3，参考位约 55","5，参考位约 63","2，参考位约 56"],"answer":0,"explanation":"参考幅度 = 头部 63 − 颈线 58 = 5，向下量出 58 − 5 = 53，仅作参考。","optionExplanations":["正确：63−58=5，58−5=53。","用了头与肩的差。","方向弄反了。","用了右肩与颈线的差。"],"skills":["等距参考"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Head and Shoulders Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/head-shoulders.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Head and shoulders (chart pattern)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Head_and_shoulders_(chart_pattern)"}],"stemEn":"Left shoulder 60, head 63, right shoulder 60.5, neckline 58. What is the reference distance, and where does it project after a break?","optionsEn":["5; the reference is about 53","3; about 55","5; about 63","2; about 56"],"explanationEn":"Reference distance = 63 − 58 = 5, projected down to 58 − 5 = 53, as a reference only.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 63−58=5 and 58−5=53.","That uses head minus shoulder.","The direction is reversed.","That uses the right shoulder."]},{"id":"method-beginner-148-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[148],"stem":"左肩、头、右肩都已出现，但价格还没有收盘跌破颈线。按本课应怎样称呼？","options":["已经完成的头肩顶","可能的头肩顶，尚未完成","失败的头肩顶","双顶"],"answer":1,"explanation":"只有收盘跌破颈线才算完成，之前只是可能。","optionExplanations":["缺少颈线跌破。","正确：完成需要收盘跌破颈线。","也没有出现失效。","这里有三个高点。"],"skills":["确认条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Head and Shoulders Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/head-shoulders.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Head and shoulders (chart pattern)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Head_and_shoulders_(chart_pattern)"}],"stemEn":"The left shoulder, head and right shoulder are all there, but price has not closed below the neckline. What should it be called?","optionsEn":["A completed head and shoulders","A possible head and shoulders, not yet complete","A failed head and shoulders","A double top"],"explanationEn":"Only a close below the neckline completes it; before that it is a possibility.","optionExplanationsEn":["The neckline break is missing.","Correct: Completion needs a close below the neckline.","No invalidation has occurred either.","There are three highs here."]},{"id":"method-advanced-148-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[148],"stem":"颈线被收盘跌破后，价格很快又收盘站回右肩高点之上。最合理的读法是？","options":["形态仍然有效，只是回测颈线","应把头肩顶改成头肩底","形态失效，看跌读法不再成立","价格会更快达到参考位"],"answer":2,"explanation":"收盘重新站回右肩之上，说明跌破没有延续。","optionExplanations":["站回右肩之上不是回测。","方向和结构都不同。","正确：这是本课的失效条件。","与失效相矛盾。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Head and Shoulders Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/head-shoulders.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Head and shoulders (chart pattern)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Head_and_shoulders_(chart_pattern)"}],"stemEn":"After a close below the neckline, price soon closes back above the right shoulder high. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["Still valid; just a neckline retest","Relabel it as an inverse head and shoulders","The pattern has failed; the bearish reading no longer holds","Price will reach the reference faster"],"explanationEn":"A close back above the right shoulder shows the break did not continue.","optionExplanationsEn":["Closing above the right shoulder is not a retest.","The structure and direction differ.","Correct: That is this lesson’s invalidation.","That contradicts the invalidation."]},{"id":"method-advanced-148-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[148],"stem":"头肩顶跌破颈线后，价格只走了参考幅度的一半就反弹。这说明什么？","options":["说明头肩顶画错了","之后还会补完剩下的一半","颈线应该重画到反弹处","参考幅度只是参考，不是目标"],"answer":3,"explanation":"参考幅度是习惯算法，价格可能提前掉头，也可能走得更远。","optionExplanations":["走不满不等于画错。","没有这种规律。","重画颈线是在迁就价格。","正确：本课强调这一点。"],"skills":["参考与目标"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Head and Shoulders Pattern","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/head-shoulders.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Head and shoulders (chart pattern)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Head_and_shoulders_(chart_pattern)"}],"stemEn":"After a neckline break, price covers only half the reference distance before bouncing. What does that show?","optionsEn":["The pattern was drawn wrongly","The rest of the distance must follow later","The neckline should be redrawn at the bounce","The reference distance is only a reference, not a guaranteed target"],"explanationEn":"The reference distance is a convention; price may turn early or go further.","optionExplanationsEn":["Falling short does not mean it was drawn wrongly.","There is no such rule.","Redrawing just fits the line to price.","Correct: This lesson stresses this."]},{"id":"method-beginner-149-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[149],"stem":"两个高点 50.0 和 50.3，中间低点 48.5。按本课 1% 的口径，两个高点算不算相近？","options":["不算：第二个高点更高","不算：相差 3%","算：只要都在 48.5 之上","算：相差 0.6%，在 1% 以内"],"answer":3,"explanation":"(50.3 − 50.0) ÷ 50.0 = 0.6%，在 1% 以内。","optionExplanations":["第二顶可以略高。","百分比算错了。","相近看两个高点的差距。","正确：0.3 ÷ 50 = 0.6%。"],"skills":["相近口径"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Double Top","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doubletop.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Double Bottom","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doublebottom.asp"}],"stemEn":"Two highs of 50.0 and 50.3 with a middle low of 48.5. Under this lesson’s 1% rule, are the highs similar?","optionsEn":["No: the second high is higher","No: they differ by 3%","Yes: as long as both are above 48.5","Yes: they differ by 0.6%, within 1%"],"explanationEn":"(50.3 − 50.0) ÷ 50.0 = 0.6%, within 1%.","optionExplanationsEn":["The second top may be slightly higher.","The percentage is wrong.","Similarity is about the two highs.","Correct: 0.3 ÷ 50 = 0.6%."]},{"id":"method-beginner-149-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[149],"stem":"双顶什么时候才算完成？","options":["收盘跌破两顶之间的低点时","第二个高点出现时","第二个高点比第一个低时","成交量放大时"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只有收盘跌破中间低点，双顶才完成。","optionExplanations":["正确：这是确认条件。","这时还只是两个高点。","高低差不是确认条件。","成交量不是确认条件。"],"skills":["确认条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Double Top","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doubletop.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Double Bottom","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doublebottom.asp"}],"stemEn":"When is a double top complete?","optionsEn":["When price closes below the low between the tops","When the second high appears","When the second high is lower","When volume rises"],"explanationEn":"Only a close below the middle low completes a double top.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: That is the confirmation condition.","At that point it is just two highs.","The difference is not the trigger.","Volume is not the trigger."]},{"id":"method-advanced-149-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[149],"stem":"两个相近高点出现后，价格没有跌破中间低点，反而收盘越过了两个高点。最合理的读法是？","options":["双顶完成，只是方向反了","双顶不成立，上涨仍在延续","应把它改称三重顶","之后会跌得更深"],"answer":1,"explanation":"双顶需要跌破中间低点才完成；先向上突破说明它没有成立。","optionExplanations":["形态没有方向反转一说。","正确：没有完成，反而被突破。","没有第三个相近高点。","没有依据。"],"skills":["失效与未完成"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Double Top","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doubletop.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Double Bottom","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doublebottom.asp"}],"stemEn":"After two similar highs, price never breaks the middle low and instead closes above both highs. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["The double top completed in the other direction","The double top does not hold; the rally continues","It should be called a triple top","The eventual drop will be deeper"],"explanationEn":"A double top needs the middle low to break; an upside break first means it never formed.","optionExplanationsEn":["A pattern does not complete “in reverse”.","Correct: It never completed and was broken upward.","There is no third similar high.","There is no basis for that."]},{"id":"method-advanced-149-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[149],"stem":"第二个高点比第一个高出 0.5%，有人据此说“不是双顶”。按本课应怎样回应？","options":["说得对，双顶需要完全等高","第二顶更高，说明会继续上涨","不必等高，在口径内仍是候选","应改画成头肩顶"],"answer":2,"explanation":"第二顶略高或略低都正常，关键是之后是否跌破中间低点。","optionExplanations":["完全等高的要求不现实。","差距很小，不能推出方向。","正确：本课允许 1% 以内的差距。","缺少第三个高点。"],"skills":["常见误解"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Double Top","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doubletop.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Double Bottom","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/doublebottom.asp"}],"stemEn":"The second high is 0.5% above the first, and someone says it is not a double top. How does this lesson respond?","optionsEn":["Right, the tops must be exactly equal","A higher second top means a rise will follow","The second top need not be equal; within the tolerance it is still a candidate","Redraw it as a head and shoulders"],"explanationEn":"A slightly higher or lower second top is normal; what matters is whether the middle low then breaks.","optionExplanationsEn":["Exact equality is unrealistic.","The gap is tiny and implies no direction.","Correct: This lesson allows up to 1%.","There is no third high."]},{"id":"method-beginner-150-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[150],"stem":"高点 80、79、78.2 逐次降低，低点 75、75.1、74.9 大致持平。这更像哪种三角形？","options":["上升三角形","对称三角形","下降三角形","矩形"],"answer":2,"explanation":"高点逐次降低、低点大致持平，符合下降三角形。","optionExplanations":["上升三角形是高点持平、低点抬高。","对称三角形的低点要逐次抬高。","正确：高点降低、低点持平。","矩形的高点也大致持平。"],"skills":["三角形分类"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Triangle chart patterns","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/triangle.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Symmetrical Triangle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/symmetricaltriangle.asp"}],"stemEn":"Highs of 80, 79 and 78.2 fall while lows of 75, 75.1 and 74.9 are roughly flat. Which triangle is this closest to?","optionsEn":["Ascending triangle","Symmetrical triangle","Descending triangle","Rectangle"],"explanationEn":"Falling highs with flat lows fit a descending triangle.","optionExplanationsEn":["Ascending has flat highs and rising lows.","Symmetrical needs rising lows.","Correct: Falling highs, flat lows.","A rectangle has flat highs too."]},{"id":"method-beginner-150-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[150],"stem":"三角形里一根K线的最高价刺出上边线，但收盘仍在线内。按本课算突破吗？","options":["算：最高价已经越过","算：三角形末端都会突破","无法判断，要看下一根颜色","不算：突破以收盘越过边线为准"],"answer":3,"explanation":"本课以收盘越过边线为突破。","optionExplanations":["本课看收盘。","定义里没有这一条。","颜色不是标准。","正确：影线刺出不算。"],"skills":["突破定义"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Triangle chart patterns","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/triangle.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Symmetrical Triangle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/symmetricaltriangle.asp"}],"stemEn":"In a triangle, a bar’s high pokes above the upper line but it closes inside. Is it a breakout here?","optionsEn":["Yes: the high went beyond","Yes: triangles always break near the end","Cannot tell without the next bar’s colour","No: a breakout needs a close beyond the line"],"explanationEn":"This lesson defines a breakout as a close beyond the line.","optionExplanationsEn":["This lesson uses the close.","The definition has no such clause.","Colour is not the test.","Correct: A wick poke does not count."]},{"id":"method-advanced-150-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[150],"stem":"上升三角形出现，有人说“它一定向上突破”。按本课应怎样回应？","options":["方向事先不确定，要等收盘突破并看后续","同意，上升三角形只会向上突破","应该反过来看空","三角形不会突破，只会继续收敛"],"answer":0,"explanation":"形态只描述收敛，突破方向和成败都要等价格给出。","optionExplanations":["正确：这是本课的立场。","也可能向下突破。","同样没有依据。","收敛终会结束。"],"skills":["方向不确定"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Triangle chart patterns","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/triangle.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Symmetrical Triangle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/symmetricaltriangle.asp"}],"stemEn":"An ascending triangle forms and someone says it is sure to break upward. How does this lesson respond?","optionsEn":["Direction is uncertain; wait for a closing break and what follows","Agreed; ascending triangles only break up","The opposite: be bearish","Triangles never break; they just keep narrowing"],"explanationEn":"The pattern only describes narrowing; direction and success come from price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: That is this lesson’s position.","It can also break down.","That has no basis either.","The narrowing eventually ends."]},{"id":"method-advanced-150-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[150],"stem":"三角形向上收盘突破，下一根就收回三角形内。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["突破依然有效","按突破失败处理，并留意下边线","重新画一个更大的三角形","说明之后会大涨"],"answer":1,"explanation":"突破后收回形态内，按失败处理，另一边的突破也可能出现。","optionExplanations":["收回内部说明没有延续。","正确：收回三角形内是失败的标志。","随意重画是在迁就价格。","没有依据。"],"skills":["突破失败"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Triangle chart patterns","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/triangle.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Symmetrical Triangle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/symmetricaltriangle.asp"}],"stemEn":"A triangle breaks upward on a close, and the next bar closes back inside. How should this be handled?","optionsEn":["The breakout still holds","Treat it as a failed breakout and watch the lower line","Redraw a larger triangle","A big rally is coming"],"explanationEn":"A close back inside after a breakout is a failure, and a break of the other side is possible.","optionExplanationsEn":["Closing inside shows no follow-through.","Correct: Closing back inside marks failure.","Redrawing at will just fits the lines to price.","There is no basis for that."]},{"id":"method-beginner-151-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[151],"stem":"旗杆从 50 涨到 56，旗面最低回到 54.5。回撤占旗杆的多少？是否满足本课口径？","options":["50%，刚好满足","25%，满足","75%，不满足","无法判断，要看成交量"],"answer":1,"explanation":"回撤 = 56 − 54.5 = 1.5，旗杆 = 6，占 25%，不超过一半。","optionExplanations":["56−54.5=1.5，不是 3。","正确：回撤 1.5，旗杆 6。","计算有误。","比例只看价格。"],"skills":["回撤比例"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Flag","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/f/flag.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Pennant","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pennant.asp"}],"stemEn":"The pole rises from 50 to 56, and the flag dips to 54.5. What share of the pole is retraced, and does it meet this lesson’s limit?","optionsEn":["50%; it just qualifies","25%; it qualifies","75%; it fails","Cannot tell without volume"],"explanationEn":"Retracement = 56 − 54.5 = 1.5 of a 6 pole, i.e. 25%, within half.","optionExplanationsEn":["56−54.5=1.5, not 3.","Correct: Retracement 1.5, pole 6.","Miscalculated.","The ratio uses price only."]},{"id":"method-beginner-151-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[151],"stem":"旗形属于哪类形态？","options":["反转形态：旗杆方向即将结束","区间形态：价格会长期横盘","中继形态：等待顺着旗杆方向延续","只是成交量形态"],"answer":2,"explanation":"旗形是中继形态，等的是旗杆方向的延续。","optionExplanations":["旗形不是反转形态。","旗面通常很短。","正确：旗形描述的是趋势中的休息。","它首先是价格形态。"],"skills":["形态分类"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Flag","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/f/flag.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Pennant","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pennant.asp"}],"stemEn":"What kind of pattern is a flag?","optionsEn":["A reversal pattern: the pole’s direction is ending","A range pattern: price will move sideways for long","A continuation pattern: it waits for the pole’s direction to resume","Only a volume pattern"],"explanationEn":"A flag is a continuation pattern awaiting the pole’s direction.","optionExplanationsEn":["A flag is not a reversal pattern.","Flags are usually short.","Correct: A flag describes a pause in a trend.","It is primarily a price pattern."]},{"id":"method-advanced-151-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[151],"stem":"旗面整理时，价格收盘跌破了旗面下沿，并回撤到旗杆的 70%。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["回撤越深，之后涨得越多","这是一面更大的旗","应改称三角旗","形态失效，不再按旗形中继看待"],"answer":3,"explanation":"跌破旗面下沿、回撤超过旗杆一半，都是失效条件。","optionExplanations":["没有这种规律。","超过一半已不满足口径。","三角旗是旗面形状不同，不是回撤更深。","正确：跌破下沿且回撤过深。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Flag","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/f/flag.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Pennant","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pennant.asp"}],"stemEn":"During the flag, price closes below the flag’s bottom and retraces 70% of the pole. How should this be handled?","optionsEn":["The deeper the pullback, the bigger the rally","It is just a bigger flag","It should be called a pennant","The pattern has failed; no longer treat it as a continuation flag"],"explanationEn":"Breaking the flag’s bottom and retracing more than half the pole are both invalidations.","optionExplanationsEn":["There is no such rule.","More than half fails the definition.","A pennant differs in shape, not depth.","Correct: It broke the bottom and retraced too deeply."]},{"id":"method-advanced-151-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[151],"stem":"旗形和三角旗的区别主要在哪里？","options":["旗面形状：平行通道与收敛三角","旗杆的方向","三角旗只出现在下跌中","旗形不需要旗杆"],"answer":0,"explanation":"两者都需要旗杆，区别在于整理部分是平行通道还是收敛三角。","optionExplanations":["正确：两者的旗杆要求相同。","两者都可以向上或向下。","两个方向都有。","旗杆是两者共同的前提。"],"skills":["相近概念"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Flag","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/f/flag.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Pennant","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pennant.asp"}],"stemEn":"What mainly distinguishes a flag from a pennant?","optionsEn":["The shape of the consolidation: parallel channel versus converging triangle","The direction of the pole","Pennants occur only in declines","A flag needs no pole"],"explanationEn":"Both need a pole; the difference is whether the consolidation is a parallel channel or a converging triangle.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Their pole requirements are the same.","Both can point up or down.","Both directions occur.","A pole is required for both."]},{"id":"method-beginner-152-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[152],"stem":"矩形上沿 30、下沿 28。收盘向上突破后，按箱体高度量出的参考位是多少？","options":["32","30","34","31"],"answer":0,"explanation":"箱高 = 30 − 28 = 2，参考位 = 30 + 2 = 32，仅作参考。","optionExplanations":["正确：30 + (30 − 28) = 32。","30 是上沿本身。","把高度算成了 4。","只加了一半高度。"],"skills":["参考幅度"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Rectangle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rectangle.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Trading Range","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tradingrange.asp"}],"stemEn":"A rectangle’s top is 30 and bottom 28. After an upside close breakout, what is the box-height reference?","optionsEn":["32","30","34","31"],"explanationEn":"Height = 30 − 28 = 2, so the reference is 30 + 2 = 32, for reference only.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 30 + (30 − 28) = 32.","30 is the top itself.","That doubles the height.","That adds only half the height."]},{"id":"method-beginner-152-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[152],"stem":"矩形整理和 134 课的交易区间是什么关系？","options":["矩形只出现在下跌中","同一种结构，叫法和侧重不同","交易区间是倾斜的通道","两者之间毫无关系"],"answer":1,"explanation":"两者都是价格在水平边界之间来回，只是视角不同。","optionExplanations":["两个方向都有。","正确：经典形态学更重突破与幅度。","区间大致水平。","描述的是同一现象。"],"skills":["相近概念"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Rectangle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rectangle.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Trading Range","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tradingrange.asp"}],"stemEn":"How does a rectangle relate to the trading range in lesson 134?","optionsEn":["Rectangles appear only in declines","Essentially the same structure, named and emphasised differently","A trading range must slope","They are unrelated"],"explanationEn":"Both describe price moving between horizontal bounds; only the perspective differs.","optionExplanationsEn":["They occur in both directions.","Correct: Classical analysis stresses the breakout and distance.","A range is roughly horizontal.","They describe the same phenomenon."]},{"id":"method-advanced-152-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[152],"stem":"上涨后出现矩形，最后价格收盘跌破下沿并持续走低。最合理的看法是？","options":["这不是矩形，因为没有顺着原趋势突破","跌破下沿是假突破，之后会回到上沿","矩形可以向任一方向突破，这次是向下","参考幅度只适用于向上突破"],"answer":2,"explanation":"矩形只描述箱体，突破方向由价格决定。","optionExplanations":["矩形不要求突破方向。","持续走低说明有跟随。","正确：方向事先不确定。","两个方向都可以量。"],"skills":["方向不确定"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Rectangle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rectangle.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Trading Range","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tradingrange.asp"}],"stemEn":"A rectangle forms after a rally, and price finally closes below the bottom and keeps falling. What is the most reasonable view?","optionsEn":["It was not a rectangle because it did not break with the trend","Breaking the bottom is false; price will return to the top","A rectangle can break either way; this time it broke down","The reference distance applies only upward"],"explanationEn":"A rectangle only describes the box; price decides the breakout direction.","optionExplanationsEn":["A rectangle has no required direction.","Continued declines show follow-through.","Correct: The direction is not known in advance.","It applies in both directions."]},{"id":"method-advanced-152-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[152],"stem":"矩形向上收盘突破后，第二根又收回箱体内。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["突破依然成立","把上沿改到突破K的高点","说明之后会向下突破","按突破失败处理，仍把它当箱体看"],"answer":3,"explanation":"收回箱体内是失败的标志，箱体仍是参考。","optionExplanations":["收回箱体内与成立矛盾。","随意挪动边界是在迁就价格。","可能，但不能下结论。","正确：收回箱体说明没有延续。"],"skills":["突破失败"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Rectangle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rectangle.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Trading Range","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/tradingrange.asp"}],"stemEn":"After an upside close breakout from a rectangle, the second bar closes back inside. How should this be handled?","optionsEn":["The breakout still holds","Move the top to the breakout bar’s high","It means a downside break will follow","Treat it as a failed breakout and keep treating it as a box"],"explanationEn":"Closing back inside marks a failure, and the box remains the reference.","optionExplanationsEn":["Closing inside contradicts that.","Moving the boundary just fits it to price.","Possible, but not a conclusion.","Correct: Closing back inside shows no continuation."]},{"id":"method-beginner-153-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[153],"stem":"上升楔形里，上下两条线哪一条更陡？","options":["上边线（连接高点的线）","两条一样陡","与斜率无关","下边线（连接低点的线）"],"answer":3,"explanation":"上升楔形的低点抬得更快，所以下边线更陡、两线收敛。","optionExplanations":["那样两线会发散。","斜率相同是通道。","斜率正是区分依据。","正确：低点抬得更快才会收敛。"],"skills":["斜率比较"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Wedge","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/wedge.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Wedge pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedge_pattern"}],"stemEn":"In a rising wedge, which of the two lines is steeper?","optionsEn":["The upper line through the highs","Both equally steep","Slope is irrelevant","The lower line through the lows"],"explanationEn":"In a rising wedge the lows rise faster, so the lower line is steeper and the lines converge.","optionExplanationsEn":["That would make the lines diverge.","Equal slopes make a channel.","Slope is exactly the distinguishing test.","Correct: The lows rising faster makes the lines converge."]},{"id":"method-beginner-153-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[153],"stem":"两条连线都向上、斜率相同、互相平行。它是上升楔形吗？","options":["不是：平行的是上升通道","是：两条线都向上","是：只要高点在抬高","不是：楔形都是向下的"],"answer":0,"explanation":"楔形的关键是收敛，平行的两线是通道。","optionExplanations":["正确：楔形要求收敛。","方向相同还不够。","还要看是否收敛。","也有上升楔形。"],"skills":["相近概念"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Wedge","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/wedge.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Wedge pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedge_pattern"}],"stemEn":"Both lines slope upward with equal slopes and stay parallel. Is it a rising wedge?","optionsEn":["No: parallel lines form a rising channel","Yes: both lines slope up","Yes: as long as highs rise","No: wedges only slope down"],"explanationEn":"A wedge must converge; parallel lines form a channel.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A wedge requires convergence.","Same direction is not enough.","Convergence is also required.","Rising wedges exist too."]},{"id":"method-advanced-153-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[153],"stem":"上升楔形和 133 课的“三推”有什么关系？","options":["两者之间完全无关","同一现象：推进变弱、空间变窄","三推只出现在下跌中","楔形要正好有三个高点"],"answer":1,"explanation":"两者都描述同向推进逐次减弱、两线收敛的现象。","optionExplanations":["两者高度重合。","正确：只是经典形态学与价格行为的不同说法。","两个方向都有。","楔形没有固定的高点个数。"],"skills":["相近概念"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Wedge","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/wedge.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Wedge pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedge_pattern"}],"stemEn":"How does a rising wedge relate to the “three pushes” of lesson 133?","optionsEn":["They are unrelated","They describe the same thing: weakening pushes in a narrowing space","Three pushes occur only in declines","A wedge must have exactly three highs"],"explanationEn":"Both describe successive pushes in one direction weakening as the lines converge.","optionExplanationsEn":["They overlap heavily.","Correct: Classical and price-action names for it.","Both directions occur.","A wedge has no fixed number of highs."]},{"id":"method-advanced-153-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[153],"stem":"上升楔形向下收盘突破后，价格又收盘回到楔形内并越过最近的高点。最合理的读法是？","options":["楔形依然有效","应改称下降楔形","形态失效，上涨可能继续","说明之后会大跌"],"answer":2,"explanation":"回到楔形内并越过最近高点，向下突破就失败了。","optionExplanations":["失效条件已经出现。","下降楔形的两线方向向下。","正确：这是本课的失效条件。","没有依据。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Wedge","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/wedge.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Wedge pattern","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedge_pattern"}],"stemEn":"After a rising wedge breaks down on a close, price closes back inside and above the latest high. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["The wedge still holds","Rename it a falling wedge","The pattern has failed; the rally may continue","A big drop is coming"],"explanationEn":"Returning inside and above the latest high means the downside break failed.","optionExplanationsEn":["The invalidation has occurred.","A falling wedge slopes down.","Correct: That is this lesson’s invalidation.","There is no basis for that."]},{"id":"method-beginner-154-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[154],"stem":"杯沿 50，杯底 44，柄回撤到 47.5。柄的回撤是否小于杯身深度的一半？","options":["不是：回撤 3.5","不是：深度是 3","是：回撤 2.5 小于 3","无法判断，要看成交量"],"answer":2,"explanation":"杯深 = 50 − 44 = 6，柄回撤 = 50 − 47.5 = 2.5，小于 3。","optionExplanations":["算成了 47.5−44。","深度是 50−44=6。","正确：50−47.5=2.5。","比例只看价格。"],"skills":["回撤比例"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Cup and Handle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/cupandhandle.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Cup and handle","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cup_and_handle"}],"stemEn":"The rim is 50, the cup bottom 44, and the handle dips to 47.5. Is the handle retracement less than half the cup depth?","optionsEn":["No: the retracement is 3.5","No: the depth is 3","Yes: 2.5 is less than half of the 6 depth (3)","Cannot tell without volume"],"explanationEn":"Cup depth = 50 − 44 = 6, handle retracement = 50 − 47.5 = 2.5, which is below 3.","optionExplanationsEn":["That computes 47.5−44.","The depth is 50−44=6.","Correct: 50−47.5=2.5.","The ratio uses price only."]},{"id":"method-beginner-154-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[154],"stem":"为什么本课强调杯身应是圆弧底而不是尖底？","options":["尖底的右边画不出柄","圆弧底的成交量总是更小","尖底只出现在加密市场","慢慢筑底与急跌急涨含义不同"],"answer":3,"explanation":"杯柄描述的是逐步筑底；急跌急涨是另一种过程（见 155 课）。","optionExplanations":["柄可以画，但含义变了。","成交量没有固定结论。","与市场无关。","正确：两种过程的风险不同。"],"skills":["形态要素"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Cup and Handle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/cupandhandle.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Cup and handle","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cup_and_handle"}],"stemEn":"Why does this lesson insist the cup be rounded rather than a sharp V?","optionsEn":["A V cannot have a handle","Rounded bottoms always have less volume","V bottoms appear only in crypto","A rounded bottom shows slow basing; a V is a sharp drop and recovery, a different story"],"explanationEn":"A cup and handle describes gradual basing; a sharp drop and recovery is a different process (see lesson 155).","optionExplanationsEn":["A handle can be drawn, but the meaning changes.","Volume has no fixed conclusion.","It is not about the market.","Correct: The two processes carry different risks."]},{"id":"method-advanced-154-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[154],"stem":"杯柄向上收盘突破杯沿后，两根之内又收回杯沿以下。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["突破失败，形态失效","突破仍然有效，只是回测","把杯沿重新画到突破K高点","说明之后会更快上涨"],"answer":0,"explanation":"收盘回到杯沿以下说明突破没有站稳。","optionExplanations":["正确：这是本课的失效条件。","收盘回到杯沿下不是回测。","随意重画是在迁就价格。","没有依据。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Cup and Handle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/cupandhandle.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Cup and handle","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cup_and_handle"}],"stemEn":"After a close above the rim, price closes back below it within two bars. How should this be handled?","optionsEn":["A failed breakout; the pattern is invalidated","Still valid; just a retest","Redraw the rim at the breakout bar’s high","A faster rally will follow"],"explanationEn":"A close back below the rim shows the breakout did not hold.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: That is this lesson’s invalidation.","A close below the rim is not a retest.","Redrawing just fits price.","There is no basis for that."]},{"id":"method-advanced-154-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[154],"stem":"关于杯柄形态的提出者，本课的写法是什么？","options":["由 Steve Nison 发明","O’Neil 推广，首创者未确认","由 Al Brooks 发明","已确认是 O’Neil 首创"],"answer":1,"explanation":"本课只写 O’Neil 系统描述，不把他写成已确认的首创者。","optionExplanations":["Nison 推广的是蜡烛图。","正确：区分推广者与首创者。","Brooks 讲的是价格行为。","本课没有这样写。"],"skills":["来源与出处"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Cup and Handle","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/cupandhandle.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Cup and handle","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cup_and_handle"}],"stemEn":"How does this lesson describe the originator of the cup and handle?","optionsEn":["Invented by Steve Nison","O’Neil described and popularised it; whether he was first is unverified","Invented by Al Brooks","Confirmed as O’Neil’s invention"],"explanationEn":"This lesson says O’Neil described it systematically, without claiming he invented it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Nison popularised candlesticks.","Correct: Distinguish popularisers from originators.","Brooks teaches price action.","This lesson does not claim that."]},{"id":"method-beginner-155-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[155],"stem":"价格 5 根K线内从 50 跌到 47.5，再 6 根涨回 49.6。按本课口径是否符合 V 形反转？","options":["不符合：跌幅只有 2.5%","符合：跌 5%，收复 84%","不符合：没有回到 50","不符合：用了 11 根K线"],"answer":1,"explanation":"跌幅 2.5 ÷ 50 = 5%，收复 (49.6 − 47.5) ÷ 2.5 = 84%，两段都在 8 根以内。","optionExplanations":["跌幅是 5%。","正确：2.5÷50=5%，2.1÷2.5=84%。","口径只要求收复八成。","两段各自都在 8 根以内。"],"skills":["口径计算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Rounding Bottom","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/roundingbottom.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Saucer","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/saucer.asp"}],"stemEn":"Price falls from 50 to 47.5 in 5 bars and rises back to 49.6 in 6 bars. Does it meet this lesson’s V-reversal thresholds?","optionsEn":["No: the drop is only 2.5%","Yes: a 5% drop with 84% recovered","No: it did not get back to 50","No: it took 11 bars"],"explanationEn":"The drop is 2.5 ÷ 50 = 5% and the recovery (49.6 − 47.5) ÷ 2.5 = 84%, each within 8 bars.","optionExplanationsEn":["The drop is 5%.","Correct: 2.5÷50=5% and 2.1÷2.5=84%.","Only 80% recovery is required.","Each leg is within 8 bars."]},{"id":"method-beginner-155-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[155],"stem":"圆弧底和 V 形反转最主要的区别是什么？","options":["圆弧底只出现在加密市场","V 形反转需要更大的成交量才能画出","反转的速度：慢慢掉头与急跌急涨","两者完全相同"],"answer":2,"explanation":"圆弧底是逐渐转向，V 形是急跌后立即急涨。","optionExplanations":["与市场无关。","画法与成交量无关。","正确：这是两者的核心差别。","速度和过程不同。"],"skills":["形态比较"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Rounding Bottom","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/roundingbottom.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Saucer","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/saucer.asp"}],"stemEn":"What mainly distinguishes a rounding bottom from a V reversal?","optionsEn":["Rounding bottoms occur only in crypto","A V needs more volume to be drawn","The speed of the turn: gradual versus sharp","They are identical"],"explanationEn":"A rounding bottom turns gradually; a V drops sharply and rebounds immediately.","optionExplanationsEn":["It is not about the market.","Drawing does not depend on volume.","Correct: That is the core difference.","Their speed and process differ."]},{"id":"method-advanced-155-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[155],"stem":"为什么本课说 V 形反转“只能事后识别”？","options":["交易所不公布实时数据","V 形反转只出现在周线上","V 形反转没有低点","急跌途中看不出会不会马上反弹"],"answer":3,"explanation":"V 形的定义依赖急涨收复，这部分在跌的时候还没发生。","optionExplanations":["数据是实时的。","不限周期。","它有明确的低点。","正确：形态要靠反弹本身来定义。"],"skills":["事后确认"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Rounding Bottom","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/roundingbottom.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Saucer","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/saucer.asp"}],"stemEn":"Why does this lesson say a V reversal can only be identified afterwards?","optionsEn":["Exchanges do not publish real-time data","V reversals appear only on weekly charts","A V reversal has no low","During a sharp fall there is no way to tell whether an immediate rebound will come"],"explanationEn":"The V is defined by the sharp recovery, which has not happened yet during the fall.","optionExplanationsEn":["The data is real-time.","It is not limited to one timeframe.","It has a clear low.","Correct: The pattern is defined by the rebound itself."]},{"id":"method-advanced-155-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[155],"stem":"与圆弧底相比，在 V 形反转的急涨中追进去，主要风险是什么？","options":["底部没有经过整理，随时可能再次急跌","V 形反转之后价格不会再波动","圆弧底的风险总是更大","V 形反转的成交量太小"],"answer":0,"explanation":"V 形缺少低位整理，失效参考离当前价很远，再次急跌的风险更大。","optionExplanations":["正确：缺少可参考的整理区。","价格会继续波动。","本课的比较方向相反。","这不是主要风险。"],"skills":["风险差异"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Rounding Bottom","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/roundingbottom.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Saucer","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/saucer.asp"}],"stemEn":"Compared with a rounding bottom, what is the main risk of chasing the sharp rise of a V reversal?","optionsEn":["The bottom had no consolidation, so another sharp drop can come at any time","After a V price no longer fluctuates","Rounding bottoms are always riskier","V reversals have too little volume"],"explanationEn":"A V lacks a base at the lows, so the invalidation level is far away and another sharp drop is a bigger risk.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: There is no base to refer to.","Price keeps fluctuating.","This lesson argues the opposite.","That is not the main risk."]},{"id":"method-beginner-156-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[156],"stem":"价格高点 50 → 52，对应同一根K线的 RSI 75 → 68。这是哪种背离？","options":["常规顶背离","常规底背离","隐藏背离","没有背离"],"answer":0,"explanation":"价格高点抬高而 RSI 高点降低，是常规顶背离。","optionExplanations":["正确：价格更高、指标更低。","底背离看的是低点。","隐藏背离是价格高点降低。","两者方向相反，就是背离。"],"skills":["背离分类"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Divergence","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/divergence.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: RSI divergence indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589127/"}],"stemEn":"Price highs go 50 → 52 while RSI at the same bars goes 75 → 68. What kind of divergence is this?","optionsEn":["Regular bearish divergence","Regular bullish divergence","Hidden divergence","No divergence"],"explanationEn":"A higher price high with a lower RSI high is regular bearish divergence.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Higher price, lower indicator.","Bullish divergence uses lows.","Hidden divergence needs a lower price high.","Opposite directions are divergence."]},{"id":"method-beginner-156-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[156],"stem":"比较背离时，指标值应该取在哪里？","options":["指标自己最近的最高点","与价格高低点同一根K线上","任意两根K线都可以","只看最后一根K线"],"answer":1,"explanation":"背离是比较同一时刻的价格与指标，必须对齐到同一根K线。","optionExplanations":["可能和价格高点不在同一根K线。","正确：这是本课强调的对齐。","这样比较没有意义。","背离需要两组高低点。"],"skills":["对齐"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Divergence","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/divergence.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: RSI divergence indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589127/"}],"stemEn":"When checking divergence, where should the indicator value be read?","optionsEn":["At the indicator’s own nearest peak","On the same bar as the price swing","On any two bars","Only on the last bar"],"explanationEn":"Divergence compares price and indicator at the same moments, so values must be on the same bars.","optionExplanationsEn":["It may not be on the price swing bar.","Correct: This is the alignment the lesson stresses.","That comparison is meaningless.","Divergence needs two swings."]},{"id":"method-advanced-156-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[156],"stem":"上涨中价格低点抬高（58 → 60），RSI 低点却降低（40 → 34）。按本课这更像什么？","options":["常规顶背离，偏向反转","常规底背离，偏向反转","隐藏看涨背离，偏向延续","不属于任何一种背离"],"answer":2,"explanation":"价格低点抬高、指标低点降低，是隐藏看涨背离。","optionExplanations":["这里比较的是低点。","常规底背离是价格低点更低。","正确：价格低点抬高、指标低点降低。","方向不一致就是背离。"],"skills":["隐藏背离"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Divergence","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/divergence.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: RSI divergence indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589127/"}],"stemEn":"In an uptrend, price lows rise (58 → 60) while RSI lows fall (40 → 34). What is this closest to?","optionsEn":["Regular bearish divergence","Regular bullish divergence","Hidden bullish divergence, often read as continuation","Not divergence at all"],"explanationEn":"A higher price low with a lower indicator low is hidden bullish divergence.","optionExplanationsEn":["This compares lows.","Regular bullish needs a lower price low.","Correct: Higher price low, lower indicator low.","Opposite directions are divergence."]},{"id":"method-advanced-156-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[156],"stem":"顶背离出现后价格继续创新高，又出现了第二次顶背离。按本课应怎样理解？","options":["第一次背离是计算错误","第二次背离之后价格会随即下跌","背离次数越多越说明会上涨","可连续出现，未确认前只是提醒"],"answer":3,"explanation":"背离只说明力度减弱，可以连续出现，需等价格确认。","optionExplanations":["背离本身不保证结果。","没有依据。","也没有依据。","正确：这是本课强调的局限。"],"skills":["确认"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Divergence","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/divergence.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: RSI divergence indicator","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000589127/"}],"stemEn":"After a bearish divergence price makes another new high and a second divergence appears. How should this be understood?","optionsEn":["The first divergence was a calculation error","Price will fall immediately after the second one","More divergences mean a rise","Divergence can repeat; without price confirmation it is only a warning"],"explanationEn":"Divergence only shows fading momentum, can repeat and needs price confirmation.","optionExplanationsEn":["Divergence does not guarantee an outcome.","There is no basis for that.","There is no basis for that either.","Correct: This is the limitation the lesson stresses."]},{"id":"method-beginner-157-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[157],"stem":"前一段平均成交量 1 万，本段价格上涨、平均成交量 1.5 万。按本课属于哪种组合？","options":["价涨量缩","价跌量增","价跌量缩","价涨量增"],"answer":3,"explanation":"价格上涨且平均成交量从 1 万增加到 1.5 万。","optionExplanations":["成交量是增加的。","价格是上涨的。","两项都不符。","正确：均量高于前一段。"],"skills":["四种组合"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Volume","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/volume.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Volume Analysis","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/volume-analysis.asp"}],"stemEn":"The prior segment averages 10,000 in volume; this segment rises on an average of 15,000. Which combination is it?","optionsEn":["Rising price, falling volume","Falling price, rising volume","Falling price, falling volume","Rising price, rising volume"],"explanationEn":"Price rose and average volume increased from 10,000 to 15,000.","optionExplanationsEn":["Volume increased.","Price rose.","Neither matches.","Correct: Average volume is above the prior segment."]},{"id":"method-beginner-157-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[157],"stem":"价格创出新高，但这一段的平均成交量比上一段低。它说明什么？","options":["上涨中的参与在减少","价格会随之下跌","上涨变得更健康","成交量数据有误"],"answer":0,"explanation":"价涨量缩只说明跟随的人变少，需要结合位置判断。","optionExplanations":["正确：价涨量缩描述的是参与变化。","量价不能单独推出方向。","缩量不说明更健康。","缩量是正常现象。"],"skills":["参与程度"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Volume","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/volume.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Volume Analysis","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/volume-analysis.asp"}],"stemEn":"Price makes a new high, but this segment’s average volume is below the prior one. What does it show?","optionsEn":["Participation in the rally is shrinking","Price will fall right away","The rally is certainly healthier","The volume data is wrong"],"explanationEn":"Rising price on falling volume only shows fewer followers; location must be considered.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Rising price on falling volume describes participation.","Volume alone does not set direction.","Falling volume does not show health.","Falling volume is normal."]},{"id":"method-advanced-157-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[157],"stem":"比较 BTC 在两个不同交易所的成交量来判断量价，主要问题是什么？","options":["两个交易所的价格完全不同","口径不同，不能直接相比","加密货币没有成交量","成交量只在日线上有效"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不同交易所、现货与合约的成交量口径不同，应在同一数据源内比较。","optionExplanations":["价格通常接近。","正确：交易所与产品口径不一致。","有成交量数据。","任何周期都有成交量。"],"skills":["数据口径"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Volume","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/volume.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Volume Analysis","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/volume-analysis.asp"}],"stemEn":"What is the main problem with comparing BTC volume across two exchanges for volume–price analysis?","optionsEn":["Prices are completely different","Their reporting differs, so they are not directly comparable","Crypto has no volume","Volume works only on daily charts"],"explanationEn":"Volume differs across exchanges and between spot and futures; compare within one source.","optionExplanationsEn":["Prices are usually close.","Correct: Exchanges and products report differently.","Volume data exists.","Every timeframe has volume."]},{"id":"method-advanced-157-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[157],"stem":"同样是价跌量增，出现在区间下沿被跌破时与出现在长期下跌末端时，读法有何不同？","options":["两者意义相同，都说明下跌","后者说明下跌将继续加速","前者像跟随，后者或是恐慌抛售","前者说明价格会随后反弹"],"answer":2,"explanation":"量价组合本身不定方向，位置决定它更像跟随还是高潮。","optionExplanations":["本课强调位置不同意义不同。","末端放量也可能是衰竭。","正确：同一组合要放在位置里读。","没有依据。"],"skills":["位置与量价"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Volume","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/volume.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Volume Analysis","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/volume-analysis.asp"}],"stemEn":"How does falling price on rising volume differ when it occurs at a range breakdown versus at the end of a long decline?","optionsEn":["They mean exactly the same","The second means the decline will accelerate","The first may be participants joining a breakdown; the second may be a panic climax","The first means an immediate bounce"],"explanationEn":"The combination alone sets no direction; location decides whether it looks like follow-through or a climax.","optionExplanationsEn":["The lesson stresses location matters.","Late heavy volume can also be exhaustion.","Correct: The same combination must be read in context.","There is no basis for that."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-158-1","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[158],"stem":"卖出准备阶段里，每根K线要满足什么条件才能计数？","options":["收盘高于前一根收盘","最高价高于 2 根之前的最高价","收盘高于 4 根之前的收盘","成交量高于前一根"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Setup 比较当根收盘与 4 根之前的收盘。","optionExplanations":["比较的是 4 根之前。","这接近计数阶段的条件。","正确：这是 Setup 的比较方式。","九转不用成交量。"],"skills":["Setup 规则"],"references":[{"title":"ProCharting: TD Sequential Indicator","url":"https://procharting.in/docs/charting/technical-indicator/overlays/td-sequential"},{"title":"Wickra docs: TD Sequential","url":"https://wickra-docs.pages.dev/Indicator-TdSequential"}],"stemEn":"In a sell setup, what must each bar satisfy to be counted?","optionsEn":["Close above the prior close","High above the high two bars earlier","Close above the close four bars earlier","Volume above the prior bar"],"explanationEn":"The setup compares each close with the close four bars earlier.","optionExplanationsEn":["The comparison is four bars back.","That resembles the countdown condition.","Correct: This is how the setup compares bars.","TD Sequential does not use volume."]},{"id":"indicator-beginner-158-2","type":"indicator","level":"beginner","topicIds":[158],"stem":"准备阶段数到第 6 根时，有一根收盘低于 4 根之前的收盘。计数应怎样处理？","options":["跳过这根，继续数 7","直接算作完成","转入计数阶段","中断归零，之后重新数"],"answer":3,"explanation":"准备阶段要求连续 9 根满足，中断即归零。","optionExplanations":["准备阶段不能跳过。","没有数到 9。","计数阶段在准备完成后才开始。","正确：Setup 要求连续满足。"],"skills":["连续性"],"references":[{"title":"ProCharting: TD Sequential Indicator","url":"https://procharting.in/docs/charting/technical-indicator/overlays/td-sequential"},{"title":"Wickra docs: TD Sequential","url":"https://wickra-docs.pages.dev/Indicator-TdSequential"}],"stemEn":"In a setup at bar 6, a bar closes below the close four bars earlier. What happens to the count?","optionsEn":["Skip it and continue at 7","Count it as complete","Move into the countdown","It resets to zero and starts again later"],"explanationEn":"The setup needs nine consecutive qualifying bars; a break resets it.","optionExplanationsEn":["The setup cannot skip bars.","It did not reach 9.","The countdown starts after a completed setup.","Correct: The setup must be consecutive."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-158-1","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[158],"stem":"准备阶段和计数阶段在“是否连续”上有什么不同？","options":["准备阶段要连续，计数阶段不要求连续","两者都要连续","两者都不要连续","准备阶段不要连续，计数阶段要连续"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Setup 必须连续 9 根；Countdown 的 13 根可以不连续。","optionExplanations":["正确：这是两者的关键区别。","计数阶段允许间断。","准备阶段要连续。","方向说反了。"],"skills":["Countdown 规则"],"references":[{"title":"ProCharting: TD Sequential Indicator","url":"https://procharting.in/docs/charting/technical-indicator/overlays/td-sequential"},{"title":"Wickra docs: TD Sequential","url":"https://wickra-docs.pages.dev/Indicator-TdSequential"}],"stemEn":"How do the setup and countdown differ regarding consecutiveness?","optionsEn":["The setup must be consecutive; the countdown need not be","Both must be consecutive","Neither needs to be","The setup need not be; the countdown must be"],"explanationEn":"The setup needs nine in a row; the countdown’s 13 can be spread out.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: That is the key difference.","The countdown allows gaps.","The setup does.","That is reversed."]},{"id":"indicator-advanced-158-2","type":"indicator","level":"advanced","topicIds":[158],"stem":"卖出准备数到 9 之后，价格继续创新高。按本课应怎样看？","options":["指标计算出错了","九转只是提示，强趋势里继续上涨很常见","之后会更猛烈地下跌","应该把计数改成从 1 重新开始数到 9"],"answer":1,"explanation":"九转提示的是可能的衰竭，不保证反转。","optionExplanations":["数到 9 本身没有错。","正确：本课强调它不是反转指令。","没有依据。","这不能改变它只是提示的性质。"],"skills":["常见误用"],"references":[{"title":"ProCharting: TD Sequential Indicator","url":"https://procharting.in/docs/charting/technical-indicator/overlays/td-sequential"},{"title":"Wickra docs: TD Sequential","url":"https://wickra-docs.pages.dev/Indicator-TdSequential"}],"stemEn":"After a sell setup reaches 9, price keeps making new highs. How should this be viewed?","optionsEn":["The indicator was miscalculated","TD is only an alert; continued rises are common in strong trends","A sharper drop will follow","Restart the count at 1 to reach 9 again"],"explanationEn":"TD flags possible exhaustion and guarantees no reversal.","optionExplanationsEn":["Reaching 9 is not an error.","Correct: The lesson stresses it is not a reversal call.","There is no basis for that.","That does not change its nature as an alert."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-159-1","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[159],"stem":"原始K线开 50、高 52、低 49、收 51。HA 收盘是多少？","options":["51","50.5","50.0","51.5"],"answer":1,"explanation":"HA 收盘 = (50 + 52 + 49 + 51) ÷ 4 = 50.5。","optionExplanations":["那是原始收盘价。","正确：(50+52+49+51)÷4。","计算有误。","只平均了高和收。"],"skills":["HA 公式"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Heikin-Ashi Technique","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/heikinashi.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Understanding Heikin Ashi charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000619436/"}],"stemEn":"A real bar opens at 50, has a high of 52 and a low of 49, and closes at 51. What is the HA close?","optionsEn":["51","50.5","50.0","51.5"],"explanationEn":"HA close = (50 + 52 + 49 + 51) ÷ 4 = 50.5.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is the real close.","Correct: (50+52+49+51)÷4.","Miscalculated.","That averages only high and close."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-159-2","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[159],"stem":"在 HA 图上设止损时，应该用哪个价格？","options":["HA 显示的最低价","HA 开盘价","普通K线上的真实价格","任何一个都可以"],"answer":2,"explanation":"下单与止损要基于真实价格。","optionExplanations":["它是计算值。","它是平均值。","正确：HA 价格不是真实成交价。","HA 价格与真实价格可能相差不少。"],"skills":["真实价格"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Heikin-Ashi Technique","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/heikinashi.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Understanding Heikin Ashi charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000619436/"}],"stemEn":"Which price should be used to place a stop on a Heikin Ashi chart?","optionsEn":["The HA low shown","The HA open","The real traded price, checked on normal candles","Any of them"],"explanationEn":"Orders and stops must use real prices.","optionExplanationsEn":["It is a calculated value.","It is an average.","Correct: HA prices are not real trades.","HA and real prices can differ a lot."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-159-1","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[159],"stem":"用 HA 图的收盘价做策略回测，最主要的问题是什么？","options":["HA 没有成交量数据","HA 只适用于日线","HA 的颜色太多","成交价不真实，回测结果会失真"],"answer":3,"explanation":"HA 的开收是平均值，用它们模拟成交会得到虚假的结果。","optionExplanations":["这不是主要问题。","它不限周期。","颜色不是问题。","正确：这是 HA 最大的陷阱。"],"skills":["回测陷阱"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Heikin-Ashi Technique","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/heikinashi.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Understanding Heikin Ashi charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000619436/"}],"stemEn":"What is the main problem with backtesting a strategy on Heikin Ashi closes?","optionsEn":["HA has no volume data","HA only works on daily charts","HA has too many colours","The fill prices are not real, so results are distorted"],"explanationEn":"HA opens and closes are averages, so simulating fills on them gives false results.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is not the main issue.","It is not limited to one timeframe.","Colour is not the issue.","Correct: This is HA’s biggest trap."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-159-2","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[159],"stem":"为什么 HA 的转色往往比普通K线晚？","options":["开盘取前一根的平均，有平滑滞后","HA 使用了未来的数据","HA 跳过了一半的K线","交易所延迟发送 HA 数据"],"answer":0,"explanation":"每根 HA 都依赖前一根的平均，所以反应更慢。","optionExplanations":["正确：平滑必然带来滞后。","它只用过去的数据。","它不跳过K线。","HA 是本地计算的。"],"skills":["平滑与滞后"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Heikin-Ashi Technique","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/heikinashi.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Understanding Heikin Ashi charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000619436/"}],"stemEn":"Why do Heikin Ashi colour changes usually lag normal candles?","optionsEn":["The HA open averages the prior HA bar, adding smoothing lag","HA uses future data","HA skips half the bars","Exchanges delay HA data"],"explanationEn":"Each HA bar depends on the prior bar’s average, so it reacts more slowly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Smoothing brings lag.","It uses only past data.","It skips no bars.","HA is computed locally."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-160-1","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[160],"stem":"砖块大小 1.0，上一块向上砖顶部 50.0。收盘 50.7，要不要画新砖？","options":["不画：没有走完一块砖","画一块向上砖","画一块向下砖","画半块砖"],"answer":0,"explanation":"向上画砖需要收盘至少到 50.0 + 1.0 = 51.0。","optionExplanations":["正确：需要到 51.0。","50.7 < 51.0。","价格是上涨的。","砖块不能拆分。"],"skills":["画砖规则"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Renko Chart","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/renkochart.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Understanding Renko charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502284/"}],"stemEn":"The brick size is 1.0 and the last up brick tops out at 50.0. The close is 50.7. Is a new brick drawn?","optionsEn":["No: the move is less than a brick","Draw one up brick","Draw one down brick","Draw half a brick"],"explanationEn":"An up brick needs a close of at least 50.0 + 1.0 = 51.0.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: It needs to reach 51.0.","50.7 < 51.0.","Price rose.","Bricks cannot be split."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-160-2","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[160],"stem":"Renko 图的横轴代表什么？","options":["每小时一格，代表时间","砖块顺序，不是时间","每块砖的成交量大小","每天一格，代表日期"],"answer":1,"explanation":"砖形图只按价格幅度画砖，横轴是顺序。","optionExplanations":["时间被去掉了。","正确：每块砖幅度相同、时间不同。","与成交量无关。","同样不是时间。"],"skills":["去掉时间"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Renko Chart","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/renkochart.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Understanding Renko charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502284/"}],"stemEn":"What does the Renko chart’s horizontal axis represent?","optionsEn":["One cell per hour","The order of bricks, not time","Volume","One cell per day"],"explanationEn":"Renko draws bricks by price distance; the axis is just their order.","optionExplanationsEn":["Time has been removed.","Correct: Each brick is the same size but takes varying time.","It is unrelated to volume.","It is not time either."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-160-1","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[160],"stem":"同一段数据，砖块大小从 0.5 改成 2.0，图形会怎样？","options":["图形保持完全不变","砖块变多，图更细","砖块变少，过滤更多","横轴改为显示时间"],"answer":2,"explanation":"砖块越大，需要的价格幅度越大，砖块越少。","optionExplanations":["砖块大小决定一切。","方向说反了。","正确：砖块越大，过滤越多。","横轴依然不是时间。"],"skills":["参数影响"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Renko Chart","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/renkochart.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Understanding Renko charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502284/"}],"stemEn":"For the same data, what happens when the brick size changes from 0.5 to 2.0?","optionsEn":["The chart does not change","More bricks","Fewer bricks, filtering more of the small swings","The axis becomes time"],"explanationEn":"Larger bricks need bigger moves, so there are fewer of them.","optionExplanationsEn":["Brick size determines everything.","That is reversed.","Correct: Larger bricks filter more.","The axis is still not time."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-160-2","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[160],"stem":"为什么 Renko 需要“两块砖”才画反向砖？","options":["为了让图形更好看","交易所规定的","反向砖需要更多成交量","减少来回小幅反复造成的假转向"],"answer":3,"explanation":"反向要求更大的幅度，可以过滤在一块砖范围内的来回。","optionExplanations":["不是外观原因。","没有这种规定。","Renko 不用成交量。","正确：这是过滤噪音的设计。"],"skills":["反向规则"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Renko Chart","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/renkochart.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Understanding Renko charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502284/"}],"stemEn":"Why does Renko need two bricks to draw a reversal brick?","optionsEn":["To make the chart prettier","An exchange rule","Reversal bricks need more volume","To cut false reversals caused by small back-and-forth swings"],"explanationEn":"Requiring a larger move for reversals filters back-and-forth within one brick.","optionExplanationsEn":["It is not about looks.","There is no such rule.","Renko does not use volume.","Correct: It is a noise-filtering design."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-161-1","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[161],"stem":"格值 1、3 格反转。X 列最高到 110，价格回落到 108，要不要换到 O 列？","options":["换：已经回落了","换：只要回落 1 格就换","在 X 列上画 O","不换：只回落了 2 格"],"answer":3,"explanation":"3 格反转需要回落到 110 − 3 = 107。","optionExplanations":["回落幅度不够。","反转需要 3 格。","同一列只能有一种符号。","正确：需要回落到 107。"],"skills":["反转格数"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Point-and-Figure Chart","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pointandfigurechart.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Learn using point and figure charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502276/"}],"stemEn":"Box size 1, three-box reversal. An X column peaks at 110 and price falls back to 108. Does a new O column start?","optionsEn":["Yes: it has fallen","Yes: one box is enough","Draw an O in the X column","No: it fell only 2 boxes, short of 3"],"explanationEn":"A three-box reversal needs a drop to 110 − 3 = 107.","optionExplanationsEn":["The drop is not big enough.","Reversal needs 3 boxes.","A column holds only one symbol type.","Correct: It needs to reach 107."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-161-2","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[161],"stem":"点数图的横轴代表什么？","options":["列的顺序，不是时间","每天一列，代表日期","每一列的成交量大小","每小时一列，代表时间"],"answer":0,"explanation":"点数图只在方向反转时换列，横轴是列的顺序。","optionExplanations":["正确：每列可以跨越不同时间。","时间被去掉了。","与成交量无关。","同样不是时间。"],"skills":["去掉时间"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Point-and-Figure Chart","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pointandfigurechart.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Learn using point and figure charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502276/"}],"stemEn":"What does a point and figure chart’s horizontal axis represent?","optionsEn":["The order of columns, not time","One column per day","Volume","One column per hour"],"explanationEn":"Point and figure starts a new column only on reversals; the axis is the column order.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Each column can span different lengths of time.","Time has been removed.","It is unrelated to volume.","It is not time either."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-161-1","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[161],"stem":"“双顶突破”在点数图上指什么？","options":["K线图上出现两个高点","X 列越过前一 X 列高点","O 列跌破前一个 O 列","两列 X 的高度一样"],"answer":1,"explanation":"X 列超过前一个 X 列的高点，是点数图的双顶突破。","optionExplanations":["这是另一种图。","正确：这是点数图的基本突破信号。","那是双底跌破。","还要越过才算。"],"skills":["点数图信号"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Point-and-Figure Chart","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pointandfigurechart.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Learn using point and figure charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502276/"}],"stemEn":"What is a “double top breakout” on a point and figure chart?","optionsEn":["Two highs on a candlestick chart","The current X column exceeds the prior X column’s highest box","An O column breaks below the prior O column","Two X columns reaching the same height"],"explanationEn":"An X column exceeding the prior X column’s high is a double top breakout.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is a different chart.","Correct: This is the basic breakout signal.","That is a double bottom breakdown.","It must exceed, not just equal."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-161-2","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[161],"stem":"同一段数据，把格值从 1 改成 2，点数图会怎样？","options":["图形完全不变","列会变得更多","符号和列都变少","会出现时间轴"],"answer":2,"explanation":"格值越大，需要更大的价格变化才记录。","optionExplanations":["格值决定记录的粒度。","方向说反了。","正确：格值越大，过滤越多。","点数图没有时间轴。"],"skills":["参数影响"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Point-and-Figure Chart","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pointandfigurechart.asp"},{"title":"TradingView: Learn using point and figure charts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502276/"}],"stemEn":"For the same data, what happens when the box size goes from 1 to 2?","optionsEn":["Nothing changes","There are more columns","Fewer symbols and columns; small swings are filtered","A time axis appears"],"explanationEn":"Bigger boxes need bigger moves to record anything.","optionExplanationsEn":["Box size sets the granularity.","That is reversed.","Correct: Bigger boxes filter more.","There is no time axis."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-162-1","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[162],"stem":"筹码分布显示的“成本集中区”是什么性质的数据？","options":["交易所公布的真实持仓","某一天的成交量","基于换手率等假设的估算","主力账户的成本记录"],"answer":2,"explanation":"筹码分布是按假设推算出来的估算值。","optionExplanations":["交易所不公布这种数据。","它是多日累积并衰减的结果。","正确：它不是真实持仓记录。","无法获得这种数据。"],"skills":["估算性质"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile indicators — basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040/"},{"title":"TradingView script: Position Cost Distribution","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/script/25py1UVB-Position-Cost-Distribution/"}],"stemEn":"What kind of data is the “cost concentration” shown by cost distribution?","optionsEn":["Real holdings published by the exchange","One day’s volume","An estimate based on turnover and other assumptions","The big players’ account records"],"explanationEn":"Cost distribution is an estimate derived from assumptions.","optionExplanationsEn":["Exchanges do not publish this.","It accumulates and decays over many days.","Correct: It is not a record of holdings.","Such data is not available."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-162-2","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[162],"stem":"筹码分布与成交量分布（Volume Profile）最主要的区别是什么？","options":["两者完全是同一个工具","成交量分布需要换手率","筹码分布不使用成交量","前者推算成本，后者只计成交"],"answer":3,"explanation":"成本分布推算谁还持有，成交量分布只统计成交过多少。","optionExplanations":["计算方法不同。","成交量分布不需要。","它以成交量为基础。","正确：两者回答的问题不同。"],"skills":["相近概念"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile indicators — basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040/"},{"title":"TradingView script: Position Cost Distribution","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/script/25py1UVB-Position-Cost-Distribution/"}],"stemEn":"What mainly distinguishes cost distribution from a volume profile?","optionsEn":["They are identical","A volume profile needs turnover","Cost distribution does not use volume","The first infers current holders’ costs; the second only tallies volume"],"explanationEn":"Cost distribution infers who still holds; a volume profile counts what traded.","optionExplanationsEn":["Their methods differ.","It does not.","It is built on volume.","Correct: They answer different questions."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-162-1","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[162],"stem":"某价位 10 天前成交很多，之后换手率很高。两种工具在该价位的显示会怎样不同？","options":["筹码分布衰减明显，成交量分布不变","两者都会衰减","两者都不变","成交量分布衰减，筹码分布不变"],"answer":0,"explanation":"高换手会让筹码分布把旧筹码衰减，成交量分布仍把旧成交算在原价位。","optionExplanations":["正确：衰减只存在于成本分布的假设里。","成交量分布只做统计。","成本分布会衰减旧筹码。","方向说反了。"],"skills":["计算假设"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile indicators — basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040/"},{"title":"TradingView script: Position Cost Distribution","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/script/25py1UVB-Position-Cost-Distribution/"}],"stemEn":"A price traded heavily 10 days ago, followed by high turnover. How will the two tools differ at that price?","optionsEn":["Cost distribution decays it a lot; the volume profile keeps it","Both decay it","Neither changes","The volume profile decays; cost distribution does not"],"explanationEn":"High turnover makes cost distribution decay old chips, while the volume profile still counts the old volume.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Decay exists only in cost distribution’s assumptions.","A volume profile only counts.","Cost distribution decays old chips.","That is reversed."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-162-2","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[162],"stem":"有人说“筹码分布显示主力成本在 50 元，所以价格不会跌破 50”。按本课应怎样回应？","options":["同意，筹码分布是真实数据","只是估算，不能当成支撑保证","应该看成交量分布才准确","价格会在 50 元附近反弹"],"answer":1,"explanation":"筹码分布基于假设，不能证明“主力成本”，更不能保证支撑。","optionExplanations":["它不是真实持仓。","正确：估算不能证明谁的成本在哪。","两者都不能保证支撑。","没有依据。"],"skills":["常见误解"],"references":[{"title":"TradingView: Volume profile indicators — basic concepts","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502040/"},{"title":"TradingView script: Position Cost Distribution","url":"https://www.tradingview.com/script/25py1UVB-Position-Cost-Distribution/"}],"stemEn":"Someone says “cost distribution shows the big players’ cost is 50, so price won’t fall below 50”. How does this lesson respond?","optionsEn":["Agreed; it is real data","It is only an estimated cost zone, not a guaranteed support","Only the volume profile is accurate","Price will bounce at 50 immediately"],"explanationEn":"Cost distribution rests on assumptions; it cannot prove anyone’s cost or guarantee support.","optionExplanationsEn":["It is not real holdings.","Correct: An estimate cannot prove anyone’s cost.","Neither guarantees support.","There is no basis for that."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-163-1","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[163],"stem":"现货 2,000，合约 2,030。按本课口径，基差和溢价率是多少？","options":["基差 −30，溢价率 −1.5%","基差 30，溢价率 1.5%","基差 30，溢价率 3%","基差 2,030，溢价率 101.5%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"基差 = 2,030 − 2,000 = 30，溢价率 = 30 ÷ 2,000 = 1.5%。","optionExplanations":["本课按合约减现货。","正确：30÷2,000=1.5%。","百分比算错了。","基差是差额。"],"skills":["基差计算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Basis","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/basis.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Contango","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/contango.asp"}],"stemEn":"Spot is 2,000 and the future 2,030. Using this lesson’s convention, what are the basis and premium rate?","optionsEn":["Basis −30, premium −1.5%","Basis 30, premium 1.5%","Basis 30, premium 3%","Basis 2,030, premium 101.5%"],"explanationEn":"Basis = 2,030 − 2,000 = 30; premium = 30 ÷ 2,000 = 1.5%.","optionExplanationsEn":["This lesson uses futures minus spot.","Correct: 30÷2,000=1.5%.","The percentage is wrong.","Basis is the difference."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-163-2","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[163],"stem":"交割合约临近到期时，基差通常会怎样？","options":["越来越大","保持不变","逐步收敛，趋近于零","变成资金费率"],"answer":2,"explanation":"到期时合约与现货价格趋于一致，基差趋近于零。","optionExplanations":["到期会迫使价格靠拢。","会随时间变化。","正确：到期时合约按现货交割或结算。","交割合约没有资金费率。"],"skills":["到期收敛"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Basis","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/basis.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Contango","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/contango.asp"}],"stemEn":"What usually happens to a dated future’s basis as expiry approaches?","optionsEn":["It keeps widening","It stays constant","It converges toward zero","It turns into the funding rate"],"explanationEn":"At expiry futures and spot converge, so basis tends to zero.","optionExplanationsEn":["Expiry forces prices together.","It changes over time.","Correct: At expiry the contract settles against spot.","Dated futures have no funding."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-163-1","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[163],"stem":"永续合约没有到期日，靠什么让它的价格贴近现货？","options":["交易所人工调整价格","每天强制交割","成交量越大价格越接近","资金费率：溢价时多头付费"],"answer":3,"explanation":"资金费率让偏离现货的一方付费，从而把价格拉回。","optionExplanations":["不是人工调整。","永续合约不交割。","成交量不是机制。","正确：这是永续合约的核心机制。"],"skills":["资金费率"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Basis","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/basis.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Contango","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/contango.asp"}],"stemEn":"A perpetual has no expiry. What keeps its price near spot?","optionsEn":["The exchange adjusts prices by hand","Daily forced delivery","Higher volume brings it closer","Funding: when at a premium, longs pay shorts"],"explanationEn":"Funding makes the side away from spot pay, pulling the price back.","optionExplanationsEn":["It is not manual.","Perpetuals do not deliver.","Volume is not the mechanism.","Correct: This is the perpetual’s core mechanism."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-163-2","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[163],"stem":"永续合约溢价快速扩大到很高，同时资金费率大幅为正。按本课应怎样理解？","options":["杠杆需求升温，不能单独定方向","这是一个明确的看涨信号","这是一个明确的看跌信号","说明现货价格算错了"],"answer":0,"explanation":"溢价和资金费率反映杠杆需求，可能意味着拥挤，但不是方向信号。","optionExplanations":["正确：本课强调它不是看涨信号。","溢价高也可能意味着拥挤。","同样不能单独推出方向。","价差是正常现象。"],"skills":["常见误解"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Basis","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/basis.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Contango","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/contango.asp"}],"stemEn":"A perpetual’s premium widens rapidly while funding turns strongly positive. How should this be understood?","optionsEn":["Leveraged long demand is rising and may be crowded; it cannot alone predict direction","A clear bullish signal","A clear bearish signal","The spot price is wrong"],"explanationEn":"Premium and funding reflect leverage demand and possible crowding, not direction.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The lesson stresses it is not a bullish signal.","A high premium may mean crowding.","It cannot alone set direction either.","A gap is normal."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-164-1","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[164],"stem":"热力图上的亮色挂单带代表什么？","options":["当时该价位的较多挂单","已经成交的大量交易","会守住的支撑位","交易所公布的目标价"],"answer":0,"explanation":"热力图画的是当时的挂单量，不是成交。","optionExplanations":["正确：它显示的是挂单。","成交量是另一回事。","挂单可以撤。","交易所不公布目标价。"],"skills":["挂单与成交"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Order Book","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/o/order-book.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Depth of Market","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/depth-of-market.asp"}],"stemEn":"What does a bright band on a liquidity heatmap represent?","optionsEn":["More unfilled orders resting at that price at the time","A large amount of executed trading","Support that will hold","A target price published by the exchange"],"explanationEn":"A heatmap plots resting orders at the time, not trades.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: It shows resting orders.","Executed volume is different.","Orders can be pulled.","Exchanges publish no targets."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-164-2","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[164],"stem":"只看一个交易所的盘口深度，主要局限是什么？","options":["这些数据都是假的","只代表一个交易所的局部","盘口只显示成交量","它比全市场更准确"],"answer":1,"explanation":"流动性分散在多个交易所，一个盘口只是局部。","optionExplanations":["数据本身是真实挂单。","正确：加密市场流动性分散。","盘口显示挂单。","局部不可能更全面。"],"skills":["数据范围"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Order Book","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/o/order-book.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Depth of Market","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/depth-of-market.asp"}],"stemEn":"What is the main limitation of looking at one exchange’s order book?","optionsEn":["The data is certainly fake","It shows only part of the market; other exchanges are invisible","You can only see volume","It is more accurate than the whole market"],"explanationEn":"Liquidity is spread across exchanges, so one book is only a part.","optionExplanationsEn":["The data shows real resting orders.","Correct: Crypto liquidity is fragmented.","The book shows resting orders.","Part of the market cannot be more complete."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-164-1","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[164],"stem":"价格接近一条大买单带时，这条带突然消失，价格直接跌穿。最合理的读法是？","options":["挂单全部成交了，支撑很强","热力图软件出错","挂单被撤走，没有形成支撑","之后价格会反弹"],"answer":2,"explanation":"挂单在价格到达前消失，说明是撤单，不是成交支撑。","optionExplanations":["成交会留下成交量与价格反应。","撤单是正常现象。","正确：挂单可撤正是本课强调的局限。","没有依据。"],"skills":["撤单"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Order Book","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/o/order-book.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Depth of Market","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/depth-of-market.asp"}],"stemEn":"As price nears a large bid band, the band suddenly vanishes and price drops through. What is the most reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["All the orders were filled, so support was strong","The heatmap software failed","The orders were pulled and formed no support","Price will bounce afterwards"],"explanationEn":"Orders vanishing before price arrived were cancelled, not filled support.","optionExplanationsEn":["Fills leave volume and a price reaction.","Cancellations are normal.","Correct: Cancellable orders are the lesson’s key limitation.","There is no basis for that."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-164-2","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[164],"stem":"为什么本课说只有真实成交和价格反应才算证据？","options":["盘口的挂单数据不公开","成交量总是比挂单大","价格只由成交量决定","挂单可撤，成交才是真交易"],"answer":3,"explanation":"挂单只表达意图且可撤，成交才是已发生的交易。","optionExplanations":["盘口是公开的。","没有这种关系。","价格由买卖成交决定，但不只看量。","正确：意图与行动的区别。"],"skills":["证据层级"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Order Book","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/o/order-book.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Depth of Market","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/depth-of-market.asp"}],"stemEn":"Why does this lesson say only executed trades and price reaction count as evidence?","optionsEn":["Order data is not public","Volume always exceeds resting size","Price depends only on volume","Orders can be changed at will; only trades show real transactions"],"explanationEn":"Resting orders only express intent and can be cancelled; trades are what actually happened.","optionExplanationsEn":["The book is public.","There is no such relation.","Price comes from trades, not volume alone.","Correct: Intent versus action."]},{"id":"method-beginner-165-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[165],"stem":"新高 80.0 之后，接下来 3 根最高价 79.6、80.2、79.9。80.0 能确认为箱顶吗？","options":["能：大多数没有超过","能：最后一根没超过就行","无法判断，要看成交量","不能：第二根超过了 80.0"],"answer":3,"explanation":"第二根最高 80.2 超过了 80.0，箱顶需要重新寻找。","optionExplanations":["规则要求连续 3 根都没超过。","要看全部 3 根。","规则只看价格。","正确：80.2 > 80.0。"],"skills":["箱顶规则"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Darvas Box Theory","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/darvasboxtheory.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Nicolas Darvas","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Darvas"}],"stemEn":"After a new high of 80.0, the next three highs are 79.6, 80.2 and 79.9. Is 80.0 confirmed as the box top?","optionsEn":["Yes: most did not exceed it","Yes: only the last bar matters","Cannot tell without volume","No: the second bar exceeded 80.0"],"explanationEn":"The second bar’s 80.2 exceeds 80.0, so the top must be found again.","optionExplanationsEn":["All three must fail to exceed it.","All three count.","The rule uses price only.","Correct: 80.2 > 80.0."]},{"id":"method-beginner-165-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[165],"stem":"达瓦斯箱体的向上突破以什么为准？","options":["收盘越过箱顶","最高价碰到箱顶","价格回到箱底","成交量放大"],"answer":0,"explanation":"收盘越过箱顶才算突破。","optionExplanations":["正确：本课的突破定义。","碰到不算越过。","那是箱内运动。","成交量不是突破的定义。"],"skills":["突破定义"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Darvas Box Theory","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/darvasboxtheory.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Nicolas Darvas","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Darvas"}],"stemEn":"What counts as an upside breakout from a Darvas box?","optionsEn":["A close above the box top","The high touching the top","Price returning to the bottom","Volume rising"],"explanationEn":"Only a close above the top is a breakout.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: This lesson’s breakout definition.","Touching is not breaking.","That is movement inside the box.","Volume is not the definition."]},{"id":"method-advanced-165-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[165],"stem":"箱体确认后，价格收盘跌破了箱底。按本课应怎样处理？","options":["把箱底下移到新低，继续沿用","箱体失效","说明之后会向上突破","箱体变成了箱顶"],"answer":1,"explanation":"跌破箱底意味着这个台阶没有守住。","optionExplanations":["随意挪动边界是在迁就价格。","正确：这是本课的失效条件。","没有依据。","规则里没有这种说法。"],"skills":["失效条件"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Darvas Box Theory","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/darvasboxtheory.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Nicolas Darvas","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Darvas"}],"stemEn":"After the box is confirmed, price closes below the bottom. How should this be handled?","optionsEn":["Move the bottom to the new low and carry on","The box is invalidated","An upside breakout is coming","The box becomes a new top"],"explanationEn":"Breaking the bottom means this step did not hold.","optionExplanationsEn":["Moving the boundary fits it to price.","Correct: That is this lesson’s invalidation.","There is no basis for that.","The rules have no such idea."]},{"id":"method-advanced-165-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[165],"stem":"为什么箱顶要等“连续 3 根没超过”才确认，而不是新高出现时就画？","options":["为了让箱子画得更大","新高出现时还没有收盘","有停顿，才知道是不是台阶","3 是一个神奇数字"],"answer":2,"explanation":"没有停顿就没有台阶，箱顶需要后续K线确认。","optionExplanations":["不是为了大小。","这不是规则的理由。","正确：规则用停顿来定义箱顶。","规则的意义在于确认停顿。"],"skills":["确认逻辑"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Darvas Box Theory","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/darvasboxtheory.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Nicolas Darvas","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolas_Darvas"}],"stemEn":"Why must the top wait for three bars that fail to exceed it, instead of being drawn at the new high?","optionsEn":["To make the box bigger","The new high has not closed yet","Only a pause shows whether this is a step at all","Three is a magic number"],"explanationEn":"Without a pause there is no step; the top needs later bars to confirm it.","optionExplanationsEn":["It is not about size.","That is not the reason.","Correct: The rule defines the top by a pause.","The point is confirming the pause."]},{"id":"method-beginner-166-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[166],"stem":"账户 50,000，N（ATR）= 2.0。按“每单位 1 个 N 的波动约等于账户 1%”，一个单位是多少份？","options":["500 份","1,000 份","250 份","25 份"],"answer":2,"explanation":"账户 1% = 500，单位 = 500 ÷ 2.0 = 250 份。","optionExplanations":["忘了除以 N。","用错了百分比。","正确：500÷2.0=250。","计算有误。"],"skills":["ATR 仓位"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Turtle Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/08/turtle-trading.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Donchian Channels","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/donchianchannels.asp"}],"stemEn":"Account 50,000, N (ATR) = 2.0. If a one-N move per unit should equal about 1% of the account, how many shares is one unit?","optionsEn":["500 shares","1,000 shares","250 shares","25 shares"],"explanationEn":"1% of the account = 500, so one unit = 500 ÷ 2.0 = 250 shares.","optionExplanationsEn":["That forgets to divide by N.","The percentage is wrong.","Correct: 500÷2.0=250.","Miscalculated."]},{"id":"method-beginner-166-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[166],"stem":"系统一的入场和离场分别看多少根K线？","options":["入场看 55 根，离场看 20 根","入场看 10 根，离场看 20 根","入场和离场都看 20 根","入场看 20 根最高，离场看 10 根最低"],"answer":3,"explanation":"系统一：20 根突破入场，10 根反向突破离场。","optionExplanations":["那是系统二。","长短说反了。","离场用更短的通道。","正确：这是系统一的规则。"],"skills":["系统规则"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Turtle Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/08/turtle-trading.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Donchian Channels","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/donchianchannels.asp"}],"stemEn":"Which lookbacks does System 1 use for entry and exit?","optionsEn":["Entry on 55 bars, exit on 20","Entry on 10 bars, exit on 20","Both use 20 bars","Entry on the 20-bar high, exit on the 10-bar low"],"explanationEn":"System 1: enter on a 20-bar break, exit on a 10-bar break the other way.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is System 2.","The lengths are reversed.","The exit uses a shorter channel.","Correct: These are System 1’s rules."]},{"id":"method-advanced-166-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[166],"stem":"入场价 60，N = 1.5，按 2N 止损应设在哪里？","options":["57","58.5","63","55.5"],"answer":0,"explanation":"止损 = 60 − 2 × 1.5 = 57。","optionExplanations":["正确：60−2×1.5=57。","只减了 1N。","方向反了。","减了 3N。"],"skills":["止损计算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Turtle Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/08/turtle-trading.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Donchian Channels","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/donchianchannels.asp"}],"stemEn":"Entry is 60 and N = 1.5. Where is the 2N stop?","optionsEn":["57","58.5","63","55.5"],"explanationEn":"Stop = 60 − 2 × 1.5 = 57.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 60−2×1.5=57.","That subtracts only 1N.","Wrong direction.","That subtracts 3N."]},{"id":"method-advanced-166-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[166],"stem":"海龟系统在连续多次假突破中小额亏损，为什么原规则仍要求继续执行？","options":["假突破之后接着是真突破","盈利靠少数大趋势，跳过会错过","亏损次数越多，下次越大","规则禁止任何人修改"],"answer":1,"explanation":"趋势跟踪的盈利集中在少数大行情，事先无法知道是哪一次。","optionExplanations":["没有这种规律。","正确：这是趋势跟踪的特点。","没有依据。","这不是理由本身。"],"skills":["趋势跟踪逻辑"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Turtle Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/08/turtle-trading.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Donchian Channels","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/donchianchannels.asp"}],"stemEn":"The Turtle system takes several small losses on false breakouts. Why do the original rules still require continuing?","optionsEn":["A true breakout always follows false ones","It profits from a few big trends, and skipping signals may miss them","More losses mean a bigger next win","No one is allowed to change the rules"],"explanationEn":"Trend-following profits concentrate in a few big moves, and you cannot know in advance which one.","optionExplanationsEn":["There is no such rule.","Correct: That is the nature of trend following.","There is no basis for that.","That is not the reason itself."]},{"id":"method-beginner-167-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[167],"stem":"三重滤网的第一层（长周期）负责什么？","options":["寻找精确的入场价","确定允许操作的方向","寻找回调","计算仓位"],"answer":1,"explanation":"第一层用趋势指标定方向。","optionExplanations":["入场在第三层。","正确：趋势方向在第一层确定。","回调在第二层。","不是第一层的任务。"],"skills":["分层任务"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Multiple Time Frames","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/07/timeframes.asp"},{"title":"The Right Trader: Triple Screen Trading System","url":"https://therighttrader.com/learn/trend-analysis/triple-screen-trading-system"}],"stemEn":"What is the first screen (long timeframe) responsible for?","optionsEn":["Finding the exact entry price","Setting the direction that is allowed","Finding pullbacks","Sizing the position"],"explanationEn":"The first screen uses a trend indicator to set direction.","optionExplanationsEn":["Entry belongs to the third screen.","Correct: Direction is set on the first screen.","Pullbacks belong to the second screen.","That is not the first screen’s job."]},{"id":"method-beginner-167-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[167],"stem":"三重滤网各层周期之间的比例大约是多少？","options":["约 100 倍","相同周期","约 5 倍","约 1.5 倍"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Elder 建议相邻周期相差约 5 倍。","optionExplanations":["跨度过大。","三层需要不同周期。","正确：例如周线、日线、小时线。","太接近，失去分工。"],"skills":["周期比例"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Multiple Time Frames","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/07/timeframes.asp"},{"title":"The Right Trader: Triple Screen Trading System","url":"https://therighttrader.com/learn/trend-analysis/triple-screen-trading-system"}],"stemEn":"Roughly what ratio separates the screens’ timeframes?","optionsEn":["About 100×","The same timeframe","About 5×","About 1.5×"],"explanationEn":"Elder suggests about 5× between adjacent timeframes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Far too wide.","The screens need different timeframes.","Correct: For example weekly, daily, hourly.","Too close to separate their roles."]},{"id":"method-advanced-167-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[167],"stem":"周线趋势向下，日线振荡指标却显示超卖。按三重滤网应怎样处理？","options":["按日线的超卖信号做多","换成更短周期找做多信号","同时做多和做空两边","不做多：第一层方向向下"],"answer":3,"explanation":"第一层方向向下时，只考虑做空方向，日线超卖不构成做多理由。","optionExplanations":["违背了第一层方向。","这是在绕过过滤。","没有这种规则。","正确：第一层不允许做多。"],"skills":["层级优先"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Multiple Time Frames","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/07/timeframes.asp"},{"title":"The Right Trader: Triple Screen Trading System","url":"https://therighttrader.com/learn/trend-analysis/triple-screen-trading-system"}],"stemEn":"The weekly trend is down, but the daily oscillator shows oversold. What does Triple Screen say?","optionsEn":["Go long on the daily oversold reading","Look for longs on a shorter timeframe","Go both long and short","Do not go long: oversold here only hints at a bounce within a downtrend"],"explanationEn":"With the first screen pointing down, only shorts are considered; a daily oversold reading is no reason to buy.","optionExplanationsEn":["That violates the first screen.","That bypasses the filter.","There is no such rule.","Correct: The first screen does not allow longs."]},{"id":"method-advanced-167-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[167],"stem":"为什么第三层用价格（例如越过前一根高点）而不是再用一个指标来入场？","options":["让价格确认回调结束","指标在小周期上无法计算","价格总是比指标更准","这样可以不设止损"],"answer":0,"explanation":"只有价格越过前高，才说明回调可能结束，避免在下跌中途买入。","optionExplanations":["正确：价格是最直接的确认。","可以计算。","不是“总是”。","仍然需要止损。"],"skills":["入场逻辑"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Multiple Time Frames","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/trading/07/timeframes.asp"},{"title":"The Right Trader: Triple Screen Trading System","url":"https://therighttrader.com/learn/trend-analysis/triple-screen-trading-system"}],"stemEn":"Why does the third screen use price, such as a break above the prior high, rather than another indicator?","optionsEn":["So price itself confirms the pullback has ended, reducing early entries","Indicators cannot be computed on short timeframes","Price is always more accurate","It removes the need for a stop"],"explanationEn":"Only a break above the prior high suggests the pullback may be over, avoiding buying mid-decline.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Price is the most direct confirmation.","They can be.","Not always.","A stop is still needed."]},{"id":"method-beginner-168-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[168],"stem":"MA5 = 20.4、MA10 = 20.8、MA20 = 20.1。这是多头排列吗？","options":["不是：MA5 低于 MA10","是：MA5 高于 MA20","是：三条都在 20 以上","无法判断，要看成交量"],"answer":0,"explanation":"多头排列需要 MA5 > MA10 > MA20，这里 MA5 < MA10。","optionExplanations":["正确：多头排列要求短在最上。","还要高于 MA10。","看的是顺序，不是数值区间。","排列只看均线。"],"skills":["排列顺序"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Moving Average","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/movingaverage.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Golden Cross","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/goldencross.asp"}],"stemEn":"MA5 = 20.4, MA10 = 20.8, MA20 = 20.1. Is this a bullish alignment?","optionsEn":["No: MA5 is below MA10, so the order is wrong","Yes: MA5 is above MA20","Yes: all three are above 20","Cannot tell without volume"],"explanationEn":"Bullish alignment needs MA5 > MA10 > MA20; here MA5 < MA10.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Bullish alignment needs the short average on top.","It must also be above MA10.","Order matters, not the range.","Alignment uses the averages only."]},{"id":"method-beginner-168-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[168],"stem":"除了顺序，本课的多头排列还要求什么？","options":["成交量放大","三条均线都在上升","价格在所有均线下方","均线之间距离相等"],"answer":1,"explanation":"顺序之外，还要三条均线都在上升。","optionExplanations":["定义不含成交量。","正确：这是定义的一部分。","方向说反了。","没有这个要求。"],"skills":["定义要素"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Moving Average","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/movingaverage.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Golden Cross","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/goldencross.asp"}],"stemEn":"Besides the order, what else does bullish alignment require here?","optionsEn":["Rising volume","All three averages rising","Price below all averages","Equal spacing between averages"],"explanationEn":"Besides the order, all three must be rising.","optionExplanationsEn":["The definition excludes volume.","Correct: That is part of the definition.","That is reversed.","There is no such requirement."]},{"id":"method-advanced-168-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[168],"stem":"为什么排列被打破时，价格往往已经离高点有一段距离？","options":["交易所延迟更新均线","均线只在收盘后计算一次","均线由过去价格计算，天然滞后","排列打破时价格正在高点"],"answer":2,"explanation":"均线是过去价格的平均，转向需要新价格把平均值拉下来。","optionExplanations":["均线在本地计算。","任何周期都在计算。","正确：滞后是均线的本性。","与滞后相矛盾。"],"skills":["滞后性"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Moving Average","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/movingaverage.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Golden Cross","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/goldencross.asp"}],"stemEn":"Why is price often well off its high by the time the alignment breaks?","optionsEn":["Exchanges update averages late","Averages are computed once a day","Averages are computed from past prices and naturally lag","Price is always at the high when it breaks"],"explanationEn":"Averages are means of past prices; turning requires new prices to drag them down.","optionExplanationsEn":["Averages are computed locally.","They are computed on every timeframe.","Correct: Lag is inherent.","That contradicts the lag."]},{"id":"method-advanced-168-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[168],"stem":"多头排列已经持续很久，有人说“排列还在，所以会继续涨”。按本课应怎样回应？","options":["同意，排列在就会继续涨","排列越久，越快下跌","应该换成更长的均线证明会涨","排列描述已发生的趋势，不预测未来"],"answer":3,"explanation":"排列只是对过去价格的描述，不能推出之后一定上涨。","optionExplanations":["排列不能保证未来。","也没有依据。","换参数不能预测未来。","正确：本课强调这一点。"],"skills":["常见误解"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Moving Average","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/movingaverage.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Golden Cross","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/goldencross.asp"}],"stemEn":"A bullish alignment has lasted a long time and someone says it will keep rising because the alignment holds. How does this lesson respond?","optionsEn":["Agreed; it rises while the alignment holds","The longer it lasts, the faster it falls","Use longer averages to prove a rise","Alignment describes the trend so far and does not predict"],"explanationEn":"Alignment only describes past prices and cannot show prices will keep rising.","optionExplanationsEn":["It guarantees nothing.","There is no basis for that.","Changing settings predicts nothing.","Correct: This lesson stresses this."]},{"id":"method-beginner-169-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[169],"stem":"最近三个高点 52、52.3、51.9，三个低点 50.1、49.9、50.2。更像趋势还是震荡？","options":["上涨趋势","下跌趋势","无法判断，要看新闻","震荡：高低点没有同向推进"],"answer":3,"explanation":"高低点在固定范围内来回，没有同向推进，是震荡。","optionExplanations":["高点没有持续抬高。","低点没有持续降低。","结构已经能看出来。","正确：高低点都在原地来回。"],"skills":["结构判断"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Trend","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/trend.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Range-Bound Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rangeboundtrading.asp"}],"stemEn":"The last three highs are 52, 52.3 and 51.9, and the lows 50.1, 49.9 and 50.2. Is this more like a trend or a range?","optionsEn":["An uptrend","A downtrend","Cannot tell without news","A range: highs and lows do not advance together"],"explanationEn":"Highs and lows swing within a fixed range without advancing: a range.","optionExplanationsEn":["Highs are not rising persistently.","Lows are not falling persistently.","The structure is enough.","Correct: Highs and lows swing in place."]},{"id":"method-beginner-169-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[169],"stem":"在震荡市里，均线交叉类工具常见的问题是什么？","options":["频繁来回交叉，错误信号多","均线完全不会发生交叉","交叉信号总是很准确","震荡中无法计算均线"],"answer":0,"explanation":"震荡中均线走平，价格反复穿越，交叉信号频繁失效。","optionExplanations":["正确：均线走平时交叉频繁。","震荡中反而交叉更多。","震荡里正好相反。","照样可以计算。"],"skills":["工具适用"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Trend","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/trend.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Range-Bound Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rangeboundtrading.asp"}],"stemEn":"In a ranging market, what is the common problem with moving-average crossover tools?","optionsEn":["They cross back and forth, giving many false signals","They never cross","Crossovers are always accurate","Averages cannot be computed"],"explanationEn":"In ranges averages flatten and price keeps crossing, so crossover signals fail often.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Flat averages cross often.","They cross more in ranges.","The opposite is true in ranges.","They can be computed."]},{"id":"method-advanced-169-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[169],"stem":"强上涨趋势中 RSI 长时间高于 70，有人据此反复做空。按本课问题出在哪？","options":["RSI 计算错了","在趋势里用了震荡市的逆势用法","应该等 RSI 到 90 再做空","在上涨中做空就是错的"],"answer":1,"explanation":"先判断是趋势，就不应把超买当作逆势理由。","optionExplanations":["读数本身没错。","正确：超买在趋势中可以持续很久。","换阈值不能解决用错场合。","问题在场合，不在方向本身。"],"skills":["工具用错场合"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Trend","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/trend.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Range-Bound Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rangeboundtrading.asp"}],"stemEn":"In a strong uptrend RSI stays above 70 for a long time, and someone keeps shorting it. What is the problem under this lesson?","optionsEn":["RSI was miscalculated","Using a range tactic against a trend","Wait for RSI 90 before shorting","Shorting is always wrong"],"explanationEn":"Once it is a trend, overbought is no reason to fade it.","optionExplanationsEn":["The reading is fine.","Correct: Overbought can last long in trends.","A new threshold does not fix the misuse.","The issue is context, not direction."]},{"id":"method-advanced-169-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[169],"stem":"ADX 读数 15，但最近高低点已开始同向抬高。最合理的判断是？","options":["ADX 低于 20，就是震荡","高低点抬高说明 ADX 算错了","可能正转向趋势，以结构为主","应该忽略价格结构"],"answer":2,"explanation":"ADX 反映的是已经发生的趋势强度，转换初期常滞后于结构变化。","optionExplanations":["阈值只是经验参考。","两者可以暂时不一致。","正确：ADX 有滞后。","本课以结构为主。"],"skills":["结构与指标"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Trend","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/trend.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Range-Bound Trading","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/rangeboundtrading.asp"}],"stemEn":"ADX reads 15, but the latest highs and lows have started rising together. What is the most reasonable judgement?","optionsEn":["ADX under 20 means a range","Rising highs and lows mean ADX is wrong","It may be shifting from range to trend; lead with structure, use the indicator as support","Ignore the price structure"],"explanationEn":"ADX reflects trend strength already present and often lags structural change early on.","optionExplanationsEn":["The threshold is only a rule of thumb.","They can disagree for a while.","Correct: ADX lags.","This lesson leads with structure."]},{"id":"method-beginner-170-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[170],"stem":"在 50 买入，失效点定在 48.5。账户 20,000，单笔最多亏 1%。不计滑点，最多买多少股？","options":["400 股：20,000 ÷ 50","4 股：200 ÷ 50","约 133 股：200 ÷ 1.5","200 股：亏损额就是股数"],"answer":2,"explanation":"可亏 20,000 × 1% = 200，单位风险 50 − 48.5 = 1.5，200 ÷ 1.5 ≈ 133 股。","optionExplanations":["这是全仓股数，没考虑止损。","应除以单位风险，不是股价。","正确：单位风险 1.5，可亏 200。","金额与股数是两回事。"],"skills":["仓位计算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stop-Loss Order","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stop-lossorder.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Trailing Stop","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/trailingstop.asp"}],"stemEn":"You buy at 50 with the invalidation at 48.5. With a 20,000 account risking at most 1% per trade and ignoring slippage, how many shares at most?","optionsEn":["400 shares: 20,000 ÷ 50","4 shares: 200 ÷ 50","About 133 shares: 200 ÷ 1.5","200 shares: the loss equals shares"],"explanationEn":"Allowed loss is 20,000 × 1% = 200; unit risk is 50 − 48.5 = 1.5; 200 ÷ 1.5 ≈ 133 shares.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is the full-account size, ignoring the stop.","Divide by unit risk, not by price.","Correct: Unit risk is 1.5 and the allowed loss is 200.","Money and share count are different things."]},{"id":"method-beginner-170-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[170],"stem":"价格跌到止损位附近，你想“再等等，也许会弹回来”，于是把止损往下挪。按本课这属于什么？","options":["给亏损留出空间的灵活调整","正确做法，因为止损经常被扫","与止损无关，只是换了目标价","临时挪远止损，让小亏可能变成大亏"],"answer":3,"explanation":"失效条件应在开仓前定好；盘中因不愿亏而挪远，是小亏变大亏的典型路径。","optionExplanations":["这是推迟认错。","被扫不是挪远的理由。","改的是止损，不是目标。","正确：计划之外的挪远就是放弃止损。"],"skills":["纪律"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stop-Loss Order","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stop-lossorder.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Trailing Stop","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/trailingstop.asp"}],"stemEn":"Price nears your stop and you think “wait, it may bounce,” so you move the stop lower. Under this lesson, what is this?","optionsEn":["A flexible adjustment that gives the loss room","Correct, because stops often get hit","Unrelated to the stop; only the target changed","Moving the stop away mid-trade, letting a small loss grow"],"explanationEn":"The invalidation should be set before entry; moving it away mid-trade to avoid a loss is the typical route from small to large losses.","optionExplanationsEn":["This is delaying the admission of error.","Getting hit is no reason to move it away.","It is the stop that changed, not the target.","Correct: Moving it away outside the plan abandons the stop."]},{"id":"method-advanced-170-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[170],"stem":"你在 100 止损卖出，之后价格重新站上 102 并满足你原来的入场条件。较合理的做法是？","options":["按新的入场与失效条件，把它当成新交易","不再碰它，因为已经错过一次","在 100 以下挂单，等回到卖出价再买","加倍买入，把上一笔的亏损赚回来"],"answer":0,"explanation":"止损后再进场不必有心理负担，但要按新条件重新计算风险，而不是为了追回上一笔。","optionExplanations":["正确：与上一笔的盈亏无关。","止损后的新信号可以重新评估。","价格不欠你一个回到原价的机会。","这是追回亏损的冲动。"],"skills":["重新进场"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stop-Loss Order","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stop-lossorder.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Trailing Stop","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/trailingstop.asp"}],"stemEn":"You stopped out at 100; later price climbs back above 102 and meets your original entry conditions. What is the more reasonable approach?","optionsEn":["Treat it as a new trade with fresh entry and invalidation","Never touch it again, since you were wrong once","Bid below 100 and wait for your sale price","Buy double to win back the last loss"],"explanationEn":"Re-entering after a stop is fine, but recompute risk under new conditions rather than trying to win back the last trade.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: It is independent of the previous trade’s result.","A new signal after a stop can be re-evaluated.","Price owes you no return to your old level.","That is the urge to recover a loss."]},{"id":"method-advanced-170-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[170],"stem":"止损价 48.5，但次日开盘跳空到 47.8，你在 47.8 成交。下面哪项正确？","options":["止损单失效了，平台应补偿差价","止损价不保证成交价，跳空会产生滑点","说明止损设得太远，应该更近","应改用限价止损，就不会亏损"],"answer":1,"explanation":"止损单触发后变为市价单，跳空时成交价可能明显差于止损价；计算仓位时要为此留余量。","optionExplanations":["止损触发后按市场价成交。","正确：这是止损单的已知局限。","跳空与距离远近无关。","限价可能根本不成交，亏损继续。"],"skills":["滑点"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stop-Loss Order","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stop-lossorder.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Trailing Stop","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/t/trailingstop.asp"}],"stemEn":"Your stop is 48.5, but the next open gaps to 47.8 and you fill at 47.8. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["The stop failed, so the platform owes you the gap","A stop price does not guarantee the fill; gaps cause slippage","The stop was too far and should be closer","Use a stop-limit and you cannot lose"],"explanationEn":"A stop becomes a market order once triggered, so a gap can fill well below the stop; leave room for this when sizing.","optionExplanationsEn":["Once triggered, a stop fills at market.","Correct: This is a known limit of stop orders.","The gap has nothing to do with stop distance.","A limit may not fill at all, and the loss continues."]},{"id":"method-beginner-171-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[171],"stem":"10 元买 100 股，跌到 8 元再买 100 股。平均成本是多少？","options":["8 元","9 元","10 元","18 元"],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均成本 = 总投入 ÷ 总股数 = (1,000 + 800) ÷ 200 = 9 元。","optionExplanations":["只看了第二笔。","正确：(1,000 + 800) ÷ 200 = 9。","只看了第一笔。","把两个价格相加了。"],"skills":["平均成本"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Pyramiding","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pyramiding.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Martingale (betting system)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martingale_(betting_system)"}],"stemEn":"You buy 100 shares at 10 and another 100 at 8. What is the average cost?","optionsEn":["8","9","10","18"],"explanationEn":"Average cost = total spent ÷ total shares = (1,000 + 800) ÷ 200 = 9.","optionExplanationsEn":["This uses only the second buy.","Correct: (1,000 + 800) ÷ 200 = 9.","This uses only the first buy.","This adds the two prices."]},{"id":"method-beginner-171-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[171],"stem":"接上题，若价格继续跌到 7 元，补仓后的总亏损与不补仓相比怎样？","options":["补仓后亏 200，比不补仓更少","两者相同，都是 300","补仓后亏 400，不补仓亏 300","补仓后不算亏损，因为成本降低了"],"answer":2,"explanation":"补仓让成本降低，但股数翻倍；价格继续跌时总亏损更大。","optionExplanations":["平均成本下降不等于亏得更少。","补仓多了 100 股。","正确：200 × (9 − 7) = 400；100 × (10 − 7) = 300。","价格低于成本就是亏损。"],"skills":["总风险"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Pyramiding","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pyramiding.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Martingale (betting system)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martingale_(betting_system)"}],"stemEn":"Continuing, if price falls to 7, how does the total loss with the extra buy compare with not adding?","optionsEn":["With the add: 200, less than without","The same, 300 each","With the add: 400; without: 300","No loss after adding, since cost fell"],"explanationEn":"Averaging lowers the cost but doubles the shares; if price keeps falling, the total loss is larger.","optionExplanationsEn":["A lower average cost does not mean a smaller loss.","The add brought 100 more shares.","Correct: 200 × (9 − 7) = 400; 100 × (10 − 7) = 300.","Price below cost is a loss."]},{"id":"method-advanced-171-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[171],"stem":"100 买 100 股，涨到 110 加 50 股，并把止损从 95 上移到 104。若触发止损，这两笔合计盈亏约是多少？","options":["亏 1,500","盈利 1,000","亏 300，只看加仓那笔","盈利约 100"],"answer":3,"explanation":"第一笔 100 × (104 − 100) = 400，加仓 50 × (104 − 110) = −300，合计约 +100；上移止损后，加仓不会把整笔交易变成亏损。","optionExplanations":["这是按旧止损 95 的算法。","没扣除加仓那笔的亏损。","要合计两笔。","正确：100 × 4 − 50 × 6 = 400 − 300 = 100。"],"skills":["金字塔加仓"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Pyramiding","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pyramiding.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Martingale (betting system)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martingale_(betting_system)"}],"stemEn":"You buy 100 at 100, add 50 at 110, and raise the stop from 95 to 104. If the stop is hit, what is the combined result, roughly?","optionsEn":["A loss of 1,500","A gain of 1,000","A loss of 300, counting only the add","A gain of about 100"],"explanationEn":"First lot 100 × (104 − 100) = 400; added lot 50 × (104 − 110) = −300; total about +100. With the raised stop, the add cannot turn the whole trade into a loss.","optionExplanationsEn":["That uses the old stop at 95.","This ignores the loss on the added lot.","Both lots must be combined.","Correct: 100 × 4 − 50 × 6 = 400 − 300 = 100."]},{"id":"method-advanced-171-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[171],"stem":"持仓已经跌破开仓时写下的失效价，你想再买一些把成本拉低。按本课应先做什么？","options":["先按计划止损，再重新评估","先补仓，等反弹再一起卖","把失效价下移，给补仓留空间","补仓的数量加倍，更快回本"],"answer":0,"explanation":"失效条件出现说明原判断已被否定，应先执行止损；若之后出现新条件，再按新交易处理。","optionExplanations":["正确：失效条件已经出现。","这是在被否定的判断上加码。","这是挪远止损。","这就是马丁格尔式加倍。"],"skills":["纪律"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Pyramiding","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pyramiding.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Martingale (betting system)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martingale_(betting_system)"}],"stemEn":"Price has broken the invalidation you wrote at entry, and you want to buy more to lower the cost. Under this lesson, what comes first?","optionsEn":["Exit as planned first, then reassess","Average down first and sell together on a bounce","Lower the invalidation to make room","Double the add to break even faster"],"explanationEn":"The invalidation shows the original idea has been rejected, so exit first; treat any later setup as a new trade.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The invalidation has occurred.","That raises the bet on a rejected idea.","That is moving the stop away.","That is martingale-style doubling."]},{"id":"method-beginner-172-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[172],"stem":"胜率 40%，平均盈利 2.5，平均亏损 1。每笔期望值是多少？","options":["0.4","1.0","−0.2","1.5"],"answer":0,"explanation":"0.4 × 2.5 − 0.6 × 1 = 1.0 − 0.6 = 0.4。","optionExplanations":["正确：0.4 × 2.5 − 0.6 × 1 = 0.4。","忘了减去亏损部分。","把胜率和败率代反了。","把盈利减亏损当成了期望值。"],"skills":["期望值计算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Expected Value","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/expected-value.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Win/Loss Ratio","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/win-loss-ratio.asp"}],"stemEn":"Win rate 40%, average win 2.5, average loss 1. What is the expectancy per trade?","optionsEn":["0.4","1.0","−0.2","1.5"],"explanationEn":"0.4 × 2.5 − 0.6 × 1 = 1.0 − 0.6 = 0.4.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 0.4 × 2.5 − 0.6 × 1 = 0.4.","This forgets to subtract the losses.","The win and loss rates are swapped.","This takes win minus loss as expectancy."]},{"id":"method-beginner-172-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[172],"stem":"盈亏比为 3（平均盈利是平均亏损的 3 倍）。不亏不赚需要的胜率约是多少？","options":["75%","25%","33%","50%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"不亏不赚胜率 = 1 ÷ (1 + 盈亏比) = 1 ÷ 4 = 25%。","optionExplanations":["这是 3 ÷ 4，写反了。","正确：1 ÷ (1 + 3) = 25%。","这是 1 ÷ 3，分母少了 1。","只有盈亏比为 1 时才是 50%。"],"skills":["盈亏比"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Expected Value","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/expected-value.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Win/Loss Ratio","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/win-loss-ratio.asp"}],"stemEn":"The payoff ratio is 3 (the average win is three times the average loss). What win rate breaks even, roughly?","optionsEn":["75%","25%","33%","50%"],"explanationEn":"Break-even win rate = 1 ÷ (1 + payoff ratio) = 1 ÷ 4 = 25%.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is 3 ÷ 4, inverted.","Correct: 1 ÷ (1 + 3) = 25%.","That is 1 ÷ 3; the denominator is missing the 1.","That holds only for a payoff ratio of 1."]},{"id":"method-advanced-172-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[172],"stem":"某人胜率 85%，平均盈利 1，平均亏损 7。下面哪项正确？","options":["胜率这么高，长期会赚钱","期望值约 +0.85，只看胜率即可","期望值约 −0.2，长期平均每笔亏钱","无法计算，需要知道交易次数"],"answer":2,"explanation":"0.85 × 1 − 0.15 × 7 = 0.85 − 1.05 = −0.2；高胜率加上大额亏损，平均每笔仍然亏钱。","optionExplanations":["期望值是负的。","漏掉了亏损部分。","正确：0.85 × 1 − 0.15 × 7 = −0.2。","期望值是每笔平均，不需要次数。"],"skills":["胜率陷阱"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Expected Value","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/expected-value.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Win/Loss Ratio","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/win-loss-ratio.asp"}],"stemEn":"A trader wins 85% of the time, with an average win of 1 and an average loss of 7. Which is correct?","optionsEn":["With such a high win rate, profits follow","Expectancy about +0.85; win rate is enough","Expectancy about −0.2; the average trade loses","Cannot tell without the number of trades"],"explanationEn":"0.85 × 1 − 0.15 × 7 = 0.85 − 1.05 = −0.2; a high win rate with large losses still loses on average.","optionExplanationsEn":["The expectancy is negative.","This omits the losses.","Correct: 0.85 × 1 − 0.15 × 7 = −0.2.","Expectancy is per trade and needs no count."]},{"id":"method-advanced-172-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[172],"stem":"你习惯盈利 1 就立刻卖出，亏损时却拖到亏 3 才卖，胜率 70%。按本课这种习惯的问题是什么？","options":["没有问题，70% 的胜率已经很好","只要把胜率提高到 75% 就会赚钱","问题在交易次数太少，与盈亏无关","期望值约 −0.2，小盈大亏把结果拖成负数"],"answer":3,"explanation":"0.7 × 1 − 0.3 × 3 = −0.2；急着锁盈、拖着亏损，是很多人胜率不低却亏钱的原因。","optionExplanations":["要看期望值，而不是胜率。","0.75 − 0.75 = 0，仍然不赚。","问题在盈亏的大小结构。","正确：0.7 × 1 − 0.3 × 3 = −0.2。"],"skills":["处置效应"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Expected Value","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/expected-value.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Win/Loss Ratio","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/w/win-loss-ratio.asp"}],"stemEn":"You sell as soon as you are up 1, but hold losers until down 3, with a 70% win rate. Under this lesson, what is the problem?","optionsEn":["None; a 70% win rate is good","Raising the win rate to 75% makes it profitable","Too few trades; size is irrelevant","Expectancy about −0.2: small wins and big losses turn it negative"],"explanationEn":"0.7 × 1 − 0.3 × 3 = −0.2; rushing to bank gains while holding losers is why many decent win rates still lose.","optionExplanationsEn":["Judge by expectancy, not win rate.","0.75 − 0.75 = 0, still no profit.","The issue is the size of wins versus losses.","Correct: 0.7 × 1 − 0.3 × 3 = −0.2."]},{"id":"method-beginner-173-1","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[173],"stem":"某股票连续 6 天上涨，你觉得“涨这么多，明天该跌了”而做空。这最接近哪种偏差？","options":["处置效应","损失厌恶","事后诸葛亮","赌徒谬误"],"answer":3,"explanation":"把连续上涨当成“该反转”的理由，就是期待短序列也要胜负守恒。","optionExplanations":["那是关于何时卖出持仓。","这里没有比较盈亏的感受。","这是事前判断，不是事后解释。","正确：以为连涨之后“该轮到跌”。"],"skills":["赌徒谬误"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Gambler’s Fallacy","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gamblersfallacy.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Loss Aversion","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/loss-psychology.asp"}],"stemEn":"A stock has risen six days in a row and you short it because “after so much, tomorrow it should fall.” Which bias is closest?","optionsEn":["The disposition effect","Loss aversion","Hindsight bias","The gambler’s fallacy"],"explanationEn":"Treating a run of gains as a reason for a reversal expects short sequences to even out.","optionExplanationsEn":["That concerns when to sell holdings.","No comparison of gain and loss feelings here.","This is a forecast, not an explanation afterwards.","Correct: Thinking a fall is due after a run of gains."]},{"id":"method-beginner-173-2","type":"method","level":"beginner","topicIds":[173],"stem":"你持有两只股票：一只浮盈 10%，一只浮亏 20%。你卖掉盈利的、留着亏损的“等回本”。这最接近哪种偏差？","options":["处置效应","锚定","赌徒谬误","事后诸葛亮"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Shefrin 与 Statman 把这种“卖出赢家、留住输家”的倾向称为处置效应。","optionExplanations":["正确：太早卖盈利、太久留亏损。","这里更直接的是卖赢留亏。","不涉及对连续序列的预期。","这里没有事后解释。"],"skills":["处置效应"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Gambler’s Fallacy","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gamblersfallacy.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Loss Aversion","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/loss-psychology.asp"}],"stemEn":"You hold two stocks, one up 10% and one down 20%. You sell the winner and keep the loser to “wait for break-even.” Which bias is closest?","optionsEn":["The disposition effect","Anchoring","The gambler’s fallacy","Hindsight bias"],"explanationEn":"Shefrin and Statman called this tendency to sell winners and keep losers the disposition effect.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Selling winners early, holding losers long.","The direct pattern is selling winners and keeping losers.","No expectation about a sequence is involved.","There is no after-the-fact explanation."]},{"id":"method-advanced-173-1","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[173],"stem":"收盘后新闻写道：“因为美元走强，某股票今天大跌。”按本课较稳妥的读法是？","options":["这就是下跌原因，以后美元走强就做空","这是事后解释，可能只是众多因素之一","新闻说的是错的，应该反着做","美元与股价无关，可以忽略"],"answer":1,"explanation":"媒体常把当天发生的事拼成因果；习思cis在书中举过自己大额卖出却被解读成其他原因的例子。","optionExplanations":["事后解释未必是真正原因。","正确：实际下跌可能来自别的大额卖单。","反着做同样没有依据。","汇率可能有影响，只是不能确定。"],"skills":["事后诸葛亮"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Gambler’s Fallacy","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gamblersfallacy.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Loss Aversion","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/loss-psychology.asp"}],"stemEn":"After the close a headline says a stock “fell sharply today because the dollar strengthened.” Under this lesson, what is the more careful reading?","optionsEn":["That is the cause; short it whenever the dollar rises","An explanation written afterwards; perhaps one of many factors","The news is wrong, so do the opposite","The dollar is unrelated to stocks; ignore it"],"explanationEn":"Media often stitch the day’s events into a cause; cis recounts his own large sales being explained as something else entirely.","optionExplanationsEn":["An explanation afterwards may not be the real cause.","Correct: The fall may have come from other large selling.","Doing the opposite has no basis either.","It may matter; it just cannot be confirmed."]},{"id":"method-advanced-173-2","type":"method","level":"advanced","topicIds":[173],"stem":"连续亏了三笔后，你想“下一笔加大仓位，一次赚回来”。较合理的做法是？","options":["照做，连亏之后赢的概率更高","改为加倍仓位，直到赢一次为止","按原来的仓位规则，必要时先暂停复盘","把止损取消，给交易更多空间"],"answer":2,"explanation":"连亏后加仓既有赌徒谬误，也有想翻本的情绪；按既定规则执行、先复盘原因更稳妥。","optionExplanations":["每笔结果彼此独立。","这就是马丁格尔式加倍。","正确：追回亏损的冲动会放大风险。","这会让亏损失去上限。"],"skills":["情绪管理"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Gambler’s Fallacy","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/g/gamblersfallacy.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Loss Aversion","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/loss-psychology.asp"}],"stemEn":"After three losses in a row you want to “size up the next trade and win it all back.” What is the more reasonable approach?","optionsEn":["Do it; after losses a win is more likely","Double up until one trade wins","Keep the usual sizing rule and pause to review if needed","Remove the stop to give the trade room"],"explanationEn":"Sizing up after losses combines the gambler’s fallacy with the urge to break even; sticking to the rule and reviewing first is more careful.","optionExplanationsEn":["Each trade’s result is independent.","That is martingale-style doubling.","Correct: The urge to win back losses magnifies risk.","That removes the cap on losses."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-174-1","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[174],"stem":"卖一 20.00 有 500 股，卖二 20.05 有 500 股。市价买 800 股，平均成交价约是多少？","options":["20.00","20.05","约 20.02","约 20.03"],"answer":2,"explanation":"(10,000 + 6,015) ÷ 800 = 20.019，约 20.02。","optionExplanations":["只有前 500 股是这个价。","只有后 300 股是这个价。","正确：(500 × 20 + 300 × 20.05) ÷ 800 ≈ 20.019。","这是两档价格的简单平均。"],"skills":["冲击成本"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Liquidity","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/liquidity.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Slippage","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/slippage.asp"}],"stemEn":"The best ask has 500 shares at 20.00 and the next 500 at 20.05. A market buy of 800 shares averages roughly what?","optionsEn":["20.00","20.05","About 20.02","About 20.03"],"explanationEn":"(10,000 + 6,015) ÷ 800 = 20.019, about 20.02.","optionExplanationsEn":["Only the first 500 fill there.","Only the last 300 fill there.","Correct: (500 × 20 + 300 × 20.05) ÷ 800 ≈ 20.019.","That is the simple average of the two prices."]},{"id":"tool-beginner-174-2","type":"tool","level":"beginner","topicIds":[174],"stem":"下面哪种情况通常意味着流动性更差？","options":["买卖价差很窄，盘口每档挂单很多","当天成交量远高于平时","价格波动很小，K线实体很短","买卖价差很宽，盘口挂单稀少"],"answer":3,"explanation":"价差宽、挂单薄，说明同样数量需要付出更大的价格代价才能成交。","optionExplanations":["这是流动性好的特征。","成交活跃通常流动性较好。","波动小不等于流动性差。","正确：小单也可能明显推动价格。"],"skills":["流动性"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Liquidity","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/liquidity.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Slippage","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/slippage.asp"}],"stemEn":"Which situation usually indicates poorer liquidity?","optionsEn":["A narrow spread and large size on every level","Volume far above normal","Small moves and short candle bodies","A wide spread and thin size on the book"],"explanationEn":"A wide spread and thin book mean the same quantity costs more price to fill.","optionExplanationsEn":["These are signs of good liquidity.","Active trading usually means better liquidity.","Low volatility is not poor liquidity.","Correct: Even small orders may move the price."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-174-1","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[174],"stem":"你想在一只日均成交额很小的股票上一次买入相当于半天成交额的数量。较稳妥的做法是？","options":["分批用限价单，接受可能买不满","用市价单一次买完，避免错过","等收盘前最后一分钟集中买入","只要价格低就不用考虑冲击"],"answer":0,"explanation":"订单越大、品种越冷门，冲击越大；拆单与限价是常见的控制方法，代价是可能成交不完。","optionExplanations":["正确：用时间换价格。","会一路吃掉更差的挂单。","临近收盘流动性未必更好。","冲击与数量相对成交量有关。"],"skills":["下单方式"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Liquidity","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/liquidity.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Slippage","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/slippage.asp"}],"stemEn":"You want to buy, in one go, half a day’s turnover in a thinly traded stock. What is the more careful approach?","optionsEn":["Work it with limit orders in batches, accepting a partial fill","One market order to avoid missing out","Buy it all in the final minute","Impact does not matter if the price is low"],"explanationEn":"The larger the order and the thinner the stock, the larger the impact; splitting and using limits is the usual control, at the cost of a possible partial fill.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Trade time for price.","It would eat through ever worse orders.","Liquidity near the close is not necessarily better.","Impact depends on size relative to volume."]},{"id":"tool-advanced-174-2","type":"tool","level":"advanced","topicIds":[174],"stem":"一位大户从 1,000 开始买入，买完时价格已到 1,100，平均成本 1,060。相对于开始时的价格，他的冲击成本约是多少？","options":["约 10%，按最后的价格算","约 6%，(1,060 − 1,000) ÷ 1,000","0，因为价格涨了他也赚了","约 4%，(1,100 − 1,060) ÷ 1,000"],"answer":1,"explanation":"(1,060 − 1,000) ÷ 1,000 = 6%；习思cis在书中用这个例子说明大单本身就很赔钱。","optionExplanations":["冲击要看平均成交价。","正确：平均价比起点高 60。","涨价是他推动的，成本已经付出。","这是平均价与终点之差。"],"skills":["冲击成本"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Liquidity","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/liquidity.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Slippage","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/slippage.asp"}],"stemEn":"A large trader starts buying at 1,000; by the end price is 1,100 and his average cost is 1,060. Relative to the starting price, what is his impact cost, roughly?","optionsEn":["About 10%, using the final price","About 6%: (1,060 − 1,000) ÷ 1,000","Zero, because price rose and he profited","About 4%: (1,100 − 1,060) ÷ 1,000"],"explanationEn":"(1,060 − 1,000) ÷ 1,000 = 6%; cis uses this example to show that large orders are costly in themselves.","optionExplanationsEn":["Impact uses the average fill.","Correct: The average is 60 above the start.","He pushed the price up and paid for it.","That is the gap from the end price."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-175-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[175],"stem":"A 公司股价 200 元、总股本 1 亿股；B 公司股价 5 元、总股本 100 亿股。哪家公司总市值更大？","options":["A，因为它的股价更高","B，市值约 500 亿","一样大，因为都是上市公司","无法比较，股价不同"],"answer":1,"explanation":"市值 = 股价 × 总股本：B 为 500 亿，A 为 200 亿。","optionExplanations":["股价高不代表市值大。","正确：5 × 100 亿 = 500 亿；200 × 1 亿 = 200 亿。","上市与否不决定市值。","市值正是用来比较的。"],"skills":["市值"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stock","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stock.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Market Capitalization","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketcapitalization.asp"}],"stemEn":"Company A trades at 200 with 100 million shares; company B trades at 5 with 10 billion shares. Which has the larger market cap?","optionsEn":["A, because its price is higher","B: 50 billion versus A’s 20 billion","The same, since both are listed","Cannot compare with different prices"],"explanationEn":"Market cap = price × shares: B is 50 billion, A is 20 billion.","optionExplanationsEn":["A higher price does not mean a larger cap.","Correct: 5 × 10 billion = 50 billion; 200 × 100 million = 20 billion.","Listing does not set market cap.","Market cap exists for exactly this."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-175-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[175],"stem":"持有某公司股票，下面哪项描述正确？","options":["公司每年都会按约定利率付利息","只要不卖出就不会亏损","你是股东，分享利润也承担亏损风险","公司破产时股东最先拿回本金"],"answer":2,"explanation":"股票是所有权凭证，分红不是固定利息，破产清偿时股东排在最后。","optionExplanations":["那是债券的特征。","账面价值照样会下跌。","正确：股票代表所有权。","股东排在债权人之后。"],"skills":["股东权利"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stock","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stock.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Market Capitalization","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketcapitalization.asp"}],"stemEn":"Which is true of holding a company’s shares?","optionsEn":["The company pays interest at an agreed rate","You cannot lose as long as you do not sell","You are a shareholder, sharing profits and the risk of loss","Shareholders are repaid first in bankruptcy"],"explanationEn":"Shares are ownership; dividends are not fixed interest, and shareholders are paid last in bankruptcy.","optionExplanationsEn":["That describes bonds.","The value still falls on paper.","Correct: Shares represent ownership.","Shareholders rank behind creditors."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-175-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[175],"stem":"某股票从 2 元涨到 4 元，另一只从 200 元涨到 300 元。哪只涨幅更大？","options":["200 元那只，涨了 100 元","一样，都涨了一倍","无法比较，股价差太多","2 元那只，涨了 100%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"涨幅 = 涨的金额 ÷ 起点价格；低价股涨同样的百分比所需金额更小。","optionExplanations":["要看百分比，不是金额。","300 不是 200 的两倍。","百分比可以直接比较。","正确：(4 − 2) ÷ 2 = 100%；(300 − 200) ÷ 200 = 50%。"],"skills":["涨跌幅"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stock","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stock.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Market Capitalization","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketcapitalization.asp"}],"stemEn":"One stock rises from 2 to 4, another from 200 to 300. Which rose more in percentage terms?","optionsEn":["The 200 one, up 100","The same; both doubled","Cannot compare such different prices","The 2 one, up 100%"],"explanationEn":"Percentage change = amount gained ÷ starting price.","optionExplanationsEn":["Compare percentages, not amounts.","300 is not double 200.","Percentages compare directly.","Correct: (4 − 2) ÷ 2 = 100%; (300 − 200) ÷ 200 = 50%."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-175-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[175],"stem":"公司宣布 1 拆 2（每 1 股变成 2 股），拆股前股价 100 元。不考虑其他因素，拆股后会怎样？","options":["股价约 50 元，你的股数翻倍，总价值不变","股价仍是 100 元，你的资产翻倍","股价约 50 元，你的资产减半","公司总市值翻倍"],"answer":0,"explanation":"拆股后股数 × 股价不变：200 股 × 50 = 100 股 × 100。","optionExplanations":["正确：只是把同一块蛋糕切得更小。","拆股不创造价值。","股数同时翻倍。","股价减半抵消了股数翻倍。"],"skills":["拆股"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stock","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stock.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Market Capitalization","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketcapitalization.asp"}],"stemEn":"A company announces a 2-for-1 split; the price is 100 before the split. Ignoring other factors, what happens?","optionsEn":["The price is about 50, your shares double, total value unchanged","The price stays 100 and your wealth doubles","The price is about 50 and your wealth halves","The company’s market cap doubles"],"explanationEn":"After a split, shares × price is unchanged: 200 × 50 = 100 × 100.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The same cake is cut into smaller slices.","A split creates no value.","Your share count also doubles.","The halved price offsets the doubled count."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-176-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[176],"stem":"你在 A 股周二上午买入一只股票，周二下午想卖出。按 T+1 规则会怎样？","options":["不能卖出，最早周三才能卖","可以卖出，只要价格变了","可以卖出，但要多付印花税","要等一周后才能卖出"],"answer":0,"explanation":"A 股 T+1：当日买入，下一个交易日起才能卖出。","optionExplanations":["正确：当天买入的股票下一个交易日可卖。","T+1 限制当天卖出。","规则不是靠付费解除的。","是下一个交易日。"],"skills":["交易规则"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Stock Market Circuit Breakers","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/glossary/stock-market-circuit-breakers"},{"title":"Investopedia: Broker","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/broker.asp"}],"stemEn":"You buy an A-share on Tuesday morning and want to sell Tuesday afternoon. Under T+1, what happens?","optionsEn":["You cannot; the earliest is Wednesday","You can sell as long as the price changed","You can, but pay extra stamp duty","You must wait a week"],"explanationEn":"A-shares are T+1: bought today, sellable from the next trading day.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Shares bought today can be sold next trading day.","T+1 blocks same-day selling.","Paying more does not lift the rule.","It is the next trading day."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-176-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[176],"stem":"下面哪个市场通常是一天 24 小时、周末也在交易？","options":["美股常规交易时段","主流加密资产交易所","A 股","港股"],"answer":1,"explanation":"加密资产交易所多数 24/7 运行，股票市场有固定交易时段。","optionExplanations":["美东 9:30–16:00。","正确：多为全天候交易。","有固定的交易时段。","有固定交易时段与午休。"],"skills":["交易时间"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Stock Market Circuit Breakers","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/glossary/stock-market-circuit-breakers"},{"title":"Investopedia: Broker","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/broker.asp"}],"stemEn":"Which market usually trades 24 hours a day, weekends included?","optionsEn":["US regular trading hours","Major crypto exchanges","A-shares","Hong Kong stocks"],"explanationEn":"Most crypto exchanges run 24/7, while stock markets have fixed sessions.","optionExplanationsEn":["9:30–16:00 Eastern.","Correct: Most trade around the clock.","They have fixed sessions.","Fixed sessions with a lunch break."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-176-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[176],"stem":"A 股某主板股票昨收 20.00 元，涨跌幅限制 10%。今天理论上的最高成交价是多少？","options":["20.20 元","30.00 元","22.00 元","没有上限"],"answer":2,"explanation":"涨停价 = 昨收 × (1 + 10%) = 22.00 元。","optionExplanations":["这是 1%。","这是 50%。","正确：20 × 1.1 = 22。","主板有涨跌幅限制。"],"skills":["涨跌停"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Stock Market Circuit Breakers","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/glossary/stock-market-circuit-breakers"},{"title":"Investopedia: Broker","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/broker.asp"}],"stemEn":"A main-board A-share closed yesterday at 20.00 with a 10% limit. What is today’s theoretical maximum price?","optionsEn":["20.20","30.00","22.00","No limit"],"explanationEn":"Limit-up = previous close × 1.1 = 22.00.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is 1%.","That is 50%.","Correct: 20 × 1.1 = 22.","The main board has a daily limit."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-176-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[176],"stem":"某券商佣金万分之 2.5、每笔最低 5 元。你每次只买 2,000 元的股票。实际佣金率约是多少？","options":["0.025%，按费率算","0.5%，买卖各算一次","0，小额交易免佣金","0.25%，5 ÷ 2,000"],"answer":3,"explanation":"按费率只有 0.5 元，但最低收 5 元，5 ÷ 2,000 = 0.25%。","optionExplanations":["2,000 × 0.025% = 0.5，低于最低收费。","题目只问一次买入。","有最低收费。","正确：实际收 5 元，是标价的 10 倍。"],"skills":["交易费用"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Stock Market Circuit Breakers","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/glossary/stock-market-circuit-breakers"},{"title":"Investopedia: Broker","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/broker.asp"}],"stemEn":"A broker charges 0.025% with a 5 minimum per trade, and you buy only 2,000 each time. What is the effective commission rate?","optionsEn":["0.025%, the stated rate","0.5%, counting buy and sell","0; small trades are free","0.25%: 5 ÷ 2,000"],"explanationEn":"The rate gives 0.5, but the minimum is 5, so 5 ÷ 2,000 = 0.25%.","optionExplanationsEn":["2,000 × 0.025% = 0.5, below the minimum.","The question asks about one buy.","There is a minimum charge.","Correct: You pay 5, ten times the stated rate."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-177-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[177],"stem":"你最在乎“马上成交”，对价格差几分钱不太在意。较适合用哪种单？","options":["限价单","撤单","不下单，等收盘","市价单"],"answer":3,"explanation":"市价单按当时最好价格立即成交，适合优先成交的需求。","optionExplanations":["限价单可能不成交。","撤单不会买入。","没有下单就没有成交。","正确：优先保证成交。"],"skills":["订单类型"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Types of Orders","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/how-stock-markets-work/types-orders"},{"title":"Investopedia: Market Order","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketorder.asp"}],"stemEn":"You care most about filling right away and not about a few cents. Which order fits better?","optionsEn":["A limit order","A cancellation","No order; wait for the close","A market order"],"explanationEn":"A market order fills immediately at the best price available.","optionExplanationsEn":["A limit order may not fill.","Cancelling buys nothing.","No order means no fill.","Correct: It prioritises execution."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-177-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[177],"stem":"你挂了 20.00 元的限价买单，价格最低只跌到 20.05 元。结果会怎样？","options":["不成交，单子继续挂着或到期","按 20.05 元成交","按 20.00 元强制成交","自动改为市价单成交"],"answer":0,"explanation":"限价买单只在限价或更低价成交，价格没到就不会成交。","optionExplanations":["正确：价格没有到达限价。","高于你的限价，不会成交。","没有人愿意在那里卖。","限价单不会自动改类型。"],"skills":["限价单"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Types of Orders","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/how-stock-markets-work/types-orders"},{"title":"Investopedia: Market Order","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketorder.asp"}],"stemEn":"You place a buy limit at 20.00, but price only falls to 20.05. What happens?","optionsEn":["No fill; the order stays open or expires","It fills at 20.05","It is forced to fill at 20.00","It switches to a market order"],"explanationEn":"A buy limit fills only at the limit or lower.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Price never reached the limit.","That is above your limit.","No one sold there.","It does not change type automatically."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-177-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[177],"stem":"卖一价 10.02 元，你挂了 10.10 元的限价买单。较可能的结果是？","options":["按 10.10 元成交","先按 10.02 元起成交","不成交，因为高于市价","被系统拒绝"],"answer":1,"explanation":"限价买单写的是“最高愿付价格”，有更低卖价时按更低价成交。","optionExplanations":["有更低的卖价可成交。","正确：限价单会按更有利的价格成交。","买单高于卖价会立即成交。","这是正常委托。"],"skills":["成交价格"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Types of Orders","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/how-stock-markets-work/types-orders"},{"title":"Investopedia: Market Order","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketorder.asp"}],"stemEn":"The best offer is 10.02 and you place a buy limit at 10.10. What is the likely result?","optionsEn":["It fills at 10.10","It fills from 10.02 upward","No fill, as it is above market","The system rejects it"],"explanationEn":"A buy limit states the most you will pay; it fills at lower offers when present.","optionExplanationsEn":["A lower offer is available.","Correct: A limit fills at better prices when available.","A buy above the offer fills at once.","It is a normal order."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-177-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[177],"stem":"你挂了 1,000 股限价买单，收盘时只成交了 300 股，委托设为“当日有效”。之后会怎样？","options":["1,000 股全部作废，包括已成交的","第二天自动按市价买满","300 股已成交，剩余 700 股的委托失效","剩余部分永久挂着"],"answer":2,"explanation":"部分成交的部分有效；当日有效的未成交部分在收盘后取消。","optionExplanations":["已成交部分有效。","不会自动改成市价。","正确：当日有效的单子收盘后不再保留。","那是撤单前有效（GTC）的情况。"],"skills":["部分成交"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Types of Orders","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/how-stock-markets-work/types-orders"},{"title":"Investopedia: Market Order","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketorder.asp"}],"stemEn":"You place a day-only limit buy for 1,000 shares and by the close only 300 have filled. What happens next?","optionsEn":["All 1,000 are void, filled ones included","It buys the rest at market next day","300 shares are yours; the remaining 700 expire","The rest stays open forever"],"explanationEn":"Filled parts stand; the unfilled part of a day order is cancelled at the close.","optionExplanationsEn":["Filled shares stand.","It does not turn into a market order.","Correct: Day orders do not carry over.","That would be GTC."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-178-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[178],"stem":"“标普 500 今天涨了 1%”最准确的含义是？","options":["美国市场里所有股票都各涨了 1%","标普公司自己的股价涨了 1%","500 只成分股加权后整体涨约 1%","美国经济在这一天增长了 1%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"指数反映成分股的加权整体表现，个股可能涨也可能跌。","optionExplanations":["成分股涨跌各不相同。","指数不是公司股价。","正确：指数代表一篮子的整体。","指数不是经济增速。"],"skills":["指数含义"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Market Index","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketindex.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Exchange-Traded Fund (ETF)","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/etf.asp"}],"stemEn":"What does “the S&P 500 rose 1% today” mean most precisely?","optionsEn":["Every US stock rose 1%","S&P’s own share price rose 1%","The cap-weighted basket of 500 stocks rose about 1%","The US economy grew 1%"],"explanationEn":"An index reflects the weighted basket; individual stocks may rise or fall.","optionExplanationsEn":["Constituents move differently.","An index is not a company’s stock.","Correct: An index represents the basket overall.","An index is not economic growth."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-178-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[178],"stem":"下面哪项关于 ETF 的说法正确？","options":["ETF 只在每天收盘后按净值申购","ETF 不会亏损","ETF 就是指数本身","ETF 可以像股票一样在交易所买卖"],"answer":3,"explanation":"ETF 在交易所上市交易，许多以跟踪指数为目标，但不保本。","optionExplanations":["ETF 在交易时段内买卖。","跟踪的资产下跌，ETF 也会跌。","ETF 是跟踪指数的基金。","正确：这是 ETF 的基本特征。"],"skills":["ETF"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Market Index","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketindex.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Exchange-Traded Fund (ETF)","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/etf.asp"}],"stemEn":"Which statement about ETFs is correct?","optionsEn":["ETFs can only be bought at the close at NAV","ETFs cannot lose money","An ETF is the index itself","ETFs trade on an exchange like stocks"],"explanationEn":"ETFs are exchange-listed funds, many tracking an index, with no capital guarantee.","optionExplanationsEn":["ETFs trade during the session.","If its assets fall, so does the ETF.","An ETF is a fund that tracks an index.","Correct: That is the defining feature."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-178-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[178],"stem":"某市值加权指数中，最大的 5 只股票占 40% 权重。某天这 5 只平均涨 2%，其余成分股平均跌 0.5%。指数约变化多少？","options":["+0.5%","−0.5%","+1.5%","+0.75%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"按权重相加：0.4 × 2% − 0.6 × 0.5% = 0.8% − 0.3% = 0.5%。","optionExplanations":["正确：0.4 × 2% + 0.6 × (−0.5%) = 0.5%。","忽略了大权重股的上涨。","这是简单相减，没有加权。","这是两组涨跌幅的简单平均。"],"skills":["加权计算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Market Index","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketindex.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Exchange-Traded Fund (ETF)","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/etf.asp"}],"stemEn":"In a cap-weighted index the top five stocks make up 40%. One day they rise 2% on average and the rest fall 0.5%. Roughly how does the index move?","optionsEn":["+0.5%","−0.5%","+1.5%","+0.75%"],"explanationEn":"Weight the moves: 0.4 × 2% − 0.6 × 0.5% = 0.8% − 0.3% = 0.5%.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 0.4 × 2% + 0.6 × (−0.5%) = 0.5%.","This ignores the heavyweights’ gain.","A plain difference, not weighted.","A simple average of the two groups."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-178-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[178],"stem":"日经 225 按股价加权。下面哪种情况对它的影响更大？","options":["低价小盘股涨停","高价股每股涨 100 日元","市值最大的公司涨 1 日元","影响相同，因为都是成分股"],"answer":1,"explanation":"价格加权指数里，每股价格变动的金额越大，对指数的影响越大，与市值无关。","optionExplanations":["每股涨幅金额很小。","正确：价格加权看每股价格的变动。","价格加权不看市值。","权重因股价而异。"],"skills":["加权方式"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Market Index","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/marketindex.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Exchange-Traded Fund (ETF)","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/e/etf.asp"}],"stemEn":"The Nikkei 225 is price-weighted. Which has the larger effect on it?","optionsEn":["A low-priced small stock hitting limit-up","A high-priced stock rising 100 yen per share","The largest company by cap rising 1 yen","The same, since all are members"],"explanationEn":"In a price-weighted index, the larger the per-share yen move, the bigger the effect, regardless of market cap.","optionExplanationsEn":["The yen move per share is small.","Correct: Price weighting tracks per-share moves.","Price weighting ignores market cap.","Weights differ by price."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-179-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[179],"stem":"代币 X 单价 0.01 美元，流通量 1,000 亿枚；代币 Y 单价 50 美元，流通量 1,000 万枚。哪个流通市值更大？","options":["Y，单价高得多","X，约 10 亿美元","一样大","无法比较，单价差太多"],"answer":1,"explanation":"流通市值 = 单价 × 流通量：X 为 10 亿，Y 为 5 亿。","optionExplanations":["要乘以流通量。","正确：0.01 × 1,000 亿 = 10 亿；50 × 1,000 万 = 5 亿。","计算结果不同。","市值可以直接比较。"],"skills":["市值"],"references":[{"title":"Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System (white paper)","url":"https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf"},{"title":"Investopedia: Cryptocurrency","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/cryptocurrency.asp"}],"stemEn":"Token X costs 0.01 with 100 billion circulating; token Y costs 50 with 10 million circulating. Which has the larger circulating cap?","optionsEn":["Y, its price is far higher","X: 1 billion versus Y’s 500 million","The same","Cannot compare such different prices"],"explanationEn":"Circulating cap = price × circulating supply: X is 1 billion, Y is 500 million.","optionExplanationsEn":["Multiply by supply.","Correct: 0.01 × 100 billion = 1 billion; 50 × 10 million = 500 million.","The results differ.","Market caps compare directly."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-179-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[179],"stem":"下面哪项最符合“代币（token）”的常见用法？","options":["一条区块链自己的原生资产","交易所发给用户的积分","发行在已有区块链上的资产","只在一家交易所上市的币"],"answer":2,"explanation":"代币通常发行在以太坊等已有区块链上，币通常是链的原生资产。","optionExplanations":["那通常叫币（coin）。","积分不是链上资产。","正确：例如很多稳定币。","与发行在哪无关。"],"skills":["币与代币"],"references":[{"title":"Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System (white paper)","url":"https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf"},{"title":"Investopedia: Cryptocurrency","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/cryptocurrency.asp"}],"stemEn":"Which best matches the usual meaning of a “token”?","optionsEn":["A blockchain’s own native asset","Points an exchange gives users","An asset issued on an existing blockchain","A coin sold on only one exchange"],"explanationEn":"Tokens usually live on existing chains such as Ethereum; coins are usually native assets.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is usually a coin.","Points are not on-chain assets.","Correct: Many stablecoins are examples.","This is unrelated to where it is issued."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-179-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[179],"stem":"某代币流通 2 亿枚、总量 20 亿枚，价格 3 美元。完全稀释估值（FDV）是多少？","options":["6 亿美元","66 亿美元","2 亿美元","60 亿美元"],"answer":3,"explanation":"FDV = 价格 × 总量 = 3 × 20 亿 = 60 亿美元，是流通市值的 10 倍。","optionExplanations":["这是流通市值。","把两种市值相加了。","这是流通量，不是金额。","正确：3 × 20 亿 = 60 亿。"],"skills":["完全稀释估值"],"references":[{"title":"Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System (white paper)","url":"https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf"},{"title":"Investopedia: Cryptocurrency","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/cryptocurrency.asp"}],"stemEn":"A token has 200 million circulating and 2 billion total, priced at 3. What is the fully diluted value (FDV)?","optionsEn":["600 million","6.6 billion","200 million","6 billion"],"explanationEn":"FDV = price × total supply = 3 × 2 billion = 6 billion, ten times the circulating cap.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is the circulating cap.","This adds the two caps.","That is the supply, not a value.","Correct: 3 × 2 billion = 6 billion."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-179-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[179],"stem":"同名的代币 USDT 在多条区块链上都有发行。从交易所提币时，较稳妥的做法是？","options":["确认接收地址支持的网络，并先小额测试","只要名称相同，选哪条链都可以","选手续费最低的链即可","让交易所自动决定"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一资产在不同链上地址格式与网络不同，提币前要核对网络并先小额测试。","optionExplanations":["正确：这是防止选错链的基本步骤。","链不匹配可能导致资产丢失。","便宜的链可能不被对方支持。","网络需要你自己确认。"],"skills":["选择网络"],"references":[{"title":"Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System (white paper)","url":"https://bitcoin.org/bitcoin.pdf"},{"title":"Investopedia: Cryptocurrency","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/cryptocurrency.asp"}],"stemEn":"The same-named USDT exists on several blockchains. When withdrawing from an exchange, what is the more careful approach?","optionsEn":["Confirm the network the receiving address supports and test with a small amount","Any chain works if the name matches","Pick whichever chain is cheapest","Let the exchange choose automatically"],"explanationEn":"The same asset uses different networks; check the network and test small first.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: This guards against picking the wrong chain.","A chain mismatch can lose the funds.","The cheapest chain may not be supported.","You must confirm the network yourself."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-180-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[180],"stem":"有人自称交易所客服，说“为了帮你解冻账户，请提供钱包助记词”。较合理的反应是？","options":["拒绝，并通过官方渠道核实","提供助记词，尽快解冻","只提供前 6 个单词","截图发给对方，避免抄错"],"answer":0,"explanation":"谁有助记词谁就能动用资产；任何索要助记词的人都应视为诈骗。","optionExplanations":["正确：正规平台不会索要助记词。","助记词等于资产控制权。","部分泄露同样危险。","截图同样是泄露。"],"skills":["助记词安全"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Private Key","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/private-key.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Cryptocurrency Wallet","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bitcoin-wallet.asp"}],"stemEn":"Someone claiming to be exchange support says “to unfreeze your account, send your recovery phrase.” What is the reasonable response?","optionsEn":["Refuse and verify through official channels","Send it to unfreeze quickly","Send only the first six words","Send a screenshot to avoid typos"],"explanationEn":"Whoever holds the phrase controls the funds; anyone asking for it should be treated as a scam.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Legitimate platforms never ask.","The phrase is control of the assets.","A partial leak is still dangerous.","A screenshot is still a leak."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-180-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[180],"stem":"资产放在交易所账户里，主要要承担哪类风险？","options":["自己弄丢助记词","平台倒闭、冻结或被盗","区块链停止运行","价格不会再变动"],"answer":1,"explanation":"托管意味着信任平台；平台出问题时，提币可能受阻。","optionExplanations":["托管时私钥在平台手里。","正确：你依赖平台保管。","这与托管方式无关。","价格照常波动。"],"skills":["托管风险"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Private Key","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/private-key.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Cryptocurrency Wallet","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bitcoin-wallet.asp"}],"stemEn":"Keeping assets in an exchange account mainly exposes you to which risk?","optionsEn":["Losing your own recovery phrase","The platform failing, freezing or being hacked","The blockchain stopping","Prices stop changing"],"explanationEn":"Custody means trusting the platform; if it fails, withdrawals may be blocked.","optionExplanationsEn":["With custody the platform holds the keys.","Correct: You rely on the platform.","That is unrelated to custody.","Prices still move."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-180-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[180],"stem":"你准备把一大笔 USDT 从交易所提到新钱包。下面哪种顺序较稳妥？","options":["一次全部提出，这样能节省手续费","先提余额，再用小额做一次测试","核对地址网络，小额测试后再提余额","地址复制粘贴后不必再核对一遍"],"answer":2,"explanation":"先小额测试能在出错时把损失限制在很小的金额。","optionExplanations":["出错时全部受损。","顺序反了。","正确：多付一次手续费换安全。","剪贴板可能被恶意软件替换。"],"skills":["提币流程"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Private Key","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/private-key.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Cryptocurrency Wallet","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bitcoin-wallet.asp"}],"stemEn":"You plan to move a large amount of USDT from an exchange to a new wallet. Which order is more careful?","optionsEn":["Withdraw it all at once to save fees","Send the bulk first, then a small test","Check address and network, send a small test, then the rest after it arrives","No need to recheck a pasted address"],"explanationEn":"A small test limits any loss to a tiny amount.","optionExplanationsEn":["An error would hit everything.","The order is reversed.","Correct: One extra fee buys safety.","Malware can swap clipboard contents."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-180-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[180],"stem":"自托管钱包的手机丢了，但你把助记词抄在纸上妥善保存。较可能的结果是？","options":["资产永久丢失","需要联系区块链官方客服找回","大约能找回一半资产","可在新设备上用助记词恢复钱包"],"answer":3,"explanation":"资产在链上，助记词能在新设备上恢复对它的控制；但也要尽快转移，以防手机里的数据被人利用。","optionExplanations":["资产记录在链上，不在手机里。","区块链没有客服。","有助记词即可完整恢复。","正确：助记词就是恢复用的备份。"],"skills":["恢复钱包"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Private Key","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/private-key.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Cryptocurrency Wallet","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/bitcoin-wallet.asp"}],"stemEn":"You lose the phone with your self-custody wallet, but your recovery phrase is safely written on paper. What is the likely outcome?","optionsEn":["The assets are lost forever","You must contact the blockchain’s support","Only half can be recovered","You can restore the wallet on a new device with the phrase"],"explanationEn":"Assets live on-chain and the phrase restores control on a new device; move them soon in case the phone’s data is misused.","optionExplanationsEn":["Assets are recorded on-chain, not in the phone.","A blockchain has no support desk.","With the phrase, everything is restored.","Correct: The phrase is the recovery backup."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-181-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[181],"stem":"USDC 属于哪类稳定币？","options":["算法型，靠代码调节供应","加密资产超额抵押型","与美元无关的独立代币","法币储备型，由发行方持有储备"],"answer":3,"explanation":"USDC 由发行方持有美元储备支持，属于法币储备型。","optionExplanations":["它有现金与国债储备。","那更接近 DAI。","它以 1 美元为锚。","正确：储备包括现金与短期国债等。"],"skills":["稳定币类型"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stablecoin","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stablecoin.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Stablecoin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stablecoin"}],"stemEn":"What type of stablecoin is USDC?","optionsEn":["Algorithmic, adjusting supply by code","Crypto-overcollateralized","Unrelated to the dollar","Fiat-reserve, backed by the issuer’s reserves"],"explanationEn":"USDC is backed by dollar reserves held by the issuer.","optionExplanationsEn":["It holds cash and Treasury reserves.","That is closer to DAI.","It targets 1 dollar.","Correct: Reserves include cash and short-term Treasuries."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-181-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[181],"stem":"某稳定币报价 0.98 美元，这种情况叫什么？","options":["脱锚","分红","拆分","正常的利息扣除"],"answer":0,"explanation":"价格偏离锚定价称为脱锚，可能短暂也可能持续。","optionExplanations":["正确：偏离了 1 美元的目标价。","稳定币不分红。","价格偏离不是拆分。","没有这种机制。"],"skills":["脱锚"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stablecoin","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stablecoin.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Stablecoin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stablecoin"}],"stemEn":"A stablecoin trades at 0.98. What is this called?","optionsEn":["A depeg","A dividend","A split","A normal interest deduction"],"explanationEn":"Trading away from the peg is a depeg, brief or lasting.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: It has moved off its 1-dollar target.","Stablecoins pay no dividend.","A price drift is not a split.","There is no such mechanism."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-181-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[181],"stem":"2022 年 UST 的崩溃最能说明哪一点？","options":["所有稳定币都会在同一年崩溃","靠算法与激励维持的锚定在压力下可能失效","只要价格曾经是 1 美元就不会再跌","稳定币价格与市场情绪无关"],"answer":1,"explanation":"算法型稳定币依赖市场信心与套利机制，信心崩溃时锚定可能彻底失效。","optionExplanations":["其他主要稳定币没有崩溃。","正确：UST 没有足额的外部储备。","UST 跌到接近零。","挤兑正是情绪推动的。"],"skills":["设计风险"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stablecoin","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stablecoin.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Stablecoin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stablecoin"}],"stemEn":"What does the 2022 collapse of UST illustrate best?","optionsEn":["All stablecoins collapse in the same year","A peg held by algorithms and incentives can fail under stress","A coin once at 1 dollar cannot fall","Stablecoin prices ignore sentiment"],"explanationEn":"Algorithmic stablecoins rely on confidence and arbitrage; when confidence breaks, the peg can fail completely.","optionExplanationsEn":["Other major stablecoins did not.","Correct: UST lacked full external reserves.","UST fell near zero.","The run was driven by sentiment."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-181-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[181],"stem":"你有 10,000 美元等着找机会，打算全部换成一种稳定币放在一家交易所。较稳妥的调整是？","options":["不用调整，稳定币等于现金","全部换成收益最高的算法稳定币","分散到不同发行方和法币账户","全部换成波动更大的币，等反弹"],"answer":2,"explanation":"稳定币有发行方风险，交易所有平台风险；分散能避免单点出问题时全部受损。","optionExplanations":["稳定币不是银行存款。","高收益往往伴随高风险。","正确：同时降低发行方与平台风险。","这改变了“等待”的本意。"],"skills":["分散风险"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Stablecoin","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/s/stablecoin.asp"},{"title":"Wikipedia: Stablecoin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stablecoin"}],"stemEn":"You have 10,000 waiting for an opportunity and plan to hold it all in one stablecoin on one exchange. What is a more careful adjustment?","optionsEn":["No change; stablecoins equal cash","Switch everything to the highest-yield algorithmic coin","Spread across issuers and consider keeping some in a fiat account","Buy volatile coins and wait for a bounce"],"explanationEn":"Stablecoins carry issuer risk and exchanges platform risk; spreading avoids losing everything to one failure.","optionExplanationsEn":["Stablecoins are not bank deposits.","High yield usually means high risk.","Correct: This cuts both issuer and platform risk.","That abandons the idea of waiting."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-182-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[182],"stem":"用 500 美元保证金开了价值 5,000 美元的仓位。杠杆是多少倍？","options":["5 倍","50 倍","10 倍","0.1 倍"],"answer":2,"explanation":"杠杆 = 5,000 ÷ 500 = 10 倍。","optionExplanations":["5,000 ÷ 500 = 10。","算多了一个数量级。","正确：仓位价值 ÷ 保证金 = 10。","把分子分母倒过来了。"],"skills":["杠杆计算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Leverage","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/leverage.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Margin Call","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/margincall.asp"}],"stemEn":"You open a 5,000 position with 500 of margin. What is the leverage?","optionsEn":["5×","50×","10×","0.1×"],"explanationEn":"Leverage = 5,000 ÷ 500 = 10×.","optionExplanationsEn":["5,000 ÷ 500 = 10.","Off by a factor of ten.","Correct: Position value ÷ margin = 10.","The ratio is inverted."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-182-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[182],"stem":"现货买入的比特币下跌 30%，你没有借钱。会怎样？","options":["被交易所强制平仓卖出","亏光全部本金，一分不剩","要追加资金维持仓位","浮亏 30%，币仍在手里"],"answer":3,"explanation":"现货全额买入，下跌只是浮亏，不存在强平。","optionExplanations":["现货不借钱不会被强平。","跌 30% 不是跌 100%。","现货没有保证金。","正确：亏损在卖出前是浮亏。"],"skills":["现货"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Leverage","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/leverage.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Margin Call","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/margincall.asp"}],"stemEn":"Bitcoin you bought spot falls 30% and you did not borrow. What happens?","optionsEn":["The exchange liquidates you","You lose all your capital","You must add margin","A 30% paper loss; you still hold the bitcoin"],"explanationEn":"Fully paid spot only shows a paper loss; there is no liquidation.","optionExplanationsEn":["Unborrowed spot is not liquidated.","A 30% fall is not 100%.","Spot has no margin.","Correct: The loss is unrealized until you sell."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-182-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[182],"stem":"20 倍杠杆做多，不计手续费与维持保证金，价格反向波动约多少会亏光保证金？","options":["约 5%","约 20%","约 2%","约 50%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"粗估亏光保证金的反向波动 ≈ 1 ÷ 杠杆 = 5%；实际强平更早发生。","optionExplanations":["正确：1 ÷ 20 = 5%。","那是 5 倍杠杆的情况。","那是 50 倍杠杆。","那是 2 倍杠杆。"],"skills":["强平估算"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Leverage","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/leverage.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Margin Call","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/margincall.asp"}],"stemEn":"A 20× long, ignoring fees and maintenance margin: roughly how large an adverse move wipes out the margin?","optionsEn":["About 5%","About 20%","About 2%","About 50%"],"explanationEn":"The wipe-out move ≈ 1 ÷ leverage = 5%; real liquidation comes earlier.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 1 ÷ 20 = 5%.","That would be 5×.","That would be 50×.","That would be 2×."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-182-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[182],"stem":"你判断某币会涨，用 25 倍杠杆做多。价格先跌 6% 再涨 20%。较可能的结果是？","options":["赚 500%，方向判断正确","下跌途中已被强平，没有赶上反弹","赚 14%，涨跌相抵","不赚不亏，因为最终上涨"],"answer":1,"explanation":"25 倍杠杆约 4% 的反向波动就会亏光保证金；看对方向也可能在途中被强平。","optionExplanations":["途中已触及强平。","正确：1 ÷ 25 = 4%，跌 6% 已超过。","杠杆仓位不能这样相抵。","仓位已经不存在。"],"skills":["杠杆风险"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia: Leverage","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/leverage.asp"},{"title":"Investopedia: Margin Call","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/margincall.asp"}],"stemEn":"You expect a coin to rise and go 25× long. Price first falls 6%, then rises 20%. What is the likely result?","optionsEn":["A 500% gain; the direction was right","Liquidated during the dip, missing the rally","A 14% gain, netting the moves","Break-even since price ended higher"],"explanationEn":"At 25×, about a 4% adverse move erases the margin; being right on direction does not prevent liquidation on the way.","optionExplanationsEn":["Liquidation came first.","Correct: 1 ÷ 25 = 4%; a 6% drop exceeds it.","A leveraged position cannot net like that.","The position no longer exists."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-183-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[183],"stem":"网友推荐一个“每天固定收益 1%、保本”的项目。较合理的判断是？","options":["收益稳定，可以先投一点试试","这是典型危险信号，不应投入","只要对方有营业执照就可信","可以投入，但只投借来的钱"],"answer":1,"explanation":"每天 1% 一年复利超过 37 倍，承诺保本的高收益几乎可以确定有问题。","optionExplanations":["诈骗也常先让人小赚。","正确：保本加高额固定收益几乎不存在。","执照可以伪造。","借钱只会放大损失。"],"skills":["识别骗局"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Ponzi Schemes","url":"https://www.investor.gov/protect-your-investments/fraud/types-fraud/ponzi-scheme"},{"title":"Investopedia: Pump-and-Dump","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pumpanddump.asp"}],"stemEn":"An online contact recommends a project with “a fixed 1% daily return, capital guaranteed.” What is the reasonable judgement?","optionsEn":["Steady returns; try a small amount","A classic red flag; do not invest","Trust it if they show a business licence","Invest, but only with borrowed money"],"explanationEn":"1% a day compounds to over 37× a year; guaranteed high returns are almost certainly fraudulent.","optionExplanationsEn":["Scams often let you win small first.","Correct: Guaranteed high fixed returns hardly exist.","Licences can be faked.","Borrowing only magnifies losses."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-183-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[183],"stem":"你收到短信：“账户异常，点击链接验证。”链接域名和交易所官网只差一个字母。较合理的做法是？","options":["点击链接，尽快验证","回复短信询问是否真实","不点链接，自行打开官网核实","把账号密码发给短信号码确认"],"answer":2,"explanation":"钓鱼链接常仿冒官网域名，只通过自己确认过的官方入口登录。","optionExplanations":["这是钓鱼网站的常见手法。","对方会说是真的。","正确：绕开对方提供的入口。","这等于交出账户。"],"skills":["钓鱼防范"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Ponzi Schemes","url":"https://www.investor.gov/protect-your-investments/fraud/types-fraud/ponzi-scheme"},{"title":"Investopedia: Pump-and-Dump","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pumpanddump.asp"}],"stemEn":"A text says “unusual account activity, click to verify,” and the link differs from the exchange’s domain by one letter. What should you do?","optionsEn":["Click and verify quickly","Reply to ask whether it is real","Do not click; open the official app or type the address yourself","Send your credentials to the number"],"explanationEn":"Phishing links mimic real domains; log in only through entrances you verified yourself.","optionExplanationsEn":["This is a classic phishing trick.","They will say it is real.","Correct: Bypass the link you were given.","That hands over the account."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-183-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[183],"stem":"总资金 50,000，你定下单笔最多亏 2%。某笔交易入场 100、止损 96。最多买多少股？","options":["500 股","10 股","1,000 股","250 股"],"answer":3,"explanation":"可亏 50,000 × 2% = 1,000，每股风险 4，最多 250 股。","optionExplanations":["这是全仓股数。","1,000 ÷ 100 用错了分母。","把亏损金额当成了股数。","正确：1,000 ÷ 4 = 250。"],"skills":["资金管理"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Ponzi Schemes","url":"https://www.investor.gov/protect-your-investments/fraud/types-fraud/ponzi-scheme"},{"title":"Investopedia: Pump-and-Dump","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pumpanddump.asp"}],"stemEn":"With 50,000 in capital and a 2% maximum loss per trade, you enter at 100 with a stop at 96. How many shares at most?","optionsEn":["500 shares","10 shares","1,000 shares","250 shares"],"explanationEn":"Allowed loss 1,000; risk per share 4; at most 250 shares.","optionExplanationsEn":["That is the full-capital size.","1,000 ÷ 100 uses the wrong divisor.","This treats the loss amount as shares.","Correct: 1,000 ÷ 4 = 250."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-183-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[183],"stem":"你在一个群里看到“某小币明天必拉，现在上车”，群主催促大家马上买入。较可能的情况是？","options":["可能是拉高出货，先买后卖给跟风者","群主有内部消息，跟着买就能赚钱","小币涨得快，越早买进越安全","只要群里人多就不会是骗局"],"answer":0,"explanation":"喊单群常由组织者先建仓，再制造紧迫感让跟风者接盘。","optionExplanations":["正确：紧迫感是操纵的工具。","这是拉盘砸盘的常见话术。","流动性差，跌得也快。","人数多不代表可信。"],"skills":["拉盘砸盘"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov: Ponzi Schemes","url":"https://www.investor.gov/protect-your-investments/fraud/types-fraud/ponzi-scheme"},{"title":"Investopedia: Pump-and-Dump","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/pumpanddump.asp"}],"stemEn":"In a chat group you see “this small coin will pump tomorrow, get in now,” with the admin urging everyone to buy at once. What is most likely?","optionsEn":["Possibly a pump-and-dump: organisers buy first and sell to followers","The admin has inside info; following pays","Small coins rise fast; earlier is safer","A big group cannot be a scam"],"explanationEn":"Organisers often buy first, then create urgency so followers buy their coins.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Urgency is a manipulation tool.","A typical pump-and-dump script.","Thin liquidity means fast falls too.","Size does not mean legitimacy."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-184-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[184],"stem":"某企业本季度销售货物100万元并全额收到现金，生产支出60万元现金，利润表净利润40万元。该企业当期经营现金流是？","options":["净流入现金40万元","净流出现金20万元","账面变动为零元整","净流入现金60万元"],"answer":0,"explanation":"销售收现100万元减去支出60万元，经营现金净流入40万元，与净利润一致。","optionExplanations":["正确：销售收现100万减去付现支出60万，经营现金净流量为正40万元。","错误：销售现金流入大于经营支出，现金流为正向净流入而非流出。","错误：收支实际发生差额40万元，账面现金流并不为零。","错误：60万元为生产成本支出，不是经营净现金流入额。"],"skills":["现金流计算","三张报表读法"],"references":[{"title":"SEC Beginners' Guide to Financial Statements","url":"https://www.sec.gov/about/reports-publications/beginners-guide-financial-statements"}],"stemEn":"A business collected $100,000 cash from sales and paid $60,000 cash for costs, reporting $40,000 net income. What is its operating cash flow?","optionsEn":["Net inflow of $40,000","Net outflow of $20,000","Zero net change in cash","Net inflow of $60,000"],"explanationEn":"Operating cash flow equals cash received ($100k) minus cash paid ($60k), which is a net positive $40k, matching net income.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Cash inflow of $100,000 minus outflow of $60,000 leaves $40,000 in operating cash flow.","Incorrect: Inflow exceeded outflow, creating positive cash flow rather than a net deficit.","Incorrect: Net cash changed by $40,000 rather than remaining neutral.","Incorrect: $60,000 was the cash expense, not the net cash generated."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-184-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[184],"stem":"关于三张财务报表各自核心功能的表述，符合会计准则的是哪一项？","options":["利润表能够展示时点资产","资产负债表展示时点家底","现金流量表记录企业估值","资产负债表仅记录当期成本"],"answer":1,"explanation":"资产负债表反映企业在特定日期的资产、负债与权益静态全貌。","optionExplanations":["错误：利润表反映特定期间的经营成果流量，而非特定时点的静态资产。","正确：资产负债表反映特定时点的资产、负债及股东权益状况。","错误：现金流量表记录现金实际流动，不衡量二级市场估值倍数。","错误：当期成本属于利润表核算范畴，资产负债表记录累计存量。"],"skills":["三张报表结构","会计基础"],"references":[{"title":"SEC Beginners' Guide to Financial Statements","url":"https://www.sec.gov/about/reports-publications/beginners-guide-financial-statements"}],"stemEn":"Which statement correctly describes the primary accounting purpose of the core financial reports?","optionsEn":["Income statements show point-in-time assets","Balance sheets show snapshot financial health","Cash flow statements show market valuations","Balance sheets only track current-term costs"],"explanationEn":"The balance sheet reflects the accumulated assets, liabilities, and equity at a specific point in time.","optionExplanationsEn":["Incorrect: The income statement tracks performance over a period rather than point-in-time balances.","Correct: The balance sheet provides a financial snapshot of assets, liabilities, and equity at a fixed date.","Incorrect: The cash flow statement tracks liquidity movements, not equity valuations.","Incorrect: Operating expenses belong on the income statement rather than the balance sheet."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-184-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[184],"stem":"一家企业连续三年账面净利润高速增长，但经营活动现金流常年净流出，最合理的分析是？","options":["说明企业盈利质量极佳","证明公司不存在破产可能","可能存在货款回收缓慢风险","反映公司产品全额现金结算"],"answer":2,"explanation":"净利润增长但经营现金流为负，通常反映赊销严重、应收账款堆积或存货积压。","optionExplanations":["错误：缺乏真金白银支持的高增长往往伴随盈利质量恶化。","错误：持续垫资与现金净流出会耗尽流动性，带来潜在偿债危机。","正确：净利润与现金流持续背离往往源于大量应收账款未收回或存货积压。","错误：若全额现金结算，经营现金流通常会紧随净利润呈现正向流入。"],"skills":["报表勾稽分析","财务陷阱识别"],"references":[{"title":"SEC Beginners' Guide to Financial Statements","url":"https://www.sec.gov/about/reports-publications/beginners-guide-financial-statements"}],"stemEn":"A firm reports rising net income over three years while operating cash flow stays negative. What is the most plausible interpretation?","optionsEn":["The firm demonstrates stellar earnings quality","The firm is free from all bankruptcy dangers","The firm may face severe receivable collection delays","The firm receives all sales strictly in hard cash"],"explanationEn":"Persistent divergence between profits and cash flow typically points to uncollected receivables or inventory build-ups.","optionExplanationsEn":["Incorrect: Rapid paper profit growth without cash flow indicates deteriorating earnings quality.","Incorrect: Depleted cash reserves increase solvency and liquidity hazards.","Correct: A persistent gap between accrual profit and cash flow often stems from unpaid customer debt.","Incorrect: Immediate cash receipts would generate robust operating cash inflows."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-184-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[184],"stem":"查阅在美股、A股与港股上市公司的官方原始财报，正确的公开披露平台组合是哪一组？","options":["纽交所商户端与东方财富网","商业财经论坛与同花顺软件","彭博商业终端与雪球网主页","SEC官网与巨潮网及披露易"],"answer":3,"explanation":"美股官方披露为SEC EDGAR，A股为巨潮资讯网，港股为港交所披露易。","optionExplanations":["错误：纽交所商户端并非美股主文档法定入口，第三方软件非官方信披平台。","错误：商业论坛与行情软件属于二级中介，数据存在清洗二次加工滞后。","错误：商业数据终端与社区网站并非证券监管机构指定的原始报告法定平台。","正确：美股通过SEC EDGAR，A股通过巨潮资讯网，港股通过披露易获取原始报告。"],"skills":["原始财报检索","合规披露渠道"],"references":[{"title":"SEC EDGAR Search System","url":"https://www.sec.gov/edgar/search/"},{"title":"巨潮资讯网（中国证监会指定信息披露平台）","url":"http://www.cninfo.com.cn/"}],"stemEn":"Which set of platforms represents the official regulatory filing channels for U.S., A-share, and HK-listed company reports?","optionsEn":["NYSE merchant web and Eastmoney portal","Commercial financial forums and Flush apps","Bloomberg Terminal and Xueqiu user feeds","SEC EDGAR, CNINFO, and HKEXnews"],"explanationEn":"Statutory original filings are hosted by SEC EDGAR (US), CNINFO (China A-shares), and HKEXnews (Hong Kong).","optionExplanationsEn":["Incorrect: Exchange portals and commercial tools do not host primary statutory EDGAR files.","Incorrect: Public discussion forums and brokers provide secondary processed market data.","Incorrect: Subscription terminals and social feeds are not statutory regulatory repositories.","Correct: SEC EDGAR, CNINFO, and HKEXnews are designated regulatory disclosure platforms."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-185-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[185],"stem":"某股票市价为60元，过去12个月累计每股收益为3元，该股票当前的滚动市盈率（TTM）是多少？","options":["市盈率指标为20倍","市盈率指标为60倍","市盈率指标为180倍","市盈率指标为5倍整"],"answer":0,"explanation":"滚动市盈率 P/E（TTM）= 股价 ÷ EPS（TTM）= 60 ÷ 3 = 20倍。","optionExplanations":["正确：市盈率 = 股价 ÷ 每股收益 = 60 ÷ 3 = 20倍。","错误：60倍直接使用了股价数值，未除以每股收益。","错误：180倍是将股价与每股收益相乘得出的数值，公式颠倒。","错误：5倍计算错误，60 ÷ 3 的商为20而非5。"],"skills":["市盈率计算","估值基础"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov Price-Earnings (P/E) Ratio","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/glossary/price-earnings-pe-ratio"}],"stemEn":"A stock trades at $60, and its trailing 12-month earnings per share (EPS) is $3. What is its Trailing P/E (TTM)?","optionsEn":["P/E multiple is 20x","P/E multiple is 60x","P/E multiple is 180x","P/E multiple is 5x"],"explanationEn":"P/E (TTM) = Share Price / Trailing EPS = 60 / 3 = 20x.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: P/E = Share price / EPS = 60 / 3 = 20x.","Incorrect: 60x merely takes the nominal share price without dividing by earnings.","Incorrect: 180x erroneously multiplies the price by EPS instead of dividing.","Incorrect: 60 divided by 3 results in 20, not 5."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-185-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[185],"stem":"关于滚动市盈率（TTM）与预测市盈率（Forward P/E）的差别，下列说法正确的是哪一项？","options":["两者计算公式的分母完全相同","前者基于历史数据后者基于预期","预测市盈率采用过去经审计年报","滚动市盈率反映未来发展潜力"],"answer":1,"explanation":"TTM采用过去12个月已发生的历史实际利润，Forward采用未来分析师预测利润。","optionExplanations":["错误：两者的分母分别为过去已实现EPS和未来预测EPS，分母不同。","正确：TTM基于过去12个月已实现的财务数据，Forward基于分析师对未来的盈利预期。","错误：预测市盈率采用未来预测盈利，历史审计年报对应静态或TTM市盈率。","错误：滚动市盈率体现历史业绩成果，未来增长潜力主要由预期指标反映。"],"skills":["TTM与预测市盈率","估值指标辨析"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov Price-Earnings (P/E) Ratio","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/glossary/price-earnings-pe-ratio"}],"stemEn":"What is the primary difference between Trailing P/E (TTM) and Forward P/E?","optionsEn":["Both ratios use identical denominator EPS values","TTM uses past data while forward relies on forecasts","Forward P/E uses historical audited annual reports","Trailing P/E captures future company growth prospects"],"explanationEn":"TTM P/E is calculated using audited past 12-month earnings, while Forward P/E uses consensus analyst projections for future periods.","optionExplanationsEn":["Incorrect: The denominators differ; TTM uses past realized earnings while Forward uses expected earnings.","Correct: Trailing P/E reflects historical realized performance, whereas Forward P/E reflects forward expectations.","Incorrect: Forward P/E looks ahead to future periods rather than relying on past audited numbers.","Incorrect: Trailing P/E reflects past historical financial performance rather than future projections."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-185-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[185],"stem":"一家处于成长期的高科技软件公司当期净利润为负数，投资者评估该企业相对估值时通常会怎样处理？","options":["使用负数市盈率进行排序比较","直接认定该股票缺乏商业价值","转而参考市销率或单位营收指标","将分母设定为一元强行计算倍数"],"answer":2,"explanation":"亏损企业市盈率分母为负无经济意义，常采用市销率（P/S）或毛利指标替代评估。","optionExplanations":["错误：负市盈率在经济学与估值学中失去倍数对比意义，软件通常显示为N/A。","错误：早期高成长科技企业前期研发投入大常处亏损，不等于没有商业前景。","正确：亏损企业EPS为负导致市盈率失效，分析师通常改用市销率（P/S）或现金流倍数等指标。","错误：人为修改分母会扭曲会计真实性，属于错误评估手段。"],"skills":["亏损企业估值","市销率应用"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia Price-to-Sales (P/S) Ratio","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/price-to-salesratio.asp"}],"stemEn":"A high-growth SaaS tech firm reports negative net income. How do investors typically evaluate its relative market valuation?","optionsEn":["Rank peers using negative P/E figures directly","Deem the business completely devoid of enterprise value","Adopt Price-to-Sales or unit revenue metrics instead","Set denominator EPS to one dollar to force calculations"],"explanationEn":"When net earnings are negative, P/E becomes mathematically meaningless, prompting analysts to use Price-to-Sales (P/S) or gross margins.","optionExplanationsEn":["Incorrect: Negative P/E ratios are economically meaningless and typically reported as N/A.","Incorrect: Early-stage growth firms often incur upfront R&D losses while expanding enterprise scale.","Correct: Analysts substitute invalid P/E multiples with Price-to-Sales (P/S) or revenue growth metrics.","Incorrect: Arbitrarily overriding financial denominators generates misleading and invalid ratios."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-185-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[185],"stem":"关于估值指标在跨行业比较与投资应用中的局限性，下列说法最严谨的是哪一项？","options":["低市盈率股票在任何市场都会上涨","银行与软件企业的市销率能直接比","高市净率代表公司财务濒临危机","跨行业对比常受资本结构差异误导"],"answer":3,"explanation":"不同行业资本密集度、负债率和商业模式差异巨大，估值倍数不可脱离行业直接横向比较。","optionExplanations":["错误：低估值股票可能属于陷入业务衰退的价值陷阱，不保证上涨。","错误：重资产银行与轻资产软件公司的商业模式与资本构成不同，不能直接对比。","错误：轻资产高科技公司账面资产少但无形资产高，市净率较高通常属于正常现象。","正确：轻资产公司与重资产制造业的资产结构和成长模式完全不同，跨行业比较极易产生误导。"],"skills":["价值陷阱防范","行业估值边界"],"references":[{"title":"Investopedia Price-to-Earnings (P/E) Ratio Definition","url":"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/price-earningsratio.asp"}],"stemEn":"Which statement most accurately describes the core limitation of valuation multiples in comparative analysis?","optionsEn":["Low P/E stocks consistently gain across all markets","Bank and software firm P/S multiples compare directly","High P/B ratios indicate immediate corporate insolvency","Cross-sector comparisons mislead due to capital structures"],"explanationEn":"Different industries have distinct capital intensity, leverage, and growth rates, making direct cross-sector multiple comparison misleading.","optionExplanationsEn":["Incorrect: Low-multiple securities frequently represent structural value traps rather than underpriced assets.","Incorrect: Financial institutions and asset-light tech firms possess vastly different accounting profiles.","Incorrect: High P/B ratios are standard for technology businesses with substantial intangible value.","Correct: Diverse capital intensity, leverage, and margin profiles across industries invalidate raw cross-sector multiple comparisons."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-186-1","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[186],"stem":"某公司当季EPS为2.00元，此前市场分析师平均共识预期为1.60元，该公司的盈利惊喜（Surprise）是？","options":["超出市场预期0.40元","低于市场预期0.40元","与市场共识完全持平","盈利超出幅度达两倍"],"answer":0,"explanation":"实际公布EPS（2.00元）高于市场预期（1.60元），超出差额为0.40元（+25%）。","optionExplanations":["正确：实际值2.00元减去预期值1.60元，盈利惊喜为正向超出0.40元。","错误：实际数据高于预期，属于正向超预期而非低于预期。","错误：实际值与预期值之间存在0.40元的显著差异，并非持平。","错误：超出比例为 0.40 ÷ 1.60 = 25%，并未达到两倍。"],"skills":["盈利惊喜计算","业绩读法"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov How to Read a 10-K/10-Q Bulletin","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/how-read"}],"stemEn":"A company reports quarterly EPS of $2.00 versus the analyst consensus estimate of $1.60. What is the earnings surprise?","optionsEn":["Beat consensus by $0.40","Missed estimates by $0.40","Matched consensus exactly","Exceeded forecast by two-fold"],"explanationEn":"Actual EPS ($2.00) minus consensus estimate ($1.60) yields a positive beat of $0.40 (+25%).","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Actual earnings of $2.00 exceeded the $1.60 consensus by $0.40.","Incorrect: The reported figure was higher than projected, representing a beat rather than a miss.","Incorrect: There is a clear positive delta of $0.40 rather than zero variance.","Incorrect: The beat was 25% (0.40 / 1.60), not a twofold increase."]},{"id":"basics-beginner-186-2","type":"basics","level":"beginner","topicIds":[186],"stem":"美股公司通常选择在什么时段披露季度财务报告，从而容易导致次日开盘发生价格跳空？","options":["盘中连续交易时段正午","盘前或盘后非正式时段","周末休市深夜零点时分","交易所常规集合竞价前"],"answer":1,"explanation":"美股财报普遍在盘前（BMO）或盘后（AMC）公布，场外资金重新定价常引发跳空开盘。","optionExplanations":["错误：为避免盘中行情异常剧烈波动，上市公司通常极少在正午交易中途突发财报。","正确：美股财报绝大多数在盘前（BMO）或盘后（AMC）披露，隔夜信息发酵常使次日开盘产生跳空缺口。","错误：上市公司披露财报遵循工作日信息发布日程，极少选择周末半夜常规发布。","错误：主要披露窗口为盘前数小时或盘后，而非仅限集合竞价瞬间。"],"skills":["财报发布时点","跳空机制"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov How to Read a 10-K/10-Q Bulletin","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/how-read"}],"stemEn":"When do U.S. listed companies typically release quarterly earnings, often resulting in overnight stock price gaps?","optionsEn":["During continuous midday market trading","Before market open or after market close","At midnight during weekend holiday breaks","Right at the official opening bell second"],"explanationEn":"Firms typically release earnings Before Market Open (BMO) or After Market Close (AMC), prompting order imbalances that gap opening prices.","optionExplanationsEn":["Incorrect: Releases during active trading hours are avoided to reduce disorderly intraday volatility.","Correct: Most corporations schedule releases BMO or AMC, allowing new data to be digested and priced in gaps at the open.","Incorrect: Earnings releases adhere to scheduled business days rather than weekend midnights.","Incorrect: Announcements occur well before or after market hours, not right at the opening bell."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-186-1","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[186],"stem":"某公司当季净利润大幅超出华尔街预期，但盘后股价却意外暴跌10%，最可能的原因是？","options":["财报公布后成交量未能跟上","分析师集体上调了目标价格","管理层下调未来业绩指引","该企业宣布全额派发现金股利"],"answer":2,"explanation":"股价由未来现金流预期贴现决定，管理层大幅下调未来指引往往击溃长期估值模型。","optionExplanations":["错误：暴跌通常伴随成交量急剧放大，成交量不足不是导致大跌的核心原因。","错误：目标价上调通常反映积极情绪，不会直接诱发股价暴跌。","正确：当季利润代表过去，若管理层对下季度或全年的业绩指引大幅下调，市场会迅速下调未来现金流估值。","错误：正常现金分红体现股东回报，通常不会引发业绩公布后盘后暴跌10%的剧烈反应。"],"skills":["业绩指引解读","预期差博弈"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov How to Read a 10-K/10-Q Bulletin","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/how-read"}],"stemEn":"A corporation beats quarterly consensus profit expectations, yet its stock drops 10% after hours. What is the most probable catalyst?","optionsEn":["Trading volume failed to expand immediately","Wall Street analysts raised target price targets","Management lowered forward earnings guidance","The board authorized a regular quarterly cash dividend"],"explanationEn":"Stock prices reflect discounted future cash flows; lowering forward guidance forces analysts to downgrade forward financial models.","optionExplanationsEn":["Incorrect: Post-earnings gap-downs typically trade on heavy volume; light volume is not the fundamental catalyst.","Incorrect: Upward target revisions signal positive sentiment rather than an immediate 10% selloff.","Correct: While trailing results beat, downward revisions in forward guidance degrade expected future cash flows.","Incorrect: Routine cash dividend announcements reward shareholders and do not trigger double-digit post-earnings plunges."]},{"id":"basics-advanced-186-2","type":"basics","level":"advanced","topicIds":[186],"stem":"在财报公布前，某热门股票两周内累计上涨30%。财报公布虽然双超预期，开盘却高开低走收阴线，这种现象通常称为？","options":["资产负债表存量出清效应","财务粉饰带来的均值回归","无套利均衡下的跨期对冲","利好预期充分兑现后的获利抛售"],"answer":3,"explanation":"这属于经典的“利好兑现成利空”（Sell the News），买入预期、卖出事实引发资金获利了结。","optionExplanations":["错误：资产负债表存量调整属于会计账目计量，并非描述短线交易买卖冲动的术语。","错误：题目说明业绩经检验双超预期，价格下跌源于交易行为而非财务粉饰被揭发。","错误：跨期对冲属于衍生品保值策略，与财报公布日的情绪获利回吐无关。","正确：利好消息此前已被股价大幅上涨所提前透支，财报落地后交易资金倾向于锁定利润（Sell the News）。"],"skills":["利好兑现识别","市场微观结构"],"references":[{"title":"Investor.gov How to Read a 10-K/10-Q Bulletin","url":"https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/general-resources/news-alerts/alerts-bulletins/investor-bulletins/how-read"}],"stemEn":"Ahead of earnings, a stock rallied 30%. Despite beating revenue and EPS estimates, it opened high and closed down. This is commonly known as:","optionsEn":["Balance sheet inventory liquidation pressure","Accounting restatements mean reversion","No-arbitrage intertemporal hedging","Selling the news following priced-in expectations"],"explanationEn":"When expectations are fully priced in ahead of time, market participants often sell the fact to lock in gains ('Sell the News').","optionExplanationsEn":["Incorrect: Inventory liquidation relates to operational assets rather than market pricing phenomena.","Incorrect: The prompt indicates a genuine beat; the selloff reflects profit-taking rather than financial fraud.","Incorrect: Intertemporal hedging is a derivative risk management practice unrelated to event-driven selloffs.","Correct: When strong results are fully priced in during a pre-earnings surge, traders frequently take profits on the news."]},{"id":"information-beginner-01","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[1,2],"stem":"某次核心CPI月环比：前值0.4%，市场一致预期0.2%，实际0.3%，口径一致且没有修正。应怎样描述本次结果？","options":["低于前值，也低于预期","低于前值，但高于预期","高于前值，但低于预期","消费价格比上月下降0.1%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"0.3%低于0.4%，但高于0.2%；“较上月放慢”与“比市场想的热”可以同时成立。","optionExplanations":["0.3%比0.2%高，不能说低于预期。","0.3%低于0.4%，但高于0.2%；“较上月放慢”与“比市场想的热”可以同时成立。","两组大小关系均颠倒了。","0.3%仍是价格上涨；回落的是涨幅，不是价格水平。"],"skills":["预期差","涨幅与水平"],"references":[{"title":"BLS — Consumer Price Index FAQ","url":"https://www.bls.gov/cpi/questions-and-answers.htm"}],"stemEn":"A core CPI month-over-month release: prior 0.4%, consensus 0.2%, actual 0.3%, on the same basis and with no revision. How should the result be described?","optionsEn":["Below the prior reading and below expectations","Below the prior reading, but above expectations","Above the prior reading, but below expectations","Consumer prices fell 0.1% from last month"],"explanationEn":"0.3% is below 0.4% but above 0.2%; \"slowing from last month\" and \"hotter than the market expected\" can both be true.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 0.3% is above 0.2%, so it is not below expectations.","Correct: 0.3% is below 0.4% but above 0.2%; \"slowing from last month\" and \"hotter than the market expected\" can both be true.","Wrong: Both comparisons are reversed.","Wrong: 0.3% is still a price rise; what fell was the rate of increase, not the price level."]},{"id":"information-beginner-02","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[12,13],"stem":"假设某小经济体共有100名劳动力，其中95人就业、5人失业。下月没有人找到工作，但2名失业者停止找工作并退出劳动力。新的失业率约为多少？","options":["3.0%（3除以100）","3.1%（3除以98）","5.1%（5除以98）","5.0%（退出者仍算失业）"],"answer":1,"explanation":"失业人数3，劳动力98，3÷98约3.1%。失业率下降并不代表这2人找到了工作。","optionExplanations":["错误：退出者已不在劳动力内，分母应是98。","正确：失业3人，劳动力98人，3÷98约3.1%。","错误：失业者已减为3人。","错误：停止找工作者不再计入失业。"],"skills":["分母变化","就业解读"],"references":[{"title":"BLS — Employment Situation Technical Note","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.tn.htm"}],"stemEn":"Suppose a small economy has a labour force of 100: 95 employed and 5 unemployed. Next month nobody finds a job, but 2 unemployed people stop looking and leave the labour force. What is the new unemployment rate, approximately?","optionsEn":["3.0% (3 divided by 100)","3.1% (3 divided by 98)","5.1% (5 divided by 98)","5.0% (those who left still count as unemployed)"],"explanationEn":"3 unemployed in a labour force of 98: 3 ÷ 98 ≈ 3.1%. A lower unemployment rate does not mean those 2 people found jobs.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Those who left are no longer in the labour force, so the denominator is 98.","Correct: 3 unemployed and a labour force of 98, so 3 ÷ 98 ≈ 3.1%.","Wrong: Unemployment has already dropped to 3 people.","Wrong: People who stop looking are no longer counted as unemployed."]},{"id":"information-beginner-03","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[23],"stem":"某次ISM制造业PMI由48升至49，其余信息未知。就该扩散指数本身，哪种解读正确？","options":["活动已由收缩转为扩张状态","制造业产出较上月增长约1%","活动仍偏收缩，但收缩程度缓和","活动收缩在加深，因读数低于50"],"answer":2,"explanation":"从48升至49是改善，但仍低于50；这与“已经扩张”不同。","optionExplanations":["错误：49仍低于50，不算扩张。","错误：PMI是扩散指数，不是产出增速。","正确：从48升至49是改善，但仍低于50。","错误：读数上升说明收缩在缓和。"],"skills":["扩散指数","改善与扩张"],"references":[{"title":"ISM — PMI reports and methodology","url":"https://www.ismworld.org/supply-management-news-and-reports/reports/ism-pmi-reports/"}],"stemEn":"The ISM manufacturing PMI rises from 48 to 49, with nothing else known. Judging this diffusion index alone, which reading is correct?","optionsEn":["Activity has moved from contraction to expansion","Manufacturing output grew about 1% from last month","Activity still leans to contraction, but less so","Contraction is deepening because the reading is below 50"],"explanationEn":"Rising from 48 to 49 is an improvement but still below 50, which is different from \"already expanding\".","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 49 is still below 50, so it is not expansion.","Wrong: PMI is a diffusion index, not an output growth rate.","Correct: Rising from 48 to 49 is an improvement but still below 50.","Wrong: A rising reading means contraction is easing."]},{"id":"information-beginner-04","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[31,33],"stem":"为了练习区分名义与实际，假设一家商店只卖同一种商品：上月卖100件，每件10元；本月仍卖100件，每件11元。哪项最准确？","options":["销售额增长10%，实物销量没有增长","销售额增长10%，实物销量也增长10%","销售额不变，只有商品单价上涨","扣除涨价后，实物销量下降约9.1%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"销售额从1000变1100，但件数仍为100。现实零售报告以金额计，不能直接当成真实消费量。","optionExplanations":["销售额从1000变1100，但件数仍为100。现实零售报告以金额计，不能直接当成真实消费量。","本月仍卖100件，数量没有增加。","件数不变不代表金额不变，金额是单价乘数量。","9.1%不是件数变化；题设直接给出了数量不变。"],"skills":["金额与数量","价格调整"],"references":[{"title":"Census — Monthly Retail Trade Survey","url":"https://www.census.gov/retail/mrts/about_the_surveys.html"}],"stemEn":"To practise telling nominal from real, suppose a shop sells just one item: last month 100 units at 10 each; this month still 100 units at 11 each. Which is most accurate?","optionsEn":["Sales rose 10%, but unit volume did not grow","Sales rose 10%, and unit volume also grew 10%","Sales were unchanged; only the unit price rose","After stripping out the price rise, unit volume fell about 9.1%"],"explanationEn":"Sales went from 1000 to 1100, but units stayed at 100. Real retail reports are in money terms and cannot be read directly as real consumption volume.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Sales went from 1000 to 1100, but units stayed at 100. Real retail reports are in money terms and cannot be read directly as real consumption volume.","Wrong: This month still sold 100 units, so quantity did not rise.","Wrong: Unchanged units do not mean unchanged sales; sales are price times quantity.","Wrong: 9.1% is not the change in units; the question states quantity was unchanged."]},{"id":"information-beginner-05","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[41,42],"stem":"同一期住房报告中，建筑许可增加，新屋开工减少。下面哪句话成立？","options":["许可增多代表当月落成住房增多","两项统计的是同一件事，报告矛盾","开工减少说明已批许可大批失效","获批计划增多，但实际动工减少"],"answer":3,"explanation":"许可和开工处在不同阶段，可以一升一降；获批不保证当月动工。","optionExplanations":["错误：许可是获批，不是已建成。","错误：两项统计的是不同阶段，并不矛盾。","错误：开工少不代表许可作废。","正确：许可与开工处在不同阶段，可以一升一降。"],"skills":["领先与实现","住房阶段"],"references":[{"title":"Census — New Residential Construction","url":"https://www.census.gov/construction/nrc/index.html"}],"stemEn":"In the same housing report, building permits rose and housing starts fell. Which statement holds?","optionsEn":["More permits mean more homes completed this month","The two measure the same thing, so the report contradicts itself","Fewer starts mean many approved permits have lapsed","More projects were approved, but fewer actually broke ground"],"explanationEn":"Permits and starts are different stages, so one can rise while the other falls; approval does not guarantee construction starts that month.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A permit is an approval, not a finished home.","Wrong: The two measure different stages and do not contradict.","Wrong: Fewer starts do not mean permits were cancelled.","Correct: Permits and starts are different stages, so one can rise while the other falls."]},{"id":"information-beginner-06","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[36,35],"stem":"假设某季度可支配个人收入为100单位，个人储蓄为6单位；下一季度收入为120，储蓄仍为6。新的个人储蓄率是多少？","options":["5%（6除以120，比率会下降）","6%（储蓄额没变，比率也不变）","7.2%（原储蓄率乘以收入增幅）","20%（等于收入增长的百分比）"],"answer":0,"explanation":"6÷120=5%；金额不变，比率也可以下降。","optionExplanations":["正确：6÷120=5%，金额不变比率也可以下降。","错误：分母变大了，比率会变。","错误：储蓄率应是储蓄除以收入。","错误：收入增速不是储蓄率。"],"skills":["比例","居民财务"],"references":[{"title":"BEA — Personal Saving Rate","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-saving-rate"}],"stemEn":"Suppose disposable personal income in a quarter is 100 units and personal saving is 6; next quarter income is 120 and saving is still 6. What is the new personal saving rate?","optionsEn":["5% (6 divided by 120; the rate falls)","6% (saving is unchanged, so the rate is too)","7.2% (the old rate times the income growth)","20% (equal to income growth)"],"explanationEn":"6 ÷ 120 = 5%; the amount can stay the same while the rate falls.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 6 ÷ 120 = 5%; the amount can stay the same while the rate falls.","Wrong: The denominator grew, so the rate changes.","Wrong: The saving rate is saving divided by income.","Wrong: Income growth is not the saving rate."]},{"id":"information-beginner-07","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[52,54],"stem":"假设居民用商业银行存款缴税100，资金转入财政部在美联储的TGA；美联储资产、现金及其他负债均不变。银行准备金会怎样变化？","options":["增加100，因为政府收到了资金","减少100，对应TGA增加100","不变，因为只是账户改了名称","减少200，税款与TGA各算一次"],"answer":1,"explanation":"美联储资产固定，TGA增加100由准备金减少100抵消。这并不等于股市必跌。","optionExplanations":["错误：资金进入TGA，是从准备金中转出。","正确：美联储资产固定，TGA增加100由准备金减少100抵消。","错误：这是不同的负债项目，会互相替换。","错误：同一笔钱只变动一次。"],"skills":["资金结算","准备金"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve — TGA and the Fed balance sheet","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/fluctuations-in-the-treasury-general-account-and-their-effect-on-the-feds-balance-sheet-20250806.html"}],"stemEn":"Suppose households pay 100 in taxes from commercial bank deposits, and the money moves into the Treasury's TGA at the Fed; Fed assets, currency and other liabilities are unchanged. How do bank reserves change?","optionsEn":["Up 100, because the government received money","Down 100, matching the 100 rise in the TGA","Unchanged, because only the account name changed","Down 200, counting the tax and the TGA once each"],"explanationEn":"With Fed assets fixed, the 100 rise in the TGA is offset by a 100 fall in reserves. This does not mean stocks must fall.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Money moving into the TGA is transferred out of reserves.","Correct: With Fed assets fixed, the 100 rise in the TGA is offset by a 100 fall in reserves.","Wrong: These are different liability items that replace each other.","Wrong: The same money moves only once."]},{"id":"information-beginner-08","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[61],"stem":"某次国债拍卖公布：投标总额240亿美元、接受投标总额100亿美元。按“投标总额÷接受总额”定义，投标倍数是多少？","options":["2.4倍","0.42倍","140倍","3.4倍"],"answer":0,"explanation":"240÷100=2.4。它是拍卖需求指标之一，不等同于国债价格涨幅。","optionExplanations":["240÷100=2.4。它是拍卖需求指标之一，不等同于国债价格涨幅。","这是接受总额除以投标总额，把分子分母倒置。","240减100得到金额差140，不是倍数。","相加再除以100不符合给出的定义。"],"skills":["拍卖需求","单位"],"references":[{"title":"TreasuryDirect — Auction announcements and results","url":"https://www.treasurydirect.gov/auctions/auction-results/"}],"stemEn":"A Treasury auction reports $24 billion tendered and $10 billion accepted. Using \"total tendered ÷ total accepted\", what is the bid-to-cover ratio?","optionsEn":["2.4","0.42","140","3.4"],"explanationEn":"24 ÷ 10 = 2.4. It is one measure of auction demand and is not the same as a rise in Treasury prices.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 24 ÷ 10 = 2.4. It is one measure of auction demand and is not the same as a rise in Treasury prices.","Wrong: This divides accepted by tendered, inverting the ratio.","Wrong: Subtracting gives a money gap, not a ratio.","Wrong: Adding and then dividing does not match the given definition."]},{"id":"information-beginner-09","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[64],"stem":"同一交易日，完整覆盖的三只同类现货加密ETF净流量分别为+80、-50、-10百万美元，均采用同一口径。该组ETF当日合计怎样？","options":["净流出20百万美元","净流入20百万美元","净流入80百万美元","净流入140百万美元"],"answer":1,"explanation":"带上正负号求和是+20百万美元；不能只看最热门的一只。","optionExplanations":["80-50-10为正20，不是负20。","带上正负号求和是+20百万美元；不能只看最热门的一只。","80只是一只ETF的净流入，遗漏了另外两只的净流出。","140是绝对值之和，不是净流量。"],"skills":["净流量汇总","平台范围"],"references":[{"title":"iShares — IBIT holdings, shares and net assets","url":"https://www.ishares.com/us/products/333011/ishares-bitcoin-trust-etf"}],"stemEn":"On one trading day, three similar spot crypto ETFs, fully covered and on the same basis, have net flows of +80, −50 and −10 million dollars. What is the group's total for the day?","optionsEn":["Net outflow of $20 million","Net inflow of $20 million","Net inflow of $80 million","Net inflow of $140 million"],"explanationEn":"Summing with signs gives +$20 million; you cannot look only at the most popular fund.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 80 − 50 − 10 is +20, not −20.","Correct: Summing with signs gives +$20 million; you cannot look only at the most popular fund.","Wrong: 80 is only one ETF's inflow and leaves out the other two outflows.","Wrong: 140 is the sum of absolute values, not the net flow."]},{"id":"information-beginner-10","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[65],"stem":"今天是4月20日。某稳定币最新公开鉴证报告只对3月31日的储备余额与流通币量作出结论。它直接支持哪项？","options":["证明4月20日储备仍足额覆盖币量","说明发行商整体业务已通过审计","仅对3月31日时点的储备给出结论","确保今后币价会稳定在1美元附近"],"answer":2,"explanation":"先看报告日期和鉴证范围；不要把时点储备鉴证扩展成实时全面保证。","optionExplanations":["错误：报告只覆盖3月31日，不能延伸到今天。","错误：鉴证范围只是储备与流通量。","正确：先看报告日期和鉴证范围。","错误：历史时点的鉴证不保证未来价格。"],"skills":["鉴证范围","信息时点"],"references":[{"title":"Circle — Reserve transparency and assurance reports","url":"https://www.circle.com/transparency"}],"stemEn":"Today is 20 April. A stablecoin's latest public attestation reports only on reserve balances and tokens outstanding as of 31 March. What does it directly support?","optionsEn":["That reserves still fully cover tokens on 20 April","That the issuer's whole business has passed an audit","A conclusion about reserves at the 31 March point only","That the token will stay near $1 from now on"],"explanationEn":"Check the report date and scope first; don't stretch a point-in-time reserve attestation into a real-time, all-round guarantee.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The report covers only 31 March and cannot be extended to today.","Wrong: The attestation covers only reserves and tokens outstanding.","Correct: Check the report date and the attestation scope first.","Wrong: An attestation at a past date does not guarantee future prices."]},{"id":"information-beginner-11","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[66,68],"stem":"假设某央行会前政策利率5.00%，市场已充分计入降息至4.50%；实际只降至4.75%。只比较这次利率决定与会前预期，结果应称为什么？","options":["相对预期偏松25个基点，因为利率下降了","与预期一致，因为方向同样是降息","相对预期偏紧50个基点，因为少降一半","相对预期偏紧25个基点，因为少降了25"],"answer":3,"explanation":"实际降息25个基点，但比预期少降25个基点。市场反应比较的是已计入的路径。","optionExplanations":["要与预期而非会前利率比较。","方向相同，但幅度不一致。","少降的是25个基点，不是50。","正确，实际只降25，预期降50。"],"skills":["基点","政策意外"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve — Monetary policy goals and transmission","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/monetary-policy-what-are-its-goals-how-does-it-work.htm"}],"stemEn":"Suppose a central bank's policy rate is 5.00% before the meeting and markets fully priced a cut to 4.50%; it actually cut only to 4.75%. Comparing only this decision with prior expectations, what should the result be called?","optionsEn":["25 bp more dovish than expected, because rates fell","In line with expectations, because the direction was a cut","50 bp more hawkish than expected, because the cut was half","25 bp more hawkish than expected, because it cut 25 less"],"explanationEn":"It cut 25 bp, but 25 bp less than expected. Market reaction compares against the path already priced in.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Compare with expectations, not the pre-meeting rate.","Wrong: The direction matched, but the size did not.","Wrong: The shortfall was 25 bp, not 50.","Correct: It cut only 25, against 50 expected."]},{"id":"information-beginner-12","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[70],"stem":"某周EIA商业原油库存（不含战略储备）市场预期减少200万桶，实际减少500万桶。只看库存相对预期这一项，哪项正确？","options":["比预期少去库300万桶，对油价偏支持","比预期多去库300万桶，对油价偏利空","库存下降500万桶，即需求增加500万桶","比预期多去库300万桶，对油价偏支持"],"answer":3,"explanation":"-500万比-200万少300万，供应缓冲低于预期，可支持油价；需求、进出口等仍需合看。","optionExplanations":["错误：实际去库比预期更多，不是更少。","错误：多去库代表供应缓冲更小，偏支持油价。","错误：库存变化还受进出口等因素影响。","正确：-500万比-200万少300万，供应缓冲低于预期。"],"skills":["预期差","能源传导"],"references":[{"title":"EIA — Weekly Petroleum Status Report","url":"https://www.eia.gov/petroleum/supply/weekly/"}],"stemEn":"In one week, EIA commercial crude inventories (excluding the strategic reserve) were expected to fall 2 million barrels and actually fell 5 million. Looking only at inventories versus expectations, which is correct?","optionsEn":["A draw 3 million smaller than expected, supportive for oil","A draw 3 million larger than expected, bearish for oil","A 5 million fall in inventory means demand rose 5 million","A draw 3 million larger than expected, supportive for oil"],"explanationEn":"−5 million is 3 million less than −2 million, so the supply buffer is smaller than expected, which can support oil; demand, imports and exports still need to be read together.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The actual draw was larger than expected, not smaller.","Wrong: A larger draw means a smaller supply buffer, which leans supportive for oil.","Wrong: Inventory changes also depend on imports, exports and more.","Correct: −5 million is 3 million less than −2 million, so the supply buffer is smaller than expected."]},{"id":"information-advanced-01","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[1],"stem":"假设某CPI同比指数采用同一未季调口径：去年本月指数100，本月103；市场预期同比3.2%。上月公布同比3.4%。哪项同时描述了价格水平与本次意外？","options":["物价同比上涨3.0%，且低于预期0.2个百分点","物价同比上涨3.0%，且高于预期0.2个百分点","物价同比上涨3.2%，且与市场预期基本一致","物价同比上涨3.4%，且高于预期0.2个百分点"],"answer":0,"explanation":"103÷100-1=3%；3%-3.2%=-0.2个百分点。这是低于预期的通胀涨幅。","optionExplanations":["正确：103÷100-1=3%，比预期3.2%低0.2个百分点。","错误：3.0%低于预期3.2%。","错误：3.2%是预期值，不是实际值。","错误：3.4%是上月读数，不是本月。"],"skills":["指数计算","同比与环比"],"references":[{"title":"BLS — Consumer Price Index FAQ","url":"https://www.bls.gov/cpi/questions-and-answers.htm"}],"stemEn":"Suppose a CPI index on one non-seasonally-adjusted basis was 100 in the same month last year and is 103 this month; consensus for the year-over-year rate was 3.2%, and last month's reported rate was 3.4%. Which describes both the price level and this surprise?","optionsEn":["Prices up 3.0% year over year, 0.2 point below expectations","Prices up 3.0% year over year, 0.2 point above expectations","Prices up 3.2% year over year, broadly in line with consensus","Prices up 3.4% year over year, 0.2 point above expectations"],"explanationEn":"103 ÷ 100 − 1 = 3%; 3% − 3.2% = −0.2 percentage point. This is inflation below expectations.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 103 ÷ 100 − 1 = 3%, which is 0.2 point below the 3.2% expected.","Wrong: 3.0% is below the expected 3.2%.","Wrong: 3.2% is the forecast, not the actual.","Wrong: 3.4% is last month's reading, not this month's."]},{"id":"information-advanced-02","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[11],"stem":"某次非农公布当月新增就业25万人；此前两个月的新增就业分别从20万修正为15万、从18万修正为12万。相较发布前已经知道的累计就业路径，加入新月与修正后，累计净增加多少？","options":["14万人","25万人","36万人","11万人"],"answer":0,"explanation":"前两月合计下修5+6=11万，再加新月25万，累计路径净增加14万。它不是当月新增人数。","optionExplanations":["前两月合计下修5+6=11万，再加新月25万，累计路径净增加14万。它不是当月新增人数。","25万是新月数字，未计此前月份下修。","把下修11万错加成上修，才会得到36万。","11万只是两次下修的绝对值，遗漏了新月新增。"],"skills":["数据修正","增量合并"],"references":[{"title":"BLS — Employment Situation Technical Note","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.tn.htm"}],"stemEn":"A payrolls report shows 250,000 jobs added this month; the two prior months are revised from 200,000 to 150,000 and from 180,000 to 120,000. Compared with the cumulative path known before the release, how much does the cumulative total rise net once the new month and revisions are included?","optionsEn":["140,000","250,000","360,000","110,000"],"explanationEn":"The two prior months are revised down a combined 50,000 + 60,000 = 110,000; adding the new 250,000 gives a net 140,000. This is not the number of jobs added this month.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The two prior months are revised down a combined 50,000 + 60,000 = 110,000; adding the new 250,000 gives a net 140,000. This is not the number of jobs added this month.","Wrong: 250,000 is the new month alone, ignoring the downward revisions.","Wrong: You get 360,000 only by wrongly adding the 110,000 revision as an upgrade.","Wrong: 110,000 is only the size of the two downward revisions and leaves out the new month."]},{"id":"information-advanced-03","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[21],"stem":"假设真实GDP同一价格口径从上季100增至本季101。按BEA季度环比折年率算法，折年增速四舍五入到小数点后两位是多少？","options":["4.00%","4.06%","3.03%","12.68%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"(101÷100)^4-1约4.0604%，因此约4.06%；它不是未来一年实际增长预测。","optionExplanations":["错误：这是简单乘以4，没有复利。","正确：(101÷100)^4-1约4.06%。","错误：这是用3次方折算，次数错了。","错误：这是用12次方折算，应为4次方。"],"skills":["折年率","复利"],"references":[{"title":"BEA — Why quarterly growth is annualized","url":"https://www.bea.gov/help/faq/122"}],"stemEn":"Suppose real GDP at constant prices rises from 100 last quarter to 101 this quarter. Using the BEA's annualised quarterly growth method, what is the annualised rate to two decimal places?","optionsEn":["4.00%","4.06%","3.03%","12.68%"],"explanationEn":"(101 ÷ 100)^4 − 1 ≈ 4.0604%, so about 4.06%; it is not a forecast of real growth over the next year.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This simply multiplies by 4 without compounding.","Correct: (101 ÷ 100)^4 − 1 ≈ 4.06%.","Wrong: This compounds to the 3rd power, the wrong exponent.","Wrong: This compounds to the 12th power; it should be the 4th."]},{"id":"information-advanced-04","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[33,31],"stem":"某简化消费篮子的名义支出从100增至101，完全匹配该篮子的价格指数从100增至102。忽略统计链式加总问题，以“名义金额÷价格指数”换算，实际消费量增速四舍五入到小数点后两位是多少？","options":["实际消费量下降1.00%","实际消费量增长1.00%","实际消费量下降0.98%","实际消费量增长0.99%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"1.01÷1.02-1约-0.9804%；金额略升仍可对应真实消费量下降。","optionExplanations":["错误：这是用差值直接相减。","错误：名义涨幅小于价格涨幅，实际量下降。","正确：1.01÷1.02-1约-0.98%。","错误：这是把除法颠倒了。"],"skills":["名义与实际","通胀调整"],"references":[{"title":"BEA — NIPA Handbook, real measures and price indexes","url":"https://www.bea.gov/resources/methodologies/nipa-handbook"}],"stemEn":"Nominal spending on a simplified basket rises from 100 to 101, and a price index exactly matching that basket rises from 100 to 102. Ignoring chain-weighting issues and converting as nominal ÷ price index, what is real consumption growth to two decimal places?","optionsEn":["Real consumption falls 1.00%","Real consumption rises 1.00%","Real consumption falls 0.98%","Real consumption rises 0.99%"],"explanationEn":"1.01 ÷ 1.02 − 1 ≈ −0.9804%; spending can rise slightly while real consumption falls.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This subtracts the changes directly.","Wrong: Nominal growth is below price growth, so real volume falls.","Correct: 1.01 ÷ 1.02 − 1 ≈ −0.98%.","Wrong: This inverts the division."]},{"id":"information-advanced-05","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[41,42],"stem":"某月新屋开工报“季调折年率120万套”，同表未季调实际当月开工为9万套。哪句话正确？","options":["120万÷12=10万，所以9万有误","120万是过去12个月实际开工的累计","120万是全年计划数，9万是当月实绩","折年率是季调节奏换算，9万不矛盾"],"answer":3,"explanation":"折年率描述经季调后的节奏，不是原始当月套数，也不是已经发生的全年总量。","optionExplanations":["错误：季调与原始当月数本就不同。","错误：折年率不是已发生的全年总量。","错误：折年率不是计划数。","正确：折年率描述季调后的节奏，不是原始当月套数。"],"skills":["季调","年率与实际量"],"references":[{"title":"Census — New Residential Construction","url":"https://www.census.gov/construction/nrc/index.html"}],"stemEn":"One month's housing starts are reported at a \"seasonally adjusted annual rate of 1.2 million\", while the same table shows 90,000 actual, unadjusted starts for the month. Which statement is correct?","optionsEn":["1.2 million ÷ 12 = 100,000, so 90,000 is wrong","1.2 million is the actual total of the past 12 months","1.2 million is the full-year plan; 90,000 is the month's actual","The annual rate converts the adjusted pace, so 90,000 is not a contradiction"],"explanationEn":"The annual rate describes the seasonally adjusted pace; it is neither the raw monthly count nor a full-year total that has already happened.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Seasonally adjusted and raw monthly figures naturally differ.","Wrong: The annual rate is not a full-year total that has already happened.","Wrong: The annual rate is not a plan.","Correct: The annual rate describes the seasonally adjusted pace, not the raw monthly count."]},{"id":"information-advanced-06","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[51,52,53,54],"stem":"在简化美联储资产负债表中，准备金=总资产−现金−TGA−ON RRP−其他负债。某周资产减少20、现金增加10、TGA增加30、ON RRP减少40，其他负债不变，单位均为十亿美元。准备金变化是多少？","options":["增加20","增加40","减少100","减少20"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Δ准备金=-20-10-30-(-40)=-20，即减少200亿美元；ON RRP下降只抵消了部分压力。","optionExplanations":["忽略部分负债变化或颠倒符号会得到正数。","40是ON RRP下降金额，不是所有项目合并后的结果。","将ON RRP下降也当作抽走准备金，会把符号用反。","Δ准备金=-20-10-30-(-40)=-20，即减少200亿美元；ON RRP下降只抵消了部分压力。"],"skills":["资产负债表","符号计算"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve — TGA and the Fed balance sheet","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/notes/feds-notes/fluctuations-in-the-treasury-general-account-and-their-effect-on-the-feds-balance-sheet-20250806.html"}],"stemEn":"In a simplified Fed balance sheet, reserves = total assets − currency − TGA − ON RRP − other liabilities. In one week assets fall 20, currency rises 10, the TGA rises 30 and ON RRP falls 40, with other liabilities unchanged, all in billions of dollars. How do reserves change?","optionsEn":["Up 20","Up 40","Down 100","Down 20"],"explanationEn":"Δreserves = −20 − 10 − 30 − (−40) = −20, a fall of $20 billion; the drop in ON RRP offsets only part of the pressure.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Ignoring some liability changes or flipping signs gives a positive number.","Wrong: 40 is the drop in ON RRP, not the combined result of all items.","Wrong: Treating the ON RRP drop as also draining reserves flips its sign.","Correct: Δreserves = −20 − 10 − 30 − (−40) = −20, a fall of $20 billion; the drop in ON RRP offsets only part of the pressure."]},{"id":"information-advanced-07","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[59],"stem":"仅为演示SOFR使用的“成交量加权中位数”，假设所有合资格隔夜回购都已筛选完：4.80%的成交量20，4.90%的成交量40，5.20%的成交量40。累计量越过50%的利率是哪一个？","options":["4.90%，该档累计量达60%","5.00%，按成交量加权平均数","4.97%，三个利率的简单平均数","4.80%，排在最前面的最低利率"],"answer":0,"explanation":"总量100；4.80%累计20，加入4.90%累计60，因此中位数在4.90%这一档。","optionExplanations":["正确：4.80%累计20，加入4.90%累计60，中位数在4.90%。","错误：加权平均不是中位数。","错误：简单平均也不是加权中位数。","错误：累计量在这里只有20%。"],"skills":["加权中位数","融资成本"],"references":[{"title":"NY Fed — SOFR definition and methodology","url":"https://www.newyorkfed.org/markets/reference-rates/sofr"}],"stemEn":"Just to illustrate the volume-weighted median used by SOFR, assume all eligible overnight repo trades are already screened: volume 20 at 4.80%, 40 at 4.90% and 40 at 5.20%. At which rate does cumulative volume cross 50%?","optionsEn":["4.90%, where cumulative volume reaches 60%","5.00%, the volume-weighted mean","4.97%, the simple average of the three rates","4.80%, the lowest rate, listed first"],"explanationEn":"Total volume is 100; 4.80% brings the cumulative total to 20, and adding 4.90% brings it to 60, so the median is in the 4.90% bucket.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 4.80% gives 20 cumulative, adding 4.90% gives 60, so the median is 4.90%.","Wrong: A weighted mean is not a median.","Wrong: A simple average is not a weighted median either.","Wrong: Cumulative volume here is only 20%."]},{"id":"information-advanced-08","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[62,63],"stem":"假设某季度财政部发行国债9000亿美元，其中7000亿用于偿还到期本金；无回购等其他本金调整。该季度政府收入5000亿、支出6500亿。国债净发行与预算赤字分别为多少？","options":["9000亿、1500亿","2000亿、6500亿","1500亿、2000亿","2000亿、1500亿"],"answer":3,"explanation":"净发行9000-7000=2000亿；赤字6500-5000=1500亿。现金余额等融资调整可使两者不同。","optionExplanations":["9000亿是总发行，未扣到期本金。","6500亿是支出，不是支出减收入。","把净发行与赤字交换了；两者也不要求每季度完全相等。","净发行9000-7000=2000亿；赤字6500-5000=1500亿。现金余额等融资调整可使两者不同。"],"skills":["净发行","赤字与融资"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Treasury — Quarterly refunding and borrowing estimates","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/policy-issues/financing-the-government/quarterly-refunding"},{"title":"U.S. Treasury — Understanding the national deficit","url":"https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/americas-finance-guide/national-deficit/"}],"stemEn":"Suppose the Treasury issues $900 billion of debt in a quarter, $700 billion of it to repay maturing principal, with no buybacks or other principal adjustments. That quarter government receipts are $500 billion and outlays $650 billion. What are net issuance and the budget deficit?","optionsEn":["$900 billion and $150 billion","$200 billion and $650 billion","$150 billion and $200 billion","$200 billion and $150 billion"],"explanationEn":"Net issuance is 900 − 700 = $200 billion; the deficit is 650 − 500 = $150 billion. Financing adjustments such as the cash balance can make the two differ.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: $900 billion is gross issuance, before netting maturing principal.","Wrong: $650 billion is outlays, not outlays minus receipts.","Wrong: This swaps net issuance and the deficit; the two need not match each quarter anyway.","Correct: Net issuance is 900 − 700 = $200 billion; the deficit is 650 − 500 = $150 billion. Financing adjustments such as the cash balance can make the two differ."]},{"id":"information-advanced-09","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[64],"stem":"假设一只只持有比特币的ETF，期初100枚币、每枚100美元；期末110枚、每枚120美元。忽略现金、费用与其他资产。若把期末多出的币全部按期末价格计，新增持币价值与总资产增幅分别是多少？","options":["1200美元、32%","3200美元、32%","1200美元、20%","1000美元、10%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"新增10枚×120=1200；资产由10000变13200，增长32%。资产涨幅同时含币价变化，不等于净流入增幅。","optionExplanations":["新增10枚×120=1200；资产由10000变13200，增长32%。资产涨幅同时含币价变化，不等于净流入增幅。","3200是总资产增加额，包含原有100枚的价格上涨。","20%只是币价涨幅；持币数量也增长。","1000按期初价给新增币估值，不符合题设；10%仅为持币数量增幅。"],"skills":["价格与资金","ETF资产拆分"],"references":[{"title":"iShares — IBIT holdings, shares and net assets","url":"https://www.ishares.com/us/products/333011/ishares-bitcoin-trust-etf"}],"stemEn":"Suppose an ETF holds only bitcoin: 100 coins at $100 each at the start, 110 coins at $120 each at the end. Ignoring cash, fees and other assets, and valuing all the extra coins at the ending price, what are the value of the added coins and the growth in total assets?","optionsEn":["$1,200 and 32%","$3,200 and 32%","$1,200 and 20%","$1,000 and 10%"],"explanationEn":"10 new coins × 120 = 1,200; assets go from 10,000 to 13,200, up 32%. Asset growth also includes the price change, so it is not the same as the growth from net inflows.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 10 new coins × 120 = 1,200; assets go from 10,000 to 13,200, up 32%. Asset growth also includes the price change, so it is not the same as the growth from net inflows.","Wrong: 3,200 is the total rise in assets, including the price gain on the original 100 coins.","Wrong: 20% is only the price gain; the number of coins also grew.","Wrong: 1,000 values the new coins at the starting price, which the question rules out; 10% is only the growth in coin count."]},{"id":"information-advanced-10","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[65],"stem":"某教学模型中，某稳定币流通负债100，储备为现金30、短债80。假设短债立即卖出只能收回账面价值的95%，现金足额可用，且没有其他费用或负债。本次压力假设下可动用储备及覆盖率是多少？","options":["110、110%","106、106%","104.5、104.5%","95、95%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"30+80×95%=106；106÷100=106%。这只回答指定压力假设，不是对真实发行商的保证。","optionExplanations":["110是未施加折价的账面储备，未按压力假设计算。","30+80×95%=106；106÷100=106%。这只回答指定压力假设，不是对真实发行商的保证。","将5%折价错误施加到现金和短债全部110上会得到104.5。","95%是短债回收率，不是混合储备对负债的覆盖率。"],"skills":["储备压力测试","资产与负债"],"references":[{"title":"Circle — Reserve transparency and assurance reports","url":"https://www.circle.com/transparency"}],"stemEn":"In a teaching model, a stablecoin has 100 of outstanding liabilities, with reserves of 30 in cash and 80 in short-term bills. Suppose the bills can be sold immediately for only 95% of book value, cash is fully available, and there are no other costs or liabilities. Under this stress assumption, what are usable reserves and coverage?","optionsEn":["110 and 110%","106 and 106%","104.5 and 104.5%","95 and 95%"],"explanationEn":"30 + 80 × 95% = 106; 106 ÷ 100 = 106%. This answers only the stated stress assumption and is no guarantee about a real issuer.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 110 is book reserves with no haircut, not the stressed figure.","Correct: 30 + 80 × 95% = 106; 106 ÷ 100 = 106%. This answers only the stated stress assumption and is no guarantee about a real issuer.","Wrong: Applying the 5% haircut to the full 110 including cash gives 104.5, which is wrong.","Wrong: 95% is the recovery rate on the bills, not the coverage of liabilities by the mixed reserves."]},{"id":"information-advanced-11","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[66,67,68,69],"stem":"某简化估值模型只有一年后确定收到的100元，没有其他现金流。折现率由5%升至6%，现金流预期和风险溢价均不变。现值约怎样变化？","options":["从95.24降至94.00","从95.24降至94.34","从95.00降至94.00","从95.24升至96.15"],"answer":1,"explanation":"100÷1.05≈95.24，100÷1.06≈94.34。它说明一条利率传导渠道，不是对真实市场的单变量预测。","optionExplanations":["错误：94.00是按100×(1-6%)得出的错误数。","正确：100÷1.05≈95.24，100÷1.06≈94.34。","错误：现值应按1/(1+r)折现。","错误：折现率上升，现值下降。"],"skills":["折现","利率传导"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve — Monetary policy goals and transmission","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/monetary-policy-what-are-its-goals-how-does-it-work.htm"}],"stemEn":"A simplified valuation model has only a certain cash flow of 100 in one year, nothing else. The discount rate rises from 5% to 6% with cash-flow expectations and risk premium unchanged. Roughly how does present value change?","optionsEn":["From 95.24 down to 94.00","From 95.24 down to 94.34","From 95.00 down to 94.00","From 95.24 up to 96.15"],"explanationEn":"100 ÷ 1.05 ≈ 95.24 and 100 ÷ 1.06 ≈ 94.34. This shows one channel of rate transmission, not a single-variable forecast of real markets.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 94.00 comes from the incorrect 100 × (1 − 6%).","Correct: 100 ÷ 1.05 ≈ 95.24 and 100 ÷ 1.06 ≈ 94.34.","Wrong: Present value should be discounted by 1/(1 + r).","Wrong: A higher discount rate lowers present value."]},{"id":"information-advanced-12","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[71],"stem":"某周美国本土48州地下工作气库存（无重分类或其他统计调整）：前周3000、本周3080、当周五年均值3100，单位为十亿立方英尺；市场原本预期本周注入100。只根据这些数字，哪项正确？","options":["实际注入80，库存比五年均值高20","实际注入100，库存比五年均值低20","实际注入80，比预期多20，库存低于五年均值20","实际注入80，比预期少20，库存低于五年均值20"],"answer":3,"explanation":"注入量3080-3000=80，较预期少20；库存水平3080-3100=-20。注入仍为正，不等于库存下降。","optionExplanations":["3080小于3100，是低20而不是高20。","实际注入由3080-3000算出为80；100只是预期。","80少于预期100，方向反了。","注入量3080-3000=80，较预期少20；库存水平3080-3100=-20。注入仍为正，不等于库存下降。"],"skills":["变化与水平","能源基准"],"references":[{"title":"EIA — Weekly Natural Gas Storage Report","url":"https://ir.eia.gov/ngs/ngs.html"}],"stemEn":"Weekly working gas in underground storage for the Lower 48 (no reclassifications or other adjustments): prior week 3000, this week 3080, five-year average for the week 3100, all in billion cubic feet; the market expected an injection of 100. Based only on these numbers, which is correct?","optionsEn":["Actual injection 80; storage 20 above the five-year average","Actual injection 100; storage 20 below the five-year average","Actual injection 80, 20 more than expected; storage 20 below average","Actual injection 80, 20 less than expected; storage 20 below average"],"explanationEn":"The injection is 3080 − 3000 = 80, 20 less than expected; the storage level is 3080 − 3100 = −20. A positive injection is not a fall in storage.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 3080 is below 3100, so it is 20 below, not above.","Wrong: The actual injection is 3080 − 3000 = 80; 100 was only the forecast.","Wrong: 80 is less than the expected 100, so the direction is reversed.","Correct: The injection is 3080 − 3000 = 80, 20 less than expected; the storage level is 3080 − 3100 = −20. A positive injection is not a fall in storage."]},{"id":"information-beginner-13","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[3],"stem":"某月PCE物价指数的水平值从123.0升到123.4。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["价格水平较上月约上升0.4%","价格水平较上月约下降0.33%","价格水平较上月约上升0.33%","价格水平较上月约上升3.3%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"(123.4−123.0)÷123.0≈0.33%。指数点本身不是涨幅，要换算成环比或同比。","optionExplanations":["错误：指数点数不是百分比。","错误：指数上升表示价格上升。","正确：(123.4−123.0)÷123.0≈0.33%。","错误：小数点位置错了。"],"skills":["水平与变化","单位换算"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expenditures-price-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"One month the PCE price index level rises from 123.0 to 123.4. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["The price level rose about 0.4% from last month","The price level fell about 0.33% from last month","The price level rose about 0.33% from last month","The price level rose about 3.3% from last month"],"explanationEn":"(123.4 − 123.0) ÷ 123.0 ≈ 0.33%. Index points are not a growth rate; convert them to a monthly or yearly change.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Index points are not a percentage.","Wrong: A rising index means prices rose.","Correct: (123.4 − 123.0) ÷ 123.0 ≈ 0.33%.","Wrong: The decimal point is misplaced."]},{"id":"information-advanced-13","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[4],"stem":"核心PCE月率初值0.3%。下个月发布时，上月被修订为0.2%，新月份为0.3%。较完整的描述是？","options":["上月下修，但近两月累计通胀不受影响","近两月累计通胀比原先以为的更高","两月读数相同，所以没有新增信息","上月下修，近两月累计通胀低于预估"],"answer":3,"explanation":"读核心PCE要同时看修订；只比较新值与旧初值会忽略前值变化。","optionExplanations":["错误：上月下修会改变累计水平。","错误：上月被下修，累计更低。","错误：前值修订本身就是新增信息。","正确：读核心PCE要同时看修订。"],"skills":["修订","累计变化"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expenditures-price-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The first estimate of monthly core PCE was 0.3%. In the next month's release, that month is revised to 0.2% and the new month is 0.3%. What is the more complete description?","optionsEn":["Last month was revised down, but two-month cumulative inflation is unaffected","Two-month cumulative inflation is higher than previously thought","Both months read the same, so there is no new information","Last month was revised down, so two-month cumulative inflation is lower than thought"],"explanationEn":"Read core PCE together with its revisions; comparing only the new value with the old first estimate misses the change in the prior month.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A downward revision to last month changes the cumulative level.","Wrong: Last month was revised down, so the cumulative total is lower.","Wrong: The revision itself is new information.","Correct: Read core PCE together with its revisions."]},{"id":"information-beginner-14","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[5],"stem":"PPI报告显示：最终需求季调环比+0.2%，未季调12个月同比+2.1%。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["同比应约等于环比乘以12，对不上就说明数据有误","季调环比为正，说明价格高于一年前同月的水平","PPI记录居民在零售端实际支付的价格，与CPI同口径","环比与同比的比较基期不同，两者可以同时成立"],"answer":3,"explanation":"环比比较上一个月并做季调，同比比较一年前且未季调。","optionExplanations":["月度环比会波动，同比是12个月累计变化，不能简单乘12来验证。","环比为正只说明比上个月高，与一年前比较的是同比。","PPI站在卖方，记录生产者出售时收到的价格，不是居民付的价格。","环比比上一个月且季调，同比比一年前且未季调，基期不同所以可以并存。"],"skills":["环比与同比","口径"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ppi.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A PPI report shows final demand +0.2% month over month seasonally adjusted, and +2.1% over 12 months not seasonally adjusted. Which reading is correct?","optionsEn":["Year over year should be about monthly × 12; a mismatch means bad data","A positive adjusted monthly change means prices are above the same month last year","PPI records prices households pay at retail, on the same basis as CPI","Monthly and yearly changes use different base periods, so both can hold"],"explanationEn":"The monthly change compares with last month and is seasonally adjusted; the yearly change compares with a year ago and is not.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Monthly changes fluctuate and the yearly change is a 12-month cumulative change, so multiplying by 12 is no check.","Wrong: A positive monthly change only means higher than last month; comparing with a year ago is the yearly change.","Wrong: PPI takes the seller's side, recording prices producers receive, not prices households pay.","Correct: The monthly change compares with last month and is seasonally adjusted, the yearly with a year ago unadjusted; different bases mean both can hold."]},{"id":"information-advanced-14","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[6],"stem":"某月整体PPI环比−0.3%，剔除食品与能源的核心PPI环比+0.3%。较合理的解读是？","options":["核心上升属统计误差，整体下降才反映真实趋势","整体下降说明生产端价格压力已经全面消退","核心转正说明食品能源价格同期也在上涨","食品或能源拖累整体，核心价格压力仍在"],"answer":3,"explanation":"两者方向不同时，先拆分波动大的分项，再判断趋势。","optionExplanations":["核心剔除了噪声大的分项，不能当作误差随意忽略。","核心仍上涨，说明压力并未消退，不能只凭整体数字下结论。","整体为负而核心为正，恰恰更可能是食品能源在下降。","整体为负而核心为正，通常说明波动大的食品能源在拖累整体，核心压力仍在。"],"skills":["分项拆解","波动来源"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ppi.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"One month headline PPI is −0.3% month over month, while core PPI excluding food and energy is +0.3%. What is the more reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["The core rise is statistical noise; only the headline fall shows the real trend","The headline fall shows producer price pressure has fully eased","Core turning positive means food and energy prices also rose","Food or energy dragged the headline down; core price pressure remains"],"explanationEn":"When the two move in different directions, break out the volatile components first and then judge the trend.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Core strips out the noisy components and cannot simply be dismissed as error.","Wrong: Core is still rising, so pressure has not eased; don't judge from the headline alone.","Wrong: A negative headline with positive core more likely means food and energy fell.","Correct: A negative headline with positive core usually means volatile food and energy dragged the total down, while core pressure remains."]},{"id":"information-beginner-15","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[7],"stem":"进口物价指数全部进口品环比+0.5%，但剔除燃料后的进口品价格+0.0%。这更可能说明什么？","options":["本月涨幅主要由燃料价格的上涨带来","非燃料商品的涨幅大于燃料，把整体向上拉动","美元走强把进口品的美元价格推高","进口数量增加，非燃料类需求同步升温"],"answer":0,"explanation":"先比较全部与剔除燃料的分项，可以看出涨幅来源。","optionExplanations":["剔除燃料后几乎持平，说明0.5%的上涨主要来自燃料分项。","剔除燃料后为0.0%，说明非燃料并未上涨。","美元走强通常压低以美元计价的进口价格，且读数无法单凭此推出。","进口物价指数衡量价格而不是数量。"],"skills":["分项来源","价格与数量"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ximpim.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The import price index for all imports is +0.5% month over month, but imports excluding fuel are +0.0%. What does this more likely show?","optionsEn":["This month's rise came mainly from higher fuel prices","Non-fuel goods rose more than fuel and pulled the total up","A stronger dollar pushed up the dollar prices of imports","Import volumes rose, with non-fuel demand heating up too"],"explanationEn":"Comparing the total with the ex-fuel component shows where the rise came from.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Ex-fuel is almost flat, so the 0.5% rise came mainly from fuel.","Wrong: Ex-fuel is 0.0%, so non-fuel goods did not rise.","Wrong: A stronger dollar usually lowers dollar-priced import prices, and the readings alone cannot show this.","Wrong: The import price index measures prices, not volumes."]},{"id":"information-advanced-15","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[8],"stem":"出口物价指数：全部出口品环比+0.6%，其中农产品出口+3.0%，非农产品出口+0.2%。较完整的描述是？","options":["非农产品涨幅拉动整体，农产品只起次要作用","农产品涨价是主因，非农产品涨幅较为温和","出口价格普遍大幅上涨，农产品与非农相差不大","出口数量上升约0.6%，其中农产品数量增长最多"],"answer":1,"explanation":"农产品价格波动大，分项拆开后才知道总体上涨来自哪里。","optionExplanations":["非农只涨0.2%，不可能是整体上涨的主因。","农产品+3.0%远高于非农+0.2%，总体上涨主要来自农产品。","3.0%与0.2%相差悬殊，不能说两者差不多。","出口物价指数衡量价格，不是出口数量。"],"skills":["分项","口径"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ximpim.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Export price index: all exports +0.6% month over month, with agricultural exports +3.0% and non-agricultural exports +0.2%. What is the more complete description?","optionsEn":["Non-agricultural gains drove the total; agriculture played a minor role","Agricultural prices were the main driver; non-agricultural gains were modest","Export prices rose broadly and sharply, with little gap between the two","Export volumes rose about 0.6%, led by agricultural volumes"],"explanationEn":"Agricultural prices are volatile; only by breaking out the components can you see where the overall rise came from.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Non-agricultural rose only 0.2%, so it cannot be the main driver.","Correct: Agriculture's +3.0% far exceeds non-agricultural +0.2%, so the overall rise came mainly from agriculture.","Wrong: 3.0% and 0.2% are far apart, so they are not similar.","Wrong: The export price index measures prices, not export volumes."]},{"id":"information-beginner-16","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[9],"stem":"ECI报告：总薪酬季调季度变化+0.9%，未季调12个月变化+3.9%。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["一个对比上季度，一个对比一年前","季度变化乘以4应等于12个月变化","0.9%是年化值，3.9%是单季涨幅","ECI等同于平均时薪，只是按季度发布"],"answer":0,"explanation":"ECI按固定岗位结构比较薪酬成本，季度与12个月两个口径各有用途。","optionExplanations":["0.9%是比上一季度的变化，3.9%是比一年前的变化，两个基期不同。","季度变化会波动，12个月变化是累计结果，不必等于季度乘4。","3.9%是12个月变化，不是单季涨幅。","ECI按固定岗位结构衡量薪酬成本，与平均时薪不是同一指标。"],"skills":["期间","口径差异"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/eci.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"An ECI report: total compensation +0.9% quarter over quarter seasonally adjusted, +3.9% over 12 months not seasonally adjusted. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["One compares with last quarter, the other with a year ago","The quarterly change times 4 should equal the 12-month change","0.9% is annualised and 3.9% is a single-quarter rise","The ECI is the same as average hourly earnings, just published quarterly"],"explanationEn":"The ECI compares compensation costs on a fixed job mix; the quarterly and 12-month measures each have their uses.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 0.9% is the change from the previous quarter and 3.9% the change from a year ago; the bases differ.","Wrong: Quarterly changes fluctuate and the 12-month change is cumulative, so it need not equal 4 times the quarter.","Wrong: 3.9% is the 12-month change, not a single quarter.","Wrong: The ECI measures compensation cost on a fixed job mix and is not the same as average hourly earnings."]},{"id":"information-advanced-16","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[10],"stem":"密歇根大学报告：未来1年通胀预期从3.4%降到3.0%，未来5—10年预期维持3.0%。初值只覆盖当月部分样本。较稳妥的解读是？","options":["短期与长期预期均明显回落，通胀压力已经缓解","短期预期回落、长期持平，初值仍可能被修订","预期降至3.0%说明实际通胀已经降到3.0%","初值与终值通常一致，之后一般不再修订"],"answer":1,"explanation":"先区分两个预期期限，再记录是初值还是终值。","optionExplanations":["长期预期维持3.0%，并没有下降。","1年预期从3.4%降到3.0%，5—10年维持3.0%，初值只覆盖部分样本。","预期是调查读数，不等于实际CPI通胀。","初值只覆盖部分样本，终值可能修订。"],"skills":["期限","初值与终值"],"references":[{"title":"密歇根大学消费者调查：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.sca.isr.umich.edu/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A University of Michigan report: 1-year inflation expectations fall from 3.4% to 3.0%, while 5–10-year expectations hold at 3.0%. The preliminary reading covers only part of the month's sample. What is the more careful reading?","optionsEn":["Both short- and long-term expectations fell clearly, so inflation pressure has eased","Short-term expectations fell, long-term held, and the preliminary reading may still be revised","Expectations at 3.0% mean actual inflation has fallen to 3.0%","Preliminary and final readings usually match and are rarely revised"],"explanationEn":"First separate the two expectation horizons, then note whether it is the preliminary or final reading.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Long-term expectations held at 3.0% and did not fall.","Correct: 1-year expectations fell from 3.4% to 3.0%, 5–10-year held at 3.0%, and the preliminary reading covers only part of the sample.","Wrong: Expectations are a survey reading, not actual CPI inflation.","Wrong: The preliminary reading covers only part of the sample, so the final may be revised."]},{"id":"information-beginner-17","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[14],"stem":"就业报告显示平均时薪从35.00美元升到35.14美元。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["把0.14美元直接读成百分比，约上升0.14%","把0.14美元直接乘以100，环比约上升14%","按0.14÷35.00计算，环比约上升0.4%","按0.14÷3.50计算，环比约上升4%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"0.14÷35.00≈0.4%。先读水平的单位，再看变化率。","optionExplanations":["变化需要除以基数35.00才是百分比。","0.14美元不能直接乘100当作百分比。","0.14÷35.00≈0.4%，平均时薪环比约上升0.4%。","基数是35.00而不是3.50，少算了一位。"],"skills":["单位","变化率"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The jobs report shows average hourly earnings rising from $35.00 to $35.14. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["Reading the $0.14 directly as a percentage, up about 0.14%","Multiplying $0.14 by 100, up about 14% month over month","Taking 0.14 ÷ 35.00, up about 0.4% month over month","Taking 0.14 ÷ 3.50, up about 4% month over month"],"explanationEn":"0.14 ÷ 35.00 ≈ 0.4%. Read the unit of the level first, then the rate of change.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The change must be divided by the base of 35.00 to become a percentage.","Wrong: $0.14 cannot simply be multiplied by 100 to make a percentage.","Correct: 0.14 ÷ 35.00 ≈ 0.4%, so average hourly earnings rose about 0.4% month over month.","Wrong: The base is 35.00, not 3.50; a decimal place was dropped."]},{"id":"information-advanced-17","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[15],"stem":"平均每周工时从34.4小时降到34.2小时，同时非农新增就业为正。较完整的理解是？","options":["就业人数增加而人均工时减少，需结合总投入判断","工时下降说明企业削减雇员，就业市场正在转弱","0.2小时的变动很小，对总劳动投入影响可以不计","工时减少意味着每小时工资同步下降，收入承压"],"answer":0,"explanation":"工时变化0.2小时乘以庞大的就业人数，也会影响总工作时间。","optionExplanations":["人数增加、人均工时下降，需合并看总劳动投入，0.2小时乘以庞大的人数也有影响。","非农新增为正，说明人数在增加，不是裁员。","0.2小时乘以庞大的就业人数，对总工时并不小。","工时衡量时间，不决定每小时工资的方向。"],"skills":["人数与工时","总量"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Average weekly hours fall from 34.4 to 34.2 while nonfarm payrolls rise. What is the more complete understanding?","optionsEn":["More people are working but fewer hours each, so judge total labour input","Falling hours mean firms are cutting staff and the job market is weakening","A 0.2-hour change is tiny and can be ignored for total labour input","Fewer hours mean hourly pay is falling too, squeezing income"],"explanationEn":"A 0.2-hour change multiplied by a huge workforce also affects total hours worked.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Headcount is up and hours per worker down, so look at total labour input combined; 0.2 hours times a huge workforce matters.","Wrong: Positive payrolls mean headcount is rising, not layoffs.","Wrong: 0.2 hours times a huge workforce is not small for total hours.","Wrong: Hours measure time and do not set the direction of hourly pay."]},{"id":"information-beginner-18","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[16],"stem":"本周初请失业金为24万，上周修订为23万；4周移动平均为22.5万。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["单周上升，但噪声大，宜看4周均值","上升1万表示失业率上升，劳动市场明显转弱","24万是当前全美失业者的总人数","上周的23万已是定稿数据，之后不再被修订"],"answer":0,"explanation":"初请每周都有噪声，4周平均和修订前值可以帮助判断是否形成趋势。","optionExplanations":["初请单周噪声大，4周平均和修订前值更能判断是否形成趋势。","初请只是新申请人数，单周小幅变化不等于失业率上升。","初请只统计当周新申请的人，不是失业者总数。","上周数据发布后仍可能被修订。"],"skills":["单周与平均","修订"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工部 DOL：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.dol.gov/ui/data.pdf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Initial jobless claims are 240,000 this week; last week was revised to 230,000; the 4-week moving average is 225,000. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["The single week rose, but it is noisy, so watch the 4-week average","A 10,000 rise means unemployment rose and the job market clearly weakened","240,000 is the total number of unemployed people in the US right now","Last week's 230,000 is final and will not be revised again"],"explanationEn":"Initial claims are noisy each week; the 4-week average and revised prior readings help judge whether a trend is forming.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Weekly claims are noisy; the 4-week average and revised prior readings better show whether a trend is forming.","Wrong: Initial claims are only new filings; a small weekly change does not mean the unemployment rate rose.","Wrong: Initial claims count only new filings that week, not all unemployed people.","Wrong: Last week's figure can still be revised after release."]},{"id":"information-advanced-18","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[17],"stem":"初请失业金保持稳定，但续请失业金连续数周上升。较合理的解读是？","options":["初请稳定，说明劳动力市场正在明显改善","续请上升表示新增裁员人数在连续几周增加","续请与初请统计的是同一批人，二者应同步变化","新增裁员不多，但失业者找到新工作的速度变慢"],"answer":3,"explanation":"续请反映仍在领取的人数，上升可能说明再就业速度放慢。","optionExplanations":["续请上升恰恰提示再就业变慢，不能说明明显改善。","新裁员看初请，初请稳定说明新增裁员并未增加。","初请是新申请人数，续请是仍在领取的人数，不是同一批。","初请稳定说明新裁员不多，续请上升说明仍在领取的人再就业变慢。"],"skills":["存量与流量","时间差"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工部 DOL：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.dol.gov/ui/data.pdf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Initial jobless claims are steady, but continuing claims have risen for several weeks. What is the more reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["Steady initial claims show the labour market is clearly improving","Rising continuing claims mean new layoffs have increased for weeks","Continuing and initial claims count the same people and should move together","New layoffs are few, but the unemployed are finding work more slowly"],"explanationEn":"Continuing claims reflect how many are still receiving benefits; a rise can mean slower re-employment.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Rising continuing claims point to slower re-employment, not clear improvement.","Wrong: New layoffs show up in initial claims, and steady initial claims mean they have not increased.","Wrong: Initial claims are new filings and continuing claims are people still receiving benefits; they are not the same group.","Correct: Steady initial claims mean few new layoffs, while rising continuing claims mean those still on benefits are finding work more slowly."]},{"id":"information-beginner-19","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[18],"stem":"JOLTS职位空缺从800万降到760万，同时空缺率从4.8%降到4.6%。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["空缺减少40万，对应新增失业者约40万人","劳动需求有所降温，但空缺不等于实际招聘","实际招聘人数同步减少了40万，空缺即招聘","空缺率4.6%相当于失业率为4.6%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"空缺、招聘、离职是JOLTS中不同的表，要分开读。","optionExplanations":["空缺减少不等于失业者增加。","空缺下降表明需求降温，但空缺、招聘、离职是不同的表。","空缺是职位数量，实际招聘在JOLTS另一张表。","空缺率分母是就业加空缺，不是失业率。"],"skills":["空缺与招聘","口径"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/jolts.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"JOLTS job openings fall from 8.0 million to 7.6 million, and the openings rate from 4.8% to 4.6%. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["400,000 fewer openings means about 400,000 more unemployed","Labour demand has cooled somewhat, but openings are not actual hires","Actual hiring also fell by 400,000; openings are hires","An openings rate of 4.6% is equivalent to a 4.6% unemployment rate"],"explanationEn":"Openings, hires and separations are separate tables in JOLTS and should be read separately.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Fewer openings do not mean more unemployed.","Correct: Falling openings show cooling demand, but openings, hires and separations are different tables.","Wrong: Openings are a count of positions; actual hires are in another JOLTS table.","Wrong: The openings rate's denominator is employment plus openings; it is not the unemployment rate."]},{"id":"information-advanced-19","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[19],"stem":"JOLTS主动离职率从2.6%降到2.1%。较合理的理解是？","options":["自愿离职意愿下降，工资上涨压力可能减轻","离职率下降说明企业裁员增多，劳动市场转弱","离职率下降0.5，对应失业率约上升0.5个百分点","离职减少表明员工信心提升，工资压力正在加大"],"answer":0,"explanation":"主动离职率下降通常表示员工自愿跳槽的意愿下降；它是比率，要与招聘率一起看。","optionExplanations":["主动离职率下降表示员工跳槽意愿减弱，工资压力可能放缓。","主动离职不是裁员，裁员在另一类别。","离职率与失业率是不同指标，不能一对一换算。","离职减少通常意味着信心偏弱，工资压力反而放缓。"],"skills":["比率","工资压力线索"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/jolts.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The JOLTS quits rate falls from 2.6% to 2.1%. What is the more reasonable understanding?","optionsEn":["Willingness to quit voluntarily has fallen, so wage pressure may ease","A lower quits rate means more layoffs and a weaker job market","A 0.5 drop in quits means unemployment rose about 0.5 point","Fewer quits show rising worker confidence and growing wage pressure"],"explanationEn":"A lower quits rate usually means workers are less willing to change jobs voluntarily; it is a rate and should be read with the hires rate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A lower quits rate means workers are less willing to switch jobs, so wage pressure may slow.","Wrong: Quits are not layoffs; layoffs are a separate category.","Wrong: The quits rate and the unemployment rate are different measures and cannot be converted one to one.","Wrong: Fewer quits usually point to weaker confidence, and wage pressure slows instead."]},{"id":"information-beginner-20","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[20],"stem":"ADP报告私营部门新增就业+15万，两天后BLS非农报告私营部门新增+9万。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["差距较大说明BLS非农数据存在计算错误","ADP是BLS非农的初值，之后会被官方数据替代","两者统计范围相同，都包含政府部门就业","两者来源与方法不同，差异并不少见"],"answer":3,"explanation":"ADP基于其薪资客户数据，BLS基于官方调查，覆盖和口径不同。","optionExplanations":["两份数据方法不同，差异大不代表任何一方算错。","ADP是独立的私营机构数据，不是BLS的初值。","ADP只覆盖私营部门，不含政府。","ADP基于其薪资客户数据，BLS基于官方调查，覆盖和口径不同。"],"skills":["来源差异","口径"],"references":[{"title":"ADP Research 与斯坦福数字经济实验室：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://adpemploymentreport.com/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"ADP reports +150,000 private-sector jobs; two days later the BLS payrolls report shows +90,000 private jobs. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["The large gap shows the BLS payroll data contains a calculation error","ADP is the preliminary BLS payroll figure and will be replaced by official data","Both cover the same scope, including government jobs","They differ in source and method, so gaps are not unusual"],"explanationEn":"ADP is based on its payroll clients' data and BLS on official surveys, so coverage and definitions differ.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The two use different methods, so a big gap does not mean either is wrong.","Wrong: ADP is an independent private data set, not a BLS preliminary figure.","Wrong: ADP covers only the private sector, not government.","Correct: ADP is based on its payroll clients' data and BLS on official surveys, so coverage and definitions differ."]},{"id":"information-advanced-20","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[22],"stem":"某季度实际GDP折年增长2.8%，实际GDI折年增长1.4%。较稳妥的解读是？","options":["GDP是官方首选，GDI可以不用参考","GDI增速反映居民可支配收入，与GDP无关","两侧估算有差距，可参考平均并留意修订","同季度出现两个增速，说明至少一个数据有错误"],"answer":2,"explanation":"理论上GDP与GDI应相同，实际有统计误差。","optionExplanations":["GDI从收入侧衡量产出，是有价值的交叉验证。","GDI是收入法的总产出，不是居民可支配收入。","理论上GDP与GDI应相同，实际有统计误差，差距大时可参考平均并留意修订。","统计误差使两者不同，并不说明数据有错。"],"skills":["统计差异","修订"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/gross-domestic-income"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"In one quarter real GDP grows at a 2.8% annualised rate and real GDI at 1.4%. What is the more careful reading?","optionsEn":["GDP is the official preferred measure, so GDI can be ignored","GDI growth reflects disposable household income and is unrelated to GDP","The two estimates differ; consider the average and watch for revisions","Two growth rates in one quarter mean at least one is wrong"],"explanationEn":"In theory GDP and GDI should be equal, but in practice there is statistical discrepancy.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: GDI measures output from the income side and is a valuable cross-check.","Wrong: GDI is total output measured by income, not disposable household income.","Correct: In theory GDP and GDI should be equal, but there is statistical discrepancy; when the gap is large, consider the average and watch for revisions.","Wrong: Statistical discrepancy makes them differ; it does not mean the data is wrong."]},{"id":"information-beginner-21","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[24],"stem":"ISM服务业PMI从52.0降到50.8。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["读数跌破前值，说明服务业已经转入收缩","服务业产出较上月下降约1.2%","50.8%的受访服务企业表示本月盈利","仍处扩张区间，但扩张的广度有所减弱"],"answer":3,"explanation":"扩散指数50是“不变”分界，从52降到50.8仍是扩张但放缓。","optionExplanations":["50.8仍高于50，不是收缩。","扩散指数不是产出变化的百分比。","PMI不衡量盈利企业占比。","50是分界，50.8仍高于50，但比52弱。"],"skills":["扩散指数","50分界"],"references":[{"title":"美国供应管理协会 ISM：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.ismworld.org/supply-management-news-and-reports/reports/ism-pmi-reports/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The ISM services PMI falls from 52.0 to 50.8. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["Falling below the prior reading means services have moved into contraction","Services output fell about 1.2% from last month","50.8% of surveyed service firms said they were profitable this month","It is still in expansion, but the breadth of expansion has narrowed"],"explanationEn":"For a diffusion index, 50 is the no-change line; falling from 52 to 50.8 is still expansion, but slower.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 50.8 is still above 50, so it is not contraction.","Wrong: A diffusion index is not a percentage change in output.","Wrong: PMI does not measure the share of profitable firms.","Correct: 50 is the dividing line; 50.8 is still above it, but weaker than 52."]},{"id":"information-advanced-21","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[25],"stem":"标普全球美国制造业PMI初值为49.6，终值修订为50.1，同期ISM制造业PMI为48.7。较稳妥的理解是？","options":["ISM与标普口径相同，读数不同即有误","终值修订只是技术调整，不改初值含义","初值样本不全，两家机构方法也不同","49.6和48.7均低于50，故50.1不可信"],"answer":2,"explanation":"比较前先确认初值/终值，再区分不同机构的PMI。","optionExplanations":["两家机构样本和方法不同，读数可以不同。","初值49.6修订为50.1，已越过50，含义有变化。","比较前要先确认初值或终值，再区分不同机构的PMI。","终值是更完整样本的结果，不能因初值而否定。"],"skills":["初值与终值","机构差异"],"references":[{"title":"标普全球 S&P Global：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.pmi.spglobal.com/Public/Release/PressReleases"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The S&P Global US manufacturing PMI flash reading was 49.6 and the final was revised to 50.1, while the ISM manufacturing PMI for the same period was 48.7. What is the more careful understanding?","optionsEn":["ISM and S&P use the same method, so different readings mean an error","The final revision is only technical and does not change the flash's meaning","The flash sample was incomplete, and the two bodies use different methods","49.6 and 48.7 are both below 50, so 50.1 is not credible"],"explanationEn":"Before comparing, check whether it is a flash or final reading, then tell the different bodies' PMIs apart.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The two bodies differ in sample and method, so their readings can differ.","Wrong: The flash of 49.6 was revised to 50.1, crossing 50, so the meaning changed.","Correct: Before comparing, check whether it is a flash or final reading, then tell the different bodies' PMIs apart.","Wrong: The final comes from a fuller sample and cannot be dismissed because of the flash."]},{"id":"information-beginner-22","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[26],"stem":"标普全球美国服务业PMI商业活动指数为50.0。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["50表示业务活动较上月增长了约50%","50表示服务业整体已经进入明显收缩","回答活动增加与减少的企业大致相当","50表示企业报告的价格较上月上涨约50%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"50表示增加与减少的企业大体平衡，不代表增长50%。","optionExplanations":["扩散指数不是增长率。","50是分界，不是收缩。","50表示改善与恶化大体平衡。","商业活动指数不衡量价格涨幅。"],"skills":["平衡点","扩散指数"],"references":[{"title":"标普全球 S&P Global：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.pmi.spglobal.com/Public/Release/PressReleases"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The S&P Global US services PMI business activity index is 50.0. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["50 means business activity grew about 50% from last month","50 means services overall have moved into clear contraction","Firms reporting more activity roughly equal those reporting less","50 means firms reported prices up about 50% from last month"],"explanationEn":"50 means firms reporting increases and decreases are roughly balanced, not 50% growth.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A diffusion index is not a growth rate.","Wrong: 50 is the dividing line, not contraction.","Correct: 50 means improvement and deterioration are roughly balanced.","Wrong: The business activity index does not measure price increases."]},{"id":"information-advanced-22","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[27],"stem":"工业产出总指数环比+0.4%，但制造业−0.1%，公用事业+3.5%。较完整的解读是？","options":["总指数上涨说明制造业带动，工厂生产在扩张","总指数主要由公用事业带动，制造业略有下降","公用事业大涨表明工业需求过热，生产正在加速","总指数上升表明三大分项在本月都同步上升"],"answer":1,"explanation":"先拆分制造业、采矿业和公用事业，避免把天气驱动的变化当成制造业改善。","optionExplanations":["制造业−0.1%，不是总指数的推动力。","公用事业+3.5%带动总指数，制造业−0.1%略降，需拆分来看。","公用事业多受天气影响，不代表需求过热。","制造业本月下降，并非同步上升。"],"skills":["分项拆解","天气因素"],"references":[{"title":"美国联邦储备委员会 Federal Reserve：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g17/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The total industrial production index is +0.4% month over month, but manufacturing is −0.1% and utilities +3.5%. What is the more complete reading?","optionsEn":["The total rose because manufacturing led, so factory output is expanding","The total was driven mainly by utilities, while manufacturing dipped","A big jump in utilities shows overheating industrial demand and faster production","The total rising means all three major components rose together this month"],"explanationEn":"Break out manufacturing, mining and utilities first, so a weather-driven change isn't mistaken for a manufacturing improvement.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Manufacturing was −0.1%, so it did not drive the total.","Correct: Utilities at +3.5% lifted the total while manufacturing dipped 0.1%, so break it down.","Wrong: Utilities are mostly driven by weather, not overheating demand.","Wrong: Manufacturing fell this month, so they did not all rise together."]},{"id":"information-beginner-23","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[28],"stem":"产能利用率从77.5%升到78.0%。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["产能利用率上升了0.5个基点","工业产出较上月增长了约0.5%","产能利用率越高，经济就越健康","产能利用率上升了0.5个百分点"],"answer":3,"explanation":"产能利用率本身是百分比，变化用百分点表示。","optionExplanations":["0.5个百分点是50个基点，不是0.5个基点。","产能利用率不是产出增速。","利用率过高也可能意味着瓶颈与通胀压力，并非越高越好。","产能利用率本身是百分比，变化用百分点表示。"],"skills":["百分点","水平含义"],"references":[{"title":"美国联邦储备委员会 Federal Reserve：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g17/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Capacity utilization rises from 77.5% to 78.0%. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["Capacity utilization rose 0.5 basis point","Industrial output grew about 0.5% from last month","The higher the utilization, the healthier the economy","Capacity utilization rose 0.5 percentage point"],"explanationEn":"Capacity utilization is itself a percentage, so its change is expressed in percentage points.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 0.5 percentage point is 50 basis points, not 0.5 basis point.","Wrong: Capacity utilization is not output growth.","Wrong: Very high utilization can also mean bottlenecks and inflation pressure, so higher is not always better.","Correct: Capacity utilization is itself a percentage, so its change is expressed in percentage points."]},{"id":"information-advanced-23","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[29],"stem":"耐用品订单环比+4.0%，但剔除运输设备后−0.2%。较稳妥的解读是？","options":["设备投资需求普遍强劲，各类订单同步增长","订单增长4%表示实际出货已经增长了4%","运输设备带动了增长，其余订单略有下降","4%代表耐用品价格涨了4%，并非数量增加"],"answer":2,"explanation":"运输类订单波动很大，剔除后能更好地观察基础需求。","optionExplanations":["剔除运输后下降，说明增长并不普遍。","订单是未来意向，不等于出货。","剔除运输设备后−0.2%，说明增长主要来自运输类。","订单额不是价格指数。"],"skills":["剔除波动项","订单与出货"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/manufacturing/m3/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Durable goods orders are +4.0% month over month, but −0.2% excluding transportation. What is the more careful reading?","optionsEn":["Equipment investment demand is broadly strong, with all orders rising together","4% order growth means actual shipments already rose 4%","Transportation drove the gain; other orders dipped slightly","4% means durable goods prices rose 4%, not quantities"],"explanationEn":"Transportation orders are very volatile; excluding them gives a better view of underlying demand.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Orders fell excluding transportation, so the gain was not broad.","Wrong: Orders are future intentions, not shipments.","Correct: Excluding transportation it was −0.2%, so the gain came mainly from transportation.","Wrong: Order value is not a price index."]},{"id":"information-beginner-24","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[30],"stem":"非国防资本品（剔除飞机）订单环比+0.8%，出货+0.1%。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["订单偏向未来意向，出货更接近当期投资","订单+0.8%说明本季度设备投资已增长0.8%","订单与出货统计同一环节，同月应大致相同","该系列包含飞机与国防订单，因此波动较大"],"answer":0,"explanation":"订单上升可能领先未来出货，但不等于已经完成投资。","optionExplanations":["订单上升可能领先未来出货，但不等于已经完成投资。","订单不是已完成的投资。","订单与出货处于不同环节，可以不同。","该系列已剔除飞机与国防。"],"skills":["领先与同步","口径"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/manufacturing/m3/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Nondefense capital goods orders excluding aircraft are +0.8% month over month, and shipments +0.1%. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["Orders lean towards future intentions; shipments are closer to current investment","+0.8% orders mean equipment investment grew 0.8% this quarter","Orders and shipments measure the same stage and should be similar in a month","This series includes aircraft and defense orders, so it is volatile"],"explanationEn":"Rising orders may lead future shipments, but they are not completed investment.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Rising orders may lead future shipments, but they are not completed investment.","Wrong: Orders are not completed investment.","Wrong: Orders and shipments are different stages and can differ.","Wrong: This series already excludes aircraft and defense."]},{"id":"information-advanced-24","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[32],"stem":"零售销售总额环比+0.7%，控制组环比+0.1%。第三方日历把“控制组”定义为另一种剔除方式。较稳妥的做法是？","options":["总额增长0.7%已足够说明消费走强，无需看分项","先核对官方控制组的口径，再与总额比较","控制组指剔除通胀后的实际销售额，可直接对比","第三方日历口径与官方相同，数值可直接对比"],"answer":1,"explanation":"控制组通常剔除汽车、汽油、建材和餐饮，第三方口径可能不同。","optionExplanations":["总额受汽车、汽油影响，控制组只涨0.1%提示不能直接下结论。","控制组通常剔除汽车、汽油、建材和餐饮，第三方口径可能不同。","控制组是剔除部分品类，不是剔除通胀。","第三方口径可能不同，需要先核对。"],"skills":["剔除口径","名义值"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/retail/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Total retail sales are +0.7% month over month and the control group +0.1%. A third-party calendar defines the \"control group\" with different exclusions. What is the more careful approach?","optionsEn":["0.7% total growth is enough to show strong spending, no need for components","Check the official control-group definition first, then compare with the total","The control group is inflation-adjusted real sales and can be compared directly","The third-party calendar uses the official definition, so the numbers compare directly"],"explanationEn":"The control group usually excludes autos, gasoline, building materials and food services; third-party definitions may differ.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The total is affected by autos and gasoline; the control group's 0.1% says you cannot jump to a conclusion.","Correct: The control group usually excludes autos, gasoline, building materials and food services; third-party definitions may differ.","Wrong: The control group excludes certain categories; it does not adjust for inflation.","Wrong: Third-party definitions may differ, so check first."]},{"id":"information-beginner-25","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[34],"stem":"个人收入环比+0.5%，同期PCE物价指数环比+0.3%。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["个人收入涨0.5%，实际收入也涨0.5%","物价上涨0.3%，说明实际收入减少了0.3%","个人收入主要包括工资，其他收入不计入","名义收入扣除物价后，购买力约增0.2%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"个人收入是名义值，要与物价比较才能估计实际变化。","optionExplanations":["0.5%是名义值，没有扣除物价。","收入涨0.5%快于物价0.3%，实际收入是增加的。","个人收入还包括资产收入、转移支付等。","个人收入是名义值，要与物价比较才能估计实际变化。"],"skills":["名义与实际","口径"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-income"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Personal income rises 0.5% month over month while the PCE price index rises 0.3%. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["Personal income rose 0.5%, so real income also rose 0.5%","Prices rose 0.3%, so real income fell 0.3%","Personal income is mainly wages; other income is not counted","After prices, purchasing power rose about 0.2%"],"explanationEn":"Personal income is nominal; compare it with prices to estimate the real change.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 0.5% is nominal and has not been adjusted for prices.","Wrong: Income rose 0.5%, faster than prices at 0.3%, so real income increased.","Wrong: Personal income also includes asset income, transfer payments and more.","Correct: Personal income is nominal; compare it with prices to estimate the real change."]},{"id":"information-advanced-25","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[37],"stem":"谘商会消费者信心指数从105降到98，其中现况指数基本不变，预期指数大幅下降。较合理的解读是？","options":["现况与预期都在恶化，就业市场已经转弱","98表示98%的受访者对经济有信心","现况稳定，但居民对未来更悲观","信心走弱会让下月零售销售同步下降"],"answer":2,"explanation":"拆开现况与预期，可以看出变化主要来自前瞻部分。","optionExplanations":["现况指数基本不变，不能说当前已恶化。","指数不是持信心者的百分比。","现况指数基本不变，预期指数大幅下降，变化主要来自前瞻部分。","信心指数只是情绪读数，不是销售的机械预测。"],"skills":["现况与预期","指数点"],"references":[{"title":"The Conference Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.conference-board.org/topics/consumer-confidence"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Conference Board consumer confidence index falls from 105 to 98, with the present situation index roughly unchanged and the expectations index down sharply. What is the more reasonable reading?","optionsEn":["Both present conditions and expectations are worsening, so the job market has weakened","98 means 98% of respondents are confident about the economy","Present conditions are steady, but households are gloomier about the future","Weaker confidence will make next month's retail sales fall in step"],"explanationEn":"Splitting present conditions from expectations shows the change came mainly from the forward-looking part.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The present situation index is roughly unchanged, so current conditions have not worsened.","Wrong: The index is not the percentage of confident respondents.","Correct: Present conditions are roughly unchanged while expectations fell sharply, so the change came mainly from the forward-looking part.","Wrong: A confidence index is a sentiment reading, not a mechanical forecast of sales."]},{"id":"information-beginner-26","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[38],"stem":"密歇根大学消费者信心初值为65.0，终值修订为63.5。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["63.5表示63.5%的消费者对经济有信心","修订幅度较大，说明这次调查结果已经失效","初值样本不完整，修订属于常见现象","信心指数与通胀预期是同一个读数的不同叫法"],"answer":2,"explanation":"读密歇根数据要标明初值或终值。","optionExplanations":["指数不是百分比比例。","修订来自更完整的样本，不代表无效。","读密歇根数据要标明初值或终值，修订是常态。","信心指数与通胀预期是不同的调查结果。"],"skills":["初值与终值","指数点"],"references":[{"title":"University of Michigan Surveys of Consumers official release and methodology","url":"https://www.sca.isr.umich.edu/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The University of Michigan consumer sentiment preliminary reading is 65.0 and the final is revised to 63.5. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["63.5 means 63.5% of consumers are confident about the economy","The large revision shows this survey result is invalid","The preliminary sample is incomplete, so revisions are common","The sentiment index and inflation expectations are the same reading under different names"],"explanationEn":"When reading Michigan data, label whether it is preliminary or final.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The index is not a percentage share.","Wrong: Revisions come from a fuller sample and do not mean the result is invalid.","Correct: When reading Michigan data, label whether it is preliminary or final; revisions are normal.","Wrong: The sentiment index and inflation expectations are different survey results."]},{"id":"information-advanced-26","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[39],"stem":"消费者信贷报告显示“循环信贷增长年化12%”，当前余额约1万亿美元。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["年化12%换算后，当月新增约1200亿美元","按年化12%推算，当月约增加100亿美元","年化12%表示余额增加了12倍，约12万亿美元","年化12%意味着未来一年余额将按此速度增长"],"answer":1,"explanation":"年化率放大了单月变化；12%÷12×1万亿≈100亿美元。读数前要区分余额、月增量和年化率。","optionExplanations":["1200亿是一整年的增量，不是当月。","12%÷12×1万亿≈100亿美元。","12%是百分比，不是12倍。","年化只是把单月变化放大，不是对未来的承诺。"],"skills":["年化","存量与流量"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g19/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"A consumer credit report shows \"revolving credit grew at a 12% annual rate\", with a current balance of about $1 trillion. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["A 12% annual rate means about $120 billion was added this month","At a 12% annual rate, about $10 billion was added this month","A 12% annual rate means the balance grew 12-fold, to about $12 trillion","A 12% annual rate means the balance will grow at that pace over the next year"],"explanationEn":"An annual rate magnifies a single month's change: 12% ÷ 12 × $1 trillion ≈ $10 billion. Tell apart the balance, the monthly increase and the annual rate before reading it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: $120 billion is a full year's increase, not one month's.","Correct: 12% ÷ 12 × $1 trillion ≈ $10 billion.","Wrong: 12% is a percentage, not a 12-fold increase.","Wrong: Annualising only scales up one month's change; it is no promise about the future."]},{"id":"information-beginner-27","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[40],"stem":"美联储银行数据中居民贷款逾期率从2.5%升到2.8%。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["逾期率上升了0.3个基点","银行已经损失了2.8%的贷款","各机构的逾期率定义大体相同","逾期占比上升了0.3个百分点"],"answer":3,"explanation":"逾期率与核销率、纽约联储严重逾期率口径不同。","optionExplanations":["0.3个百分点是30个基点。","逾期不等于已经损失，核销才是损失。","逾期率与核销率、严重逾期率口径不同。","2.8%−2.5%=0.3个百分点。"],"skills":["口径","百分点"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board；可辅看 New York Fed official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/chargeoff/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"In Fed bank data, the household loan delinquency rate rises from 2.5% to 2.8%. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["The delinquency rate rose 0.3 basis point","Banks have already lost 2.8% of their loans","Different bodies define delinquency in roughly the same way","The delinquent share rose 0.3 percentage point"],"explanationEn":"The delinquency rate differs in definition from the charge-off rate and the New York Fed's serious delinquency rate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 0.3 percentage point is 30 basis points.","Wrong: Delinquency is not a loss; charge-offs are losses.","Wrong: The delinquency rate differs in definition from charge-off and serious delinquency rates.","Correct: 2.8% − 2.5% = 0.3 percentage point."]},{"id":"information-advanced-27","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[43],"stem":"成屋销售季调年率从400万套升到412万套，中位价同比+5%，同期高价房成交占比明显上升。较稳妥的解读是？","options":["本月卖出了412万套，比上月多出12万套","中位价上涨5%说明同类房屋平均涨价5%","销售增加说明待售库存也在同步下降","销售加快，但中位价会受成交结构影响"],"answer":3,"explanation":"中位价受高低价房成交比例影响，要结合其他房价指数。","optionExplanations":["412万是季调年率，不是当月成交数。","中位价上涨可能来自高价房占比上升。","销售与库存是不同指标，不能互推。","销售年率上升，中位价受高低价房成交比例影响。"],"skills":["年率","结构效应"],"references":[{"title":"National Association of Realtors NAR official release and methodology","url":"https://www.nar.realtor/research-and-statistics/housing-statistics/existing-home-sales"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Existing-home sales at a seasonally adjusted annual rate rise from 4.00 million to 4.12 million, the median price is up 5% year over year, and the share of high-priced sales rose markedly. What is the more careful reading?","optionsEn":["4.12 million homes sold this month, 120,000 more than last month","A 5% rise in the median price means comparable homes rose 5% on average","Higher sales mean inventory for sale is falling in step","Sales picked up, but the median price is affected by the mix of sales"],"explanationEn":"The median price depends on the mix of high- and low-priced sales, so read it alongside other house price indices.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 4.12 million is a seasonally adjusted annual rate, not the month's sales count.","Wrong: A rise in the median may come from a larger share of high-priced homes.","Wrong: Sales and inventory are different measures and cannot be inferred from each other.","Correct: The sales rate rose, and the median price depends on the mix of high- and low-priced sales."]},{"id":"information-beginner-28","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[44],"stem":"新屋销售季调年率环比+8%，但报告显示该变化的90%置信区间为±18%。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["环比+8%说明新屋需求较上月大幅升温","置信区间±18%说明该数据有误，不应采用","8%代表新屋价格较上月上涨的幅度","单月变化可能不显著，宜结合趋势判断"],"answer":3,"explanation":"新屋销售样本误差大，单月数字不宜过度解读。","optionExplanations":["置信区间比变化还大，不能认定需求大幅上升。","置信区间描述的是抽样误差，不是错误。","这是销售量变化，不是价格。","±18%的置信区间大于8%，单月数字不宜过度解读。"],"skills":["统计误差","趋势"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Census Bureau / HUD official release and methodology","url":"https://www.census.gov/construction/nrs/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"New-home sales at a seasonally adjusted annual rate are +8% month over month, but the report shows a 90% confidence interval of ±18% for the change. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["+8% shows new-home demand heated up sharply from last month","A ±18% confidence interval means the data is wrong and should not be used","8% is how much new-home prices rose from last month","The monthly change may not be significant, so judge by the trend"],"explanationEn":"New-home sales have large sampling error, so don't over-read a single month.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The confidence interval is larger than the change, so you cannot conclude demand jumped.","Wrong: The confidence interval describes sampling error, not a mistake.","Wrong: This is a change in sales volume, not price.","Correct: A ±18% confidence interval exceeds 8%, so don't over-read a single month."]},{"id":"information-advanced-28","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[45],"stem":"成屋签约销售指数为72.5。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["本月签约了72.5万套房子","72.5%的挂牌房屋已经卖出","签约数据就等于已完成过户的交易","约为基期水平的72.5%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"签约后还要过户才计入成屋销售，因此它常被视为领先指标。","optionExplanations":["它是指数点，不是套数。","指数不是成交比例。","签约可能取消，过户有时间差。","签约后还要过户才计入成屋销售，因此它常被视为领先指标。"],"skills":["基期","领先关系"],"references":[{"title":"National Association of Realtors NAR official release and methodology","url":"https://www.nar.realtor/research-and-statistics/housing-statistics/pending-home-sales"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The pending home sales index is 72.5. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["725,000 homes went under contract this month","72.5% of listed homes have sold","Contract signings are the same as closed sales","About 72.5% of the base-period level"],"explanationEn":"A signed contract still has to close before it counts as an existing-home sale, so it is often seen as a leading indicator.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It is an index level, not a count of homes.","Wrong: The index is not a share of homes sold.","Wrong: Contracts can be cancelled, and closing comes later.","Correct: A signed contract still has to close before it counts as an existing-home sale, so it is often seen as a leading indicator."]},{"id":"information-beginner-29","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[46],"stem":"Case-Shiller 20城房价指数同比+4%，最新发布的是约两个月前的数据，并采用三个月移动窗口。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["反映本周最新房价，是房价的实时指标","反映较早时期、经过平滑的价格变化","全美房屋平均涨价约4%，覆盖各个城市","三个月移动窗口使它比单月数据更快反映拐点"],"answer":1,"explanation":"发布滞后与移动平均让它更平滑也更慢。","optionExplanations":["它是约两个月前的数据，并非本周。","发布滞后与移动平均让它更平滑也更慢。","它只是20个城市的指数。","移动窗口让它更平滑也更慢。"],"skills":["时滞","平滑"],"references":[{"title":"S&P Dow Jones Indices official release and methodology","url":"https://www.spglobal.com/spdji/en/index-family/indicators/sp-cotality-case-shiller/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Case-Shiller 20-city home price index is +4% year over year; the latest release covers data from about two months ago and uses a three-month moving window. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["It reflects this week's latest home prices, a real-time indicator","It reflects smoothed price changes from an earlier period","Home prices nationwide rose about 4% on average, covering every city","The three-month window lets it catch turning points faster than monthly data"],"explanationEn":"The publication lag and moving average make it smoother and slower.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It covers data from about two months ago, not this week.","Correct: The publication lag and moving average make it smoother and slower.","Wrong: It covers only 20 cities.","Wrong: The moving window makes it smoother and slower."]},{"id":"information-advanced-29","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[47],"stem":"FHFA月度购房价格指数季调环比+0.3%，季度扩展指数同比+5.1%。能否把两者直接拼成一条连续序列？","options":["两者同为FHFA指数，可以直接拼成连续序列","两者属于不同系列，不能直接拼成连续序列","季度值等于三个月度值之和，可以直接拼接","把环比乘以12得到同比，即可拼成序列"],"answer":1,"explanation":"月度购房指数与季度扩展指数是不同系列。","optionExplanations":["同一机构发布不代表同一系列。","月度购房指数与季度扩展指数是不同系列。","季度扩展指数不是三个月度值简单相加。","环比乘12不等于同比。"],"skills":["系列差异","频率"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Housing Finance Agency FHFA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.fhfa.gov/fhfa-house-price-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The FHFA monthly purchase-only index is +0.3% month over month seasonally adjusted, and the quarterly expanded-data index is +5.1% year over year. Can the two be spliced directly into one continuous series?","optionsEn":["Both are FHFA indices, so they can be spliced directly","They are different series and cannot be spliced directly","The quarterly value is the sum of three monthly values, so they splice directly","Multiplying the monthly change by 12 gives the yearly change, so they splice"],"explanationEn":"The monthly purchase-only index and the quarterly expanded-data index are different series.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Coming from the same agency does not make them the same series.","Correct: The monthly purchase-only index and the quarterly expanded-data index are different series.","Wrong: The quarterly expanded index is not a simple sum of three monthly values.","Wrong: Monthly change times 12 is not the yearly change."]},{"id":"information-beginner-30","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[48],"stem":"MBA抵押贷款申请总指数周环比+10%，其中再融资指数+25%，购房指数−2%。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["购房需求强劲回升，带动申请总量增长10%","主要来自再融资，购房申请略有下降","再融资增加代表新增购房贷款，房价因此上行","总指数+10%说明房价较上周上涨了约10%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"利率小幅下降就可能带动再融资大增，购房与再融资要分开看。","optionExplanations":["购房指数−2%，并未回升。","再融资+25%带动总指数，购房−2%。","再融资是置换旧贷款，不是新增购房。","MBA指数衡量申请量，不是房价。"],"skills":["分项","利率敏感"],"references":[{"title":"Mortgage Bankers Association MBA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.mba.org/news-and-research/research-and-economics/single-family-research/weekly-applications-survey"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The MBA mortgage applications composite index is +10% week over week, with the refinance index +25% and the purchase index −2%. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["Purchase demand rebounded strongly, lifting total applications 10%","It came mainly from refinancing, while purchase applications dipped","More refinancing means new purchase loans, so home prices rise","+10% in the composite means home prices rose about 10% from last week"],"explanationEn":"A small drop in rates can trigger a surge in refinancing, so read purchase and refinance separately.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The purchase index was −2%, so it did not rebound.","Correct: Refinancing at +25% drove the composite, while purchases were −2%.","Wrong: Refinancing replaces existing loans; it is not new purchase lending.","Wrong: The MBA index measures application volume, not home prices."]},{"id":"information-advanced-30","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[49],"stem":"Freddie Mac的30年期固定抵押贷款平均利率从6.0%升到6.5%。下面哪项描述正确？","options":["上升了0.5个百分点，即50个基点","上升了5个基点，即0.05个百分点","上升了0.5个基点，即0.005个百分点","上升了500个基点，即5个百分点"],"answer":0,"explanation":"6.5−6.0=0.5个百分点=50个基点。","optionExplanations":["6.5−6.0=0.5个百分点=50个基点。","5个基点只有0.05个百分点。","0.5个基点只有0.005个百分点。","500个基点是5个百分点，放大了十倍。"],"skills":["基点","平均与个体"],"references":[{"title":"Freddie Mac official release and methodology","url":"https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Freddie Mac's average 30-year fixed mortgage rate rises from 6.0% to 6.5%. Which description is correct?","optionsEn":["Up 0.5 percentage point, i.e. 50 basis points","Up 5 basis points, i.e. 0.05 percentage point","Up 0.5 basis point, i.e. 0.005 percentage point","Up 500 basis points, i.e. 5 percentage points"],"explanationEn":"6.5 − 6.0 = 0.5 percentage point = 50 basis points.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 6.5 − 6.0 = 0.5 percentage point = 50 basis points.","Wrong: 5 basis points is only 0.05 percentage point.","Wrong: 0.5 basis point is only 0.005 percentage point.","Wrong: 500 basis points is 5 percentage points, ten times too large."]},{"id":"information-beginner-31","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[50],"stem":"NAHB房屋建筑商信心指数为46。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["读数46表示房价较高点已下跌约4%","读数46表示仅有46%的新房已经成功卖出","低于50，说明看差市况的建筑商多于看好的","50以下说明新屋开工量已下降了约54%"],"answer":2,"explanation":"指数以50为分界，衡量建筑商对市况的看法，不是房价或销售比例。","optionExplanations":["指数不是房价变化。","指数不是销售比例。","指数以50为分界，衡量建筑商对市况的看法。","指数衡量看法，不是开工量变化。"],"skills":["50分界","调查指数"],"references":[{"title":"National Association of Home Builders NAHB official release and methodology","url":"https://www.nahb.org/news-and-economics/housing-economics/indices/housing-market-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The NAHB homebuilder confidence index is 46. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["46 means home prices have fallen about 4% from their peak","46 means only 46% of new homes have sold","Below 50, more builders see conditions as poor than good","Below 50 means housing starts have fallen about 54%"],"explanationEn":"The index uses 50 as its dividing line and measures builders' views of conditions, not prices or sales shares.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The index is not a change in home prices.","Wrong: The index is not a sales share.","Correct: The index uses 50 as its dividing line and measures builders' views of conditions.","Wrong: The index measures views, not changes in starts."]},{"id":"information-advanced-31","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[55],"stem":"2020年5月美联储把储蓄存款重分类进M1，M1随即大幅跳升。这次重分类对M2有什么影响？","options":["M2同步大幅上升，因为储蓄存款并入了M1","M2随之下降，因为储蓄存款被移出了M2","M2的历史数据因此失效，无法再与此前比较","M2不受影响，储蓄存款原本就在M2内"],"answer":3,"explanation":"读货币供应量要留意定义变化造成的断点。","optionExplanations":["储蓄存款原本就在M2内，不会因此新增。","储蓄存款仍在M2内，没有被移出。","M2口径总量未变，历史数据仍可比较。","储蓄存款本来就在M2内，重分类只是从M2内的一部分移入M1。"],"skills":["定义变化","序列断点"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h6/current/default.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"In May 2020 the Fed reclassified savings deposits into M1, and M1 jumped sharply. What did this reclassification do to M2?","optionsEn":["M2 also jumped, because savings deposits were merged into M1","M2 fell, because savings deposits were moved out of M2","M2's history became invalid and can no longer be compared","M2 was unaffected; savings deposits were already in M2"],"explanationEn":"When reading money supply, watch for breaks caused by definition changes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Savings deposits were already in M2, so nothing was added.","Wrong: Savings deposits are still in M2; they were not moved out.","Wrong: M2's total definition did not change, so its history is still comparable.","Correct: Savings deposits were already in M2; the reclassification only moved part of M2 into M1."]},{"id":"information-beginner-32","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[56],"stem":"美联储H.8数据显示：商业银行存款总额基本不变，但小银行存款下降、大银行存款增加。较合理的理解是？","options":["小银行存款下降，反映银行体系存款大幅外流","大银行存款增加，说明存款总量也在增加","存款在银行间转移，总量并未明显流出","季调与未季调序列在这里读数相同，无需区分"],"answer":2,"explanation":"总量与结构是两件事，需分开观察。","optionExplanations":["总量基本不变，说明并非大幅外流。","大行增加、小行减少，相抵后总量不变。","总量不变，结构变化，需分开观察。","季调与未季调通常不同，需要区分。"],"skills":["总量与结构","季调"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"Fed H.8 data show total commercial bank deposits roughly unchanged, with small-bank deposits down and large-bank deposits up. What is the more reasonable understanding?","optionsEn":["Falling small-bank deposits reflect a large outflow from the banking system","Rising large-bank deposits mean total deposits are rising too","Deposits moved between banks; there was no clear outflow in total","Seasonally adjusted and unadjusted series read the same here, so no need to tell them apart"],"explanationEn":"The total and the mix are two separate things and should be watched separately.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The total is roughly unchanged, so there was no large outflow.","Wrong: Large banks gained and small banks lost, netting to an unchanged total.","Correct: The total is unchanged while the mix shifted, so watch them separately.","Wrong: Seasonally adjusted and unadjusted series usually differ and need telling apart."]},{"id":"information-advanced-32","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[57],"stem":"H.8数据显示某类商业银行贷款“年化增长6%”，另一份资料说同一时期该项贷款周增0.1%。较稳妥的做法是？","options":["年化6%折成周率约0.5%，与0.1%相互冲突","年化6%等于该项贷款在本周增长了6%","先统一频率与季调口径，再比较大小","贷款余额与贷款增速是同一个指标，可以互换"],"answer":2,"explanation":"年化率把短期变化放大，周率很小，口径不同就不能直接比大小。","optionExplanations":["年化6%除以52约0.12%，与0.1%并不冲突。","年化率不是单周涨幅。","年化率把短期变化放大，周率很小，口径不同不能直接比大小。","余额是存量，增速是变化率。"],"skills":["频率换算","存量与流量"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"H.8 data show one category of commercial bank loans growing at a \"6% annual rate\", while another source says the same loans rose 0.1% in a week over the same period. What is the more careful approach?","optionsEn":["6% annual is about 0.5% a week, which conflicts with 0.1%","6% annual means the loans grew 6% this week","Put both on the same frequency and seasonal basis before comparing","Loan balances and loan growth are the same measure and interchangeable"],"explanationEn":"An annual rate magnifies short-term changes while a weekly rate is small; on different bases they cannot be compared directly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 6% divided by 52 is about 0.12%, which does not conflict with 0.1%.","Wrong: An annual rate is not a one-week rise.","Correct: An annual rate magnifies short-term changes while a weekly rate is small; on different bases they cannot be compared directly.","Wrong: A balance is a stock; growth is a rate of change."]},{"id":"information-beginner-33","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[58],"stem":"SLOOS调查显示工商业贷款标准“净收紧比例”为30。下面哪项理解正确？","options":["收紧占比减放松占比，差为30个百分点","工商业贷款的平均利率上调了30个基点","工商业贷款余额较上季度下降了约30%","约30%的银行已经停止发放工商业贷款"],"answer":0,"explanation":"它反映标准方向的分布，不是利率或贷款量变化。","optionExplanations":["净收紧比例是收紧银行占比减放松银行占比。","它反映标准的方向，不是利率变化。","它不是贷款量变化。","它是净比例，不是停止放贷的银行占比。"],"skills":["净比例","调查口径"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/data/sloos.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The SLOOS survey shows a \"net percentage tightening\" of 30 for commercial and industrial loan standards. Which understanding is correct?","optionsEn":["The share tightening minus the share easing is 30 percentage points","The average rate on C&I loans rose 30 basis points","C&I loan balances fell about 30% from last quarter","About 30% of banks have stopped making C&I loans"],"explanationEn":"It reflects the distribution of how standards changed, not rates or loan volumes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Net tightening is the share of banks tightening minus the share easing.","Wrong: It reflects the direction of standards, not rate changes.","Wrong: It is not a change in loan volume.","Wrong: It is a net share, not the share of banks that stopped lending."]},{"id":"information-advanced-33","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[60],"stem":"美联储H.4.1显示贴现窗口一级信贷余额从20亿美元升到150亿美元。较稳妥的解读是？","options":["借款猛增表明银行体系已经发生系统性危机","150亿美元是美联储批准给银行的授信额度","贴现窗口借款增加就等于美联储降息放水","部分银行流动性需求上升，需结合背景判断"],"answer":3,"explanation":"余额是实际借款，不是授信额度；一周跳升需要结合背景判断。","optionExplanations":["一周跳升不足以断定系统性危机。","余额是实际借款，不是批准额度。","贴现窗口借款与降息是不同事物。","余额是实际借款，不是授信额度；一周跳升需要结合背景判断。"],"skills":["余额与额度","背景判断"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h41/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","stemEn":"The Fed's H.4.1 shows primary credit at the discount window rising from $2 billion to $15 billion. What is the more careful reading?","optionsEn":["The surge in borrowing shows a systemic banking crisis has begun","$15 billion is the credit line the Fed approved for banks","More discount-window borrowing is the same as the Fed cutting rates","Some banks' liquidity needs rose; judge it in context"],"explanationEn":"The balance is actual borrowing, not a credit line; a one-week jump should be judged in context.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A one-week jump is not enough to diagnose a systemic crisis.","Wrong: The balance is actual borrowing, not an approved limit.","Wrong: Discount-window borrowing and rate cuts are different things.","Correct: The balance is actual borrowing, not a credit line; a one-week jump should be judged in context."]},{"id":"information-beginner-34","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[1],"stem":"CPI报告Table 1里，新闻头条最常引用的“月度变化”是哪种口径？","options":["季调后的12个月变化","季调后的1个月变化","未季调的指数水平","未季调的1个月变化"],"answer":1,"explanation":"月度比较用季调数据，去掉季节性规律。","optionExplanations":["12个月变化是同比，不是头条的月度变化。","月度比较用季调数据，去掉季节性规律。","指数水平不是变化。","月度比较通常用季调数据，不用未季调。"],"skills":["口径","季调"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/cpi.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In Table 1 of the CPI report, which measure is the \"monthly change\" most often quoted in headlines?","optionsEn":["The seasonally adjusted 12-month change","The seasonally adjusted 1-month change","The unadjusted index level","The unadjusted 1-month change"],"explanationEn":"Month-to-month comparisons use seasonally adjusted data to remove seasonal patterns.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The 12-month change is year over year, not the headline monthly change.","Correct: Month-to-month comparisons use seasonally adjusted data to remove seasonal patterns.","Wrong: An index level is not a change.","Wrong: Monthly comparisons usually use adjusted, not unadjusted, data."]},{"id":"information-beginner-35","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[2],"stem":"核心CPI在整体CPI的基础上剔除了哪两类？","options":["食品和住房","食品和能源","能源和二手车","住房和医疗"],"answer":1,"explanation":"核心CPI即 All items less food and energy。","optionExplanations":["核心CPI剔除食品与能源，住房仍包含在内。","核心CPI即 All items less food and energy。","核心CPI不单独剔除二手车。","住房与医疗都包含在核心CPI内。"],"skills":["定义","剔除项"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/cpi.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which two categories does core CPI exclude from headline CPI?","optionsEn":["Food and housing","Food and energy","Energy and used cars","Housing and medical care"],"explanationEn":"Core CPI is All items less food and energy.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Core CPI excludes food and energy; housing is still included.","Correct: Core CPI is All items less food and energy.","Wrong: Core CPI does not separately exclude used cars.","Wrong: Housing and medical care are both included in core CPI."]},{"id":"information-advanced-34","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[2],"stem":"美联储2%通胀目标的正式参照是哪个指标？","options":["整体CPI","整体PCE物价指数","核心PCE物价指数","核心CPI"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：目标参考整体PCE；核心CPI不是正式口径。","optionExplanations":["CPI是另一个机构的另一指标。","课程提醒：目标参考整体PCE；核心CPI不是正式口径。","核心PCE常用来看趋势，但正式目标是整体PCE。","核心CPI常被关注，但不是正式目标口径。"],"skills":["口径","政策目标"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/cpi.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which measure is the formal reference for the Fed's 2% inflation target?","optionsEn":["Headline CPI","The headline PCE price index","The core PCE price index","Core CPI"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, the target refers to headline PCE; core CPI is not the formal measure.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: CPI is a different measure from a different agency.","Correct: As the lesson notes, the target refers to headline PCE; core CPI is not the formal measure.","Wrong: Core PCE is often used to gauge the trend, but the formal target is headline PCE.","Wrong: Core CPI gets a lot of attention, but it is not the formal target measure."]},{"id":"information-beginner-36","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[3],"stem":"PCE物价指数由哪个机构、在哪份报告里发布？","options":["BEA，个人收入与支出报告","BLS，消费者物价指数报告","Census，零售销售报告","美联储，FOMC经济预测摘要"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：打开 Personal Income and Outlays，在价格表找 PCE price index。","optionExplanations":["课程：打开 Personal Income and Outlays，在价格表找 PCE price index。","BLS发布的是CPI，不是PCE。","Census的零售销售报告不含PCE物价指数。","美联储不发布PCE物价指数。"],"skills":["来源","查找"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expenditures-price-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which agency publishes the PCE price index, and in which report?","optionsEn":["BEA, the Personal Income and Outlays report","BLS, the Consumer Price Index report","Census, the retail sales report","The Fed, the FOMC Summary of Economic Projections"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: open Personal Income and Outlays and find the PCE price index in the price tables.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The lesson: open Personal Income and Outlays and find the PCE price index in the price tables.","Wrong: BLS publishes CPI, not PCE.","Wrong: The Census retail sales report does not include the PCE price index.","Wrong: The Fed does not publish the PCE price index."]},{"id":"information-advanced-35","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[3],"stem":"PCE物价指数与CPI常见差别之一是什么？","options":["权重和范围不同，CPI含雇主医保代付部分","PCE只含商品价格，CPI才同时含服务价格","二者样本权重相同，只有发布机构有所不同","权重和范围不同，PCE含雇主医保代付部分"],"answer":3,"explanation":"例如雇主或医保替居民付的医疗费用计入PCE；权重也随消费结构更新。","optionExplanations":["代付部分计入的是PCE，不是CPI。","PCE同时包含商品与服务。","两者权重与范围本就不同。","例如雇主或医保替居民付的医疗费用计入PCE；权重也随消费结构更新。"],"skills":["比较","覆盖范围"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expenditures-price-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is one common difference between the PCE price index and CPI?","optionsEn":["Different weights and scope; CPI includes employer-paid health care","PCE covers only goods prices; CPI covers services as well","Their sample weights are the same; only the publishing agency differs","Different weights and scope; PCE includes employer-paid health care"],"explanationEn":"For example, medical costs paid for households by employers or insurers are counted in PCE, and its weights update with spending patterns.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The employer-paid part is counted in PCE, not CPI.","Wrong: PCE covers both goods and services.","Wrong: The two have different weights and scope.","Correct: For example, medical costs paid for households by employers or insurers are counted in PCE, and its weights update with spending patterns."]},{"id":"information-beginner-37","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[4],"stem":"在BEA价格表里，核心PCE物价指数对应的系列名称是？","options":["Market-based PCE price index","PCE excluding energy goods only","PCE excluding food and energy","PCE excluding food and housing"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：在BEA价格表找 PCE excluding food and energy。","optionExplanations":["Market-based是另一类口径，不是核心PCE。","只剔除能源商品不是核心PCE。","课程：在BEA价格表找 PCE excluding food and energy。","核心PCE剔除食品和能源，不剔除住房。"],"skills":["查找","系列名称"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expenditures-price-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In the BEA price tables, what is the series name for the core PCE price index?","optionsEn":["Market-based PCE price index","PCE excluding energy goods only","PCE excluding food and energy","PCE excluding food and housing"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: in the BEA price tables, find PCE excluding food and energy.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Market-based is a different measure, not core PCE.","Wrong: Excluding only energy goods is not core PCE.","Correct: The lesson: in the BEA price tables, find PCE excluding food and energy.","Wrong: Core PCE excludes food and energy, not housing."]},{"id":"information-advanced-36","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[4],"stem":"核心PCE环比0.25%。若之后12个月每月都一样，一年复合约为多少？","options":["约3.00%，恰好等于月率直接乘12","约3.04%，略高于月率直接乘12","约2.96%，略低于月率直接乘12","约3.30%，复利要多加一个月的增幅"],"answer":1,"explanation":"(1.0025)^12−1≈3.04%；课程提醒不要把单月乘12当精确年率。","optionExplanations":["复利会略高于简单乘12。","(1.0025)^12−1≈3.04%。","复利不会低于简单乘12。","复利只按12期计算，没有多出一个月。"],"skills":["年化","复利"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/personal-consumption-expenditures-price-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Core PCE is 0.25% month over month. If every month for the next 12 is the same, what is the compounded one-year rate, approximately?","optionsEn":["About 3.00%, exactly the monthly rate times 12","About 3.04%, slightly above the monthly rate times 12","About 2.96%, slightly below the monthly rate times 12","About 3.30%, since compounding adds an extra month"],"explanationEn":"(1.0025)^12 − 1 ≈ 3.04%; the lesson warns not to treat one month times 12 as an exact annual rate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Compounding comes out slightly above simply multiplying by 12.","Correct: (1.0025)^12 − 1 ≈ 3.04%.","Wrong: Compounding is never below simply multiplying by 12.","Wrong: Compounding uses 12 periods only; there is no extra month."]},{"id":"information-beginner-38","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[5],"stem":"PPI报告Table 1中，代表“总体PPI”的是哪个系列？","options":["Crude materials","Final demand goods","Final demand","Intermediate demand"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：在PPI Table 1找 Final demand，不要把中间需求当总PPI。","optionExplanations":["Crude materials是原材料分项。","Final demand goods只是商品部分。","课程：在PPI Table 1找 Final demand，不要把中间需求当总PPI。","Intermediate demand是中间需求，不是总体PPI。"],"skills":["查找","系列名称"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ppi.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In Table 1 of the PPI report, which series represents headline PPI?","optionsEn":["Crude materials","Final demand goods","Final demand","Intermediate demand"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: find Final demand in PPI Table 1, and don't take intermediate demand as headline PPI.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Crude materials is a raw-materials component.","Wrong: Final demand goods is only the goods portion.","Correct: The lesson: find Final demand in PPI Table 1, and don't take intermediate demand as headline PPI.","Wrong: Intermediate demand is not headline PPI."]},{"id":"information-advanced-37","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[5],"stem":"某月PPI上涨0.5%。对CPI最稳妥的说法是？","options":["CPI会按相同比例传导，当月同步上涨0.5%","不会等比例传导，可能只传导一部分或延后","CPI涨幅会超过0.5%，因为零售环节还会加价","CPI会在下个月补涨0.5%，时间错后一期"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：企业可能压利润、换供应商或晚些才调价。","optionExplanations":["PPI不会按相同比例传到CPI。","企业可能压利润、换供应商或晚些才调价。","没有理由认为CPI涨幅一定更大。","传导幅度与时间并不固定。"],"skills":["传导","解读"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ppi.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"PPI rises 0.5% in a month. What is the most careful statement about CPI?","optionsEn":["CPI will pass it through one for one and rise 0.5% the same month","It won't pass through proportionally; maybe only partly, or later","CPI will rise more than 0.5% because retailers add a markup","CPI will catch up by 0.5% next month, one period later"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, firms may squeeze margins, switch suppliers or raise prices later.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: PPI does not pass through to CPI in the same proportion.","Correct: Firms may squeeze margins, switch suppliers or raise prices later.","Wrong: There is no reason CPI must rise more.","Wrong: The size and timing of pass-through are not fixed."]},{"id":"information-beginner-39","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[6],"stem":"“Final demand less foods, energy, and trade services”与“less foods and energy”是什么关系？","options":["是两个不同的系列，比较前需对齐口径","是同一系列的两种叫法，数值本应一致","前者为季调数据，后者为未季调数据","前者按同比发布，后者按环比发布"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：两者是不同系列，不能混用；日历里的“核心PPI”定义也可能不同。","optionExplanations":["课程：两者是不同系列，不能混用；日历里的核心PPI定义也可能不同。","多剔除了贸易服务，是不同系列。","区别在于剔除项目，不是季调与否。","区别在于剔除项目，不是同比或环比。"],"skills":["口径","核心定义"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ppi.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does \"Final demand less foods, energy, and trade services\" relate to \"less foods and energy\"?","optionsEn":["They are two different series; align definitions before comparing","They are two names for one series and should match","The first is seasonally adjusted, the second unadjusted","The first is reported year over year, the second month over month"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: they are different series and must not be mixed up; a calendar's \"core PPI\" may also be defined differently.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The lesson: they are different series and must not be mixed up; a calendar's core PPI may also be defined differently.","Wrong: It excludes trade services as well, so it is a different series.","Wrong: The difference is what is excluded, not seasonal adjustment.","Wrong: The difference is what is excluded, not yearly versus monthly."]},{"id":"information-advanced-38","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[6],"stem":"PPI中的“trade services”分项主要衡量什么？","options":["运输仓储服务本身的价格变化","进出口贸易的结算价格变化","批发零售商所得差价的变化","批发零售商销售数量的变化"],"answer":2,"explanation":"BLS的贸易服务指数衡量批发、零售商所得差价的变化，所以它会放大或抵消商品价格。","optionExplanations":["运输仓储是另一类服务。","进出口价格由进出口物价指数衡量。","BLS的贸易服务指数衡量批发、零售商所得差价的变化，所以它会放大或抵消商品价格。","贸易服务衡量差价，不是销量。"],"skills":["分项","含义"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ppi.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the \"trade services\" component of PPI mainly measure?","optionsEn":["Price changes for transportation and warehousing services","Price changes in import and export settlements","Changes in the margins earned by wholesalers and retailers","Changes in wholesalers' and retailers' sales volumes"],"explanationEn":"The BLS trade services index measures changes in margins earned by wholesalers and retailers, so it can amplify or offset goods prices.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Transportation and warehousing is a different service category.","Wrong: Import and export prices are measured by the import/export price indexes.","Correct: The BLS trade services index measures changes in margins earned by wholesalers and retailers, so it can amplify or offset goods prices.","Wrong: Trade services measure margins, not volumes."]},{"id":"information-beginner-40","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[7],"stem":"美国进口物价指数通常是否包含关税？","options":["通常不含关税，不是进口商含税总成本","包含各项关税，反映进口商的含税成本","只包含针对个别国家加征的那部分关税","月度报告不含，仅在年度修订时才并入"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程提醒：通常不含关税本身，不能把它当进口商含税总成本。","optionExplanations":["课程提醒：通常不含关税本身，不能把它当进口商含税总成本。","进口物价指数通常不含关税。","没有只含部分国家关税的口径。","年度修订也不会并入关税。"],"skills":["口径","关税"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ximpim.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Does the US import price index usually include tariffs?","optionsEn":["Usually not; it is not the importer's tariff-inclusive total cost","Yes, all tariffs, reflecting importers' tariff-inclusive cost","Only the extra tariffs on specific countries","Not monthly; they are added only in annual revisions"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, it usually excludes tariffs themselves, so it cannot be treated as importers' total cost including tariffs.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: As the lesson notes, it usually excludes tariffs themselves, so it cannot be treated as importers' total cost including tariffs.","Wrong: The import price index usually excludes tariffs.","Wrong: There is no measure that includes only some countries' tariffs.","Wrong: Annual revisions do not add tariffs either."]},{"id":"information-advanced-39","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[7],"stem":"进出口物价报告里，月度变化通常是哪种口径？","options":["通常季调后再年化","季调后的同比","以美元金额计的变化","通常未季调"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程注明：通常未季调环比与同比，先核对未季调标记。","optionExplanations":["不是年化。","同比与季调是两回事。","它是价格指数变化，不是金额。","课程注明：通常未季调环比与同比，先核对未季调标记。"],"skills":["口径","季调"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ximpim.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In the import/export price report, what basis are monthly changes usually on?","optionsEn":["Usually seasonally adjusted and then annualised","Seasonally adjusted year over year","Changes measured in dollar amounts","Usually not seasonally adjusted"],"explanationEn":"The lesson notes that monthly and yearly changes are usually not seasonally adjusted, so check for the unadjusted label first.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: They are not annualised.","Wrong: Year over year and seasonal adjustment are different things.","Wrong: It is a price index change, not a dollar amount.","Correct: The lesson notes that monthly and yearly changes are usually not seasonally adjusted, so check for the unadjusted label first."]},{"id":"information-beginner-41","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[8],"stem":"出口物价指数衡量的是什么？","options":["美国出口商品的价格变化","美国出口商品的总金额变化","美国出口商品的数量变化","美国贸易顺差的规模变化"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：这不是贸易顺差，也不是出口金额。","optionExplanations":["课程：这不是贸易顺差，也不是出口金额。","出口物价指数不是金额。","出口物价指数不是数量。","贸易顺差是进出口金额之差，与它无关。"],"skills":["定义","易混"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ximpim.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the export price index measure?","optionsEn":["Price changes of US export goods","Changes in the total value of US exports","Changes in the volume of US exports","Changes in the size of the US trade surplus"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: it is neither the trade surplus nor the value of exports.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The lesson: it is neither the trade surplus nor the value of exports.","Wrong: The export price index is not a dollar value.","Wrong: The export price index is not a volume.","Wrong: The trade surplus is the gap between export and import values and is unrelated."]},{"id":"information-beginner-42","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[8],"stem":"想把出口价格上涨拆成农产品与其他，应在报告里找哪两个分项？","options":["Fuel exports与Nonfuel exports","Agricultural与Nonagricultural exports","Goods exports与Services exports","Capital goods与Consumer goods exports"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：读 All exports 后分别看这两个分项。","optionExplanations":["这是燃料拆分，不是农产品。","正确，对应农产品与其他。","这是货物与服务拆分。","这是按用途拆分。"],"skills":["查找","分项"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/ximpim.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"To split a rise in export prices into agricultural and other, which two components should you find in the report?","optionsEn":["Fuel exports and Nonfuel exports","Agricultural and Nonagricultural exports","Goods exports and Services exports","Capital goods and Consumer goods exports"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: read All exports, then look at these two components separately.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is a fuel split, not agriculture.","Correct: These correspond to agricultural and other.","Wrong: That is a goods versus services split.","Wrong: That is a split by end use."]},{"id":"information-beginner-43","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[9],"stem":"雇佣成本指数（ECI）多久发布一次？","options":["每月一次","每半年一次","每季度一次","每年一次"],"answer":2,"explanation":"ECI为季度数据。","optionExplanations":["月度是多数就业数据的频率，ECI不是。","频率偏低，实际是每季度。","正确，ECI为季度数据。","频率偏低，实际是每季度。"],"skills":["频率","基础"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/eci.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How often is the Employment Cost Index (ECI) published?","optionsEn":["Monthly","Every six months","Quarterly","Annually"],"explanationEn":"The ECI is quarterly data.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Monthly is the frequency of most jobs data, but not the ECI.","Wrong: Too infrequent; it is actually quarterly.","Correct: The ECI is quarterly data.","Wrong: Too infrequent; it is actually quarterly."]},{"id":"information-advanced-40","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[9],"stem":"ECI与就业报告的平均时薪相比，主要优点是什么？","options":["把股票期权的市值变动也计入，口径更完整","每周发布一次，时效性比平均时薪更强","样本只含大型企业，因此数据精确度更高","用固定岗位权重，受岗位构成变化影响较小"],"answer":3,"explanation":"平均时薪会因低薪或高薪岗位人数变化而跳动，ECI用固定权重减少这种影响。","optionExplanations":["ECI不含股票期权市值变化。","ECI按季度发布，平均时薪才是月度。","ECI覆盖各类雇主，不是只含大企业。","平均时薪会因低薪或高薪岗位人数变化而跳动，ECI用固定权重减少这种影响。"],"skills":["比较","构成效应"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/eci.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the ECI's main advantage over average hourly earnings in the jobs report?","optionsEn":["It also counts changes in stock-option value, so it is more complete","It is published weekly, so it is more timely","Its sample covers only large firms, so it is more precise","It uses fixed job weights, so shifts in job mix affect it less"],"explanationEn":"Average hourly earnings jump when the number of low- or high-paid jobs changes; the ECI's fixed weights reduce that effect.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The ECI does not include changes in stock-option value.","Wrong: The ECI is quarterly; average hourly earnings are monthly.","Wrong: The ECI covers all kinds of employers, not just large firms.","Correct: Average hourly earnings jump when the number of low- or high-paid jobs changes; the ECI's fixed weights reduce that effect."]},{"id":"information-beginner-44","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[10],"stem":"密歇根大学报告中的“未来1年通胀预期”是什么？","options":["美联储对明年通胀的预测","实际CPI的前瞻估计","债券市场隐含的通胀率","受访消费者预期的中位数"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：读数是预期中位数，不要当央行预测。","optionExplanations":["那是央行的经济预测。","它是调查结果，不是统计估计。","那是盈亏平衡通胀率。","课程：读数是预期中位数，不要当央行预测。"],"skills":["定义","易混"],"references":[{"title":"密歇根大学消费者调查：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.sca.isr.umich.edu/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the \"1-year inflation expectation\" in the University of Michigan report?","optionsEn":["The Fed's forecast for next year's inflation","A forward estimate of actual CPI","The inflation rate implied by the bond market","The median expectation of surveyed consumers"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the reading is a median expectation; don't treat it as a central bank forecast.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is the central bank's economic projection.","Wrong: It is a survey result, not a statistical estimate.","Wrong: That is breakeven inflation.","Correct: The lesson: the reading is a median expectation; don't treat it as a central bank forecast."]},{"id":"information-beginner-45","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[10],"stem":"同一个月的密歇根初值和终值有什么区别？","options":["终值只调查专业分析师而非普通居民","终值在月末发布，样本比初值更完整","初值描述上个月的情况，终值描述当月","初值与终值使用的问卷题目有所不同"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：初值只覆盖当月部分样本，终值更新。","optionExplanations":["两者调查对象都是消费者。","课程：初值只覆盖当月部分样本，终值更新。","两者都描述同一个月。","两者使用同一份问卷。"],"skills":["初值终值","修订"],"references":[{"title":"密歇根大学消费者调查：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.sca.isr.umich.edu/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the difference between the Michigan preliminary and final readings for the same month?","optionsEn":["The final surveys only professional analysts, not households","The final comes out at month-end with a fuller sample than the preliminary","The preliminary describes last month; the final describes this month","The preliminary and final use different survey questions"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the preliminary covers only part of the month's sample, and the final updates it.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Both survey consumers.","Correct: The lesson: the preliminary covers only part of the month's sample, and the final updates it.","Wrong: Both describe the same month.","Wrong: Both use the same questionnaire."]},{"id":"information-beginner-46","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[11],"stem":"就业报告中的非农新增就业人数来自哪项调查？","options":["对企业的机构调查（CES）","对家庭的住户调查（CPS）","各州失业保险的申请记录","ADP提供的私营部门薪资数据"],"answer":0,"explanation":"非农岗位来自对企业的调查。","optionExplanations":["非农岗位来自对企业的调查。","家庭调查用于计算失业率。","失业保险申请是初请、续请的来源。","ADP是私营机构数据，不是BLS非农来源。"],"skills":["来源","调查"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which survey does the nonfarm payrolls number in the jobs report come from?","optionsEn":["The establishment survey of employers (CES)","The household survey (CPS)","State unemployment insurance claims","ADP's private-sector payroll data"],"explanationEn":"Nonfarm payrolls come from the survey of employers.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Nonfarm payrolls come from the survey of employers.","Wrong: The household survey is used for the unemployment rate.","Wrong: Unemployment insurance filings are the source of initial and continuing claims.","Wrong: ADP is private-company data, not the BLS payroll source."]},{"id":"information-beginner-47","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[11],"stem":"就业报告Table B-1的变化以“千人”为单位，读到“250”表示什么？","options":["表示新增约25万个岗位","表示新增约250万个岗位","表示新增约2.5万个岗位","表示新增约250个岗位"],"answer":0,"explanation":"250千=25万。","optionExplanations":["250千=25万。","把千当成万了。","少算了一位。","忘记单位是千人。"],"skills":["单位","读表"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Changes in Table B-1 of the jobs report are in thousands. What does a reading of \"250\" mean?","optionsEn":["About 250,000 jobs added","About 2.5 million jobs added","About 25,000 jobs added","About 250 jobs added"],"explanationEn":"250 thousand = 250,000.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 250 thousand = 250,000.","Wrong: This reads thousands as tens of thousands.","Wrong: This drops a digit.","Wrong: This forgets that the unit is thousands."]},{"id":"information-beginner-48","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[12],"stem":"失业率（U-3）来自哪项调查？","options":["对企业的薪资调查（CES）","各州每周失业金申请记录","对家庭的抽样调查（CPS）","JOLTS职位空缺调查"],"answer":2,"explanation":"失业率由对住户的抽样调查得出。","optionExplanations":["CES用于非农就业与时薪。","申请记录是初请数据，不用于计算失业率。","失业率由对住户的抽样调查得出。","JOLTS衡量空缺、招聘、离职。"],"skills":["来源","调查"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which survey does the unemployment rate (U-3) come from?","optionsEn":["The payroll survey of employers (CES)","States' weekly jobless claims records","The household sample survey (CPS)","The JOLTS job openings survey"],"explanationEn":"The unemployment rate comes from a sample survey of households.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: CES is used for nonfarm payrolls and hourly earnings.","Wrong: Claims records are initial-claims data and are not used to calculate the unemployment rate.","Correct: The unemployment rate comes from a sample survey of households.","Wrong: JOLTS measures openings, hires and separations."]},{"id":"information-beginner-49","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[12],"stem":"失业率从4.1%升到4.3%，正确的说法是？","options":["上升了约4.9个百分点","上升了0.2%的相对幅度","上升了约2个百分点","上升了0.2个百分点"],"answer":3,"explanation":"4.3%减4.1%得0.2，百分比之间的差用百分点表示。","optionExplanations":["错误：4.9是相对涨幅的数字，却错用了百分点单位。","错误：0.2是绝对差值，写成0.2%会把百分点与相对涨幅混淆。","错误：把差值小数点错位放大了十倍。","正确：4.3%减4.1%得0.2，百分比之间的差用百分点表示。"],"skills":["百分点","单位"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The unemployment rate rises from 4.1% to 4.3%. Which statement is correct?","optionsEn":["It rose about 4.9 percentage points","It rose 0.2% in relative terms","It rose about 2 percentage points","It rose 0.2 percentage point"],"explanationEn":"4.3% minus 4.1% is 0.2; differences between percentages are expressed in percentage points.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: 4.9 is the relative increase but is wrongly given in percentage points.","Wrong: 0.2 is the absolute difference; writing 0.2% confuses percentage points with relative change.","Wrong: The decimal point is shifted, inflating the difference tenfold.","Correct: 4.3% minus 4.1% is 0.2; differences between percentages are expressed in percentage points."]},{"id":"information-beginner-50","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[13],"stem":"劳动参与率的计算方法是？","options":["就业人数÷16岁以上非机构人口","劳动力÷16岁以上非机构人口","失业人数÷16岁以上非机构人口","劳动力÷包括儿童的全国总人口"],"answer":1,"explanation":"参与率用劳动力（就业加失业）除以适龄非机构平民人口。","optionExplanations":["错误：分子只有就业人数，这是就业人口比而不是参与率。","正确：参与率用劳动力（就业加失业）除以适龄非机构平民人口。","错误：失业人数只是劳动力的一部分，分子不对。","错误：分母应是16岁以上非机构人口，不含儿童。"],"skills":["定义","公式"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How is the labour force participation rate calculated?","optionsEn":["Employed ÷ civilian noninstitutional population aged 16+","Labour force ÷ civilian noninstitutional population aged 16+","Unemployed ÷ civilian noninstitutional population aged 16+","Labour force ÷ total population including children"],"explanationEn":"The participation rate is the labour force (employed plus unemployed) divided by the working-age civilian noninstitutional population.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: With only the employed on top, this is the employment–population ratio, not participation.","Correct: The participation rate is the labour force (employed plus unemployed) divided by the working-age civilian noninstitutional population.","Wrong: The unemployed are only part of the labour force, so the numerator is wrong.","Wrong: The denominator should be the noninstitutional population aged 16 and over, excluding children."]},{"id":"information-advanced-41","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[13],"stem":"为什么课程建议同时看25—54岁的参与率？","options":["排除老龄化退休的影响，更接近周期变化","该群体样本最大，调查误差因此更小","该群体含青年学生，更能反映新入职潮","该群体数据按周更新，比总体参与率更及时"],"answer":0,"explanation":"25至54岁多处于工作年龄，能减少退休潮对总参与率的干扰。","optionExplanations":["正确：25至54岁多处于工作年龄，能减少退休潮对总参与率的干扰。","错误：课程给的理由是剔除老龄化退休，而不是样本量。","错误：25至54岁已基本完成学业，并不以学生为主。","错误：参与率均为月度数据，没有按年龄段更早发布。"],"skills":["解读","结构因素"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Why does the lesson suggest also looking at the 25–54 participation rate?","optionsEn":["It strips out ageing-driven retirement and is closer to cyclical change","This group has the largest sample, so survey error is smaller","This group includes young students, so it better shows waves of new hires","This group's data updates weekly, so it is timelier than the total"],"explanationEn":"People aged 25 to 54 are mostly of working age, which reduces the effect of retirement waves on total participation.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: People aged 25 to 54 are mostly of working age, which reduces the effect of retirement waves on total participation.","Wrong: The lesson's reason is removing ageing and retirement, not sample size.","Wrong: People aged 25 to 54 have mostly finished school and are not mainly students.","Wrong: Participation rates are all monthly; no age group is published earlier."]},{"id":"information-beginner-51","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[14],"stem":"就业报告里“all employees”与“production and nonsupervisory”两种平均时薪是什么关系？","options":["前者为名义时薪，后者为实际时薪","前者为同比增速，后者为环比增速","覆盖对象不同的两个系列，不能混用","同一系列，后者只是前者的季调版本"],"answer":2,"explanation":"all employees覆盖全部雇员，另一个只含生产和非管理人员，是不同系列。","optionExplanations":["错误：两者都是名义时薪，区别在覆盖人群而非是否扣除物价。","错误：两个系列都是时薪水平，与同比环比无关。","正确：all employees覆盖全部雇员，另一个只含生产和非管理人员，是不同系列。","错误：它们的统计对象不同，并非同一系列的季调与否。"],"skills":["口径","查找"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How do the jobs report's two average hourly earnings series, \"all employees\" and \"production and nonsupervisory\", relate?","optionsEn":["The first is nominal and the second real hourly pay","The first is year-over-year growth, the second month-over-month","Two series covering different workers; don't mix them up","The same series; the second is just the seasonally adjusted version"],"explanationEn":"All employees covers every employee, while the other covers only production and nonsupervisory workers; they are different series.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Both are nominal pay; the difference is who is covered, not price adjustment.","Wrong: Both series are pay levels, unrelated to yearly or monthly change.","Correct: All employees covers every employee, while the other covers only production and nonsupervisory workers; they are different series.","Wrong: They cover different workers; it is not a question of seasonal adjustment."]},{"id":"information-beginner-52","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[14],"stem":"平均时薪同比+4%，同期CPI同比+3%。实际工资大约怎样？","options":["上升约1%","上升约7%","上升约4%","下降约1%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"实际≈名义−物价≈1%；课程提醒名义工资增长不能直接当实际收入增长。","optionExplanations":["实际≈名义−物价≈1%；课程提醒名义工资增长不能直接当实际收入增长。","不应相加。","忽略了物价。","方向错误。"],"skills":["名义与实际","计算"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Average hourly earnings are +4% year over year and CPI +3%. Roughly what happened to real wages?","optionsEn":["Up about 1%","Up about 7%","Up about 4%","Down about 1%"],"explanationEn":"Real ≈ nominal − prices ≈ 1%; the lesson warns that nominal wage growth is not real income growth.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Real ≈ nominal − prices ≈ 1%; the lesson warns that nominal wage growth is not real income growth.","Wrong: They should not be added.","Wrong: This ignores prices.","Wrong: The direction is wrong."]},{"id":"information-advanced-42","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[15],"stem":"某月就业人数+0.1%，平均每周工时−0.6%。总工时（就业×工时）大约变化多少？","options":["约+0.1%","约−0.5%","约−0.6%","约−0.7%"],"answer":1,"explanation":"(1+0.001)×(1−0.006)−1约为−0.5%，要把人数与工时合起来看。","optionExplanations":["错误：只看了就业人数，忽略了工时下降。","正确：(1+0.001)×(1−0.006)−1约为−0.5%，要把人数与工时合起来看。","错误：只看了工时变化，忽略了就业人数上升。","错误：把两项变化符号弄反后相减，得出偏大的降幅。"],"skills":["计算","总投入"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In one month employment is +0.1% and average weekly hours −0.6%. Roughly how much do total hours (employment × hours) change?","optionsEn":["About +0.1%","About −0.5%","About −0.6%","About −0.7%"],"explanationEn":"(1 + 0.001) × (1 − 0.006) − 1 ≈ −0.5%; headcount and hours must be read together.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This looks only at employment and ignores the fall in hours.","Correct: (1 + 0.001) × (1 − 0.006) − 1 ≈ −0.5%; headcount and hours must be read together.","Wrong: This looks only at hours and ignores the rise in employment.","Wrong: This flips a sign and subtracts, overstating the fall."]},{"id":"information-beginner-53","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[15],"stem":"平均每周工时数据在就业报告的哪张表？","options":["Table A-1","Table B-3","Table B-2","Table B-1"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：在Table B-2找 Average weekly hours。","optionExplanations":["A-1是家庭调查表。","B-3是平均时薪。","课程：在Table B-2找 Average weekly hours。","B-1是岗位数。"],"skills":["查找","表格"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which table of the jobs report has average weekly hours?","optionsEn":["Table A-1","Table B-3","Table B-2","Table B-1"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: find Average weekly hours in Table B-2.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A-1 is a household survey table.","Wrong: B-3 is average hourly earnings.","Correct: The lesson: find Average weekly hours in Table B-2.","Wrong: B-1 is payroll jobs."]},{"id":"information-beginner-54","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[16],"stem":"美国初请失业金数据多久发布一次？","options":["每月一次，通常在月初周五公布","每两周一次，通常在周三公布","每周一次，通常在周四公布","每季一次，通常在季末后公布"],"answer":2,"explanation":"初请失业金是周度数据，通常周四公布。","optionExplanations":["错误：这是月度非农就业报告的节奏，不是初请。","错误：初请不是双周数据，而是每周公布。","正确：初请失业金是周度数据，通常周四公布。","错误：季度发布是GDP等数据的节奏，初请远比这频繁。"],"skills":["频率","基础"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工部 DOL：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.dol.gov/ui/data.pdf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How often is US initial jobless claims data published?","optionsEn":["Monthly, usually on the first Friday","Every two weeks, usually on Wednesday","Weekly, usually on Thursday","Quarterly, usually after quarter-end"],"explanationEn":"Initial jobless claims are weekly data, usually released on Thursday.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is the rhythm of the monthly payrolls report, not claims.","Wrong: Claims are not biweekly; they come out every week.","Correct: Initial jobless claims are weekly data, usually released on Thursday.","Wrong: Quarterly is the rhythm of data such as GDP; claims are far more frequent."]},{"id":"information-beginner-55","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[16],"stem":"初请失业金24万表示什么？","options":["本周获批领取失业救济的新增人数","本周正在领取失业救济的总人数","本周新增失业者的完整统计人数","本周首次提交失业保险申请的件数"],"answer":3,"explanation":"初请是首次申请的件数，申请不等于获批。","optionExplanations":["错误：申请不等于获批，初请统计的是申请件数。","错误：正在领取的存量人数对应续请，不是初请。","错误：初请并不完整覆盖所有失业者，也不是新增失业人数。","正确：初请是首次申请的件数，申请不等于获批。"],"skills":["定义","易混"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工部 DOL：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.dol.gov/ui/data.pdf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What do initial jobless claims of 240,000 represent?","optionsEn":["The number newly approved for unemployment benefits this week","The total number receiving unemployment benefits this week","A complete count of people newly unemployed this week","The number of first-time unemployment insurance claims filed this week"],"explanationEn":"Initial claims count first-time filings; filing is not approval.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Filing is not approval; initial claims count filings.","Wrong: The stock of people receiving benefits is continuing claims, not initial claims.","Wrong: Initial claims do not fully cover all unemployed people and are not new unemployment.","Correct: Initial claims count first-time filings; filing is not approval."]},{"id":"information-beginner-56","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[17],"stem":"续请失业金的统计周与初请相比是怎样？","options":["一般比初请的统计周再落后一周","比初请的统计周提前一周左右","比初请的统计周滞后约一个月","与初请相同，只是公布日期不同"],"answer":0,"explanation":"续请的统计周一般比初请再落后一周，别拿错日期。","optionExplanations":["正确：续请的统计周一般比初请再落后一周，别拿错日期。","错误：方向反了，续请是落后而不是提前。","错误：滞后的幅度被夸大，一般只差一周。","错误：两者的统计周并不相同，续请再落后一周。"],"skills":["时间","读表"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工部 DOL：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.dol.gov/ui/data.pdf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does the reference week of continuing claims compare with initial claims?","optionsEn":["It usually lags initial claims by one more week","It is about one week ahead of initial claims","It lags initial claims by about a month","Same as initial claims; only the release date differs"],"explanationEn":"Continuing claims' reference week usually lags initial claims by one more week, so don't mix up the dates.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Continuing claims' reference week usually lags initial claims by one more week, so don't mix up the dates.","Wrong: The direction is reversed; continuing claims lag rather than lead.","Wrong: The lag is overstated; it is usually only one week.","Wrong: The reference weeks are not the same; continuing claims lag by one more week."]},{"id":"information-advanced-43","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[17],"stem":"续请失业金连续下降。哪种情况也会造成这种下降？","options":["初请快速上升，更多人进入领取队列","部分人领取期限耗尽，仍未找到工作","企业缩减招聘，失业者更难重新就业","经济转弱，领取失业金者逐步增多"],"answer":1,"explanation":"领取期限耗尽的人不再被统计为续请，即使仍未就业。","optionExplanations":["错误：这会使续请上升而不是下降。","正确：领取期限耗尽的人不再被统计为续请，即使仍未就业。","错误：失业者找不到工作会停留在领取队列，续请不会因此下降。","错误：领取者增多对应续请上升，与下降相反。"],"skills":["局限","解读"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工部 DOL：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.dol.gov/ui/data.pdf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Continuing claims keep falling. Which situation could also cause this decline?","optionsEn":["Initial claims rising fast, with more people entering the benefit rolls","Some people exhausting their benefits without finding work","Firms cutting hiring, making it harder for the unemployed to find work","A weakening economy, with more people gradually claiming benefits"],"explanationEn":"People who exhaust their benefits are no longer counted in continuing claims, even if they are still out of work.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This would make continuing claims rise, not fall.","Correct: People who exhaust their benefits are no longer counted in continuing claims, even if they are still out of work.","Wrong: Unemployed people who cannot find work stay on the rolls, so continuing claims would not fall.","Wrong: More claimants means continuing claims rise, the opposite of a fall."]},{"id":"information-advanced-44","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[18],"stem":"职位空缺率=空缺÷(就业+空缺)。空缺800万、就业15,200万，空缺率约为多少？","options":["5.0%","5.3%","4.8%","8.0%"],"answer":0,"explanation":"800÷(15200+800)=5.0%。","optionExplanations":["正确：800÷(15200+800)=5.0%。","错误：分母漏掉了空缺本身，只用了800÷15200。","错误：分母多加了一次空缺，算成了800÷16800。","错误：把分母误取为10000，没有按公式计算。"],"skills":["计算","比率"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/jolts.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Job openings rate = openings ÷ (employment + openings). With 8 million openings and 152 million employed, what is the openings rate, approximately?","optionsEn":["5.0%","5.3%","4.8%","8.0%"],"explanationEn":"8 ÷ (152 + 8) = 5.0%.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 8 ÷ (152 + 8) = 5.0%.","Wrong: The denominator leaves out openings, using only 8 ÷ 152.","Wrong: The denominator adds openings twice, giving 8 ÷ 168.","Wrong: This takes 100 million as the denominator instead of using the formula."]},{"id":"information-beginner-57","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[18],"stem":"JOLTS中“职位空缺”和“招聘人数（Hires）”有什么不同？","options":["空缺是已入职人数，招聘是待填岗位数","招聘人数就是非农新增就业的另一称呼","空缺是已经招满的岗位，招聘是新增空缺","空缺是待填岗位，招聘是已经入职的人数"],"answer":3,"explanation":"空缺是尚未填补的岗位，招聘是实际入职的人数。","optionExplanations":["错误：把两个概念的含义互换了。","错误：非农新增还要扣除离职，不等于招聘人数。","错误：空缺是尚未招满的岗位，描述与定义相反。","正确：空缺是尚未填补的岗位，招聘是实际入职的人数。"],"skills":["定义","区分"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/jolts.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In JOLTS, how do job openings differ from hires?","optionsEn":["Openings are people who started; hires are unfilled positions","Hires are just another name for nonfarm payroll gains","Openings are filled positions; hires are new vacancies","Openings are unfilled positions; hires are people who actually started"],"explanationEn":"Openings are positions not yet filled; hires are the number of people who actually started work.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This swaps the two meanings.","Wrong: Payroll gains also net out separations, so they are not equal to hires.","Wrong: Openings are positions not yet filled; this description is the reverse.","Correct: Openings are positions not yet filled; hires are the number of people who actually started work."]},{"id":"information-beginner-58","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[19],"stem":"JOLTS里的主动离职（Quits）属于哪一类？","options":["离职中被企业裁员和解雇的部分","离职中因退休或工作调动的部分","离职中员工主动提出离开的部分","新入职员工在试用期内离开的部分"],"answer":2,"explanation":"Quits指员工主动辞职，是离职的一个分项。","optionExplanations":["错误：裁员与解雇属于另一分项，不是Quits。","错误：退休、调职归在其他离职类别，不都属于Quits。","正确：Quits指员工主动辞职，是离职的一个分项。","错误：Quits不按是否试用期划分，而按主动离开界定。"],"skills":["分类","定义"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/jolts.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which category do quits belong to in JOLTS?","optionsEn":["The part of separations that are layoffs and discharges","The part of separations due to retirement or transfers","The part of separations where employees chose to leave","New hires who leave during their probation period"],"explanationEn":"Quits are voluntary resignations, one component of separations.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Layoffs and discharges are a separate component, not quits.","Wrong: Retirements and transfers fall under other separations, not quits.","Correct: Quits are voluntary resignations, one component of separations.","Wrong: Quits are not defined by probation status but by leaving voluntarily."]},{"id":"information-beginner-59","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[19],"stem":"比较不同年份的主动离职，课程建议看比率还是人数？","options":["看人数，因为人数最直接反映离职规模","看人数，因为比率的分母每月都在变","看各行业人数，因为总量会掩盖差异","看比率，因为就业规模每年都在变"],"answer":3,"explanation":"就业规模会变，应看Total nonfarm rate而不只看人数。","optionExplanations":["错误：不同年份就业规模不同，人数无法直接比较。","错误：分母随规模变化正是要用比率校正的原因。","错误：比较不同年份应先用总比率校正规模，而不是只看行业人数。","正确：就业规模会变，应看Total nonfarm rate而不只看人数。"],"skills":["读表","比率"],"references":[{"title":"美国劳工统计局 BLS：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/jolts.toc.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"When comparing quits across years, does the lesson suggest looking at the rate or the count?","optionsEn":["The count, because it most directly shows the scale of quitting","The count, because the rate's denominator changes every month","Counts by industry, because the total masks differences","The rate, because employment levels change from year to year"],"explanationEn":"Employment levels change, so look at the Total nonfarm rate rather than just the count.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Employment levels differ across years, so counts cannot be compared directly.","Wrong: A denominator that changes with scale is exactly why the rate is used to correct for it.","Wrong: To compare years, first correct for scale with the total rate rather than only industry counts.","Correct: Employment levels change, so look at the Total nonfarm rate rather than just the count."]},{"id":"information-beginner-60","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[20],"stem":"ADP全国就业报告覆盖哪些就业？","options":["私营部门与联邦、州政府合计就业","仅覆盖制造业和建筑业的就业","私营部门（不含政府）的就业","仅覆盖大型上市公司的就业"],"answer":2,"explanation":"ADP只覆盖私营部门。","optionExplanations":["错误：ADP不含政府部门，合计口径对应非农总数。","错误：ADP覆盖私营各行业，不限于这两类。","正确：ADP只覆盖私营部门。","错误：ADP覆盖各类私营企业，不限于大型上市公司。"],"skills":["范围","基础"],"references":[{"title":"ADP Research 与斯坦福数字经济实验室：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://adpemploymentreport.com/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which jobs does the ADP National Employment Report cover?","optionsEn":["Private-sector plus federal and state government jobs combined","Only manufacturing and construction jobs","Private-sector jobs (excluding government)","Only jobs at large listed companies"],"explanationEn":"ADP covers only the private sector.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: ADP excludes government; the combined measure matches total nonfarm.","Wrong: ADP covers all private industries, not just these two.","Correct: ADP covers only the private sector.","Wrong: ADP covers all kinds of private firms, not just large listed ones."]},{"id":"information-beginner-61","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[20],"stem":"ADP报告中的Pay Insights是什么？","options":["工资变化数据，与岗位数分开","对下一份非农岗位数的预测模型","岗位数的另一种季调口径","官方非农工资调查的提前版本"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Pay Insights是工资数据，要与岗位数分开。","optionExplanations":["正确：Pay Insights是工资数据，要与岗位数分开。","错误：Pay Insights是工资数据，不是预测模型。","错误：它讲工资而不是岗位，与季调口径无关。","错误：它是ADP自己的数据，并非官方调查的提前版。"],"skills":["分项","区分"],"references":[{"title":"ADP Research 与斯坦福数字经济实验室：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://adpemploymentreport.com/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is Pay Insights in the ADP report?","optionsEn":["Pay-change data, separate from the job count","A model forecasting the next payrolls number","Another seasonally adjusted version of the job count","An early version of the official payroll wage survey"],"explanationEn":"Pay Insights is pay data and should be kept separate from the job count.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Pay Insights is pay data and should be kept separate from the job count.","Wrong: Pay Insights is pay data, not a forecasting model.","Wrong: It covers pay rather than jobs and has nothing to do with seasonal adjustment.","Wrong: It is ADP's own data, not an early version of an official survey."]},{"id":"information-beginner-62","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[21],"stem":"实际GDP季度环比折年率为2%。这个季度本身大约增长了多少？","options":["2%","8%","约0.2%","约0.5%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"折年率≈(1+季度增长)^4−1；2%折年约对应0.5%的季度增长。","optionExplanations":["那是折年率本身。","错误地再乘4。","计算错误。","折年率≈(1+季度增长)^4−1；2%折年约对应0.5%的季度增长。"],"skills":["折年率","换算"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/gdp/gross-domestic-product"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Real GDP grows at a 2% annualised quarterly rate. Roughly how much did the quarter itself grow?","optionsEn":["2%","8%","About 0.2%","About 0.5%"],"explanationEn":"Annualised rate ≈ (1 + quarterly growth)^4 − 1, so 2% annualised is about 0.5% quarterly growth.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is the annualised rate itself.","Wrong: This wrongly multiplies by 4 again.","Wrong: Calculation error.","Correct: Annualised rate ≈ (1 + quarterly growth)^4 − 1, so 2% annualised is about 0.5% quarterly growth."]},{"id":"information-beginner-63","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[21],"stem":"BEA的GDP对同一季度会发布几轮估计？","options":["公布一次后仅在十年普查时修订","多轮估计，之后还会年度修订","每月滚动更新，但不再有年度修订","初值公布后每周根据高频数据更新"],"answer":1,"explanation":"GDP有多轮估计与年度修订。","optionExplanations":["错误：GDP修订频繁得多，包括多轮估计和年度修订。","正确：GDP有多轮估计与年度修订。","错误：GDP是季度估计，且仍有年度修订。","错误：GDP不按周更新，而是按轮次与年度修订。"],"skills":["修订","发布节奏"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/gdp/gross-domestic-product"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How many rounds of estimates does the BEA publish for GDP for the same quarter?","optionsEn":["One release, revised only in ten-year benchmarks","Several estimates, followed by annual revisions","Rolling monthly updates, with no annual revisions","Weekly updates from high-frequency data after the first release"],"explanationEn":"GDP has several rounds of estimates plus annual revisions.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: GDP is revised far more often, including several estimates and annual revisions.","Correct: GDP has several rounds of estimates plus annual revisions.","Wrong: GDP estimates are quarterly and still have annual revisions.","Wrong: GDP is not updated weekly but by estimate rounds and annual revisions."]},{"id":"information-beginner-64","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[22],"stem":"GDI是从哪一侧估算经济规模？","options":["生产侧：各行业增加值","收入侧：工资、利润等收入","支出侧：消费、投资、政府、净出口","货币侧：货币供给"],"answer":1,"explanation":"GDI加总生产过程中产生的收入。","optionExplanations":["那是行业增加值口径。","GDI加总生产过程中产生的收入。","那是GDP支出法。","不是货币指标。"],"skills":["定义","估算方法"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/gross-domestic-income"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"From which side does GDI estimate the size of the economy?","optionsEn":["Production: value added by industry","Income: wages, profits and other income","Expenditure: consumption, investment, government, net exports","Money: the money supply"],"explanationEn":"GDI adds up the income generated in production.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is the industry value-added measure.","Correct: GDI adds up the income generated in production.","Wrong: That is the expenditure approach to GDP.","Wrong: It is not a monetary measure."]},{"id":"information-advanced-45","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[22],"stem":"GDP与GDI读数差距大时，BEA另外公布了什么可以参考？","options":["GDP与GNP的平均值","GDP与国民总收入的比值","GDP与GDI的平均值","GDI与个人收入的平均值"],"answer":2,"explanation":"BEA公布GDP与GDI平均值，两者差距大时可作参考。","optionExplanations":["错误：BEA给出的平均是GDP与GDI之间的，而不是GNP。","错误：BEA没有用比值来调和两者。","正确：BEA公布GDP与GDI平均值，两者差距大时可作参考。","错误：个人收入是另一份报告，不是GDP与GDI的调和值。"],"skills":["读表","平均"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/gross-domestic-income"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"When GDP and GDI readings are far apart, what else does the BEA publish for reference?","optionsEn":["The average of GDP and GNP","The ratio of GDP to gross national income","The average of GDP and GDI","The average of GDI and personal income"],"explanationEn":"The BEA publishes the average of GDP and GDI, which helps when the two are far apart.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The BEA's average is of GDP and GDI, not GNP.","Wrong: The BEA does not reconcile them with a ratio.","Correct: The BEA publishes the average of GDP and GDI, which helps when the two are far apart.","Wrong: Personal income is a separate report, not a reconciliation of GDP and GDI."]},{"id":"information-beginner-65","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[23],"stem":"按ISM的算法（改善的比例全部计入、不变的计一半），某扩散指数：30%回答改善、40%不变、30%变差。指数为多少？","options":["50","70","0","30"],"answer":0,"explanation":"改善全部计入，不变计一半：30+40÷2=50。","optionExplanations":["正确：改善全部计入，不变计一半：30+40÷2=50。","错误：把不变的也全部计入，算成30+40。","错误：用改善减变差得到净差额，而不是ISM的扩散算法。","错误：只数了改善的比例，漏掉不变的一半。"],"skills":["计算","扩散指数"],"references":[{"title":"美国供应管理协会 ISM：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.ismworld.org/supply-management-news-and-reports/reports/ism-pmi-reports/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"Using ISM's method (count the full share improving and half the share unchanged), a diffusion index has 30% improving, 40% unchanged and 30% worse. What is the index?","optionsEn":["50","70","0","30"],"explanationEn":"Count improving in full and unchanged at half: 30 + 40 ÷ 2 = 50.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Count improving in full and unchanged at half: 30 + 40 ÷ 2 = 50.","Wrong: This counts all of the unchanged share, giving 30 + 40.","Wrong: This takes improving minus worse, a net balance rather than ISM's diffusion method.","Wrong: This counts only the improving share and leaves out half the unchanged."]},{"id":"information-advanced-46","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[23],"stem":"ISM制造业的供应商交货指数上升，表示什么？","options":["交货变快，说明供应链压力正在缓解","交货变慢，可能因需求强或供给受阻","供应商数量增加，交货竞争更激烈","供应商报价上涨，原料成本上升"],"answer":1,"explanation":"供应商交货指数上升表示交货变慢，原因可能是需求强也可能是供给受阻。","optionExplanations":["错误：方向反了，指数上升表示交货变慢。","正确：供应商交货指数上升表示交货变慢，原因可能是需求强也可能是供给受阻。","错误：该指数问的是交货速度，不是供应商数量。","错误：价格由另一个分项衡量，不是交货指数。"],"skills":["分项","解读"],"references":[{"title":"美国供应管理协会 ISM：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.ismworld.org/supply-management-news-and-reports/reports/ism-pmi-reports/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does a rise in the ISM manufacturing Supplier Deliveries index mean?","optionsEn":["Faster deliveries, showing supply-chain pressure is easing","Slower deliveries, possibly from strong demand or supply constraints","More suppliers, so delivery competition is fiercer","Suppliers raising prices, so input costs are rising"],"explanationEn":"A rising Supplier Deliveries index means slower deliveries, which can come from strong demand or from supply constraints.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The direction is reversed; a rising index means slower deliveries.","Correct: A rising Supplier Deliveries index means slower deliveries, which can come from strong demand or supply constraints.","Wrong: The index asks about delivery speed, not the number of suppliers.","Wrong: Prices are measured by another component, not the deliveries index."]},{"id":"information-beginner-66","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[24],"stem":"ISM服务业报告的“Services PMI”与“Business Activity”分项是什么关系？","options":["总指数等同于商业活动分项的同比值","总指数是商业活动与价格两项的平均","商业活动是总指数的季调前原始读数","总指数由多个分项合成，非商业活动"],"answer":3,"explanation":"总指数由几个分项合成，不是单独的Business Activity。","optionExplanations":["错误：总指数不是商业活动的同比，而是多个分项合成。","错误：合成总指数的分项不包括价格，也不止两项。","错误：两者是不同指数，并非季调前后关系。","正确：总指数由几个分项合成，不是单独的Business Activity。"],"skills":["结构","区分"],"references":[{"title":"美国供应管理协会 ISM：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.ismworld.org/supply-management-news-and-reports/reports/ism-pmi-reports/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does the ISM services report's \"Services PMI\" relate to its \"Business Activity\" component?","optionsEn":["The headline index equals Business Activity's year-over-year value","The headline index is the average of Business Activity and Prices","Business Activity is the headline index before seasonal adjustment","The headline index combines several components, not just Business Activity"],"explanationEn":"The headline index is built from several components; it is not Business Activity alone.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The headline is not Business Activity's yearly change but a composite of several components.","Wrong: The components that form the headline do not include Prices, and there are more than two.","Wrong: They are different indices, not before-and-after seasonal adjustment.","Correct: The headline index is built from several components; it is not Business Activity alone."]},{"id":"information-beginner-67","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[24],"stem":"ISM服务业Prices分项为60，含义是什么？","options":["服务价格较上月平均上涨约6%","报告涨价的企业占比正好是六成","涨价的企业明显多于降价的企业","服务企业利润率同比提升六成"],"answer":2,"explanation":"扩散指数衡量回答的广度，不是涨幅。","optionExplanations":["错误：扩散指数衡量回答的广度，不是价格涨幅。","错误：指数60是综合涨价、持平后的读数，不等于涨价企业占比。","正确：扩散指数衡量回答的广度，不是涨幅。","错误：Prices分项问价格，不反映利润率。"],"skills":["扩散指数","单位"],"references":[{"title":"美国供应管理协会 ISM：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.ismworld.org/supply-management-news-and-reports/reports/ism-pmi-reports/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The ISM services Prices component reads 60. What does that mean?","optionsEn":["Service prices rose about 6% on average from last month","Exactly 60% of firms reported higher prices","Firms raising prices clearly outnumber those cutting them","Service firms' profit margins rose 60% year over year"],"explanationEn":"A diffusion index measures how widespread responses are, not the size of the increase.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A diffusion index measures how widespread responses are, not the size of price increases.","Wrong: 60 combines firms reporting higher and unchanged prices, so it is not the share reporting increases.","Correct: A diffusion index measures how widespread responses are, not the size of the increase.","Wrong: The Prices component asks about prices and does not reflect margins."]},{"id":"information-beginner-68","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[25],"stem":"标普全球PMI的Flash和Final是什么？","options":["Flash是季调数据，Final是未季调数据","Flash覆盖全球，Final仅覆盖美国","Flash是月度调查，Final是季度汇总","Flash是初值，Final是之后的终值"],"answer":3,"explanation":"Flash为初值，Final为之后的终值，需先确认是哪一个。","optionExplanations":["错误：两者区别在发布先后，不在是否季调。","错误：两者覆盖范围相同，区别是初值与终值。","错误：它们都是同一个月度调查的不同发布版本。","正确：Flash为初值，Final为之后的终值，需先确认是哪一个。"],"skills":["初值终值","术语"],"references":[{"title":"标普全球 S&P Global：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.pmi.spglobal.com/Public/Release/PressReleases"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What are Flash and Final in S&P Global PMIs?","optionsEn":["Flash is seasonally adjusted; Final is unadjusted","Flash covers the world; Final covers only the US","Flash is a monthly survey; Final is a quarterly summary","Flash is the preliminary reading; Final is the later final reading"],"explanationEn":"Flash is the preliminary reading and Final the later final reading; check which one you have first.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The difference is release timing, not seasonal adjustment.","Wrong: Both cover the same scope; the difference is preliminary versus final.","Wrong: Both are releases of the same monthly survey.","Correct: Flash is the preliminary reading and Final the later final reading; check which one you have first."]},{"id":"information-advanced-47","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[25],"stem":"市场预期“ISM制造业49.5”，标普制造业PMI公布50.2。能说“超出预期”吗？","options":["不能，预期须对应同一机构的同一指标","能，同为制造业PMI，数值可直接比较","不能，高于50属于扩张而非超预期","能，二者相差不足一点，可视为同口径"],"answer":0,"explanation":"预期要与对应机构的指标比较，不能拿ISM的预期去比标普的实际值。","optionExplanations":["正确：预期要与对应机构的指标比较，不能拿ISM的预期去比标普的实际值。","错误：两家机构的PMI编制方法不同，不能互相对照。","错误：是否超预期要看同一指标的预期，与是否高于50是两回事。","错误：数值接近不等于口径相同。"],"skills":["口径","比较"],"references":[{"title":"标普全球 S&P Global：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.pmi.spglobal.com/Public/Release/PressReleases"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The market expects \"ISM manufacturing 49.5\", and the S&P manufacturing PMI comes in at 50.2. Can you call it \"above expectations\"?","optionsEn":["No; the forecast must match the same body's same indicator","Yes; both are manufacturing PMIs, so the numbers compare directly","No; above 50 is expansion, not a beat","Yes; they differ by less than a point, so they count as the same basis"],"explanationEn":"A forecast must be compared with the matching body's indicator; you cannot compare an ISM forecast with an S&P actual.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: A forecast must be compared with the matching body's indicator; you cannot compare an ISM forecast with an S&P actual.","Wrong: The two bodies compile their PMIs differently, so they cannot be checked against each other.","Wrong: A beat depends on the same indicator's forecast, which is separate from being above 50.","Wrong: Similar numbers do not mean the same basis."]},{"id":"information-beginner-69","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[26],"stem":"标普全球的“Composite Output Index”是什么？","options":["只衡量服务业商业活动的综合指数","合并制造业与服务业产出的综合指数","各国PMI加权后得出的全球汇总指数","仅覆盖制造业产出的分项指数"],"answer":1,"explanation":"综合指数合并制造业与服务业的产出，不能当作服务业。","optionExplanations":["错误：综合指数同时包含制造业，不能当服务业用。","正确：综合指数合并制造业与服务业的产出，不能当作服务业。","错误：它是同一国家制造业与服务业的合并，不是跨国平均。","错误：它还包括服务业，不止制造业。"],"skills":["定义","易混"],"references":[{"title":"标普全球 S&P Global：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.pmi.spglobal.com/Public/Release/PressReleases"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is S&P Global's \"Composite Output Index\"?","optionsEn":["A composite measuring only services business activity","A composite combining manufacturing and services output","A global index weighting together countries' PMIs","A component covering only manufacturing output"],"explanationEn":"The composite combines manufacturing and services output and cannot be treated as services alone.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The composite also includes manufacturing and cannot be used as a services measure.","Correct: The composite combines manufacturing and services output and cannot be treated as services alone.","Wrong: It combines one country's manufacturing and services, not a cross-country average.","Wrong: It also includes services, not just manufacturing."]},{"id":"information-beginner-70","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[26],"stem":"标普服务业商业活动指数为51，低于预期的52。较稳妥的说法是？","options":["已经收缩，因为读数低于市场预期","仍在扩张，只是不及市场预期","仍在扩张，并且好于市场预期","产出较上月下降，因为读数低于52"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高于50表示活动整体增加；低于预期不等于收缩。","optionExplanations":["错误：收缩看是否低于50，而不是是否低于预期。","正确：高于50表示活动整体增加；低于预期不等于收缩。","错误：51低于预期的52，不是好于预期。","错误：52是预期值，不是荣枯线，读数51仍高于50。"],"skills":["读数","预期"],"references":[{"title":"标普全球 S&P Global：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.pmi.spglobal.com/Public/Release/PressReleases"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The S&P services business activity index is 51, below the expected 52. What is the more careful statement?","optionsEn":["It has contracted, because the reading is below expectations","It is still expanding, just short of expectations","It is still expanding and better than expected","Output fell from last month, because the reading is below 52"],"explanationEn":"Above 50 means activity increased overall; missing expectations is not contraction.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Contraction means below 50, not below expectations.","Correct: Above 50 means activity increased overall; missing expectations is not contraction.","Wrong: 51 is below the expected 52, not better.","Wrong: 52 is the forecast, not the 50 dividing line; 51 is still above 50."]},{"id":"information-beginner-71","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[27],"stem":"工业产出（G.17）由哪个机构发布？","options":["ISM","BLS","BEA","美联储"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：在美联储G.17找 Industrial production。","optionExplanations":["ISM发布PMI调查。","BLS发布就业与物价。","BEA发布GDP。","课程：在美联储G.17找 Industrial production。"],"skills":["来源","基础"],"references":[{"title":"美国联邦储备委员会 Federal Reserve：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g17/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which agency publishes industrial production (G.17)?","optionsEn":["ISM","BLS","BEA","The Federal Reserve"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: find Industrial production in the Fed's G.17.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: ISM publishes PMI surveys.","Wrong: BLS publishes jobs and price data.","Wrong: BEA publishes GDP.","Correct: The lesson: find Industrial production in the Fed's G.17."]},{"id":"information-beginner-72","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[27],"stem":"工业产出总指数的三大分项是？","options":["制造业、建筑业、运输业","制造业、采矿业、公用事业","耐用品、非耐用品、公用事业","采矿业、建筑业、公用事业"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：再分 Manufacturing、Mining 和 Utilities。","optionExplanations":["建筑与运输不是工业产出的分项。","正确，三大分项。","耐用品与非耐用品是制造业内部细分。","建筑业不在工业产出内。"],"skills":["结构","分项"],"references":[{"title":"美国联邦储备委员会 Federal Reserve：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g17/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What are the three major components of the total industrial production index?","optionsEn":["Manufacturing, construction, transportation","Manufacturing, mining, utilities","Durable goods, nondurable goods, utilities","Mining, construction, utilities"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: it splits into Manufacturing, Mining and Utilities.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Construction and transportation are not industrial production components.","Correct: These are the three major components.","Wrong: Durable and nondurable goods are subdivisions within manufacturing.","Wrong: Construction is not part of industrial production."]},{"id":"information-beginner-73","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[28],"stem":"产能利用率的含义是？","options":["新订单占当月实际产出的比例","工厂开工天数占全年天数的比例","在岗工人数占工厂编制的比例","实际产出占可持续最大产能之比"],"answer":3,"explanation":"利用率衡量产能被用了多少。","optionExplanations":["错误：订单与产出的比值不是产能利用率。","错误：利用率用产出与产能比较，不数开工天数。","错误：这是人员配置比例，不是产出与产能之比。","正确：利用率衡量产能被用了多少。"],"skills":["定义","基础"],"references":[{"title":"美国联邦储备委员会 Federal Reserve：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g17/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does capacity utilization mean?","optionsEn":["New orders as a share of the month's actual output","Factory operating days as a share of the year","Workers on duty as a share of a factory's headcount","Actual output as a share of sustainable maximum capacity"],"explanationEn":"Utilization measures how much capacity is being used.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: An orders-to-output ratio is not capacity utilization.","Wrong: Utilization compares output with capacity; it does not count operating days.","Wrong: That is a staffing ratio, not output versus capacity.","Correct: Utilization measures how much capacity is being used."]},{"id":"information-beginner-74","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[28],"stem":"产能利用率读数为何要与长期均值比较？","options":["长期均值就是美联储设定的目标水平","长期均值用来把读数换算成同比增速","提供历史参照，判断读数偏高或偏低","长期均值可以剔除季节性因素的影响"],"answer":2,"explanation":"长期均值给读数一个历史参照，帮助判断偏高还是偏低。","optionExplanations":["错误：长期均值不是政策目标，只是历史参照。","错误：均值用于对比水平，不用于换算增速。","正确：长期均值给读数一个历史参照，帮助判断偏高还是偏低。","错误：剔除季节性靠季调处理，不是靠长期均值。"],"skills":["参照","解读"],"references":[{"title":"美国联邦储备委员会 Federal Reserve：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g17/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"Why compare capacity utilization with its long-run average?","optionsEn":["The long-run average is the Fed's target level","The long-run average converts the reading into a yearly growth rate","It gives a historical reference to judge whether the reading is high or low","The long-run average removes seasonal effects"],"explanationEn":"The long-run average gives the reading a historical reference for judging whether it is high or low.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The long-run average is not a policy target, only a historical reference.","Wrong: The average is for comparing levels, not converting to growth.","Correct: The long-run average gives the reading a historical reference for judging whether it is high or low.","Wrong: Seasonal effects are removed by seasonal adjustment, not by a long-run average."]},{"id":"information-beginner-75","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[29],"stem":"耐用品订单的Advance report与之后的完整M3报告是什么关系？","options":["先发Advance初步数据，之后M3会修订","Advance是上月数据，M3是本月数据","Advance仅含运输设备，M3含全部商品","Advance为季调值，M3为未季调值"],"answer":0,"explanation":"初步数据会被后续的完整报告修订。","optionExplanations":["正确：初步数据会被后续的完整报告修订。","错误：两者是同一统计月的初步和完整版本，不是不同月份。","错误：两者统计对象相同，区别在是否为初步数据。","错误：区别是初步与完整，而不是季调与否。"],"skills":["修订","发布节奏"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/manufacturing/m3/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does the durable goods Advance report relate to the later full M3 report?","optionsEn":["The Advance data come first, and M3 revises them later","Advance is last month's data; M3 is this month's","Advance covers only transportation; M3 covers all goods","Advance is seasonally adjusted; M3 is unadjusted"],"explanationEn":"Preliminary data are revised by the later full report.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Preliminary data are revised by the later full report.","Wrong: Both are preliminary and full versions of the same month, not different months.","Wrong: Both cover the same goods; the difference is whether the data are preliminary.","Wrong: The difference is preliminary versus full, not seasonal adjustment."]},{"id":"information-advanced-48","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[29],"stem":"耐用品订单金额增长3%。下面哪项也可能是原因之一？","options":["订单金额按不变价格统计，已剔除物价","出货金额同期也增加了约3%","企业利润同期也增加了约3%","商品价格上涨，即使订购数量没变"],"answer":3,"explanation":"金额上升可能含涨价，数量未必变化。","optionExplanations":["错误：订单金额是名义金额，没有剔除价格。","错误：出货是另一个统计项，不是订单金额增长的原因。","错误：利润不是订单金额的构成部分。","正确：金额上升可能含涨价，数量未必变化。"],"skills":["名义","解读"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/manufacturing/m3/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The value of durable goods orders rose 3%. Which could also be one of the reasons?","optionsEn":["Order values are at constant prices, already net of inflation","Shipment values also rose about 3% over the same period","Corporate profits also rose about 3% over the same period","Goods prices rose, even if quantities ordered did not change"],"explanationEn":"A rise in value can include price increases; quantities need not have changed.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Order values are nominal and not adjusted for prices.","Wrong: Shipments are a separate measure, not a cause of growth in order values.","Wrong: Profits are not part of order values.","Correct: A rise in value can include price increases; quantities need not have changed."]},{"id":"information-beginner-76","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[30],"stem":"“核心资本品订单”通常指哪个系列？","options":["非国防资本品，不含飞机","非国防资本品，含飞机","全部耐用品，不含运输设备","全部资本品，仅不含飞机"],"answer":0,"explanation":"核心资本品订单指Nondefense capital goods excluding aircraft。","optionExplanations":["正确：核心资本品订单指Nondefense capital goods excluding aircraft。","错误：飞机波动大，核心系列特意剔除。","错误：这是剔除运输的耐用品，不是核心资本品。","错误：还应排除国防资本品，不是全部资本品。"],"skills":["定义","查找"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/manufacturing/m3/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which series does \"core capital goods orders\" usually refer to?","optionsEn":["Nondefense capital goods, excluding aircraft","Nondefense capital goods, including aircraft","All durable goods, excluding transportation","All capital goods, excluding only aircraft"],"explanationEn":"Core capital goods orders means Nondefense capital goods excluding aircraft.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Core capital goods orders means Nondefense capital goods excluding aircraft.","Wrong: Aircraft are volatile, so the core series deliberately excludes them.","Wrong: That is durables excluding transportation, not core capital goods.","Wrong: Defense capital goods must also be excluded, not all capital goods kept."]},{"id":"information-advanced-49","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[30],"stem":"估算GDP中当季设备投资，更接近用核心资本品的哪一项？","options":["未完成订单","出货","新订单","库存"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：不要用订单直接替代GDP设备投资所用的出货资料。","optionExplanations":["未完成订单是存量。","课程：不要用订单直接替代GDP设备投资所用的出货资料。","订单偏向未来意向。","库存是另一项目。"],"skills":["用途","区分"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/manufacturing/m3/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"To estimate this quarter's equipment investment in GDP, which core capital goods measure is closer?","optionsEn":["Unfilled orders","Shipments","New orders","Inventories"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: don't substitute orders for the shipment data used for equipment investment in GDP.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Unfilled orders are a stock.","Correct: The lesson: don't substitute orders for the shipment data used for equipment investment in GDP.","Wrong: Orders lean towards future intentions.","Wrong: Inventories are a different item."]},{"id":"information-beginner-77","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[31],"stem":"Census的零售销售报告是否剔除了价格变化？","options":["有，已按CPI折算为实际销售额","只对汽油价格做了剔除，其余仍是名义值","没有，报告给出的是名义金额","有，已按各品类价格指数折成销量"],"answer":2,"explanation":"零售销售报告不直接剔除价格。","optionExplanations":["错误：报告是名义金额，没有按CPI折算。","错误：报告整体没有剔除任何品类的价格。","正确：零售销售报告不直接剔除价格。","错误：报告不提供折算后的销量。"],"skills":["名义","口径"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/retail/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Does the Census retail sales report strip out price changes?","optionsEn":["Yes, converted to real sales using CPI","Only gasoline prices are removed; the rest is nominal","No, the report gives nominal dollar amounts","Yes, converted to volumes using category price indices"],"explanationEn":"The retail sales report does not strip out prices directly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The report is in nominal dollars and is not deflated by CPI.","Wrong: The report does not strip out prices for any category.","Correct: The retail sales report does not strip out prices directly.","Wrong: The report does not provide deflated volumes."]},{"id":"information-beginner-78","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[32],"stem":"零售销售控制组通常剔除哪些类别？","options":["汽车、加油站、食品杂货和餐饮","汽车、加油站、建材和餐饮","汽车、加油站、建材和网购","汽车、加油站、服装和家具"],"answer":1,"explanation":"控制组排除汽车、加油站、建材和餐饮四类。","optionExplanations":["错误：食品杂货留在控制组内，排除的是建材。","正确：控制组排除汽车、加油站、建材和餐饮四类。","错误：网购留在控制组内，排除的是餐饮。","错误：服装和家具留在控制组内。"],"skills":["定义","剔除项"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/retail/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which categories does the retail sales control group usually exclude?","optionsEn":["Autos, gas stations, grocery and food services","Autos, gas stations, building materials and food services","Autos, gas stations, building materials and online shopping","Autos, gas stations, clothing and furniture"],"explanationEn":"The control group excludes four categories: autos, gas stations, building materials and food services.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Grocery stays in the control group; building materials are excluded.","Correct: The control group excludes autos, gas stations, building materials and food services.","Wrong: Online shopping stays in the control group; food services are excluded.","Wrong: Clothing and furniture stay in the control group."]},{"id":"information-advanced-50","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[32],"stem":"零售销售控制组是名义还是实际数据？","options":["名义","按年化折算的实际数","既不是名义也不是实际，是指数","实际"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：控制组不是实际消费，读数是季调名义销售环比。","optionExplanations":["课程：控制组不是实际消费，读数是季调名义销售环比。","不是实际数。","它是金额变化。","未剔除价格。"],"skills":["名义","口径"],"references":[{"title":"美国人口普查局 Census：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.census.gov/retail/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Is the retail sales control group nominal or real data?","optionsEn":["Nominal","Real, on an annualised basis","Neither nominal nor real; it is an index","Real"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the control group is not real consumption; the reading is the seasonally adjusted month-over-month change in nominal sales.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The lesson: the control group is not real consumption; the reading is the seasonally adjusted month-over-month change in nominal sales.","Wrong: It is not a real figure.","Wrong: It is a change in dollar amounts.","Wrong: Prices are not stripped out."]},{"id":"information-beginner-79","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[33],"stem":"Real PCE的链式美元分项，能不能直接相加得到总数？","options":["可以，与名义金额一样逐项相加","通常不能，链式分项加总会有差异","只有商品类分项之间可以直接相加","可以，只需先按价格指数换算后相加"],"answer":1,"explanation":"链式美元分项通常不能简单相加。","optionExplanations":["错误：链式美元不具备名义金额那样的可加性。","正确：链式美元分项通常不能简单相加。","错误：没有某一类可以保证直接相加。","错误：链式美元已经过链式处理，再换算也不能保证加总。"],"skills":["计算","链式美元"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-income"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Can the chained-dollar components of real PCE be added up directly to get the total?","optionsEn":["Yes, item by item, just like nominal amounts","Usually not; adding chained components produces a residual","Only goods components can be added directly","Yes, after first converting them with price indices"],"explanationEn":"Chained-dollar components usually cannot simply be added up.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Chained dollars are not additive the way nominal amounts are.","Correct: Chained-dollar components usually cannot simply be added up.","Wrong: No category is guaranteed to add up directly.","Wrong: Chained dollars have already been chain-weighted, and converting again does not make them add up."]},{"id":"information-beginner-80","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[34],"stem":"个人收入的主要来源分项包括哪些？","options":["工资报酬、转移支付、股票资本利得","工资报酬、企业留存利润、折旧补贴","工资报酬、转移支付、利息股息等","工资报酬、个人所得税、社保缴款"],"answer":2,"explanation":"个人收入由工资报酬、转移支付、利息股息等多项构成。","optionExplanations":["错误：资本利得不计入个人收入。","错误：企业留存利润不属于个人收入。","正确：个人收入由工资报酬、转移支付、利息股息等多项构成。","错误：税和社保缴款是扣减项，不是收入来源。"],"skills":["结构","分项"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-income"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What are the main source components of personal income?","optionsEn":["Compensation, transfer payments, stock capital gains","Compensation, retained corporate profits, depreciation allowances","Compensation, transfer payments, interest and dividends, etc.","Compensation, personal income taxes, social insurance contributions"],"explanationEn":"Personal income is made up of compensation, transfer payments, interest and dividends and other items.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Capital gains are not counted in personal income.","Wrong: Retained corporate profits are not personal income.","Correct: Personal income is made up of compensation, transfer payments, interest and dividends and other items.","Wrong: Taxes and social insurance contributions are deductions, not income sources."]},{"id":"information-beginner-81","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[34],"stem":"名义个人收入增长0.5%，同期价格也上涨0.5%。实际收入大约怎样？","options":["大致持平，实际购买力变化很小","增长约0.5%，因为名义收入增加了","下降约0.5%，因为物价也在上涨","增长约1%，名义增幅加上物价涨幅"],"answer":0,"explanation":"实际收入约等于名义收入减物价变动，约为0。","optionExplanations":["正确：实际收入约等于名义收入减物价变动，约为0。","错误：没有扣除同期物价上涨。","错误：物价涨幅被名义增长抵消，不会出现负增长。","错误：实际收入要扣除物价，而不是相加。"],"skills":["名义与实际","计算"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-income"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Nominal personal income rises 0.5% while prices also rise 0.5%. Roughly what happens to real income?","optionsEn":["About flat; purchasing power barely changes","Up about 0.5%, because nominal income rose","Down about 0.5%, because prices rose too","Up about 1%, nominal growth plus price growth"],"explanationEn":"Real income is roughly nominal income minus the price change, about 0.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Real income is roughly nominal income minus the price change, about 0.","Wrong: This does not subtract the price rise.","Wrong: The price rise is offset by nominal growth, so there is no decline.","Wrong: Real income subtracts prices rather than adding them."]},{"id":"information-beginner-82","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[35],"stem":"可支配个人收入（DPI）如何计算？","options":["个人收入减去个人当期税","个人收入减去个人消费支出","工资收入减去个人当期税","个人收入减去个人储蓄"],"answer":0,"explanation":"DPI=个人收入−个人当期税。","optionExplanations":["正确，DPI=个人收入−个人当期税。","那是剩余的储蓄，不是DPI。","起点是个人收入，不只是工资。","那得到的是消费类支出，不是DPI。"],"skills":["定义","公式"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-income"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How is disposable personal income (DPI) calculated?","optionsEn":["Personal income minus personal current taxes","Personal income minus personal consumption expenditures","Wage income minus personal current taxes","Personal income minus personal saving"],"explanationEn":"DPI = personal income − personal current taxes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: DPI = personal income − personal current taxes.","Wrong: That leaves saving, not DPI.","Wrong: The starting point is personal income, not just wages.","Wrong: That gives spending, not DPI."]},{"id":"information-advanced-51","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[35],"stem":"税前工资没变，但政府减税。DPI会怎样？","options":["不变，因为DPI只看税前工资","下降，因为减税会拉低政府转移支付","无法判断，DPI与税收负担没有关系","上升，因为税后可支配的钱变多"],"answer":3,"explanation":"减税使税后可支配收入增加。","optionExplanations":["错误：DPI是税后收入，税收变化会改变它。","错误：减税并不会自动减少转移支付，DPI应上升。","错误：DPI定义就是扣税后的收入，与税收直接相关。","正确：减税使税后可支配收入增加。"],"skills":["解读","税收"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA：统计发布与数据表","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-income"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Pre-tax wages are unchanged, but the government cuts taxes. What happens to DPI?","optionsEn":["Unchanged, because DPI looks only at pre-tax wages","Falls, because tax cuts reduce government transfers","Cannot tell; DPI is unrelated to the tax burden","Rises, because more after-tax money is available"],"explanationEn":"A tax cut raises after-tax disposable income.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: DPI is after-tax income, so tax changes affect it.","Wrong: Tax cuts do not automatically reduce transfers; DPI should rise.","Wrong: DPI is defined as income after taxes, so it is directly tied to taxes.","Correct: A tax cut raises after-tax disposable income."]},{"id":"information-beginner-83","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[36],"stem":"个人储蓄率的计算方法是？","options":["个人储蓄÷GDP","存款余额÷可支配收入","个人储蓄÷个人收入","个人储蓄÷可支配收入"],"answer":3,"explanation":"储蓄率是本期流量比例，分母是DPI。","optionExplanations":["分母不是GDP。","课程提醒：不是存款余额。","分母应是可支配收入。","储蓄率是本期流量比例，分母是DPI。"],"skills":["定义","公式"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-saving-rate"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How is the personal saving rate calculated?","optionsEn":["Personal saving ÷ GDP","Deposit balances ÷ disposable income","Personal saving ÷ personal income","Personal saving ÷ disposable income"],"explanationEn":"The saving rate is a ratio of current-period flows, with DPI as the denominator.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The denominator is not GDP.","Wrong: As the lesson notes, it is not deposit balances.","Wrong: The denominator should be disposable income.","Correct: The saving rate is a ratio of current-period flows, with DPI as the denominator."]},{"id":"information-beginner-84","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[36],"stem":"储蓄率从4%升到5%，正确的说法是？","options":["上升了1%（相对涨幅）","上升了1个百分点（绝对变化）","上升了5个百分点（期末数值）","上升了20%（相对涨幅）"],"answer":1,"explanation":"4%升到5%是增加1个百分点。","optionExplanations":["错误：相对涨幅其实是25%，1%并不对应。","正确：4%升到5%是增加1个百分点。","错误：5是期末水平，不是变化量。","错误：把分母取成了新值，正确的相对涨幅是25%。"],"skills":["百分点","单位"],"references":[{"title":"美国经济分析局 BEA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.bea.gov/data/income-saving/personal-saving-rate"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The saving rate rises from 4% to 5%. Which statement is correct?","optionsEn":["It rose 1% (relative change)","It rose 1 percentage point (absolute change)","It rose 5 percentage points (the ending value)","It rose 20% (relative change)"],"explanationEn":"Going from 4% to 5% is a rise of 1 percentage point.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The relative increase is actually 25%, not 1%.","Correct: Going from 4% to 5% is a rise of 1 percentage point.","Wrong: 5 is the ending level, not the change.","Wrong: This uses the new value as the base; the correct relative increase is 25%."]},{"id":"information-beginner-85","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[37],"stem":"谘商会消费者信心指数的基期是？","options":["当年1月=100","2000年=100","1985年=100","2010年=50"],"answer":2,"explanation":"该指数以1985年为100。","optionExplanations":["基期固定。","不是2000年。","该指数以1985年为100。","不是50。"],"skills":["基期","单位"],"references":[{"title":"The Conference Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.conference-board.org/topics/consumer-confidence"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the base period of the Conference Board consumer confidence index?","optionsEn":["January of the current year = 100","2000 = 100","1985 = 100","2010 = 50"],"explanationEn":"The index uses 1985 = 100.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The base period is fixed.","Wrong: Not 2000.","Correct: The index uses 1985 = 100.","Wrong: Not 50."]},{"id":"information-advanced-52","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[37],"stem":"谘商会报告中的“劳动力差异”（认为工作好找的比例−认为难找的比例）主要反映什么？","options":["官方统计的失业人数变化","企业未来几个月的招聘计划","每周首次申请失业金的件数","消费者对就业松紧的感受"],"answer":3,"explanation":"劳动力差异来自调查，反映消费者对找工作难易的感受。","optionExplanations":["错误：它是调查感受，不是官方失业统计。","错误：它来自消费者而不是企业。","错误：这是初请失业金，与消费者调查无关。","正确：劳动力差异来自调查，反映消费者对找工作难易的感受。"],"skills":["分项","解读"],"references":[{"title":"The Conference Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.conference-board.org/topics/consumer-confidence"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the Conference Board's \"labor differential\" (share saying jobs are plentiful minus share saying jobs are hard to get) mainly reflect?","optionsEn":["Changes in the official count of unemployed","Firms' hiring plans for the coming months","The number of weekly initial jobless claims","Consumers' sense of how tight the job market is"],"explanationEn":"The labor differential comes from the survey and reflects consumers' sense of how easy it is to find work.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It is a survey perception, not official unemployment data.","Wrong: It comes from consumers, not firms.","Wrong: That is initial claims, unrelated to the consumer survey.","Correct: The labor differential comes from the survey and reflects consumers' sense of how easy it is to find work."]},{"id":"information-beginner-86","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[38],"stem":"密歇根消费者信心指数的单位是什么？","options":["有信心的受访者所占百分比","较上月变动的年化增长率","相对基期的指数点数值","消费者预期的收入变动百分比"],"answer":2,"explanation":"总指数是相对基期的指数点数，通胀预期才是百分比。","optionExplanations":["错误：总指数不是信心人群的占比。","错误：总指数是水平读数，不是年化增速。","正确：总指数是相对基期的指数点数，通胀预期才是百分比。","错误：预期类分项才用百分比，总指数不是。"],"skills":["单位","易混"],"references":[{"title":"University of Michigan Surveys of Consumers official release and methodology","url":"https://www.sca.isr.umich.edu/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is the unit of the Michigan consumer sentiment index?","optionsEn":["The percentage of respondents who are confident","An annualised growth rate from last month","Index points relative to a base period","The percentage change in income consumers expect"],"explanationEn":"The headline index is in index points relative to a base period; only inflation expectations are in percent.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The headline index is not a share of confident people.","Wrong: The headline is a level reading, not an annualised growth rate.","Correct: The headline index is in index points relative to a base period; only inflation expectations are in percent.","Wrong: Only the expectations components use percentages; the headline does not."]},{"id":"information-beginner-87","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[38],"stem":"同一份密歇根报告里，信心指数升4点、通胀预期升0.5，两者怎么比较？","options":["单位不同，不能直接比较大小","4大于0.5，所以信心变化更大","两者相加即为总体变化","按基期折算后，通胀预期变化更大"],"answer":0,"explanation":"指数点与百分点是不同单位。","optionExplanations":["正确：指数点与百分点是不同单位。","错误：单位不同，数字大小不能直接比较。","错误：不同单位的数值不能相加。","错误：报告没有这样的折算比较，两者本身单位不同。"],"skills":["单位","比较"],"references":[{"title":"University of Michigan Surveys of Consumers official release and methodology","url":"https://www.sca.isr.umich.edu/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In the same Michigan report, sentiment rises 4 points and inflation expectations rise 0.5. How should they be compared?","optionsEn":["The units differ, so their sizes cannot be compared directly","4 is bigger than 0.5, so sentiment changed more","Add them to get the overall change","After converting to the base period, inflation expectations changed more"],"explanationEn":"Index points and percentage points are different units.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Index points and percentage points are different units.","Wrong: With different units, the size of the numbers cannot be compared directly.","Wrong: Values in different units cannot be added.","Wrong: The report offers no such conversion; the two simply have different units."]},{"id":"information-beginner-88","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[39],"stem":"美联储G.19消费者信贷报告不包括什么？","options":["信用卡等可循环使用的信贷","汽车贷款等按期分期偿还的贷款","学生贷款等长期分期偿还的贷款","房产担保的贷款，如按揭房贷"],"answer":3,"explanation":"G.19不是房贷总额，不包括不动产担保贷款。","optionExplanations":["错误：信用卡等循环信贷属于G.19。","错误：汽车贷款等非循环信贷属于G.19。","错误：学生贷款属于G.19的非循环信贷。","正确：G.19不是房贷总额，不包括不动产担保贷款。"],"skills":["范围","易混"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g19/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the Fed's G.19 consumer credit report not include?","optionsEn":["Revolving credit such as credit cards","Installment loans such as auto loans","Long-term installment loans such as student loans","Loans secured by real estate, such as mortgages"],"explanationEn":"G.19 is not total mortgage debt; it excludes loans secured by real estate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Revolving credit such as credit cards is part of G.19.","Wrong: Nonrevolving credit such as auto loans is part of G.19.","Wrong: Student loans are part of G.19's nonrevolving credit.","Correct: G.19 is not total mortgage debt; it excludes loans secured by real estate."]},{"id":"information-beginner-89","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[39],"stem":"G.19中“循环信贷”主要指什么？","options":["信用卡等可反复借还的信贷","汽车贷款等分期偿还的信贷","学生贷款等长期偿还的信贷","期限在一年以内、要按期还清的短期贷款"],"answer":0,"explanation":"循环信贷以信用卡为主。","optionExplanations":["正确：循环信贷以信用卡为主。","错误：这是非循环的分期信贷。","错误：学生贷款也属于非循环信贷。","错误：循环信贷看是否可反复借还，不是看期限。"],"skills":["分类","定义"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/g19/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does \"revolving credit\" in G.19 mainly refer to?","optionsEn":["Credit such as credit cards that can be borrowed and repaid repeatedly","Installment credit such as auto loans","Long-term credit such as student loans","Short-term loans under a year that must be paid off on schedule"],"explanationEn":"Revolving credit is mainly credit cards.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Revolving credit is mainly credit cards.","Wrong: That is nonrevolving installment credit.","Wrong: Student loans are also nonrevolving credit.","Wrong: Revolving credit is defined by repeated borrowing and repayment, not by term."]},{"id":"information-beginner-90","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[40],"stem":"逾期率与核销率有什么区别？","options":["逾期衡量已确认损失，核销衡量仍在拖欠","逾期看仍在拖欠，核销看已确认损失","逾期衡量新增贷款，核销衡量提前还款","两者口径相同，只是季调方式不同"],"answer":1,"explanation":"逾期看仍在拖欠的贷款，核销看已确认的损失。","optionExplanations":["错误：把两个概念的含义互换了。","正确：逾期看仍在拖欠的贷款，核销看已确认的损失。","错误：两者都不是衡量新增或提前还款。","错误：它们是不同的列，含义不同。"],"skills":["区分","定义"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board；可辅看 New York Fed official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/chargeoff/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does the delinquency rate differ from the charge-off rate?","optionsEn":["Delinquency measures confirmed losses; charge-offs measure ongoing arrears","Delinquency tracks loans still in arrears; charge-offs track confirmed losses","Delinquency measures new loans; charge-offs measure early repayment","They are the same measure with different seasonal adjustment"],"explanationEn":"Delinquency looks at loans still in arrears; charge-offs look at confirmed losses.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This swaps the two meanings.","Correct: Delinquency looks at loans still in arrears; charge-offs look at confirmed losses.","Wrong: Neither measures new lending or early repayment.","Wrong: They are different columns with different meanings."]},{"id":"information-advanced-53","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[40],"stem":"银行贷款余额大增，逾期贷款金额不变，逾期率下降。较稳妥的理解是？","options":["借款人还款能力明显提高，逾期自然减少","逾期贷款被银行核销后，已不再计入","主要因分母变大，未必代表借款人更健康","银行放宽了逾期天数的认定标准所致"],"answer":2,"explanation":"分母扩大或核销可降低逾期率，但不一定代表借款人恢复健康。","optionExplanations":["错误：逾期金额没变，所以并不是还款能力提高。","错误：题目说逾期金额不变，所以不是核销导致。","正确：分母扩大或核销可降低逾期率，但不一定代表借款人恢复健康。","错误：题目没有提到标准变化，较稳妥的解释是分母变大。"],"skills":["分母效应","解读"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board；可辅看 New York Fed official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/chargeoff/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Bank loan balances jump, delinquent loan amounts are unchanged, and the delinquency rate falls. What is the more careful understanding?","optionsEn":["Borrowers' ability to repay improved clearly, so delinquencies naturally fell","Delinquent loans were charged off and are no longer counted","It is mainly a larger denominator and doesn't necessarily mean healthier borrowers","Banks loosened the number of days past due needed to count as delinquent"],"explanationEn":"A larger denominator or charge-offs can lower the delinquency rate without borrowers necessarily being healthier.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Delinquent amounts did not change, so repayment ability did not improve.","Wrong: The question says delinquent amounts are unchanged, so charge-offs are not the cause.","Correct: A larger denominator or charge-offs can lower the delinquency rate without borrowers necessarily being healthier.","Wrong: No change in standards is mentioned; the more careful explanation is the larger denominator."]},{"id":"information-advanced-54","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[41],"stem":"某月新屋开工突然大增，主要来自一栋大型公寓开工。较稳妥的理解是？","options":["该月住房需求明显走强，可视为趋势转折","独栋住宅开工大幅增加，房屋供给快速增长","大型项目开工说明开发商整体信心明显回升","一栋公寓含多套，月度跳动要看趋势"],"answer":3,"explanation":"公寓一栋含很多套，会使总数跳动。","optionExplanations":["错误：单个大型项目造成的跳动不足以说明趋势。","错误：增幅主要来自公寓，而不是独栋。","错误：单个项目不代表整体开发商信心。","正确：公寓一栋含很多套，会使总数跳动。"],"skills":["波动","解读"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Census Bureau / HUD official release and methodology","url":"https://www.census.gov/construction/nrc/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Housing starts suddenly jump in one month, mainly from one large apartment building breaking ground. What is the more careful understanding?","optionsEn":["Housing demand clearly strengthened that month, so treat it as a trend turn","Single-family starts rose sharply, so housing supply is growing fast","A large project starting shows developers' overall confidence has clearly recovered","One building holds many units, so watch the trend in monthly jumps"],"explanationEn":"One apartment building holds many units, which can make the total jump.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A jump from a single large project is not enough to show a trend.","Wrong: The gain came mainly from apartments, not single-family homes.","Wrong: One project does not represent developers' overall confidence.","Correct: One apartment building holds many units, which can make the total jump."]},{"id":"information-beginner-91","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[42],"stem":"建筑许可数据覆盖哪里？","options":["覆盖全美各县，与开工口径基本一致","只覆盖需许可的地区，与开工口径有别","仅覆盖大城市地区，不含郊区和乡镇","仅统计独栋住宅，不含公寓和联排住宅"],"answer":1,"explanation":"许可数据只覆盖需要许可的地区。","optionExplanations":["错误：许可只覆盖需要许可的地区，口径与开工不完全一致。","正确：许可数据只覆盖需要许可的地区。","错误：覆盖范围看是否需要许可，不按城市规模。","错误：许可数据也包括多户住宅。"],"skills":["覆盖范围","口径"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Census Bureau / HUD official release and methodology","url":"https://www.census.gov/construction/nrc/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Where do building permit data cover?","optionsEn":["Every US county, on basically the same basis as starts","Only areas that require permits, on a different basis from starts","Only big-city areas, excluding suburbs and towns","Only single-family homes, excluding apartments and townhouses"],"explanationEn":"Permit data cover only areas that require permits.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Permits cover only areas that require them, so the basis is not exactly the same as starts.","Correct: Permit data cover only areas that require permits.","Wrong: Coverage depends on whether permits are required, not city size.","Wrong: Permit data also include multifamily housing."]},{"id":"information-beginner-92","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[43],"stem":"成屋销售由哪个机构发布？","options":["联邦住房金融局（FHFA）","美联储（Federal Reserve）","美国人口普查局（Census）","全国房地产经纪人协会（NAR）"],"answer":3,"explanation":"成屋销售由NAR发布。","optionExplanations":["FHFA发布房价指数。","美联储不发布。","Census发布新屋销售。","成屋销售由NAR发布。"],"skills":["来源","基础"],"references":[{"title":"National Association of Realtors NAR official release and methodology","url":"https://www.nar.realtor/research-and-statistics/housing-statistics/existing-home-sales"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Which organisation publishes existing-home sales?","optionsEn":["The Federal Housing Finance Agency (FHFA)","The Federal Reserve","The US Census Bureau","The National Association of Realtors (NAR)"],"explanationEn":"Existing-home sales are published by NAR.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: FHFA publishes a house price index.","Wrong: The Fed does not publish it.","Wrong: Census publishes new-home sales.","Correct: Existing-home sales are published by NAR."]},{"id":"information-advanced-55","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[43],"stem":"成屋销售统计的是哪个时点的交易？","options":["买卖双方签约的时点","购房者提交贷款申请的时点","完成交割过户的时点","房屋挂牌上市的时点"],"answer":2,"explanation":"成屋销售是交割口径，滞后于签约。","optionExplanations":["错误：成屋销售按交割计入，签约时点对应待完成销售。","错误：贷款申请不是计入销售的时点。","正确：成屋销售是交割口径，滞后于签约。","错误：挂牌只是出售的开始，不是成交。"],"skills":["统计时点","区分"],"references":[{"title":"National Association of Realtors NAR official release and methodology","url":"https://www.nar.realtor/research-and-statistics/housing-statistics/existing-home-sales"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"At what point in a transaction are existing-home sales counted?","optionsEn":["When buyer and seller sign the contract","When the buyer applies for a mortgage","When the sale closes and title transfers","When the home is listed for sale"],"explanationEn":"Existing-home sales are counted at closing, which lags the contract signing.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Existing-home sales count at closing; contract signing corresponds to pending sales.","Wrong: The mortgage application is not when a sale is counted.","Correct: Existing-home sales are counted at closing, which lags the contract signing.","Wrong: Listing is only the start of selling, not a completed sale."]},{"id":"information-beginner-93","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[44],"stem":"新屋销售统计的是哪个时点？","options":["买卖双方签订合同时","开发商完成交房过户时","房屋竣工验收完成时","项目破土动工的当月"],"answer":0,"explanation":"新屋销售在签约时计入，签约也可能取消。","optionExplanations":["正确：新屋销售在签约时计入，签约也可能取消。","错误：交割过户是成屋销售的口径。","错误：新屋销售不按竣工时点统计。","错误：动工对应新屋开工，不是销售。"],"skills":["统计时点","区分"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Census Bureau / HUD official release and methodology","url":"https://www.census.gov/construction/nrs/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"At what point are new-home sales counted?","optionsEn":["When buyer and seller sign a contract","When the builder hands over the home and title transfers","When construction is completed and inspected","In the month the project breaks ground"],"explanationEn":"New-home sales are counted at contract signing, and contracts can be cancelled.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: New-home sales are counted at contract signing, and contracts can be cancelled.","Wrong: Closing and title transfer is the basis for existing-home sales.","Wrong: New-home sales are not counted at completion.","Wrong: Breaking ground corresponds to housing starts, not sales."]},{"id":"information-beginner-94","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[44],"stem":"新屋销售主要覆盖哪类住房？","options":["主要是新建的公寓楼单元","主要是已使用过的二手住宅","主要是用于出租的新建住房","主要是新建的独栋住宅"],"answer":3,"explanation":"新屋销售范围主要是新建独栋住宅。","optionExplanations":["错误：范围主要是独栋，公寓不是主体。","错误：二手房对应成屋销售。","错误：新屋销售统计的是出售而非租赁。","正确：新屋销售范围主要是新建独栋住宅。"],"skills":["范围","定义"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Census Bureau / HUD official release and methodology","url":"https://www.census.gov/construction/nrs/index.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What type of housing do new-home sales mainly cover?","optionsEn":["Mainly units in newly built apartment buildings","Mainly previously owned homes","Mainly newly built homes for rent","Mainly newly built single-family homes"],"explanationEn":"New-home sales mainly cover newly built single-family homes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The scope is mainly single-family; apartments are not the core.","Wrong: Previously owned homes correspond to existing-home sales.","Wrong: New-home sales count sales, not rentals.","Correct: New-home sales mainly cover newly built single-family homes."]},{"id":"information-beginner-95","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[45],"stem":"成屋签约销售指数的100代表什么？","options":["2001年的平均签约水平","2010年的平均签约水平","上一个年度的平均签约水平","历史最高月份的签约水平"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：100代表2001年平均水平。","optionExplanations":["正确，100代表2001年平均。","基期是2001年。","基期固定，不随年度滚动。","基期是平均水平，不是历史高点。"],"skills":["基期","单位"],"references":[{"title":"National Association of Realtors NAR official release and methodology","url":"https://www.nar.realtor/research-and-statistics/housing-statistics/pending-home-sales"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does 100 represent in the pending home sales index?","optionsEn":["The average level of contract activity in 2001","The average level of contract activity in 2010","The average level of contract activity in the previous year","The level in the highest month on record"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: 100 represents the 2001 average.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: 100 represents the 2001 average.","Wrong: The base period is 2001.","Wrong: The base period is fixed and does not roll yearly.","Wrong: The base is an average level, not the historical peak."]},{"id":"information-beginner-96","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[45],"stem":"签约销售与之后的成屋销售有什么关系？","options":["签约后当月即体现为成屋销售","签约后基本都会完成交割，不会取消","签约后一两个月才体现为交割","两者统计同一批交易，仅发布月份不同"],"answer":2,"explanation":"签约不等于交割，中间还可能取消。","optionExplanations":["错误：成屋销售按交割计入，通常滞后一两个月。","错误：签约可能因贷款等原因取消，不一定交割。","正确：签约不等于交割，中间还可能取消。","错误：成屋销售滞后于签约，统计时点不同。"],"skills":["时滞","关系"],"references":[{"title":"National Association of Realtors NAR official release and methodology","url":"https://www.nar.realtor/research-and-statistics/housing-statistics/pending-home-sales"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How do pending (contract) sales relate to later existing-home sales?","optionsEn":["A signed contract shows up as an existing-home sale the same month","Nearly all signed contracts close and are never cancelled","Contracts show up as closings one or two months later","They count the same deals; only the release month differs"],"explanationEn":"A signed contract is not a closing, and it can still be cancelled in between.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Existing-home sales count at closing, usually one or two months later.","Wrong: Contracts can be cancelled, for example over financing, and may not close.","Correct: A signed contract is not a closing, and it can still be cancelled in between.","Wrong: Existing-home sales lag contracts, so they are counted at different points."]},{"id":"information-beginner-97","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[46],"stem":"Case-Shiller房价指数采用什么方法？","options":["重复销售：同一房屋前后成交价","对当月全部成交价取中位数计算","用银行评估价格做加权平均计算","对各地区挂牌价格做简单平均"],"answer":0,"explanation":"Case-Shiller采用同一房屋前后成交价的重复销售法。","optionExplanations":["正确：Case-Shiller采用同一房屋前后成交价的重复销售法。","错误：这不是重复销售法，没有跟踪同一房屋。","错误：指数用成交价而不是评估价。","错误：指数不用挂牌价。"],"skills":["方法","定义"],"references":[{"title":"S&P Dow Jones Indices official release and methodology","url":"https://www.spglobal.com/spdji/en/index-family/indicators/sp-cotality-case-shiller/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What method does the Case-Shiller home price index use?","optionsEn":["Repeat sales: the same home's earlier and later sale prices","The median of all sale prices in the month","A weighted average of bank appraisal values","A simple average of listing prices across regions"],"explanationEn":"Case-Shiller uses the repeat-sales method based on the same home's earlier and later sale prices.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Case-Shiller uses the repeat-sales method based on the same home's earlier and later sale prices.","Wrong: This is not repeat sales; it does not track the same home.","Wrong: The index uses sale prices, not appraisals.","Wrong: The index does not use listing prices."]},{"id":"information-beginner-98","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[46],"stem":"Case-Shiller最新发布的数据大约对应哪个时期？","options":["约对应本周内的房价","约对应两个月前的房价","约对应半年前的房价","约对应去年同期的房价"],"answer":1,"explanation":"发布时点落后当前市场约两个月。","optionExplanations":["错误：发布有明显滞后，不是实时数据。","正确：发布时点落后当前市场约两个月。","错误：滞后约两个月，没有那么久。","错误：它是最近的数据，只是略有滞后。"],"skills":["时滞","读数"],"references":[{"title":"S&P Dow Jones Indices official release and methodology","url":"https://www.spglobal.com/spdji/en/index-family/indicators/sp-cotality-case-shiller/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Roughly what period does the latest Case-Shiller release correspond to?","optionsEn":["Prices within the current week","Prices from about two months ago","Prices from about six months ago","Prices from the same period last year"],"explanationEn":"The release lags the current market by about two months.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The release has a clear lag and is not real-time data.","Correct: The release lags the current market by about two months.","Wrong: The lag is about two months, not that long.","Wrong: It is recent data, just with some lag."]},{"id":"information-beginner-99","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[47],"stem":"FHFA房价指数主要基于哪类交易？","options":["房利美、房地美担保或收购的抵押贷款","新建与二手住宅的全部成交，含现金交易","FHA与VA政府担保贷款的住房交易","各大城市高端住宅的挂牌与成交记录"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：样本不含所有住宅。","optionExplanations":["正确，样本不含所有住宅。","样本只覆盖特定贷款交易，不含现金交易。","FHFA指数基于房利美、房地美相关贷款。","它并不专门针对高价房。"],"skills":["样本","定义"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Housing Finance Agency FHFA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.fhfa.gov/fhfa-house-price-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What kind of transactions is the FHFA house price index mainly based on?","optionsEn":["Mortgages guaranteed or purchased by Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac","All new and existing home sales, including cash deals","Home sales with FHA and VA government-backed loans","Listings and sales of high-end homes in major cities"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the sample does not include all homes.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The sample does not include all homes.","Wrong: The sample covers only certain loan transactions and excludes cash deals.","Wrong: The FHFA index is based on Fannie Mae- and Freddie Mac-related loans.","Wrong: It is not specifically about high-priced homes."]},{"id":"information-advanced-56","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[47],"stem":"FHFA有全交易、购房、扩展等口径。比较前应先做什么？","options":["先把几种口径取平均再比较","先确认使用同一口径和频率","优先选用更新最频繁的口径","各口径经季调后可直接混合比较"],"answer":1,"explanation":"比较前应确认使用同一口径和频率。","optionExplanations":["错误：不同口径的平均没有明确含义。","正确：比较前应确认使用同一口径和频率。","错误：口径选择应以可比为准，而非更新频率。","错误：即使季调，不同口径也不应混用。"],"skills":["口径","比较"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Housing Finance Agency FHFA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.fhfa.gov/fhfa-house-price-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"FHFA has all-transactions, purchase-only, expanded-data and other measures. What should you do before comparing?","optionsEn":["Average the measures first, then compare","Confirm you are using the same measure and frequency","Prefer whichever measure updates most often","Once seasonally adjusted, the measures can be mixed freely"],"explanationEn":"Before comparing, confirm you are using the same measure and frequency.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: An average of different measures has no clear meaning.","Correct: Before comparing, confirm you are using the same measure and frequency.","Wrong: Choose the measure for comparability, not update frequency.","Wrong: Even seasonally adjusted, different measures should not be mixed."]},{"id":"information-beginner-100","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[48],"stem":"MBA抵押贷款申请数据多久发布一次？","options":["每周","每天","每季","每月"],"answer":0,"explanation":"MBA为周度数据（通常周三）。","optionExplanations":["MBA为周度数据（通常周三）。","不是每天。","不是季度。","不是月度。"],"skills":["频率","基础"],"references":[{"title":"Mortgage Bankers Association MBA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.mba.org/news-and-research/research-and-economics/single-family-research/weekly-applications-survey"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How often is MBA mortgage application data published?","optionsEn":["Weekly","Daily","Quarterly","Monthly"],"explanationEn":"MBA data are weekly (usually Wednesday).","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: MBA data are weekly (usually Wednesday).","Wrong: Not daily.","Wrong: Not quarterly.","Wrong: Not monthly."]},{"id":"information-beginner-101","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[48],"stem":"MBA的贷款“申请”与“放款”是什么关系？","options":["申请量等同于当周放款量","放款先发生，之后才有申请","申请只统计已获批准的贷款","申请是意向，不等于放款"],"answer":3,"explanation":"申请不等于放款。","optionExplanations":["错误：申请不会全部放款。","错误：先申请后放款。","错误：申请是提交的意向，不是已批准的。","正确：申请不等于放款。"],"skills":["定义","区分"],"references":[{"title":"Mortgage Bankers Association MBA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.mba.org/news-and-research/research-and-economics/single-family-research/weekly-applications-survey"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How do MBA loan \"applications\" relate to loan \"originations\"?","optionsEn":["Applications equal that week's originations","Originations happen first, then applications","Applications count only approved loans","Applications are intentions, not originations"],"explanationEn":"Applications are not originations.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Not every application becomes a loan.","Wrong: Applications come first, then originations.","Wrong: Applications are submitted intentions, not approvals.","Correct: Applications are not originations."]},{"id":"information-beginner-102","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[49],"stem":"Freddie Mac的PMMS利率多久发布一次？","options":["每周一次，通常在周四公布","每月一次，通常在月初公布","每日更新，随利率实时变动","每季一次，通常在季末公布"],"answer":0,"explanation":"PMMS为周度调查，通常周四公布。","optionExplanations":["正确：PMMS为周度调查，通常周四公布。","错误：PMMS不是月度数据。","错误：PMMS不是每日更新。","错误：PMMS远比季度频繁。"],"skills":["频率","基础"],"references":[{"title":"Freddie Mac official release and methodology","url":"https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How often is Freddie Mac's PMMS rate published?","optionsEn":["Weekly, usually on Thursday","Monthly, usually early in the month","Daily, moving with rates in real time","Quarterly, usually at quarter-end"],"explanationEn":"PMMS is a weekly survey, usually released on Thursday.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: PMMS is a weekly survey, usually released on Thursday.","Wrong: PMMS is not monthly data.","Wrong: PMMS is not updated daily.","Wrong: PMMS is far more frequent than quarterly."]},{"id":"information-beginner-103","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[49],"stem":"PMMS显示30年期利率6.5%，你实际拿到的报价为什么可能不同？","options":["PMMS是上季度的平均利率，已经过时","各州法律规定的上限利率各不相同","你的信用、首付与费用条件不同","PMMS是对未来利率的预测，会再调整"],"answer":2,"explanation":"你的信用、首付、费用会让实际报价不同。","optionExplanations":["错误：PMMS每周更新，并非上季度数据。","错误：房贷利率并非由各州上限直接决定。","正确：你的信用、首付、费用会让实际报价不同。","错误：PMMS是调查结果而不是预测。"],"skills":["解读","个体差异"],"references":[{"title":"Freddie Mac official release and methodology","url":"https://www.freddiemac.com/pmms"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"PMMS shows a 30-year rate of 6.5%. Why might the quote you actually get differ?","optionsEn":["PMMS is last quarter's average rate, so it is out of date","Each state's legal rate cap is different","Your credit, down payment and fees differ","PMMS is a forecast of future rates and will be adjusted"],"explanationEn":"Your credit, down payment and fees can make your actual quote different.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: PMMS updates weekly; it is not last quarter's data.","Wrong: Mortgage rates are not set directly by state caps.","Correct: Your credit, down payment and fees can make your actual quote different.","Wrong: PMMS is a survey result, not a forecast."]},{"id":"information-beginner-104","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[50],"stem":"NAHB住房市场指数超过50意味着什么？","options":["新房销量较上期增加，销售进入扩张区间","受访建筑商中偏正面的回答多于偏负面的","新屋开工量较上期上升，建设进入扩张区间","独栋住宅价格较上期上涨，进入升值区间"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：超过50意味着偏正面回答多于负面。","optionExplanations":["它测的是建筑商心态，不是已卖出的销量。","正确，超过50表示偏正面回答占多数。","它是情绪调查，不是开工数量。","50不是房价涨跌分界。"],"skills":["读数","扩散指数"],"references":[{"title":"National Association of Home Builders NAHB official release and methodology","url":"https://www.nahb.org/news-and-economics/housing-economics/indices/housing-market-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does an NAHB Housing Market Index above 50 mean?","optionsEn":["New-home sales rose from the prior period and are in expansion","More surveyed builders gave positive than negative answers","Housing starts rose from the prior period and construction is expanding","Single-family prices rose from the prior period and are appreciating"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: above 50 means more positive answers than negative ones.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: It measures builder sentiment, not homes already sold.","Correct: Above 50 means positive answers are in the majority.","Wrong: It is a sentiment survey, not a count of starts.","Wrong: 50 is not a dividing line for price changes."]},{"id":"information-advanced-57","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[50],"stem":"NAHB指数能否当作新屋开工总量来用？","options":["不能，它只统计多户公寓，不含独栋住宅","不能，它是建筑商情绪调查，不是开工数量","能，两者都衡量建设，季节调整后数值相同","能，指数点数乘以固定倍数即得开工套数"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：不能把它当成开工总量。","optionExplanations":["结论对但理由错，该指数调查的正是独栋住宅建筑商。","正确，课程提醒不能把它当作开工总量。","调查指数与开工数量是不同类型的数据，数值不会相同。","指数没有固定倍数可换算成套数。"],"skills":["区分","易混"],"references":[{"title":"National Association of Home Builders NAHB official release and methodology","url":"https://www.nahb.org/news-and-economics/housing-economics/indices/housing-market-index"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Can the NAHB index be used as total housing starts?","optionsEn":["No; it counts only multifamily apartments, not single-family homes","No; it is a builder sentiment survey, not a count of starts","Yes; both measure construction and match after seasonal adjustment","Yes; index points times a fixed multiple give the number of starts"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, it cannot be used as total starts.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Right conclusion, wrong reason: the index surveys single-family builders.","Correct: As the lesson notes, it cannot be used as total starts.","Wrong: A survey index and a count of starts are different kinds of data and will not match.","Wrong: There is no fixed multiple to convert the index into a number of homes."]},{"id":"information-beginner-105","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[51],"stem":"H.4.1表头写“百万美元”，某项为7,000,000，表示多少？","options":["700万美元","7000亿美元","70亿美元","7万亿美元"],"answer":3,"explanation":"7,000,000百万=7万亿。课程：1,000,000百万美元才是1万亿美元。","optionExplanations":["把单位当成美元。","少了一个数量级。","少了三个数量级。","7,000,000百万=7万亿。课程：1,000,000百万美元才是1万亿美元。"],"skills":["单位","换算"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h41/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"An H.4.1 table header says \"millions of dollars\", and one item reads 7,000,000. How much is that?","optionsEn":["$7 million","$700 billion","$7 billion","$7 trillion"],"explanationEn":"7,000,000 million = 7 trillion. The lesson: 1,000,000 million dollars is 1 trillion dollars.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This treats the unit as dollars.","Wrong: This is short by one order of magnitude.","Wrong: This is short by three orders of magnitude.","Correct: 7,000,000 million = 7 trillion. The lesson: 1,000,000 million dollars is 1 trillion dollars."]},{"id":"information-advanced-58","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[51],"stem":"H.4.1里“周三时点数”与“周均值”是什么关系？","options":["周均值是周三当天的数，时点数是整周平均","时点数是周均值的移动平均，两者可混用","口径不同，比较时应固定使用同一种口径","两者只在季节调整上不同，数值可互换"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：周三时点数与周均值不同。","optionExplanations":["把两个概念说反了，时点数才是周三当天的数。","时点数不是周均值的平滑，混用会造成误读。","正确，周三时点数与周均值口径不同。","两者的差别在统计时点而非季节调整。"],"skills":["口径","读表"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h41/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How do the \"Wednesday level\" and the \"week average\" in H.4.1 relate?","optionsEn":["The week average is Wednesday's figure; the level is the weekly average","The level is a moving average of the week average, so they can be mixed","They are different measures; stick to one when comparing","They differ only in seasonal adjustment, so the values are interchangeable"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the Wednesday level and the week average are different.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This swaps the two; the level is Wednesday's figure.","Wrong: The level is not a smoothed week average, and mixing them misleads.","Correct: The Wednesday level and the week average are different measures.","Wrong: The difference is the point in time measured, not seasonal adjustment."]},{"id":"information-beginner-106","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[52],"stem":"居民在商业银行的存款，与银行存放在美联储的准备金，是什么关系？","options":["准备金是存款扣掉贷款后的余额，可相加","属于不同主体的账目，两者不能直接相加","存款是资产、准备金是负债，相加得总资金","准备金是居民存款在央行的备份，数额应一致"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：别把居民银行存款与银行在央行的准备金相加。","optionExplanations":["准备金并非存款的剩余部分，相加会重复计算。","正确，居民存款与银行准备金不能相加。","存款是银行负债，准备金是银行资产，且不能相加。","准备金不是存款备份，两者数额并不一致。"],"skills":["区分","账目"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h41/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"How do households' deposits at commercial banks relate to the reserves banks hold at the Fed?","optionsEn":["Reserves are deposits minus loans, so they can be added","They are accounts of different parties and cannot simply be added","Deposits are assets and reserves are liabilities; together they give total funds","Reserves are a central-bank copy of household deposits and should match"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, don't add household bank deposits to banks' reserves at the central bank.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Reserves are not what is left of deposits, and adding them double-counts.","Correct: Household deposits and bank reserves cannot be added.","Wrong: Deposits are bank liabilities and reserves are bank assets, and they cannot be added.","Wrong: Reserves are not a copy of deposits, and the amounts do not match."]},{"id":"information-beginner-107","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[53],"stem":"ON RRP利率与SOFR是什么关系？","options":["前者是市场成交利率，后者是美联储提供的工具利率","两者都是美联储设定的政策利率，适用对象不同","前者是美联储提供的工具利率，后者是市场成交利率","前者是隔夜利率，后者是期限一个月的利率"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：别与SOFR成交利率混淆。","optionExplanations":["说反了，SOFR才是市场成交利率。","SOFR由市场交易形成，并非美联储设定。","正确，ON RRP利率是工具利率，SOFR是成交利率。","SOFR本身也是隔夜利率，并非一个月期。"],"skills":["区分","利率"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Bank of New York official release and methodology","url":"https://www.newyorkfed.org/markets/desk-operations/reverse-repo"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does the ON RRP rate relate to SOFR?","optionsEn":["The first is a market transaction rate; the second is a Fed facility rate","Both are Fed-set policy rates for different counterparties","The first is a Fed facility rate; the second is a market transaction rate","The first is overnight; the second is a one-month rate"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: don't confuse it with SOFR, a transaction rate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This is reversed; SOFR is the market transaction rate.","Wrong: SOFR is formed by market trades, not set by the Fed.","Correct: The ON RRP rate is a facility rate and SOFR a transaction rate.","Wrong: SOFR is also an overnight rate, not one-month."]},{"id":"information-advanced-59","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[53],"stem":"ON RRP余额下降。下面哪项最稳妥？","options":["说明美联储在收紧流动性，通常偏利空风险资产","说明货币基金资金进入市场，通常利好风险资产","先查资金流向（如转入国债或存款），再下结论","说明美联储调低了政策利率，通常偏利多风险资产"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：下降不是机械利好，上升不是机械利空；先分清交易对手与现金去向。","optionExplanations":["余额下降不等于收紧，资金可能只是转向其他资产。","资金可能流向国债等，并不必然进入风险资产。","正确，下降不是机械利好，要先分清资金去向。","余额变化不代表利率调整。"],"skills":["解读","资金去向"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Bank of New York official release and methodology","url":"https://www.newyorkfed.org/markets/desk-operations/reverse-repo"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"The ON RRP balance falls. Which is the most careful statement?","optionsEn":["The Fed is tightening liquidity, usually bearish for risk assets","Money-fund cash is entering markets, usually bullish for risk assets","Check where the money went (e.g. into Treasuries or deposits) before concluding","The Fed cut its policy rate, usually bullish for risk assets"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, a fall is not mechanically bullish and a rise not mechanically bearish; first identify the counterparties and where the cash went.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A falling balance is not tightening; the money may simply have moved into other assets.","Wrong: The money may have gone into Treasuries and does not necessarily enter risk assets.","Correct: A fall is not mechanically bullish; first identify where the money went.","Wrong: A change in the balance does not mean a rate change."]},{"id":"information-advanced-60","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[54],"stem":"其他项目不变，财政部在美联储的TGA余额上升。银行准备金会怎样？","options":["上升","下降","不变","翻倍"],"answer":1,"explanation":"资金从银行体系流入TGA，准备金相应减少。","optionExplanations":["方向错误。","资金从银行体系流入TGA，准备金相应减少。","TGA变化会影响准备金。","没有这种关系。"],"skills":["资产负债表","关系"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Treasury / Federal Reserve official release and methodology","url":"https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/daily-treasury-statement/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"With everything else unchanged, the Treasury's TGA balance at the Fed rises. What happens to bank reserves?","optionsEn":["They rise","They fall","They are unchanged","They double"],"explanationEn":"Money flows from the banking system into the TGA, so reserves fall correspondingly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Wrong direction.","Correct: Money flows from the banking system into the TGA, so reserves fall correspondingly.","Wrong: Changes in the TGA do affect reserves.","Wrong: There is no such relationship."]},{"id":"information-beginner-108","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[55],"stem":"M2除了M1之外，还包括什么？","options":["小额定期存款和零售货币市场基金","大额定期存单和机构货币市场基金","银行在美联储的准备金和库存现金","政府持有的国债和外汇储备"],"answer":0,"explanation":"M2=M1+小额定期存款+零售货币市场基金等。","optionExplanations":["正确，M2=M1+小额定期存款+零售货币基金。","这类更大口径的资产不属于M2的新增部分。","准备金属于基础货币范畴，不是M2的组成。","政府资产不计入M2。"],"skills":["定义","构成"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h6/current/default.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Besides M1, what else does M2 include?","optionsEn":["Small time deposits and retail money market funds","Large CDs and institutional money market funds","Banks' reserves at the Fed and vault cash","Government-held Treasuries and foreign exchange reserves"],"explanationEn":"M2 = M1 + small time deposits + retail money market funds and so on.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: M2 = M1 + small time deposits + retail money funds.","Wrong: These broader assets are not the extra part of M2.","Wrong: Reserves belong to the monetary base, not M2.","Wrong: Government assets are not counted in M2."]},{"id":"information-beginner-109","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[55],"stem":"名义M2同比增长5%，同期物价上涨4%。实际购买力大约增长多少？","options":["约9%","约5%","约−1%","约1%"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：名义M2增长若物价也涨，实际购买力未必同幅增加。","optionExplanations":["把增速与物价相加了，应相减。","忽略了物价上涨，名义值不等于实际值。","相减时用反了方向，应是名义减物价。","正确，约5%−4%≈1%。"],"skills":["名义与实际","计算"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h6/current/default.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Nominal M2 grows 5% year over year while prices rise 4%. Roughly how much does real purchasing power grow?","optionsEn":["About 9%","About 5%","About −1%","About 1%"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: if prices also rise, real purchasing power does not grow as much as nominal M2.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This adds growth and inflation; they should be subtracted.","Wrong: This ignores the price rise; nominal is not real.","Wrong: This subtracts in the wrong direction; it should be nominal minus prices.","Correct: About 5% − 4% ≈ 1%."]},{"id":"information-beginner-110","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[56],"stem":"H.8存款数据分季调与未季调。比较时应注意什么？","options":["应固定使用同一口径，不要混用季调与未季调","未季调值已经平滑了季节波动，更适合看环比","季调值只在年底修订发布，平时只看未季调","两者可以混用，前提是时间跨度保持一致"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：季调和未季调分开。","optionExplanations":["正确，两种口径不能混用。","未季调数据才保留季节性，并未剔除。","季调数据平时就会发布，并非只在年底。","时间跨度一致也不能抵消口径差异。"],"skills":["口径","季调"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"H.8 deposit data come seasonally adjusted and unadjusted. What should you watch when comparing?","optionsEn":["Stick to one basis; don't mix adjusted and unadjusted","Unadjusted values already smooth seasonal swings, so they suit month-to-month views","Adjusted values are published only at year-end; otherwise use unadjusted","They can be mixed as long as the time span is the same"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: keep seasonally adjusted and unadjusted separate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The two bases must not be mixed.","Wrong: Unadjusted data keep seasonality; they do not remove it.","Wrong: Adjusted data are published regularly, not only at year-end.","Wrong: A matching time span does not cancel out the difference in basis."]},{"id":"information-advanced-61","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[56],"stem":"某周银行存款大幅下降，恰逢季度缴税日。较稳妥的理解是？","options":["说明储户转向货币基金，趋势已经确立","反映银行主动压缩负债，是政策收紧信号","多与缴税季节因素有关，需看后续几周","多半是统计误差，下周会自动修正回去"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：税款支付、季末与重分类会扰动周数，别拿一周判断挤兑。","optionExplanations":["一周变动不足以确立趋势，且缴税是更直接的原因。","缴税日的波动不是银行的主动收缩。","正确，一周数据不足以判断挤兑。","这是真实的资金流动，不是统计误差。"],"skills":["季节扰动","解读"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"Bank deposits fall sharply in a week that coincides with a quarterly tax date. What is the more careful understanding?","optionsEn":["Savers are moving to money funds, and the trend is established","Banks are actively shrinking liabilities, a sign of policy tightening","It is likely tied to the tax-season effect; watch the next few weeks","It is probably a statistical error that will correct itself next week"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, tax payments, quarter-end and reclassifications disturb weekly figures, so don't diagnose a bank run from one week.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: One week is not enough to establish a trend, and taxes are the more direct cause.","Wrong: Tax-date swings are not banks actively shrinking.","Correct: One week of data is not enough to diagnose a run.","Wrong: This is a real flow of funds, not a statistical error."]},{"id":"information-beginner-111","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[57],"stem":"H.8的商业银行贷款主要分哪几类？","options":["工商贷款、房地产贷款、消费贷款等","按期限分为短期、中期、长期贷款","按借款地区分为本州、跨州、海外贷款","按担保方式分为抵押、信用、担保贷款"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：分工商、房地产与消费贷款。","optionExplanations":["正确，H.8按用途分工商、房地产与消费贷款。","H.8的主要分类不按期限划分。","H.8不按借款地区分类。","H.8不按担保方式作主要分类。"],"skills":["分类","结构"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What are the main categories of commercial bank loans in H.8?","optionsEn":["C&I loans, real estate loans, consumer loans and more","Short-, medium- and long-term loans by maturity","In-state, out-of-state and overseas loans by borrower region","Secured, unsecured and guaranteed loans by collateral"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: they split into C&I, real estate and consumer loans.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: H.8 groups loans by use into C&I, real estate and consumer loans.","Wrong: H.8's main categories are not by maturity.","Wrong: H.8 does not classify by borrower region.","Wrong: H.8's main categories are not by collateral type."]},{"id":"information-advanced-62","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[57],"stem":"工商贷款余额突然上升。下面哪种情况会让余额上升，却不代表企业有新增投资？","options":["企业把部分银行贷款转为发行债券","企业提前偿还了一部分到期贷款","企业提取已有的循环额度","银行核销了一批无法收回的坏账"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：余额增加不一定代表新增投资；必须检查循环额度提款和资产转移。","optionExplanations":["改用债券融资会让银行贷款余额下降，而不是上升。","提前还款会让余额下降。","课程提醒：余额增加不一定代表新增投资；必须检查循环额度提款和资产转移。","核销坏账会让账面余额下降。"],"skills":["解读","提款"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"C&I loan balances suddenly rise. Which situation would raise balances without meaning new business investment?","optionsEn":["Firms replacing some bank loans with bond issuance","Firms repaying some maturing loans early","Firms drawing on existing revolving credit lines","Banks charging off a batch of uncollectible loans"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, a rising balance does not necessarily mean new investment; check revolving-line drawdowns and asset transfers.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Switching to bond financing lowers bank loan balances rather than raising them.","Wrong: Early repayment lowers balances.","Correct: As the lesson notes, a rising balance does not necessarily mean new investment; check revolving-line drawdowns and asset transfers.","Wrong: Charging off bad loans lowers book balances."]},{"id":"information-beginner-112","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[58],"stem":"SLOOS（高级信贷员调查）通常多久进行一次？","options":["通常每月一次","通常每季度一次","通常每半年一次","通常每年一次"],"answer":1,"explanation":"SLOOS通常按季度进行。","optionExplanations":["月度是多数经济数据的频率，SLOOS不是。","正确，SLOOS通常按季度进行。","半年一次的频率偏低，实际是每季度。","年度频率偏低，实际是每季度。"],"skills":["频率","基础"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/data/sloos.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How often is the SLOOS (Senior Loan Officer Opinion Survey) usually conducted?","optionsEn":["Usually monthly","Usually quarterly","Usually every six months","Usually annually"],"explanationEn":"SLOOS is usually conducted quarterly.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Monthly is the frequency of most economic data, but not SLOOS.","Correct: SLOOS is usually conducted quarterly.","Wrong: Every six months is too infrequent; it is actually quarterly.","Wrong: Annual is too infrequent; it is actually quarterly."]},{"id":"information-advanced-63","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[58],"stem":"SLOOS中关于“贷款需求”的问题，净比例为正表示什么？","options":["报告需求增强的银行多于报告减弱的","报告收紧标准的银行多于报告放松的","银行贷款余额较上季增长了该比例","报告利差扩大的银行多于报告缩小的"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：正负号先看问题问的是收紧还是需求增强。","optionExplanations":["正确，需求问题的净比例为正表示增强者多。","这是贷款标准问题的含义，不是需求问题。","净比例是回答者占比之差，不是贷款量增速。","这是另一类问题，与需求净比例无关。"],"skills":["读数","问题类型"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/data/sloos.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In SLOOS questions about loan demand, what does a positive net percentage mean?","optionsEn":["More banks reported stronger demand than weaker demand","More banks reported tightening standards than easing","Bank loan balances grew by that percentage from last quarter","More banks reported wider spreads than narrower ones"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: before reading the sign, check whether the question asks about tightening or stronger demand.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: For demand questions, a positive net percentage means more banks saw stronger demand.","Wrong: That is the meaning for lending-standards questions, not demand questions.","Wrong: The net percentage is a difference in respondent shares, not loan growth.","Wrong: That is a different type of question, unrelated to the demand net percentage."]},{"id":"information-beginner-113","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[59],"stem":"SOFR是哪种利率？","options":["以美国国债为抵押的隔夜回购利率","银行间无抵押隔夜拆借的联邦基金利率","美联储向银行提供贴现贷款的收费利率","银行向企业放贷的三个月期基准利率"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：SOFR不是无抵押联邦基金利率。","optionExplanations":["正确，SOFR是国债抵押隔夜回购利率。","那是联邦基金利率，不是SOFR。","那是贴现利率，不是SOFR。","SOFR是隔夜利率，不是三个月期贷款基准。"],"skills":["定义","易混"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Bank of New York official release and methodology","url":"https://www.newyorkfed.org/markets/reference-rates/sofr"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What kind of rate is SOFR?","optionsEn":["An overnight repo rate collateralised by Treasuries","The fed funds rate for unsecured overnight interbank lending","The rate the Fed charges banks for discount loans","A three-month benchmark rate for bank lending to firms"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: SOFR is not the unsecured fed funds rate.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: SOFR is an overnight repo rate collateralised by Treasuries.","Wrong: That is the fed funds rate, not SOFR.","Wrong: That is the discount rate, not SOFR.","Wrong: SOFR is an overnight rate, not a three-month lending benchmark."]},{"id":"information-beginner-114","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[59],"stem":"SOFR为4.30%，这个数字的含义是？","options":["隔夜利率，借一晚需支付4.30%的利息","月度利率，借一个月约需付4.30%","年化利率，借一晚约付4.30%/360","年化利率，借一晚约付4.30%/12"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：利率是年化百分比，5%不是借一晚上收5%。","optionExplanations":["把年化数字当成一晚的利息，高估了成本。","SOFR是年化的隔夜利率，不是月度利率。","正确，年化利率要折算到一晚。","除以12是折算为月度，分母用错。"],"skills":["年化","单位"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Bank of New York official release and methodology","url":"https://www.newyorkfed.org/markets/reference-rates/sofr"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"SOFR is 4.30%. What does this number mean?","optionsEn":["An overnight rate: borrowing for one night costs 4.30% interest","A monthly rate: borrowing for a month costs about 4.30%","An annualised rate: one night costs about 4.30%/360","An annualised rate: one night costs about 4.30%/12"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: rates are annualised percentages; 5% does not mean paying 5% for one night.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This treats the annual figure as one night's interest, overstating the cost.","Wrong: SOFR is an annualised overnight rate, not a monthly rate.","Correct: An annualised rate must be scaled down to one night.","Wrong: Dividing by 12 converts to a monthly figure; the denominator is wrong."]},{"id":"information-beginner-115","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[60],"stem":"贴现窗口一级信贷（Primary credit）主要面向谁？","options":["资本不足、需要救助的存款机构","需要短期周转的大型非银行企业","持有美元业务的外国商业银行","财务状况健全的存款类机构"],"answer":3,"explanation":"一级信贷提供给财务状况健全的存款机构。","optionExplanations":["那更接近二级信贷的对象。","贴现窗口面向存款机构，不是企业。","一级信贷的对象不是外国银行。","正确，一级信贷面向健全的存款机构。"],"skills":["定义","对象"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h41/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Who is discount-window primary credit mainly for?","optionsEn":["Undercapitalised depository institutions needing a rescue","Large non-bank companies needing short-term funding","Foreign commercial banks with dollar operations","Depository institutions in sound financial condition"],"explanationEn":"Primary credit is provided to depository institutions in sound financial condition.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: That is closer to who secondary credit is for.","Wrong: The discount window serves depository institutions, not companies.","Wrong: Primary credit is not aimed at foreign banks.","Correct: Primary credit serves sound depository institutions."]},{"id":"information-advanced-64","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[60],"stem":"贴现窗口借款余额增加，能说明银行资本不足吗？","options":["能，借款说明银行资产已经低于其负债","不能，借款只反映流动性，不等于资本缺口","能，借款越多就说明资本充足率越低","不能，借款只算央行资产，与银行财务无关"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：借款余额不是银行资本缺口；流动性与偿付能力不同。","optionExplanations":["借款只说明需要流动性，不说明资不抵债。","正确，流动性与偿付能力是两回事。","借款与资本充足率没有这种直接对应。","理由错，借款确实体现在银行的资产负债表上。"],"skills":["区分","解读"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h41/current/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"Discount-window borrowing rises. Does that show banks are undercapitalised?","optionsEn":["Yes; borrowing shows banks' assets have fallen below their liabilities","No; borrowing reflects liquidity needs, not a capital shortfall","Yes; the more borrowing, the lower the capital ratio","No; borrowing counts only as a Fed asset and has nothing to do with bank finances"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, borrowing balances are not a capital shortfall; liquidity and solvency are different.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Borrowing only shows a need for liquidity, not insolvency.","Correct: Liquidity and solvency are two different things.","Wrong: There is no such direct link between borrowing and capital ratios.","Wrong: Wrong reason: the borrowing does appear on banks' balance sheets."]},{"id":"information-beginner-116","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[61],"stem":"美国国债拍卖结果里的“尾差（tail）”通常指什么？","options":["中标收益率低于发行前交易收益率的基点数","投标倍数较前几次拍卖平均的差额","一级交易商获配比例较近期平均的差额","中标收益率高出发行前收益率的基点数"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：尾差常用基点表示。","optionExplanations":["方向说反了，尾差是中标收益率偏高的部分。","那是投标倍数的变化，不是尾差。","那是交易商承接比例的变化，不是尾差。","正确，尾差常用基点表示。"],"skills":["术语","读表"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Treasury / TreasuryDirect official release and methodology","url":"https://www.treasurydirect.gov/auctions/announcements-data-results/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the \"tail\" in a US Treasury auction result usually mean?","optionsEn":["How many basis points the stop-out yield came in below the pre-auction yield","The gap between the bid-to-cover ratio and its recent average","The gap between primary dealers' allotment and its recent average","How many basis points the stop-out yield came in above the pre-auction yield"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the tail is usually expressed in basis points.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: This is reversed; the tail is how much higher the stop-out yield came in.","Wrong: That is a change in the bid-to-cover ratio, not the tail.","Wrong: That is a change in dealer takedown, not the tail.","Correct: The tail is usually expressed in basis points."]},{"id":"information-advanced-65","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[61],"stem":"美国国债拍卖的“高收益率（high yield）”有什么含义？","options":["最高中标收益率，中标者都按此获配","最低中标收益率，中标者按各自报价获配","拍卖当日二级市场的最终收盘收益率","最高投标收益率，包含未中标的报价"],"answer":0,"explanation":"美国国债采用单一价格拍卖，所有中标者都按高收益率获配。","optionExplanations":["正确，美债采用单一价格拍卖。","说反了，且美债不是按各自报价获配。","高收益率是拍卖结果，不是二级市场收盘价。","高收益率只看中标的报价，不含未中标的。"],"skills":["机制","定义"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Treasury / TreasuryDirect official release and methodology","url":"https://www.treasurydirect.gov/auctions/announcements-data-results/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the \"high yield\" in a US Treasury auction mean?","optionsEn":["The highest accepted yield, at which all winning bidders are awarded","The lowest accepted yield, with winners awarded at their own bids","The final closing yield in the secondary market on auction day","The highest bid yield, including bids that were not accepted"],"explanationEn":"US Treasuries use single-price auctions, so all winning bidders are awarded at the high yield.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: Treasuries use single-price auctions.","Wrong: This is reversed, and Treasuries are not awarded at each bidder's own price.","Wrong: The high yield is an auction result, not a secondary-market close.","Wrong: The high yield counts only accepted bids, not rejected ones."]},{"id":"information-beginner-117","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[62],"stem":"国债“发行总额”与“净借款”是什么关系？","options":["净借款=发行总额+到期本金","净借款=发行总额−偿还的到期本金","净借款=发行总额−财政赤字","净借款=财政赤字，与发行总额无关"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程：净借款不等于发行，也不等于赤字。","optionExplanations":["加号用错，到期本金应当扣除。","正确，净借款是扣除到期偿还后的新增。","净借款不是用赤字去减发行总额。","净借款既不等于赤字，也与发行额有关。"],"skills":["定义","计算"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Department of the Treasury official release and methodology","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/policy-issues/financing-the-government/quarterly-refunding"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How do gross Treasury issuance and net borrowing relate?","optionsEn":["Net borrowing = gross issuance + maturing principal","Net borrowing = gross issuance − maturing principal repaid","Net borrowing = gross issuance − budget deficit","Net borrowing = budget deficit, unrelated to gross issuance"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: net borrowing equals neither issuance nor the deficit.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The plus sign is wrong; maturing principal should be subtracted.","Correct: Net borrowing is new debt after repaying maturing principal.","Wrong: Net borrowing is not issuance minus the deficit.","Wrong: Net borrowing does not equal the deficit and does depend on issuance."]},{"id":"information-advanced-66","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[62],"stem":"财政部上调了季末TGA目标余额。其他不变，借款需求会怎样？","options":["减少，因为账户余额提高后可少发新债","不变，因为借款需求只由财政赤字决定","增加，因为需要多借钱把账户余额补到目标","不变，因为TGA目标只影响准备金不影响发债"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：TGA目标也能改变融资需要。","optionExplanations":["目标提高要更多现金，反而需要多借。","TGA目标也会改变融资需要。","正确，TGA目标提高会增加融资需要。","TGA目标直接影响财政部需要借多少。"],"skills":["机制","TGA"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Department of the Treasury official release and methodology","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/policy-issues/financing-the-government/quarterly-refunding"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The Treasury raises its end-of-quarter TGA target. With everything else unchanged, what happens to borrowing needs?","optionsEn":["They fall, because a higher balance means less new debt","They stay the same, because borrowing needs depend only on the deficit","They rise, because more must be borrowed to bring the balance up to target","They stay the same, because the TGA target affects reserves, not issuance"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the TGA target can also change financing needs.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A higher target needs more cash, so more must be borrowed.","Wrong: The TGA target also changes financing needs.","Correct: A higher TGA target raises financing needs.","Wrong: The TGA target directly affects how much the Treasury must borrow."]},{"id":"information-beginner-118","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[63],"stem":"美国联邦政府财年从哪个月开始？","options":["1月","4月","7月","10月"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：美国财年10月开始，不能把财年累计当公历年累计。","optionExplanations":["1月是公历年开始，不是财年。","4月是英国等国的财年起点。","7月是部分州与国家的财年起点。","正确，美国财年从10月开始。"],"skills":["财年","基础"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Treasury Fiscal Service official release and methodology","url":"https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-treasury-statement/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"In which month does the US federal fiscal year begin?","optionsEn":["January","April","July","October"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the US fiscal year starts in October, so don't treat fiscal-year-to-date totals as calendar-year totals.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: January starts the calendar year, not the fiscal year.","Wrong: April is the fiscal-year start in the UK and some other countries.","Wrong: July is the fiscal-year start for some states and countries.","Correct: The US fiscal year starts in October."]},{"id":"information-advanced-67","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[63],"stem":"某月财政赤字为1000亿美元。当月国债余额是否正好增加1000亿？","options":["会，国债增加额按定义恰好等于赤字","不会，赤字由税收补足，国债余额不受影响","不会，赤字由央行直接垫付，不计入国债","不一定，TGA等现金余额变动会影响借款"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：不可直接用月赤字推国债新增同额。","optionExplanations":["两者不相等，还要看现金余额等因素。","赤字正是需要借债弥补的缺口。","赤字主要靠发债融资，不是央行垫付。","正确，不能直接用月赤字推算国债新增。"],"skills":["区分","融资"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Treasury Fiscal Service official release and methodology","url":"https://fiscaldata.treasury.gov/datasets/monthly-treasury-statement/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","reviewed":"2026-10-30 blind re-solve: wording adjusted","stemEn":"The budget deficit for a month is $100 billion. Does Treasury debt outstanding rise by exactly $100 billion that month?","optionsEn":["Yes; by definition the rise in debt equals the deficit","No; the deficit is covered by taxes, so debt is unaffected","No; the central bank funds the deficit directly, outside Treasury debt","Not necessarily; changes in cash balances such as the TGA affect borrowing"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: you cannot infer an equal rise in debt directly from the monthly deficit.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The two are not equal; cash balances and other factors also matter.","Wrong: The deficit is exactly the gap that must be covered by borrowing.","Wrong: The deficit is financed mainly by issuing debt, not by central-bank advances.","Correct: You cannot infer the rise in debt directly from the monthly deficit."]},{"id":"information-beginner-119","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[64],"stem":"某加密ETF资产规模增加了，但当天净流量为0。最可能的原因是？","options":["当天数据错误","申购与赎回金额相等","资产价格上涨","净流量被漏报"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：价格上涨造成资产规模增加不等于资金流入。","optionExplanations":["可以同时成立。","申赎相等时净流量为0，但不会让规模增加。","课程：价格上涨造成资产规模增加不等于资金流入。","0与未发布不同。"],"skills":["区分","流量与规模"],"references":[{"title":"ETF发行商；供应商汇总如Farside official release and methodology","url":"https://www.ishares.com/us/products/333011/ishares-bitcoin-trust-etf"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"A crypto ETF's assets grew, but its net flow that day was 0. What is the most likely reason?","optionsEn":["That day's data is wrong","Creations and redemptions were equal","The asset's price rose","The net flow was not reported"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: assets rising because prices rose is not the same as money flowing in.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Both can be true at once.","Wrong: Equal creations and redemptions give a net flow of 0 but do not grow assets.","Correct: The lesson: assets rising because prices rose is not the same as money flowing in.","Wrong: 0 is different from not published."]},{"id":"information-beginner-120","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[65],"stem":"稳定币的储备“鉴证报告”与“审计”是什么关系？","options":["不同：鉴证范围比审计更广","相同：两者都是全面审计","相同：两者都每天更新","不同：鉴证只核对某个时点"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：鉴证不是审计，通常只针对某个时点核对储备，范围更窄。","optionExplanations":["覆盖更窄。","两者不同。","通常按月或季。","鉴证（attestation）通常只核对某个时点的储备是否足额，范围比审计窄，不能代替审计。"],"skills":["区分","定义"],"references":[{"title":"稳定币发行商与独立鉴证会计师；以Circle USDC为例 official release and methodology","url":"https://www.circle.com/transparency"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How does a stablecoin reserve \"attestation\" relate to an \"audit\"?","optionsEn":["Different: an attestation is broader than an audit","The same: both are full audits","The same: both update daily","Different: an attestation checks only one point in time"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: an attestation is not an audit; it usually checks reserves at a single point in time and is narrower in scope.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Its scope is narrower.","Wrong: The two are different.","Wrong: They are usually monthly or quarterly.","Correct: An attestation usually checks only whether reserves were sufficient at one point in time; it is narrower than an audit and cannot replace one."]},{"id":"information-beginner-121","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[66],"stem":"FOMC点阵图代表什么？","options":["委员对未来利率路径作出的集体承诺","上一次会议各委员对利率决定的投票记录","官员各自的条件预测，不是对利率的承诺","利率期货市场隐含的未来政策利率路径"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程提醒：点阵图是官员条件预测，不是承诺。","optionExplanations":["点阵图不是承诺，条件变化路径就会变。","点阵图是对未来的预测，不是投票记录。","正确，点阵图是官员的条件预测。","那是市场定价，不是官员的预测。"],"skills":["定义","解读"],"references":[{"title":"Federal Reserve Board official release and methodology","url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/monetarypolicy/fomccalendars.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What does the FOMC dot plot represent?","optionsEn":["A collective commitment by members to a future rate path","The voting record of members on the last rate decision","Officials' individual conditional projections, not a rate commitment","The future policy rate path implied by rate futures"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, the dot plot is officials' conditional projections, not a commitment.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The dot plot is not a commitment; the path changes when conditions change.","Wrong: The dot plot projects the future; it is not a voting record.","Correct: The dot plot is officials' conditional projections.","Wrong: That is market pricing, not officials' projections."]},{"id":"information-beginner-122","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[67],"stem":"ECB的三个关键利率是？","options":["存款便利利率、欧元短期利率、回购操作利率","存款便利利率、主要再融资利率、边际贷款利率","再融资利率、同业拆借利率、紧急流动性利率","主要再融资利率、长期再融资利率、资产购买利率"],"answer":1,"explanation":"课程提醒：若只说ECB利率却不说明哪个工具，会把不同数值混在一起。","optionExplanations":["后两者不是ECB的关键利率名称。","正确，这是ECB的三个关键利率。","这个组合不是ECB的三个关键利率。","长期再融资与资产购买不属于三个关键利率。"],"skills":["工具","定义"],"references":[{"title":"European Central Bank ECB official release and methodology","url":"https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/govcdec/mopo/html/index.en.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What are the ECB's three key interest rates?","optionsEn":["Deposit facility rate, euro short-term rate, repo operations rate","Deposit facility rate, main refinancing rate, marginal lending rate","Refinancing rate, interbank rate, emergency liquidity rate","Main refinancing rate, longer-term refinancing rate, asset purchase rate"],"explanationEn":"As the lesson notes, saying \"the ECB rate\" without naming the instrument mixes different values together.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The last two are not names of ECB key rates.","Correct: These are the ECB's three key rates.","Wrong: This combination is not the ECB's three key rates.","Wrong: Longer-term refinancing and asset purchases are not among the three key rates."]},{"id":"information-advanced-68","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[67],"stem":"ECB决议当天，声明和记者会是什么关系？","options":["先召开记者会，随后发布利率声明","声明与记者会同时进行，内容基本一致","记者会在次日举行，声明当天公布","先发布利率声明，随后召开记者会"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：除利率外，预测与表述同样重要。","optionExplanations":["顺序说反了。","两者是先后进行的两个环节，记者会还有额外内容。","记者会在决议当天举行，不在次日。","正确，声明在先，记者会在后。"],"skills":["发布流程","阅读"],"references":[{"title":"European Central Bank ECB official release and methodology","url":"https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/govcdec/mopo/html/index.en.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"On an ECB decision day, how do the statement and the press conference relate?","optionsEn":["The press conference comes first, then the rate statement","They happen at the same time with essentially the same content","The press conference is the next day; the statement comes out that day","The rate statement comes first, then the press conference"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: besides rates, the projections and wording matter just as much.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The order is reversed.","Wrong: They are two sequential steps, and the press conference adds content.","Wrong: The press conference is held on decision day, not the next day.","Correct: The statement comes first, then the press conference."]},{"id":"information-beginner-123","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[68],"stem":"英国央行MPC投票7−2维持利率，这个投票比例透露什么？","options":["委员间存在分歧，少数票可能透露政策方向","利率调整了7个基点，另有2个基点待定","9位委员中有2位反对，所以议案没有通过","投票比例只是惯例记录，不含方向信息"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：投票变化可提前透露政策分歧。","optionExplanations":["正确，投票比例可提前反映分歧。","投票比例不是基点数。","7票多数赞成，议案已通过。","少数票往往透露政策分歧与方向。"],"skills":["投票","解读"],"references":[{"title":"Bank of England official release and methodology","url":"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"The Bank of England's MPC votes 7–2 to hold rates. What does the vote split reveal?","optionsEn":["Members are divided, and the minority may signal the policy direction","Rates moved 7 basis points, with 2 more pending","2 of 9 members opposed, so the motion failed","The vote split is just a formality and carries no directional information"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: shifts in the vote can reveal policy divisions in advance.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The vote split can reveal divisions in advance.","Wrong: The vote split is not a number of basis points.","Wrong: A 7-vote majority was in favour, so the motion passed.","Wrong: Minority votes often reveal policy divisions and direction."]},{"id":"information-beginner-124","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[69],"stem":"日本央行的政策决议公布时间有什么特点？","options":["固定在东京时间中午，可以提前设好提醒","固定在会议结束后的次日早晨公布","不固定，需按当次日程关注发布时间","固定在美联储决议之后的同一小时"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：公告时间不固定。","optionExplanations":["时间并不固定，不能按中午设定。","不是次日，通常当天会议结束后公布。","正确，公告时间不固定。","与美联储决议时间没有固定对应。"],"skills":["时间","基础"],"references":[{"title":"Bank of Japan BOJ official release and methodology","url":"https://www.boj.or.jp/en/mopo/mpmdeci/index.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is distinctive about when the Bank of Japan announces its policy decision?","optionsEn":["It is fixed at noon Tokyo time, so you can set a reminder in advance","It is fixed for the morning after the meeting ends","It is not fixed, so watch the timing for each meeting","It is fixed for the same hour after the Fed's decision"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: the announcement time is not fixed.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: The time is not fixed, so you cannot set it for noon.","Wrong: It is not the next day; it usually comes out the same day once the meeting ends.","Correct: The announcement time is not fixed.","Wrong: It has no fixed link to the Fed's decision time."]},{"id":"information-advanced-69","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[69],"stem":"阅读日本央行决议时，应以什么为准？","options":["以早期负利率和YCC的介绍为准","以美联储同期声明的措辞为参照","以当次声明的政策工具与利率为准","以媒体对上次会议的总结为准"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：不应用过时的负利率或YCC说明代替当次声明。","optionExplanations":["过时的政策说明可能已不适用。","日本央行的决议要看其自己的声明。","正确，不应用过时说明代替当次声明。","上次会议的总结不能代替当次声明。"],"skills":["阅读","时效"],"references":[{"title":"Bank of Japan BOJ official release and methodology","url":"https://www.boj.or.jp/en/mopo/mpmdeci/index.htm"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"When reading a Bank of Japan decision, what should you go by?","optionsEn":["Earlier explanations of negative rates and YCC","The wording of the Fed's statement at the same time","The policy tools and rates in that meeting's statement","Media summaries of the previous meeting"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: don't substitute outdated explanations of negative rates or YCC for the current statement.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Outdated policy explanations may no longer apply.","Wrong: A BoJ decision should be read from the BoJ's own statement.","Correct: Don't substitute outdated explanations for the current statement.","Wrong: A summary of the previous meeting cannot replace the current statement."]},{"id":"information-beginner-125","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[70],"stem":"EIA每周原油库存报告通常在哪天发布？","options":["周三","周二","周四","周五"],"answer":0,"explanation":"EIA周报通常周三发布（假期顺延）。","optionExplanations":["正确，EIA原油周报通常周三发布。","周二晚上是API报告的发布时间，不是EIA。","周四是EIA天然气库存报告的发布日。","周五不是EIA原油周报的发布日。"],"skills":["时间","基础"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Energy Information Administration EIA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.eia.gov/petroleum/supply/weekly/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"On which day is the EIA weekly crude inventory report usually released?","optionsEn":["Wednesday","Tuesday","Thursday","Friday"],"explanationEn":"The EIA weekly report usually comes out on Wednesday (delayed by holidays).","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: The EIA weekly crude report usually comes out on Wednesday.","Wrong: Tuesday evening is when the API report comes out, not the EIA.","Wrong: Thursday is when the EIA natural gas storage report comes out.","Wrong: Friday is not the release day for the EIA crude report."]},{"id":"information-beginner-126","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[70],"stem":"API原油库存与EIA原油库存是什么关系？","options":["API是另一份行业估计，不是EIA数据","API是EIA报告发布前的初值，之后被修订","API由EIA编制，面向行业提前发布","API是EIA数据的行业版本，二者数值相同"],"answer":0,"explanation":"课程：API是另一份行业估计，不是EIA。","optionExplanations":["正确，API与EIA是两份不同的数据。","API并非EIA的初值。","API由行业协会发布，不是EIA编制。","两者数值常有差异。"],"skills":["来源","区分"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Energy Information Administration EIA official release and methodology","url":"https://www.eia.gov/petroleum/supply/weekly/"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"How do API crude inventories relate to EIA crude inventories?","optionsEn":["API is a separate industry estimate, not EIA data","API is the preliminary EIA figure, revised later","API is compiled by the EIA and released early to industry","API is the industry version of EIA data, with the same numbers"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: API is a separate industry estimate, not the EIA.","optionExplanationsEn":["Correct: API and EIA are two different data sets.","Wrong: API is not a preliminary EIA figure.","Wrong: API is published by an industry association, not compiled by the EIA.","Wrong: The two often differ."]},{"id":"information-beginner-127","type":"information","level":"beginner","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[71],"stem":"EIA天然气库存报告的单位Bcf是什么？","options":["十亿立方米","十亿英热单位","十亿立方英尺","十亿桶"],"answer":2,"explanation":"课程：常用Bcf，十亿立方英尺。","optionExplanations":["单位制不同，美国用立方英尺。","英热单位是热值，不是体积。","正确，Bcf是十亿立方英尺。","桶是原油单位，不是天然气。"],"skills":["单位","基础"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Energy Information Administration EIA official release and methodology","url":"https://ir.eia.gov/ngs/ngs.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"What is Bcf, the unit in the EIA natural gas storage report?","optionsEn":["Billion cubic metres","Billion British thermal units","Billion cubic feet","Billion barrels"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: Bcf, billion cubic feet, is commonly used.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: Different system of units; the US uses cubic feet.","Wrong: A British thermal unit measures heat content, not volume.","Correct: Bcf is billion cubic feet.","Wrong: Barrels are a unit for crude oil, not natural gas."]},{"id":"information-advanced-70","type":"information","level":"advanced","topicIds":[],"infoIds":[71],"stem":"把本周天然气库存与五年均值比较，应注意什么？","options":["与上月的平均库存比较，反映最新趋势","与全年的平均库存比较，数据更平滑","与去年同期的价格比较，判断供需","与五年同一周的均值比较，剔除季节性"],"answer":3,"explanation":"课程：与五年均值比要用同一周。","optionExplanations":["月度均值混合了不同季节，不符合同一周的要求。","全年均值会掩盖季节性差异。","库存要和库存比，不是和价格比。","正确，库存有季节性，要同一周对比。"],"skills":["比较","季节性"],"references":[{"title":"U.S. Energy Information Administration EIA official release and methodology","url":"https://ir.eia.gov/ngs/ngs.html"}],"added":"2026-10-30","batch":"basic-usage","stemEn":"When comparing this week's natural gas storage with the five-year average, what should you watch?","optionsEn":["Compare with last month's average storage to reflect the latest trend","Compare with the full-year average storage for smoother data","Compare with prices a year ago to judge supply and demand","Compare with the five-year average for the same week to remove seasonality"],"explanationEn":"The lesson: comparisons with the five-year average must use the same week.","optionExplanationsEn":["Wrong: A monthly average mixes different seasons and does not meet the same-week requirement.","Wrong: A full-year average hides seasonal differences.","Wrong: Storage should be compared with storage, not with prices.","Correct: Storage is seasonal, so compare the same week."]}];
